, and so anybody in town would take

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0214"/>
it

          <ptr target="#la8789" type="alt" xml:id="te0214"/>
in a minute, let alone a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0313"/>
hair-ball

          <app from="pr0313" n="21.15 (72.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1471">
            <lem wit="A">hair-ball</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
hair-

              <lb/>
ball

            </rdg>
          </app>
. Well,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0215"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la8790" type="alt" xml:id="te0215"/>
knowed a potato would do that, before, but I had forgot it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e6987">
Jim put the quarter under the hair-ball and got down and listened again. This time he said the hair-ball was all right. He said it would tell my whole fortune if I wanted it to. I

