        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e7316">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">had shut</hi>
the door to. Then I turned around, and there he was. I used to be scared of him all the time, he tanned me so much. I reckoned I was scared now, too; but in a minute I see I was mistaken. That is, after the first jolt, as you may say, when my breath

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0223"/>
sort

          <ptr target="#la8798" type="alt" xml:id="te0223"/>
of hitched—he being so unexpected; but right away after, I see I warn’t scared of him worth bothering about.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7324">
He was most fifty, and he looked it. His hair was long and tangled and greasy, and hung down, and you could see his eyes shining

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0224"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0346"/>
through,

          <app from="pr0346" n="23.17 (76.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1537">
            <lem wit="MS1a">through,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
through

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0347"/>
like

          <ptr target="#la8799" type="alt" xml:id="te0224"/>
          <app from="pr0347" n="23.17 (76.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la1539">
            <lem wit="A">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">like as if</rdg>
          </app>
he was behind vines. It was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0348"/>
black;

          <app from="pr0348" n="23.18 (76.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1541">
            <lem wit="MS1a">black;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">black,</rdg>
          </app>
no gray; so was his long, mixed-up whiskers. There warn’t no color in his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0349"/>
face where

          <app from="pr0349" n="23.20 (76.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1543">
            <lem wit="MS1a">face where</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">face where,</rdg>
          </app>
his face showed; it was white; not like another man’s white, but a white to make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0350"/>
a body

          <app from="pr0350" n="23.21 (76.16)" type="e" xml:id="la1545">
            <lem wit="A">a body</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you</rdg>
          </app>
sick, a white to make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0351"/>
a body’s

          <app from="pr0351" n="23.21–22 (76.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1547">
            <lem wit="A">a body’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">your</rdg>
          </app>
flesh crawl—a tree-toad white, a fish-belly white. As for his clothes—just rags, that was all.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0225"/>
He

          <ptr target="#la8800" type="alt" xml:id="te0225"/>
had one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0352"/>
ancle

          <app from="pr0352" n="23.23 (76.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la1549">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ancle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ankle</rdg>
          </app>
resting on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0353"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr0353" n="23.23 (76.21)" type="e" xml:id="la1551">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
knee; the boot on that foot was busted, and two of his toes stuck through, and he worked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0354"/>
them,

          <app from="pr0354" n="23.25 (77.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la1553">
            <lem wit="MS1a">them,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
them

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now and then. His hat was laying on the floor; an old black slouch with the top caved in, like a lid.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7406">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0355"/>
stood,

          <app from="pr0355" n="23.27 (77.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1555">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stood,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
stood

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a-looking at him; he set there a-looking at me, with his chair tilted back a little. I set the candle down. I noticed the window was up;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0226"/>
so

          <ptr target="#la8801" type="alt" xml:id="te0226"/>
he had clumb in by the shed. He kept a-looking me all over.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0356"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0356" n="23.30 (77.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la1557">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7429">
“Starchy clothes—very. You think you’re a good deal of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0357"/>
big-bug,

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
          <app from="pr0357" n="23.31–32 (77.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la1559">
            <lem wit="A">
big-bug,

              <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">swell, don’t</rdg>
          </app>
you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7443">
          <pb n="24" xml:id="pb0024"/>
“Maybe I am, maybe I ain’t,” I says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7446">
“Don’t you give me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0358"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0227"/>
none

          <ptr target="#la8802" type="alt" xml:id="te0227"/>
          <app from="pr0358" n="24.2 (78.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1561">
            <lem wit="A">none</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
any/

              <add>none</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0359"/>
o’

          <app from="pr0359" n="24.2 (78.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1563">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
your lip,” says he. “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0360"/>
You’ve put on considerble

          <app from="pr0360" n="24.2–3 (78.5–7)" type="e" xml:id="la1565">
            <lem wit="A">You’ve . . . considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Yes, a nice swell—a mighty nice swell. You’re putting on considerable</rdg>
          </app>
many frills since I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0361"/>
been

          <app from="pr0361" n="24.3 (78.8)" type="e" xml:id="la1567">
            <lem wit="A">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ben</rdg>
          </app>
away. I’ll take you down a peg before I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0362"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0013"/>
git

          <ptr target="#tb0013" type="te" xml:id="tv0013"/>
          <app from="pr0362" n="✱24.4 (78.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la1569">
            <lem wit="MS1a">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">get</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0228"/>
done

          <ptr target="#la8803" type="alt" xml:id="te0228"/>
with you. You’re educated, too, they say; can read and write.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="se0087"/>
You think you’re better’n your father, now, don’t you, because he can’t

          <ptr target="#as0049" type="an" xml:id="se0088"/>
?

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’ll take it out of you. Who told you you might meddle with such

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0363"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0229"/>
hifalut’n

          <ptr target="#la8804" type="alt" xml:id="te0229"/>
          <app from="pr0363" n="24.7 (78.19)" type="e" xml:id="la1571">
            <lem wit="A">hifalut’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
hifalutin/

              <add>hifalut’n</add>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1573">see Alterations</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
foolishness, hey?—who told you you could?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7520">“The widow. She told me.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7522">
“The widow,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0364"/>
hey?—and

          <app from="pr0364" n="24.10 (79.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la1574">
            <lem wit="A">hey?—and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
hey?—

              <lb/>
And

            </rdg>
          </app>
who told the widow she could put in her shovel about a thing that ain’t none of her business?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7535">“Nobody never told her.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7537">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0365"/>
Well

          <app from="pr0365" n="24.13 (79.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la1576">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
I’ll learn her how to meddle. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0366"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr0366" n="24.13 (79.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la1578">
            <lem wit="MS1a">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
—you drop that school,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0367"/>
you

          <app from="pr0367" n="24.14 (79.14)" type="e" xml:id="la1580">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">do you</rdg>
          </app>
hear? I’ll learn people to bring up a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0230"/>
boy

          <ptr target="#la8805" type="alt" xml:id="te0230"/>
to put on airs over his own father and let on to be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0368"/>
better’n

          <app from="pr0368" n="24.15 (79.18)" type="e" xml:id="la1582">
            <lem wit="A">better’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">better than</rdg>
          </app>
what

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0369"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
          <app from="pr0369" n="24.15 (79.19)" type="e" xml:id="la1584">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he</rdg>
          </app>
is. You

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0231"/>
lemme

          <ptr target="#la8806" type="alt" xml:id="te0231"/>
catch you fooling around that school again,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0232"/>
you hear?

          <ptr target="#la8807" type="alt" xml:id="te0232"/>
Your mother couldn’t read, and she couldn’t write, nuther, before she died. None of the family couldn’t, before

          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
died.

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
can’t; and here

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0370"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr0370" n="24.19 (80.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la1586">
            <lem wit="A">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you are</rdg>
          </app>
a-swelling yourself up like this. I ain’t the man to stand it—you hear? Say—lemme hear you read.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7610">
I

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="se0089"/>
took up a book and begun something about General Washington and the wars

          <ptr target="#as0050" type="an" xml:id="se0090"/>
. When I’d read about a half a minute, he fetched the book a whack with his hand and knocked it across the house. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7616">
“It’s so. You can do it. I had my doubts when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0371"/>
you

          <app from="pr0371" n="24.25 (81.2)" type="e" xml:id="la1588">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they</rdg>
          </app>
told me. Now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0372"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr0372" n="24.26 (81.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la1590">
            <lem wit="MS1a">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
; you stop that putting on frills. I won’t have it. I’ll lay for you, my smarty; and if I catch you about that school I’ll tan you good. First you know you’ll get religion, too.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0233"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la8808" type="alt" xml:id="te0233"/>
never

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0374"/>
see

          <app from="pr0374" n="24.28 (81.10)" type="e" xml:id="la1594">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
such a son.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7647">
He took up a little blue and yaller picture of some

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0234"/>
cows

          <ptr target="#la8809" type="alt" xml:id="te0234"/>
and a boy, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0373"/>
says—

          <app from="pr0373" n="24.30 (81.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la1592">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7660">“What’s this?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7662">“It’s something they give me for learning my lessons good.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7664">He tore it up, and says—</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7666">
“I’ll give you something better—I’ll give you a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0375"/>
cowhide

          <app from="pr0375" n="24.34 (82.2)" type="e" xml:id="la1596">
            <lem wit="A">cowhide</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">rawhide</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7676">He set there a-mumbling and a-growling a minute, and then he says—</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7678">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Ain’t</hi>
you a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0235"/>
sweet-scented

          <ptr target="#la8810" type="alt" xml:id="te0235"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0376"/>
dandy,

          <app from="pr0376" n="24.37 (82.7)" type="e" xml:id="la1598">
            <lem wit="A">dandy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">swell</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0236"/>
though?

          <ptr target="#la8811" type="alt" xml:id="te0236"/>
A bed; and bedclothes; and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0377"/>
look’n-glass

          <app from="pr0377" n="24.38 (82.9)" type="e" xml:id="la1600">
            <lem wit="A">look’n-glass</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">looking-glass</rdg>
          </app>
; and a piece of carpet on the floor—and

          <pb n="25" xml:id="pb0025"/>
your own father got to sleep with the hogs in the tanyard.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0237"/>
I never see such a son.

          <ptr target="#la8812" type="alt" xml:id="te0237"/>
I bet I’ll take some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0378"/>
o’ these

          <app from="pr0378" n="25.2 (82.14)" type="e" xml:id="la1602">
            <lem wit="A">o’ these</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of these</rdg>
          </app>
frills out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0379"/>
o’ you

          <app from="pr0379" n="25.2 (82.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1604">
            <lem wit="A">o’ you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of you</rdg>
          </app>
before

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0238"/>
I’m

          <ptr target="#la8813" type="alt" xml:id="te0238"/>
done with you. Why there ain’t no end to your airs—they say you’re rich. Hey?—how’s that?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7734">“They lie—that’s how.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7736">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0380"/>
Looky-here

          <app from="pr0380" n="25.6 (82.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la1606">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Looky here</rdg>
          </app>
—mind how you talk to me; I’m a-standing about all I can stand, now—so don’t gimme no sass.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0381"/>
I’ve been

          <app from="pr0381" n="25.7 (83.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1608">
            <lem wit="A">I’ve been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I ben</rdg>
          </app>
in town two days, and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0239"/>
hain’t

          <ptr target="#la8814" type="alt" xml:id="te0239"/>
heard nothing but about you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0382"/>
bein’

          <app from="pr0382" n="25.8 (83.7)" type="e" xml:id="la1610">
            <lem wit="A">bein’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">being</rdg>
          </app>
rich. I heard about it away down the river, too. That’s why I come. You git me that money to-morrow—I want it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7767">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0383"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr0383" n="25.11 (83.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1614">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0384"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0240"/>
no

          <ptr target="#la8815" type="alt" xml:id="te0240"/>
          <app from="pr0384" n="25.11 (83.13)" type="e" xml:id="ly1614">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
any/

              <add>no</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
money.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7789">“It’s a lie. Judge Thatcher’s got it. You git it. I want it.”</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y02501">
          <graphic url="y02501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">huck and his father</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7796">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0385"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr0385" n="25.13 (83.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1616">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0386"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0241"/>
no

          <ptr target="#la8816" type="alt" xml:id="te0241"/>
          <app from="pr0386" n="25.13 (83.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1618">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
any/

              <add>no</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
money, I tell you. You ask Judge Thatcher; he’ll tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0387"/>
you the same

          <app from="pr0387" n="25.14 (83.19)" type="e" xml:id="la1620">
            <lem wit="A">you the same</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7827">“All right. I’ll ask him; and I’ll make him pungle, too, or I’ll know the reason why. Say—how much you got in your pocket? I want it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7829">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0388"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr0388" n="25.17 (84.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la1622">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
got only a dollar, and I want that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0389"/>
to—

          <app from="pr0389" n="25.17 (84.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1624">
            <lem wit="MS1a">to—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">to——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7847">“It don’t make no difference what you want it for—you just shell it out.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7849">
He took it and bit

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0390"/>
it,

          <app from="pr0390" n="25.20 (84.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1626">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0242"/>
to

          <ptr target="#la8817" type="alt" xml:id="te0242"/>
see if it was good, and then he said he was

          <pb n="26" xml:id="pb0026"/>
going down town

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0391"/>
to

          <app from="pr0391" n="26.1 (84.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1628">
            <lem wit="A">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
get some whisky; said he hadn’t had a drink all day. When he had got out on the shed, he put his head in again, and cussed me for putting on frills and trying to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0243"/>
be

          <ptr target="#la8818" type="alt" xml:id="te0243"/>
better than him; and when I reckoned he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0392"/>
gone

          <app from="pr0392" n="26.4 (85.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1630">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gone</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">gone,</rdg>
          </app>
he come back and put his head in again, and told me to mind about that school, because he was going to lay for me and lick me if I didn’t drop that.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7885">Next day he was drunk, and he went to Judge Thatcher’s and bullyragged him and tried to make him give up the money, but he couldn’t, and then he swore he’d make the law force him.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7888">
The judge and the widow went to law to get the court to take me away from him and let one of them be my guardian; but it was a new judge that had just come, and he didn’t know the old man; so he said courts mustn’t interfere and separate

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0244"/>
families

          <ptr target="#la8819" type="alt" xml:id="te0244"/>
if they could help it; said he’d druther not take a child away from its father.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0245"/>
So

          <ptr target="#la8820" type="alt" xml:id="te0245"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0246"/>
Judge

          <ptr target="#la8821" type="alt" xml:id="te0246"/>
Thatcher and the widow had to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0247"/>
quit

          <ptr target="#la8822" type="alt" xml:id="te0247"/>
on the business.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7906">
That pleased the old man till he couldn’t rest. He said he’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0393"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0248"/>
cowhide

          <ptr target="#la8823" type="alt" xml:id="te0248"/>
          <app from="pr0393" n="26.17 (86.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1632">
            <lem wit="A">cowhide</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">raw-hide</rdg>
          </app>
me till I was black and blue if I didn’t raise some money for him. I borrowed three dollars from Judge

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0394"/>
Thatcher

          <app from="pr0394" n="26.18 (86.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la1634">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Thatcher</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Thatcher,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0249"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0395"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0395" n="26.18 (86.20)" type="e" xml:id="la1636">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#la8824" type="alt" xml:id="te0249"/>
took it and got drunk and went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0396"/>
a-blowing

          <app from="pr0396" n="26.19 (86.21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la1638">
            <lem wit="A">a-blowing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
a-

              <lb/>
blowing

            </rdg>
          </app>
around and cussing and whooping and carrying on; and he kept it up all over town, with a tin

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0397"/>
pan

          <app from="pr0397" n="26.20 (87.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la1640">
            <lem wit="MS1a">pan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pan,</rdg>
          </app>
till most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0398"/>
midnight

          <app from="pr0398" n="26.21 (87.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la1642">
            <lem wit="A">midnight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
mid-

              <lb/>
night

            </rdg>
          </app>
; then they jailed him, and next day they had him before

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0399"/>
court

          <app from="pr0399" n="26.22 (87.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1644">
            <lem wit="MS1a">court</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">court,</rdg>
          </app>
and jailed him again for a week. But he said

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
was satisfied; said he was boss of his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0400"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0250"/>
son

          <ptr target="#la8825" type="alt" xml:id="te0250"/>
          <app from="pr0400" n="26.23 (87.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1646">
            <lem wit="MS1a">son</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">son,</rdg>
          </app>
and he’d make it warm for

          <hi rend="italic">him.</hi>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e7990">
When he got out the

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="se0091"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0401"/>
new

          <app from="pr0401" n="26.25 (87.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1648">
            <lem wit="A">new</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1650">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
judge said he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0402"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr0402" n="26.25 (87.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1651">
            <lem wit="A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
to make a man of him

          <ptr target="#as0051" type="an" xml:id="se0092"/>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0251"/>
So

          <ptr target="#la8826" type="alt" xml:id="te0251"/>
he took him to his own house, and dressed him up clean and nice, and had him to breakfast and dinner and supper with the family, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0252"/>
was

          <ptr target="#la8827" type="alt" xml:id="te0252"/>
just old pie to him, so to speak. And after supper he talked to him about temperance and such things till the old man cried, and said he’d been a fool, and fooled away his life; but now he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0403"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr0403" n="26.31 (88.8)" type="e" xml:id="la1653">
            <lem wit="A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
to turn over a new

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0253"/>
leaf

          <ptr target="#la8828" type="alt" xml:id="te0253"/>
and be a man nobody wouldn’t be ashamed of, and he hoped the judge would help him and not look down on him. The judge said he could hug him for them words; so

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0014"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
cried, and his wife she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0404"/>
cried, and the old man

          <app from="pr0404" n="✱26.34 (88.17–18)" type="hc" xml:id="la1655">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cried, and the old man</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1657">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
cried again;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0405"/>
said

          <app from="pr0405" n="✱26.34 (88.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la1658">
            <lem wit="MS1a">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pap said</rdg>
          </app>
he’d

          <ptr target="#tb0014" type="te" xml:id="tv0014"/>
been a man that had always been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0406"/>
misunderstood,

          <app from="pr0406" n="26.35 (88.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la1660">
            <lem wit="MS1a">misunderstood,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
misunderstood

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before, and the judge said he believed it. The old man said that what a man wanted

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0254"/>
that

          <ptr target="#la8829" type="alt" xml:id="te0254"/>
was down, was sympathy; and the judge said it was so;

          <pb n="27" xml:id="pb0027"/>
so they cried again. And when it was bedtime, the old man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0407"/>
rose

          <app from="pr0407" n="27.1 (89.1)" type="e" xml:id="la1662">
            <lem wit="A">rose</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he rose</rdg>
          </app>
up and held out his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0408"/>
hand

          <app from="pr0408" n="27.2 (89.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1664">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hand</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hand,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8089">
“Look at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0409"/>
it,

          <app from="pr0409" n="27.3 (89.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la1666">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0410"/>
gentlemen

          <app from="pr0410" n="27.3 (89.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la1668">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gentlemen</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">gentlemen,</rdg>
          </app>
and ladies all; take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0411"/>
a-hold

          <app from="pr0411" n="27.3 (89.11)" type="e" xml:id="la1670">
            <lem wit="MS1a">a-hold</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ahold</rdg>
          </app>
of it; shake it. There’s a hand that was the hand of a hog; but it ain’t so no more; it’s the hand of a man that’s started in on a new

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0412"/>
life

          <app from="pr0412" n="27.5 (89.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la1672">
            <lem wit="MS1a">life</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">life,</rdg>
          </app>
and ’ll die before he’ll go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0413"/>
back. You

          <app from="pr0413" n="27.6 (89.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la1674">
            <lem wit="A">back. You</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
back.—

              <lb/>
You

            </rdg>
          </app>
mark them words—don’t forget I said them. It’s a clean

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0414"/>
hand,

          <app from="pr0414" n="27.7 (89.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la1676">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hand,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
hand

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0415"/>
now; shake

          <app from="pr0415" n="27.7 (89.21–90.1)" type="e" xml:id="la1678">
            <lem wit="A">now; shake</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
now.—

              <milestone unit="page"/>
Shake

            </rdg>
          </app>
it—don’t be afeard.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y02701">
          <graphic url="y02701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">reforming the drunkard</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8156">
So they shook it, one after the other, all around, and cried.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0416"/>
The judge’s wife

          <app from="pr0416" n="27.8–9 (90.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1680">
            <lem wit="A">The judge’s wife</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Mrs. Thatcher</rdg>
          </app>
she kissed it.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0255"/>
Then the old man he signed a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0417"/>
pledge—

          <ptr target="#la8830" type="alt" xml:id="te0255"/>
made his mark

          <app from="pr0417" n="27.9–10 (90.5)" type="e" xml:id="la1682">
            <lem wit="A">pledge—made his mark</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pledge</rdg>
          </app>
. The judge said it was the holiest time on record, or something like that. Then they tucked the old man into a beautiful

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0256"/>
room

          <ptr target="#la8831" type="alt" xml:id="te0256"/>
, which was the spare room, and in the night

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0418"/>
some time

          <app from="pr0418" n="27.12 (90.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la1684">
            <lem wit="MS1a">some time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sometime</rdg>
          </app>
he got powerful thirsty and clumb out onto the porch-roof and slid down a stanchion and traded his new coat for a jug of forty-rod, and clumb back again and had a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0419"/>
old

          <app from="pr0419" n="27.15 (90.20)" type="e" xml:id="la1686">
            <lem wit="A">old</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1688">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
time; and towards daylight he crawled

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0002"/>
out again, drunk as a fiddler, and rolled off the porch and broke his left arm in two places and was most froze to death when somebody found him after

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0257"/>
sun-up

          <ptr target="#la8832" type="alt" xml:id="te0257"/>
. And when they come to look at that spare room, they had to take soundings before they could navigate it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8207">
          <pb n="28" xml:id="pb0028"/>
The judge he felt kind of sore. He said he reckoned a body could reform the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0420"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0015"/>
old

          <ptr target="#tb0015" type="te" xml:id="tv0015"/>
          <app from="pr0420" n="✱28.2 (91.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la1689">
            <lem wit="MS1a">old</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ole</rdg>
          </app>
man with a shot-gun, maybe, but he didn’t know no other way

          <ptr target="#mt0002" type="alt" xml:id="wn0002"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8222">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y02801">
            <graphic url="y02801.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">falling from grace</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0261">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter VI.</head>
        <pb n="29" xml:id="pb0029"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8232">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y02901">
            <graphic url="y02901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0421"/>
Chapter VI.

              <app from="pr0421" n="29 title (92 title)" type="e" xml:id="la1691">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter VI.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">CHAP. 7.</rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">Well,</hi>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2901">
            <graphic url="hf2901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">getting out of the way</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e8250">
pretty soon the old man was up and around again, and then he went for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0422"/>
Judge Thatcher

          <app from="pr0422" n="29.3 (92.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1693">
            <lem wit="A">Judge Thatcher</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">the judge</rdg>
          </app>
in the courts to make him give up that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0258"/>
money,

          <ptr target="#la8833" type="alt" xml:id="te0258"/>
and he went for me, too, for not stopping school. He catched me a couple of times and thrashed me, but I went to school just the same, and dodged him or out-run him most of the time. I didn’t want to go to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0423"/>
school,

          <app from="pr0423" n="29.12 (93.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1695">
            <lem wit="MS1a">school,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
school

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
much, before, but I reckoned I’d go now to spite

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0424"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0424" n="29.13 (93.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1697">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
. That law trial was a slow business; appeared

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0425"/>
like

          <app from="pr0425" n="29.15 (93.6)" type="e" xml:id="la1699">
            <lem wit="A">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">as if</rdg>
          </app>
they warn’t ever going to get started on it; so every now

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0016"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0426"/>
and then, all winter, the old man would lay for me and catch me, and then

          <app from="pr0426" n="✱29.16–17 (93.8–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la1701">
            <lem wit="MS1a">and then, all winter, the old man would lay for me and catch me, and then</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and then</rdg>
          </app>
I’d borrow

          <ptr target="#tb0016" type="te" xml:id="tv0016"/>
two or three dollars off of the judge for him, to keep from getting a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0427"/>
cowhiding

          <app from="pr0427" n="29.18–19 (93.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1703">
            <lem wit="A">cowhiding</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">raw-hiding</rdg>
          </app>
. Every time he got money he got drunk; and every time he got drunk he raised

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0259"/>
Cain around

          <ptr target="#la8834" type="alt" xml:id="te0259"/>
town; and every time he raised Cain he got jailed. He was just suited—this kind of thing was right in his line.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8314">
He got to hanging around the widow’s too much, and so she told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0428"/>
him,

          <app from="pr0428" n="29.24 (94.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la1705">
            <lem wit="MS1a">him,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
him

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at last, that if he didn’t quit using around there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0429"/>
she would

          <app from="pr0429" n="29.24 (94.9)" type="e" xml:id="la1707">
            <lem wit="A">she would</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">she’d</rdg>
          </app>
make trouble for him. Well,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0260"/>
          <hi rend="italic">wasn’t</hi>
          <ptr target="#la8835" type="alt" xml:id="te0260"/>
he mad? He said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0430"/>
he would

          <app from="pr0430" n="29.25 (94.11)" type="e" xml:id="la1709">
            <lem wit="A">he would</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he’d</rdg>
          </app>
show who was Huck Finn’s boss. So he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0261"/>
watched out

          <ptr target="#la8836" type="alt" xml:id="te0261"/>
for me one day in the spring, and catched me, and took me up the river about three

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0431"/>
mile

          <app from="pr0431" n="29.27 (94.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la1711">
            <lem wit="MS1a">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mile,</rdg>
          </app>
in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0432"/>
skiff

          <app from="pr0432" n="29.28 (94.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la1713">
            <lem wit="MS1a">skiff</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">skiff,</rdg>
          </app>
and crossed over to the Illinois shore where it was woody and there warn’t no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0262"/>
houses

          <ptr target="#la8837" type="alt" xml:id="te0262"/>
but an old log hut in a place where the timber was so thick you couldn’t find it if you didn’t know where it was.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8371">
He kept me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0433"/>
with

          <app from="pr0433" n="29.32 (95.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la1715">
            <lem wit="A">with</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">right with</rdg>
          </app>
him all the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0434"/>
time

          <app from="pr0434" n="29.32 (95.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la1717">
            <lem wit="MS1a">time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">time,</rdg>
          </app>
and I never got a chance to run off. We lived in that old cabin, and he always locked the door and

          <pb n="30" xml:id="pb0030"/>
put the key under his head, nights. He had a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0435"/>
gun,

          <app from="pr0435" n="30.1 (95.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1719">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gun,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
gun

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
which

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0263"/>
he

          <ptr target="#la8838" type="alt" xml:id="te0263"/>
had stole, I reckon, and we fished and hunted, and that was what we lived on. Every little while he locked me in and went down to the store, three miles, to the ferry, and traded fish and game for whisky and fetched it home and got drunk and had a good time, and licked me. The widow she found out where I was,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0436"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0436" n="30.6 (96.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la1721">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, and she sent a man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0437"/>
over

          <app from="pr0437" n="30.7 (96.5)" type="e" xml:id="la1723">
            <lem wit="A">over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1725">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to try to get hold of me, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0438"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0438" n="30.7 (96.6)" type="e" xml:id="la1726">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
drove him off with the gun, and it warn’t long after that till I was used to being where I was, and liked it, all but the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0439"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0264"/>
cowhide

          <ptr target="#la8839" type="alt" xml:id="te0264"/>
          <app from="pr0439" n="30.9 (96.11)" type="e" xml:id="la1728">
            <lem wit="A">cowhide</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">raw-hide</rdg>
          </app>
part.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y03001">
          <graphic url="y03001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">solid comfort</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8446">
It was kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0265"/>
lazy

          <ptr target="#la8840" type="alt" xml:id="te0265"/>
and jolly, laying off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0440"/>
comfortable,

          <app from="pr0440" n="30.10 (96.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la1730">
            <lem wit="MS1a">comfortable,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
comfortable

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all day, smoking and fishing, and no books nor study. Two months or more run along, and my clothes got to be all rags and dirt, and I didn’t see how I’d ever got to like it so well at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0441"/>
widow’s

          <app from="pr0441" n="30.13 (97.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la1732">
            <lem wit="MS1a">widow’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">widow’s,</rdg>
          </app>
where you had to wash, and eat on a plate, and comb up, and go to bed and get up regular, and be forever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0266"/>
bothering over

          <ptr target="#la8841" type="alt" xml:id="te0266"/>
a book and have old Miss Watson pecking at you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0442"/>
all the time

          <app from="pr0442" n="30.16 (97.8)" type="e" xml:id="la1734">
            <lem wit="A">all the time</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">constant</rdg>
          </app>
. I didn’t want to go back no more.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0267"/>
I had

          <ptr target="#la8842" type="alt" xml:id="te0267"/>
stopped cussing, because the widow

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0268"/>
didn’t like it; but now I took to it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0443"/>
again,

          <app from="pr0443" n="30.18 (97.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la1736">
            <lem wit="MS1a">again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
again

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
because

          <ptr target="#la8843" type="alt" xml:id="te0268"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0444"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0444" n="30.18 (97.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1738">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0269"/>
hadn’t

          <ptr target="#la8844" type="alt" xml:id="te0269"/>
no objections. It was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0270"/>
pretty good times

          <ptr target="#la8845" type="alt" xml:id="te0270"/>
up in the woods there,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0271"/>
take it all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0445"/>
around

          <app from="pr0445" n="30.19 (97.16)" type="e" xml:id="la1740">
            <lem wit="A">around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">round</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#la8846" type="alt" xml:id="te0271"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8525">
But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0446"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0446" n="30.20 (97.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la1742">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0447"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0447" n="30.20 (97.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1744">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
got too handy with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0448"/>
hick’ry

          <app from="pr0448" n="30.20 (97.18)" type="e" xml:id="la1746">
            <lem wit="A">hick’ry</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hickory</rdg>
          </app>
, and I couldn’t stand it. I was all over welts.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0272"/>
He got to going away so much, too, and

          <pb n="31" xml:id="pb0031"/>
locking me in.

          <ptr target="#la8847" type="alt" xml:id="te0272"/>
Once he locked me in and was gone three days. It was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0273"/>
dreadful

          <ptr target="#la8848" type="alt" xml:id="te0273"/>
lonesome. I judged he had got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0449"/>
drownded

          <app from="pr0449" n="31.2 (98.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la1748">
            <lem wit="MS1a">drownded</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">drowned</rdg>
          </app>
and I wasn’t ever going to get out any more.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0274"/>
I was scared.

          <ptr target="#la8849" type="alt" xml:id="te0274"/>
I made up my mind I would fix up some way to leave there. I had tried to get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0275"/>
out of that cabin

          <ptr target="#la8850" type="alt" xml:id="te0275"/>
many a time, but I couldn’t find no way. There warn’t a window to it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0276"/>
big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0450"/>
enough

          <app from="pr0450" n="31.6 (98.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1750">
            <lem wit="MS1a">enough</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">enought</rdg>
          </app>
for a dog to get through. I couldn’t get up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0451"/>
chimbly

          <app from="pr0451" n="31.7 (98.12)" type="e" xml:id="la1752">
            <lem wit="A">chimbly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">chimney,</rdg>
          </app>
, it was too narrow.

          <ptr target="#la8851" type="alt" xml:id="te0276"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0277"/>
The

          <ptr target="#la8852" type="alt" xml:id="te0277"/>
door was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0278"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0452"/>
thick,

          <app from="pr0452" n="31.7 (98.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la1754">
            <lem wit="MS1a">thick,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
thick

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
solid oak

          <ptr target="#la8853" type="alt" xml:id="te0278"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0453"/>
slabs

          <app from="pr0453" n="31.7 (98.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1756">
            <lem wit="A">slabs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1758">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0279"/>
Pap was pretty careful not to leave a knife or anything in the cabin when he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0454"/>
was

          <app from="pr0454" n="31.9 (99.3)" type="e" xml:id="la1759">
            <lem wit="A">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">went</rdg>
          </app>
away; I reckon I had hunted the place over as much as a hundred times; well, I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0455"/>
most

          <app from="pr0455" n="31.10 (99.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la1761">
            <lem wit="MS1a">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’most</rdg>
          </app>
all the time at it, because it was about the only way to put in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0280"/>
the time

          <ptr target="#la8855" type="alt" xml:id="te0280"/>
. But this time I found something at last; I found an old rusty wood-saw without any handle; it was laid in between a rafter and the clapboards of the roof. I greased it up and went to work. There was an old horse-blanket nailed against the logs at the far end of the cabin behind the table, to keep the wind from blowing through the chinks and putting the candle out. I got under the table and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0456"/>
raised

          <app from="pr0456" n="31.17 (99.20)" type="e" xml:id="la1763">
            <lem wit="A">raised</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">raised up</rdg>
          </app>
the blanket and went to work to saw a section of the big bottom log out, big enough to let me through. Well, it was a good long job, but I was getting towards the end of it when I heard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0457"/>
pap’s

          <app from="pr0457" n="31.20 (99.25)" type="e" xml:id="la1765">
            <lem wit="A">pap’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap’s</rdg>
          </app>
gun in the woods. I got rid of the signs of my work, and dropped the blanket and hid my saw, and pretty soon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0458"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0458" n="31.22 (99.28)" type="e" xml:id="la1767">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
come in.

          <ptr target="#la8854" type="alt" xml:id="te0279"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8672">
Pap warn’t in a good humor—so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0304"/>
he was his natural self. He said he was down to town, and everything was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0282"/>
going

          <ptr target="#la8857" type="alt" xml:id="te0282"/>
wrong. His lawyer said he reckoned he would win his lawsuit and get the money, if they ever got started on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0459"/>
trial,

          <app from="pr0459" n="31.26 (100.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1769">
            <lem wit="MS1a">trial,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">trial;</rdg>
          </app>
but then there was ways to put it off a long

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0460"/>
time

          <app from="pr0460" n="31.27 (100.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la1771">
            <lem wit="MS1a">time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">time,</rdg>
          </app>
and Judge Thatcher knowed how to do it. And he said people allowed there’d be another trial to get me away from him and give me to the widow for my guardian, and they guessed it would win, this time. This

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0283"/>
shook

          <ptr target="#la8858" type="alt" xml:id="te0283"/>
me up considerable, because I didn’t want to go back to the widow’s any more and be so cramped up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0461"/>
sivilized

          <app from="pr0461" n="31.32 (101.3)" type="e" xml:id="la1773">
            <lem wit="A">sivilized</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">civilized</rdg>
          </app>
, as they called it. Then the old man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0284"/>
got

          <ptr target="#la8859" type="alt" xml:id="te0284"/>
to cussing, and cussed everything and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0462"/>
everybody

          <app from="pr0462" n="31.33 (101.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la1775">
            <lem wit="A">everybody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">every body</rdg>
          </app>
he could think of, and then cussed them all over again to make sure he hadn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0285"/>
skipped

          <ptr target="#la8860" type="alt" xml:id="te0285"/>
any, and after that he polished off with a kind of a general cuss all round, including a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0286"/>
considerable

          <ptr target="#la8861" type="alt" xml:id="te0286"/>
parcel of people which he didn’t know the names of, and so called them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0463"/>
What’s-his-name

          <app from="pr0463" n="31.37 (101.18–19)" type="hc" xml:id="la1777">
            <lem wit="MS1a">What’s-his-name</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">what’s-his-name</rdg>
          </app>
, when he got to them, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0287"/>
went

          <ptr target="#la8862" type="alt" xml:id="te0287"/>
right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0288"/>
along

          <ptr target="#la8863" type="alt" xml:id="te0288"/>
with his cussing.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8748">
          <pb n="32" xml:id="pb0032"/>
He said

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0289"/>
he would like

          <ptr target="#la8864" type="alt" xml:id="te0289"/>
to see the widow get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0290"/>
me. He said he would

          <ptr target="#la8865" type="alt" xml:id="te0290"/>
watch out, and if they tried to come any such game on him he knowed of a place six or seven

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0464"/>
mile

          <app from="pr0464" n="32.3 (102.7)" type="e" xml:id="la1779">
            <lem wit="A">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">miles</rdg>
          </app>
off, to stow me in, where

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0291"/>
they

          <ptr target="#la8866" type="alt" xml:id="te0291"/>
might hunt till they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0292"/>
dropped

          <ptr target="#la8867" type="alt" xml:id="te0292"/>
and they couldn’t find me. That

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0293"/>
made me pretty uneasy again,

          <ptr target="#la8868" type="alt" xml:id="te0293"/>
but only for a minute; I reckoned I wouldn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0294"/>
stay

          <ptr target="#la8869" type="alt" xml:id="te0294"/>
on hand till he got that chance.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8786">
The old man made me go to the skiff and fetch the things he had got. There was a fifty-pound sack

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0003"/>
of corn meal, and a side of bacon,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0295"/>
ammunition, and

          <ptr target="#la8870" type="alt" xml:id="te0295"/>
a four-gallon jug of whisky, and an old book and two newspapers for wadding, besides some tow. I toted up a load, and went back and set down on the bow of the skiff to rest. I thought it all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0465"/>
over

          <app from="pr0465" n="32.12 (103.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1781">
            <lem wit="MS1a">over</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">over,</rdg>
          </app>
and I reckoned I would walk off with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0296"/>
the gun

          <ptr target="#la8871" type="alt" xml:id="te0296"/>
and some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0466"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0017"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0297"/>
fishing

          <ptr target="#la8872" type="alt" xml:id="te0297"/>
lines

          <app from="pr0466" n="✱32.13 (103.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la1783">
            <lem wit="MS1a">fishing lines</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lines</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0017" type="te" xml:id="tv0017"/>
, and take to the woods when I run away. I guessed I wouldn’t stay in one place, but just tramp right across the country, mostly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0467"/>
night-times

          <app from="pr0467" n="32.15 (103.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la1785">
            <lem wit="C">night-times</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
night-

              <lb/>
times

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">night times</rdg>
          </app>
, and hunt and fish to

          <ptr target="#mt0003" type="alt" xml:id="wn0003"/>
keep alive, and so get so far away that the old man nor the widow couldn’t ever find me any more. I judged I would saw

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0298"/>
out and

          <ptr target="#la8873" type="alt" xml:id="te0298"/>
leave that night if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0468"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0468" n="32.17 (104.7)" type="e" xml:id="la1787">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
got drunk enough, and I reckoned he would. I got so full of it I didn’t notice

          <pb n="33" xml:id="pb0033"/>
how long I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0469"/>
staying

          <app from="pr0469" n="33.1 (104.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1789">
            <lem wit="MS1a">staying</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">staying,</rdg>
          </app>
till the old man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0299"/>
hollered

          <ptr target="#la8874z" type="alt" xml:id="te0299"/>
and asked me

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0300"/>
whether

          <ptr target="#la8875" type="alt" xml:id="te0300"/>
I was asleep or drownded.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y03201">
          <graphic url="y03201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">thinking it over</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8872">
I got the things all up to the cabin, and then it was about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0470"/>
dark. While

          <app from="pr0470" n="33.3–4 (104.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la1791">
            <lem wit="A">dark. While</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
dark.—

              <lb/>
While

            </rdg>
          </app>
I was cooking supper the old

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0301"/>
man

          <ptr target="#la8876" type="alt" xml:id="te0301"/>
took a swig or two and got sort of warmed up, and went to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0302"/>
ripping

          <ptr target="#la8877" type="alt" xml:id="te0302"/>
again. He had been drunk over in town, and laid in the gutter all night, and he was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0303"/>
a

          <ptr target="#la8878" type="alt" xml:id="te0303"/>
sight to look at. A body would a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0001"/>
thought

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0281"/>
he

          <ptr target="#la8856" type="alt" xml:id="te0281"/>
was Adam, he was just all mud

          <ptr target="#as0052" type="an" xml:id="sa0001"/>
          <ptr target="#la8879" type="alt" xml:id="te0304"/>
. Whenever his liquor begun to work,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0002"/>
he most always went for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0471"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0018"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0305"/>
govment

          <ptr target="#la8880" type="alt" xml:id="te0305"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0018" type="te" xml:id="tv0018"/>
          <ptr target="#as0053" type="an" xml:id="sa0002"/>
. This

          <app from="pr0471" n="✱33.9 (105.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la1793">
            <lem wit="A">govment. This</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
govment.—

              <lb/>
This

            </rdg>
          </app>
time he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e8926">
“Call

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0472"/>
this

          <app from="pr0472" n="33.10 (105.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1795">
            <lem wit="A">this</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0473"/>
govment

          <app from="pr0473" n="33.10 (105.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1797">
            <lem wit="A">govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0474"/>
Why

          <app from="pr0474" n="33.10 (105.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la1799">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">why</rdg>
          </app>
, just look at it and see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0306"/>
what

          <ptr target="#la8881" type="alt" xml:id="te0306"/>
it’s like. Here’s the law a-standing ready to take a man’s son away from him—a man’s own son, which he has had all the trouble and all the anxiety and all the expense of raising. Yes, just as that man has got that son raised at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0307"/>
last,

          <ptr target="#la8882" type="alt" xml:id="te0307"/>
and ready to go to work and begin to do suthin’ for

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
and give him a rest, the law up and goes for him. And they call

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0475"/>
govment!

          <app from="pr0475" n="33.16 (106.10)" type="e" xml:id="la1801">
            <lem wit="A">govment!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment.</rdg>
          </app>
That ain’t all,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0476"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0308"/>
nuther

          <ptr target="#la8883" type="alt" xml:id="te0308"/>
          <app from="pr0476" n="33.16 (106.11)" type="e" xml:id="la1803">
            <lem wit="A">nuther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
neither/

              <add>nuther</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. The law backs that old Judge Thatcher up and helps him to keep me out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0477"/>
o’

          <app from="pr0477" n="33.17 (106.14)" type="e" xml:id="la1805">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
my property. Here’s what the law does. The law takes a man worth six thousand dollars and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0478"/>
up’ards

          <app from="pr0478" n="33.19 (106.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la1807">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up’ards</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">upards</rdg>
          </app>
, and jams him into an old trap of a cabin like this, and lets him go round in clothes that ain’t fitten for a hog. They call that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0479"/>
govment!

          <app from="pr0479" n="33.21 (107.1)" type="e" xml:id="la1809">
            <lem wit="A">govment!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment.</rdg>
          </app>
A man can’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0480"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0309"/>
git

          <ptr target="#la8884" type="alt" xml:id="te0309"/>
          <app from="pr0480" n="33.21 (107.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1811">
            <lem wit="MS1a">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">get</rdg>
          </app>
his rights in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0481"/>
a govment

          <app from="pr0481" n="33.21 (107.3)" type="e" xml:id="la1813">
            <lem wit="A">a govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
like this. Sometimes I’ve a mighty notion to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0310"/>
just

          <ptr target="#la8885" type="alt" xml:id="te0310"/>
leave the country for good and all. Yes, and I

          <hi rend="italic">told</hi>
’em so; I told old

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0311"/>
Thatcher

          <ptr target="#la8886" type="alt" xml:id="te0311"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0482"/>
so

          <app from="pr0482" n="33.23 (107.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1815">
            <lem wit="MS1a">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, to his face. Lots of ’em heard me, and can

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0312"/>
tell

          <ptr target="#la8887" type="alt" xml:id="te0312"/>
what I said. Says I, for two cents I’d leave the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0483"/>
blamed

          <app from="pr0483" n="33.25 (107.14)" type="e" xml:id="la1817">
            <lem wit="A">blamed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">blame</rdg>
          </app>
country and never come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0484"/>
a-near

          <app from="pr0484" n="33.25 (107.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la1819">
            <lem wit="MS1a">a-near</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">anear</rdg>
          </app>
it agin. Them’s the very words. I says, look at my hat—if you call it a hat—but the lid raises up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0485"/>
the rest of

          <app from="pr0485" n="33.27 (107.19)" type="e" xml:id="la1821">
            <lem wit="A">the rest of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1823">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
it goes down till it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0486"/>
below

          <app from="pr0486" n="33.27 (107.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la1824">
            <lem wit="A">below</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">under</rdg>
          </app>
my chin, and then it ain’t rightly a hat at all, but more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0487"/>
like my head was shoved up through

          <app from="pr0487" n="33.28–29 (108.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la1826">
            <lem wit="A">like . . . through</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a cravat, or</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0488"/>
j’int

          <app from="pr0488" n="33.29 (108.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1828">
            <lem wit="MS1a">j’int</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jint</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0489"/>
o’

          <app from="pr0489" n="33.29 (108.2)" type="e" xml:id="la1830">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0490"/>
stove pipe

          <app from="pr0490" n="33.29 (108.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1832">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stove pipe</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stove-pipe</rdg>
          </app>
. Look at it, says I—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0491"/>
such

          <app from="pr0491" n="33.29 (108.3)" type="e" xml:id="la1834">
            <lem wit="A">such</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sich</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0492"/>
hat

          <app from="pr0492" n="33.29 (108.4)" type="e" xml:id="la1836">
            <lem wit="A">hat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hat as that</rdg>
          </app>
for me to wear—one of the wealthiest men in this town, if I could git my rights.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9138">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0493"/>
“O

          <app from="pr0493" n="33.32 (108.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la1838">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes, this is a wonderful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0494"/>
govment

          <app from="pr0494" n="33.32 (108.9)" type="e" xml:id="la1840">
            <lem wit="A">govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
, wonderful.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0495"/>
Why

          <app from="pr0495" n="33.32 (108.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la1842">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0496"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr0496" n="33.32–33 (108.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la1844">
            <lem wit="MS1a">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
. There was a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0003"/>
free nigger there, from Ohio;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0313"/>
a mulatter, most as white as a white man.

          <ptr target="#la8888" type="alt" xml:id="te0313"/>
He had the whitest shirt on you ever see,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0314"/>
too,

          <ptr target="#la8889" type="alt" xml:id="te0314"/>
and the shiniest hat; and there ain’t a man in that town that’s got as fine clothes as what he had; and he had a gold watch and chain, and a silver-headed cane—the awfulest old gray-headed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0497"/>
nabob

          <app from="pr0497" n="33.37 (108.21)" type="e" xml:id="la1846">
            <lem wit="A">nabob</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">swell</rdg>
          </app>
in the State. And what do you think? they said he was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0315"/>
p’fessor

          <ptr target="#la8890" type="alt" xml:id="te0315"/>
in a

          <pb n="34" xml:id="pb0034"/>
college, and could talk all kinds of languages

          <ptr target="#as0054" type="an" xml:id="si0003"/>
, and knowed everything. And that ain’t the wust. They said

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0004"/>
he could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0498"/>
          <hi rend="italic">vote</hi>
          <app from="pr0498" n="34.2 (109.7)" type="e" xml:id="la1848">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">vote</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">vote</rdg>
          </app>
, when he was at home

          <ptr target="#as0055" type="an" xml:id="sa0004"/>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0499"/>
Well

          <app from="pr0499" n="34.3 (109.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la1850">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
that let

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0500"/>
me

          <app from="pr0500" n="34.3 (109.9)" type="e" xml:id="la1852">
            <lem wit="A">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
out. Thinks I, what is the country a-coming to? It was ’lection day, and I was just about to go and vote, myself, if I warn’t too drunk to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0501"/>
git

          <app from="pr0501" n="34.5 (109.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la1854">
            <lem wit="MS1a">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">get</rdg>
          </app>
there; but when they told me there was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0502"/>
state

          <app from="pr0502" n="34.6 (109.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la1856">
            <lem wit="MS1a">state</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">State</rdg>
          </app>
in this country where they’d let that nigger vote, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0316"/>
drawed

          <ptr target="#la8891" type="alt" xml:id="te0316"/>
out. I says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0503"/>
I’ll

          <app from="pr0503" n="34.7 (109.20)" type="e" xml:id="la1858">
            <lem wit="A">I’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’ll

            </rdg>
          </app>
never vote agin. Them’s the very words I said; they all heard me; and the country may

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0504"/>
rot,

          <app from="pr0504" n="34.8 (110.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la1860">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rot,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rot

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for all me—I’ll never vote agin as long as I live. And to see the cool way of that nigger—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0505"/>
why

          <app from="pr0505" n="34.10 (110.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la1862">
            <lem wit="MS1a">why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">why,</rdg>
          </app>
he wouldn’t a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0506"/>
give

          <app from="pr0506" n="34.10 (110.6)" type="e" xml:id="la1864">
            <lem wit="A">give</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">given</rdg>
          </app>
me the road if I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0507"/>
hadn’t

          <app from="pr0507" n="34.10 (110.7)" type="e" xml:id="la1866">
            <lem wit="A">hadn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">had n’t</rdg>
          </app>
shoved him out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0508"/>
o’

          <app from="pr0508" n="34.10 (110.8)" type="e" xml:id="la1868">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
the way. I says to the people, why ain’t this nigger put up at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0509"/>
auction

          <app from="pr0509" n="34.11 (110.11)" type="e" xml:id="la1870">
            <lem wit="A">auction</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">oction</rdg>
          </app>
and sold?—that’s what

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0510"/>
I

          <app from="pr0510" n="34.12 (110.12)" type="e" xml:id="la1872">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
want to know. And what do you reckon they said?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0511"/>
Why

          <app from="pr0511" n="34.13 (110.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la1874">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
they said

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0005"/>
he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0512"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr0512" n="34.13 (110.15)" type="e" xml:id="la1876">
            <lem wit="A">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
be sold till he’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0513"/>
been

          <app from="pr0513" n="34.13 (110.16)" type="e" xml:id="la1878">
            <lem wit="A">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ben</rdg>
          </app>
in the State six months

          <ptr target="#as0056" type="an" xml:id="sa0005"/>
, and he hadn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0514"/>
been

          <app from="pr0514" n="34.14 (110.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1880">
            <lem wit="A">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ben</rdg>
          </app>
there that long yet. There, now—that’s a specimen. They call

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0515"/>
that a govment

          <app from="pr0515" n="34.15 (110.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la1882">
            <lem wit="A">that a govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
gov’ment!—

              <lb/>
Here’s a gov’ment

            </rdg>
          </app>
that can’t sell a free nigger till he’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0516"/>
been

          <app from="pr0516" n="34.16 (111.1)" type="e" xml:id="la1884">
            <lem wit="A">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ben</rdg>
          </app>
in the State six months. Here’s a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0517"/>
govment

          <app from="pr0517" n="34.16 (111.3)" type="e" xml:id="la1886">
            <lem wit="A">govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
that calls

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0518"/>
itself a govment

          <app from="pr0518" n="34.17 (111.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la1888">
            <lem wit="A">itself a govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">itself a gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
, and lets on to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0519"/>
be a govment

          <app from="pr0519" n="34.17 (111.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la1890">
            <lem wit="A">be a govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">be a gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
, and thinks it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0520"/>
is

          <app from="pr0520" n="34.18 (111.5)" type="e" xml:id="la1892">
            <lem wit="A">is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0521"/>
govment

          <app from="pr0521" n="34.18 (111.6)" type="e" xml:id="la1894">
            <lem wit="A">govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
, and yet’s got to set

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0522"/>
stock still

          <app from="pr0522" n="34.18 (111.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1896">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stock still</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stock-still</rdg>
          </app>
for six whole months before it can take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0523"/>
a-hold

          <app from="pr0523" n="34.19 (111.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1898">
            <lem wit="MS1a">a-hold</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ahold</rdg>
          </app>
of a prowling, thieving,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0524"/>
infernal

          <app from="pr0524" n="34.19 (111.10)" type="e" xml:id="la1900">
            <lem wit="A">infernal,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1902">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, white-shirted free

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0525"/>
nigger

          <app from="pr0525" n="34.20 (111.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la1903">
            <lem wit="MS1a">nigger</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">nigger,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0526"/>
and—

          <app from="pr0526" n="34.20 (111.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la1905">
            <lem wit="MS1a">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9465">
Pap was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0527"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr0527" n="34.21 (111.12)" type="e" xml:id="la1907">
            <lem wit="A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
on so, he never noticed where his old limber legs was taking him to, so he went head over heels over the tub of salt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0528"/>
pork

          <app from="pr0528" n="34.23 (111.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la1909">
            <lem wit="MS1a">pork</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pork,</rdg>
          </app>
and barked both shins, and the rest of his speech was all the hottest kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0317"/>
language

          <ptr target="#la8892" type="alt" xml:id="te0317"/>
—mostly hove at the nigger and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0529"/>
govment

          <app from="pr0529" n="34.24–25 (111.22)" type="e" xml:id="la1911">
            <lem wit="A">govment</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gov’ment</rdg>
          </app>
, though he give the tub

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0318"/>
some,

          <ptr target="#la8893" type="alt" xml:id="te0318"/>
too, all along, here and there. He hopped around the cabin

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0319"/>
considerable

          <ptr target="#la8894" type="alt" xml:id="te0319"/>
, first on one leg and then on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0320"/>
the other,

          <ptr target="#la8895" type="alt" xml:id="te0320"/>
holding first one shin and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0321"/>
then the other

          <ptr target="#la8896" type="alt" xml:id="te0321"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0322"/>
one,

          <ptr target="#la8897" type="alt" xml:id="te0322"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0323"/>
and

          <ptr target="#la8898" type="alt" xml:id="te0323"/>
at last he let out with his left foot all of a sudden and fetched the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0324"/>
tub

          <ptr target="#la8899" type="alt" xml:id="te0324"/>
a rattling

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0325"/>
kick.

          <ptr target="#la8900" type="alt" xml:id="te0325"/>
But it warn’t good judgment, because that was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0326"/>
the

          <ptr target="#la8901" type="alt" xml:id="te0326"/>
boot that had a couple of his toes

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0327"/>
leaking

          <ptr target="#la8902" type="alt" xml:id="te0327"/>
out of the front end of it; so now he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0328"/>
raised

          <ptr target="#la8903" type="alt" xml:id="te0328"/>
a howl that fairly made a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0530"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0329"/>
body’s hair raise

          <app from="pr0530" n="34.31 (112.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la1913">
            <lem wit="A">body’s hair raise</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">body shiver</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#la8904" type="alt" xml:id="te0329"/>
and down he went in the dirt, and rolled there, and held his toes; and the cussing he done then laid over anything

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0330"/>
he had

          <ptr target="#la8905" type="alt" xml:id="te0330"/>
ever done previous. He

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0331"/>
said

          <ptr target="#la8906" type="alt" xml:id="te0331"/>
so his own self, afterwards. He had heard old Sowberry Hagan in his best days, and he said it laid over him, too; but I reckon that was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0332"/>
sort

          <ptr target="#la8907" type="alt" xml:id="te0332"/>
of piling it on, maybe.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y03501">
          <graphic url="y03501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">raising a howl</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9571">
After supper

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0531"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0531" n="34.37 (113.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1915">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0532"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0333"/>
took

          <ptr target="#la8908" type="alt" xml:id="te0333"/>
          <app from="pr0532" n="34.37 (113.13)" type="e" xml:id="la1917">
            <lem wit="A">took</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">took to</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0533"/>
jug

          <app from="pr0533" n="34.37 (113.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la1919">
            <lem wit="MS1a">jug</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jug,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0334"/>
said

          <ptr target="#la8909" type="alt" xml:id="te0334"/>
he had enough whisky there for two drunks and one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0534"/>
delirium

          <app from="pr0534" n="34.38 (113.16)" type="e" xml:id="la1921">
            <lem wit="A">delirium</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">delirrum</rdg>
          </app>
tremens.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0335"/>
That was always

          <pb n="35" xml:id="pb0035"/>
his word.

          <ptr target="#la8910" type="alt" xml:id="te0335"/>
I judged he would be blind drunk in about an hour, and then I would steal

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0336"/>
the

          <ptr target="#la8911" type="alt" xml:id="te0336"/>
key, or saw myself out, one or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0535"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr0535" n="35.2 (114.1)" type="e" xml:id="la1923">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0536"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0337"/>
drank and drank

          <app from="pr0536" n="35.3 (114.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1925">
            <lem wit="MS1a">drank and drank</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">drank, and drank</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#la8912" type="alt" xml:id="te0337"/>
and tumbled

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0338"/>
down

          <ptr target="#la8913" type="alt" xml:id="te0338"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0339"/>
on

          <ptr target="#la8914" type="alt" xml:id="te0339"/>
his blankets,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0537"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0537" n="35.3 (114.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la1927">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
; but luck didn’t run my way. He didn’t go sound asleep, but was uneasy. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0538"/>
groaned

          <app from="pr0538" n="35.5 (114.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1929">
            <lem wit="MS1a">groaned</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">groaned,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0539"/>
moaned

          <app from="pr0539" n="35.5 (114.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1931">
            <lem wit="MS1a">moaned</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">moaned,</rdg>
          </app>
and thrashed around this way and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0540"/>
that

          <app from="pr0540" n="35.5 (114.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la1933">
            <lem wit="MS1a">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">that,</rdg>
          </app>
for a long time. At last I got so sleepy I couldn’t keep my eyes open, all I could do, and so before I knowed what I was about I was sound asleep, and the candle

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0340"/>
burning

          <ptr target="#la8915" type="alt" xml:id="te0340"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9687">
I don’t know how long I was asleep, but all of a sudden there was an awful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0541"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0341"/>
scream,

          <app from="pr0541" n="35.10 (114.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la1935">
            <lem wit="MS1a">scream,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
scream

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#la8916" type="alt" xml:id="te0341"/>
and I was up. There was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0006"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0542"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0542" n="35.10 (114.21)" type="e" xml:id="la1937">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
, looking wild and skipping around

          <ptr target="#as0057" type="an" xml:id="sa0006"/>
every which way and yelling about snakes. He said they was crawling up his legs; and then he would give a jump and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0543"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0342"/>
scream

          <app from="pr0543" n="35.13 (115.6)" type="e" xml:id="la1939">
            <lem wit="A">scream</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a scream</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#la8917" type="alt" xml:id="te0342"/>
and say one had bit him on the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0343"/>
cheek—

          <ptr target="#la8918" type="alt" xml:id="te0343"/>
but I couldn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0544"/>
no

          <app from="pr0544" n="35.14 (115.9)" type="e" xml:id="la1941">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
snakes. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0545"/>
started,

          <app from="pr0545" n="35.14 (115.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la1943">
            <lem wit="MS1a">started,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
started

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and run round and round the cabin,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0344"/>
hollering

          <ptr target="#la8919" type="alt" xml:id="te0344"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0546"/>
Take

          <app from="pr0546" n="35.15 (115.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la1945">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Take</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">take</rdg>
          </app>
him off! take him off! he’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0345"/>
biting

          <ptr target="#la8920" type="alt" xml:id="te0345"/>
me on the neck!” I never see a man look so wild in the eyes. Pretty soon he was all fagged

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0547"/>
out

          <app from="pr0547" n="35.16 (115.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la1947">
            <lem wit="MS1a">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">out,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0346"/>
fell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0548"/>
down,

          <app from="pr0548" n="35.17 (115.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la1949">
            <lem wit="MS1a">down,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
down

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
panting

          <ptr target="#la8921" type="alt" xml:id="te0346"/>
;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0347"/>
then

          <ptr target="#la8922" type="alt" xml:id="te0347"/>
he rolled over and over, wonderful fast,

          <pb n="36" xml:id="pb0036"/>
kicking things every which way, and striking and grabbing at the air with his hands, and screaming, and saying there was devils

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0348"/>
ahold

          <ptr target="#la8923" type="alt" xml:id="te0348"/>
of him. He wore out,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0549"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0549" n="36.3 (116.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la1951">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, and laid still a while, moaning. Then he laid

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0349"/>
stiller,

          <ptr target="#la8924" type="alt" xml:id="te0349"/>
and didn’t make a sound. I could hear the owls and the wolves, away

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0350"/>
off

          <ptr target="#la8925" type="alt" xml:id="te0350"/>
in the woods, and it seemed terrible still. He was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0351"/>
laying

          <ptr target="#la8926" type="alt" xml:id="te0351"/>
over by the corner.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0550"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0550" n="36.6 (116.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la1953">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he raised up, part way, and listened, with his head to one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0352"/>
side

          <ptr target="#la8927" type="alt" xml:id="te0352"/>
. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0551"/>
says,

          <app from="pr0551" n="36.7 (116.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la1955">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
says

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
very

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0552"/>
low:

          <app from="pr0552" n="36.7 (116.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1957">
            <lem wit="A">low:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">low,</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9842">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0007"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0353"/>
“Tramp

          <ptr target="#la8928" type="alt" xml:id="te0353"/>
—tramp—tramp; that’s the dead

          <ptr target="#as0058" type="an" xml:id="sa0007"/>
; tramp—tramp—tramp; they’re

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0553"/>
coming

          <app from="pr0553" n="36.9 (116.20)" type="e" xml:id="la1959">
            <lem wit="A">coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a coming</rdg>
          </app>
after me; but I won’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0554"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0354"/>
go—

          <app from="pr0554" n="36.9 (116.21)" type="e" xml:id="la1961">
            <lem wit="A">go—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">go; . . . . . . . .</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0555"/>
O

          <app from="pr0555" n="36.9 (116.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la1963">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#la8929" type="alt" xml:id="te0354"/>
they’re here! don’t touch me—don’t! hands off—they’re cold; let go—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0556"/>
O

          <app from="pr0556" n="36.10 (117.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la1965">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, let a poor devil

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0557"/>
alone!

          <app from="pr0557" n="36.11 (117.3)" type="e" xml:id="la1967">
            <lem wit="A">alone!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">alone.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9894">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0355"/>
Then

          <ptr target="#la8930" type="alt" xml:id="te0355"/>
he went down on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0356"/>
all

          <ptr target="#la8931" type="alt" xml:id="te0356"/>
fours and crawled off begging them to let him alone, and he rolled himself up in his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0558"/>
blanket

          <app from="pr0558" n="36.13 (117.8)" type="e" xml:id="la1969">
            <lem wit="A">blanket</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">blankets</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0559"/>
wallowed

          <app from="pr0559" n="36.13 (117.9)" type="e" xml:id="la1971">
            <lem wit="A">wallowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">rolled</rdg>
          </app>
in under the old pine table, still

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0560"/>
a begging

          <app from="pr0560" n="36.14 (117.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la1973">
            <lem wit="MS1a">a begging</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a-begging</rdg>
          </app>
; and then he went to crying. I could hear him through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0561"/>
blanket

          <app from="pr0561" n="36.15 (117.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la1975">
            <lem wit="A">blanket</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">blankets</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e9937">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0562"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0562" n="36.16 (117.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la1977">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he rolled out and jumped up on his feet looking wild, and he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0563"/>
see

          <app from="pr0563" n="36.17 (117.17)" type="e" xml:id="la1979">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
me and went for me. He chased me round and round the place, with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0564"/>
clasp-knife

          <app from="pr0564" n="36.18 (117.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la1981">
            <lem wit="A">clasp-knife</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
butcher-

              <lb/>
knife

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0357"/>
calling

          <ptr target="#la8932" type="alt" xml:id="te0357"/>
me the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0565"/>
angel of death

          <app from="pr0565" n="36.18 (117.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la1983">
            <lem wit="MS1a">angel of death</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Angel of Death</rdg>
          </app>
and saying he would kill me and then I couldn’t come for him no more. I begged, and told him I was only Huck, but he laughed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0566"/>
          <hi rend="italic">such</hi>
          <app from="pr0566" n="36.20 (118.6)" type="e" xml:id="la1985">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">such</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">such</rdg>
          </app>
a screechy laugh, and roared and cussed, and kept on chasing me up. Once when I turned short and dodged under his arm he made a grab and got me by the jacket between my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0567"/>
shoulders

          <app from="pr0567" n="36.23 (118.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la1987">
            <lem wit="MS1a">shoulders</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shoulders,</rdg>
          </app>
and I thought I was gone; but I slid out of the jacket quick as lightning, and saved myself. Pretty soon he was all tired

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0568"/>
out

          <app from="pr0568" n="36.25 (118.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la1989">
            <lem wit="MS1a">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">out,</rdg>
          </app>
and dropped down with his back against the door, and said he would rest a minute and then kill me. He put his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0569"/>
knife

          <app from="pr0569" n="36.27 (119.2)" type="e" xml:id="la1991">
            <lem wit="A">knife</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">butcher knife</rdg>
          </app>
under him, and said he would sleep and get strong, and then he would see who was who.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10012">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0358"/>
So

          <ptr target="#la8933" type="alt" xml:id="te0358"/>
he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0359"/>
dozed

          <ptr target="#la8934" type="alt" xml:id="te0359"/>
off, pretty soon.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0570"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0570" n="36.29 (119.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la1993">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I got the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0571"/>
split-bottom

          <app from="pr0571" n="36.29 (119.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la1995">
            <lem wit="A">split-bottom</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
split-

              <lb/>
bottom

            </rdg>
          </app>
chair and clumb up, as easy as I could, not to make any noise, and got down

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0360"/>
the gun

          <ptr target="#la8935" type="alt" xml:id="te0360"/>
. I slipped the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0572"/>
ramrod

          <app from="pr0572" n="36.31 (119.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la1997">
            <lem wit="A">ramrod</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
ram-

              <lb/>
rod

            </rdg>
          </app>
down it to make sure it was loaded, and then I laid it across the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0361"/>
turnip barrel,

          <ptr target="#la8936" type="alt" xml:id="te0361"/>
pointing towards pap, and set down behind it to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0362"/>
wait

          <ptr target="#la8937" type="alt" xml:id="te0362"/>
for him to stir. And

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0363"/>
how

          <ptr target="#la8938" type="alt" xml:id="te0363"/>
slow and still the time did drag along.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0266">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter VII.</head>
        <pb n="37" xml:id="pb0037"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10071">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y03701">
            <graphic url="y03701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0573"/>
Chapter VII.

              <app from="pr0573" n="37 title (120 title)" type="e" xml:id="la1999">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter VII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">CHAP. 8.</rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0019"/>
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0574"/>
Git

              <app from="pr0574" n="✱37.1 (120.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2001">
                <lem wit="A">Git</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
“

                  <hi rend="italic">Git</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <ptr target="#tb0019" type="te" xml:id="tv0019"/>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3701">
            <graphic url="hf3701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">
git

                <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0579"/>
up!

              </hi>
              <app from="pr0579" n="37 caption" type="e" xml:id="la2011">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">up</hi>
!

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="lyz013">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">up</hi>
.

                </rdg>
              </app>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e10113">
up!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0575"/>
What

          <app from="pr0575" n="37.1 (120.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2003">
            <lem wit="MS1a">What</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">what</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0364"/>
’bout!”

          <ptr target="#la8939" type="alt" xml:id="te0364"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10126">
I opened my eyes and looked around, trying to make out where I was. It was after sun-up, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0365"/>
I had

          <ptr target="#la8940" type="alt" xml:id="te0365"/>
been sound

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0576"/>
asleep. Pap

          <app from="pr0576" n="37.5 (120.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la2005">
            <lem wit="A">asleep. Pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
asleep.—

              <lb/>
Pap

            </rdg>
          </app>
was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0366"/>
standing

          <ptr target="#la8941" type="alt" xml:id="te0366"/>
over me, looking sour—and sick, too. He says—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10147">
“What you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0577"/>
doin’

          <app from="pr0577" n="37.8 (120.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2007">
            <lem wit="A">doin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">doing</rdg>
          </app>
with this gun?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10157">
I judged he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0578"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr0578" n="37.10 (120.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2009">
            <lem wit="A">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
know nothing

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0367"/>
about

          <ptr target="#la8942" type="alt" xml:id="te0367"/>
what

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0368"/>
he had

          <ptr target="#la8943" type="alt" xml:id="te0368"/>
been doing, so I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10176">
“Somebody tried to get in, so I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0369"/>
laying

          <ptr target="#la8944" type="alt" xml:id="te0369"/>
for him.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10182">“Why didn’t you roust me out?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10184">“Well I tried to, but I couldn’t; I couldn’t budge you.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10186">
“Well, all right. Don’t stand there palavering all day, but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0370"/>
out with you and

          <ptr target="#la8945" type="alt" xml:id="te0370"/>
see if there’s a fish on the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0371"/>
lines

          <ptr target="#la8946" type="alt" xml:id="te0371"/>
for breakfast. I’ll be along in a minute.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10197">
He unlocked the door and I cleared out, up the river bank. I noticed some pieces of limbs and such things floating down, and a sprinkling of bark; so I knowed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0372"/>
the river

          <ptr target="#la8947" type="alt" xml:id="te0372"/>
had begun to rise. I reckoned I would have great times, now, if I was over at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0580"/>
town

          <app from="pr0580" n="37.24 (122.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2014">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
. The

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0008"/>
June rise

          <ptr target="#as0059" type="an" xml:id="sa0008"/>
used to be always luck for me; because as soon as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0373"/>
that

          <ptr target="#la8948" type="alt" xml:id="te0373"/>
rise begins, here comes cord-wood floating down, and pieces of log rafts—sometimes a dozen logs

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0581"/>
together; so

          <app from="pr0581" n="37.27 (122.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la2016">
            <lem wit="A">together; so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">together. So</rdg>
          </app>
all you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0374"/>
have

          <ptr target="#la8949" type="alt" xml:id="te0374"/>
to do is to catch them and sell them to the wood yards and the sawmill.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10233">
I went along up the bank with one eye out for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0582"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0582" n="37.29 (123.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2018">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0583"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr0583" n="37.29 (123.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2020">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
one out for what the rise might fetch along.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0584"/>
Well

          <app from="pr0584" n="37.30 (123.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2022">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
all at once, here comes a canoe; just a beauty, too, about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0375"/>
thirteen or fourteen

          <ptr target="#la8950" type="alt" xml:id="te0375"/>
foot long, riding high like a duck. I shot head first off of the bank, like a frog, clothes and all on, and struck out for the canoe. I just

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0376"/>
expected

          <ptr target="#la8951" type="alt" xml:id="te0376"/>
          <pb n="38" xml:id="pb0038"/>
there’d be somebody laying down in it, because people often done that to fool folks, and when a chap had pulled a skiff out most to it they’d raise up and laugh at him. But it warn’t so this time. It was a drift-canoe, sure enough, and I clumb in and paddled her ashore. Thinks I, the old man will be

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0377"/>
glad

          <ptr target="#la8952" type="alt" xml:id="te0377"/>
when he sees this—she’s worth

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0585"/>
ten

          <app from="pr0585" n="38.6 (124.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2024">
            <lem wit="A">ten</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">twenty</rdg>
          </app>
dollars. But when I got to shore

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0586"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0586" n="38.6 (124.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2026">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
wasn’t in sight yet, and as I was running her into a little creek like a gully, all hung over with vines

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0378"/>
and willows,

          <ptr target="#la8953" type="alt" xml:id="te0378"/>
I struck another idea; I judged I’d hide her good, and then,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0587"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0379"/>
’stead

          <ptr target="#la8954" type="alt" xml:id="te0379"/>
          <app from="pr0587" n="38.9 (124.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2028">
            <lem wit="MS1a">’stead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stead</rdg>
          </app>
of taking to the woods when I run off, I’d go down the river about fifty mile and camp in one place for good, and not have such a rough time tramping on foot.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10305">
It was pretty close to the shanty, and I thought I heard the old man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0588"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0380"/>
coming

          <ptr target="#la8955" type="alt" xml:id="te0380"/>
          <app from="pr0588" n="38.13 (125.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2030">
            <lem wit="MS1a">coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">coming,</rdg>
          </app>
all the time; but I got her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0589"/>
hid

          <app from="pr0589" n="38.13 (125.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2032">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hid</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hid;</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0590"/>
then I

          <app from="pr0590" n="38.13 (125.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2034">
            <lem wit="A">then I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">stepped</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0381"/>
out

          <ptr target="#la8956" type="alt" xml:id="te0381"/>
and looked around a bunch of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0591"/>
willows;

          <app from="pr0591" n="38.14 (125.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la2036">
            <lem wit="MS1a">willows;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">willows,</rdg>
          </app>
and there was the old man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0382"/>
down the path apiece

          <ptr target="#la8957" type="alt" xml:id="te0382"/>
just drawing a bead on a bird with his gun. So he hadn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0383"/>
seen anything.

          <ptr target="#la8958" type="alt" xml:id="te0383"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10353">
When he got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0592"/>
along

          <app from="pr0592" n="38.17 (125.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la2038">
            <lem wit="MS1a">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">along,</rdg>
          </app>
I was hard at it taking up a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0593"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0384"/>
trot-line

          <ptr target="#la8959" type="alt" xml:id="te0384"/>
          <app from="pr0593" n="38.17 (125.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2040">
            <lem wit="MS1a">trot-line</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“trot” line</rdg>
          </app>
. He

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0385"/>
abused

          <ptr target="#la8960" type="alt" xml:id="te0385"/>
me a little for being so slow, but I told him I fell in the river and that was what made me so long. I knowed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0386"/>
he would

          <ptr target="#la8961" type="alt" xml:id="te0386"/>
see I was wet, and then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0387"/>
he would

          <ptr target="#la8962" type="alt" xml:id="te0387"/>
be asking questions. We got five cat-fish off of the lines

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0004"/>
and went home.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10389">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y03801">
            <graphic url="y03801.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">the shanty</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10395">
          <pb n="39" xml:id="pb00039"/>
While we laid off, after

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0388"/>
breakfast,

          <ptr target="#la8963" type="alt" xml:id="te0388"/>
to sleep up, both of us being

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0389"/>
about

          <ptr target="#la8964" type="alt" xml:id="te0389"/>
wore out, I got to thinking that if I could fix up some way to keep

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0594"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0594" n="39.3 (126.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2042">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
and the widow from trying to follow me, it would be a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0390"/>
certainer

          <ptr target="#la8965" type="alt" xml:id="te0390"/>
thing than trusting to luck to get far enough off before they missed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0391"/>
me; you

          <ptr target="#la8966" type="alt" xml:id="te0391"/>
see, all kinds of things might happen. Well, I didn’t see no way for a while, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0595"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0392"/>
by and by

          <ptr target="#la8967" type="alt" xml:id="te0392"/>
          <app from="pr0595" n="39.6 (126.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2044">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0596"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0393"/>
pap

          <ptr target="#la8968" type="alt" xml:id="te0393"/>
          <app from="pr0596" n="39.6 (126.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2046">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
raised

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0597"/>
up,

          <app from="pr0597" n="39.6 (126.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2048">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a minute, to drink another barrel of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0394"/>
water,

          <ptr target="#la8969" type="alt" xml:id="te0394"/>
and he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10456">
“Another time a man comes a-prowling round

          <ptr target="#mt0004" type="alt" xml:id="wn0004"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0005"/>
here, you roust me out, you hear? That man warn’t here for no good. I’d a shot him. Next time, you roust me out, you hear?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10461">
Then he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0395"/>
dropped

          <ptr target="#la8970" type="alt" xml:id="te0395"/>
down and went to sleep again—but what

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0396"/>
he had

          <ptr target="#la8971" type="alt" xml:id="te0396"/>
been saying give me the very idea I wanted. I says to myself, I can fix it now so nobody won’t think of following me.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10471">
About twelve o’clock we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0397"/>
turned

          <ptr target="#la8972" type="alt" xml:id="te0397"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0398"/>
out and

          <ptr target="#la8973" type="alt" xml:id="te0398"/>
went along up the bank. The river was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0399"/>
coming

          <ptr target="#la8974" type="alt" xml:id="te0399"/>
up pretty fast, and lots of drift-wood going by on the rise.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0598"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0598" n="39.16 (127.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2050">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
By-and-

              <lb/>
by

            </rdg>
          </app>
, along

          <ptr target="#mt0005" type="alt" xml:id="wn0005"/>
comes part of a log raft—nine logs fast together. We

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0400"/>
went

          <ptr target="#la8975" type="alt" xml:id="te0400"/>
out with the skiff and towed it ashore. Then we had dinner. Anybody but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0599"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0599" n="39.18 (128.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2052">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
would a waited and seen the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0600"/>
day

          <app from="pr0600" n="39.18 (128.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2054">
            <lem wit="A">day</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">rise</rdg>
          </app>
through, so as to catch

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0601"/>
more

          <app from="pr0601" n="39.19 (128.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2056">
            <lem wit="A">more</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">some more</rdg>
          </app>
stuff; but that warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0602"/>
pap’s

          <app from="pr0602" n="39.19 (128.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2058">
            <lem wit="A">pap’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap’s</rdg>
          </app>
style. Nine logs was enough for one time; he must shove right over to town and sell. So he locked me in and took the skiff and started off towing the raft about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0603"/>
half past

          <app from="pr0603" n="39.22 (128.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2060">
            <lem wit="MS1a">half past</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half-past</rdg>
          </app>
three. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0401"/>
judged he

          <ptr target="#la8976" type="alt" xml:id="te0401"/>
wouldn’t come back that night.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0402"/>
I waited till I reckoned he had got a good start,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0604"/>
then

          <ptr target="#la8977" type="alt" xml:id="te0402"/>
          <app from="pr0604" n="39.23 (129.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2062">
            <lem wit="A">then</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and then</rdg>
          </app>
I out with my saw and went to work on that log again. Before he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0605"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr0605" n="39.24 (129.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2064">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
side of the river I was out of the hole; him and his raft was just a speck on the water away off yonder.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10567">
I took the sack of corn meal and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0606"/>
took it

          <app from="pr0606" n="39.27 (129.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2066">
            <lem wit="A">took it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">lugged it</rdg>
          </app>
to where the canoe

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0403"/>
was hid,

          <ptr target="#la8978" type="alt" xml:id="te0403"/>
and shoved the vines and branches apart and put it in;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0404"/>
then I done the same with the side of bacon; then the whisky jug;

          <ptr target="#la8979" type="alt" xml:id="te0404"/>
I took all the coffee and sugar there was, and all the ammunition; I took the wadding; I took the bucket and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0405"/>
gourd

          <ptr target="#la8980" type="alt" xml:id="te0405"/>
, I took a dipper and a tin cup,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0406"/>
and my old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0607"/>
saw,

          <app from="pr0607" n="39.32 (130.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2068">
            <lem wit="MS1a">saw,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
saw

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and two blankets,

          <ptr target="#la8981" type="alt" xml:id="te0406"/>
and the skillet and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0608"/>
coffee pot

          <app from="pr0608" n="39.32–33 (130.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la2070">
            <lem wit="MS1a">coffee pot</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">coffee-pot</rdg>
          </app>
. I took

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0609"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0407"/>
fish lines

          <app from="pr0609" n="39.33 (130.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2072">
            <lem wit="MS1a">fish lines</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fish-lines</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0009"/>
matches

          <ptr target="#as0060" type="an" xml:id="sa0009"/>
and

          <ptr target="#la8982" type="alt" xml:id="te0407"/>
other things—everything that was worth a cent. I cleaned out the place. I wanted an

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0610"/>
ax

          <app from="pr0610" n="39.34 (130.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2074">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ax</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">axe</rdg>
          </app>
, but there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0611"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0408"/>
wasn’t

          <app from="pr0611" n="39.35 (130.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2076">
            <lem wit="A">wasn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">warn’t</rdg>
          </app>
any,

          <ptr target="#la8983" type="alt" xml:id="te0408"/>
only the one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0409"/>
out

          <ptr target="#la8984" type="alt" xml:id="te0409"/>
at the wood pile, and I knowed why I was going to leave that. I fetched out the gun, and now I was done.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10651">
I had wore the ground a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0612"/>
deal

          <app from="pr0612" n="39.38 (130.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2078">
            <lem wit="MS1a">deal</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">deal,</rdg>
          </app>
crawling out of the hole and dragging out so many things. So I fixed that as good as I could from

          <pb n="40" xml:id="pb0040"/>
the outside by scattering dust on the place, which covered up the smoothness

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0006"/>
and the sawdust. Then I fixed the piece of log back into its

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0613"/>
place

          <app from="pr0613" n="40.3 (131.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2080">
            <lem wit="MS1a">place</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">place,</rdg>
          </app>
and put two rocks under it and one against it to hold it there,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0410"/>
—for it was bent

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0614"/>
up,

          <app from="pr0614" n="40.4 (131.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2082">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at that place, and didn’t quite touch ground.

          <ptr target="#la8985" type="alt" xml:id="te0410"/>
If you stood four or five foot away and didn’t know it was sawed, you wouldn’t ever notice it; and besides, this was the back of the cabin and it warn’t likely anybody would go fooling around there.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10687">
It was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0615"/>
grass,

          <app from="pr0615" n="40.9 (131.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2084">
            <lem wit="MS1a">grass,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
grass

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
clear to the canoe; so I hadn’t left a track. I followed around to see. I stood on the bank and looked out over the river. All safe. So I took the gun and went up a piece

          <ptr target="#mt0006" type="alt" xml:id="wn0006"/>
into the woods and was hunting around for some birds, when I see a wild pig; hogs soon went wild in them bottoms after

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0411"/>
they had

          <ptr target="#la8986" type="alt" xml:id="te0411"/>
got away from the prairie farms. I shot this fellow and took him into camp.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y04001">
          <graphic url="y04001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">shooting the pig</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10708">
I took the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0616"/>
ax

          <app from="pr0616" n="40.15 (132.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2086">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ax</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">axe</rdg>
          </app>
and smashed in the door—I beat it and hacked it considerable, a-doing it. I fetched the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0412"/>
pig

          <ptr target="#la8987" type="alt" xml:id="te0412"/>
in and took him back nearly to the table and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0413"/>
hacked

          <ptr target="#la8988" type="alt" xml:id="te0413"/>
into his throat with the ax, and laid him down on the ground to bleed—I say ground, because it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
ground—hard packed, and no boards. Well, next I took an old sack and put a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0414"/>
lot

          <ptr target="#la8989" type="alt" xml:id="te0414"/>
of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0415"/>
big

          <ptr target="#la8990" type="alt" xml:id="te0415"/>
rocks in it,—all I could drag—and I started it from the pig and dragged it to the door and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0416"/>
through the woods

          <ptr target="#la8991" type="alt" xml:id="te0416"/>
down

          <pb n="41" xml:id="pb0041"/>
to the river and dumped it in, and down it sunk, out of sight. You could easy see that something had been dragged over the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0617"/>
ground

          <app from="pr0617" n="41.2 (133.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2088">
            <lem wit="A">ground</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">floor</rdg>
          </app>
. I did wish Tom Sawyer was there, I knowed he would take an interest in this kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0417"/>
business

          <ptr target="#la8992" type="alt" xml:id="te0417"/>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0418"/>
and throw

          <ptr target="#la8993" type="alt" xml:id="te0418"/>
in the fancy touches. Nobody could spread himself like Tom Sawyer in such a thing as that.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10762">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0419"/>
Well

          <ptr target="#la8994" type="alt" xml:id="te0419"/>
, last I pulled out some of my hair, and bloodied the ax

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0618"/>
good

          <app from="pr0618" n="41.6 (133.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la2090">
            <lem wit="MS1a">good</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">good,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0007"/>
stuck it on the back side, and slung the ax in the corner. Then I took up the pig and held him to my breast with my jacket

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0420"/>
(so he couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0619"/>
drip,)

          <app from="pr0619" n="41.9 (134.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2092">
            <lem wit="MS1a">drip,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
drip

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
)

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#la8995" type="alt" xml:id="te0420"/>
till I got a good piece below the house and then dumped him into the river. Now I thought of something else. So I went and got the bag of meal and my old saw out of the canoe and fetched them to the house. I took the bag to where it used to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0620"/>
stand

          <app from="pr0620" n="41.12 (134.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2094">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stand</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stand,</rdg>
          </app>
and ripped a hole in the bottom of it with the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0621"/>
saw

          <app from="pr0621" n="41.13 (134.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2096">
            <lem wit="MS1a Ab">saw</lem>
            <rdg wit="Aa Can">was</rdg>
          </app>
, for there warn’t no knives and forks on the place—pap done everything with his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0421"/>
clasp-knife

          <ptr target="#la8996" type="alt" xml:id="te0421"/>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0422"/>
about

          <ptr target="#la8997" type="alt" xml:id="te0422"/>
the cooking. Then I carried the sack

          <ptr target="#mt0007" type="alt" xml:id="wn0007"/>
about a hundred yards across the grass and through the willows east of the house, to a shallow lake that was five mile wide and full of rushes—and ducks too, you might say, in the season. There was a slough or a creek leading out of it on the other side, that went miles away, I don’t know where, but it didn’t go to the river. The meal sifted out and made a little track all the way

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0423"/>
to

          <ptr target="#la8998" type="alt" xml:id="te0423"/>
the lake. I dropped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0622"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0424"/>
pap’s

          <ptr target="#la8999" type="alt" xml:id="te0424"/>
          <app from="pr0622" n="41.22 (135.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2098">
            <lem wit="A">pap’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap’s</rdg>
          </app>
whetstone

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0623"/>
there,

          <app from="pr0623" n="41.22 (135.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2100">
            <lem wit="MS1a">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too, so as to look

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0624"/>
like

          <app from="pr0624" n="41.22 (135.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2102">
            <lem wit="A">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">as if</rdg>
          </app>
it had been done by accident. Then I tied up the rip in the meal sack with a string, so it wouldn’t leak no more, and took it and my saw to the canoe again.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10848">
It was about dark, now; so I dropped the canoe down

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0425"/>
the river

          <ptr target="#la9000" type="alt" xml:id="te0425"/>
under some willows that hung over the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0625"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0426"/>
bank

          <ptr target="#la9001" type="alt" xml:id="te0426"/>
,

          <app from="pr0625" n="41.26 (136.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2104">
            <lem wit="A">bank,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
bank

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and waited for the moon to rise. I made fast to a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0427"/>
willow;

          <ptr target="#la9002" type="alt" xml:id="te0427"/>
then I took a bite to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0428"/>
eat,

          <ptr target="#la9003" type="alt" xml:id="te0428"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0626"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0626" n="41.28 (136.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2106">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
laid down in the canoe to smoke a pipe and lay out a plan. I says to myself, they’ll follow the track of that sackful of rocks to the shore and then drag the river for me. And they’ll follow that meal track to the lake and go browsing down the creek that leads out of it to find the robbers that killed me and took the things. They won’t ever hunt the river for anything but my dead carcass. They’ll soon get tired of that, and won’t bother no more about me. All right; I can stop anywhere I want to.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0010"/>
Jackson’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0429"/>
Island

          <ptr target="#as0061" type="an" xml:id="sa0010"/>
is

          <ptr target="#la9004" type="alt" xml:id="te0429"/>
good enough for me; I know that island pretty well, and nobody ever comes there. And then I can paddle over to town, nights, and slink around and pick up things I want.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0430"/>
Jackson’s

          <ptr target="#la9005" type="alt" xml:id="te0430"/>
Island’s the place.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10895">
          <pb n="42" xml:id="pb0042"/>
I was pretty tired, and the first thing I knowed, I was asleep. When I woke up I didn’t know where I was, for a minute. I set up and looked around,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0431"/>
a little

          <ptr target="#la9006" type="alt" xml:id="te0431"/>
scared. Then I remembered. The river looked miles and miles across. The moon was so bright I could a counted the drift logs that went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0627"/>
a-slipping

          <app from="pr0627" n="42.5 (138.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la2108">
            <lem wit="C">a-slipping</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
a-

              <lb/>
slipping

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">a slipping</rdg>
          </app>
along, black and still,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0628"/>
hundreds

          <app from="pr0628" n="42.5 (138.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2110">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hundreds</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hundred</rdg>
          </app>
of yards out from shore. Everything was dead quiet, and it looked late, and

          <hi rend="italic">smelt</hi>
late. You know what I mean—I don’t know the words to put it in.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e10926">
I took a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0629"/>
gap

          <app from="pr0629" n="42.9 (139.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2112">
            <lem wit="A">gap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gape</rdg>
          </app>
and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0630"/>
stretch

          <app from="pr0630" n="42.9 (139.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la2114">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stretch</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stretch,</rdg>
          </app>
and was just

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0432"/>
going

          <ptr target="#la9007" type="alt" xml:id="te0432"/>
to unhitch and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0631"/>
start

          <app from="pr0631" n="42.10 (139.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2116">
            <lem wit="MS1a">start</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">start,</rdg>
          </app>
when I heard a sound away over the water. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0632"/>
listened. Pretty

          <app from="pr0632" n="42.10 (139.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la2118">
            <lem wit="A">listened. Pretty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
listened.—

              <lb/>
Pretty

            </rdg>
          </app>
soon I made it out. It was that dull kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0633"/>
a regular

          <app from="pr0633" n="42.11 (139.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2120">
            <lem wit="A">a regular</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">regular</rdg>
          </app>
sound that comes from oars working in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0433"/>
rowlocks

          <ptr target="#la9008" type="alt" xml:id="te0433"/>
when it’s a still night. I peeped out through the willow branches, and there it was—a skiff, away across the water. I couldn’t tell how many was in it. It kept

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0634"/>
a-coming

          <app from="pr0634" n="42.14–15 (139.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2122">
            <lem wit="A">a-coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
a-

              <lb/>
coming

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and when it was abreast of me I see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0008"/>
there warn’t but one man in it. Thinks I, maybe it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0635"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0635" n="42.16 (140[1].3)" type="e" xml:id="la2124">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
, though I warn’t expecting him. He dropped below me, with the current, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0636"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0636" n="42.17 (140[1].6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2126">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he come a-swinging up shore in the easy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0637"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0434"/>
water

          <ptr target="#la9009" type="alt" xml:id="te0434"/>
          <app from="pr0637" n="42.18 (140[1].8)" type="hc" xml:id="la2128">
            <lem wit="MS1a">water</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">water,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0435"/>
he

          <ptr target="#la9010" type="alt" xml:id="te0435"/>
went by so close I could a reached out the gun and touched him. Well, it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0638"/>
pap

          <app from="pr0638" n="42.19 (140[1].12)" type="e" xml:id="la2130">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
, sure enough—and sober, too, by the way he laid to his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0639"/>
oars.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11037">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0436"/>
I

          <app from="pr0639" n="42.20–21 (140[1].14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la2132">
            <lem wit="A">oars. [¶] I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
oars.

              <lb/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">chap</hi>
. 8 [¶] I

            </rdg>
          </app>
didn’t

          <ptr target="#la9011" type="alt" xml:id="te0436"/>
lose no time. The next minute I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0640"/>
a-spinning

          <app from="pr0640" n="42.21 (140[1].16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la2134">
            <lem wit="A">a-spinning</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
a-

              <lb/>
spinning

            </rdg>
          </app>
down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0641"/>
stream,

          <app from="pr0641" n="42.22 (140[1].17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2136">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stream,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
stream

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
soft but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0642"/>
quick,

          <app from="pr0642" n="42.22 (140[1].18)" type="hc" xml:id="la2138">
            <lem wit="MS1a">quick,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
quick

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the shade of the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0437"/>
bank.

          <ptr target="#la9012" type="alt" xml:id="te0437"/>
I made two mile and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0643"/>
half

          <app from="pr0643" n="42.23 (140[1].20)" type="hc" xml:id="la2140">
            <lem wit="MS1a">half</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half,</rdg>
          </app>
and then struck out a quarter

          <ptr target="#mt0008" type="alt" xml:id="wn0008"/>
of a mile or more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0644"/>
towards

          <app from="pr0644" n="42.23 (140[2].1)" type="e" xml:id="la2142">
            <lem wit="A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">toward</rdg>
          </app>
the middle of the river, because pretty soon I would be passing the ferry landing and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0645"/>
people

          <app from="pr0645" n="42.25 (140[2].5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la2144">
            <lem wit="A">people</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">people there</rdg>
          </app>
might see me and hail me. I got out amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0646"/>
drift wood

          <app from="pr0646" n="42.26 (140[2].8)" type="hc" xml:id="la2146">
            <lem wit="MS1a">drift wood</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">drift-wood</rdg>
          </app>
and then laid down in the bottom of the canoe and let her float. I laid there and had a good rest and a smoke out of my pipe,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0438"/>
looking

          <ptr target="#la9013" type="alt" xml:id="te0438"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0647"/>
away

          <app from="pr0647" n="42.28 (140[2].14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la2148">
            <lem wit="A">away</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">away up</rdg>
          </app>
into the sky, not a cloud in it. The sky looks

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0439"/>
ever so

          <ptr target="#la9014" type="alt" xml:id="te0439"/>
deep when you lay down on your back in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0648"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0440"/>
moonshine

          <ptr target="#la9015" type="alt" xml:id="te0440"/>
          <app from="pr0648" n="42.29–30 (140[2].19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2150">
            <lem wit="A">moonshine</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
moon-

              <lb/>
shine

            </rdg>
          </app>
; I never knowed it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0649"/>
before. And

          <app from="pr0649" n="42.30 (140[2].21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la2152">
            <lem wit="A">before. And</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
before.—

              <lb/>
And

            </rdg>
          </app>
how far a body can hear on the water such

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0650"/>
nights!

          <app from="pr0650" n="42.31 (141.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2154">
            <lem wit="A">nights!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nights.</rdg>
          </app>
I heard people talking at the ferry landing. I heard what they said, too, every word of it. One man said it was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0441"/>
getting

          <ptr target="#la9016" type="alt" xml:id="te0441"/>
towards the long days and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0651"/>
the short

          <app from="pr0651" n="42.33 (141.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2156">
            <lem wit="A">the short</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">short</rdg>
          </app>
nights, now.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0652"/>
T’other

          <app from="pr0652" n="42.33 (141.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2158">
            <lem wit="C">T’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’Tother</rdg>
          </app>
one said

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
warn’t one of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0442"/>
the short ones,

          <ptr target="#la9017" type="alt" xml:id="te0442"/>
he reckoned—and then they laughed, and he said it over again

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0443"/>
and they

          <ptr target="#la9018" type="alt" xml:id="te0443"/>
laughed again; then they waked up another fellow and told him, and laughed,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0653"/>
but he

          <app from="pr0653" n="42.36 (141.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2160">
            <lem wit="A">but he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
but

              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0444"/>
laugh;

          <ptr target="#la9019" type="alt" xml:id="te0444"/>
he ripped out something brisk and said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0654"/>
let

          <app from="pr0654" n="42.37 (141.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la2162">
            <lem wit="MS1a Aa Can">let</lem>
            <rdg wit="Ab">le</rdg>
          </app>
him alone. The first fellow said he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0445"/>
’lowed

          <ptr target="#la9020" type="alt" xml:id="te0445"/>
to tell it to his old woman—she would

          <pb n="43" xml:id="pb0043"/>
think it was pretty good; but he said that warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0655"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr0655" n="43.1 (142.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2164">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
to some things

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0656"/>
he had

          <app from="pr0656" n="43.2 (142.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2166">
            <lem wit="A">he had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he’d</rdg>
          </app>
said in his time. I heard one man say it was nearly three

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0657"/>
o’clock

          <app from="pr0657" n="43.3 (142.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la2168">
            <lem wit="MS1a">o’clock</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">o’clock,</rdg>
          </app>
and he hoped daylight wouldn’t wait

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0446"/>
more than

          <ptr target="#la9021" type="alt" xml:id="te0446"/>
about a week longer. After

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0658"/>
that

          <app from="pr0658" n="43.4 (142.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la2170">
            <lem wit="MS1a">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">that,</rdg>
          </app>
the talk got further and further

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0659"/>
away

          <app from="pr0659" n="43.4 (142.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la2172">
            <lem wit="MS1a">away</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">away,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0447"/>
I couldn’t

          <ptr target="#la9022" type="alt" xml:id="te0447"/>
make out the words any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0660"/>
more

          <app from="pr0660" n="43.5 (142.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2174">
            <lem wit="MS1a">more</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">more,</rdg>
          </app>
but I could hear the mumble; and now and then a laugh, too, but it seemed a long ways off.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y04301">
          <graphic url="y04301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">taking a rest</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11292">
I was away below the ferry now. I rose up and there was Jackson’s Island, about two mile and a half down stream,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0661"/>
heavy-timbered

          <app from="pr0661" n="43.8 (143.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2176">
            <lem wit="A">heavy-timbered</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heavy timbered</rdg>
          </app>
and standing up out of the middle of the river, big and dark and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0662"/>
solid

          <app from="pr0662" n="43.9 (143.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2178">
            <lem wit="A">solid</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">solemn</rdg>
          </app>
, like a steamboat without any lights. There warn’t any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0663"/>
signs

          <app from="pr0663" n="43.10 (143.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2180">
            <lem wit="A">signs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sign</rdg>
          </app>
of the bar at the head—it was all under water, now.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11319">
It didn’t take me long to get there. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0448"/>
shot

          <ptr target="#la9023" type="alt" xml:id="te0448"/>
past the head at a ripping rate, the current was so swift, and then I got into the dead water and landed on the side towards the Illinois shore. I run the canoe into a deep dent in the bank that I knowed about;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0449"/>
I had

          <ptr target="#la9024" type="alt" xml:id="te0449"/>
to part the willow branches to get in;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0450"/>
and

          <ptr target="#la9025" type="alt" xml:id="te0450"/>
when I made fast nobody could a seen the canoe from the outside.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11335">
I went up and set down on a log at the head of the island and looked out on the big river and the black

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0664"/>
drift wood

          <app from="pr0664" n="43.19 (144.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2182">
            <lem wit="MS1a">drift wood</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">driftwood</rdg>
          </app>
, and away over to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0665"/>
town

          <app from="pr0665" n="43.20 (144.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2184">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
, three mile away, where there was three or four lights

          <pb n="44" xml:id="pb0044"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0451"/>
twinkling

          <ptr target="#la9026" type="alt" xml:id="te0451"/>
. A monstrous big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0666"/>
lumber-raft

          <app from="pr0666" n="44.1 (144.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la2186">
            <lem wit="C">lumber-raft</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
lumber-

              <lb/>
raft

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">lumber raft</rdg>
          </app>
was about a mile up stream, coming along down, with a lantern in the middle of it. I watched it come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0452"/>
creeping

          <ptr target="#la9027" type="alt" xml:id="te0452"/>
down, and when it was most abreast of where I stood I heard a man say, “Stern

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0667"/>
oars

          <app from="pr0667" n="44.4 (145.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2188">
            <lem wit="A">oars</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">oar</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0668"/>
there!—heave

          <app from="pr0668" n="44.4 (145.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la2190">
            <lem wit="C">there!—heave</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
there!—

              <lb/>
heave

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">there! heave</rdg>
          </app>
her head to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0669"/>
stabboard!

          <app from="pr0669" n="44.5 (145.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la2192">
            <lem wit="A">stabboard!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
star-

              <lb/>
board, Bill.

            </rdg>
          </app>
”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0453"/>
I heard that just as plain as if the man was by my side.

          <ptr target="#la9028" type="alt" xml:id="te0453"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11410">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0670"/>
There was

          <app from="pr0670" n="44.6 (145.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2194">
            <lem wit="A">There was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I noticed</rdg>
          </app>
a little gray in the sky, now; so I stepped into the woods and laid down for a nap before breakfast.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0271">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter VIII.</head>
        <pb n="45" xml:id="pb0045"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11423">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y04501">
            <graphic url="y04501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0671"/>
Chapter VIII.

              <app from="pr0671" n="45 title (146.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2196">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter VIII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2198">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0011"/>
The

            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf4501">
            <graphic url="hf4501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">in the woods</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e11442">
sun was up so high when I waked, that I judged it was after eight

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0672"/>
o’clock

          <app from="pr0672" n="45.3 (146.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2199">
            <lem wit="A">o’clock</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">oclock</rdg>
          </app>
. I laid there in the grass and the cool shade,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0454"/>
thinking

          <ptr target="#la9029" type="alt" xml:id="te0454"/>
about things and feeling rested and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0673"/>
ruther

          <app from="pr0673" n="45.5 (146.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2201">
            <lem wit="A">ruther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2203">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
comfortable and satisfied. I could see the sun out at one or two holes, but mostly it was big trees all about, and gloomy in there amongst them. There was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0455"/>
freckled

          <ptr target="#la9030" type="alt" xml:id="te0455"/>
places on the ground where the light sifted down through the leaves, and the freckled places swapped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0674"/>
about,

          <app from="pr0674" n="45.13 (146.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2204">
            <lem wit="MS1a">about,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
about

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a little, showing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0675"/>
there was

          <app from="pr0675" n="45.14 (146.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2206">
            <lem wit="A">there was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that there was</rdg>
          </app>
a little breeze up there. A couple of squirrels set on a limb and jabbered at me very friendly

          <ptr target="#as0062" type="an" xml:id="sa0011"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11489">
I was powerful lazy and comfortable—didn’t want to get up and cook breakfast. Well, I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0456"/>
dozing

          <ptr target="#la9031" type="alt" xml:id="te0456"/>
off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0676"/>
again

          <app from="pr0676" n="45.18 (147.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2208">
            <lem wit="MS1a">again</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">again,</rdg>
          </app>
when I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0677"/>
thinks I hears

          <app from="pr0677" n="45.18 (147.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2210">
            <lem wit="A">thinks I hears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">thought I heard</rdg>
          </app>
a deep sound

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0678"/>
of

          <app from="pr0678" n="45.19 (147.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2212">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">go</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0679"/>
Boom

          <app from="pr0679" n="45.19 (147.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la2214">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Boom</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">boom</rdg>
          </app>
!” away up the river. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0680"/>
rouses

          <app from="pr0680" n="45.19 (147.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2216">
            <lem wit="A">rouses</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">roused</rdg>
          </app>
up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0681"/>
rests

          <app from="pr0681" n="45.19 (147.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2218">
            <lem wit="A">rests</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">rested</rdg>
          </app>
on my elbow and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0682"/>
listens

          <app from="pr0682" n="45.20 (147.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2220">
            <lem wit="A">listens</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">listened</rdg>
          </app>
; pretty soon I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0683"/>
hears

          <app from="pr0683" n="45.20 (147.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2222">
            <lem wit="A">hears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
it again. I hopped up and went and looked out at a hole in the leaves, and I see a bunch of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0457"/>
smoke

          <ptr target="#la9032" type="alt" xml:id="te0457"/>
laying on the water a long ways up—about abreast the ferry. And there was the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0684"/>
ferry boat

          <app from="pr0684" n="45.23 (147.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2224">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ferry boat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
full of people, floating along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0685"/>
down

          <app from="pr0685" n="45.23 (147.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2226">
            <lem wit="A">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2228">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. I knowed what was the matter, now. “Boom!” I see the white smoke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0686"/>
squirt

          <app from="pr0686" n="45.25 (148.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2229">
            <lem wit="A">squirt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">belch</rdg>
          </app>
out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0687"/>
ferryboat’s

          <app from="pr0687" n="45.25 (148.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la2231">
            <lem wit="C">ferryboat’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
ferry-

              <lb/>
boat’s

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat’s</rdg>
          </app>
side. You see, they was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0012"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0020"/>
firing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0688"/>
cannons

          <app from="pr0688" n="✱45.25 (148.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2233">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cannons</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cannon</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0020" type="te" xml:id="tv0020"/>
over the water, trying to make my carcass come to the top

          <ptr target="#as0063" type="an" xml:id="sa0012"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11619">
I was pretty hungry, but it warn’t going to do for me to start a fire, because they might see the smoke. So I set there and watched the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0689"/>
cannon-smoke

          <app from="pr0689" n="45.29 (148.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la2235">
            <lem wit="C">cannon-smoke</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">
cannon-

              <lb/>
smoke

            </rdg>
          </app>
and listened to the boom. The river was a mile wide, there, and it always looks pretty on a summer morning—so I was

          <pb n="46" xml:id="pb0046"/>
having a good enough time seeing them hunt for my remainders, if I only had a bite to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0458"/>
eat

          <ptr target="#la9033" type="alt" xml:id="te0458"/>
. Well, then I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0459"/>
happened

          <ptr target="#la9034" type="alt" xml:id="te0459"/>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0460"/>
think

          <ptr target="#la9035" type="alt" xml:id="te0460"/>
how they always put

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0013"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0690"/>
quicksilver

          <app from="pr0690" n="46.3 (149.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la2237">
            <lem wit="A">quicksilver</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
quick-

              <lb/>
silver

            </rdg>
          </app>
in loaves of bread and float them off because they always go right to the drownded carcass

          <ptr target="#as0064" type="an" xml:id="sa0013"/>
and stop there. So says I, I’ll keep a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0691"/>
look-out;

          <app from="pr0691" n="46.5 (149.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2239">
            <lem wit="MS1a">look-out;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lookout,</rdg>
          </app>
and if any of them’s floating around after me, I’ll give them a show. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0461"/>
changed

          <ptr target="#la9036" type="alt" xml:id="te0461"/>
to the Illinois edge of the island to see what luck I could have, and I warn’t disappointed. A big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0692"/>
double-loaf

          <app from="pr0692" n="46.7–8 (149.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2241">
            <lem wit="C">double-loaf</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
double-

              <lb/>
loaf

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">double loaf</rdg>
          </app>
come along, and I most got it, with a long

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0462"/>
stick,

          <ptr target="#la9037" type="alt" xml:id="te0462"/>
but my foot slipped and she floated out further. Of course I was where the current set in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0693"/>
the closest

          <app from="pr0693" n="46.10 (150.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2243">
            <lem wit="A">the closest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">closest</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0694"/>
the shore

          <app from="pr0694" n="46.10 (150.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2245">
            <lem wit="A">the shore</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">shore</rdg>
          </app>
—I knowed enough for that. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0695"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0695" n="46.11 (150.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2247">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
along comes another one, and this time

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tga464"/>
I won.

          <ptr target="#la9038" type="alt" xml:id="te0463"/>
I took out the plug and shook out the little dab of quicksilver, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tp0464"/>
set

          <ptr target="#la9039" type="alt" xml:id="te0464"/>
my teeth

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0696"/>
in. It

          <app from="pr0696" n="46.13 (150.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2249">
            <lem wit="A">in. It</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
in.—

              <lb/>
It

            </rdg>
          </app>
was “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0697"/>
baker’s

          <app from="pr0697" n="46.13 (150.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2251">
            <lem wit="A">baker’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">bakers’</rdg>
          </app>
bread”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0465"/>
—what the quality eat—none of your low-down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0698"/>
corn-pone.

          <app from="pr0698" n="46.14 (150.13–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2253">
            <lem wit="A">corn-pone.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">corn-pone. Says I, you started out to look up this corpse, and you’ve filled your contract to a dot; you couldn’t done better under no circumstances.</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#la9040" type="alt" xml:id="te0465"/>
        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y04601">
          <graphic url="y04601.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">watching the boat</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11757">
I got a good place amongst the leaves, and set there on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0699"/>
log

          <app from="pr0699" n="46.15 (151.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2255">
            <lem wit="MS1a">log</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">log,</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="47" xml:id="pb0047"/>
munching the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0700"/>
bread, and

          <app from="pr0700" n="47.1 (151.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2257">
            <lem wit="C">bread, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">bread,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">bread and</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0466"/>
watching

          <ptr target="#la9041" type="alt" xml:id="te0466"/>
the ferry-boat, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0467"/>
very

          <ptr target="#la9042" type="alt" xml:id="te0467"/>
well satisfied. And then something struck me. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0468"/>
says,

          <ptr target="#la9043" type="alt" xml:id="te0468"/>
now I reckon the widow or the parson or somebody prayed that this bread would find me, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0469"/>
here

          <ptr target="#la9044" type="alt" xml:id="te0469"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0470"/>
it has

          <ptr target="#la9045" type="alt" xml:id="te0470"/>
gone and done it. So there ain’t no doubt but there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0701"/>
is

          <app from="pr0701" n="47.5 (151.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2259">
            <lem wit="A">is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
something in that thing. That is, there’s something in it when a body like the widow or the parson prays, but it don’t work for me, and I reckon it don’t work for only just the right kind.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11807">
I lit a pipe and had a good long smoke and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0471"/>
went

          <ptr target="#la9046" type="alt" xml:id="te0471"/>
on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0702"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0472"/>
watching

          <ptr target="#la9047" type="alt" xml:id="te0472"/>
. The

          <app from="pr0702" n="47.8 (152.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la2261">
            <lem wit="A">watching. The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
watching.—

              <lb/>
The

            </rdg>
          </app>
ferry-boat was floating with the current, and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0703"/>
allowed I’d have a chance

          <app from="pr0703" n="47.9–10 (152.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2263">
            <lem wit="A">allowed . . . chance</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">calculated</rdg>
          </app>
to see who was aboard when she come along, because she would come in close, where the bread did. When

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0704"/>
she’d got pretty well along down towards me

          <app from="pr0704" n="47.11–12 (152.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la2265">
            <lem wit="A">she’d . . . me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">she was within two hundred yards</rdg>
          </app>
, I put out my pipe and went to where I fished out the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0705"/>
bread

          <app from="pr0705" n="47.13 (152.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2267">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bread</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">bread,</rdg>
          </app>
and laid down behind a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0706"/>
log

          <app from="pr0706" n="47.13 (152.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2269">
            <lem wit="A">log</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">big log</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0473"/>
on

          <ptr target="#la9048" type="alt" xml:id="te0473"/>
the bank in a little open place. Where the log forked I could peep through.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11863">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0707"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0707" n="47.15 (152.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la2271">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
she come along, and she drifted in so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0474"/>
close

          <ptr target="#la9049" type="alt" xml:id="te0474"/>
that they could a run out a plank and walked ashore. Most everybody was on the boat. Pap, and Judge Thatcher, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0014"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0021"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0708"/>
Becky

          <app from="pr0708" n="✱47.17 (153.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2273">
            <lem wit="C">Becky</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">Bessie</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0021" type="te" xml:id="tv0021"/>
Thatcher

          <ptr target="#as0065" type="an" xml:id="sa0014"/>
, and Jo Harper, and Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0709"/>
Sawyer

          <app from="pr0709" n="47.18 (153.4–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2275">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Sawyer</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sawyer,</rdg>
          </app>
and his old

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0022"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0710"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0475"/>
aunt

          <ptr target="#la9050" type="alt" xml:id="te0475"/>
          <app from="pr0710" n="✱47.18 (153.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2277">
            <lem wit="C">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Polly

          <ptr target="#tb0022" type="te" xml:id="tv0022"/>
, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0015"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0476"/>
Sid

          <ptr target="#la9051" type="alt" xml:id="te0476"/>
          <ptr target="#as0066" type="an" xml:id="sa0015"/>
and Mary, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0477"/>
plenty

          <ptr target="#la9052" type="alt" xml:id="te0477"/>
more. Everybody was talking about the murder, but the captain broke in and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11923">
“Look sharp, now; the current sets in the closest here, and maybe he’s washed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0478"/>
ashore

          <ptr target="#la9053" type="alt" xml:id="te0478"/>
and got tangled amongst the brush at the water’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0711"/>
edge—I

          <app from="pr0711" n="47.23 (153.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la2279">
            <lem wit="MS1a">edge—I</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">edge. I</rdg>
          </app>
hope

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0479"/>
so

          <ptr target="#la9054" type="alt" xml:id="te0479"/>
, anyway.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11943">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0712"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0480"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la9055" type="alt" xml:id="te0480"/>
          <app from="pr0712" n="47.24 (153.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2281">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
didn’t hope so. They all crowded up and leaned over the rails,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0713"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0481"/>
nearly

          <ptr target="#la9056" type="alt" xml:id="te0481"/>
          <app from="pr0713" n="47.25 (153.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2283">
            <lem wit="A">nearly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">almost</rdg>
          </app>
in my face, and kept still, watching with all their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0714"/>
might

          <app from="pr0714" n="47.25 (154.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2285">
            <lem wit="A">might</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">eyes</rdg>
          </app>
. I could see them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0482"/>
first-rate,

          <ptr target="#la9057" type="alt" xml:id="te0482"/>
but they couldn’t see me. Then the captain sung out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e11978">
“Stand away!” and the cannon let off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0483"/>
such a

          <ptr target="#la9058" type="alt" xml:id="te0483"/>
blast right before

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0484"/>
me

          <ptr target="#la9059" type="alt" xml:id="te0484"/>
that it made me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0715"/>
deef

          <app from="pr0715" n="47.29 (154.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2287">
            <lem wit="A">deef</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">deaf</rdg>
          </app>
with the noise and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0716"/>
pretty near

          <app from="pr0716" n="47.29 (154.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2289">
            <lem wit="A">pretty near</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2291">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
blind with the smoke, and I judged I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0485"/>
gone.

          <ptr target="#la9060" type="alt" xml:id="te0485"/>
If

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0717"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0486"/>
they’d a

          <app from="pr0717" n="47.30 (154.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2292">
            <lem wit="A">they’d a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they had</rdg>
          </app>
had

          <ptr target="#la9061" type="alt" xml:id="te0486"/>
some bullets

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0718"/>
in

          <app from="pr0718" n="47.30 (154.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la2294">
            <lem wit="MS1a">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">in,</rdg>
          </app>
I reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0719"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0487"/>
they’d

          <ptr target="#la9062" type="alt" xml:id="te0487"/>
          <app from="pr0719" n="47.31 (154.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2296">
            <lem wit="A">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they would</rdg>
          </app>
a got the corpse they was after. Well, I see I warn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0488"/>
hurt,

          <ptr target="#la9063" type="alt" xml:id="te0488"/>
thanks to goodness. The boat floated on and went out of sight around the shoulder of the island. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0720"/>
could hear

          <app from="pr0720" n="47.33 (154.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2298">
            <lem wit="A">could hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
the booming, now and then, further and further

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0721"/>
off

          <app from="pr0721" n="47.34 (154.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2300">
            <lem wit="A">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">away</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0722"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0722" n="47.34 (154.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la2302">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0489"/>
after an hour,

          <ptr target="#la9064" type="alt" xml:id="te0489"/>
I didn’t hear it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0723"/>
no

          <app from="pr0723" n="47.35 (155.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2304">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
more. The island was three mile long. I judged

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0490"/>
they had

          <ptr target="#la9065" type="alt" xml:id="te0490"/>
got to the foot, and was giving it up. But they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0724"/>
didn’t,

          <app from="pr0724" n="47.36 (155.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2306">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
didn’t

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0725"/>
awhile

          <app from="pr0725" n="47.36 (155.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2308">
            <lem wit="MS1a">awhile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a while</rdg>
          </app>
. They turned around the foot of the island and started up the channel on the Missouri side, under steam, and booming once

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0726"/>
in

          <app from="pr0726" n="47.38 (155.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2310">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
a while as

          <pb n="48" xml:id="pb0048"/>
they went. I crossed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0727"/>
over

          <app from="pr0727" n="48.1 (155.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2312">
            <lem wit="A">over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2314">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to that side and watched them. When they got abreast the head of the island they quit shooting and dropped over to the Missouri shore and went home to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0728"/>
town

          <app from="pr0728" n="48.3 (155.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2315">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12131">
I knowed I was all right now. Nobody else

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0491"/>
would

          <ptr target="#la9066" type="alt" xml:id="te0491"/>
come a-hunting after me. I got my traps out of the canoe and made me a nice camp in the thick woods. I made a kind of a tent out of my blankets to put my things under so the rain couldn’t get at them. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0729"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0492"/>
catched

          <ptr target="#la9067" type="alt" xml:id="te0492"/>
          <app from="pr0729" n="48.7 (156.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2317">
            <lem wit="A">catched</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">caught</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0730"/>
catfish

          <app from="pr0730" n="48.7 (156.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2319">
            <lem wit="MS1a">catfish</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cat-fish</rdg>
          </app>
and haggled him open with my saw, and towards sundown I started my camp fire and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0731"/>
had

          <app from="pr0731" n="48.9 (156.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2321">
            <lem wit="A">had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">had a big</rdg>
          </app>
supper. Then I set out a line to catch some fish for breakfast.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12164">
When it was dark I set by my camp fire smoking, and feeling pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0732"/>
satisfied

          <app from="pr0732" n="48.12 (156.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2323">
            <lem wit="A">satisfied</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">content</rdg>
          </app>
; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0733"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0733" n="48.12 (156.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la2325">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
it got sort of lonesome, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0734"/>
so

          <app from="pr0734" n="48.12 (156.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2327">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2329">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I went and set on the bank and listened

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0009"/>
to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0735"/>
currents

          <app from="pr0735" n="48.13 (157.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2330">
            <lem wit="A">currents</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">current</rdg>
          </app>
washing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0736"/>
along

          <app from="pr0736" n="48.13 (157.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2332">
            <lem wit="A">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">against the shore</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0737"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0493"/>
counted the stars and drift-logs and rafts that come down, and then went to bed; there ain’t no better way to put in time when you are lonesome; you can’t stay so, you soon get over it.

          <ptr target="#la9068" type="alt" xml:id="te0493"/>
        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y04901">
          <graphic url="y04901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">discovering the camp fire</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12220">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0494"/>
And

          <ptr target="#la9069" type="alt" xml:id="te0494"/>
          <app from="pr0737" n="48.14–17 (157.2–7)" type="e" xml:id="la2334">
            <lem wit="A">counted . . . it. [¶] And</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
looked at the stars, and out over the river watching the rafts come down. So for an hour, and then to bed.

              <lb/>
              <hi rend="italic">CHAP. 9.</hi>
[¶] And

            </rdg>
          </app>
so for three days and nights. No difference—just the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0495"/>
same

          <ptr target="#la9070" type="alt" xml:id="te0495"/>
thing. But the next day I went exploring

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0738"/>
around

          <app from="pr0738" n="48.18 (157.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2336">
            <lem wit="A">around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2338">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
down through the island. I was boss of it; it all belonged to me,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0496"/>
so

          <ptr target="#la9071" type="alt" xml:id="te0496"/>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0739"/>
say

          <app from="pr0739" n="48.19 (157.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2339">
            <lem wit="A">say</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">speak</rdg>
          </app>
, and I wanted to know all about it; but mainly I wanted to put in the time. I found

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0740"/>
plenty

          <app from="pr0740" n="48.21 (157.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2341">
            <lem wit="A">plenty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">no end of</rdg>
          </app>
strawberries, ripe and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0741"/>
prime; and

          <app from="pr0741" n="48.21 (157.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2343">
            <lem wit="A">prime; and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">good; and I found</rdg>
          </app>
green summer-grapes, and green

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0742"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0497"/>
razberries;

          <ptr target="#la9072" type="alt" xml:id="te0497"/>
          <app from="pr0742" n="48.22 (157.21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la2345">
            <lem wit="A">razberries;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">raspberries; yes,</rdg>
          </app>
and the green

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0743"/>
blackberries

          <app from="pr0743" n="48.22 (157.22–158.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2347">
            <lem wit="A">blackberries</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
black-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
berries

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#mt0009" type="alt" xml:id="wn0009"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0744"/>
was

          <app from="pr0744" n="48.22 (158.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2349">
            <lem wit="A">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">were</rdg>
          </app>
just beginning to show. They would all come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0745"/>
handy

          <app from="pr0745" n="48.23 (158.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2351">
            <lem wit="A">handy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">good and handy</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0746"/>
by and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0498"/>
by

          <app from="pr0746" n="48.23 (158.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2353">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, I judged.

          <ptr target="#la9073" type="alt" xml:id="te0498"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12325">
Well, I went fooling along in the deep woods till I judged I warn’t far from the foot of the island. I had my gun along, but I hadn’t shot

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0747"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr0747" n="48.26 (158.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2355">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">at anything</rdg>
          </app>
; it was for protection;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0748"/>
thought I would

          <app from="pr0748" n="48.26 (158.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2357">
            <lem wit="A">thought I would</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I calculated to</rdg>
          </app>
kill some game

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0749"/>
nigh

          <app from="pr0749" n="48.26 (158.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2359">
            <lem wit="A">nigh</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nearer</rdg>
          </app>
home. About this time I mighty near stepped on a good sized snake, and it went sliding off through the grass and flowers, and I after it, trying to get a shot at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0750"/>
it

          <app from="pr0750" n="48.29 (158.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2361">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it with my gun</rdg>
          </app>
. I clipped along, and all of a sudden I

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0016"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0751"/>
bounded

          <app from="pr0751" n="48.29 (158.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2363">
            <lem wit="A">bounded</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">bounced</rdg>
          </app>
right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0752"/>
onto

          <app from="pr0752" n="48.30 (159.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2365">
            <lem wit="MS1a">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">on to</rdg>
          </app>
the ashes of a camp fire that was still

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0753"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0499"/>
smoking

          <ptr target="#la9074" type="alt" xml:id="te0499"/>
          <ptr target="#as0067" type="an" xml:id="sa0016"/>
.

          <app from="pr0753" n="48.30 (159.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2367">
            <lem wit="A">smoking.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">smoking!</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12389">
My heart jumped

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0500"/>
up

          <ptr target="#la9075" type="alt" xml:id="te0500"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0754"/>
amongst my lungs

          <app from="pr0754" n="48.31 (159.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2369">
            <lem wit="A">amongst my lungs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">into my throat</rdg>
          </app>
. I never waited

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0755"/>
for

          <app from="pr0755" n="48.31 (159.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2371">
            <lem wit="A">for</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2373">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0756"/>
look

          <app from="pr0756" n="48.31 (159.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la2374">
            <lem wit="A">look</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">look any</rdg>
          </app>
further, but uncocked my gun and went sneaking back on my tip-toes as fast as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0757"/>
ever I could

          <app from="pr0757" n="48.33 (159.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la2376">
            <lem wit="A">ever I could</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I could move along</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0758"/>
Every now

          <app from="pr0758" n="48.33 (159.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2378">
            <lem wit="A">Every now</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Now</rdg>
          </app>
and then I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0759"/>
stopped,

          <app from="pr0759" n="48.33 (159.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la2380">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stopped,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
stopped

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a second, amongst the thick leaves, and listened; but my breath come so hard I couldn’t hear nothing else. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0501"/>
slunk

          <ptr target="#la9076" type="alt" xml:id="te0501"/>
along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0760"/>
another piece

          <app from="pr0760" n="48.35 (159.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2382">
            <lem wit="A">another piece</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2383">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
further, then listened again; and so on, and so on; if I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0761"/>
see

          <app from="pr0761" n="48.36 (159.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2384">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
a stump, I took it for a man; if I trod on a stick and broke it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0502"/>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0762"/>
made me feel like a person had cut one of my breaths in two and I only got half, and the short half, too.

          <ptr target="#la9077" type="alt" xml:id="te0502"/>
          <app from="pr0762" n="48.37–39 (160.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la2385">
            <lem wit="A">made . . . too</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nearly took my breath away</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12477">
          <pb n="49" xml:id="pb0049"/>
When I got to camp I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0763"/>
warn’t feeling very brash, there warn’t much sand in my craw

          <app from="pr0763" n="49.1–2 (160.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2386">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t feeling . . . craw</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was about sick</rdg>
          </app>
; but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0503"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la9078" type="alt" xml:id="te0503"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0504"/>
says,

          <ptr target="#la9079" type="alt" xml:id="te0504"/>
this ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0505"/>
no

          <ptr target="#la9080" type="alt" xml:id="te0505"/>
time to be fooling around. So I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0506"/>
got

          <ptr target="#la9081" type="alt" xml:id="te0506"/>
all my traps into my canoe again so as to have them out of sight, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0507"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la9082" type="alt" xml:id="te0507"/>
put out the fire and scattered the ashes around to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0764"/>
look

          <app from="pr0764" n="49.4 (160.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la2387">
            <lem wit="A">look</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">make it look</rdg>
          </app>
like an old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0765"/>
last-year’s

          <app from="pr0765" n="49.5 (160.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la2388">
            <lem wit="MS1a">last-year’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">last year’s</rdg>
          </app>
camp, and then clumb a tree.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12525">
I reckon I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0766"/>
up

          <app from="pr0766" n="49.6 (160.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2389">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2390">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the tree two hours; but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0767"/>
didn’t see nothing

          <app from="pr0767" n="49.6 (160.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2391">
            <lem wit="A">didn’t see nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">never seen anything</rdg>
          </app>
, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0768"/>
didn’t hear nothing

          <app from="pr0768" n="49.7 (160.21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la2392">
            <lem wit="A">didn’t hear nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">never heard anything</rdg>
          </app>
—I only

          <hi rend="italic">thought</hi>
I heard and seen

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0508"/>
as much as

          <ptr target="#la9083" type="alt" xml:id="te0508"/>
a thousand things.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0769"/>
Well

          <app from="pr0769" n="49.8 (161.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2393">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
I couldn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0509"/>
stay up

          <ptr target="#la9084" type="alt" xml:id="te0509"/>
there forever; so at last I got down, but I kept in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0770"/>
the thick

          <app from="pr0770" n="49.9 (161.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2394">
            <lem wit="A">the thick</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">thick</rdg>
          </app>
woods and on the lookout all the time. All I could get to eat was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0510"/>
berries and

          <ptr target="#la9085" type="alt" xml:id="te0510"/>
what was left over from breakfast.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12585">
By the time it was night I was pretty hungry. So when it was good and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0771"/>
dark

          <app from="pr0771" n="49.13 (161.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la2395">
            <lem wit="MS1a">dark</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dark,</rdg>
          </app>
I slid out from shore

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0511"/>
before moonrise

          <ptr target="#la9086" type="alt" xml:id="te0511"/>
and paddled over to the Illinois bank—about a quarter of a mile. I went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0772"/>
out in

          <app from="pr0772" n="49.14 (161.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2396">
            <lem wit="A">out in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">into</rdg>
          </app>
the woods and cooked a supper, and I had about made up my mind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0773"/>
I would

          <app from="pr0773" n="49.15 (161.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2397">
            <lem wit="A">I would</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">to</rdg>
          </app>
stay there all night, when I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0774"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0512"/>
hear

          <ptr target="#la9087" type="alt" xml:id="te0512"/>
a

          <hi rend="italic">plunkety-plunk, plunkety-plunk</hi>
, and

          <pb n="50" xml:id="pb0050"/>
says to myself, horses coming

          <app from="pr0774" n="49.16–50.1 (162.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la2398">
            <lem wit="A">hear . . . coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard horses</rdg>
          </app>
; and next I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0775"/>
hear

          <app from="pr0775" n="50.1 (162.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2399">
            <lem wit="A">hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
people’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0513"/>
voices

          <ptr target="#la9088" type="alt" xml:id="te0513"/>
. I got everything into the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0514"/>
canoe

          <ptr target="#la9089" type="alt" xml:id="te0514"/>
as quick as I could, and then went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0515"/>
creeping

          <ptr target="#la9090" type="alt" xml:id="te0515"/>
through the woods to see what I could find out. I hadn’t got far when I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0776"/>
hear

          <app from="pr0776" n="50.4 (162.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2400">
            <lem wit="A">hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
a man say:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12664">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0777"/>
We better

          <app from="pr0777" n="50.5 (162.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2401">
            <lem wit="A">We better</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">It’s just as well to</rdg>
          </app>
camp

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0778"/>
here

          <app from="pr0778" n="50.5 (162.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2402">
            <lem wit="A">here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">here, anyway</rdg>
          </app>
, if we can find a good place; the horses

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0779"/>
is

          <app from="pr0779" n="50.5 (162.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2403">
            <lem wit="A">is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">are</rdg>
          </app>
about beat out. Let’s look around.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12691">
I didn’t wait, but shoved out and paddled away

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0780"/>
easy

          <app from="pr0780" n="50.7 (162.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2404">
            <lem wit="A">easy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">soft and easy</rdg>
          </app>
. I tied up in the old place, and reckoned I would sleep in the canoe.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12701">
I didn’t sleep much. I couldn’t, somehow, for thinking. And every time I waked up I thought somebody had me by the neck. So the sleep didn’t do me no good.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0781"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0781" n="50.11 (163.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2405">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I says to myself, I can’t live this way;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0782"/>
I’m agoing

          <app from="pr0782" n="50.12 (163.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2406">
            <lem wit="A">I’m agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I mean</rdg>
          </app>
to find out who it is that’s here on the island with me; I’ll find it out or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0783"/>
bust

          <app from="pr0783" n="50.13 (163.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2407">
            <lem wit="A">bust</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">die</rdg>
          </app>
. Well, I felt better, right off.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e12728">
So I took my paddle and slid out from shore just a step or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0784"/>
two

          <app from="pr0784" n="50.14 (163.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la2408">
            <lem wit="MS1a">two</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">two,</rdg>
          </app>
and then let the canoe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0785"/>
drop

          <app from="pr0785" n="50.15 (163.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2409">
            <lem wit="A">drop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">drift</rdg>
          </app>
along down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0786"/>
amongst

          <app from="pr0786" n="50.15 (164.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2410">
            <lem wit="A">amongst</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">in</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0516"/>
shadows. The moon was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0787"/>
shining,

          <app from="pr0787" n="50.16 (164.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2411">
            <lem wit="A">shining,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">shining, now;</rdg>
          </app>
and outside

          <ptr target="#la9091" type="alt" xml:id="te0516"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0517"/>
of

          <ptr target="#la9092" type="alt" xml:id="te0517"/>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0518"/>
shadows it

          <ptr target="#la9093" type="alt" xml:id="te0518"/>
made it most as light as day. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0788"/>
poked along

          <app from="pr0788" n="50.17 (164.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2412">
            <lem wit="A">poked along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">drifted</rdg>
          </app>
well onto an hour, everything still as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0789"/>
rocks and sound asleep

          <app from="pr0789" n="50.18 (164.6–9)" type="e" xml:id="la2413">
            <lem wit="A">rocks . . . asleep</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">death, except that kind of creatures that’s always making noises in the night</rdg>
          </app>
. Well by this time I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0790"/>
most

          <app from="pr0790" n="50.18 (164.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2414">
            <lem wit="A">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nearly</rdg>
          </app>
down to the foot of the island. A

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0519"/>
little

          <ptr target="#la9094" type="alt" xml:id="te0519"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0791"/>
ripply

          <app from="pr0791" n="50.19 (164.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la2415">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ripply</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ripply,</rdg>
          </app>
cool breeze begun to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0792"/>
blow

          <app from="pr0792" n="50.19 (164.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la2416">
            <lem wit="A">blow,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">shiver along amongst the willows</rdg>
          </app>
, and that was as good as saying the night was about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0793"/>
done

          <app from="pr0793" n="50.20 (164.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2417">
            <lem wit="A">done</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gone</rdg>
          </app>
. I give her a turn with the paddle and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0794"/>
brung

          <app from="pr0794" n="50.21 (164.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2418">
            <lem wit="A">brung</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">brought</rdg>
          </app>
her nose to shore; then I got my gun and slipped out and into the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0520"/>
edge of the

          <ptr target="#la9095" type="alt" xml:id="te0520"/>
woods. I set down there on a log and looked out through the leaves. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0795"/>
see

          <app from="pr0795" n="50.23 (165.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2419">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
the moon go off watch and the darkness

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0796"/>
begin to blanket

          <app from="pr0796" n="50.24 (165.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2420">
            <lem wit="A">begin to blanket</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">spread itself over</rdg>
          </app>
the river. But in a little while I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0797"/>
see a

          <app from="pr0797" n="50.24 (165.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2421">
            <lem wit="A">see a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw a little</rdg>
          </app>
pale streak

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0798"/>
over

          <app from="pr0798" n="50.25 (165.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2422">
            <lem wit="A">over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">above</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0799"/>
tree tops

          <app from="pr0799" n="50.25 (165.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2423">
            <lem wit="MS1a">tree tops</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tree-tops</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0800"/>
and knowed

          <app from="pr0800" n="50.25 (165.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la2424">
            <lem wit="A">and knowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">away down the river, and I knowed</rdg>
          </app>
the day was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0801"/>
coming. So

          <app from="pr0801" n="50.25 (165.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2425">
            <lem wit="A">coming. So</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
coming.—

              <lb/>
So

            </rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0802"/>
took

          <app from="pr0802" n="50.26 (165.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2426">
            <lem wit="A">took</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">shouldered</rdg>
          </app>
my gun and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0803"/>
slipped off

          <app from="pr0803" n="50.26 (165.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2427">
            <lem wit="A">slipped off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">went slipping away</rdg>
          </app>
towards where I had run across that camp fire, stopping every minute

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0804"/>
or two to

          <app from="pr0804" n="50.27 (165.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la2428">
            <lem wit="A">or two to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">to look all around and</rdg>
          </app>
listen.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0805"/>
But

          <app from="pr0805" n="50.27 (165.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2429">
            <lem wit="A">But</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2430">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I hadn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0806"/>
no

          <app from="pr0806" n="50.27 (165.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la2431">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pretty good</rdg>
          </app>
luck, somehow; I couldn’t seem to find the place. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0807"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr0807" n="50.28 (165.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2432">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, sure enough, I catched a glimpse of fire, away through the trees. I went for it, cautious and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0521"/>
slow.

          <ptr target="#la9096" type="alt" xml:id="te0521"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0808"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0808" n="50.30 (166.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la2433">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I was close enough to have a look, and there laid a man on the ground.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0809"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0522"/>
It most give me the fan-tods.

          <ptr target="#la9097" type="alt" xml:id="te0522"/>
He

          <app from="pr0809" n="50.31–32 (166.10–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2434">
            <lem wit="A">It . . . fan-tods. He</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">My heart fell to thumping. The man</rdg>
          </app>
had a blanket around his head, and his head was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0523"/>
nearly

          <ptr target="#la9098" type="alt" xml:id="te0523"/>
in the fire. I set there behind a clump of bushes,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0810"/>
in about

          <app from="pr0810" n="50.33 (166.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2435">
            <lem wit="A">in about</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">within</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0524"/>
six

          <ptr target="#la9099" type="alt" xml:id="te0524"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0525"/>
foot

          <ptr target="#la9100" type="alt" xml:id="te0525"/>
of

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0023"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0811"/>
him,

          <app from="pr0811" n="✱50.34 (166.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2436">
            <lem wit="A">him,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
him

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0023" type="te" xml:id="tv0023"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0526"/>
kept my eyes on him steady.

          <ptr target="#la9101" type="alt" xml:id="te0526"/>
It was getting

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0812"/>
gray

          <app from="pr0812" n="50.34 (166.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2437">
            <lem wit="A">gray</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gray with</rdg>
          </app>
daylight, now. Pretty soon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0813"/>
he gapped, and

          <app from="pr0813" n="50.35 (166.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la2438">
            <lem wit="A">he gapped, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">the man</rdg>
          </app>
stretched

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0814"/>
himself,

          <app from="pr0814" n="50.35 (166.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2439">
            <lem wit="A">himself,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
himself

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0815"/>
and hove

          <app from="pr0815" n="50.35 (166.21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la2440">
            <lem wit="A">and hove</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
and

              <lb/>
and hove

            </rdg>
          </app>
off the blanket, and it was Miss Watson’s Jim! I bet I was glad to see him. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13044">“Hello, Jim!” and skipped out.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13046">
          <pb n="51" xml:id="pb0051"/>
He bounced up and stared at me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0816"/>
wild

          <app from="pr0816" n="51.1 (167.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la2441">
            <lem wit="A">wild</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">with his eyes wide open</rdg>
          </app>
. Then he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0817"/>
drops

          <app from="pr0817" n="51.1 (167.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2442">
            <lem wit="A">drops</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dropped</rdg>
          </app>
down on his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0818"/>
knees

          <app from="pr0818" n="51.2 (167.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2443">
            <lem wit="MS1a">knees</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">knees,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0819"/>
puts

          <app from="pr0819" n="51.2 (167.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2444">
            <lem wit="A">puts</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">put</rdg>
          </app>
his hands together and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13082">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0820"/>
Doan’

          <app from="pr0820" n="51.3 (167.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2445">
            <lem wit="A">Doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Don’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0527"/>
hurt

          <ptr target="#la9102" type="alt" xml:id="te0527"/>
me—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0821"/>
don’t!

          <app from="pr0821" n="51.3 (167.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2446">
            <lem wit="A">don’t!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">don’t.</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0822"/>
hain’t ever

          <app from="pr0822" n="51.3 (167.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2447">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t never</rdg>
          </app>
done no harm to a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0823"/>
ghos’. I

          <app from="pr0823" n="51.3 (167.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la2448">
            <lem wit="A">ghos’. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
ghos’.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0824"/>
awluz

          <app from="pr0824" n="51.4 (167.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2449">
            <lem wit="A">awluz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">always</rdg>
          </app>
liked dead people,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0825"/>
en done

          <app from="pr0825" n="51.4 (167.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2450">
            <lem wit="A">en done</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and done</rdg>
          </app>
all I could for ’em. You go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0826"/>
en git

          <app from="pr0826" n="51.4 (167.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2451">
            <lem wit="A">en git</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and git</rdg>
          </app>
in de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0827"/>
river

          <app from="pr0827" n="51.5 (167.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2452">
            <lem wit="A">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">riber</rdg>
          </app>
agin, whah you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0528"/>
b’longs,

          <ptr target="#la9103" type="alt" xml:id="te0528"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0828"/>
en doan’

          <app from="pr0828" n="51.5 (167.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2453">
            <lem wit="A">en doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and don’t</rdg>
          </app>
do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0829"/>
nuffn

          <app from="pr0829" n="51.5 (167.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2454">
            <lem wit="A">nuffn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nuffin</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0830"/>
ole

          <app from="pr0830" n="51.5 (167.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la2455">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ole</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Ole</rdg>
          </app>
Jim,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0831"/>
’at’uz awluz

          <app from="pr0831" n="51.5–6 (167.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2456">
            <lem wit="A">’at ’uz awluz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dat was always</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0529"/>
yo’

          <ptr target="#la9104" type="alt" xml:id="te0529"/>
fren’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13194">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ahm016"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y05101">
            <graphic url="y05101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">jim and the ghost</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
          <ptr target="#as0068" type="an" xml:id="sam016"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13202">
Well, I warn’t long making him understand I warn’t dead. I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0530"/>
ever so

          <ptr target="#la9105" type="alt" xml:id="te0530"/>
glad to see Jim. I warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0832"/>
lonesome

          <app from="pr0832" n="51.8 (168.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2457">
            <lem wit="MS1a">lonesome</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lonesome,</rdg>
          </app>
now. I told him I warn’t afraid of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0833"/>
          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
          <app from="pr0833" n="51.9 (168.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2458">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">him</rdg>
          </app>
telling the people where I was. I talked along, but he only set there and looked at me; never said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0834"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr0834" n="51.10 (168.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2459">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
. Then I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0835"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0531"/>
says

          <ptr target="#la9106" type="alt" xml:id="te0531"/>
          <app from="pr0835" n="51.10 (168.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2460">
            <lem wit="A">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">said</rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13245">
“It’s good daylight.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0836"/>
Le’s get

          <app from="pr0836" n="51.11 (168.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2461">
            <lem wit="A">Le’s get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Let’s be getting</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0532"/>
breakfast.

          <ptr target="#la9107" type="alt" xml:id="te0532"/>
Make up your camp fire good.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13258">
“What’s de use

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0533"/>
er

          <ptr target="#la9108" type="alt" xml:id="te0533"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0837"/>
makin’

          <app from="pr0837" n="51.13 (168.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2462">
            <lem wit="A">makin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">making</rdg>
          </app>
up de camp fire to cook

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0838"/>
strawbries en

          <app from="pr0838" n="51.13 (168.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la2463">
            <lem wit="A">strawbries en</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">strawberries and</rdg>
          </app>
sich truck? But you got a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0839"/>
gun—

          <app from="pr0839" n="51.14 (168.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la2464">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gun—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">gun,</rdg>
          </app>
hain’t you? Den we kin

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0534"/>
git

          <ptr target="#la9109" type="alt" xml:id="te0534"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0840"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0535"/>
sumfn

          <ptr target="#la9110" type="alt" xml:id="te0535"/>
          <app from="pr0840" n="51.14 (168.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2465">
            <lem wit="A">sumfn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sumfin</rdg>
          </app>
better

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0841"/>
den strawbries

          <app from="pr0841" n="51.15 (168.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2466">
            <lem wit="A">den strawbries</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dan strawberries</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13311">
“Strawberries and such truck,” I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0842"/>
says. “

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0536"/>
Is

          <ptr target="#la9111" type="alt" xml:id="te0536"/>
          <app from="pr0842" n="51.16 (169.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2467">
            <lem wit="A">says. “Is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">says, “is</rdg>
          </app>
that what you live on?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13324">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0843"/>
couldn’

          <app from="pr0843" n="51.17 (169.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2468">
            <lem wit="A">couldn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">couldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
git

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0844"/>
nuffn

          <app from="pr0844" n="51.17 (169.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2469">
            <lem wit="A">nuffn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nothing</rdg>
          </app>
else,” he says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13342">“Why, how long you been on the island, Jim?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13344">
“I come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0845"/>
heah

          <app from="pr0845" n="51.19 (169.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2470">
            <lem wit="A">heah</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">here</rdg>
          </app>
de night

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0537"/>
arter

          <ptr target="#la9112" type="alt" xml:id="te0537"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0846"/>
you’s

          <app from="pr0846" n="51.19 (169.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2471">
            <lem wit="A">you’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you was</rdg>
          </app>
killed.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13365">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0538"/>
“What, all that

          <ptr target="#la9113" type="alt" xml:id="te0538"/>
time?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13370">
          <pb n="52" xml:id="pb0052"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0847"/>
Yes-indeedy

          <app from="pr0847" n="52.1 (169.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2472">
            <lem wit="A">Yes-indeedy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Yes, indeedy</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13381">
“And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0848"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr0848" n="52.2 (169.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2473">
            <lem wit="A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hain’t</rdg>
          </app>
you had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0849"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr0849" n="52.2 (169.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2474">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
but that kind of rubbage to eat?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13399">
“No,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0850"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0539"/>
sah

          <ptr target="#la9114" type="alt" xml:id="te0539"/>
          <app from="pr0850" n="52.3 (169.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2475">
            <lem wit="A">sah</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
sir/

              <add>sah</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0851"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0540"/>
nuffn

          <ptr target="#la9115" type="alt" xml:id="te0540"/>
          <app from="pr0851" n="52.3 (169.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2476">
            <lem wit="A">nuffn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
nothing/

              <add>nuth’n</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
else.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13426">
“Well, you must be most starved, ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0852"/>
you?”

          <app from="pr0852" n="52.4 (169.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2477">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you?”</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you?’</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13435">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0853"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr0853" n="52.5 (169.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2478">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
I could eat a hoss. I think I could. How long

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0854"/>
you

          <app from="pr0854" n="52.5 (170.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2479">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">has you</rdg>
          </app>
ben on de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0855"/>
islan’?

          <app from="pr0855" n="52.6 (170.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2480">
            <lem wit="A">islan’?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">island.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13462">
“Since the night I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0856"/>
got

          <app from="pr0856" n="52.7 (170.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2481">
            <lem wit="A">got</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
killed.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13473">
“No!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0857"/>
W’y

          <app from="pr0857" n="52.8 (170.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2482">
            <lem wit="C">W’y</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Why</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">W’y,</rdg>
          </app>
what has

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0541"/>
you

          <ptr target="#la9116" type="alt" xml:id="te0541"/>
lived on? But you got a gun.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0858"/>
O

          <app from="pr0858" n="52.8 (170.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2483">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes, you got a gun. Dat’s good. Now you kill

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0859"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0542"/>
sumfn

          <ptr target="#la9117" type="alt" xml:id="te0542"/>
,

          <app from="pr0859" n="52.9 (170.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2484">
            <lem wit="C">sumfn,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
suffin/

              <add>sumfin,</add>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">sumfn</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0860"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0543"/>
en

          <ptr target="#la9118" type="alt" xml:id="te0543"/>
          <app from="pr0860" n="52.9 (170.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2485">
            <lem wit="A">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
an’/

              <add>en</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I’ll make up de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0861"/>
fire.”

          <app from="pr0861" n="52.9 (170.13–16)" type="e" xml:id="la2486">
            <lem wit="A">fire.”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
fire.”

              <lb/>
[¶]“No, you follow me, and bring some brands along.”

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13534">
So we went over to where the canoe was, and while he built a fire in a grassy open place amongst the trees, I fetched meal and bacon and coffee, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0862"/>
coffee pot

          <app from="pr0862" n="52.12 (171.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2487">
            <lem wit="MS1a">coffee pot</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">coffee-pot</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0863"/>
frying pan

          <app from="pr0863" n="52.12 (171.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la2488">
            <lem wit="MS1a">frying pan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">frying-pan</rdg>
          </app>
, and sugar and tin cups, and the nigger was set back considerable, because he reckoned it was all done with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0864"/>
witchcraft

          <app from="pr0864" n="52.14 (171.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la2489">
            <lem wit="A">witchcraft</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
witch-

              <lb/>
craft

            </rdg>
          </app>
. I catched a good big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0865"/>
catfish

          <app from="pr0865" n="52.14 (171.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2490">
            <lem wit="MS1a">catfish</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cat-fish</rdg>
          </app>
, too, and Jim cleaned him with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0866"/>
knife

          <app from="pr0866" n="52.15 (171.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2491">
            <lem wit="MS1a">knife</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">knife,</rdg>
          </app>
and fried

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0867"/>
him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13581">
When

          <app from="pr0867" n="52.15–16 (171.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2492">
            <lem wit="A">him. [¶] When</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
him.—

              <lb/>
[¶] When

            </rdg>
          </app>
breakfast was ready, we lolled on the grass and eat it smoking hot. Jim laid it in with all his might, for he was most about starved. Then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0544"/>
when

          <ptr target="#la9119" type="alt" xml:id="te0544"/>
we had got pretty well stuffed, we laid off and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0868"/>
lazied

          <app from="pr0868" n="52.19 (171.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2494">
            <lem wit="A">lazied</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">smoked</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13603">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0869"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr0869" n="52.20 (171.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2495">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
Jim says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13612">
“But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0870"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr0870" n="52.21 (171.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la2496">
            <lem wit="MS1a">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
, Huck, who

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0871"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr0871" n="52.21 (172.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2497">
            <lem wit="A">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0545"/>
it dat

          <ptr target="#la9120" type="alt" xml:id="te0545"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0872"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr0872" n="52.21 (172.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2498">
            <lem wit="A">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
killed in dat shanty,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0873"/>
ef

          <app from="pr0873" n="52.22 (172.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2499">
            <lem wit="A">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">if</rdg>
          </app>
it warn’t you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13649">
Then I told him the whole thing, and he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0546"/>
said

          <ptr target="#la9121" type="alt" xml:id="te0546"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0874"/>
it

          <app from="pr0874" n="52.23 (172.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2500">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I</rdg>
          </app>
was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0547"/>
smart

          <ptr target="#la9122" type="alt" xml:id="te0547"/>
. He said Tom Sawyer couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0875"/>
get

          <app from="pr0875" n="52.24 (172.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2501">
            <lem wit="A">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">got</rdg>
          </app>
up no better plan than what I had. Then I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13675">
“How do you come to be here, Jim, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0876"/>
how’d

          <app from="pr0876" n="52.26 (172.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2502">
            <lem wit="A">how’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">how did</rdg>
          </app>
you get here?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13685">
He looked pretty uneasy, and didn’t say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0877"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr0877" n="52.27 (172.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la2503">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
for a minute. Then he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13695">“Maybe I better not tell.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13697">“Why, Jim?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13699">
“Well, dey’s reasons. But you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0878"/>
wouldn’

          <app from="pr0878" n="52.31 (172.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2504">
            <lem wit="A">wouldn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">wouldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
tell on me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0879"/>
ef

          <app from="pr0879" n="52.31 (173.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2505">
            <lem wit="A">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">if</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0880"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr0880" n="52.31 (173.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2506">
            <lem wit="A">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
to tell you, would you, Huck?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13727">“Blamed if I would, Jim.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13729">
“Well, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0881"/>
b’lieve

          <app from="pr0881" n="52.34 (173.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2507">
            <lem wit="A">b’lieve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">believes</rdg>
          </app>
you, Huck. I—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0882"/>
          <hi rend="italic">run off</hi>
          <app from="pr0882" n="52.34 (173.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la2508">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">run off</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">run off</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13749">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0548"/>
“Jim!”

          <ptr target="#la9123" type="alt" xml:id="te0548"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13753">“But mind, you said you wouldn’t tell—you know you said you wouldn’t tell, Huck.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13755">
“Well, I did. I said I wouldn’t, and I’ll stick to it. Honest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0883"/>
          <hi rend="italic">injun</hi>
,

          <app from="pr0883" n="52.38 (173.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2509">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="italic">injun</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">injun,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">injun</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0549"/>
will.

          <ptr target="#la9124" type="alt" xml:id="te0549"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0017"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0884"/>
People

          <app from="pr0884" n="52.39 (173.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la2510">
            <lem wit="A">People</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I reckon people</rdg>
          </app>
would call me a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0885"/>
low-down ablitionist

          <app from="pr0885" n="52.39 (173.20–21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2511">
            <lem wit="MS1a">low-down ablitionist</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">low down ablitionist</rdg>
          </app>
and despise me

          <pb n="53" xml:id="pb0053"/>
for keeping mum

          <ptr target="#as0069" type="an" xml:id="sa0017"/>
—but that don’t make no difference. I ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0886"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr0886" n="53.1 (174.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2512">
            <lem wit="A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
to tell, and I ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0887"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr0887" n="53.2 (174.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2513">
            <lem wit="A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0888"/>
there,

          <app from="pr0888" n="53.2 (174.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2514">
            <lem wit="MS1a">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
anyways. So now,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0889"/>
le’s

          <app from="pr0889" n="53.2 (174.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2515">
            <lem wit="A">le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">let’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0550"/>
know

          <ptr target="#la9125" type="alt" xml:id="te0550"/>
all about it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e13834">
“Well, you see, it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0890"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr0890" n="53.4 (174.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2516">
            <lem wit="A">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
dis way. Ole

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0891"/>
missus

          <app from="pr0891" n="53.4 (174.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2517">
            <lem wit="MS1a">missus</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Missus</rdg>
          </app>
—dat’s Miss Watson—she pecks on me all de time,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0892"/>
en

          <app from="pr0892" n="53.5 (174.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2518">
            <lem wit="A">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
treats me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0893"/>
pooty

          <app from="pr0893" n="53.5 (174.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2519">
            <lem wit="A">pooty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pretty</rdg>
          </app>
rough, but she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0894"/>
awluz

          <app from="pr0894" n="53.5 (174.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2520">
            <lem wit="A">awluz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">always</rdg>
          </app>
said she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0895"/>
wouldn’

          <app from="pr0895" n="53.6 (174.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2521">
            <lem wit="A">wouldn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">wouldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0018"/>
sell me down to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0896"/>
Orleans

          <ptr target="#as0070" type="an" xml:id="sa0018"/>
. But

          <app from="pr0896" n="53.6 (174.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la2522">
            <lem wit="A">Orleans. But</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Orleans.—

              <lb/>
But

            </rdg>
          </app>
I noticed dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0897"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr0897" n="53.6 (174.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2523">
            <lem wit="A">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
a nigger trader

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0898"/>
roun’

          <app from="pr0898" n="53.7 (174.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2524">
            <lem wit="A">roun’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">around</rdg>
          </app>
de place considable, lately,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0899"/>
en

          <app from="pr0899" n="53.7 (174.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2525">
            <lem wit="A">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
I begin to git oneasy. Well, one night I creeps to de do’,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0900"/>
pooty

          <app from="pr0900" n="53.8 (175.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2526">
            <lem wit="A">pooty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pretty</rdg>
          </app>
late,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0551"/>
en

          <ptr target="#la9126" type="alt" xml:id="te0551"/>
de do’ warn’t quite shet,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0901"/>
en

          <app from="pr0901" n="53.9 (175.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2527">
            <lem wit="A">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
I hear ole missus tell de widder she gwyne to sell me down to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0552"/>
Orleans,

          <ptr target="#la9127" type="alt" xml:id="te0552"/>
but she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0902"/>
didn’

          <app from="pr0902" n="53.10 (175.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2528">
            <lem wit="A">didn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
want to, but she could git

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ah0019"/>
eight

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0903"/>
hund’d

          <app from="pr0903" n="53.11 (175.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2529">
            <lem wit="A">hund’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hundred</rdg>
          </app>
dollars for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0904"/>
me

          <app from="pr0904" n="53.11 (175.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2530">
            <lem wit="MS1a">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">me,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0071" type="an" xml:id="sa0019"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0905"/>
en

          <app from="pr0905" n="53.11 (175.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2531">
            <lem wit="A">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0906"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr0906" n="53.11 (175.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2532">
            <lem wit="A">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
sich a big stack

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr0907"/>
o’

          <app from="pr0907" n="53.11 (175.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2533">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
money she

