be glad

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0715"/>
er

          <ptr target="#la9430" type="alt" xml:id="te0715"/>
de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0716"/>
chanst

          <ptr target="#la9432" type="alt" xml:id="te0716"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16617">
“Well, it’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0717"/>
all

          <ptr target="#la9434" type="alt" xml:id="te0717"/>
right, anyway, Jim,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1124"/>
long

          <app from="pr1124" n="57.11 (191.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2762">
            <lem wit="A">long</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">as long</rdg>
          </app>
as you’re going to be rich again some time or other.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16631">
“Yes—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0718"/>
en

          <ptr target="#la9436" type="alt" xml:id="te0718"/>
I’s rich now, come to look at it. I owns

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1125"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0719"/>
mysef

          <ptr target="#la9438" type="alt" xml:id="te0719"/>
          <app from="pr1125" n="57.13 (192.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2763">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">mysef</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">myse’f</rdg>
          </app>
, en I’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1126"/>
wuth

          <app from="pr1126" n="57.14 (192.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2764">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wuth</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">worth seben or</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0720"/>
eight

          <ptr target="#la9440" type="alt" xml:id="te0720"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0721"/>
hund’d

          <ptr target="#la9442" type="alt" xml:id="te0721"/>
dollars.

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0026"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1127"/>
I wisht I had de money, I wouldn’ want no mo’.

          <app from="pr1127" n="✱57.14–15 (192.4–6)" type="e" xml:id="la2765">
            <lem wit="A">I wisht . . . wouldn’ . . . mo’.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I wisht . . . wouldn’t . . . mo’.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">But live stock’s too resky, Huck;—I wisht I had de eight hund’d dollars en somebody else had de nigger.</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0026" type="te" xml:id="tv0026"/>
”

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0277">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter IX.</head>
        <pb n="58" xml:id="pb0058"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y05801">
          <graphic url="y05801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1128"/>
Chapter IX.

            <app from="pr1128" n="58 title (192.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2766">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter IX.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1a">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2767">not in; extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf5801">
          <graphic url="hf5801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">exploring the cave</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e16694">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">I wanted</hi>
to go and look at a place

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0722"/>
right

          <ptr target="#la9444" type="alt" xml:id="te0722"/>
about the middle of the island, that I’d found when I was exploring; so we started, and soon got to it, because the island was only three miles long and a quarter of a mile wide.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16702">
This place was a tolerable

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1129"/>
long

          <app from="pr1129" n="58.10 (192.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la2768">
            <lem wit="MS1a">long,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
long

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, steep hill or ridge, about forty foot high. We had a rough time getting to the top, the sides was so steep and the bushes so thick. We tramped and clumb around all over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1130"/>
it

          <app from="pr1130" n="58.15 (193.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2769">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1132"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1132" n="58.16 (193.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2771">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
found a good big cavern in the rock, most up to the top on the side towards Illinois. The cavern was as big as two or three rooms bunched together, and Jim could stand up straight in it. It was cool in there. Jim was for putting our traps in there, right away, but I said we didn’t want to be climbing up and down there all the time.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16729">
Jim said if we had the canoe hid in a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1133"/>
place

          <app from="pr1133" n="58.24 (194.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2772">
            <lem wit="MS1a">place</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">place,</rdg>
          </app>
and had all the traps in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1134"/>
cavern

          <app from="pr1134" n="58.25 (194.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la2773">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cavern</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cavern,</rdg>
          </app>
we could rush there if anybody was to come to the island, and they would never find us without dogs. And besides, he said them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0723"/>
little

          <ptr target="#la9446" type="alt" xml:id="te0723"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0724"/>
birds

          <ptr target="#la9448" type="alt" xml:id="te0724"/>
had said it was going to rain, and did I want the things to get wet?

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16755">
So we went back and got the canoe and paddled up abreast the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1135"/>
cavern

          <app from="pr1135" n="58.30 (194.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2774">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cavern</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cavern,</rdg>
          </app>
and lugged all the traps up there. Then we hunted up a place close by to hide the canoe in, amongst the thick willows. We took some fish off of the lines and set them again, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1136"/>
begun

          <app from="pr1136" n="58.32 (194.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2775">
            <lem wit="A">begun</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">began</rdg>
          </app>
to get ready for dinner.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16773">
          <pb n="59" xml:id="pb0059"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1137"/>
The

          <app from="pr1137" n="59.1 (195.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2777">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2776">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
The

            </rdg>
          </app>
door of the cavern was big enough to roll a hogshead in, and on one side of the door the floor stuck out a little bit and was flat and a good place to build a fire on. So we built it there and cooked dinner.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16787">
We spread the blankets inside for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pl1137"/>
carpet

          <app from="pl1137" n="59.5 (195.12)" type="hc" xml:id="ln2777">
            <lem wit="MS1a">carpet</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">carpet,</rdg>
          </app>
and eat our dinner in there. We put all the other things handy at the back of the cavern. Pretty soon it darkened up and begun to thunder and lighten; so the birds was right about it. Directly it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1138"/>
begun

          <app from="pr1138" n="59.8 (195.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2778">
            <lem wit="A">begun</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">began</rdg>
          </app>
to rain, and it rained like all fury,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0725"/>
too,

          <ptr target="#la9450" type="alt" xml:id="te0725"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1139"/>
I

          <app from="pr1139" n="59.9 (195.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2779">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you</rdg>
          </app>
never

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1140"/>
see

          <app from="pr1140" n="59.9 (196.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2780">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
the wind blow so. It was one of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0726"/>
these

          <ptr target="#la9452" type="alt" xml:id="te0726"/>
regular summer storms. It would get so dark that it looked all blue-black outside, and lovely; and the rain would thrash along by so thick

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0727"/>
that

          <ptr target="#la9454" type="alt" xml:id="te0727"/>
the trees off a little ways looked dim and spider-webby; and here would come a blast of wind that would bend the trees down and turn up the pale

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1141"/>
underside

          <app from="pr1141" n="59.14 (196.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la2781">
            <lem wit="A">underside</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
under-

              <lb/>
side

            </rdg>
          </app>
of the leaves; and then a perfect ripper of a gust would follow along and set the branches to tossing their arms as if they was just wild; and next, when it was just about the bluest and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1142"/>
blackest

          <app from="pr1142" n="59.17 (197.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2782">
            <lem wit="A">blackest—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">blackest,</rdg>
          </app>
—

          <hi rend="italic">fst!</hi>
it was as bright as glory and you’d have a little glimpse of tree-tops

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0728"/>
a-plunging about,

          <ptr target="#la9456" type="alt" xml:id="te0728"/>
away off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0729"/>
yonder

          <ptr target="#la9458" type="alt" xml:id="te0729"/>
in the storm, hundreds of yards further than you could see before; dark as sin again in a second, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0730"/>
now

          <ptr target="#la9460" type="alt" xml:id="te0730"/>
you’d hear the thunder let go with an awful crash and then go rumbling, grumbling, tumbling down the sky towards the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1143"/>
underside

          <app from="pr1143" n="59.22 (197.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2783">
            <lem wit="MS1a">underside</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">under side</rdg>
          </app>
of the world, like rolling empty barrels

          <pb n="60" xml:id="pb0060"/>
down stairs, where it’s long stairs and they bounce a good deal, you know.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y05901">
          <graphic url="y05901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">in the cave</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16886">
“Jim, this is

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0731"/>
nice,” I

          <ptr target="#la9462" type="alt" xml:id="te0731"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1144"/>
says

          <app from="pr1144" n="60.3 (198.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2784">
            <lem wit="A">says.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">says;</rdg>
          </app>
. “I wouldn’t want to be nowhere else

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1145"/>
but

          <app from="pr1145" n="60.4 (198.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2785">
            <lem wit="A">but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">than</rdg>
          </app>
here. Pass me along another

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1146"/>
hunk

          <app from="pr1146" n="60.4 (198.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2786">
            <lem wit="A">hunk</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">piece</rdg>
          </app>
of fish and some hot corn-bread.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16916">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="vn0001"/>
“Well, you wouldn’t a ben here,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1147"/>
’f

          <app from="pr1147" n="60.6 (198.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2787">
            <lem wit="A">’f</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">if</rdg>
          </app>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1148"/>
hadn’t a

          <app from="pr1148" n="60.6 (198.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2788">
            <lem wit="A">hadn’t a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hadn’t</rdg>
          </app>
ben for Jim. You’d a ben down dah in de woods widout any dinner,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1149"/>
en

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0732"/>
gittn’

          <ptr target="#la9464" type="alt" xml:id="te0732"/>
mos’

          <app from="pr1149" n="60.7 (198.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la2789">
            <lem wit="A">en gittn’ mos’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and gittin’ most</rdg>
          </app>
drownded, too, dat you would, honey. Chickens knows when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1150"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr1150" n="60.8 (198.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2790">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">its</rdg>
          </app>
gwyne to rain,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0733"/>
en

          <ptr target="#la9466" type="alt" xml:id="te0733"/>
so do de birds,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1151"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0734"/>
chile.”

          <ptr target="#la9468" type="alt" xml:id="te0734"/>
          <ptr target="#as0082" type="an" xml:id="nv0001"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e16966">
The river

          <app from="pr1151" n="60.9–10 (198.15–214.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2791">
            <lem wit="A">chile.” [¶] The river</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
child.” [¶] “I been . . . agin.”

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2792">extra line space</note>
[¶] The river

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2793">
see

                <ref corresp="#la0541" type="chapterref">Appendix C</ref>
, pp. 534–38, for full text of rejected passage

              </note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0880"/>
on raising

          <ptr target="#la9760" type="alt" xml:id="te0880"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0881"/>
and raising for ten or twelve days,

          <ptr target="#la9762" type="alt" xml:id="te0881"/>
till at last it was over the banks. The water was three or four

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1152"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0882"/>
foot

          <ptr target="#la9764" type="alt" xml:id="te0882"/>
          <app from="pr1152" n="60.11 (214.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2794">
            <lem wit="A">foot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
feet/

              <add>foot</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
deep on the island

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1153"/>
in the low places

          <app from="pr1153" n="60.12 (214.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2795">
            <lem wit="A">in . . . places</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2796">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and on the Illinois bottom. On

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1154"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0883"/>
that side

          <ptr target="#la9766" type="alt" xml:id="te0883"/>
          <app from="pr1154" n="60.12–13 (214.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la2797">
            <lem wit="A">that side</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that side (the east side)</rdg>
          </app>
it was a good many miles wide; but on the Missouri side it was the same old distance across—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1155"/>
a half

          <app from="pr1155" n="60.14 (214.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2798">
            <lem wit="A">a half</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">half</rdg>
          </app>
a mile—because the Missouri shore was just a wall of high

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1156"/>
bluffs.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17032">
Daytimes

          <app from="pr1156" n="60.15–16 (214.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la2799">
            <lem wit="A">bluffs. [¶] Daytimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
bluffs.—

              <lb/>
[¶] Daytimes

            </rdg>
          </app>
we paddled all over the island in the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0884"/>
canoe.

          <ptr target="#la9768" type="alt" xml:id="te0884"/>
It was mighty cool and shady in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0885"/>
the deep

          <ptr target="#la9770" type="alt" xml:id="te0885"/>
woods even if the sun was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0886"/>
blazing

          <ptr target="#la9772" type="alt" xml:id="te0886"/>
outside. We went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0887"/>
winding

          <ptr target="#la9774" type="alt" xml:id="te0887"/>
in and out amongst the trees; and sometimes the vines hung so thick we had to back away and go some other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1157"/>
way

          <app from="pr1157" n="60.20 (215.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2800">
            <lem wit="A">way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">course</rdg>
          </app>
. Well, on every old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1158"/>
broken-down

          <app from="pr1158" n="60.20 (215.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2801">
            <lem wit="A">broken-down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">broke-down</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1159"/>
tree

          <app from="pr1159" n="60.20 (215.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la2802">
            <lem wit="MS1a">tree</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tree,</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1160"/>
could

          <app from="pr1160" n="60.20 (215.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2803">
            <lem wit="A">could</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">would</rdg>
          </app>
see rabbits, and snakes, and such things; and when the island had been overflowed a day or

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0888"/>
two,

          <ptr target="#la9776" type="alt" xml:id="te0888"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1161"/>
they

          <app from="pr1161" n="60.22 (215.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2804">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">the wild creatures</rdg>
          </app>
got so tame, on account of being hungry, that you could paddle right up and put your hand on them if you wanted to; but not the snakes

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0889"/>
and turtles

          <ptr target="#la9778" type="alt" xml:id="te0889"/>
—they would slide off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1162"/>
in

          <app from="pr1162" n="60.24 (215.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2805">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">into</rdg>
          </app>
the water. The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1163"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0890"/>
ridge

          <ptr target="#la9780" type="alt" xml:id="te0890"/>
          <app from="pr1163" n="60.25 (215.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2806">
            <lem wit="A">ridge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">high ridge</rdg>
          </app>
our cavern was in, was full of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0891"/>
them.

          <ptr target="#la9782" type="alt" xml:id="te0891"/>
We could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1164"/>
a

          <app from="pr1164" n="60.26 (215.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2807">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">have</rdg>
          </app>
had pets enough if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0892"/>
we’d

          <ptr target="#la9784" type="alt" xml:id="te0892"/>
wanted them.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17143">
One night we catched a little section of a lumber raft—nice pine planks. It was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0893"/>
twelve foot

          <ptr target="#la9786" type="alt" xml:id="te0893"/>
wide and about fifteen or sixteen foot long, and the top stood above water six or seven inches, a solid level floor. We could see saw-logs go by in the daylight, sometimes, but we let them go; we didn’t show ourselves in daylight.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17149">
Another night, when we was up at the head of the island,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0894"/>
just before daylight,

          <ptr target="#la9788" type="alt" xml:id="te0894"/>
here comes a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1165"/>
frame

          <app from="pr1165" n="60.33 (216.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2808">
            <lem wit="A">frame</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">small frame</rdg>
          </app>
house down, on the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0895"/>
west

          <ptr target="#la9790" type="alt" xml:id="te0895"/>
side. She was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1166"/>
two-story

          <app from="pr1166" n="60.34 (216.21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la2809">
            <lem wit="A">two-story</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">two-story-and-a half</rdg>
          </app>
, and tilted over,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0896"/>
considerable

          <ptr target="#la9792" type="alt" xml:id="te0896"/>
. We paddled out and got aboard—clumb in at an up-stairs

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0897"/>
window

          <ptr target="#la9794" type="alt" xml:id="te0897"/>
. But it was too dark to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1167"/>
see,

          <app from="pr1167" n="60.36 (217.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2810">
            <lem wit="MS1a">see,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
see

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet, so we made the canoe fast and set in her to wait for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1168"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr1168" n="60.37 (217.7–9)" type="e" xml:id="la2811">
            <lem wit="A">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">daylight; and besides there was a smell in there that warn’t agreeable</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y06101">
          <graphic url="y06101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">jim sees a dead man</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17206">
The light begun to come before we got to the foot of the island.

          <pb n="61" xml:id="pb0061"/>
Then we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1169"/>
looked

          <app from="pr1169" n="61.1 (217.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2812">
            <lem wit="A">looked</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">begun to look</rdg>
          </app>
in at the window. We could make out a bed, and a table, and two old chairs, and lots of things around about on the floor; and there was clothes hanging against the wall. There was something laying on the floor in the far corner that looked like a man. So

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0027"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1170"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0898"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la9796" type="alt" xml:id="te0898"/>
          <app from="pr1170" n="✱61.5 (218.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2813">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jim</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0027" type="te" xml:id="tv0027"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17231">
“Hello,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0899"/>
you!

          <ptr target="#la9798" type="alt" xml:id="te0899"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17237">
But it didn’t budge. So

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0900"/>
I

          <ptr target="#la9800" type="alt" xml:id="te0900"/>
hollered again, and then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0901"/>
Jim

          <ptr target="#la9802" type="alt" xml:id="te0901"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17247">
“De man ain’t asleep

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0902"/>
—he’s

          <ptr target="#la9804" type="alt" xml:id="te0902"/>
dead. You hold still—I’ll go

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0903"/>
en

          <ptr target="#la9806" type="alt" xml:id="te0903"/>
see.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17258">
He went and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0904"/>
bent down and

          <ptr target="#la9808" type="alt" xml:id="te0904"/>
looked, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17264">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0905"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1171"/>
It’s

          <ptr target="#la9810" type="alt" xml:id="te0905"/>
          <app from="pr1171" n="61.10 (218.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2814">
            <lem wit="A">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">My! it’s</rdg>
          </app>
a dead

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1172"/>
man.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0906"/>
Yes

          <app from="pr1172" n="61.10 (218.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2815">
            <lem wit="A">man. Yes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">man, yes</rdg>
          </app>
, indeedy;

          <ptr target="#la9812" type="alt" xml:id="te0906"/>
naked,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1173"/>
too. He’s

          <app from="pr1173" n="61.10 (218.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2816">
            <lem wit="A">too. He’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
too.—

              <lb/>
He’s

            </rdg>
          </app>
ben shot in de back. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1175"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr1175" n="61.11 (218.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2818">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
he’s ben dead two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1176"/>
er

          <app from="pr1176" n="61.11 (218.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2819">
            <lem wit="A">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">or</rdg>
          </app>
three days. Come in, Huck, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1177"/>
doan’

          <app from="pr1177" n="61.12 (218.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2820">
            <lem wit="A">doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">don’t you</rdg>
          </app>
look at his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0907"/>
face

          <ptr target="#la9814" type="alt" xml:id="te0907"/>
—it’s too

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1178"/>
gashly

          <app from="pr1178" n="61.12 (218.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2821">
            <lem wit="A">gashly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dreadful</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17337">
I didn’t look at him at all.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0908"/>
Jim throwed some old rags over him, but he needn’t done it;

          <ptr target="#la9816" type="alt" xml:id="te0908"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1179"/>
I

          <app from="pr1179" n="61.14 (218.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2822">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
didn’t want to see him. There was heaps of old greasy cards scattered around over the floor, and old whisky

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0909"/>
bottles, and a couple of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1180"/>
masks,

          <app from="pr1180" n="61.16 (219.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2823">
            <lem wit="MS1a">masks,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
masks

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1181"/>
out

          <app from="pr1181" n="61.16 (219.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2824">
            <lem wit="A">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2825">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of black cloth;

          <ptr target="#la9818" type="alt" xml:id="te0909"/>
and all over the walls was the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1182"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0910"/>
ignorantest

          <ptr target="#la9820" type="alt" xml:id="te0910"/>
          <app from="pr1182" n="61.17 (219.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2826">
            <lem wit="A">ignorantest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
vulgarest/

              <add>ignorantest</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
kind of words and pictures, made with charcoal. There was two old dirty calico

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1183"/>
dresses

          <app from="pr1183" n="61.18 (219.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la2827">
            <lem wit="MS1a">dresses</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dresses,</rdg>
          </app>
and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1184"/>
sun bonnet

          <app from="pr1184" n="61.18 (219.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2828">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sun bonnet</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sun-bonnet,</rdg>
          </app>
and some women’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1185"/>
under-clothes

          <app from="pr1185" n="61.19 (219.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la2829">
            <lem wit="MS1a">under-clothes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">under-clothes,</rdg>
          </app>
hanging against the wall, and some men’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1186"/>
clothing

          <app from="pr1186" n="61.20 (219.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2830">
            <lem wit="A">clothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">clothes</rdg>
          </app>
, too. We put the lot into the canoe; it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1187"/>
might

          <app from="pr1187" n="61.20 (219.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2831">
            <lem wit="A">might</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">might all</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="62" xml:id="pb0062"/>
come good. There was a boy’s old speckled straw hat on the floor; I took

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1188"/>
that,

          <app from="pr1188" n="62.2 (219.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2832">
            <lem wit="MS1a">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too. And there was a bottle that had had milk in it; and it had a rag

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1189"/>
stopper

          <app from="pr1189" n="62.3 (219.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2833">
            <lem wit="A">stopper</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">stopper that they call a “sugar teat,”</rdg>
          </app>
for a baby to suck. We would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1190"/>
a took

          <app from="pr1190" n="62.3 (219.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2834">
            <lem wit="A">a took</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">have took</rdg>
          </app>
the bottle,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1191"/>
but

          <app from="pr1191" n="62.3 (220.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2835">
            <lem wit="A">but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">but we found</rdg>
          </app>
it was broke. There was a seedy old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1192"/>
chest

          <app from="pr1192" n="62.4 (220.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2836">
            <lem wit="MS1a">chest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">chest,</rdg>
          </app>
and an old hair trunk with the hinges broke. They stood open,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1193"/>
but there warn’t

          <app from="pr1193" n="62.5 (220.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2837">
            <lem wit="A">but there warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and</rdg>
          </app>
nothing left in them that was any account. The way things was scattered about, we reckoned the people left in a hurry and warn’t fixed so as to carry off most of their stuff.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17479">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="vn0002"/>
We got an old tin lantern, and a butcher knife without any handle,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1194"/>
and a bran-new Barlow knife worth two bits in any store,

          <app from="pr1194" n="62.10 (220.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2838">
            <lem wit="A">and a bran-new . . . store,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2839">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and a lot of tallow candles, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0911"/>
a tin candlestick, and

          <ptr target="#la9822" type="alt" xml:id="te0911"/>
a gourd, and a tin cup, and a ratty old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1195"/>
bed quilt

          <app from="pr1195" n="62.12 (220.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la2840">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bed quilt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">bed-quilt</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1196"/>
off

          <app from="pr1196" n="62.12 (220.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2841">
            <lem wit="A">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">off of</rdg>
          </app>
the bed, and a reticule with needles and pins and beeswax and buttons and thread

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1197"/>
and all such truck

          <app from="pr1197" n="62.13 (220.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2842">
            <lem wit="A">and all such truck</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2843">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in it, and a hatchet and some nails, and a fish-line as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0912"/>
thick

          <ptr target="#la9824" type="alt" xml:id="te0912"/>
as my little finger, with some monstrous hooks on it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0913"/>
and a roll of buckskin,

          <ptr target="#la9826" type="alt" xml:id="te0913"/>
and a leather dog-collar, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1198"/>
horseshoe

          <app from="pr1198" n="62.16 (221.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2844">
            <lem wit="MS1a">horseshoe</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">horse-shoe</rdg>
          </app>
, and some vials of medicine that didn’t have no label on them; and just as we was leaving I found a tolerable good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1199"/>
curry-comb

          <app from="pr1199" n="62.18 (221.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2845">
            <lem wit="C">curry-comb</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
curry-

              <lb/>
comb

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">curry-comb,</rdg>
          </app>
and Jim he found a ratty old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1200"/>
fiddle-bow

          <app from="pr1200" n="62.18–19 (221.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la2846">
            <lem wit="MS1a">fiddle-bow</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fiddle-bow,</rdg>
          </app>
and a wooden leg. The straps was broke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1201"/>
off of

          <app from="pr1201" n="62.19 (221.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2847">
            <lem wit="A">off of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">off</rdg>
          </app>
it, but barring that, it was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0914"/>
a

          <ptr target="#la9828" type="alt" xml:id="te0914"/>
good

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0915"/>
enough

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1202"/>
leg,

          <ptr target="#la9830" type="alt" xml:id="te0915"/>
though it was too long for me and not long enough for Jim, and we couldn’t find the other one, though we hunted all around

          <app from="pr1202" n="62.20–22 (221.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2848">
            <lem wit="A">leg, though . . . around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">leg</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0083" type="an" xml:id="nv0002"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17584">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1203"/>
And so, take

          <app from="pr1203" n="62.23 (221.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2849">
            <lem wit="A">And so, take</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Take</rdg>
          </app>
it all around, we made a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0916"/>
good

          <ptr target="#la9832" type="alt" xml:id="te0916"/>
haul.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0917"/>
When

          <ptr target="#la9834" type="alt" xml:id="te0917"/>
we was ready to shove

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1204"/>
off

          <app from="pr1204" n="62.24 (221.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2850">
            <lem wit="MS1a">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">off,</rdg>
          </app>
we was a quarter of a mile below the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1205"/>
island

          <app from="pr1205" n="62.24 (222.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la2851">
            <lem wit="MS1a">island</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">island,</rdg>
          </app>
and it was pretty broad day; so I made Jim lay down in the canoe and cover up with the quilt,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0918"/>
because

          <ptr target="#la9836" type="alt" xml:id="te0918"/>
if he set

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1206"/>
up,

          <app from="pr1206" n="62.26 (222.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2852">
            <lem wit="A">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
people could tell he was a nigger a good ways off. I paddled over to the Illinois shore, and drifted down most a half a mile doing it. I crept up the dead water under the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1207"/>
bank

          <app from="pr1207" n="62.29 (222.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2853">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bank</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">bank,</rdg>
          </app>
and hadn’t no accidents and didn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1208"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr1208" n="62.29 (222.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2854">
            <lem wit="A">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
. We got home all safe.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0281">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter X.</head>
        <pb n="63" xml:id="pb0063"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17651">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y06301">
            <graphic url="y06301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1209"/>
Chapter X.

              <app from="pr1209" n="63 title (222.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2855">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter X.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2856">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf6301">
            <graphic url="hf6301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">they found eight dollars</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e17667">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">After</hi>
breakfast I wanted to talk about the dead man and guess out how he come to be killed, but Jim didn’t want to. He said it would fetch bad luck; and besides, he said, he might come and ha’nt us; he said a man that warn’t buried was more likely to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0919"/>
go a-ha’nting

          <ptr target="#la9838" type="alt" xml:id="te0919"/>
around than one that was planted and comfortable. That sounded pretty reasonable, so I didn’t say no more; but I couldn’t keep from studying over it and wishing I knowed who shot the man, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0920"/>
what

          <ptr target="#la9840" type="alt" xml:id="te0920"/>
they done it for.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17679">
We rummaged the clothes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1210"/>
we’d

          <app from="pr1210" n="63.18 (223.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2857">
            <lem wit="A">we’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">we had</rdg>
          </app>
got, and found

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0921"/>
eight

          <ptr target="#la9842" type="alt" xml:id="te0921"/>
dollars in silver sewed up in the lining of an old blanket

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1211"/>
overcoat

          <app from="pr1211" n="63.19 (224.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la2858">
            <lem wit="C">overcoat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">
over-

              <lb/>
coat

            </rdg>
          </app>
. Jim said he reckoned the people in that house stole the coat, because if they’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1212"/>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0922"/>
knowed

          <ptr target="#la9844" type="alt" xml:id="te0922"/>
          <app from="pr1212" n="63.20 (224.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2859">
            <lem wit="A">a knowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
known/

              <add>knowed</add>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2860">see Alterations</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the money was there they wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1213"/>
a

          <app from="pr1213" n="63.21 (224.7)" type="e" xml:id="la2861">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2862">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
left it. I said I reckoned they killed him, too; but Jim didn’t want to talk about that. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17729">
“Now you think it’s bad luck; but what did you say when I fetched in the snake-skin that I found on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1214"/>
the top

          <app from="pr1214" n="63.24 (224.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2863">
            <lem wit="A">the top</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">top</rdg>
          </app>
of the ridge day before yesterday? You said it was the

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="vn0003"/>
worst bad luck in the world to touch a snake-skin

          <ptr target="#as0084" type="an" xml:id="nv0003"/>
with my hands. Well, here’s your bad luck! We’ve raked in all this truck and eight dollars besides. I wish we could have some bad luck like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1215"/>
this

          <app from="pr1215" n="63.28 (225.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2864">
            <lem wit="A">this</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that</rdg>
          </app>
every day, Jim.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17752">“Never you mind, honey, never you mind. Don’t you git too peart. It’s a-comin’. Mind I tell you, it’s a-comin’.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17754">
It did come,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1216"/>
too. It

          <app from="pr1216" n="63.31 (225.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2865">
            <lem wit="A">too. It</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
too.—

              <lb/>
It

            </rdg>
          </app>
was a Tuesday that we had that talk. Well,

          <pb n="64" xml:id="pb0064"/>
after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1217"/>
dinner,

          <app from="pr1217" n="64.1 (225.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2866">
            <lem wit="MS1a">dinner,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
dinner

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Friday, we was laying around in the grass at the upper end of the ridge, and got out of tobacco. I went to the cavern to get some, and found a rattlesnake in there. I killed him, and curled him up on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0923"/>
the foot of

          <ptr target="#la9846" type="alt" xml:id="te0923"/>
Jim’s blanket, ever so natural, thinking there’d be some fun when Jim found him there. Well, by night I forgot all about the snake, and when Jim flung himself down on the blanket while I struck a light, the snake’s mate was there, and bit him.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y06401">
          <graphic url="y06401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">jim and the snake</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17786">
He jumped up yelling, and the first thing the light showed was the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0924"/>
varmint

          <ptr target="#la9848" type="alt" xml:id="te0924"/>
curled up and ready for another

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0925"/>
spring

          <ptr target="#la9850" type="alt" xml:id="te0925"/>
. I laid him out in a second with a stick, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0004"/>
Jim grabbed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1218"/>
pap’s

          <app from="pr1218" n="64.10 (226.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2867">
            <lem wit="A">pap’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap’s</rdg>
          </app>
whisky jug and begun to pour it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0926"/>
down

          <ptr target="#as0085" type="an" xml:id="vn0004"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17811">
He

          <ptr target="#la9852" type="alt" xml:id="te0926"/>
was barefooted, and the snake bit him right on the heel. That all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1219"/>
comes

          <app from="pr1219" n="64.13 (227.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2868">
            <lem wit="A">comes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">come</rdg>
          </app>
of my being such a fool as to not remember that

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0005"/>
wherever you leave a dead snake its mate always comes

          <ptr target="#as0086" type="an" xml:id="vn0005"/>
there and curls around

          <pb n="65" xml:id="pb0065"/>
it. Jim told me to chop off the snake’s head and throw it away, and then skin the body and roast a piece of it. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1220"/>
done it

          <app from="pr1220" n="65.2 (227.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2869">
            <lem wit="MS1a">done it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">done it,</rdg>
          </app>
and he eat it and said it would help

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0927"/>
cure

          <ptr target="#la9854" type="alt" xml:id="te0927"/>
him. He made me take off the rattles and tie them around his wrist, too.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0928"/>
He said that that would help.

          <ptr target="#la9856" type="alt" xml:id="te0928"/>
Then I slid out quiet and throwed the snakes clear away amongst the bushes; for I warn’t going to let Jim find out it was all my fault, not if I could help it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17848">
Jim sucked and sucked at the jug, and now and then he got out of his head and pitched around and yelled; but every time he come to himself he went to sucking at the jug again. His foot swelled up pretty big, and so did his leg; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1221"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1221" n="65.11 (228.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2870">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
the drunk begun to come, and so I judged he was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1222"/>
right; but I’d druther been bit with a snake than pap’s whisky

          <app from="pr1222" n="65.12–13 (228.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2871">
            <lem wit="A">right; but . . . whisky</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">right</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y06601">
          <graphic url="y06601.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">old hank bunker</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17871">
Jim was laid up for four days and nights. Then the swelling was all gone and he was around again. I made up my mind I wouldn’t ever take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1223"/>
aholt

          <app from="pr1223" n="65.16 (228.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2872">
            <lem wit="A">aholt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hold</rdg>
          </app>
of a snake-skin again with my hands, now that I see what had come of it. Jim said he reckoned I would believe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1224"/>
him,

          <app from="pr1224" n="65.17 (229.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la2873">
            <lem wit="MS1a">him,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
him

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
next time. And he said that handling a snake-skin was such awful bad luck that maybe we hadn’t got to the end of it yet. He said he druther

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0006"/>
see the new moon over his left shoulder

          <ptr target="#as0087" type="an" xml:id="vn0006"/>
as much as a thousand times than take up a snake-skin in his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1225"/>
hand

          <app from="pr1225" n="65.21 (229.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2874">
            <lem wit="A">hand</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hands</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1226"/>
Well

          <app from="pr1226" n="65.21 (229.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la2875">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
I was getting to feel that way myself, though I’ve always reckoned that looking at the new moon over your left shoulder is one of the carelessest and foolishest things a body can do. Old Hank Bunker done it once, and bragged about it; and in less than two years he got drunk and fell off of the shot tower and spread himself out so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0929"/>
that

          <ptr target="#la9858" type="alt" xml:id="te0929"/>
he was just a kind of a layer, as you may say; and they slid him edgeways between two barn doors for a coffin,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0930"/>
and buried him so,

          <ptr target="#la9860" type="alt" xml:id="te0930"/>
so they say, but I didn’t see it. Pap told me. But anyway, it all come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0931"/>
of

          <ptr target="#la9862" type="alt" xml:id="te0931"/>
looking at the moon that way, like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1227"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0932"/>
fool

          <ptr target="#la9864" type="alt" xml:id="te0932"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e17929">
Well

          <app from="pr1227" n="65.30–31 (230.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la2876">
            <lem wit="A">fool. [¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
fool.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2877">extra line space</note>
[¶] Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, the days went along, and the river went down between its banks again; and about the first thing we done was to bait one of the big hooks with a skinned rabbit

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0933"/>
and set it

          <ptr target="#la9866" type="alt" xml:id="te0933"/>
and catch a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0007"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1228"/>
catfish

          <app from="pr1228" n="65.33 (231.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2878">
            <lem wit="MS1a">catfish</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cat-fish</rdg>
          </app>
that was as big as a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1229"/>
man

          <app from="pr1229" n="65.34 (231.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2879">
            <lem wit="A">man</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">big man</rdg>
          </app>
, being six foot two inches long, and weighed over two hundred pounds

          <ptr target="#as0088" type="an" xml:id="vn0007"/>
. We couldn’t handle him, of course; he would a flung us into Illinois. We

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0934"/>
just

          <ptr target="#la9868" type="alt" xml:id="te0934"/>
set there and watched him rip and tear around till he drownded. We found a brass button in his stomach, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1230"/>
round

          <app from="pr1230" n="65.38 (231.17)" type="e" xml:id="la2880">
            <lem wit="A">round</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">round hard</rdg>
          </app>
ball, and lots of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1231"/>
rubbage

          <app from="pr1231" n="65.38 (231.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2881">
            <lem wit="A">rubbage</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">rubbish</rdg>
          </app>
. We split the ball open

          <pb n="66" xml:id="pb0066"/>
with the hatchet, and there was a spool in it. Jim said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1232"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr1232" n="66.1 (231.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2882">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he had</rdg>
          </app>
had it there a long time, to coat it over so and make a ball of it. It was as big a fish as was ever catched in the Mississippi, I reckon. Jim said he hadn’t ever seen a bigger one. He would a been worth a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1233"/>
deal

          <app from="pr1233" n="66.4 (232.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2883">
            <lem wit="MS1a">deal,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
deal

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, over at the village. They peddle out such a fish as that by the pound in the market house there; everybody buys some of him; his meat’s as white as snow and makes a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1234"/>
good

          <app from="pr1234" n="66.7 (232.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la2884">
            <lem wit="A">good</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">wonderful good</rdg>
          </app>
fry.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y06701">
          <graphic url="y06701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">a fair fit.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18018">
Next morning I said it was getting

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0935"/>
slow

          <ptr target="#la9870" type="alt" xml:id="te0935"/>
and dull, and I wanted to get a stirring up, some way. I said I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1235"/>
reckoned

          <app from="pr1235" n="66.9 (232.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2885">
            <lem wit="A">reckoned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">reckond</rdg>
          </app>
I would slip over the river and find out what was going on. Jim liked that notion; but he said I must go in the dark and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0936"/>
look

          <ptr target="#la9872" type="alt" xml:id="te0936"/>
sharp. Then he studied it over and said, couldn’t I put on some of them old things and dress up like a girl? That was a good notion, too. So we shortened up one of the calico gowns and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0937"/>
turned up

          <ptr target="#la9874" type="alt" xml:id="te0937"/>
my trowser-legs

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0938"/>
to

          <ptr target="#la9876" type="alt" xml:id="te0938"/>
my knees and got into it. Jim hitched it behind with the hooks, and it was a fair fit. I put on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1236"/>
sun bonnet

          <app from="pr1236" n="66.16 (233.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la2886">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sun bonnet</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sun-bonnet</rdg>
          </app>
and tied it under my chin, and then for a body

          <pb n="67" xml:id="pb0067"/>
to look in and see my face was like looking down a joint of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1237"/>
stovepipe. Jim

          <app from="pr1237" n="67.1–2 (234.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la2887">
            <lem wit="A">stove-pipe. Jim</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
stove-pipe.—

              <lb/>
Jim

            </rdg>
          </app>
said nobody would know

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0939"/>
me, even

          <ptr target="#la9878" type="alt" xml:id="te0939"/>
in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1238"/>
daytime

          <app from="pr1238" n="67.2 (234.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la2888">
            <lem wit="A">daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
day-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
          </app>
, hardly. I practiced around all day to get the hang of the things, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1239"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1239" n="67.3–4 (234.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2889">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I could do pretty well in them, only Jim said I didn’t walk like a girl; and he said I must quit pulling up my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1240"/>
gown

          <app from="pr1240" n="67.5 (234.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2890">
            <lem wit="A">gown</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">clothes</rdg>
          </app>
to get at my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1241"/>
britches

          <app from="pr1241" n="67.5 (234.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2891">
            <lem wit="A">britches</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">breeches</rdg>
          </app>
pocket. I took notice, and done better.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18106">
I started up the Illinois shore in the canoe just after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1242"/>
dark.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18110">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0013"/>
I

          <app from="pr1242" n="67.7–8 (234.18–235.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2892">
            <lem wit="A">dark. [¶] I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
dark.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] I

            </rdg>
          </app>
started across

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0940"/>
to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1243"/>
town

          <app from="pr1243" n="67.8 (235.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2893">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#la9880" type="alt" xml:id="te0940"/>
from a little below the ferry landing,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1244"/>
and

          <app from="pr1244" n="67.9 (235.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2894">
            <lem wit="A">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">so that</rdg>
          </app>
the drift of the current

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1245"/>
fetched

          <app from="pr1245" n="67.9 (235.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2895">
            <lem wit="A">fetched</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">would fetch</rdg>
          </app>
me in at the bottom of the town. I tied up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0941"/>
and

          <ptr target="#la9882" type="alt" xml:id="te0941"/>
started along the bank. There was a light burning in a little shanty that hadn’t been lived in for a long time, and I wondered

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1246"/>
who

          <app from="pr1246" n="67.12 (235.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2896">
            <lem wit="A">who</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">who it was that</rdg>
          </app>
had took up quarters

          <ptr target="#mt0013" type="alt" xml:id="wn0013"/>
there. I slipped up and peeped in at the window. There was a woman about forty year

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1247"/>
old,

          <app from="pr1247" n="67.13 (236.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2897">
            <lem wit="MS1a">old,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
old

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in there, knitting by a candle that was on a pine table. I didn’t know her face; she was a stranger, for you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1248"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr1248" n="67.15 (236.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2898">
            <lem wit="A">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">could n’t</rdg>
          </app>
start a face in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1249"/>
that town

          <app from="pr1249" n="67.15 (236.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2899">
            <lem wit="A">that town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">the village</rdg>
          </app>
that I didn’t know. Now this was lucky, because I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0942"/>
weakening

          <ptr target="#la9884" type="alt" xml:id="te0942"/>
; I was getting afraid I had come; people might know my voice and find me out. But if this woman had been in such a little town two days she could tell me all I wanted to know; so I knocked at the door, and made up my mind I wouldn’t forget I was a girl.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0286">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XI.</head>
        <pb n="68" xml:id="pb0068"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18197">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y06801">
            <graphic url="y06801.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1250"/>
Chapter XI.

              <app from="pr1250" n="68 title (237.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2900">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XI.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2901">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf6801">
            <graphic url="hf6801.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">come in.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e18214">
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0028"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">
Come

            <ptr target="#tb0028" type="te" xml:id="tv0028"/>
in

          </hi>
,” says the woman, and I did. She says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18221">
“Take a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0943"/>
cheer.”

          <ptr target="#la9886" type="alt" xml:id="te0943"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18226">I done it. She looked me all over with her little shiny eyes, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18228">“What might your name be?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18230">“Sarah Williams.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18232">
“Where

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1251"/>
’bouts

          <app from="pr1251" n="68.9 (237.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2902">
            <lem wit="A">’bouts</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">abouts</rdg>
          </app>
do you live? In this neighborhood?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18242">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1252"/>
No’m

          <app from="pr1252" n="68.11 (237.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2903">
            <lem wit="A">No’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">No mum</rdg>
          </app>
. In

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0009"/>
Hookerville, seven mile below

          <ptr target="#as0089" type="an" xml:id="vn0009"/>
. I’ve walked all the way and I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1253"/>
all tired

          <app from="pr1253" n="68.13 (237.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2904">
            <lem wit="A">all tired</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">tired</rdg>
          </app>
out.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18265">“Hungry, too, I reckon. I’ll find you something.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18268">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1254"/>
No’m

          <app from="pr1254" n="68.16 (237.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2905">
            <lem wit="A">No’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">No mum</rdg>
          </app>
, I ain’t hungry. I was so hungry I had to stop two mile below here at a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0944"/>
farm;

          <ptr target="#la9888" type="alt" xml:id="te0944"/>
so I ain’t hungry no more. It’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0945"/>
what

          <ptr target="#la9890" type="alt" xml:id="te0945"/>
makes me so late. My mother’s down sick, and out of money and everything, and I come to tell my uncle Abner Moore. He lives at the upper end of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1255"/>
the town

          <app from="pr1255" n="68.21 (238.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2906">
            <lem wit="A">the town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">town</rdg>
          </app>
, she says. I hain’t ever been here before. Do you know him?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18295">
“No; but I don’t know everybody yet. I haven’t lived here

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0946"/>
quite

          <ptr target="#la9892" type="alt" xml:id="te0946"/>
two

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0947"/>
weeks.

          <ptr target="#la9894" type="alt" xml:id="te0947"/>
It’s a considerable ways to the upper end of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1256"/>
the town

          <app from="pr1256" n="68.24 (238.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2907">
            <lem wit="A">the town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">town</rdg>
          </app>
. You better stay here all night. Take off your bonnet.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18314">
“No,” I says, “I’ll rest a while, I reckon, and go on. I ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0948"/>
afeard

          <ptr target="#la9896" type="alt" xml:id="te0948"/>
of the dark.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18320">
She said she wouldn’t let me go by myself, but her husband would be in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1257"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1257" n="68.29 (239.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2908">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
by-

              <lb/>
and-by

            </rdg>
          </app>
, maybe in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1258"/>
a hour

          <app from="pr1258" n="68.29 (239.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2909">
            <lem wit="A">a hour</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">an hour</rdg>
          </app>
and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1259"/>
half,

          <app from="pr1259" n="68.29 (239.10)" type="e" xml:id="la2910">
            <lem wit="A">half,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
half

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1260"/>
she’d

          <app from="pr1260" n="68.29 (239.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la2911">
            <lem wit="A">she’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">she would</rdg>
          </app>
send him along with me. Then she got to talking about her husband, and about her relations up the river, and her relations down the river, and about how much better off they used to was, and how they didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0949"/>
know

          <ptr target="#la9898" type="alt" xml:id="te0949"/>
          <pb n="69" xml:id="pb0069"/>
but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1261"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr1261" n="69.1 (239.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2912">
            <lem wit="A">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they had</rdg>
          </app>
made a mistake coming to our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1262"/>
town

          <app from="pr1262" n="69.1 (240.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2913">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
, instead of letting

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1263"/>
well

          <app from="pr1263" n="69.2 (240.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2914">
            <lem wit="A">well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">well enough</rdg>
          </app>
alone—and so on and so on, till

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0950"/>
I was

          <ptr target="#la9900" type="alt" xml:id="te0950"/>
afeard

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0951"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
had

          <ptr target="#la9902" type="alt" xml:id="te0951"/>
made a mistake coming to her to find out what was going on in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1264"/>
town

          <app from="pr1264" n="69.3 (240.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2915">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1265"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1265" n="69.4 (240.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la2916">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
she dropped onto

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1266"/>
pap

          <app from="pr1266" n="69.4 (240.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2917">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1267"/>
murder

          <app from="pr1267" n="69.4 (240.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la2918">
            <lem wit="MS1a">murder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">murder,</rdg>
          </app>
and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1268"/>
I was pretty willing to let her clatter

          <app from="pr1268" n="69.4–5 (240.11)" type="e" xml:id="la2919">
            <lem wit="A">I . . . clatter</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">she boomed</rdg>
          </app>
right along. She told about me and Tom Sawyer finding the six thousand dollars (only she got it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1269"/>
ten,)

          <app from="pr1269" n="69.6 (240.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2920">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ten,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
ten

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
)

            </rdg>
          </app>
and all about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1270"/>
pap

          <app from="pr1270" n="69.7 (240.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2921">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
and what a hard lot he was, and what a hard lot I was, and at last she got down to where I was murdered. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18457">
“Who done it? We’ve heard considerable about these goings on, down in Hookerville, but we don’t know who

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1271"/>
’twas

          <app from="pr1271" n="69.10 (241.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2922">
            <lem wit="A">’twas</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it was</rdg>
          </app>
that killed Huck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1272"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0952"/>
Finn.”

          <ptr target="#la9904" type="alt" xml:id="te0952"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18471">
“Well

          <app from="pr1272" n="69.11–12 (241.6–9)" type="e" xml:id="la2923">
            <lem wit="C">Finn.” [¶] “Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Finn.”—

              <lb/>
[¶] “Well

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Finn.” [¶] “Well,</rdg>
          </app>
I reckon there’s a right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0953"/>
smart

          <ptr target="#la9906" type="alt" xml:id="te0953"/>
chance of people

          <hi rend="italic">here</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1273"/>
that’d

          <app from="pr1273" n="69.12–13 (241.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la2924">
            <lem wit="A">that ’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that would</rdg>
          </app>
like to know who killed him. Some thinks old Finn

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0954"/>
done

          <ptr target="#la9908" type="alt" xml:id="te0954"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1274"/>
it,

          <app from="pr1274" n="69.13 (241.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2925">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
himself.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18509">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1275"/>
No—is

          <app from="pr1275" n="69.15 (241.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2926">
            <lem wit="A">No—is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">No! Is</rdg>
          </app>
that so?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18519">“Most everybody thought it at first. He’ll never know how nigh he come to getting lynched. But before night they changed around and judged it was done by a runaway nigger named Jim.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18521">
“Why

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1276"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
—

          <app from="pr1276" n="69.19 (242.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2927">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
—

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
——

            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18537">
I stopped. I reckoned I better keep still. She run

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0955"/>
on,

          <ptr target="#la9910" type="alt" xml:id="te0955"/>
and never

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1277"/>
noticed

          <app from="pr1277" n="69.21 (242.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la2928">
            <lem wit="A">noticed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">noticed that</rdg>
          </app>
I had put in at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1278"/>
all

          <app from="pr1278" n="69.21 (242.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2929">
            <lem wit="A">all.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">all:</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18560">
“The nigger run off the very night Huck Finn was killed. So there’s a reward out for him—three hundred dollars. And there’s a reward out for old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1279"/>
Finn,

          <app from="pr1279" n="69.24 (242.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2930">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Finn,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Finn

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too—two hundred dollars. You see, he come to town the morning after the murder, and told about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1280"/>
it, and was out with ’em on the ferry-boat hunt, and right away after he up

          <app from="pr1280" n="69.25–26 (242.19)" type="e" xml:id="la2931">
            <lem wit="A">it, and was . . . up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it</rdg>
          </app>
and left. Before night they wanted to lynch him, but he was gone, you see. Well, next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1281"/>
day

          <app from="pr1281" n="✱69.31 (243.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2932">
            <lem wit="A">day</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">day,</rdg>
          </app>
they found out the nigger was gone; they found out he hadn’t ben seen

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0956"/>
sence

          <ptr target="#la9912" type="alt" xml:id="te0956"/>
ten o’clock the night the murder was done. So then they put it on him, you see, and while they was full of it,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0029"/>
next day

          <ptr target="#tb0029" type="te" xml:id="tv0029"/>
back comes old Finn and went boo-hooing to Judge Thatcher to get money to hunt for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0957"/>
the

          <ptr target="#la9914" type="alt" xml:id="te0957"/>
nigger all over Illinois with. The judge give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1282"/>
him some

          <app from="pr1282" n="69.33 (243.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2933">
            <lem wit="A">him some</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it to him</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0958"/>
that

          <ptr target="#la9916" type="alt" xml:id="te0958"/>
evening he got drunk and was around till after midnight with a couple of mighty hard looking strangers, and then went off with them. Well, he hain’t come back

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0959"/>
sence

          <ptr target="#la9918" type="alt" xml:id="te0959"/>
, and they ain’t looking for him back till this thing blows over a little, for people

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1283"/>
thinks

          <app from="pr1283" n="69.37 (244.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2934">
            <lem wit="A">thinks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">think</rdg>
          </app>
now that he killed his boy and fixed things

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1284"/>
so

          <app from="pr1284" n="69.38 (244.6)" type="e" xml:id="la2935">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">so as</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0960"/>
folks

          <ptr target="#la9920" type="alt" xml:id="te0960"/>
would think robbers done it, and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1285"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr1285" n="69.38 (244.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2936">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he would</rdg>
          </app>
get

          <pb n="70" xml:id="pb0070"/>
Huck’s money without having to bother a long time with a lawsuit. People

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1286"/>
do say

          <app from="pr1286" n="70.2 (244.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2937">
            <lem wit="A">do say</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">say</rdg>
          </app>
he warn’t any too good to do it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1287"/>
O

          <app from="pr1287" n="70.2 (244.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la2938">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, he’s sly, I reckon. If he don’t come back for a year, he’ll be all right. You can’t prove anything on him, you know; everything will be quieted

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1288"/>
down

          <app from="pr1288" n="70.4 (244.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la2939">
            <lem wit="MS1a">down,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
down

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, then, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1289"/>
he’ll

          <app from="pr1289" n="70.5 (244.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2940">
            <lem wit="A">he’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he will</rdg>
          </app>
walk into Huck’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1290"/>
money as

          <app from="pr1290" n="70.5 (244.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2941">
            <lem wit="A">money as</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">money just as</rdg>
          </app>
easy as nothing.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18690">
“Yes, I reckon so,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1291"/>
’m

          <app from="pr1291" n="70.6 (245.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2942">
            <lem wit="A">’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">mum</rdg>
          </app>
. I don’t see nothing in the way of it. Has everybody quit thinking the nigger done it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18700">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1292"/>
O

          <app from="pr1292" n="70.8 (245.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la2943">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, no, not everybody. A good many

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1293"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0961"/>
thinks

          <app from="pr1293" n="70.8 (245.8)" type="e" xml:id="la2944">
            <lem wit="A">thinks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">think</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#la9922" type="alt" xml:id="te0961"/>
he done it. But they’ll get the nigger pretty soon, now, and maybe they can scare it out of him.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18720">“Why, are they after him yet?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18722">
“Well, you’re innocent, ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1294"/>
you!

          <app from="pr1294" n="70.12 (245.16)" type="e" xml:id="la2945">
            <lem wit="A">you!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you!?</rdg>
          </app>
Does three hundred dollars lay

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1295"/>
round

          <app from="pr1295" n="70.13 (245.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2946">
            <lem wit="A">round</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">around</rdg>
          </app>
every day for people to pick

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1296"/>
up? Some

          <app from="pr1296" n="70.13 (245.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la2947">
            <lem wit="A">up? Some</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
up?—

              <lb/>
Some

            </rdg>
          </app>
folks

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1297"/>
thinks

          <app from="pr1297" n="70.13 (245.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2948">
            <lem wit="A">thinks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">think</rdg>
          </app>
the nigger ain’t far from here. I’m one of them—but I hain’t talked it around. A few days ago I was talking with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1298"/>
an

          <app from="pr1298" n="70.15 (246.3)" type="e" xml:id="la2949">
            <lem wit="A">an</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">the</rdg>
          </app>
old couple that lives next door in the log

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1299"/>
shanty

          <app from="pr1299" n="70.16 (246.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2950">
            <lem wit="MS1a">shanty</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shanty,</rdg>
          </app>
and they happened to say hardly anybody ever goes to that island over yonder that they call

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1300"/>
Jackson’s island

          <app from="pr1300" n="70.17 (246.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la2951">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Jackson’s island</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jackson’s Island</rdg>
          </app>
. Don’t anybody live there? says I. No, nobody, says they. I didn’t say any more, but I done some thinking. I was pretty near certain

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1301"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr1301" n="70.19 (246.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2952">
            <lem wit="A">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I had</rdg>
          </app>
seen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1302"/>
smoke,

          <app from="pr1302" n="70.20 (246.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la2953">
            <lem wit="MS1a">smoke,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
smoke

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
over there,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0962"/>
about the head of the island,

          <ptr target="#la9924" type="alt" xml:id="te0962"/>
a day or two before that, so I says to myself, like as not that nigger’s hiding over there; anyway, says I, it’s worth the trouble to give the place a hunt. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1303"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr1303" n="70.22 (247.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2954">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
seen any smoke

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0963"/>
sence

          <ptr target="#la9926" type="alt" xml:id="te0963"/>
, so I reckon maybe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1304"/>
he’s

          <app from="pr1304" n="70.23 (247.4)" type="e" xml:id="la2955">
            <lem wit="A">he’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he has</rdg>
          </app>
gone, if it was him; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1305"/>
husband’s

          <app from="pr1305" n="70.24 (247.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la2956">
            <lem wit="A">husband’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">husband is</rdg>
          </app>
going over to see—him and another man. He was gone up the river; but he got back to-day and I told him as soon as he got here two hours ago.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18834">
I had got so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1306"/>
uneasy

          <app from="pr1306" n="70.27 (247.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2957">
            <lem wit="A">uneasy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">uneasy that</rdg>
          </app>
I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1307"/>
set

          <app from="pr1307" n="70.27 (247.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2958">
            <lem wit="A">set</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">keep</rdg>
          </app>
still. I had to do something with my hands; so I took up a needle off of the table and went to threading it. My hands shook, and I was making a bad job of it. When the woman stopped talking, I looked up, and she was looking at me pretty curious, and smiling a little. I put down the needle and thread and let on to be interested—and I was, too—and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18852">
“Three hundred dollars is a power of money. I wish

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0964"/>
my

          <ptr target="#la9928" type="alt" xml:id="te0964"/>
mother could get it. Is your husband going over there to-night?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18858">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0965"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1308"/>
O

          <app from="pr1308" n="70.35 (248.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la2959">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes. He

          <ptr target="#la9930" type="alt" xml:id="te0965"/>
went up town with the man I was telling you of, to get a boat and see if they could borrow another gun. They’ll go over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0966"/>
after

          <ptr target="#la9932" type="alt" xml:id="te0966"/>
midnight.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18875">
“Couldn’t they see better if they was to wait till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1309"/>
daytime

          <app from="pr1309" n="70.38 (248.21–249.1)" type="e" xml:id="la2960">
            <lem wit="C">daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
day-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
time

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
day-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18891">
          <pb n="71" xml:id="pb0071"/>
“Yes. And couldn’t the nigger see better, too? After midnight he’ll likely be asleep, and they can slip around through the woods and hunt up his camp fire all the better for the dark, if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1310"/>
he’s

          <app from="pr1310" n="71.3 (249.9)" type="e" xml:id="la2961">
            <lem wit="A">he’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he has</rdg>
          </app>
got one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18902">
“I didn’t think of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0967"/>
that.”

          <ptr target="#la9934" type="alt" xml:id="te0967"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18907">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y07101">
            <graphic url="y07101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">him and another man.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18915">The woman kept looking at me pretty curious, and I didn’t feel a bit comfortable. Pretty soon she says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18917">“What did you say your name was, honey?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18919">“M—Mary Williams.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18921">
Somehow it didn’t seem to me that I said it was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1311"/>
Mary,

          <app from="pr1311" n="71.9 (250.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2962">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Mary,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Mary

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1312"/>
before;

          <app from="pr1312" n="71.9 (250.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la2963">
            <lem wit="MS1a">before;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
before

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
so I didn’t look up; seemed to me I said it was Sarah; so I felt sort of cornered, and was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1313"/>
afeard

          <app from="pr1313" n="71.11 (250.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2964">
            <lem wit="MS1a">afeard</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">afeared</rdg>
          </app>
maybe I was looking it, too. I wished the woman would say something more; the longer she set still, the uneasier I was. But now she says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18946">“Honey, I thought you said it was Sarah when you first come in?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18948">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1314"/>
O

          <app from="pr1314" n="71.15 (250.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la2965">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1315"/>
yes’m

          <app from="pr1315" n="71.15 (250.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2966">
            <lem wit="A">yes’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">yes, mum</rdg>
          </app>
, I did. Sarah Mary Williams. Sarah’s my first name. Some calls me Sarah, some calls me Mary.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18965">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1316"/>
O

          <app from="pr1316" n="71.17 (250.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la2967">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, that’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1317"/>
the

          <app from="pr1317" n="71.17 (250.20)" type="e" xml:id="la2968">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they</rdg>
          </app>
way of it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18983">
          <pb n="72" xml:id="pb0072"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1318"/>
Yes’m

          <app from="pr1318" n="72.1 (250.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2969">
            <lem wit="A">Yes’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Yes, mum</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e18994">
I was feeling better, then, but I wished I was out of there, anyway. I couldn’t look

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1319"/>
up,

          <app from="pr1319" n="72.3 (251.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2970">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19004">
Well, the woman fell to talking about how hard times was, and how poor they had to live, and how the rats was as free as if they owned the place, and so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1320"/>
forth

          <app from="pr1320" n="72.6 (251.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2971">
            <lem wit="MS1a">forth</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">forth,</rdg>
          </app>
and so on, and then I got easy again. She was right about the rats.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1321"/>
You’d

          <app from="pr1321" n="72.7 (251.14)" type="e" xml:id="la2972">
            <lem wit="A">You’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">You would</rdg>
          </app>
see one stick his nose out of a hole in the corner every little while. She said she had to have things handy to throw at them when she was alone, or they wouldn’t give her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1322"/>
no

          <app from="pr1322" n="72.10 (251.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2973">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
peace. She showed me a bar of lead, twisted up into a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0968"/>
knot

          <ptr target="#la9936" type="alt" xml:id="te0968"/>
, and said she was a good shot with it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1323"/>
generly

          <app from="pr1323" n="72.11 (252.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la2974">
            <lem wit="A">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">generally</rdg>
          </app>
, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1324"/>
she’d

          <app from="pr1324" n="72.11 (252.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2975">
            <lem wit="A">she’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">she had</rdg>
          </app>
wrenched her arm a day or two ago, and didn’t know whether she could throw true, now. But she watched for a chance, and directly she banged away at a rat, but she missed him wide, and said “Ouch!” it hurt her arm so. Then she told me to try for the next one. I wanted to be getting away before the old man got back, but of course I didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0969"/>
let on.

          <ptr target="#la9938" type="alt" xml:id="te0969"/>
I got the thing, and the first rat that showed his nose I let

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1325"/>
drive, and if he’d a stayed where he was he’d a been a tolerable sick rat

          <app from="pr1325" n="72.17–18 (253.1–3)" type="e" xml:id="la2976">
            <lem wit="A">drive, and if . . . rat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">drive and only missed him about an inch</rdg>
          </app>
. She said that that was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1326"/>
first rate

          <app from="pr1326" n="72.19 (253.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2977">
            <lem wit="MS1a">first rate</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
first-

              <lb/>
rate

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and she reckoned I would hive the next one. She went and got the lump of lead and fetched it back and brought along a hank of yarn, which she wanted me to help her with. I held up my two hands and she put the hank over them and went on talking about her and her husband’s matters. But she broke off to say:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19075">
“Keep your eye on the rats. You better have the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0970"/>
lead

          <ptr target="#la9940" type="alt" xml:id="te0970"/>
in your lap, handy.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19082">
So she dropped the lump into my lap, just at that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1327"/>
moment

          <app from="pr1327" n="72.27 (254.2)" type="e" xml:id="la2978">
            <lem wit="A">moment,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
moment

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, and I clapped my legs together on it and she went on talking. But only about a minute. Then she took off the hank and looked me straight in the face, but very pleasant, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19092">
“Come, now—what’s your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1328"/>
real

          <app from="pr1328" n="72.33 (254.12)" type="e" xml:id="la2979">
            <lem wit="A">real</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">real</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
name?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19103">“Wh-what, mum?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19105">“What’s your real name? Is it Bill, or Tom, or Bob?—or what is it?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19107">I reckon I shook like a leaf, and I didn’t know hardly what to do. But I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19109">
“Please to don’t poke fun at a poor girl like me, mum. If I’m in the way, here,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1329"/>
I’ll—

          <app from="pr1329" n="72.38 (255.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la2980">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’ll—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">I’ll——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19119">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1330"/>
No

          <app from="pr1330" n="73.1 (255.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2981">
            <lem wit="MS1a">No</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">No,</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1331"/>
won’t. Set

          <app from="pr1331" n="73.1 (255.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la2982">
            <lem wit="A">won’t. Set</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
won’t.—

              <lb/>
Set

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1332"/>
down,

          <app from="pr1332" n="73.1 (255.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la2983">
            <lem wit="MS1a">down,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
down

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and stay where you are. I ain’t going to hurt you, and I ain’t going to tell on you, nuther. You just tell me your secret, and trust me. I’ll keep it; and what’s more, I’ll help you.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1333"/>
So’ll

          <app from="pr1333" n="73.4 (255.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2984">
            <lem wit="A">So’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">So shall</rdg>
          </app>
my old man, if you want him to. You see, you’re a runaway ’prentice—that’s all.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0971"/>
It ain’t

          <ptr target="#la9942" type="alt" xml:id="te0971"/>
anything. There ain’t any harm in it. You’ve been treated bad, and you made up your mind to cut. Bless you, child, I wouldn’t tell on you. Tell me all about it, now—that’s a good boy.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19159">
So I said it wouldn’t be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1334"/>
no

          <app from="pr1334" n="73.9 (256.5)" type="e" xml:id="la2985">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
use to try to play it any longer, and I would just make a clean breast and tell her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1335"/>
everything,

          <app from="pr1335" n="73.10 (256.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la2986">
            <lem wit="A">everything,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
everything

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
but she mustn’t go back on her promise. Then I told her

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0010"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0972"/>
my

          <ptr target="#la9944" type="alt" xml:id="te0972"/>
father and mother was dead, and the law had bound me out

          <ptr target="#as0090" type="an" xml:id="vn0010"/>
to a mean old farmer in the country thirty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1336"/>
mile

          <app from="pr1336" n="73.13 (256.15)" type="e" xml:id="la2987">
            <lem wit="A">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">miles</rdg>
          </app>
back from the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1337"/>
river

          <app from="pr1337" n="73.13 (256.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la2988">
            <lem wit="MS1a">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">river,</rdg>
          </app>
and he treated me so bad I couldn’t stand it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1338"/>
no

          <app from="pr1338" n="73.14 (256.18)" type="e" xml:id="la2989">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
longer; he went away to be gone a couple of days, and so I took my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1339"/>
chance

          <app from="pr1339" n="73.15 (256.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la2990">
            <lem wit="MS1a">chance,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
chance

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1340"/>
and stole

          <app from="pr1340" n="73.15 (256.21)" type="e" xml:id="la2991">
            <lem wit="A">and stole</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">stole</rdg>
          </app>
some of his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0973"/>
daughter’s

          <ptr target="#la9946" type="alt" xml:id="te0973"/>
old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1341"/>
clothes

          <app from="pr1341" n="73.16 (256.22)" type="e" xml:id="la2992">
            <lem wit="MS1a">clothes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">clothes,</rdg>
          </app>
and cleared out, and I had been three

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0974"/>
nights

          <ptr target="#la9948" type="alt" xml:id="te0974"/>
coming the thirty miles; I traveled nights, and hid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1342"/>
daytimes

          <app from="pr1342" n="73.17 (257.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la2993">
            <lem wit="MS1a">daytimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-times</rdg>
          </app>
and slept, and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0975"/>
bag of

          <ptr target="#la9950" type="alt" xml:id="te0975"/>
bread and meat I carried from home lasted me all the way and I had a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1343"/>
plenty. I

          <app from="pr1343" n="73.19 (257.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la2994">
            <lem wit="A">plenty. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
plenty.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
said I believed my uncle

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0976"/>
Abner

          <ptr target="#la9952" type="alt" xml:id="te0976"/>
Moore would take care of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1344"/>
me

          <app from="pr1344" n="73.20 (257.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la2995">
            <lem wit="MS1a">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">me,</rdg>
          </app>
and so that was why I struck out for this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1345"/>
town

          <app from="pr1345" n="73.21 (257.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la2996">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1346"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0977"/>
Goshen

          <ptr target="#la9954" type="alt" xml:id="te0977"/>
.

          <app from="pr1346" n="73.21 (257.13)" type="e" xml:id="la2997">
            <lem wit="C">Goshen.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">Goshen.”</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19298">
“Goshen, child? This ain’t Goshen. This is St. Petersburg.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0011"/>
Goshen’s ten mile further up the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0978"/>
river

          <ptr target="#as0091" type="an" xml:id="vn0011"/>
.

          <ptr target="#la9956" type="alt" xml:id="te0978"/>
Who told you this was Goshen?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19308">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kk0001"/>
Why

          <app from="kk0001" n="73.24 (257.20)" type="hc" xml:id="kkq002">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
a man I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1347"/>
met,

          <app from="pr1347" n="73.24 (257.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la2998">
            <lem wit="MS1a">met,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
met

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1349"/>
daybreak

          <app from="pr1349" n="73.24 (257.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3000">
            <lem wit="MS1a">daybreak</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-break</rdg>
          </app>
this morning, just as I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1350"/>
going

          <app from="pr1350" n="73.24 (257.22)" type="e" xml:id="la3001">
            <lem wit="A">going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">about</rdg>
          </app>
to turn into the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0979"/>
woods

          <ptr target="#la9958" type="alt" xml:id="te0979"/>
for my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1351"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0980"/>
regular

          <ptr target="#la9960" type="alt" xml:id="te0980"/>
          <app from="pr1351" n="73.25 (258.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3002">
            <lem wit="A">regular</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">reglar</rdg>
          </app>
sleep. He told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1352"/>
me

          <app from="pr1352" n="73.25 (258.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3003">
            <lem wit="A">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">me that</rdg>
          </app>
when the roads forked I must take the right hand, and five mile would fetch me to Goshen.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19366">
“He was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1353"/>
drunk,

          <app from="pr1353" n="73.28 (258.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3004">
            <lem wit="MS1a">drunk,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
drunk

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I reckon. He told you just exactly wrong.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19377">
“Well, he did act like he was drunk, but it ain’t no matter now. I got to be moving along. I’ll fetch Goshen before

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1354"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr1354" n="73.30 (258.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3005">
            <lem wit="MS1a">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-light</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19387">
“Hold on a minute. I’ll put you up a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1355"/>
snack

          <app from="pr1355" n="73.33 (258.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3006">
            <lem wit="MS1a">snack</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">snack,</rdg>
          </app>
to eat. You might want it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19397">So she put me up a snack and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19399">
“Say—when a cow’s laying down, which end

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0981"/>
of

          <ptr target="#la9962" type="alt" xml:id="te0981"/>
her gets up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0982"/>
first? Answer

          <ptr target="#la9964" type="alt" xml:id="te0982"/>
up prompt, now—don’t stop to study over it. Which end gets up first?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19409">“The hind end, mum.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19411">“Well, then, a horse?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19413">
          <pb n="74" xml:id="pb0074"/>
“The for’rard end, mum.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19416">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1356"/>
“Which

          <app from="pr1356" n="74.2 (259.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3007">
            <lem wit="MS1a">“Which</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
Which

            </rdg>
          </app>
side of a tree does the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0983"/>
most

          <ptr target="#la9966" type="alt" xml:id="te0983"/>
moss grow on?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19429">“North side.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19431">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0012"/>
“If fifteen cows

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1357"/>
is

          <app from="pr1357" n="74.4 (259.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3008">
            <lem wit="A">is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">are</rdg>
          </app>
browsing on a hillside, how many of them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1358"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0984"/>
eats

          <ptr target="#la9968" type="alt" xml:id="te0984"/>
          <app from="pr1358" n="74.4 (259.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3009">
            <lem wit="A">eats</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">eat</rdg>
          </app>
with their heads

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1359"/>
pointed

          <app from="pr1359" n="74.5 (259.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3010">
            <lem wit="A">pointed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pointed just exactly in</rdg>
          </app>
the same direction?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19461">
“The whole fifteen, mum.”

          <ptr target="#as0092" type="an" xml:id="vn0012"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19465">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y07401">
            <graphic url="y07401.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">she puts up a snack</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19471">
“Well, I reckon you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0985"/>
          <hi rend="italic">have</hi>
          <ptr target="#la9970" type="alt" xml:id="te0985"/>
lived in the country. I thought maybe you was trying to hocus me again. What’s your real name, now?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19478">“George Peters, mum.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19480">
“Well, try to remember it, George. Don’t forget and tell me it’s Elexander before you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0986"/>
go,

          <ptr target="#la9972" type="alt" xml:id="te0986"/>
and then get out by saying it’s George-Elexander when I catch you. And don’t go about women in that old calico. You do a girl tolerable poor, but you might fool men, maybe. Bless you,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0013"/>
child, when you set out to thread a needle,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0987"/>
don’t

          <ptr target="#la9974" type="alt" xml:id="te0987"/>
hold the thread still and fetch the needle up to it; hold the needle still and poke the thread at it—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1360"/>
that’s

          <app from="pr1360" n="74.16 (261.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3011">
            <lem wit="A">that’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that is</rdg>
          </app>
the way a woman

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1361"/>
most always

          <app from="pr1361" n="74.16 (261.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3012">
            <lem wit="A">most always</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3013">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
does;

          <pb n="75" xml:id="pb0075"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1362"/>
but

          <app from="pr1362" n="75.1 (261.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3014">
            <lem wit="A">but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3015">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a man always does

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1363"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr1363" n="75.1 (261.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3016">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
way

          <ptr target="#as0093" type="an" xml:id="vn0013"/>
. And when you throw at a rat or anything, hitch yourself up a tip-toe, and fetch your hand up over your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1364"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0988"/>
head,

          <ptr target="#la9976" type="alt" xml:id="te0988"/>
          <app from="pr1364" n="75.3 (261.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3017">
            <lem wit="MS1a">head,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
head

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
as awkard as you can, and miss your rat about six or seven

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0989"/>
foot

          <ptr target="#la9978" type="alt" xml:id="te0989"/>
. Throw

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1365"/>
stiff-armed,

          <app from="pr1365" n="75.4 (261.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3018">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stiff-armed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stiff-armed</rdg>
          </app>
from the shoulder,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1366"/>
like

          <app from="pr1366" n="75.4 (261.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3019">
            <lem wit="A">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and as if</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0990"/>
there

          <ptr target="#la9980" type="alt" xml:id="te0990"/>
was a pivot there for it to turn on—like a girl; not from the wrist and elbow, with your arm out to one side, like a boy. And mind you, when a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0014"/>
girl tries to catch anything in her lap, she throws her knees apart

          <ptr target="#as0094" type="an" xml:id="vn0014"/>
; she don’t clap them together, the way you did when you catched the lump of lead. Why, I spotted you for a boy when you was threading the needle;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1367"/>
and

          <app from="pr1367" n="75.10 (262.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3020">
            <lem wit="A">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3021">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I contrived the other things just to make certain. Now trot along to your uncle, Sarah Mary Williams George Elexander Peters, and if you get into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1368"/>
trouble,

          <app from="pr1368" n="75.12 (262.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3022">
            <lem wit="MS1a">trouble,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
trouble

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you send word to Mrs. Judith Loftus, which is me, and I’ll do what I can to get you out of it. Keep the river road, all the way, and next time you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1369"/>
tramp

          <app from="pr1369" n="75.14 (263.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3023">
            <lem wit="MS1a">tramp</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tramp,</rdg>
          </app>
take shoes and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1370"/>
socks

          <app from="pr1370" n="75.15 (263.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3024">
            <lem wit="A">socks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">stockings</rdg>
          </app>
with you. The river road’s a rocky one, and your feet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1371"/>
’ll

          <app from="pr1371" n="75.15 (263.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3025">
            <lem wit="A">’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">will</rdg>
          </app>
be in a condition when you get to Goshen, I reckon.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19613">
I went up the bank about fifty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1372"/>
yards

          <app from="pr1372" n="75.17 (263.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3026">
            <lem wit="MS1a">yards</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">yards,</rdg>
          </app>
and then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0991"/>
I doubled

          <ptr target="#la9982" type="alt" xml:id="te0991"/>
on my tracks and slipped back to where my canoe was, a good piece below the house. I jumped in and was off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0992"/>
in a hurry.

          <ptr target="#la9984" type="alt" xml:id="te0992"/>
I went up stream far

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1373"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0993"/>
enough

          <ptr target="#la9986" type="alt" xml:id="te0993"/>
          <app from="pr1373" n="75.20 (263.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3027">
            <lem wit="A">enough</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">enough so as</rdg>
          </app>
to make the head of the island, and then started across. I took off the sun-bonnet, for I didn’t want no blinders on, then. When I was about the middle, I hear the clock begin to strike; so I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1374"/>
stops and listens

          <app from="pr1374" n="75.22–23 (264.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3028">
            <lem wit="A">stops and listens</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">stopped and listened</rdg>
          </app>
; the sound come faint over the water, but clear—eleven. When I struck the head of the island I never

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0994"/>
waited

          <ptr target="#la9988" type="alt" xml:id="te0994"/>
to blow, though I was most winded, but I shoved right into the timber where my old camp used to be, and started a good fire

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1375"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0995"/>
there

          <ptr target="#la9990" type="alt" xml:id="te0995"/>
on a high-and-dry spot

          <app from="pr1375" n="75.26 (264.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3029">
            <lem wit="A">there . . . spot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">there</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19666">
Then I jumped in the canoe and dug out for our

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0996"/>
place

          <ptr target="#la9992" type="alt" xml:id="te0996"/>
a mile and a half below, as hard as I could go. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1376"/>
landed

          <app from="pr1376" n="75.28 (265.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3030">
            <lem wit="MS1a">landed</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">landed,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1377"/>
slopped

          <app from="pr1377" n="75.28 (265.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3031">
            <lem wit="A">slopped</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">tore</rdg>
          </app>
through the timber and up the ridge and into the cavern. There Jim laid, sound asleep on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1378"/>
ground. I

          <app from="pr1378" n="75.30 (265.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la3032">
            <lem wit="A">ground. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
ground.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1379"/>
roused

          <app from="pr1379" n="75.30 (265.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3033">
            <lem wit="A">roused</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">rousted</rdg>
          </app>
him out and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19706">“Git up and hump yourself, Jim! There ain’t a minute to lose. They’re after us!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19708">
Jim never asked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1380"/>
no questions

          <app from="pr1380" n="75.33 (265.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3034">
            <lem wit="A">no questions</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a question</rdg>
          </app>
, he never said a word; but the way he worked for the next half an hour showed about how he was scared. By that time everything we had in the world was on our raft and she was ready to be shoved out from the willow cove where she was hid. We put out the camp fire at the cavern the first thing, and didn’t show a candle outside after

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0997"/>
that.

          <ptr target="#la9994" type="alt" xml:id="te0997"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19721">
          <pb n="76" xml:id="pb0076"/>
I took the canoe out from shore a little piece and took a look, but if there was a boat around I couldn’t see it, for stars and shadows ain’t good to see by. Then we got out the raft and slipped along down in the shade, past the foot of the island

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1381"/>
dead still

          <app from="pr1381" n="76.4 (266.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3035">
            <lem wit="A">dead still</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3036">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, never saying a word.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19733">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y07601">
            <graphic url="y07601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">hump</hi>
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1382"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">yourself!</hi>
              <app from="pr1382" n="76 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3037">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">yourself</hi>
!

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="ln3038">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">yourself</hi>
.

                </rdg>
              </app>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0291">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XII.</head>
        <pb n="77" xml:id="pb0077"/>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e98197">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y07701">
            <graphic url="y07701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1383"/>
Chapter XII.

              <app from="pr1383" n="77 title (266.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3039">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3040">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf7701">
            <graphic url="hf7701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">on the raft</hi>
.

            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1384"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">It</hi>
              <app from="pr1384" n="77.1 (266.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3041">
                <lem wit="A">[¶] It</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3042">
no

                    <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
                  </note>
It

                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e19788">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">must</hi>
a been close onto one o’clock when we got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0998"/>
below

          <ptr target="#la9996" type="alt" xml:id="te0998"/>
the island at last, and the raft did seem to go mighty slow. If a boat was to come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1385"/>
along

          <app from="pr1385" n="77.5 (267.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3043">
            <lem wit="MS1a">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">along,</rdg>
          </app>
we was going to take to the canoe and break for the Illinois shore; and it was well a boat didn’t come, for we hadn’t ever thought to put the gun

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1386"/>
into

          <app from="pr1386" n="77.9 (267.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3044">
            <lem wit="A">into</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">in</rdg>
          </app>
the canoe, or a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1387"/>
fishing-line

          <app from="pr1387" n="77.10 (267.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3045">
            <lem wit="MS1a">fishing-line,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fishing-line</rdg>
          </app>
, or anything to eat. We was in ruther too much of a sweat to think of so many things.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1388"/>
It warn’t good judgment to put

          <hi rend="italic">everything</hi>
on the raft

          <app from="pr1388" n="77.13–15 (267.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3046">
            <lem wit="A">It . . . raft.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3047">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19833">
If the men went to the island, I just expect they found the camp fire I built, and watched it all night for Jim to come. Anyways, they stayed away from us, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg0999"/>
if

          <ptr target="#la9998" type="alt" xml:id="te0999"/>
my building the fire never fooled them it warn’t no fault of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1389"/>
mine. I

          <app from="pr1389" n="77.19 (268.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3048">
            <lem wit="A">mine. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">mine—I</rdg>
          </app>
played it as low-down on them as I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1390"/>
could.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19849">
When

          <app from="pr1390" n="77.20–21 (268.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3049">
            <lem wit="A">could. [¶] When</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
could.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3050">extra line space</note>
[¶] When

            </rdg>
          </app>
the first streak of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1391"/>
day begun

          <app from="pr1391" n="77.21 (268.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3051">
            <lem wit="A">day begun</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dawn begin</rdg>
          </app>
to show, we tied up to a tow-head in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1000"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l10000" type="alt" xml:id="te1000"/>
big bend on the Illinois side, and hacked off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1392"/>
cottonwood

          <app from="pr1392" n="77.22 (268.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3052">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cottonwood</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cotton-wood</rdg>
          </app>
branches with the hatchet and covered up the raft with them so she looked like there had been a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1393"/>
cave-in

          <app from="pr1393" n="77.24 (268.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3053">
            <lem wit="A">cave-in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">cave</rdg>
          </app>
in the bank there. A tow-head is a sand-bar that has

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1394"/>
cottonwoods

          <app from="pr1394" n="77.25 (268.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3054">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cottonwoods</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cotton-woods</rdg>
          </app>
on it as thick as harrow-teeth.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19897">
We had mountains on the Missouri shore and heavy timber on the Illinois side, and the channel was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1001"/>
down

          <ptr target="#l10002" type="alt" xml:id="te1001"/>
the Missouri

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1002"/>
shore

          <ptr target="#l10004" type="alt" xml:id="te1002"/>
at that place, so we warn’t afraid of anybody running across us. We laid there all day and watched the rafts and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1395"/>
steamboats

          <app from="pr1395" n="77.30 (269.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3055">
            <lem wit="A">steamboats</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
steam-

              <lb/>
boats

            </rdg>
          </app>
spin down the Missouri shore, and up-bound steamboats fight the big river in the middle. I told Jim all about the time I had jabbering with that

          <pb n="78" xml:id="pb0078"/>
woman; and Jim said she was a smart one, and if she was to start after us herself

          <hi rend="italic">she</hi>
wouldn’t set down and watch a camp fire—no, sir, she’d fetch

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0014"/>
a dog. Well, then, I said, why couldn’t she tell her husband to fetch a dog? Jim said he bet she did think of it by the time the men was ready to start, and he believed they must a gone up town to get a dog and so they lost all that time, or else we wouldn’t be here on a tow-head sixteen or seventeen mile below the village—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1396"/>
no

          <app from="pr1396" n="78.8 (270.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3056">
            <lem wit="MS1a">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">no,</rdg>
          </app>
indeedy, we would be in that same old town again. So I said I didn’t care what was the reason they didn’t get us, as long as they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1397"/>
didn’t.

          <ptr target="#mt0014" type="alt" xml:id="wn0014"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e19937">
When

          <app from="pr1397" n="78.10–11 (270.19–271.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3057">
            <lem wit="A">didn’t. [¶] When</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
didn’t.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3058">chapter sink</note>
[¶] When

            </rdg>
          </app>
it was beginning to come on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1398"/>
dark

          <app from="pr1398" n="78.11 (271.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3059">
            <lem wit="MS1a">dark</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dark,</rdg>
          </app>
we poked our heads out of the cottonwood thicket and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1003"/>
looked

          <ptr target="#l10006" type="alt" xml:id="te1003"/>
up, and down, and across; nothing in sight; so Jim took up some of the top planks of the raft and built a snug wigwam to get under in blazing weather and rainy, and to keep the things dry. Jim made a floor for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1399"/>
wigwam

          <app from="pr1399" n="78.15 (271.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3060">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wigwam</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wigwam,</rdg>
          </app>
and raised it a foot or more above the level of the raft, so now the blankets and all the traps was out of the reach of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1400"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr1400" n="78.17 (272.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3061">
            <lem wit="A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
waves. Right in the middle of the wigwam we made a layer of dirt about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1401"/>
five or six

          <app from="pr1401" n="78.18 (272.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3062">
            <lem wit="A">five or six</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">three</rdg>
          </app>
inches deep with a frame around it for to hold it to its place; this was to build a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1004"/>
fire

          <ptr target="#l10008" type="alt" xml:id="te1004"/>
on in sloppy weather or chilly; the wigwam would keep it from being seen. We made an extra steering oar, too, because one of the others might get broke, on a snag or something. We fixed up a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1005"/>
short

          <ptr target="#l10010" type="alt" xml:id="te1005"/>
forked

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0015"/>
stick to hang the old lantern

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1006"/>
on; because

          <ptr target="#l10012" type="alt" xml:id="te1006"/>
we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1007"/>
must

          <ptr target="#l10014" type="alt" xml:id="te1007"/>
always

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1008"/>
light

          <ptr target="#l10016" type="alt" xml:id="te1008"/>
the lantern whenever we see a steamboat coming down stream, to keep from getting run over; but we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1009"/>
wouldn’t have to

          <ptr target="#l10018" type="alt" xml:id="te1009"/>
light it for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1402"/>
up-stream

          <app from="pr1402" n="78.26 (273.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3063">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up-stream</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up-

              <lb/>
stream

            </rdg>
          </app>
boats unless we see we was in what they call a “crossing;” for the river was pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1403"/>
high,

          <app from="pr1403" n="78.27 (273.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3064">
            <lem wit="MS1a">high,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
high

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1404"/>
very low banks being still a little under water; so up-bound

          <app from="pr1404" n="78.27–28 (273.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la3065">
            <lem wit="A">very . . . up-bound</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
and up-

              <lb/>
bound

            </rdg>
          </app>
boats didn’t always run the channel, but hunted easy water.

          <ptr target="#as0095" type="an" xml:id="vn0015"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20047">
This second night we run

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0016"/>
between seven and eight hours, with a current that was making over four mile an hour

          <ptr target="#as0096" type="an" xml:id="vn0016"/>
. We catched fish, and talked, and we took a swim now and then to keep off sleepiness. It was kind of solemn, drifting down the big still river, laying on our backs looking up at the stars, and we didn’t ever feel like talking loud, and it warn’t often that we laughed, only a little kind of a low chuckle. We had mighty good weather, as a general thing, and nothing ever happened to us at all, that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1010"/>
night, nor

          <ptr target="#l10020" type="alt" xml:id="te1010"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1405"/>
next

          <app from="pr1405" n="78.37 (274.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3066">
            <lem wit="MS1a">next</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">next,</rdg>
          </app>
nor the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1406"/>
next.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20068">
          <pb n="79" xml:id="pb0079"/>
Every

          <app from="pr1406" n="78.38–79.1 (274.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la3067">
            <lem wit="A">next. [¶] Every</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
next.—

              <lb/>
[¶] Every

            </rdg>
          </app>
night we passed towns, some of them away up on black

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1407"/>
hill sides

          <app from="pr1407" n="79.2 (274.16–17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3068">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hill sides</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hillsides</rdg>
          </app>
, nothing but just a shiny bed of lights, not a house could you see.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0017"/>
The fifth night we passed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1408"/>
St.

          <app from="pr1408" n="79.3 (274.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3069">
            <lem wit="A">St.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
St

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Louis

          <ptr target="#as0097" type="an" xml:id="vn0017"/>
, and it was like the whole world lit up. In

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1409"/>
St.

          <app from="pr1409" n="79.4 (275.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3070">
            <lem wit="A">St.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
St

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Petersburg they used to say there was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1011"/>
twenty or thirty

          <ptr target="#l10022" type="alt" xml:id="te1011"/>
thousand people in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1410"/>
St.

          <app from="pr1410" n="79.5 (275.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3071">
            <lem wit="A">St.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
St

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Louis, but I never believed it till I see that wonderful spread of lights at two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1411"/>
o’clock

          <app from="pr1411" n="79.6 (275.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3072">
            <lem wit="A">o’clock</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">oclock</rdg>
          </app>
that still night. There warn’t a sound there; everybody was asleep.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20129">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y07901">
            <graphic url="y07901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">he sometimes lifted a chicken</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20136">
Every night, now, I used to slip

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1412"/>
ashore

          <app from="pr1412" n="79.8 (275.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3073">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ashore</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ashore,</rdg>
          </app>
towards ten

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1413"/>
o’clock

          <app from="pr1413" n="79.8 (275.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3074">
            <lem wit="MS1a">o’clock</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">o’clock,</rdg>
          </app>
at some little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1414"/>
village

          <app from="pr1414" n="79.9 (275.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3075">
            <lem wit="MS1a">village</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">village,</rdg>
          </app>
and buy ten or fifteen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1415"/>
cents’

          <app from="pr1415" n="79.9 (275.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3076">
            <lem wit="A">cents’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">cents</rdg>
          </app>
worth of meal or bacon or other stuff to eat; and sometimes I lifted a chicken that warn’t roosting comfortable, and took him along. Pap always said, take a chicken when you get a chance, because if you don’t want him yourself you can easy find somebody that does, and a good deed ain’t ever forgot. I never see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1416"/>
pap

          <app from="pr1416" n="79.14 (276.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3077">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
when he didn’t want the chicken himself, but that is what he used to say, anyway.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20179">
Mornings, before

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1417"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr1417" n="79.16 (276.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la3078">
            <lem wit="A">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
day-

              <lb/>
light

            </rdg>
          </app>
, I slipped into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1418"/>
corn-fields

          <app from="pr1418" n="79.16 (276.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3079">
            <lem wit="C">corn-fields</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
corn-

              <lb/>
fields

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">corn fields</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1012"/>
borrowed a

          <ptr target="#l10024" type="alt" xml:id="te1012"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1419"/>
watermelon

          <app from="pr1419" n="79.17 (276.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3080">
            <lem wit="A">watermelon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
water-

              <lb/>
melon

            </rdg>
          </app>
, or a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1420"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1013"/>
mushmelon

          <ptr target="#l10026" type="alt" xml:id="te1013"/>
          <app from="pr1420" n="79.17 (276.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3081">
            <lem wit="MS1a">mushmelon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
mush-

              <lb/>
melon

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1014"/>
or a punkin, or some new

          <pb n="80" xml:id="pb0080"/>
corn,

          <ptr target="#l10028" type="alt" xml:id="te1014"/>
or things of that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1421"/>
kind.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1015"/>
Pap

          <ptr target="#l10030" type="alt" xml:id="te1015"/>
          <app from="pr1421" n="80.1 (276.18–20)" type="e" xml:id="la3082">
            <lem wit="A">kind. Pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
kind.—

              <lb/>
Pap

            </rdg>
          </app>
always said it warn’t no harm to borrow things, if you was meaning to pay them back,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1422"/>
sometime,

          <app from="pr1422" n="80.2 (277.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3083">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sometime,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sometime;</rdg>
          </app>
but the widow said it warn’t anything but a soft name for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1423"/>
stealing

          <app from="pr1423" n="80.3 (277.4–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3084">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stealing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stealing,</rdg>
          </app>
and no decent body would do it. Jim said he reckoned the widow was partly right and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1424"/>
pap

          <app from="pr1424" n="80.5 (277.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3085">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
was partly right; so the best way would be for us to pick out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1425"/>
two or three

          <app from="pr1425" n="80.6 (277.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3086">
            <lem wit="A">two or three</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">one or two</rdg>
          </app>
things from the list and say we wouldn’t borrow them any more—then he reckoned it wouldn’t be no harm to borrow the others. So we talked it over all one night, drifting along down the river, trying to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1016"/>
make

          <ptr target="#l10032" type="alt" xml:id="te1016"/>
up our minds whether to drop the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1426"/>
watermelons

          <app from="pr1426" n="80.10 (277.22)" type="e" xml:id="la3087">
            <lem wit="A">watermelons</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">water-melons</rdg>
          </app>
, or the cantelopes, or the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1017"/>
mushmelons

          <ptr target="#l10034" type="alt" xml:id="te1017"/>
, or what. But towards

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1427"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr1427" n="80.11 (278.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3088">
            <lem wit="MS1a">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
day-

              <lb/>
light

            </rdg>
          </app>
we got it all settled satisfactory, and concluded to drop

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0030"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1018"/>
crabapples

          <ptr target="#l10036" type="alt" xml:id="te1018"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0030" type="te" xml:id="tv0030"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1019"/>
p’simmons

          <ptr target="#l10038" type="alt" xml:id="te1019"/>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1020"/>
We

          <ptr target="#l10040" type="alt" xml:id="te1020"/>
warn’t feeling just right, before that, but it was all comfortable now. I was glad the way it come out, too, because crabapples ain’t ever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1021"/>
good,

          <ptr target="#l10042" type="alt" xml:id="te1021"/>
and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1022"/>
p’simmons

          <ptr target="#l10044" type="alt" xml:id="te1022"/>
wouldn’t be ripe for two or three months yet.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20334">We shot a water-fowl, now and then, that got up too early in the morning or didn’t go to bed early enough in the evening. Take it all around, we lived pretty high.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20336">
The fifth night below

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1428"/>
St.

          <app from="pr1428" n="80.19 (279.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3089">
            <lem wit="A">St.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
St

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Louis we had a big storm after midnight, with a power of thunder and lightning, and the rain poured down in a solid sheet. We

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1429"/>
staid

          <app from="pr1429" n="80.21 (279.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3090">
            <lem wit="MS1a">staid</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stayed</rdg>
          </app>
in the wigwam and let the raft take care of itself. When the lightning glared out we could see a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0018"/>
big straight river ahead, and high rocky bluffs on both sides.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1430"/>
By and by says I, “Hel-

          <hi rend="italic">lo</hi>
, Jim, looky yonder!” It was

          <app from="pr1430" n="80.23–24 (279.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la3091">
            <lem wit="C">By and by . . . was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">And we passed by</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by . . . was</rdg>
          </app>
a steamboat that had killed herself on a rock

          <ptr target="#as0098" type="an" xml:id="vn0018"/>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1431"/>
We was drifting straight down for her.

          <app from="pr1431" n="80.25 (279.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3092">
            <lem wit="A">We . . . her.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3093">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
The lightning showed her very distinct. She was leaning over, with part of her upper deck above water, and you could see every little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1432"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1023"/>
chimblyguy

          <ptr target="#l10046" type="alt" xml:id="te1023"/>
          <app from="pr1432" n="80.27–28 (280.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3094">
            <lem wit="A">chimbly-guy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">chimney-guy</rdg>
          </app>
clean and clear, and a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0019"/>
chair by the big bell, with an old slouch hat hanging on the back of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1433"/>
it

          <ptr target="#as0099" type="an" xml:id="vn0019"/>
when the flashes come

          <app from="pr1433" n="80.29 (280.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3095">
            <lem wit="A">it . . . come</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="ed" xml:id="nt1000"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20406">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0020"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0031"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0015"/>
Well,

          <ptr target="#as0100" type="an" xml:id="vn0020"/>
it being away in the night, and stormy, and all so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1434"/>
mysterious-like

          <app from="pr1434" n="80.30–31 (81-A-1.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la3096">
            <lem wit="A">mysterious-like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
mysterious-

              <lb/>
like

            </rdg>
          </app>
, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1024"/>
felt just

          <ptr target="#l10048" type="alt" xml:id="te1024"/>
the way any other boy would a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1435"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1025"/>
felt,

          <app from="pr1435" n="80.31 (81-A-1.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3097">
            <lem wit="MS2">felt,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
felt

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10050" type="alt" xml:id="te1025"/>
when I see that wreck laying there so mournful and lonesome in the middle of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1436"/>
river.

          <app from="pr1436" n="80.33 (81-A-1.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3098">
            <lem wit="A">river.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">river:</rdg>
          </app>
I wanted to get aboard of her and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1026"/>
slink

          <ptr target="#l10052" type="alt" xml:id="te1026"/>
around a little, and see what there was there. So I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20449">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1437"/>
Le’s

          <app from="pr1437" n="80.35 (81-A-1.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3099">
            <lem wit="A">Le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Less</rdg>
          </app>
land on her, Jim.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20459">But Jim was dead against it, at first. He says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20461">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1438"/>
doan

          <app from="pr1438" n="80.37 (81-A-1.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3100">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
want to go fool’n

          <ptr target="#mt0015" type="alt" xml:id="wn0015"/>
’long er no wrack. We’s doin’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1027"/>
blame’ well,

          <ptr target="#l10054" type="alt" xml:id="te1027"/>
en we better let

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1028"/>
blame’ well

          <ptr target="#l10056" type="alt" xml:id="te1028"/>
alone, as de good book says. Like as not dey’s a watchman on dat wrack.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20482">
          <pb n="81" xml:id="pb0081"/>
“Watchman your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1439"/>
grandmother

          <app from="pr1439" n="81.1 (81-2.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la3101">
            <lem wit="A">grandmother</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
grand-

              <lb/>
mother

            </rdg>
          </app>
,” I says; “there ain’t nothing to watch but the texas and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1440"/>
pilot house

          <app from="pr1440" n="81.2 (81-2.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3102">
            <lem wit="MS2">pilot house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pilot-house</rdg>
          </app>
; and do you reckon anybody’s going to resk his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1029"/>
life

          <ptr target="#l10058" type="alt" xml:id="te1029"/>
for a texas and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1441"/>
pilot house

          <app from="pr1441" n="81.3 (81-2.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3103">
            <lem wit="MS2">pilot house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pilot-house</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1030"/>
such

          <ptr target="#l10060" type="alt" xml:id="te1030"/>
a night as this, when it’s likely to break up and wash off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1031"/>
down the river

          <ptr target="#l10062" type="alt" xml:id="te1031"/>
any minute?” Jim couldn’t say nothing to that, so he didn’t try. “And besides,” I says, “we might borrow something worth having, out of the captain’s stateroom.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1032"/>
Seegars,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1442"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
          <app from="pr1442" n="81.7 (81-3verso.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3104">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’ll

            </rdg>
          </app>
bet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1443"/>
you

          <app from="pr1443" n="81.7 (81-3verso.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3105">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you!</rdg>
          </app>
—and cost five cents apiece, solid cash. Steamboat captains is always rich, and get sixty dollars a month, and

          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
don’t care a cent what a thing costs, you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1033"/>
know,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0032"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1444"/>
long

          <app from="pr1444" n="✱81.10 (81-3verso.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3106">
            <lem wit="A">long</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’s long</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10066" type="alt" xml:id="te1033"/>
as

          <ptr target="#tb0032" type="te" xml:id="tv0032"/>
they want it. Stick a candle in your pocket; I can’t rest, Jim, till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1445"/>
we

          <app from="pr1445" n="81.11 (81-3verso.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3107">
            <lem wit="A">we</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I</rdg>
          </app>
give her a rummaging. Do you reckon Tom Sawyer would ever go by this thing? Not for pie, he wouldn’t. He’d call it an adventure—that’s what he’d call it; and he’d land on that wreck if it was his last act. And wouldn’t he throw style into it?—wouldn’t he spread himself, nor nothing? Why, you’d think it was Christopher

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1446"/>
C’lumbus

          <app from="pr1446" n="81.16 (81-3verso.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3108">
            <lem wit="A">C’lumbus</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Columbus</rdg>
          </app>
discovering Kingdom-Come. I wish Tom Sawyer

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
here.

          <ptr target="#l10064" type="alt" xml:id="te1032"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20586">
Jim he grumbled a little, but give in. He said we mustn’t talk any more than we could help, and then talk mighty low.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1034"/>
The lightning showed us the wreck again, just in time, and we

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0021"/>
fetched

          <ptr target="#l10068" type="alt" xml:id="te1034"/>
the starboard derrick, and made fast there.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20594">
The deck was high out, here. We went sneaking down the slope of it to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1447"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1035"/>
labboard

          <ptr target="#l10070" type="alt" xml:id="te1035"/>
          <app from="pr1447" n="81.23 (81-4.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3109">
            <lem wit="A">labboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">larboard</rdg>
          </app>
, in the dark,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1036"/>
towards the texas,

          <ptr target="#l10072" type="alt" xml:id="te1036"/>
feeling our way slow with our feet, and spreading our hands out to fend off the guys, for it was so dark we couldn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1448"/>
no sign of

          <app from="pr1448" n="81.25 (81-4.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3110">
            <lem wit="A">no sign of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3111">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
them. Pretty soon we struck the forward end of the skylight, and clumb

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1037"/>
onto

          <ptr target="#l10074" type="alt" xml:id="te1037"/>
it; and the next step fetched us in front of the captain’s door, which was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1449"/>
open;

          <app from="pr1449" n="81.27 (81-5.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3112">
            <lem wit="MS2">open;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">open,</rdg>
          </app>
and by

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1450"/>
jimminy

          <app from="pr1450" n="81.28 (81-5.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3113">
            <lem wit="MS2">jimminy</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jimminy</rdg>
          </app>
, away down through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1451"/>
texas hall

          <app from="pr1451" n="81.28 (81-5.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3114">
            <lem wit="MS2">texas hall</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">texas-hall</rdg>
          </app>
we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1452"/>
see

          <app from="pr1452" n="81.28 (81-5.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3115">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">saw</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1038"/>
light!

          <ptr target="#l10076" type="alt" xml:id="te1038"/>
          <ptr target="#as0101" type="an" xml:id="vn0021"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1039"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l10078" type="alt" xml:id="te1039"/>
all in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1040"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l10080" type="alt" xml:id="te1040"/>
same second we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1453"/>
seem to hear

          <app from="pr1453" n="81.29 (81-5.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3116">
            <lem wit="A">seem to hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">heard</rdg>
          </app>
low voices in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1041"/>
yonder!

          <ptr target="#l10082" type="alt" xml:id="te1041"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20683">
Jim whispered and said he was feeling powerful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1454"/>
sick;

          <app from="pr1454" n="81.30 (81-5.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3117">
            <lem wit="MS2">sick;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sick,</rdg>
          </app>
and told me to come along. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1455"/>
says

          <app from="pr1455" n="81.31 (81-5.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3118">
            <lem wit="A">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
, all right; and was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1456"/>
going

          <app from="pr1456" n="81.31 (81-5.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3119">
            <lem wit="A">going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">about</rdg>
          </app>
to start for the raft; but just

          <anchor type="ed" xml:id="nt0018"/>
then I heard a voice wail out and say:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20712">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1457"/>
O

          <app from="pr1457" n="81.33 (81-6.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3120">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, please don’t, boys; I swear I won’t ever tell!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20722">
Another voice said,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1042"/>
pretty loud

          <ptr target="#l10084" type="alt" xml:id="te1042"/>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20728">
“It’s a lie, Jim Turner. You’ve acted this way before. You always want more’n your share of the truck, and you’ve always got it, too, because you’ve swore’t if you didn’t you’d tell. But this time you’ve said it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1458"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1043"/>
jist

          <ptr target="#l10086" type="alt" xml:id="te1043"/>
          <app from="pr1458" n="81.38 (81-6.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3121">
            <lem wit="MS2">jist</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jest</rdg>
          </app>
one time too many. You’re the meanest, treacherousest hound in this country.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20740">
          <pb n="82" xml:id="pb0082"/>
By this time Jim was gone for the raft. I was just a-biling with curiosity; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1459"/>
I says

          <app from="pr1459" n="82.2 (81-7.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3122">
            <lem wit="A">I says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says I</rdg>
          </app>
to myself,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1044"/>
Tom Sawyer wouldn’t back out now, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1460"/>
so I

          <app from="pr1460" n="82.3 (81-7.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3123">
            <lem wit="A">so I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
so

              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
won’t either;

          <ptr target="#l10088" type="alt" xml:id="te1044"/>
I’m agoing to see what’s going

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1461"/>
on

          <app from="pr1461" n="82.3 (81-7.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3124">
            <lem wit="A">on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3125">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1462"/>
here

          <app from="pr1462" n="82.3 (81-7.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3126">
            <lem wit="A">here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">here, if I die for it</rdg>
          </app>
. So I dropped on my hands and knees,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1045"/>
in the little passage,

          <ptr target="#l10090" type="alt" xml:id="te1045"/>
and crept aft in the dark, till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1463"/>
there warn’t but

          <app from="pr1463" n="82.5 (81-7.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3127">
            <lem wit="A">there warn’t but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I was within</rdg>
          </app>
about one stateroom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1464"/>
betwixt me and

          <app from="pr1464" n="82.5–6 (81-7.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3128">
            <lem wit="A">betwixt me and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
the cross-hall of the texas. Then, in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1046"/>
there

          <ptr target="#l10092" type="alt" xml:id="te1046"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1465"/>
see

          <app from="pr1465" n="82.6 (81-7.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3129">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">saw</rdg>
          </app>
a man stretched on the floor and tied hand and foot, and two men standing over him, and one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1047"/>
of them had

          <ptr target="#l10094" type="alt" xml:id="te1047"/>
a dim lantern in his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1048"/>
hand, and

          <ptr target="#l10096" type="alt" xml:id="te1048"/>
the other one had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1466"/>
a pistol

          <app from="pr1466" n="82.9 (81-7.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3130">
            <lem wit="A">a pistol</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a cocked pistol</rdg>
          </app>
. This one kept

          <anchor type="ed" xml:id="nt0020"/>
pointing the pistol

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1049"/>
at

          <ptr target="#l10098" type="alt" xml:id="te1049"/>
the man’s head on the floor and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1467"/>
saying,—

          <app from="pr1467" n="82.10 (81-8.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3131">
            <lem wit="MS2">saying,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
saying

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
—

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20847">
“I’d

          <hi rend="italic">like</hi>
to! And I orter, too, a mean skunk!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20852">
The man on the floor would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1050"/>
shrivel

          <ptr target="#l10100" type="alt" xml:id="te1050"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1468"/>
up

          <app from="pr1468" n="82.12 (81-8.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3132">
            <lem wit="MS2">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">up,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1469"/>
say,

          <app from="pr1469" n="82.12 (81-8.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3133">
            <lem wit="MS2">say,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">say:</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2005"/>
O

          <app from="pr2005" n="82.12 (81-8.7)" type="hc" xml:id="lac716">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, please don’t, Bill—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="prt006"/>
hain’t

          <app from="prt006" n="82.13 (81-8.8)" type="e" xml:id="lk3717">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
ever goin’ to tell.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20890">And every time he said that, the man with the lantern would laugh, and say:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20892">
“ ’Deed you

          <hi rend="italic">ain’t!</hi>
You never said no truer thing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2007"/>
’n

          <app from="pr2007" n="82.16 (81-8.14)" type="e" xml:id="lab718">
            <lem wit="A">’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’n’</rdg>
          </app>
that, you bet you.”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1051"/>
And once he said:

          <ptr target="#l10102" type="alt" xml:id="te1051"/>
“Hear him beg! and yit if we hadn’t got the best of him and tied him, he’d a killed us both. And what

          <hi rend="italic">for?</hi>
Jist for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1473"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1052"/>
noth’n’

          <ptr target="#l10104" type="alt" xml:id="te1052"/>
          <app from="pr1473" n="82.19 (81-9.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3137">
            <lem wit="MS2">noth’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">noth’n</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1053"/>
Jist

          <ptr target="#l10106" type="alt" xml:id="te1053"/>
because we stood on our

          <hi rend="italic">rights</hi>
—that’s what for. But I lay you ain’t agoin’ to threaten nobody any more, Jim Turner. Put

          <hi rend="italic">up</hi>
that pistol, Bill.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20934">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y08201">
            <graphic url="y08201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">please don’t</hi>
,

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1474"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">bill.</hi>
              <app from="pr1474" n="82 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3138">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">bill</hi>
.

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3139">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">bill</hi>
                  <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20957">
          <pb n="83" xml:id="pb0083"/>
Bill

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1475"/>
says

          <app from="pr1475" n="83.1 (81-9.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3140">
            <lem wit="A">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20969">
“I don’t want

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1054"/>
to, Jake Packard.

          <ptr target="#l10108" type="alt" xml:id="te1054"/>
I’m for killin’ him—and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1055"/>
didn’t

          <ptr target="#l10110" type="alt" xml:id="te1055"/>
he kill old Hatfield jist the same way—and don’t he deserve it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20979">
“But I don’t

          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
him killed, and I’ve got my reasons for it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20984">
“Bless yo’ heart for them words, Jake

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1476"/>
Packard!

          <app from="pr1476" n="83.5 (81-10.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3141">
            <lem wit="MS2">Packard!—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Packard!

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1056"/>
I’ll

          <ptr target="#l10112" type="alt" xml:id="te1056"/>
never forgit you, long’s I live!” says the man on the floor, sort of blubbering.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e20998">
Packard didn’t take no notice of that, but hung up his lantern on a nail, and started towards where I was, there in the dark, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1477"/>
motioned

          <app from="pr1477" n="83.9 (81-11.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3142">
            <lem wit="A">motioned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">motioned to</rdg>
          </app>
Bill to come. I crawfished as fast as I could, about two yards, but the boat slanted so that I couldn’t make very good time;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1478"/>
so,

          <app from="pr1478" n="83.11 (81-11.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3143">
            <lem wit="MS2">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to keep from getting run over and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1479"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1057"/>
catched,

          <app from="pr1479" n="83.11 (81-11.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3144">
            <lem wit="MS2">catched,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
catched

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10114" type="alt" xml:id="te1057"/>
I crawled into a stateroom on the upper side. The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1480"/>
men

          <app from="pr1480" n="83.12 (81-11.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3145">
            <lem wit="MS2">men</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">man</rdg>
          </app>
come a-pawing along

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1058"/>
in the dark,

          <ptr target="#l10116" type="alt" xml:id="te1058"/>
and when Packard got to my stateroom, he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21039">“Here—come in here.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21041">
And in he come, and Bill after him. But before they got in, I was up in the upper berth, cornered, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1481"/>
sorry

          <app from="pr1481" n="83.16 (81-12.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la3146">
            <lem wit="A">sorry</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mighty sorry</rdg>
          </app>
I come. Then they stood there, with their hands on the ledge of the berth, and talked. I couldn’t see them, but

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0033"/>
I could tell where they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1482"/>
was, and how close they was

          <app from="pr1482" n="✱83.18–19 (81-12.7–8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3147">
            <lem wit="MS2">was, and how close they was</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">was</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#tn1029" type="te" xml:id="tv0033"/>
by the whisky

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1483"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr1483" n="83.19 (81-12.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3148">
            <lem wit="A">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they had</rdg>
          </app>
been having. I was glad I didn’t drink whisky; but it wouldn’t made much difference, anyway, because most of the time

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1059"/>
they couldn’t a treed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1484"/>
me,

          <app from="pr1484" n="83.21 (81-12.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3149">
            <lem wit="MS2">me,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
because

          <ptr target="#l10118" type="alt" xml:id="te1059"/>
I didn’t breathe. I was too scared. And besides, a body

          <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
breathe, and hear such talk.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1485"/>
They

          <app from="pr1485" n="83.23 (81-12.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3150">
            <lem wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3151">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
They

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">[¶] They</rdg>
          </app>
talked low and earnest.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1486"/>
Bill

          <app from="pr1486" n="83.23 (81-13.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3152">
            <lem wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3153">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Bill

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">[¶] Bill</rdg>
          </app>
wanted to kill Turner. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21112">
“He’s said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1487"/>
he’ll

          <app from="pr1487" n="83.25 (81-13.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3154">
            <lem wit="A">he’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he’d</rdg>
          </app>
tell, and he will. If we was to give both our shares to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1488"/>
him,

          <app from="pr1488" n="83.26 (81-13.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3155">
            <lem wit="MS2">him,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
him

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
, it wouldn’t make no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1489"/>
difference,

          <app from="pr1489" n="83.26 (81-13.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3156">
            <lem wit="MS2">difference,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
difference

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
after the row, and the way we’ve served him. Shore’s you’re born, he’ll turn State’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1490"/>
evidence,

          <app from="pr1490" n="83.27–28 (81-13.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3157">
            <lem wit="MS2">evidence,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">evidence;</rdg>
          </app>
now you hear

          <hi rend="italic">me.</hi>
I’m for putting him out of his troubles.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21152">“So’m I,” says Packard, very quiet.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21154">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1060"/>
Blame it, I’d sorter begun to think you wasn’t.

          <ptr target="#l10120" type="alt" xml:id="te1060"/>
Well, then, that’s all right.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1491"/>
Le’s

          <app from="pr1491" n="83.31 (81-13.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3158">
            <lem wit="C">Le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Less</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Les’</rdg>
          </app>
go and do it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21170">
“Hold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1492"/>
on,

          <app from="pr1492" n="83.32 (81-14.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3159">
            <lem wit="MS2">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a minute; I hain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1493"/>
had

          <app from="pr1493" n="83.32 (81-14.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3160">
            <lem wit="A">had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1494"/>
say,

          <app from="pr1494" n="83.32 (81-14.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3161">
            <lem wit="MS2">say,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
say

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yit. You listen to me. Shooting’s good, but there’s quieter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1495"/>
ways,

          <app from="pr1495" n="83.33 (81-14.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3162">
            <lem wit="MS2">ways,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
ways

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
if the thing’s

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to be done. But what

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
say, is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1496"/>
this:

          <app from="pr1496" n="83.34 (81-14.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3163">
            <lem wit="MS2">this:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">this;</rdg>
          </app>
it ain’t good sense to go court’n around after a halter, if you can

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1497"/>
git

          <app from="pr1497" n="83.35 (81-14.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3164">
            <lem wit="A">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">get</rdg>
          </app>
at what you’re up to in some way that’s jist as good and at the same time don’t bring you into no resks. Ain’t that so?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21228">“You bet it is. But how you goin’ to manage it this time?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21231">
          <pb n="84" xml:id="pb0084"/>
“Well, my idea is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1498"/>
this:

          <app from="pr1498" n="84.1 (81-15.1–3)" type="e" xml:id="la3165">
            <lem wit="A">this:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">this. We’ll go and gag him, so’s to keep him still; then</rdg>
          </app>
we’ll rustle around and gether up whatever pickins

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1061"/>
we’ve overlooked

          <ptr target="#l10122" type="alt" xml:id="te1061"/>
in the staterooms, and shove for shore and hide the truck.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1062"/>
Then

          <ptr target="#l10124" type="alt" xml:id="te1062"/>
we’ll wait. Now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1499"/>
I

          <app from="pr1499" n="84.3 (81-15.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3166">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1063"/>
say

          <ptr target="#l10126" type="alt" xml:id="te1063"/>
it ain’t agoin’ to be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1500"/>
more’n

          <app from="pr1500" n="84.4 (81-15.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3167">
            <lem wit="MS2">more’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">more ’n</rdg>
          </app>
two hours befo’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1501"/>
this

          <app from="pr1501" n="84.4 (81-15.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3168">
            <lem wit="A">this</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thish-yer</rdg>
          </app>
wrack

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1064"/>
breaks

          <ptr target="#l10128" type="alt" xml:id="te1064"/>
up and washes off down the river. See? He’ll be drownded, and won’t have nobody to blame for it but his own self. I reckon that’s a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1502"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr1502" n="84.6 (81-15.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3169">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
sight better’n killin’ of him. I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1503"/>
unfavorable to

          <app from="pr1503" n="84.7 (81-16.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3170">
            <lem wit="A">unfavorable to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dead agin</rdg>
          </app>
killin’ a man as long as you can git around it; it ain’t good sense, it ain’t good morals. Ain’t I right?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21301">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y08401">
            <graphic url="y08401.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">it ain’t good morals.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21308">
“Yes—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1504"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr1504" n="84.9 (81-16.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3171">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
you are. But s’pose she

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
break up and wash off?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21321">
“Well, we can wait the two hours,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1505"/>
anyway, and see,

          <app from="pr1505" n="84.11 (81-16.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3172">
            <lem wit="A">anyway, and see,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3173">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1065"/>
can’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1506"/>
we?

          <app from="pr1506" n="84.11 (81-16.10–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3174">
            <lem wit="A">we?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
we?

              <hi rend="italic">Then</hi>
if the thing don’t work, it’ll still be long befo’ daylight, and we’ll come back and do the

              <hi rend="italic">next</hi>
best thing—tie a rock to him and dump him into the river.

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10130" type="alt" xml:id="te1065"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21348">
“All right, then; come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1507"/>
along

          <app from="pr1507" n="84.12 (81-17.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3175">
            <lem wit="A">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">along and less gag him</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21358">
So they started, and I lit out, all in a cold sweat, and scrambled forward. It was dark as pitch there; but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1508"/>
said,

          <app from="pr1508" n="84.14 (81-17.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3176">
            <lem wit="MS2">said,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
said

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in a kind of a coarse whisper, “Jim!” and he answered up, right at my elbow,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1066"/>
with a sort of a moan,

          <ptr target="#l10132" type="alt" xml:id="te1066"/>
and I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21372">
          <pb n="85" xml:id="pb0085"/>
“Quick, Jim,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1067"/>
it ain’t no time

          <ptr target="#l10134" type="alt" xml:id="te1067"/>
for fooling around and moaning; there’s a gang of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1068"/>
murderers

          <ptr target="#l10136" type="alt" xml:id="te1068"/>
in yonder, and if we don’t hunt up their boat and set

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1509"/>
her

          <app from="pr1509" n="85.3 (81-17.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3177">
            <lem wit="A">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
drifting down the river so these fellows can’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1069"/>
get away from

          <ptr target="#l10138" type="alt" xml:id="te1069"/>
the wreck, there’s one of ’em going to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1510"/>
be in a bad fix. But if we find their boat we can put

          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
of ’em in a bad fix—for the Sheriff ’ll get ’em

          <app from="pr1510" n="85.4–6 (81-18.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la3178">
            <lem wit="A">be in . . . get ’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">lose his life</rdg>
          </app>
. Quick—hurry!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1070"/>
I’ll

          <ptr target="#l10140" type="alt" xml:id="te1070"/>
hunt the labboard side,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1071"/>
you hunt

          <ptr target="#l10142" type="alt" xml:id="te1071"/>
the stabboard. You start at the raft,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1511"/>
and—

          <app from="pr1511" n="85.7 (81-18.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3179">
            <lem wit="MS2">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21424">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1470"/>
O

          <app from="pr1470" n="85.8 (81-18.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3134">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh,</rdg>
          </app>
my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1513"/>
lordy, lordy

          <app from="pr1513" n="85.8 (81-18.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3181">
            <lem wit="A">lordy, lordy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">lordy, lordy, lordy</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1072"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1514"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Raf</hi>
’

          <app from="pr1514" n="85.8 (81-18.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3182">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Raf</hi>
’

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Raf’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10144" type="alt" xml:id="te1072"/>
?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1073"/>
Dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2008"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr2008" n="85.8 (81-18.8)" type="e" xml:id="laq719">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
no raf’ no

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0034"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1516"/>
mo’,

          <app from="pr1516" n="✱85.8 (81-18.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3184">
            <lem wit="A">mo’,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mo;</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0034" type="te" xml:id="tv0034"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l10146" type="alt" xml:id="te1073"/>
done broke loose

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1074"/>
en gone

          <ptr target="#l10148" type="alt" xml:id="te1074"/>
!—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1517"/>
en here

          <app from="pr1517" n="85.9 (81-18.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3185">
            <lem wit="MS2">en here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’en here</rdg>
          </app>
we is!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21493">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y08501">
            <graphic url="y08501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">
                <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1518"/>
o my lordy,

              </hi>
              <app from="pr1518" n="85 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3186">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">o my lordy</hi>
,

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3187">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">oh! lordy</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">lordy!</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0297">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XIII.</head>
        <pb n="86" xml:id="pb0086"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21518">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y08601">
            <graphic url="y08601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1519"/>
Chapter XIII.

              <app from="pr1519" n="86 title (81-18.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3188">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XIII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3189">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf8601">
            <graphic url="hf8601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">in a fix</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e21534">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">
            <sic>ell</sic>
          </hi>
, I catched my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1520"/>
breath,

          <app from="pr1520" n="86.1 (81-18.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3190">
            <lem wit="MS2">breath,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
breath

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and most fainted. Shut up on a wreck with such a gang as that! But it warn’t no time to be sentimentering. We’d

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to find that boat, now—had to have it for ourselves. So we went a-quaking and shaking down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1521"/>
stabboard

          <app from="pr1521" n="86.8 (81-19.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3191">
            <lem wit="A">stabboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">starboard</rdg>
          </app>
side, and slow work it was, too—seemed a week before we got to the stern. No sign of a boat. Jim said he didn’t believe he could go any further—so scared he hadn’t hardly any strength left, he said. But I said come on, if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1075"/>
we

          <ptr target="#l10150" type="alt" xml:id="te1075"/>
get left on this wreck, we are

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1076"/>
in a fix,

          <ptr target="#l10152" type="alt" xml:id="te1076"/>
sure. So on we prowled, again. We struck for the stern of the texas, and found it, and then

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ns0021"/>
scrabbled along

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1077"/>
forwards

          <ptr target="#l10154" type="alt" xml:id="te1077"/>
on the skylight, hanging on from shutter to shutter, for the edge of the skylight was in the water. When we got pretty close to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1522"/>
cross-hall

          <app from="pr1522" n="86.21 (81-20.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la3192">
            <lem wit="A">cross-hall</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
cross-

              <lb/>
hall

            </rdg>
          </app>
door

          <ptr target="#as0102" type="an" xml:id="vv0021"/>
, there was the skiff, sure

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1523"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1078"/>
enough!

          <ptr target="#l10156" type="alt" xml:id="te1078"/>
—

          <app from="pr1523" n="86.22 (81-20.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3193">
            <lem wit="MS2">enough!—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
enough!

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I could just barely see her. I felt

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1079"/>
ever so

          <ptr target="#l10158" type="alt" xml:id="te1079"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1524"/>
thankful

          <app from="pr1524" n="86.22 (81-20.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3194">
            <lem wit="A">thankful</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">good and thankful</rdg>
          </app>
. In another second I would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1080"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l10160" type="alt" xml:id="te1080"/>
been aboard of her; but just then the door opened. One of the men stuck his head out, only about a couple of foot from me, and I thought I was gone; but he jerked it in again, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21614">
“Heave that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1525"/>
blame

          <app from="pr1525" n="86.27 (81-21.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3195">
            <lem wit="A">blame</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dam</rdg>
          </app>
lantern out o’ sight, Bill!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21624">
He flung a bag of something into the boat, and then got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1526"/>
in,

          <app from="pr1526" n="86.28 (81-21.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3196">
            <lem wit="MS2">in,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
in

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
himself, and set down. It was Packard. Then Bill

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
come out and got in. Packard says, in a low voice:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21637">
“All ready—shove

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1081"/>
off!”

          <ptr target="#l10162" type="alt" xml:id="te1081"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21642">
          <pb n="87" xml:id="pb0087"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1527"/>
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1082"/>
couldn’t

          <ptr target="#l10164" type="alt" xml:id="te1082"/>
          <app from="pr1527" n="87.1 (81-21.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la3197">
            <lem wit="A">I couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I never was so miserable in my life. I couldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
hardly hang

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1528"/>
onto

          <app from="pr1528" n="87.1 (81-21.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3198">
            <lem wit="A">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on to</rdg>
          </app>
the shutters, I was so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1083"/>
weak.

          <ptr target="#l10166" type="alt" xml:id="te1083"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1529"/>
But Bill says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21669">“Hold on—’d you go through him?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21671">“No. Didn’t you?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21673">“No. So he’s got his share o’ the cash, yet.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21676">“Well, then, come along—no use to take truck and leave money.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21678">“Say—won’t he suspicion what we’re up to?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21680">“Maybe he won’t. But we got to have it anyway. Come along.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21682">
So they got out and went in.

          <app from="pr1529" n="87.1–9 (81-22.1–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3199">
            <lem wit="A">But Bill . . . in.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
But just then comes a wail out of Turner:

              <lb/>
“O, please, boys,

              <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
leave me—

              <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
leave me to be drownded—please, please, boys, lemme go with you!”

              <lb/>
“Cuss him, he’s got his gag out, aready!” says Packard;

              <lb/>
and him and Bill jumped for the door, allowing they would fix it

              <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
time so it would stick till Christmas.

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21705">
The door slammed to, because it was on the careened side; and in a half

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1530"/>
second

          <app from="pr1530" n="87.11 (81-22.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3200">
            <lem wit="A">second</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a second</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0016"/>
was in the boat, and Jim come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1531"/>
a-tumbling

          <app from="pr1531" n="87.11 (81-23.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3201">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-tumbling</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a tumbling</rdg>
          </app>
after me. I out with my knife and cut the rope, and away we went!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21725">
We didn’t touch an oar, and we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1532"/>
didn’t speak

          <app from="pr1532" n="87.13 (81-23.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3202">
            <lem wit="MS2">didn’t speak</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">didn’ speak</rdg>
          </app>
nor whisper, nor hardly even breathe. We went gliding swift along, dead silent, past the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1084"/>
tip of the

          <ptr target="#l10168" type="alt" xml:id="te1084"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1533"/>
paddle-box

          <app from="pr1533" n="87.15 (81-23.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3203">
            <lem wit="MS2">paddle-box</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
paddle-

              <lb/>
box

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1534"/>
and past

          <app from="pr1534" n="87.15 (81-23.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3204">
            <lem wit="A">and past</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">past</rdg>
          </app>
the stern; then in a second or two more we was a hundred yards below the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1085"/>
wreck

          <ptr target="#l10170" type="alt" xml:id="te1085"/>
, and the darkness soaked her up, every last sign of her, and we was safe, and knowed it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21761">
When we was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1086"/>
three

          <ptr target="#l10172" type="alt" xml:id="te1086"/>
or four hundred yards down

          <ptr target="#mt0016" type="alt" xml:id="wn0016"/>
stream, we see the lantern show like a little spark at the texas door, for a second, and we knowed by that that the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1087"/>
rascals

          <ptr target="#l10174" type="alt" xml:id="te1087"/>
had missed their boat, and was beginning to understand that they was in just as much trouble, now, as Jim Turner was.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21773">
Then Jim manned the oars, and we took out after our raft. Now was the first time that I begun to worry about the men—I reckon I hadn’t had time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1535"/>
to,

          <app from="pr1535" n="87.26 (81-24.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3205">
            <lem wit="MS2">to,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
to

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before. I begun to think how dreadful it was, even for murderers, to be in such a fix. I says to myself,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1088"/>
there

          <ptr target="#l10176" type="alt" xml:id="te1088"/>
ain’t no telling but I might come to be a murderer myself, yet, and then how would

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
like it? So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1536"/>
says I

          <app from="pr1536" n="87.29 (81-25.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3206">
            <lem wit="A">says I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I says</rdg>
          </app>
to Jim:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21799">
“The first light we see, we’ll land a hundred yards below it or above it, in a place where it’s a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1537"/>
hiding place

          <app from="pr1537" n="87.31 (81-25.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3207">
            <lem wit="MS2">hiding place</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hiding-place</rdg>
          </app>
for you and the skiff, and then I’ll go and fix up some kind of a yarn, and get somebody to go for that gang and get them out of their scrape, so they can be hung when their time comes.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21809">
But that idea was a failure; for pretty soon it begun to storm again, and this time worse than ever. The rain poured down, and never a light showed; everybody in bed, I reckon. We boomed along down

          <pb n="88" xml:id="pb0088"/>
the river, watching for lights and watching for our raft. After

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1089"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l10178" type="alt" xml:id="te1089"/>
long

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1090"/>
time

          <ptr target="#l10180" type="alt" xml:id="te1090"/>
the rain let up, but the clouds

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0035"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1538"/>
staid

          <app from="pr1538" n="✱88.2 (81-26.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3208">
            <lem wit="A">staid</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">stayed</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0035" type="te" xml:id="tv0035"/>
, and the lightning kept whimpering, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1539"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1539" n="88.3 (81-27.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3209">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
a flash showed us a black thing ahead, floating, and we made for it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21840">
It was the raft, and mighty glad was we to get aboard of it again. We

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1540"/>
seen

          <app from="pr1540" n="88.6 (81-27.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3210">
            <lem wit="A">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">saw</rdg>
          </app>
a light, now, away down to the right, on shore. So I said I would go for it. The skiff was half full of plunder which that gang had stole, there on the wreck. We hustled it onto the raft in a pile, and I told Jim to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1091"/>
float

          <ptr target="#l10182" type="alt" xml:id="te1091"/>
along down, and show a light when he judged he had gone about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1092"/>
two

          <ptr target="#l10184" type="alt" xml:id="te1092"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1541"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1093"/>
mile

          <app from="pr1541" n="88.10 (81-28.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3211">
            <lem wit="C">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">miles</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">mile,</rdg>
          </app>
and keep it burning till I come;

          <ptr target="#l10186" type="alt" xml:id="te1093"/>
then I manned my oars and shoved for the light. As I got down towards it, three or four more showed—up on a hillside. It was a village. I closed in above the shore-light, and laid on my oars and floated. As I went by, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1094"/>
see

          <ptr target="#l10188" type="alt" xml:id="te1094"/>
it was a lantern hanging on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1542"/>
jackstaff

          <app from="pr1542" n="88.14 (81-28.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la3212">
            <lem wit="A">jackstaff</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
jack-

              <lb/>
staff

            </rdg>
          </app>
of a double-hull

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1543"/>
ferry boat

          <app from="pr1543" n="88.15 (81-28.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3213">
            <lem wit="MS2">ferry boat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1544"/>
Everything was dead still, nobody stirring. I floated in under the stern, made fast, and clumb aboard.

          <app from="pr1544" n="88.15–16 (81-28.12–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3214">
            <lem wit="MS2">Everything . . . aboard.</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3215">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I skimmed around for the watchman,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1095"/>
a-wondering whereabouts he slept;

          <ptr target="#l10190" type="alt" xml:id="te1095"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1545"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1545" n="88.17–18 (81-29.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3216">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I found him roosting on the bitts, forward, with his head down between his knees. I give his shoulder two or three little shoves, and begun to cry.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21917">He stirred up, in a kind of a startlish way; but when he see it was only me, he took a good gap and stretch, and then he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21919">
“Hello, what’s up? Don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1096"/>
cry, bub.

          <ptr target="#l10192" type="alt" xml:id="te1096"/>
What’s the trouble?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21925">I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21927">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1097"/>
“Pap

          <ptr target="#l10194" type="alt" xml:id="te1097"/>
, and mam, and sis,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1546"/>
and—

          <app from="pr1546" n="88.25 (81-29.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3217">
            <lem wit="MS2">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21940">Then I broke down. He says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21942">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1547"/>
O

          <app from="pr1547" n="88.27 (81-29.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3218">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, dang it, now,

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
take on so, we all has to have our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1548"/>
troubles,

          <app from="pr1548" n="88.27 (81-29.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3219">
            <lem wit="MS2">troubles,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
troubles

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1098"/>
this’n ’ll

          <ptr target="#l10196" type="alt" xml:id="te1098"/>
come out all right. What’s the matter with ’em?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21968">“They’re—they’re—are you the watchman of the boat?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e21970">
“Yes,” he says, kind of pretty-well-satisfied

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1549"/>
like.

          <app from="pr1549" n="88.30 (81-30.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3220">
            <lem wit="A">like.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">like,</rdg>
          </app>
“I’m the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1550"/>
captain,

          <app from="pr1550" n="88.30–31 (81-30.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3221">
            <lem wit="MS2">captain,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
captain

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and the owner, and the mate, and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1099"/>
pilot,

          <ptr target="#l10198" type="alt" xml:id="te1099"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1100"/>
and watchman,

          <ptr target="#l10200" type="alt" xml:id="te1100"/>
and head deck-hand; and sometimes I’m the freight and passengers. I ain’t as rich as old Jim Hornback, and I can’t be so blame’ generous and good to Tom, Dick and Harry

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1101"/>
as what

          <ptr target="#l10202" type="alt" xml:id="te1101"/>
he is, and slam around money the way he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1551"/>
does,

          <app from="pr1551" n="88.35 (81-30.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3222">
            <lem wit="MS2">does,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">does;</rdg>
          </app>
but I’ve told him a many a time’t I wouldn’t trade places with him; for, says I,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0022"/>
a sailor’s life’s the life for me

          <ptr target="#as0103" type="an" xml:id="vn0022"/>
, and I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1552"/>
derned

          <app from="pr1552" n="88.37 (81-31.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3223">
            <lem wit="A">derned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">durn’d</rdg>
          </app>
if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1553"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’d

          <app from="pr1553" n="88.37 (81-31.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3224">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
live two mile out o’ town, where there ain’t nothing

          <pb n="89" xml:id="pb0089"/>
ever goin’ on, not for all his spondulicks and as much more on top of it. Says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1554"/>
I—

          <app from="pr1554" n="89.2 (81-31.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3225">
            <lem wit="MS2">I—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">I——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22045">I broke in and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22047">
“They’re in an awful peck of trouble,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1555"/>
and—

          <app from="pr1555" n="89.4 (81-31.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3226">
            <lem wit="MS2">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22057">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Who</hi>
is?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22063">
“Why, pap, and mam, and sis, and Miss Hooker; and if you’d take your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1556"/>
ferry boat

          <app from="pr1556" n="89.7 (81-31.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3227">
            <lem wit="MS2">ferry boat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
and go up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1557"/>
there—

          <app from="pr1557" n="89.7 (81-31.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3228">
            <lem wit="MS2">there—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">there——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22081">“Up where? Where are they?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22083">“On the wreck.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22085">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y08901">
            <graphic url="y08901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">hello, what’s up?</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22092">“What wreck?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22094">“Why, there ain’t but one.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22096">
“What, you don’t mean the

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0023"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1102"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Walter</hi>
          <ptr target="#l10204" type="alt" xml:id="te1102"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Scott</hi>
          <ptr target="#as0104" type="an" xml:id="vn0023"/>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22106">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22108">
“Good land! what are they doin’

          <hi rend="italic">there</hi>
, for gracious sakes?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22113">“Well, they didn’t go there a-purpose.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22115">
“I bet they didn’t! Why, great

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1103"/>
goodness,

          <ptr target="#l10206" type="alt" xml:id="te1103"/>
there ain’t no chance for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1104"/>
’em

          <ptr target="#l10208" type="alt" xml:id="te1104"/>
if they don’t git off mighty quick! Why, how in the nation did they ever git into such a scrape?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22126">
          <pb n="90" xml:id="pb0090"/>
“Easy enough. Miss Hooker was a-visiting, up there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1558"/>
to

          <app from="pr1558" n="90.1 (81-32.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3229">
            <lem wit="A">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">at</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1559"/>
town—

          <app from="pr1559" n="90.2 (81-33.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3230">
            <lem wit="MS2">town—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">town——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22145">“Yes, Booth’s Landing—go on.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22147">
“She was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1560"/>
a visiting

          <app from="pr1560" n="90.4 (81-33.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3231">
            <lem wit="MS2">a visiting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a-visiting</rdg>
          </app>
, there at Booth’s Landing, and just in the edge of the evening she started over with her nigger woman in the horse-ferry, to stay all night at her friend’s house, Miss What-you-may-call-her, I disremember her name, and they lost their

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0036"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1561"/>
steering-oar,

          <app from="pr1561" n="✱90.7 (81-33.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3232">
            <lem wit="A">steering-oar,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
steering-oar

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3233">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0036" type="te" xml:id="tv0036"/>
and swung around and went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1562"/>
a-floating

          <app from="pr1562" n="90.8 (81-33.14–81–34.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3234">
            <lem wit="A">a-floating</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
floating

            </rdg>
          </app>
down, stern-first, about two mile, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1563"/>
saddle-baggsed

          <app from="pr1563" n="90.9 (81-34.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la3235">
            <lem wit="A">saddle-baggsed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
saddle-

              <lb/>
bagsed

            </rdg>
          </app>
on the wreck, and the ferry man and the nigger woman and the horses was all lost, but Miss Hooker she made a grab

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1105"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l10210" type="alt" xml:id="te1105"/>
got aboard the wreck. Well, about an hour after dark, we come along down in our trading-scow, and it was so dark we didn’t notice the wreck till we was right on it; and so

          <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1564"/>
saddle-baggsed

          <app from="pr1564" n="90.13–14 (81-34.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3236">
            <lem wit="A">saddle-baggsed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">saddle-bagsed</rdg>
          </app>
; but all of us was saved but Bill Whipple—and oh, he

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
the best

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1106"/>
cretur!

          <ptr target="#l10212" type="alt" xml:id="te1106"/>
—I most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1565"/>
wish’t

          <app from="pr1565" n="90.15 (81-34.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3237">
            <lem wit="A">wish’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wish</rdg>
          </app>
it had been me, I do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22221">
“My George!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1566"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr1566" n="90.16 (81-35.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3238">
            <lem wit="MS2">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">It’s</rdg>
          </app>
the beatenest thing I ever struck. And

          <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
what did you all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1567"/>
do?”

          <app from="pr1567" n="90.17 (81-35.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3239">
            <lem wit="A">do?”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
do?’

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3240">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22243">
“Well, we hollered and took on, but it’s so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1568"/>
wide,

          <app from="pr1568" n="90.18 (81-35.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3241">
            <lem wit="MS2">wide,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
wide

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
there, we couldn’t make nobody hear. So pap said somebody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1569"/>
got to

          <app from="pr1569" n="90.19 (81-35.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3242">
            <lem wit="A">got to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">must</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1107"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l10214" type="alt" xml:id="te1107"/>
ashore and get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1570"/>
help,

          <app from="pr1570" n="90.20 (81-35.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3243">
            <lem wit="MS2">help,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
help

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
somehow. I was the only one that could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2009"/>
swim;

          <app from="pr2009" n="90.20 (81-35.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3244">
            <lem wit="MS2">swim;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">swim,</rdg>
          </app>
so I made a dash for it, and Miss Hooker

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1572"/>
she

          <app from="pr1572" n="90.21 (81-35.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3245">
            <lem wit="A">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3246">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
said if I didn’t strike help sooner, come here and hunt up her uncle, and he’d fix the thing. I made the land about a mile below, and been fooling along ever since, trying to get people to do something, but they said, ‘What, in such a night and such a current? there ain’t no sense in it; go for the steam-ferry.’ Now

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1108"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1573"/>
if

          <app from="pr1573" n="90.26 (81-36.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3247">
            <lem wit="A">if</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">if if</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10216" type="alt" xml:id="te1108"/>
you’ll go,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1574"/>
and—

          <app from="pr1574" n="90.26 (81-36.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3248">
            <lem wit="MS2">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22309">
“By Jackson, I’d

          <hi rend="italic">like</hi>
to, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1109"/>
blame

          <ptr target="#l10218" type="alt" xml:id="te1109"/>
it I don’t know but I will; but who in the dingnation’s agoin’ to

          <hi rend="italic">pay</hi>
for it? Do you reckon your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1575"/>
pap—

          <app from="pr1575" n="90.29 (81-36.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3249">
            <lem wit="MS2">pap—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pap——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22330">
“Why

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1576"/>
          <hi rend="italic">that’s</hi>
          <app from="pr1576" n="90.30 (81-36.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3250">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
’s

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">that’s</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all right. Miss Hooker she told me,

          <hi rend="italic">particular</hi>
, that her uncle

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1577"/>
Hornback—

          <app from="pr1577" n="90.31 (81-36.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3251">
            <lem wit="MS2">Hornback—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Hornback——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22355">
“Great guns! is

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
her uncle? Looky here, you break for that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1110"/>
light

          <ptr target="#l10220" type="alt" xml:id="te1110"/>
over yonder-way, and turn out west when you git there, and about a quarter of a mile out you’ll come to the tavern; tell ’em to dart you out to Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1578"/>
Hornback’s,

          <app from="pr1578" n="90.35 (81-37.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3252">
            <lem wit="MS2">Hornback’s,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Hornback’s

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and he’ll foot the bill. And don’t you fool

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1111"/>
around

          <ptr target="#l10222" type="alt" xml:id="te1111"/>
any, because he’ll want to know the news.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1112"/>
Tell him I’ll have his niece all safe before he can get to town.

          <ptr target="#l10224" type="alt" xml:id="te1112"/>
Hump yourself, now; I’m

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1113"/>
agoing

          <ptr target="#l10226" type="alt" xml:id="te1113"/>
up around the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1579"/>
corner,

          <app from="pr1579" n="90.38 (81-37.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3253">
            <lem wit="MS2">corner,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
corner

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
here, to roust out my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1580"/>
engineer

          <app from="pr1580" n="90.38 (81-37.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3254">
            <lem wit="A">engineer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ingineer</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22402">
          <pb n="91" xml:id="pb0091"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1581"/>
struck

          <app from="pr1581" n="91.1 (81-37.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3255">
            <lem wit="A">struck</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">struck out</rdg>
          </app>
for the light, but as soon as he turned the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1114"/>
corner

          <ptr target="#l10228" type="alt" xml:id="te1114"/>
I went back and got into my skiff and bailed her out and then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1115"/>
pulled

          <ptr target="#l10230" type="alt" xml:id="te1115"/>
up shore in the easy water about six hundred

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1116"/>
yards,

          <ptr target="#l10232" type="alt" xml:id="te1116"/>
and tucked myself in among some woodboats; for I couldn’t rest easy till I could see the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1582"/>
ferryboat

          <app from="pr1582" n="91.5 (81-38.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3256">
            <lem wit="MS2">ferryboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
start. But take it all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1117"/>
around,

          <ptr target="#l10234" type="alt" xml:id="te1117"/>
I was feeling ruther

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1583"/>
comfortable,

          <app from="pr1583" n="91.6 (81-38.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3257">
            <lem wit="MS2">comfortable,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
comfortable

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
on accounts of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1118"/>
taking all

          <ptr target="#l10236" type="alt" xml:id="te1118"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1119"/>
this trouble

          <ptr target="#l10238" type="alt" xml:id="te1119"/>
for that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1120"/>
gang, for not many would a done it.

          <ptr target="#l10240" type="alt" xml:id="te1120"/>
I wished the widow knowed about it. I judged she would be proud of me for helping these rapscallions, because rapscallions and dead beats

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1121"/>
is

          <ptr target="#l10242" type="alt" xml:id="te1121"/>
the kind the widow and good people takes the most interest in.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22463">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="an0023"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y09101">
            <graphic url="y09101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">the wreck</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
          <ptr target="#as0105" type="an" xml:id="na0023"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22471">
Well, before long, here comes the wreck, dim and dusky, sliding along down! A kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1584"/>
cold

          <app from="pr1584" n="91.12 (81-39.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3258">
            <lem wit="A">cold</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a cold</rdg>
          </app>
shiver went through me, and then I struck out for her. She was very deep, and I see in a minute

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1585"/>
there

          <app from="pr1585" n="91.13 (81-39.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3259">
            <lem wit="A">there</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that there</rdg>
          </app>
warn’t much chance

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1586"/>
for

          <app from="pr1586" n="91.14 (81-39.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3260">
            <lem wit="A">for</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
anybody being alive in her. I pulled all around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1587"/>
her,

          <app from="pr1587" n="91.15 (81-39.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3261">
            <lem wit="MS2">her,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
her

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and hollered a little, but there wasn’t any answer; all dead still. I felt a little bit heavy-hearted about the gang, but not much, for I reckoned if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1588"/>
they

          <app from="pr1588" n="91.17 (81-39.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3262">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
could stand it, I could.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22516">
Then here comes the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1589"/>
ferryboat

          <app from="pr1589" n="91.18 (81-39.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3263">
            <lem wit="C">ferryboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
ferry-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
; so I shoved for the middle of the river on a long

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1590"/>
down-stream

          <app from="pr1590" n="91.19 (81-40.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la3264">
            <lem wit="A">down-stream</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
down-

              <lb/>
stream

            </rdg>
          </app>
slant; and when I judged I was out of eye-reach, I laid on my oars, and looked back and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1591"/>
see

          <app from="pr1591" n="91.20 (81-40.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3265">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">saw</rdg>
          </app>
her go and smell around the wreck for Miss Hooker’s remainders,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1122"/>
because the

          <ptr target="#l10244" type="alt" xml:id="te1122"/>
captain would know her uncle Hornback would want them; and

          <pb n="92" xml:id="pb0092"/>
then pretty soon the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1592"/>
ferryboat

          <app from="pr1592" n="92.1 (81-40.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3266">
            <lem wit="MS2">ferryboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
give it up and went for shore, and I laid into my work and went a-booming down the river.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22563">
It did seem a powerful long time before Jim’s light showed up; and when it did show, it looked like it was a thousand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1593"/>
mile

          <app from="pr1593" n="92.4 (81-41.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3267">
            <lem wit="A">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">miles</rdg>
          </app>
off. By the time I got there the sky was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1123"/>
beginning

          <ptr target="#l10246" type="alt" xml:id="te1123"/>
to get a little gray in the east; so we struck for an island, and hid the raft, and sunk the skiff, and turned in and slept like dead people.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22577">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y09201">
            <graphic url="y09201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">we turned in and slept</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0302">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XIV.</head>
        <pb n="93" xml:id="pb0093"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22587">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y09301">
            <graphic url="y09301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1594"/>
Chapter XIV.

              <app from="pr1594" n="93 title (81-41.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3268">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XIV.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3269">not in; extra line space</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf9301">
            <graphic url="hf9301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">turning over the truck</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e22603">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1595"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1124"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">
            <sic>y</sic>
and by

          </hi>
          <app from="pr1595" n="93.1 (81-41.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3270">
            <lem wit="MS2">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l10248" type="alt" xml:id="te1124"/>
when we got up, we turned over the truck the gang had stole off of the wreck, and found boots, and blankets, and clothes, and all sorts of other things, and a lot of books, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1596"/>
spyglass

          <app from="pr1596" n="93.7 (81-41.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3271">
            <lem wit="MS2">spyglass</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">spyglass,</rdg>
          </app>
and three boxes of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1125"/>
seegars

          <ptr target="#l10250" type="alt" xml:id="te1125"/>
. We hadn’t ever been this rich before, in neither of our lives. The seegars was prime. We laid off all the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1597"/>
afternoon

          <app from="pr1597" n="93.11 (81-42.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3272">
            <lem wit="MS2">afternoon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
after-

              <lb/>
noon

            </rdg>
          </app>
in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1598"/>
woods,

          <app from="pr1598" n="93.12 (81-42.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3273">
            <lem wit="MS2">woods,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
woods

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
talking, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1599"/>
me

          <app from="pr1599" n="93.12 (81-42.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3274">
            <lem wit="A">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3275">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1126"/>
reading

          <ptr target="#l10252" type="alt" xml:id="te1126"/>
the books, and having a general good time. I told Jim all about what happened inside the wreck, and at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1600"/>
ferryboat

          <app from="pr1600" n="93.16 (81-42.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3276">
            <lem wit="MS2">ferryboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ferry-boat</rdg>
          </app>
; and I said these kinds of things was adventures; but he said he didn’t want no more adventures. He said that when I went in the texas and he crawled back to get on the raft and found her gone, he nearly died; because he judged it was all up with

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
, anyway it could be fixed; for if he didn’t get saved he would get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1127"/>
drownded;

          <ptr target="#l10254" type="alt" xml:id="te1127"/>
and if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1601"/>
he

          <app from="pr1601" n="93.22 (81-43.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3277">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3278">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0017"/>
did get saved, whoever saved him would send him back home so as to get the reward, and then Miss Watson would sell him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1602"/>
south

          <app from="pr1602" n="93.24 (81-43.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3279">
            <lem wit="MS2">south</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">South</rdg>
          </app>
, sure. Well, he was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1128"/>
right;

          <ptr target="#l10256" type="alt" xml:id="te1128"/>
he was most always right; he had an uncommon level head, for a nigger.

          <ptr target="#mt0017" type="alt" xml:id="wn0017"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22702">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1129"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0024"/>
I read considerable to Jim about kings, and dukes, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1130"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1603"/>
earls

          <ptr target="#l10260" type="alt" xml:id="te1130"/>
          <app from="pr1603" n="93.26 (81-44.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3280">
            <lem wit="MS2">earls</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">earls,</rdg>
          </app>
and such, and how gaudy they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1604"/>
dressed

          <app from="pr1604" n="93.27 (81-44.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3281">
            <lem wit="MS2">dressed</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">dressed,</rdg>
          </app>
and how much style they put on, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1131"/>
called

          <ptr target="#l10262" type="alt" xml:id="te1131"/>
each other your majesty, and your grace, and your lordship, and so on, ’stead of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1605"/>
mister

          <app from="pr1605" n="93.29 (81-44.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3282">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mister</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Mister</rdg>
          </app>
; and Jim’s eyes bugged out, and he was interested. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22737">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1606"/>
didn’

          <app from="pr1606" n="93.31 (81-44.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3283">
            <lem wit="A">didn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
know dey was so many un um. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1607"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr1607" n="93.31 (81-44.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3284">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">haint</rdg>
          </app>
hearn ’bout none

          <pb n="94" xml:id="pb0094"/>
un um,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1608"/>
skasely

          <app from="pr1608" n="94.1 (81-44.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3285">
            <lem wit="A Cent">skasely</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">scasely</rdg>
          </app>
, but ole

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1609"/>
king

          <app from="pr1609" n="94.1 (81-44.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3286">
            <lem wit="MS2">king</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">King</rdg>
          </app>
Sollermun, onless you counts dem kings dat’s in a pack er k’yards. How much do a king git?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22774">
“Get?” I says; “why, they get a thousand dollars a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1610"/>
month

          <app from="pr1610" n="94.3 (81-45.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3287">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">month</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">month,</rdg>
          </app>
if they want it; they can have just as much as they want; everything belongs to them.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22784">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1611"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Ain’</hi>
          <app from="pr1611" n="94.6 (81-45.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3288">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">Ain</hi>
’

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Ain’</rdg>
          </app>
dat gay? En what dey got to do, Huck?”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y09501">
          <graphic url="y09501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1642"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">solomon and his million wives</hi>
.

            <app from="pr1642" n="95 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la3320">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">solomon and his million wives</hi>
.

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3321">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">sollermun and his wives</hi>
.

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22815">
“

          <hi rend="italic">They</hi>
don’t do nothing!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1612"/>
Why,

          <app from="pr1612" n="94.7 (81-45.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3289">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Why,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Why

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
how you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1613"/>
talk.

          <app from="pr1613" n="94.7 (81-45.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3290">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">talk.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">talk!</rdg>
          </app>
They just set around.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22836">“No—is dat so?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22839">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1132"/>
Of course

          <ptr target="#l10264" type="alt" xml:id="te1132"/>
it is. They just set

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1614"/>
around. Except

          <app from="pr1614" n="94.10 (81-45.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3291">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">around. Except</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">around, except</rdg>
          </app>
maybe when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1615"/>
there’s

          <app from="pr1615" n="94.10 (81-46.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3292">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">there’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">there ’s</rdg>
          </app>
a war; then they go to the war. But other times they just lazy around; or go hawking—just

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0025"/>
hawking and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1133"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1616"/>
sp— Sh!—

          <app from="pr1616" n="94.12 (81-46.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3293">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sp—Sh!—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sp—sh!</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0107" type="an" xml:id="vn0025"/>
          <ptr target="#l10266" type="alt" xml:id="te1133"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1617"/>
d’ you

          <app from="pr1617" n="94.12 (81-46.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3294">
            <lem wit="MS2">d’you</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">d’ you</rdg>
          </app>
hear a noise?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22883">
We

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0037"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1618"/>
skipped

          <app from="pr1618" n="✱94.13 (81-46.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3295">
            <lem wit="A Cent">skipped</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">slipped</rdg>
          </app>
out

          <ptr target="#tb0037" type="te" xml:id="tv0037"/>
and looked; but it warn’t nothing but the flutter of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1619"/>
steamboat’s

          <app from="pr1619" n="94.14 (81-46.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3296">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">steamboat’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">steam-boat’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1620"/>
wheel

          <app from="pr1620" n="94.14 (81-46.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3297">
            <lem wit="MS2">wheel</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wheel,</rdg>
          </app>
away down coming around the point; so we come back.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22912">
“Yes,” says I, “and other times, when things is dull, they fuss with the parlyment; and if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1134"/>
everybody

          <ptr target="#l10268" type="alt" xml:id="te1134"/>
don’t go just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1621"/>
so,

          <app from="pr1621" n="94.17 (81-46.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3298">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he whacks their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1622"/>
heads

          <app from="pr1622" n="94.18 (81-46.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3299">
            <lem wit="A Cent">heads</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">head</rdg>
          </app>
off. But mostly they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1623"/>
hang

          <app from="pr1623" n="94.18 (81-46.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3300">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hang</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wallow</rdg>
          </app>
round the harem.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22943">“Roun’ de which?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22945">“Harem.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22947">“What’s de harem?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22949">
“The place where he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1624"/>
keep

          <app from="pr1624" n="94.22 (81-47.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3301">
            <lem wit="A Cent">keep</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">keeps</rdg>
          </app>
his wives. Don’t you know about the harem? Solomon had one; he had about a million wives.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e22959">
“Why, yes, dat’s so;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1625"/>
I—

          <app from="pr1625" n="94.24 (81-47.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3302">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3303">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I’d done forgot it. A harem’s a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1626"/>
bo’d’n house

          <app from="pr1626" n="94.24 (81-47.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3304">
            <lem wit="MS2">bo’d’n house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">bo’d’n-house</rdg>
          </app>
, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1627"/>
reck’n.

          <app from="pr1627" n="94.25 (81-47.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3305">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon.</rdg>
          </app>
Mos’ likely dey has rackety times in de nussery. En I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1628"/>
reck’n de

          <app from="pr1628" n="94.25–26 (81-47.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3306">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n de</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon de</rdg>
          </app>
wives quarrels

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1629"/>
considable

          <app from="pr1629" n="94.26 (81-47.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3307">
            <lem wit="A Cent">considable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
; en dat ’crease de racket. Yit dey say Sollermun de wises’ man dat ever live’. I doan’ take no stock in dat.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1630"/>
Bekase why: would

          <app from="pr1630" n="94.28 (81-48.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3308">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Bekase why: would</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Becase why? Would</rdg>
          </app>
a wise man want to live in de mids’ er

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1631"/>
sich

          <app from="pr1631" n="94.28 (81-48.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3309">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">sich</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">such</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1632"/>
blimblammin’

          <app from="pr1632" n="94.29 (81-48.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3310">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blimblammin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blim-blammin’</rdg>
          </app>
all de time? No—’deed he wouldn’t. A wise man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1633"/>
’ud

          <app from="pr1633" n="94.29 (81-48.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3311">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’ud</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">would</rdg>
          </app>
take en buil’ a biler-factry; en den he could shet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1634"/>
          <hi rend="italic">down</hi>
          <app from="pr1634" n="94.30 (81-48.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3312">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">down</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">down</rdg>
          </app>
de biler-factry when he want to res’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23047">
“Well, but he

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
the wisest man, anyway; because the widow she told me so, her own self.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23052">
“I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1135"/>
doan

          <ptr target="#l10270" type="alt" xml:id="te1135"/>
k’yer what de widder say, he

          <hi rend="italic">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1635"/>
warn’t

          </hi>
          <app from="pr1635" n="94.34 (81-48.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3313">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">warn’t</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">warnt</rdg>
          </app>
no wise man, nuther. He had some er de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1136"/>
dad-fetchedes’

          <ptr target="#l10272" type="alt" xml:id="te1136"/>
ways I ever see. Does you know ’bout

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0026"/>
dat chile dat he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1636"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr1636" n="94.36 (81-49.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3314">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1637"/>
gwyne

          <app from="pr1637" n="94.36 (81-49.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3315">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">gwyne</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gwine</rdg>
          </app>
to chop in two

          <ptr target="#as0108" type="an" xml:id="vn0026"/>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23092">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1638"/>
Yes;

          <app from="pr1638" n="94.37 (81-49.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3316">
            <lem wit="MS2">Yes;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Yes,</rdg>
          </app>
the widow told me all about it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23103">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
, den!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1639"/>
Warn’

          <app from="pr1639" n="94.38 (81-49.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3317">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Warn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Warn’t</rdg>
          </app>
dat de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1137"/>
beatenes’

          <ptr target="#l10274" type="alt" xml:id="te1137"/>
notion in de worl’? You

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0038"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1138"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1640"/>
jis’

          <app from="pr1640" n="✱94.38 (81-49.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3318">
            <lem wit="MS2">jis’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">jes’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10276" type="alt" xml:id="te1138"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0038" type="te" xml:id="tv0038"/>
take

          <pb n="95" xml:id="pb0095"/>
en look at it a minute. Dah’s de stump, dah—dat’s one er de women; heah’s you—dat’s de yuther

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1139"/>
one

          <ptr target="#l10278" type="alt" xml:id="te1139"/>
; I’s Sollermun; en dish-yer dollar bill’s de chile. Bofe un you claims it.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1140"/>
What

          <ptr target="#l10280" type="alt" xml:id="te1140"/>
does I do? Does I shin aroun’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1141"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1641"/>
mongs’

          <app from="pr1641" n="95.4 (81-50.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3319">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">mongs’</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’mongs’</rdg>
          </app>
de neighbors en fine out

          <ptr target="#l10282" type="alt" xml:id="te1141"/>
which un you de bill

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
b’long to, en han’ it over to de right one, all safe en soun’, de way dat anybody dat had any gumption would? No—I take en whack de bill in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1644"/>
          <hi rend="italic">two</hi>
          <app from="pr1644" n="95.7 (81-50.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3323">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">two</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">two</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1142"/>
en give

          <ptr target="#l10284" type="alt" xml:id="te1142"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2010"/>
half un

          <app from="pr2010" n="95.7 (81-50.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="lap720">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">half un</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">haf un</rdg>
          </app>
it to you, en de yuther half to de yuther woman.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1143"/>
Dat’s

          <ptr target="#l10286" type="alt" xml:id="te1143"/>
de way Sollermun was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1645"/>
gwyne

          <app from="pr1645" n="95.8 (81-50.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3324">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">gwyne</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gwine</rdg>
          </app>
to do wid de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1144"/>
chile.

          <ptr target="#l10288" type="alt" xml:id="te1144"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1646"/>
Now

          <app from="pr1646" n="95.8 (81-50.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3325">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Now,</rdg>
          </app>
I want to ast you:

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1145"/>
what’s de use er

          <ptr target="#l10290" type="alt" xml:id="te1145"/>
dat half a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1146"/>
bill?

          <ptr target="#l10292" type="alt" xml:id="te1146"/>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1647"/>
can’t

          <app from="pr1647" n="95.9 (81-50.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3326">
            <lem wit="A Cent">can’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cain’t</rdg>
          </app>
buy

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1147"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1648"/>
noth’n

          <app from="pr1648" n="95.9 (81-50.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3327">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">noth’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">nuth’n</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10294" type="alt" xml:id="te1147"/>
wid it. En what use is a half a chile? I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1649"/>
wouldn’

          <app from="pr1649" n="95.10 (81-50.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3328">
            <lem wit="C">wouldn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">would’n</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">wouldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
give a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1148"/>
dern

          <ptr target="#l10296" type="alt" xml:id="te1148"/>
for a million un um.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23247">“But hang it, Jim, you’ve clean missed the point—blame it, you’ve missed it a thousand mile.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23249">
“Who?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1650"/>
me

          <app from="pr1650" n="95.14 (81-51.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3329">
            <lem wit="MS2">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Me</rdg>
          </app>
? Go ’long.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1149"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1651"/>
Doan

          <app from="pr1651" n="95.14 (81-51.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3330">
            <lem wit="MS2">Doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Doan’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10298" type="alt" xml:id="te1149"/>
talk to

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
’bout yo’ pints. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1652"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr1652" n="95.14 (81-51.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3331">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
I knows sense when I sees it; en dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1653"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1653" n="95.15 (81-51.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3332">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
no sense in sich

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0039"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1150"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1654"/>
doin’s

          <app from="pr1654" n="✱95.15 (81-51.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3333">
            <lem wit="A Cent">doin’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">doins</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10300" type="alt" xml:id="te1150"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0039" type="te" xml:id="tv0039"/>
as dat. De ’spute warn’t ’bout

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1655"/>
a half

          <app from="pr1655" n="95.16 (81-51.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3334">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a half</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">half</rdg>
          </app>
a chile, de ’spute was ’bout a whole chile; en de man dat think he kin settle a ’spute ’bout a whole chile wid a half a chile,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1656"/>
doan

          <app from="pr1656" n="95.18 (81-51.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3335">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
know enough to come in out’n de rain.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1657"/>
Doan

          <app from="pr1657" n="95.18 (81-51.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3336">
            <lem wit="MS2">Doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Doan’</rdg>
          </app>
talk to me ’bout Sollermun, Huck, I knows him by de back.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23327">
          <pb n="96" xml:id="pb0096"/>
“But I tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1658"/>
you you

          <app from="pr1658" n="96.1 (81-52.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3337">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">you you</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">you, you</rdg>
          </app>
don’t get the point.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y09601">
          <graphic url="y09601.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1665"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the story of “sollermun</hi>
.”

            <app from="pr1665" n="96 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la3344">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">the story of</hi>
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">sollermun</hi>
.”

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="mtp" type="ed" xml:id="de3345">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">the story of sollermun</hi>
.

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23359">
“Blame de pint! I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1659"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr1659" n="96.2 (81-52.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3338">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
I knows what I knows. En mine you, de

          <hi rend="italic">real</hi>
pint is down furder—it’s down deeper. It lays in de way Sollermun was raised. You take a man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1660"/>
dat’s

          <app from="pr1660" n="96.4 (81-52.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3339">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dat’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dats</rdg>
          </app>
got on’y one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1151"/>
er

          <ptr target="#l10302" type="alt" xml:id="te1151"/>
two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1661"/>
chillen:

          <app from="pr1661" n="96.4 (81-52.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3340">
            <lem wit="MS2">chillen:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">chillen;</rdg>
          </app>
is dat man gwyne to be waseful o’ chillen? No, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1662"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr1662" n="96.5 (81-52.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3341">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
; he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1663"/>
can’t

          <app from="pr1663" n="96.5 (81-52.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3342">
            <lem wit="A Cent">can’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cain’t</rdg>
          </app>
’ford it.

          <hi rend="italic">He</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1664"/>
know

          <app from="pr1664" n="96.6 (81-52.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3343">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">know</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">knows</rdg>
          </app>
how to value ’em. But you take a man dat’s got ’bout five million chillen runnin’ roun’ de house, en it’s diffunt.

          <hi rend="italic">He</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1152"/>
as

          <ptr target="#l10304" type="alt" xml:id="te1152"/>
soon chop a chile in two as a cat. Dey’s plenty mo’. A chile er two, mo’ er less, warn’t no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1153"/>
consekens

          <ptr target="#l10306" type="alt" xml:id="te1153"/>
to Sollermun, dad fetch him!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23431">
I never see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1154"/>
such

          <ptr target="#l10308" type="alt" xml:id="te1154"/>
a nigger. If he got a notion in his head once, there warn’t no getting it out again. He was the most down on Solomon of any nigger I ever see.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1155"/>
So

          <ptr target="#l10310" type="alt" xml:id="te1155"/>
I went to talking about other kings, and let Solomon slide. I told about Louis Sixteenth that got his head cut off in France long time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1666"/>
ago

          <app from="pr1666" n="96.14 (81-54.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3346">
            <lem wit="MS2">ago</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">age</rdg>
          </app>
; and about his

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0027"/>
little boy the dolphin, that would a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1667"/>
been a

          <app from="pr1667" n="96.15 (81-54.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3347">
            <lem wit="A">been a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">been</rdg>
          </app>
king, but they took and shut him up in jail, and some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1668"/>
say

          <app from="pr1668" n="96.16 (81-54.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3348">
            <lem wit="A">say</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
he died there.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23468">“Po’ little chap.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23470">
“But some says he got out and got away, and come to America

          <ptr target="#as0109" type="an" xml:id="vn0027"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23474">
“Dat’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1669"/>
good!

          <app from="pr1669" n="96.19 (81-54.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3349">
            <lem wit="A">good!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">good.</rdg>
          </app>
But he’ll be pooty lonesome—dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1670"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1670" n="96.19 (81-54.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3350">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
no kings here, is dey, Huck?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23492">
          <pb n="97" xml:id="pb0097"/>
“No.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23496">
“Den he cain’t git no situation. What he gwyne to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1156"/>
do?”

          <ptr target="#l10312" type="alt" xml:id="te1156"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23501">
“Well, I don’t know.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0028"/>
Some of them gets on the police

          <ptr target="#as0110" type="an" xml:id="vn0028"/>
, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="asm110"/>
some of them learns people how to talk French

          <ptr target="#as0111" type="an" xml:id="avm028"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23511">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1157"/>
Why

          <ptr target="#l10314" type="alt" xml:id="te1157"/>
, Huck,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1158"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1671"/>
doan

          <app from="pr1671" n="97.5 (81-55.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3351">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10316" type="alt" xml:id="te1158"/>
de French people talk de same way we does?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23527">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1672"/>
No,

          <app from="pr1672" n="97.6 (81-55.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3352">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">No</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">No!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1159"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1673"/>
Jim;

          <app from="pr1673" n="97.6 (81-55.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3353">
            <lem wit="A">Jim;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Jim,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10318" type="alt" xml:id="te1159"/>
you couldn’t understand a word they said—not a single word.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23549">“Well, now, I be ding-busted! How do dat come?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23551">
“

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t know; but it’s so. I got some of their jabber out of a book. Spose a man was to come to you and say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1674"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Polly-voo-franzy</hi>
          <app from="pr1674" n="97.10 (81-56.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3354">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Polly-voo-franzy</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Polly voo-franzy</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—what would you think?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23567">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1675"/>
wouldn’

          <app from="pr1675" n="97.12 (81-56.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3355">
            <lem wit="A">wouldn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wouldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1676"/>
nuff’n;

          <app from="pr1676" n="97.12 (81-56.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3356">
            <lem wit="A">nuff’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">noth’n</rdg>
          </app>
I’d take en bust him over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1677"/>
de

          <app from="pr1677" n="97.12 (81-56.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3357">
            <lem wit="A">de</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the</rdg>
          </app>
head. Dat is,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1678"/>
ef

          <app from="pr1678" n="97.13 (81-56.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3358">
            <lem wit="MS2">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">if</rdg>
          </app>
he warn’t white. I wouldn’t ’low no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1679"/>
nigger

          <app from="pr1679" n="97.13 (81-56.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3359">
            <lem wit="A">nigger</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">nigger</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to call me dat.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23611">
“Shucks, it ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1680"/>
calling

          <app from="pr1680" n="97.14 (81-56.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3360">
            <lem wit="A">calling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">calling</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you anything.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1681"/>
It’s

          <app from="pr1681" n="97.14 (81-56.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3361">
            <lem wit="A">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Its</rdg>
          </app>
only

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1682"/>
saying,

          <app from="pr1682" n="97.14 (81-56.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3362">
            <lem wit="MS2">saying,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
saying

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
do you know how to talk French.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23639">
“Well, den, why couldn’t he

          <hi rend="italic">say</hi>
it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23644">
“Why, he

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
a-saying it. That’s a Frenchman’s

          <hi rend="italic">way</hi>
of saying it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23652">
“Well, it’s a blame’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1160"/>
ridicklous

          <ptr target="#l10320" type="alt" xml:id="te1160"/>
way, en I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1683"/>
doan

          <app from="pr1683" n="97.18 (81-57.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3363">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
want to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1161"/>
hear

          <ptr target="#l10322" type="alt" xml:id="te1161"/>
no mo’ ’bout it. Dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1684"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1684" n="97.19 (81-57.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3364">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
no sense in it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23680">
“Looky here,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1685"/>
Jim,

          <app from="pr1685" n="97.20 (81-57.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3365">
            <lem wit="MS2">Jim,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jim;</rdg>
          </app>
does a cat talk

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1162"/>
like

          <ptr target="#l10324" type="alt" xml:id="te1162"/>
we do?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23694">“No, a cat don’t.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23696">“Well, does a cow?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23698">“No, a cow don’t, nuther.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23700">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1164"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1163"/>
“Does

          <ptr target="#l10328" type="alt" xml:id="te1164"/>
a cat talk like a cow, or a cow talk like a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1165"/>
cat?

          <ptr target="#l10330" type="alt" xml:id="te1165"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23710">“No, dey don’t.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23712">
“It’s natural and right for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1686"/>
’em

          <app from="pr1686" n="97.26 (81-58.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3366">
            <lem wit="A">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them</rdg>
          </app>
to talk different from each other, ain’t it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23722">
“ ’Course.”

          <ptr target="#l10326" type="alt" xml:id="te1163"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23725">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1166"/>
And ain’t

          <ptr target="#l10332" type="alt" xml:id="te1166"/>
it natural and right for a cat and a cow to talk different from

          <hi rend="italic">us?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23734">“Why, mos’ sholy it is.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23736">
“Well, then, why ain’t it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1167"/>
natural and right

          <ptr target="#l10334" type="alt" xml:id="te1167"/>
for a

          <hi rend="italic">Frenchman</hi>
to talk different from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1687"/>
us?—you

          <app from="pr1687" n="97.33 (81-59.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la3367">
            <lem wit="C">us?—you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
us?—

              <lb/>
you

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">us? You</rdg>
          </app>
answer me that.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23758">“Is a cat a man, Huck?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23760">“No.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23762">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1168"/>
“Well

          <ptr target="#l10336" type="alt" xml:id="te1168"/>
, den, dey ain’t no sense in a cat talkin’ like a man. Is a cow a man?—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1688"/>
er

          <app from="pr1688" n="97.37 (81-59.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3368">
            <lem wit="A">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or</rdg>
          </app>
is a cow a cat?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23775">“No, she ain’t either of them.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23777">
          <pb n="98" xml:id="pb0098"/>
“Well, den, she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1689"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1689" n="98.1 (81-60.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3369">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
got no business to talk like either one er the yuther of ’em. Is a Frenchman a man?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23788">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23790">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
, den! Dad blame it, why

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1690"/>
doan

          <app from="pr1690" n="98.4 (81-60.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3370">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
he

          <hi rend="italic">talk</hi>
like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1691"/>
man?—you

          <app from="pr1691" n="98.4 (81-60.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3371">
            <lem wit="MS2">man?—you</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">man? You</rdg>
          </app>
answer me

          <hi rend="italic">dat!</hi>
”

          <anchor type="ed" xml:id="nt1001"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23818">
I see it warn’t no use wasting words—you can’t learn a nigger to argue.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1169"/>
So I quit.

          <ptr target="#l10338" type="alt" xml:id="te1169"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0031" type="te" xml:id="tv0031"/>
          <ptr target="#as0106" type="an" xml:id="vn0024"/>
          <ptr target="#l10258" type="alt" xml:id="te1129"/>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0306">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XV.</head>
        <pb n="99" xml:id="pb0099"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23831">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y09901">
            <graphic url="y09901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1692"/>
Chapter XV.

              <app from="pr1692" n="99 title (280.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3372">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XV.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3373">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf9901">
            <graphic url="hf9901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">we would sell the raft.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e23848">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0029"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">
            <sic>e</sic>
judged

          </hi>
that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1170"/>
three nights

          <ptr target="#l10340" type="alt" xml:id="te1170"/>
more would fetch us to

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0030"/>
Cairo

          <ptr target="#as0112" type="an" xml:id="vn0029"/>
, at the bottom of Illinois, where the Ohio

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1693"/>
river

          <app from="pr1693" n="99.4 (280.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3374">
            <lem wit="MS1a">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">River</rdg>
          </app>
comes in, and that was what we was after. We would sell the raft and get on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1694"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr1694" n="99.7 (280.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la3375">
            <lem wit="A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
and go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1695"/>
way

          <app from="pr1695" n="99.7 (280.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3376">
            <lem wit="A">way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">away</rdg>
          </app>
up the Ohio amongst the free States

          <ptr target="#as0113" type="an" xml:id="vn0030"/>
, and then be out of trouble.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23893">
Well, the second night a fog begun to come on, and we made for a tow-head to tie to, for it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1696"/>
wouldn’t

          <app from="pr1696" n="99.13 (280.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3377">
            <lem wit="A">wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">won’t</rdg>
          </app>
do to try to run in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1697"/>
fog,

          <app from="pr1697" n="99.13 (280.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3378">
            <lem wit="MS1a">fog,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fog;</rdg>
          </app>
but when I paddled ahead in the canoe, with the line, to make fast, there warn’t anything but little saplings to tie to. I passed the line around one of them right on the edge of the cut bank,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1171"/>
but

          <ptr target="#l10342" type="alt" xml:id="te1171"/>
there was a stiff

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1698"/>
current

          <app from="pr1698" n="99.19 (281.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3379">
            <lem wit="MS1a">current</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">current,</rdg>
          </app>
and the raft come booming down so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1172"/>
lively

          <ptr target="#l10344" type="alt" xml:id="te1172"/>
she tore it out by the roots and away she went. I see the fog closing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1699"/>
down

          <app from="pr1699" n="99.21 (281.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3380">
            <lem wit="MS1a">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">down,</rdg>
          </app>
and it made me so sick

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1173"/>
and scared

          <ptr target="#l10346" type="alt" xml:id="te1173"/>
I couldn’t budge for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1174"/>
most

          <ptr target="#l10348" type="alt" xml:id="te1174"/>
a half a minute

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1175"/>
it seemed to me

          <ptr target="#l10350" type="alt" xml:id="te1175"/>
—and then there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1700"/>
no

          <app from="pr1700" n="99.22 (281.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3381">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
raft in sight; you couldn’t see twenty yards. I jumped into the canoe and run back to the stern and grabbed the paddle and set her back a stroke. But she didn’t come. I was in such a hurry I hadn’t untied her. I got up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1701"/>
tried

          <app from="pr1701" n="99.26 (282.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3382">
            <lem wit="A">tried</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">staggered back</rdg>
          </app>
to untie her, but I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1702"/>
so excited

          <app from="pr1702" n="99.26 (282.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la3383">
            <lem wit="A">so excited</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sicker than ever, now, and</rdg>
          </app>
my hands shook so I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1703"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1176"/>
couldn’t

          <ptr target="#l10352" type="alt" xml:id="te1176"/>
          <app from="pr1703" n="99.27 (282.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la3384">
            <lem wit="A">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">could n’t</rdg>
          </app>
hardly do anything with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1704"/>
them.

          <app from="pr1704" n="99.27 (282.12–15)" type="e" xml:id="la3385">
            <lem wit="A">them.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">them. I felt like all the blood and all the strength was gone out of me.</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e23992">
As soon as I got started I took out after the raft, hot and heavy, right down the tow-head. That was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1705"/>
right,

          <app from="pr1705" n="99.29 (282.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3386">
            <lem wit="MS1a">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
as far as it went, but the tow-head warn’t sixty yards long, and the minute I flew by the foot of it I shot out into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1706"/>
the solid

          <app from="pr1706" n="99.31 (283.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3387">
            <lem wit="A">the solid</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that solid</rdg>
          </app>
white

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1707"/>
fog

          <app from="pr1707" n="99.31 (283.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la3388">
            <lem wit="C">fog</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">kind of nothingness</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">fog,</rdg>
          </app>
and hadn’t no more idea which way I was going

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1177"/>
than

          <ptr target="#l10354" type="alt" xml:id="te1177"/>
a dead man.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24025">
Thinks I, it won’t do to paddle; first I know I’ll run into the bank

          <pb n="100" xml:id="pb0100"/>
or a tow-head or something;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1178"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l10356" type="alt" xml:id="te1178"/>
got to set still and float, and yet it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1708"/>
mighty fidgety business

          <app from="pr1708" n="100.2 (283.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3389">
            <lem wit="A">mighty fidgety business</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">just nearly death</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1709"/>
to have

          <app from="pr1709" n="100.2 (283.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3390">
            <lem wit="A">to have</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
to have

              <lb/>
to have

            </rdg>
          </app>
to hold your hands still at such a time. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1710"/>
whooped,

          <app from="pr1710" n="100.3 (283.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3391">
            <lem wit="MS1a">whooped,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
whooped

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and listened. Away down there,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1711"/>
somewheres

          <app from="pr1711" n="100.3 (283.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3392">
            <lem wit="A">somewheres</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">somewhere</rdg>
          </app>
, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1712"/>
hears

          <app from="pr1712" n="100.4 (283.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3393">
            <lem wit="A">hears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
a small

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1713"/>
whoop

          <app from="pr1713" n="100.4 (283.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3394">
            <lem wit="MS1a">whoop</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">whoop,</rdg>
          </app>
and up comes my spirits. I went tearing after it, listening sharp to hear it again. The next time it come, I see I warn’t heading for it but heading away to the right of it. And the next time, I was heading away to the left of it—and not gaining on it much, either, for I was flying around, this way and that and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1714"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr1714" n="100.8 (284.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3395">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
, but it was going straight ahead all the time.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24092">
I did wish the fool would think to beat a tin pan, and beat it all the time, but he never did, and it was the still places between the whoops that was making the trouble for me. Well, I fought along, and directly I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1715"/>
hears

          <app from="pr1715" n="100.13 (285.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3396">
            <lem wit="A">hears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
the whoop

          <hi rend="italic">behind</hi>
me. I was tangled good, now. That was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1716"/>
somebody

          <app from="pr1716" n="100.14 (285.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la3397">
            <lem wit="A">somebody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">either somebody</rdg>
          </app>
else’s whoop, or else I was turned around.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24113">
I throwed the paddle down. I heard the whoop again; it was behind me yet, but in a different place; it kept coming, and kept changing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1717"/>
its

          <app from="pr1717" n="100.17 (285.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3398">
            <lem wit="A">its</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3399">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
place, and I kept answering, till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1718"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1718" n="100.17 (285.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3400">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
it was in front of me again and I knowed the current had swung the canoe’s head down stream and I was all right, if that was Jim and not some other raftsman hollering. I couldn’t tell nothing about voices in a fog, for nothing don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1179"/>
look

          <ptr target="#l10358" type="alt" xml:id="te1179"/>
natural nor sound natural in a fog.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24137">
The whooping went on, and in about a minute I come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1719"/>
a booming

          <app from="pr1719" n="100.22 (286.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3401">
            <lem wit="A">a booming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">booming</rdg>
          </app>
down

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1180"/>
on a cut bank with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1720"/>
smoky

          <app from="pr1720" n="100.23 (286.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3402">
            <lem wit="A">smoky</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dim</rdg>
          </app>
ghosts of

          <ptr target="#l10360" type="alt" xml:id="te1180"/>
big trees on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1721"/>
it

          <app from="pr1721" n="100.23 (286.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3403">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it,</rdg>
          </app>
and the current throwed me off to the left and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1722"/>
shot

          <app from="pr1722" n="100.24 (286.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3404">
            <lem wit="A">shot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I shot</rdg>
          </app>
by, amongst a lot of snags that fairly roared, the current was tearing by them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1723"/>
so swift

          <app from="pr1723" n="100.25 (286.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3405">
            <lem wit="A">so swift</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">at such a rate</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24185">
In another second or two it was solid white

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1181"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1724"/>
still

          <ptr target="#l10362" type="alt" xml:id="te1181"/>
again

          <app from="pr1724" n="100.26 (287.3–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3406">
            <lem wit="A">still again</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">still, again, and nothing in sight. I whooped, and waited; whooped again; waited, and whooped again</rdg>
          </app>
. I set perfectly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1725"/>
still

          <app from="pr1725" n="100.27 (287.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3407">
            <lem wit="MS1a">still</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">still,</rdg>
          </app>
then, listening to my heart thump, and I reckon I didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1182"/>
draw

          <ptr target="#l10364" type="alt" xml:id="te1182"/>
a breath while it thumped a hundred.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24213">
I just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1726"/>
give up

          <app from="pr1726" n="100.29 (287.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3408">
            <lem wit="A">give up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">laid down in the canoe</rdg>
          </app>
, then. I knowed what the matter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1727"/>
was. That

          <app from="pr1727" n="100.29 (287.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la3409">
            <lem wit="A">was. That</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
was.—

              <lb/>
That

            </rdg>
          </app>
cut bank was an

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1728"/>
island

          <app from="pr1728" n="100.30 (287.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3410">
            <lem wit="MS1a">island</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">island,</rdg>
          </app>
and Jim had gone down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1729"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr1729" n="100.30 (287.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3411">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
side of it. It warn’t no tow-head, that you could float by in ten minutes. It had the big timber of a regular island; it might be five or six mile long and more than

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1183"/>
a half

          <ptr target="#l10366" type="alt" xml:id="te1183"/>
a mile wide.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24254">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1730"/>
kept quiet, with my ears cocked, about

          <app from="pr1730" n="100.34 (288.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3412">
            <lem wit="A">kept . . . about</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">laid there</rdg>
          </app>
fifteen minutes, I reckon. I was floating along, of course, four or five mile an hour; but you don’t ever think of that. No, you

          <hi rend="italic">feel</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1731"/>
like

          <app from="pr1731" n="100.36 (288.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3413">
            <lem wit="A">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">as if</rdg>
          </app>
you are laying dead still on the water; and if a little glimpse of a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1184"/>
snag

          <ptr target="#l10368" type="alt" xml:id="te1184"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1732"/>
slips

          <app from="pr1732" n="100.37 (288.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3414">
            <lem wit="A">slips</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">skips</rdg>
          </app>
by, you don’t think to yourself how fast

          <hi rend="italic">you’re</hi>
going, but you catch your breath and

          <pb n="101" xml:id="pb0101"/>
think,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1733"/>
My

          <app from="pr1733" n="101.1 (288.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3415">
            <lem wit="MS1a">My</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">my</rdg>
          </app>
! how that snag’s tearing along. If you think it ain’t dismal and lonesome out in a fog that way, by yourself, in the night, you try it once—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1185"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1734"/>
you’ll

          <app from="pr1734" n="101.3 (289.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la3416">
            <lem wit="A">you’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10370" type="alt" xml:id="te1185"/>
see.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y10101">
          <graphic url="y10101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">among the snags</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24315">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1186"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1735"/>
Next,

          <app from="pr1735" n="101.4 (289.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3417">
            <lem wit="A">Next,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Next I set up and listened</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10372" type="alt" xml:id="te1186"/>
for about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1736"/>
a

          <app from="pr1736" n="101.4 (289.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3418">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3419">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
half an hour,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1737"/>
I whoops

          <app from="pr1737" n="101.4 (289.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3420">
            <lem wit="A">I whoops</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and whooped</rdg>
          </app>
now and then; at last I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1738"/>
hears

          <app from="pr1738" n="101.5 (289.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3421">
            <lem wit="A">hears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">heard</rdg>
          </app>
the answer a long ways off, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1739"/>
tries

          <app from="pr1739" n="101.5 (289.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3422">
            <lem wit="A">tries</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">tried</rdg>
          </app>
to follow it, but I couldn’t do it, and directly I judged

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1740"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr1740" n="101.6 (289.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3423">
            <lem wit="A">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I had</rdg>
          </app>
got into a nest of tow-heads, for I had little dim glimpses of them on both sides of me,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1741"/>
sometimes,

          <app from="pr1741" n="101.7 (289.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3424">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sometimes,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
sometimes

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
just a narrow channel between; and some that I couldn’t see, I knowed was there, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1742"/>
I’d hear

          <app from="pr1742" n="101.9 (289.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3425">
            <lem wit="A">I’d hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I heard</rdg>
          </app>
the wash of the current against the old dead brush and trash that hung over the banks. Well, I warn’t long losing the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1743"/>
whoops

          <app from="pr1743" n="101.11 (290.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3426">
            <lem wit="MS1a">whoops</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">whoops,</rdg>
          </app>
down amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1744"/>
tow-heads

          <app from="pr1744" n="101.11 (290.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3427">
            <lem wit="MS1a">tow-heads</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tow-heads;</rdg>
          </app>
and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1187"/>
only

          <ptr target="#l10374" type="alt" xml:id="te1187"/>
tried to chase them a little while, anyway, because it was worse than chasing a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1745"/>
jack-o-lantern

          <app from="pr1745" n="101.13 (290.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3428">
            <lem wit="MS1a">jack-o-lantern</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jack-o-lantern</rdg>
          </app>
. You never knowed a sound dodge around so, and swap places so quick and so much.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24415">
I had to claw away from the bank pretty lively, four or five

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1746"/>
times,

          <app from="pr1746" n="101.15 (290.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3429">
            <lem wit="A">times,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
times

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to keep from knocking the islands out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1747"/>
river,

          <app from="pr1747" n="101.16 (290.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3430">
            <lem wit="MS1a">river,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">river;</rdg>
          </app>
and so I judged the raft must be butting into the bank every now and then, or else it would get further ahead and clear out of hearing—it was floating a little faster than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1748"/>
what

          <app from="pr1748" n="101.19 (291.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3431">
            <lem wit="A">what</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3432">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I was.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24443">
Well, I seemed to be in the open river again,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1749"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr1749" n="101.20 (291.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3433">
            <lem wit="MS1a">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, but I couldn’t hear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1750"/>
no sign of

          <app from="pr1750" n="101.21 (291.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3434">
            <lem wit="A">no sign of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3435">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a whoop nowheres. I reckoned Jim had

          <pb n="102" xml:id="pb0102"/>
fetched up on a snag,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1751"/>
maybe,

          <app from="pr1751" n="102.1 (291.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3436">
            <lem wit="A">maybe,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
maybe

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and it was all up with him. I was good and tired, so I laid down in the canoe and said I wouldn’t bother no more. I didn’t want to go to sleep, of course; but I was so sleepy I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1752"/>
help

          <app from="pr1752" n="102.4 (291.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la3437">
            <lem wit="A">help</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">quite help</rdg>
          </app>
it; so I thought I would take just one little cat-nap.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24481">
But I reckon it was more than a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1753"/>
cat nap

          <app from="pr1753" n="102.5 (292.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3438">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cat nap</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cat-nap</rdg>
          </app>
, for when I waked up the stars was shining bright, the fog was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1754"/>
gone

          <app from="pr1754" n="102.6 (292.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3439">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gone</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">gone,</rdg>
          </app>
and I was spinning down a big bend stern first. First I didn’t know where I was; I thought I was dreaming; and when things begun to come back to me, they seemed to come up dim out of last week.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24499">
It was a monstrous big river here, with the tallest and the thickest kind of timber on both banks; just a solid wall, as well as I could see, by the stars. I looked away down stream, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1755"/>
seen

          <app from="pr1755" n="102.12 (293.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3440">
            <lem wit="A">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">there was</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1188"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l10376" type="alt" xml:id="te1188"/>
black speck on the water. I took out after it; but when I got to it it warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1756"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr1756" n="102.13 (293.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la3441">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
but a couple of saw-logs made fast together. Then I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1757"/>
see

          <app from="pr1757" n="102.14 (293.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3442">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
another speck, and chased that; then another, and this time I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1758"/>
right

          <app from="pr1758" n="102.18 (293.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3443">
            <lem wit="A">right</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">left</rdg>
          </app>
. It was the raft.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24537">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y10201">
            <graphic url="y10201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">asleep on the raft</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24543">
When I got to it Jim was setting there with his head down between his knees, asleep, with his right arm hanging over the steering

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1759"/>
oar. The

          <app from="pr1759" n="102.18–19 (293.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la3444">
            <lem wit="A">oar. The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
oar.—

              <lb/>
The

            </rdg>
          </app>
other oar was smashed off, and the raft was littered up with leaves and branches and dirt. So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1760"/>
she’d

          <app from="pr1760" n="102.20 (294.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3445">
            <lem wit="A">she’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">she had</rdg>
          </app>
had a rough time.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24563">
          <pb n="103" xml:id="pb0103"/>
I made fast and laid down under Jim’s nose on the raft, and begun to gap, and stretch my fists out against Jim, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24567">“Hello, Jim, have I been asleep? Why didn’t you stir me up?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24569">
“Goodness gracious, is dat you, Huck?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1189"/>
En

          <ptr target="#l10378" type="alt" xml:id="te1189"/>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1761"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1761" n="103.4 (294.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3446">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
dead—you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1762"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1762" n="103.5 (294.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3447">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
drownded—you’s back

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1190"/>
agin

          <ptr target="#l10380" type="alt" xml:id="te1190"/>
? It’s too good for true, honey, it’s too good for true. Lemme look at you, chile, lemme feel

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1191"/>
o’

          <ptr target="#l10382" type="alt" xml:id="te1191"/>
you. No, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1763"/>
ain’ dead!

          <app from="pr1763" n="103.7 (294.21–22)" type="e" xml:id="la3448">
            <lem wit="A">ain’ dead!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t dead,</rdg>
          </app>
you’s back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1764"/>
agin, ’live

          <app from="pr1764" n="103.7 (294.22–295.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3449">
            <lem wit="MS1a">agin, ’live</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">agin,’ live</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1192"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10384" type="alt" xml:id="te1192"/>
soun’,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1193"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1765"/>
jis’

          <app from="pr1765" n="103.7 (295.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3450">
            <lem wit="C">jis’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">jes’</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">jis</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10386" type="alt" xml:id="te1193"/>
de same ole

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0040"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1766"/>
Huck—

          <app from="pr1766" n="✱103.8 (295.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3451">
            <lem wit="A">Huck—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Huck,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0040" type="te" xml:id="tv0040"/>
de same

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1767"/>
ole

          <app from="pr1767" n="103.8 (295.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3452">
            <lem wit="A">ole</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ole,</rdg>
          </app>
Huck,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1768"/>
thanks

          <app from="pr1768" n="103.8 (295.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la3453">
            <lem wit="A">thanks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">thanks be</rdg>
          </app>
to goodness!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24660">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1769"/>
“What’s

          <app from="pr1769" n="103.9 (295.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3454">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] “What’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">[¶] I says: [¶] “What’s</rdg>
          </app>
the matter with you, Jim? You been a drinking?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24669">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1194"/>
Drinkin’

          <ptr target="#l10388" type="alt" xml:id="te1194"/>
? Has

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1770"/>
I ben

          <app from="pr1770" n="103.10 (295.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3455">
            <lem wit="A">I ben</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
ben

            </rdg>
          </app>
a drinkin’? Has I had a

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0041"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1195"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1771"/>
chance

          <app from="pr1771" n="✱103.10 (295.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3456">
            <lem wit="A">chance</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
chance/

              <add>chanst</add>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3457">see Alterations</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#te1195" type="alt" xml:id="l10390"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0041" type="te" xml:id="tv0041"/>
to be a drinkin’?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24702">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1196"/>
Well

          <ptr target="#l10392" type="alt" xml:id="te1196"/>
, then, what makes you talk so wild?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24708">“How does I talk wild?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24710">
“

          <hi rend="italic">How?</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1772"/>
Why

          <app from="pr1772" n="103.14 (295.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3458">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">why</rdg>
          </app>
, hain’t you been talking about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1773"/>
my

          <app from="pr1773" n="103.14 (295.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3459">
            <lem wit="A">my</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">me</rdg>
          </app>
coming back, and all that stuff, as if I’d been gone away?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24730">
“Huck—Huck Finn, you look me in de eye; look me in de eye.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1774"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Hain’t</hi>
          <app from="pr1774" n="103.17 (296.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3460">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Hain’t</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Hain’t</rdg>
          </app>
you ben gone away?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24742">
“Gone away?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1775"/>
Why

          <app from="pr1775" n="103.18 (296.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3461">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
what in the nation do you mean?

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
hain’t been gone

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1776"/>
anywheres

          <app from="pr1776" n="103.19 (296.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3462">
            <lem wit="A">anywheres</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">away anywheres</rdg>
          </app>
. Where would I go to?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24763">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1777"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr1777" n="103.20 (296.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3463">
            <lem wit="MS1a">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
, boss, dey’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1778"/>
sumf’n

          <app from="pr1778" n="103.20 (296.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3464">
            <lem wit="A">sumf’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sumfin</rdg>
          </app>
wrong, dey is. Is I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1197"/>
          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
,

          <ptr target="#l10394" type="alt" xml:id="te1197"/>
or who

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
I? Is I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1198"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1779"/>
heah

          <app from="pr1779" n="103.21 (296.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3465">
            <lem wit="A">heah</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
here/

              <add>heah</add>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3466">see Alterations</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10396" type="alt" xml:id="te1198"/>
, or whah

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
I? Now dat’s what I wants to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1780"/>
know.

          <app from="pr1780" n="103.21 (296.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3467">
            <lem wit="C">know.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">know?</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24817">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1781"/>
Well

          <app from="pr1781" n="103.22 (296.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3468">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1782"/>
I think you’re here

          <app from="pr1782" n="103.22 (296.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3469">
            <lem wit="A">I think you’re here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
think you’re here

            </rdg>
          </app>
, plain enough, but I think you’re a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1783"/>
tangle-headed

          <app from="pr1783" n="103.23 (296.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la3470">
            <lem wit="A">tangle-headed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
tangle-

              <lb/>
headed

            </rdg>
          </app>
old fool, Jim.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24847">
“I is, is I? Well you answer me dis. Didn’t you tote out de line in de canoe,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1784"/>
fer

          <app from="pr1784" n="103.25 (297.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3471">
            <lem wit="A">fer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">for</rdg>
          </app>
to make fas’ to de tow-head?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24857">“No, I didn’t. What tow-head? I hain’t seen no tow-head.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24859">
“You hain’t seen no tow-head?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1785"/>
Looky-here

          <app from="pr1785" n="103.27 (297.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3472">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Looky here</rdg>
          </app>
—didn’t de line pull

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1199"/>
loose en

          <ptr target="#l10398" type="alt" xml:id="te1199"/>
de raf’ go a hummin’ down de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1786"/>
river

          <app from="pr1786" n="103.28 (297.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3473">
            <lem wit="A">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">riber</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1200"/>
en leave

          <ptr target="#l10400" type="alt" xml:id="te1200"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1201"/>
you en

          <ptr target="#l10402" type="alt" xml:id="te1201"/>
de canoe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1787"/>
behine

          <app from="pr1787" n="103.29 (297.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la3474">
            <lem wit="A">behine</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">behin’</rdg>
          </app>
in de fog?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24898">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1788"/>
What

          <app from="pr1788" n="103.30 (297.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3475">
            <lem wit="A">What</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">What</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
fog?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e24909">
“Why

          <hi rend="italic">de</hi>
fog. De fog dat’s ben

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1202"/>
aroun’

          <ptr target="#l10404" type="alt" xml:id="te1202"/>
all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1203"/>
night.

          <ptr target="#l10406" type="alt" xml:id="te1203"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1204"/>
En

          <ptr target="#l10408" type="alt" xml:id="te1204"/>
didn’t you whoop,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1205"/>
en didn’t

          <ptr target="#l10410" type="alt" xml:id="te1205"/>
I whoop, tell we got mix’ up in de islands

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1206"/>
en one

          <ptr target="#l10412" type="alt" xml:id="te1206"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1789"/>
un

          <app from="pr1789" n="103.33 (297.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3476">
            <lem wit="A">un</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
us got los’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1207"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10414" type="alt" xml:id="te1207"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1790"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr1790" n="103.33 (297.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3477">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
one was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1208"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1791"/>
jis’

          <app from="pr1791" n="103.33 (297.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3478">
            <lem wit="A">jis’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">jes’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10416" type="alt" xml:id="te1208"/>
as good as los’,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1792"/>
’kase

          <app from="pr1792" n="103.33 (297.22)" type="e" xml:id="la3479">
            <lem wit="A">’kase</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">’case</rdg>
          </app>
he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1793"/>
didn’

          <app from="pr1793" n="103.33 (298.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3480">
            <lem wit="A">didn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
know whah he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1794"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr1794" n="103.34 (298.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3481">
            <lem wit="A">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1209"/>
En

          <ptr target="#l10418" type="alt" xml:id="te1209"/>
didn’t I bust up agin a lot

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1210"/>
er

          <ptr target="#l10420" type="alt" xml:id="te1210"/>
dem islands

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1211"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10422" type="alt" xml:id="te1211"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1795"/>
have

          <app from="pr1795" n="103.35 (298.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3482">
            <lem wit="A">have</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hab</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1212"/>
turrible

          <ptr target="#l10424" type="alt" xml:id="te1212"/>
time

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1213"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10426" type="alt" xml:id="te1213"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1214"/>
mos’

          <ptr target="#l10428" type="alt" xml:id="te1214"/>
git drownded? Now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1796"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr1796" n="103.35 (298.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3483">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
dat so, boss—ain’t it so? You answer me dat.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25029">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1797"/>
Well

          <app from="pr1797" n="103.37 (298.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3484">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
this is too many for me, Jim. I hain’t seen no fog, nor no islands, nor no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1798"/>
troubles

          <app from="pr1798" n="103.38 (298.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3485">
            <lem wit="A">troubles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">trouble</rdg>
          </app>
, nor nothing. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1215"/>
been

          <ptr target="#l10430" type="alt" xml:id="te1215"/>
setting here talking with

          <pb n="104" xml:id="pb0104"/>
you all night till you went to sleep about ten minutes

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1216"/>
ago, and

          <ptr target="#l10432" type="alt" xml:id="te1216"/>
I reckon I done the same. You couldn’t a got drunk in that time, so of course

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1799"/>
you’ve

          <app from="pr1799" n="104.3 (298.22)" type="e" xml:id="la3486">
            <lem wit="A">you’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you</rdg>
          </app>
been dreaming.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25066">“Dad fetch it, how is I gwyne to dream all dat in ten minutes?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25068">“Well, hang it all, you did dream it, because there didn’t any of it happen.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25070">
“But Huck, it’s all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1217"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1800"/>
jis’

          <app from="pr1800" n="104.7 (299.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3487">
            <lem wit="A">jis’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">jes’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10434" type="alt" xml:id="te1217"/>
as plain to me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1801"/>
as—

          <app from="pr1801" n="104.7 (299.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3488">
            <lem wit="MS1a">as—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">as——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25090">
“It don’t make no difference how plain it is, there ain’t nothing in it. I know, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1802"/>
I’ve

          <app from="pr1802" n="104.9 (299.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3489">
            <lem wit="A">I’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I</rdg>
          </app>
been here all the time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25100">
Jim didn’t say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1803"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr1803" n="104.10 (299.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3490">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
for about five minutes, but set there studying over it. Then he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25111">
“Well, den, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1804"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr1804" n="104.12 (299.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3491">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
I did dream it,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1805"/>
Huck,

          <app from="pr1805" n="104.12 (299.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3492">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Huck,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Huck;</rdg>
          </app>
but

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="nv0031"/>
dog my cats

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1806"/>
ef

          <app from="pr1806" n="104.12 (299.22)" type="e" xml:id="la3493">
            <lem wit="A">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">if</rdg>
          </app>
it ain’t de powerfullest dream I ever see

          <ptr target="#as0114" type="an" xml:id="vn0031"/>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1218"/>
En

          <ptr target="#l10436" type="alt" xml:id="te1218"/>
I hain’t ever had no dream

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1807"/>
b’fo’

          <app from="pr1807" n="104.14 (300.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3494">
            <lem wit="A">b’fo’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">befo’</rdg>
          </app>
dat’s tired me like dis one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25155">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1808"/>
O

          <app from="pr1808" n="104.15 (300.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3495">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, well, that’s all right, because a dream

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1809"/>
does

          <app from="pr1809" n="104.15 (300.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3496">
            <lem wit="A">does</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">does</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
tire a body like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1810"/>
everything

          <app from="pr1810" n="104.16 (300.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3497">
            <lem wit="MS1a">everything</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">everything,</rdg>
          </app>
sometimes. But this one was a staving dream—tell me all about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1811"/>
it

          <app from="pr1811" n="104.17 (300.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3498">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it,</rdg>
          </app>
Jim.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25191">
So Jim went to work and told me the whole thing right through, just as it happened, only he painted it up considerable. Then he said he must start in and “ ’terpret” it, because it was sent for a warning. He said the first tow-head

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1219"/>
stood

          <ptr target="#l10438" type="alt" xml:id="te1219"/>
for a man that would try to do us some good, but the current was another man that would get us away from him. The whoops was warnings that would come to us every now and then, and if we didn’t try hard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1812"/>
to make

          <app from="pr1812" n="104.24 (301.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3499">
            <lem wit="A">to make</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and make</rdg>
          </app>
out to understand them they’d just take us into bad luck,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1813"/>
’stead

          <app from="pr1813" n="104.25 (301.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3500">
            <lem wit="A">’stead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">instead</rdg>
          </app>
of keeping us out of it. The lot of tow-heads was troubles we was going to get into with quarrelsome people and all kinds of mean folks, but if we minded our business and didn’t talk back and aggravate them, we would pull through and get out of the fog and into the big clear river, which was the free States, and wouldn’t have no more trouble.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25214">
It had clouded

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1220"/>
up pretty dark

          <ptr target="#l10440" type="alt" xml:id="te1220"/>
just after I got onto the raft, but it was clearing up again, now.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25220">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1221"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1814"/>
O

          <app from="pr1814" n="104.33 (302.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3501">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10442" type="alt" xml:id="te1221"/>
, well, that’s all interpreted well enough, as far as it goes, Jim,” I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1815"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1815" n="104.34 (302.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3502">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says;</rdg>
          </app>
“but what does

          <hi rend="italic">these</hi>
things stand for?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25244">It was the leaves and rubbish on the raft, and the smashed oar. You could see them first rate, now.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25246">
Jim looked at the trash, and then looked at me, and back at the trash again. He had got the dream fixed so strong in his head that he

          <pb n="105" xml:id="pb0105"/>
couldn’t seem to shake it loose and get the facts back into its

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1222"/>
place

          <ptr target="#l10444" type="alt" xml:id="te1222"/>
again, right away. But when he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1223"/>
did get

          <ptr target="#l10446" type="alt" xml:id="te1223"/>
the thing straightened around, he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1224"/>
looked at me steady, without ever smiling, and

          <ptr target="#l10448" type="alt" xml:id="te1224"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25263">
“What do dey

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1225"/>
stan’

          <ptr target="#l10450" type="alt" xml:id="te1225"/>
for?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1226"/>
I’s gwyne to tell you.

          <ptr target="#l10452" type="alt" xml:id="te1226"/>
When I got all wore

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1227"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1816"/>
out,

          <app from="pr1816" n="105.5 (303.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3503">
            <lem wit="MS1a">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
wid work, en wid de callin’ for you, en

          <ptr target="#l10454" type="alt" xml:id="te1227"/>
went to sleep, my heart

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1817"/>
wuz

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1228"/>
mos’

          <app from="pr1817" n="105.6 (303.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3504">
            <lem wit="A">wuz mos’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was mos’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10456" type="alt" xml:id="te1228"/>
broke

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1229"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1818"/>
bekase

          <app from="pr1818" n="105.6 (303.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3505">
            <lem wit="A">bekase</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">becase</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10458" type="alt" xml:id="te1229"/>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1819"/>
wuz los’

          <app from="pr1819" n="105.6 (303.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3506">
            <lem wit="A">wuz los’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was los’</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1230"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10460" type="alt" xml:id="te1230"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1820"/>
didn’ k’yer

          <app from="pr1820" n="105.6 (303.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3507">
            <lem wit="A">didn’ k’yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">didn’t care</rdg>
          </app>
no mo’ what become

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1821"/>
er

          <app from="pr1821" n="105.7 (303.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3508">
            <lem wit="A">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1231"/>
me en

          <ptr target="#l10462" type="alt" xml:id="te1231"/>
de raf’.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1232"/>
En

          <ptr target="#l10464" type="alt" xml:id="te1232"/>
when I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1822"/>
wake’

          <app from="pr1822" n="105.7 (304.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3509">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wake’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wake</rdg>
          </app>
up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1233"/>
en fine

          <ptr target="#l10466" type="alt" xml:id="te1233"/>
you back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1823"/>
agin

          <app from="pr1823" n="105.7 (304.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3510">
            <lem wit="C">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">agin’</rdg>
          </app>
, all safe en

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1234"/>
soun’

          <ptr target="#l10468" type="alt" xml:id="te1234"/>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1235"/>
de tears come en

          <ptr target="#l10470" type="alt" xml:id="te1235"/>
I could a got down on my knees

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1236"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10472" type="alt" xml:id="te1236"/>
kiss’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1824"/>
yo’

          <app from="pr1824" n="105.9 (304.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3511">
            <lem wit="A">yo’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you</rdg>
          </app>
foot

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1237"/>
I’s

          <ptr target="#l10474" type="alt" xml:id="te1237"/>
so thankful.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1238"/>
En

          <ptr target="#l10476" type="alt" xml:id="te1238"/>
all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1825"/>
you wuz

          <app from="pr1825" n="105.9 (304.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la3512">
            <lem wit="A">you wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
was

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1826"/>
thinkin’

          <app from="pr1826" n="105.9 (304.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3513">
            <lem wit="C">thinkin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a thinkin’</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">thinkin</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1827"/>
’bout

          <app from="pr1827" n="105.9 (304.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3514">
            <lem wit="MS1a">’bout,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’bout</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1828"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr1828" n="105.9 (304.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3515">
            <lem wit="A">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
how you could make a fool

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1829"/>
uv

          <app from="pr1829" n="105.10 (304.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3516">
            <lem wit="A">uv</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
ole Jim wid a lie. Dat truck dah is

          <hi rend="italic">trash;</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1239"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10478" type="alt" xml:id="te1239"/>
trash is what people is dat puts dirt on de head

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1240"/>
er

          <ptr target="#l10480" type="alt" xml:id="te1240"/>
dey fren’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1241"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10482" type="alt" xml:id="te1241"/>
makes ’em ashamed.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25454">
Then he got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1830"/>
up,

          <app from="pr1830" n="105.13 (304.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3517">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
slow, and walked to the wigwam, and went in there, without saying anything but that. But that was enough. It made me feel so mean I could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1831"/>
almost

          <app from="pr1831" n="105.15 (304.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3518">
            <lem wit="A">almost</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">amost</rdg>
          </app>
kissed

          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
foot to get him to take it back.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25475">
It was fifteen minutes before I could work myself up to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1242"/>
go

          <ptr target="#l10484" type="alt" xml:id="te1242"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1243"/>
humble

          <ptr target="#l10486" type="alt" xml:id="te1243"/>
myself to a nigger—but I done it, and I warn’t ever sorry for it afterwards, neither. I didn’t do him no more mean tricks, and I wouldn’t done that one if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1832"/>
I’d a

          <app from="pr1832" n="105.20 (305.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3519">
            <lem wit="A">I’d a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I had</rdg>
          </app>
knowed it would make him feel that way.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0310">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XVI.</head>
        <pb n="106" xml:id="pb0106"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25498">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y10601">
            <graphic url="y10601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1833"/>
Chapter XVI.

              <app from="pr1833" n="106 title (306 title)" type="e" xml:id="la3520">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XVI.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">CHAP.</rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1061">
            <graphic url="hf1061.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">
it

                <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1840"/>
                <hi rend="italic">amounted</hi>
                <app from="pr1840" n="106 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3527">
                  <lem wit="C">
                    <hi rend="italic">
                      <hi rend="smallcaps">amounted</hi>
                    </hi>
                  </lem>
                  <rdg wit="MS1a">
                    <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3528">not in</note>
                  </rdg>
                  <rdg wit="A">
                    <hi rend="smallcaps">amounted</hi>
                  </rdg>
                </app>
to something

                <lb/>
being a raftsman.

              </hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e25529">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">
            <sic>e</sic>
slept

          </hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1834"/>
most

          <app from="pr1834" n="106.1 (306.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3521">
            <lem wit="A">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pretty much</rdg>
          </app>
all day, and started

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1835"/>
out,

          <app from="pr1835" n="106.2 (306.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3522">
            <lem wit="MS1a">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at night, a little ways behind a monstrous long raft that was as long going by as a procession. She had four long sweeps at each end, so we judged she carried as many as thirty men, likely. She had five big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1836"/>
wigwams

          <app from="pr1836" n="106.8 (306.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3523">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wigwams</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
wig-

              <lb/>
wams

            </rdg>
          </app>
aboard, wide apart, and an open camp fire in the middle, and a tall

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1837"/>
flag pole

          <app from="pr1837" n="106.10–11 (307.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3524">
            <lem wit="MS1a">flag pole</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
flag-

              <lb/>
pole

            </rdg>
          </app>
at each end. There was a power of style about her. It

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1244"/>
          <hi rend="italic">amounted</hi>
          <ptr target="#l10488" type="alt" xml:id="te1244"/>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1245"/>
something

          <ptr target="#l10490" type="alt" xml:id="te1245"/>
being a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1838"/>
raftsman

          <app from="pr1838" n="106.14 (307.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la3525">
            <lem wit="A">raftsman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
rafts-

              <lb/>
man

            </rdg>
          </app>
on such a craft as that.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25591">
We went drifting down into a big bend, and the night clouded up and got hot. The river was very

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1839"/>
wide

          <app from="pr1839" n="106.18 (307.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3526">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wide</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wide,</rdg>
          </app>
and was walled with solid timber on both sides; you couldn’t see a break in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1841"/>
it,

          <app from="pr1841" n="106.19 (307.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3529">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
hardly ever, or a light. We talked about Cairo, and wondered whether we would know it when we got to it. I said likely we wouldn’t, because I had heard say there warn’t but about a dozen houses there, and if they didn’t happen to have them lit up, how was we going to know we was passing a town? Jim said if the two big rivers joined together there, that would show. But I said maybe we might think we was passing the foot of an island and coming into the same old river again. That disturbed Jim—and me too. So the question was, what to do? I said, paddle ashore the first time a light showed, and tell them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1842"/>
pap

          <app from="pr1842" n="106.29 (308.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3530">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1246"/>
behind,

          <ptr target="#l10492" type="alt" xml:id="te1246"/>
coming along with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1843"/>
trading scow

          <app from="pr1843" n="106.29 (308.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3531">
            <lem wit="MS1a">trading scow</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">trading-scow</rdg>
          </app>
, and was a green hand at the business, and wanted to know how far it was to Cairo. Jim thought

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1247"/>
it was

          <ptr target="#l10494" type="alt" xml:id="te1247"/>
a good idea, so we took a smoke on it and waited.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25635">
          <pb n="107" xml:id="pb0107"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0001"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1844"/>
But you know a young person can’t wait very well when

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1248"/>
he is

          <ptr target="#l10496" type="alt" xml:id="te1248"/>
impatient to find a thing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1845"/>
out

          <app from="pr1845" n="107.2 (309.9–14)" type="e" xml:id="la3534">
            <lem wit="LoM">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">out; so we hadn’t gone more than about four hundred yards before I got tired of it and wanted to think up some other way</rdg>
          </app>
. We talked it over, and by and by Jim said it was such a black night, now, that it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1846"/>
wouldn’t

          <app from="pr1846" n="107.3 (309.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3535">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">would n’t</rdg>
          </app>
be no

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0042"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1847"/>
resk

          <app from="pr1847" n="✱107.3 (309.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3536">
            <lem wit="C">resk</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a LoM">risk</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0042" type="te" xml:id="tv0042"/>
to swim down to the big raft and crawl aboard and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1848"/>
listen

          <app from="pr1848" n="107.4 (309.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3537">
            <lem wit="MS1a">listen</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">listen,</rdg>
          </app>
—they would talk about Cairo, because they would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1249"/>
be calculating to go

          <ptr target="#l10498" type="alt" xml:id="te1249"/>
ashore there for a spree, maybe, or anyway they would send boats ashore to buy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1849"/>
whisky

          <app from="pr1849" n="107.7 (310.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3538">
            <lem wit="MS1a">whisky</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">whiskey</rdg>
          </app>
or fresh meat or something. Jim had a wonderful level head, for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1850"/>
nigger;

          <app from="pr1850" n="107.8 (310.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3539">
            <lem wit="MS1a">nigger;</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">nigger:</rdg>
          </app>
he could most always start a good

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1250"/>
plan

          <ptr target="#l10500" type="alt" xml:id="te1250"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1251"/>
when

          <ptr target="#l10502" type="alt" xml:id="te1251"/>
you wanted one.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y10701">
          <graphic url="y10701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">
i swum

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1851"/>
down

            </hi>
            <app from="pr1851" n="107 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3540">
              <lem wit="C">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">down</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1a LoM">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3541">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">along the raft.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25725">
I stood up and shook my rags off and jumped into the river, and struck out for the raft’s light. By and by, when I got down nearly to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1852"/>
her

          <app from="pr1852" n="107.12 (310.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3542">
            <lem wit="MS1a">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">her,</rdg>
          </app>
I eased up and went slow and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1853"/>
cautious. But

          <app from="pr1853" n="107.12 (310.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la3543">
            <lem wit="LoM">cautious. But</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
cautious.—

              <lb/>
But

            </rdg>
          </app>
everything was all right—nobody at the sweeps. So I swum down along the raft till I was most abreast the camp fire in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1854"/>
middle. Then

          <app from="pr1854" n="107.14 (311.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3544">
            <lem wit="MS1a">middle. Then</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">middle, then</rdg>
          </app>
I crawled aboard and inched along and got in amongst some bundles of shingles on the weather side of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1855"/>
fire. There

          <app from="pr1855" n="107.16 (311.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la3545">
            <lem wit="LoM">fire. There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
fire.—

              <lb/>
There

            </rdg>
          </app>
was thirteen men there—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1252"/>
they was

          <ptr target="#l10504" type="alt" xml:id="te1252"/>
the watch on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1856"/>
deck,

          <app from="pr1856" n="107.17 (311.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3546">
            <lem wit="MS1a">deck,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
deck

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of course. And a mighty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1857"/>
rough looking

          <app from="pr1857" n="107.17 (311.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3547">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rough looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
rough-

              <lb/>
looking

            </rdg>
          </app>
lot, too. They had a jug, and tin cups, and they kept the jug moving. One man was singing—roaring, you may say; and it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1858"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0043"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr1858" n="✱107.19 (311.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3548">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">was n’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0043" type="te" xml:id="tv0043"/>
a nice song—for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1859"/>
parlor,

          <app from="pr1859" n="107.20 (311.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3549">
            <lem wit="MS1a">parlor,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
parlor

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1860"/>
anyway

          <app from="pr1860" n="107.20 (311.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3550">
            <lem wit="LoM">anyway</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
any-

              <lb/>
way

            </rdg>
          </app>
. He roared through his nose, and strung out the last word of every line very long. When he was done they all fetched a kind of Injun war-whoop, and then another

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1861"/>
was

          <app from="pr1861" n="107.22 (312.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3551">
            <lem wit="LoM">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">one</rdg>
          </app>
sung. It

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1862"/>
begun:

          <app from="pr1862" n="107.23 (312.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3552">
            <lem wit="MS1a">begun:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">begun:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <pb n="108" xml:id="pb0108"/>
          <lg>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">
              <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0044"/>
              <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0003"/>
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0018"/>
“There was a woman in our towdn,

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
In our towdn did

              <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0045"/>
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1253"/>
dwed’l

              <ptr target="#l10506" type="alt" xml:id="te1253"/>
(dwell,)

              <ptr target="#tb0045" type="te" xml:id="tv0045"/>
            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">She loved her husband dear-i-lee,</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
But another man twyste as

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1863"/>
wed’l.

            </l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1254"/>
Singing

              <ptr target="#l10508" type="alt" xml:id="te1254"/>
              <app from="pr1863" n="108.4–5 (312.6–8)" type="e" xml:id="la3553">
                <lem wit="LoM">
wed’l.

                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3554">extra line space</note>
Singing

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
wed’l.

                  <lb/>
Singing

                </rdg>
              </app>
too, riloo, riloo, riloo,

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
Ri-too, riloo,

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1864"/>
rilay - - - - e

              <app from="pr1864" n="108.6 (312.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3555">
                <lem wit="MS1a">rilay - - - - e</lem>
                <rdg wit="LoM">rilay - - - e</rdg>
              </app>
,

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">She loved her husband dear-i-lee,</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
But another man twyste as wed’l.”

              <ptr target="#tb0044" type="te" xml:id="tv0044"/>
              <ptr target="#as0116" type="an" xml:id="gs0004"/>
              <ptr target="#mt0018" type="alt" xml:id="wn0018"/>
            </l>
          </lg>
        </quote>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e25886">
And so on—fourteen verses. It was kind of poor, and when he was going to start on the next

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1255"/>
verse

          <ptr target="#l10510" type="alt" xml:id="te1255"/>
one of them said it was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0005"/>
the tune the old cow died on

          <ptr target="#as0117" type="an" xml:id="gs0006"/>
; and another one said, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1865"/>
O

          <app from="pr1865" n="108.11 (312.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3556">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, give us a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1866"/>
rest;” and

          <app from="pr1866" n="108.11 (312.18–19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3557">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rest;” and</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">rest.” And</rdg>
          </app>
another one told him to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1256"/>
take

          <ptr target="#l10512" type="alt" xml:id="te1256"/>
a walk. They made fun of him till he got mad and jumped up and begun to cuss the crowd, and said he could lam any thief in the lot.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25917">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1257"/>
They was

          <ptr target="#l10514" type="alt" xml:id="te1257"/>
all about to make a break for him, but the biggest man there jumped up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1867"/>
says:

          <app from="pr1867" n="108.16 (313.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3558">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25930">
“Set whar you are, gentlemen. Leave him to me;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1868"/>
he’s

          <app from="pr1868" n="108.17 (313.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3559">
            <lem wit="MS1a">he’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">he ’s</rdg>
          </app>
my meat.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y10801">
          <graphic url="y10801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">he jumped up in the air.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25946">
Then he jumped up in the air three times and cracked his heels

          <pb n="109" xml:id="pb0109"/>
together every time. He flung off a buckskin coat that was all hung with fringes, and says, “You lay thar tell the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1869"/>
chawin-up’s

          <app from="pr1869" n="109.2 (313.20–21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3560">
            <lem wit="MS1a">chawin-up’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">chawin-up ’s</rdg>
          </app>
done;” and flung his hat down, which was all over ribbons, and says, “You lay thar tell his sufferins is over.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25958">
Then he jumped up in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1258"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l10516" type="alt" xml:id="te1258"/>
air and cracked his heels together again and shouted

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1870"/>
out:

          <app from="pr1870" n="109.6 (314.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3561">
            <lem wit="MS1a">out:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">out:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e25971">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0007"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1871"/>
Whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1871" n="109.7 (314.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3562">
            <lem wit="LoM">Whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Whoop</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1872"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1872" n="109.7 (314.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3563">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
the old original iron-jawed,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1873"/>
brass-mounted

          <app from="pr1873" n="109.7 (314.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la3564">
            <lem wit="LoM">brass-mounted</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
brass-

              <lb/>
mounted

            </rdg>
          </app>
, copper-bellied

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0019"/>
corpse-maker from the

          <ptr target="#mt0019" type="alt" xml:id="wn0019"/>
wilds of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1874"/>
Arkansaw! Look

          <app from="pr1874" n="109.8 (314.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la3565">
            <lem wit="C">Arkansaw! Look</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Arkansaw!—

              <lb/>
              <hi rend="italic">Look</hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Arkansaw!—Look</rdg>
          </app>
at me!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1875"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1875" n="109.9 (314.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3566">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
the man they call Sudden Death and General Desolation! Sired by a hurricane, dam’d by an

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1876"/>
earthquake

          <app from="pr1876" n="109.10 (314.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3567">
            <lem wit="LoM">earthquake</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">arthquake</rdg>
          </app>
, half-brother to the cholera, nearly related to the small-pox on the mother’s side! Look at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1877"/>
me! I

          <app from="pr1877" n="109.11 (314.21–315.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3568">
            <lem wit="LoM">me! I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
me!—

              <milestone unit="page"/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1259"/>
take

          <ptr target="#l10518" type="alt" xml:id="te1259"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1260"/>
nineteen

          <ptr target="#l10520" type="alt" xml:id="te1260"/>
alligators and a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1261"/>
bar’l

          <ptr target="#l10522" type="alt" xml:id="te1261"/>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1878"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1262"/>
whisky

          <ptr target="#l10524" type="alt" xml:id="te1262"/>
          <app from="pr1878" n="109.12 (315.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3569">
            <lem wit="MS1a">whisky</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">whiskey</rdg>
          </app>
for breakfast when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1879"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1879" n="109.13 (315.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3570">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
in robust health, and a bushel of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1880"/>
rattlesnakes

          <app from="pr1880" n="109.13 (315.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3571">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rattlesnakes</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
rattle-

              <lb/>
snakes

            </rdg>
          </app>
and a dead body when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1881"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1881" n="109.14 (315.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3572">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
ailing! I split the everlasting rocks with my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1882"/>
glance

          <app from="pr1882" n="109.14 (315.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3573">
            <lem wit="MS1a">glance</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">glance,</rdg>
          </app>
and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1263"/>
squench

          <ptr target="#l10526" type="alt" xml:id="te1263"/>
the thunder when I speak!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1883"/>
Whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1883" n="109.15 (315.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3574">
            <lem wit="LoM">Whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Whoop</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1884"/>
stand

          <app from="pr1884" n="109.15 (315.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3575">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stand</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Stand</rdg>
          </app>
back and give me room according to my strength!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1885"/>
Blood’s

          <app from="pr1885" n="109.17 (315.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3576">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Blood’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Blood ’s</rdg>
          </app>
my natural drink, and the wails of the dying is music to my ear! Cast your eye on me,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1886"/>
gentlemen

          <app from="pr1886" n="109.19–20 (315.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3577">
            <lem wit="LoM">gentlemen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
gentle-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
!—and lay

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1887"/>
low,

          <app from="pr1887" n="109.20 (315.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3578">
            <lem wit="MS1a">low,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
low

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and hold your breath, for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1888"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1888" n="109.21 (315.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3579">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0046"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1889"/>
’bout

          <app from="pr1889" n="✱109.21 (315.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3580">
            <lem wit="C">’bout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">about</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">bout</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0046" type="te" xml:id="tv0046"/>
to turn myself loose!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y10901">
          <graphic url="y10901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">
went around in a

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1895"/>
little

            </hi>
            <app from="pr1895" n="109 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3586">
              <lem wit="C">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">little</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1a LoM">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3587">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">circle.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26187">
All the time he was getting this off, he was shaking his head and looking fierce, and kind of swelling around in a little circle, tucking up his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1890"/>
wristbands

          <app from="pr1890" n="109.27 (316.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3581">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wristbands</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">wrist-bands</rdg>
          </app>
, and now and then straightening up and beating his breast with his fist,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1891"/>
saying

          <app from="pr1891" n="109.29 (316.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3582">
            <lem wit="MS1a">saying</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">saying,</rdg>
          </app>
“Look at me, gentlemen!” When he got through, he jumped up and cracked his heels together three times,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1264"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l10528" type="alt" xml:id="te1264"/>
let off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1265"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l10530" type="alt" xml:id="te1265"/>
roaring “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1892"/>
whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1892" n="109.33 (316.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3583">
            <lem wit="LoM">whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Whoop</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1893"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1893" n="109.33 (316.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3584">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
the bloodiest son of a wildcat that lives!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26231">
Then the man that had started the row

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1266"/>
tilted his old slouch hat

          <ptr target="#l10532" type="alt" xml:id="te1266"/>
down over his right eye; then he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1894"/>
bent,

          <app from="pr1894" n="109.38 (316.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3585">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bent,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
bent

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="110" xml:id="pb0110"/>
stooping forward, with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1267"/>
his back sagged and

          <ptr target="#l10534" type="alt" xml:id="te1267"/>
his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1896"/>
south

          <app from="pr1896" n="110.1 (316.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3588">
            <lem wit="LoM">south</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hind</rdg>
          </app>
end sticking out far, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1268"/>
his fists a-shoving

          <ptr target="#l10536" type="alt" xml:id="te1268"/>
out and drawing in in front of him, and so went around in a little circle about three times, swelling himself up and breathing hard. Then he straightened, and jumped up and cracked his heels together three times before he lit again (that made them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1897"/>
cheer)

          <app from="pr1897" n="110.6 (317.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3589">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cheer)</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">cheer),</rdg>
          </app>
and he begun to shout like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1898"/>
this:

          <app from="pr1898" n="110.6 (317.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3590">
            <lem wit="MS1a">this:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">this:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26279">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1899"/>
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0009"/>
Whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1899" n="110.7 (317.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3591">
            <lem wit="C">[¶] “Whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">[¶] “Whoop</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3592">flush left</note>
“Whoo-oop

            </rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1900"/>
Bow

          <app from="pr1900" n="110.7 (317.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3593">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Bow</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">bow</rdg>
          </app>
your neck and spread

          <ptr target="#as0119" type="an" xml:id="gs0010"/>
, for the kingdom of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1901"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1269"/>
sorrow’s

          <ptr target="#l10538" type="alt" xml:id="te1269"/>
          <app from="pr1901" n="110.7–8 (317.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3594">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sorrow’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">sorrow ’s</rdg>
          </app>
a-coming! Hold me down to the earth, for I feel my powers a-working!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1902"/>
whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1902" n="110.9 (317.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3595">
            <lem wit="LoM">whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Whoop</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1903"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1903" n="110.9 (317.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3596">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
a child of sin,

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
let me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1904"/>
get

          <app from="pr1904" n="110.9 (317.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3597">
            <lem wit="LoM">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">git</rdg>
          </app>
a start! Smoked glass, here, for all!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1905"/>
don’t

          <app from="pr1905" n="110.10 (317.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3598">
            <lem wit="MS1a">don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Don’t</rdg>
          </app>
attempt to look at me with the naked eye,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1906"/>
gentlemen

          <app from="pr1906" n="110.11 (317.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3599">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gentlemen</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
gentle-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
! When

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1907"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1907" n="110.11 (317.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3600">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
playful I use the meridians of longitude and parallels of latitude

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1270"/>
for a seine,

          <ptr target="#l10540" type="alt" xml:id="te1270"/>
and drag the Atlantic

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1908"/>
ocean

          <app from="pr1908" n="110.12 (318.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3601">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ocean</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Ocean</rdg>
          </app>
for whales! I scratch my head with the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1271"/>
lightning

          <ptr target="#l10542" type="alt" xml:id="te1271"/>
and purr myself to sleep with the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1272"/>
thunder

          <ptr target="#l10544" type="alt" xml:id="te1272"/>
! When

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1909"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1909" n="110.14 (318.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3602">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
cold, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1910"/>
bile

          <app from="pr1910" n="110.14 (318.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3603">
            <lem wit="LoM">bile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">b’ile</rdg>
          </app>
the Gulf of Mexico and bathe in it; when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1911"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1911" n="110.15 (318.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3604">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
hot I fan myself with an equinoctial storm; when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1912"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1912" n="110.16 (318.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3605">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1273"/>
thirsty

          <ptr target="#l10546" type="alt" xml:id="te1273"/>
I reach up and suck a cloud dry like a sponge; when I range the earth hungry, famine follows

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1274"/>
in my tracks

          <ptr target="#l10548" type="alt" xml:id="te1274"/>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1913"/>
Whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1913" n="110.18 (318.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3606">
            <lem wit="C">Whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Whoop</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
Whoo-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
oop

            </rdg>
          </app>
! Bow your neck and spread! I put my hand on the sun’s face and make it night in the earth; I bite a piece out of the moon and hurry the seasons; I shake myself and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1914"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1275"/>
crumble

          <ptr target="#l10550" type="alt" xml:id="te1275"/>
          <app from="pr1914" n="110.20 (318.22)" type="e" xml:id="la3607">
            <lem wit="LoM">crumble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
disturb/

              <add>crumble</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the mountains! Contemplate me through leather—

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
use the naked eye!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1915"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr1915" n="110.21 (319.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3608">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
the man with a petrified heart and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1916"/>
biler-iron

          <app from="pr1916" n="110.22 (319.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la3609">
            <lem wit="LoM">biler-iron</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
b’iler-

              <lb/>
iron

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1917"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1276"/>
bowels

          <ptr target="#l10552" type="alt" xml:id="te1276"/>
          <app from="pr1917" n="110.22 (319.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3610">
            <lem wit="LoM">bowels</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
bowels/

              <add>innards</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1277"/>
The

          <ptr target="#l10554" type="alt" xml:id="te1277"/>
massacre of isolated communities is the pastime of my idle moments, the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1278"/>
destruction

          <ptr target="#l10556" type="alt" xml:id="te1278"/>
of nationalities the serious business of my life! The boundless vastness of the

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0047"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1918"/>
great American desert

          <app from="pr1918" n="✱110.25 (319.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3611">
            <lem wit="LoM">great American desert</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Great American Desert</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0047" type="te" xml:id="tv0047"/>
is my enclosed property, and I bury my dead on my own

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1279"/>
premises!”

          <ptr target="#l10558" type="alt" xml:id="te1279"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26513">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1919"/>
He

          <app from="pr1919" n="110.27 (319.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3612">
            <lem wit="MS1a">[¶] He</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3613">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
He

            </rdg>
          </app>
jumped up and cracked his heels together three times before he lit (they cheered him again), and as he come down he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1920"/>
shouted

          <app from="pr1920" n="110.28 (320.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3614">
            <lem wit="LoM">shouted</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">shouts</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1280"/>
out:

          <ptr target="#l10560" type="alt" xml:id="te1280"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1281"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1921"/>
Whoo-oop

          <app from="pr1921" n="110.29 (320.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3615">
            <lem wit="LoM">Whoo-oop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Whoop</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1922"/>
Bow

          <app from="pr1922" n="110.29 (320.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3616">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Bow</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">bow</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10562" type="alt" xml:id="te1281"/>
your neck and spread, for the pet child of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1923"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1282"/>
Calamity’s

          <ptr target="#l10564" type="alt" xml:id="te1282"/>
          <app from="pr1923" n="110.29–30 (320.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3617">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Calamity’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">calamity’s</rdg>
          </app>
a-coming!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26567">
Then the other one went to swelling around and blowing again—the first one—the one they called Bob;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1283"/>
next

          <ptr target="#l10566" type="alt" xml:id="te1283"/>
, the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1284"/>
Child

          <ptr target="#l10568" type="alt" xml:id="te1284"/>
of Calamity chipped in again, bigger than ever; then they both got at it at the same time, swelling round and round each other and punching their fists most into each other’s faces, and whooping and jawing like Injuns; then Bob called the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1285"/>
Child names

          <ptr target="#l10570" type="alt" xml:id="te1285"/>
, and the Child called him names back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1924"/>
again;

          <app from="pr1924" n="110.37 (320.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3618">
            <lem wit="MS1a">again;</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">again:</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1286"/>
next

          <ptr target="#l10572" type="alt" xml:id="te1286"/>
, Bob called him a heap rougher names and the Child come back at him with the very worst kind of language;

          <pb n="111" xml:id="pb0111"/>
next, Bob knocked the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1287"/>
Child’s

          <ptr target="#l10574" type="alt" xml:id="te1287"/>
hat off, and the Child picked it up and kicked

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1288"/>
Bob’s

          <ptr target="#l10576" type="alt" xml:id="te1288"/>
ribbony hat about six foot; Bob went and got it and said never mind, this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1925"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr1925" n="111.3 (321.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3619">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
going to be the last of this thing, because he was a man that never forgot and never forgive, and so the Child better look out, for there was a time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1926"/>
a-coming

          <app from="pr1926" n="111.5 (321.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3620">
            <lem wit="LoM">a-coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">coming</rdg>
          </app>
, just as sure as he was a living man, that he would have to answer

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1289"/>
to him

          <ptr target="#l10578" type="alt" xml:id="te1289"/>
with the best blood in his body. The Child said no man was willinger than he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1927"/>
was,

          <app from="pr1927" n="111.7 (322.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3621">
            <lem wit="MS1a">was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for that time to come, and he would give Bob fair warning,

          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
, never to cross his path again, for he could never rest till he had waded in his blood, for such was his nature, though he was sparing him now on account of his family, if he had one.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26638">
Both of them was edging away in different directions, growling and shaking their heads and going on about what they was going to do; but a little

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1290"/>
black-whiskered

          <ptr target="#l10580" type="alt" xml:id="te1290"/>
chap skipped up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1928"/>
says:

          <app from="pr1928" n="111.14 (322.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3622">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26651">
“Come back here, you couple of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1929"/>
chicken-livered

          <app from="pr1929" n="111.15 (323.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la3623">
            <lem wit="LoM">chicken-livered</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
chicken-

              <lb/>
livered

            </rdg>
          </app>
cowards, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1930"/>
I’ll

          <app from="pr1930" n="111.16 (323.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3624">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
thrash the two of ye!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26671">
And he done it, too. He snatched them, he jerked them this way and that, he booted them around, he knocked them sprawling faster than they could get up. Why, it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1931"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr1931" n="111.19 (323.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3625">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
two minutes till they begged like dogs—and how the other lot did yell and laugh and clap their hands all the way through, and shout “Sail in, Corpse-Maker!” “Hi! at him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1932"/>
again

          <app from="pr1932" n="111.22 (323.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3626">
            <lem wit="LoM">again</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">agin</rdg>
          </app>
, Child of Calamity!” “Bully for you, little Davy!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26689">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1933"/>
Well

          <app from="pr1933" n="111.23 (323.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3627">
            <lem wit="MS1a">[¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3628">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, it was a perfect pow-wow for a while. Bob and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1291"/>
the Child

          <ptr target="#l10582" type="alt" xml:id="te1291"/>
had red noses and black eyes when they got through. Little Davy made them own up that they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1292"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l10584" type="alt" xml:id="te1292"/>
sneaks and cowards and not fit to eat with a dog or drink with a nigger;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1293"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l10586" type="alt" xml:id="te1293"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1294"/>
Bob and the Child

          <ptr target="#l10588" type="alt" xml:id="te1294"/>
shook hands with each other, very solemn, and said they had always respected each other and was willing to let bygones be bygones. So then they washed their faces in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1934"/>
river,

          <app from="pr1934" n="111.29 (324.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3629">
            <lem wit="MS1a">river,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">river;</rdg>
          </app>
and just then there was a loud order to stand by for a crossing, and some of them went forward to man the sweeps there, and the rest went aft to handle the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1935"/>
after sweeps

          <app from="pr1935" n="111.32 (324.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3630">
            <lem wit="MS1a">after sweeps</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">after-sweeps</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#as0118" type="an" xml:id="gs0008"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26736">
I laid still and waited for fifteen minutes, and had a smoke

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0020"/>
out of a pipe that one of them left in reach; then the crossing was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1936"/>
finished

          <app from="pr1936" n="111.34 (325.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3631">
            <lem wit="MS1a">finished</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">finished,</rdg>
          </app>
and they stumped back and had a drink around and went to talking and singing again.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26748">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1937"/>
Next

          <app from="pr1937" n="111.37 (325.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3632">
            <lem wit="MS1a">[¶] Next</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3633">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Next

            </rdg>
          </app>
they got out an old fiddle, and one played, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0011"/>
another patted

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1938"/>
Juba

          <app from="pr1938" n="111.38 (325.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3634">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Juba</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">juba</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0120" type="an" xml:id="gs0012"/>
, and the rest turned themselves loose on

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0013"/>
a regular

          <pb n="112" xml:id="pb0112"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1939"/>
old-fashioned

          <app from="pr1939" n="111.38–112.1 (325.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3635">
            <lem wit="LoM">old-fashioned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
old-

              <lb/>
fashioned

            </rdg>
          </app>
keel-boat break-down

          <ptr target="#as0121" type="an" xml:id="gs0014"/>
. They couldn’t keep that up very long without getting winded, so by and by they settled around the jug

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1940"/>
again.

          <ptr target="#mt0020" type="alt" xml:id="wn0020"/>
          <app from="pr1940" n="112.3–4 (325.18–326.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3636">
            <lem wit="LoM">again. [¶] They</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
again.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] They

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26799">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1295"/>
They

          <ptr target="#l10590" type="alt" xml:id="te1295"/>
sung

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0015"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1941"/>
Jolly

          <app from="pr1941" n="112.4 (326.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3637">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Jolly</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">jolly</rdg>
          </app>
, jolly raftsman’s the life for me,”

          <ptr target="#as0122" type="an" xml:id="gs0016"/>
with a rousing chorus, and then they got to talking about differences betwixt hogs, and their different kind of habits; and next about women and their different ways; and next about the best ways to put out houses that was afire; and next about what ought to be done with the Injuns; and next about what a king had to do, and how much he got; and next about how to make cats fight;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1296"/>
and next

          <ptr target="#l10592" type="alt" xml:id="te1296"/>
about what to do when a man has fits; and next about differences betwixt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1942"/>
clear-water

          <app from="pr1942" n="112.11 (327.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3638">
            <lem wit="MS1a">clear-water</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
clear-

              <lb/>
water

            </rdg>
          </app>
rivers and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1943"/>
muddy-water

          <app from="pr1943" n="112.12 (327.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3639">
            <lem wit="LoM">muddy-water</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">muddy-water water</rdg>
          </app>
ones. The man they called

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1944"/>
Ed,

          <app from="pr1944" n="112.12 (327.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3640">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Ed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
Ed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
said

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0017"/>
the muddy Mississippi water was wholesomer to drink than the clear water of the Ohio

          <ptr target="#as0123" type="an" xml:id="gs0018"/>
; he said if you let a pint

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1297"/>
of

          <ptr target="#l10594" type="alt" xml:id="te1297"/>
this yaller Mississippi water settle, you would have about a half to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1945"/>
three-quarters

          <app from="pr1945" n="112.15 (328.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la3641">
            <lem wit="C">three-quarters</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
three-

              <lb/>
quarters

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">three quarters</rdg>
          </app>
of an

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1298"/>
inch

          <ptr target="#l10596" type="alt" xml:id="te1298"/>
of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1299"/>
mud

          <ptr target="#l10598" type="alt" xml:id="te1299"/>
in the bottom, according to the stage of the river, and then it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1946"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr1946" n="112.17 (328.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3642">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
no better

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1947"/>
than

          <app from="pr1947" n="112.17 (328.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3643">
            <lem wit="MS1a">than</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">then</rdg>
          </app>
Ohio water—what you wanted to do was to

          <pb n="113" xml:id="pb0113"/>
keep it stirred up—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1300"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l10600" type="alt" xml:id="te1300"/>
when the river was low, keep mud on hand to put in and thicken the water up the way it ought to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1948"/>
be.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y11201">
          <graphic url="y11201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">he knocked them sprawling.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26909">
The

          <app from="pr1948" n="113.2–3 (328.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3644">
            <lem wit="LoM">be. [¶] The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
be.—

              <lb/>
[¶] The

            </rdg>
          </app>
Child of Calamity said that was so; he said there was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1949"/>
nutritiousness

          <app from="pr1949" n="113.3–4 (328.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la3645">
            <lem wit="LoM">nutritiousness</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">nutriciousness</rdg>
          </app>
in the mud, and a man that drunk Mississippi water could grow corn in his stomach if he wanted to. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1950"/>
says:

          <app from="pr1950" n="113.5 (329.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3646">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26934">
“You look at the

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0048"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1951"/>
graveyards

          <app from="pr1951" n="✱113.6 (329.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la3647">
            <lem wit="LoM">graveyards</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
grave

              <lb/>
yards

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0048" type="te" xml:id="tv0048"/>
; that tells the tale. Trees won’t grow worth shucks in a Cincinnati graveyard, but in a Sent Louis graveyard they grow upwards of eight hundred foot high.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1952"/>
It’s

          <app from="pr1952" n="113.8 (329.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3648">
            <lem wit="MS1a">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">It ’s</rdg>
          </app>
all on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1953"/>
account

          <app from="pr1953" n="113.9 (329.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3649">
            <lem wit="LoM">account</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">accounts</rdg>
          </app>
of the water the people drunk before they laid up. A Cincinnati corpse don’t richen a soil any.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y11301">
          <graphic url="y11301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">an old-fashioned break-down</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e26971">
And they talked about how

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0019"/>
Ohio water

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1954"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr1954" n="113.11 (329.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3650">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
like to mix with Mississippi water. Ed said if you take the Mississippi on a rise when the Ohio is low,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1955"/>
you’ll

          <app from="pr1955" n="113.13 (330.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3651">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">you ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
find a wide band of clear water all the way down the east side of the Mississippi for a hundred

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1956"/>
mile

          <app from="pr1956" n="113.14 (330.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3652">
            <lem wit="LoM">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">miles</rdg>
          </app>
or more

          <ptr target="#as0124" type="an" xml:id="gs0020"/>
, and the minute you get out a quarter of a mile from shore and pass the line, it is all thick and yaller the rest of the way across.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27002">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1957"/>
Then

          <app from="pr1957" n="113.17 (330.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3653">
            <lem wit="MS1a">[¶] Then</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3654">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Then

            </rdg>
          </app>
they talked about how to keep tobacco from getting mouldy, and from that they went into ghosts and told about a lot that other folks had seen; but Ed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1958"/>
says:

          <app from="pr1958" n="113.19 (330.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3655">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27022">
          <pb n="114" xml:id="pb0114"/>
“Why don’t you tell something that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1959"/>
you’ve

          <app from="pr1959" n="114.1 (330.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3656">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">you ’ve</rdg>
          </app>
seen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1960"/>
yourselves? Now

          <app from="pr1960" n="114.1–2 (331.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la3657">
            <lem wit="LoM">yourselves? Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
yourselves?—

              <lb/>
Now

            </rdg>
          </app>
let me have a say. Five

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1961"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1301"/>
years

          <ptr target="#l10602" type="alt" xml:id="te1301"/>
          <app from="pr1961" n="114.2 (331.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3658">
            <lem wit="LoM">years</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">year</rdg>
          </app>
ago I was on a raft as big as this, and right along here it was a bright

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1302"/>
moonshiny

          <ptr target="#l10604" type="alt" xml:id="te1302"/>
night,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0049"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1962"/>
just after midnight,

          <app from="pr1962" n="✱114.3–4 (331.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la3659">
            <lem wit="C">just after midnight,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
just after mid-

              <lb/>
night,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3660">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0049" type="te" xml:id="tv0049"/>
and I was on watch and boss of the stabboard oar forrard, and one of my pards was a man named Dick Allbright, and he come along to where I was

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0050"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1963"/>
setting

          <app from="pr1963" n="✱114.6 (331.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3661">
            <lem wit="MS1a">setting</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">sitting</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0050" type="te" xml:id="tv0050"/>
, forrard—gaping and stretching, he was—and stooped down on the edge of the raft and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1303"/>
washed

          <ptr target="#l10606" type="alt" xml:id="te1303"/>
his face in the river, and come and set down by me and got out his pipe, and had just got it filled, when he looks up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1964"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1964" n="114.9 (332.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3662">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1965"/>
‘Why

          <app from="pr1965" n="114.9 (332.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3663">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3664">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Why

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Why</rdg>
          </app>
looky-here,’ he says, ‘ain’t that Buck Miller’s place, over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1304"/>
yander

          <ptr target="#l10608" type="alt" xml:id="te1304"/>
in the bend?’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1966"/>
‘Yes

          <app from="pr1966" n="114.11 (332.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3665">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3666">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Yes

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Yes</rdg>
          </app>
,’ says I, ‘it is—why?’ He laid his pipe down and leant his head

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1967"/>
on

          <app from="pr1967" n="114.12 (332.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3667">
            <lem wit="LoM">on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">in</rdg>
          </app>
his hand, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1968"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1968" n="114.12 (332.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3668">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1969"/>
‘I

          <app from="pr1969" n="114.12 (332.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3669">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3670">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘I

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘I</rdg>
          </app>
thought

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1970"/>
we’d

          <app from="pr1970" n="114.12 (332.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3671">
            <lem wit="MS1a">we’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">we ’d</rdg>
          </app>
be furder down.’ I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1971"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1971" n="114.12 (332.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3672">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1972"/>
‘I

          <app from="pr1972" n="114.12 (332.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3673">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3674">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘I

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘I</rdg>
          </app>
thought it too, when I went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1305"/>
off

          <ptr target="#l10610" type="alt" xml:id="te1305"/>
watch’—we was standing six hours on and six off—‘but the boys told me,’ I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1306"/>
says

          <ptr target="#l10612" type="alt" xml:id="te1306"/>
, ‘that the raft didn’t seem to hardly move, for the last

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1973"/>
hour,’

          <app from="pr1973" n="114.15 (332.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3675">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hour,’</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">hour,’—</rdg>
          </app>
says I, ‘though

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1974"/>
she’s

          <app from="pr1974" n="114.15 (332.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3676">
            <lem wit="MS1a">she’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">she ’s</rdg>
          </app>
a slipping along all right, now,’ says I. He give a kind of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1975"/>
groan

          <app from="pr1975" n="114.16 (332.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3677">
            <lem wit="MS1a">groan</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">groan,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1976"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1976" n="114.16 (333.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3678">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1977"/>
‘I’ve

          <app from="pr1977" n="114.17 (333.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3679">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3680">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘I’ve

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘I’ve</rdg>
          </app>
seed a raft act so before, along here,’ he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1978"/>
says;

          <app from="pr1978" n="114.17 (333.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3681">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says;</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,</rdg>
          </app>
‘ ’pears to me the current has most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1979"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1307"/>
quit,

          <ptr target="#l10614" type="alt" xml:id="te1307"/>
          <app from="pr1979" n="114.18 (333.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3682">
            <lem wit="MS1a">quit,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
quit

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
above the head of this bend durin’ the last

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0021"/>
two years,’ he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1980"/>
says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27257">
“Well

          <app from="pr1980" n="114.19–20 (333.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la3683">
            <lem wit="LoM">says. [¶] “Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
says.—

              <lb/>
[¶] “Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, he raised up two or three times, and looked

          <ptr target="#mt0021" type="alt" xml:id="wn0021"/>
away off and around on the water. That started me at it, too. A body is always doing what he sees somebody else doing, though there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1981"/>
mayn’t

          <app from="pr1981" n="114.22 (333.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3684">
            <lem wit="MS1a">mayn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">may n’t</rdg>
          </app>
be no sense in it. Pretty soon I see a black something floating on the water away off to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1308"/>
stabboard

          <ptr target="#l10616" type="alt" xml:id="te1308"/>
and quartering behind us. I see he was looking at it, too. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1982"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1982" n="114.25 (334.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3685">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1983"/>
‘What’s

          <app from="pr1983" n="114.25 (334.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3686">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3687">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘What’s

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘What ’s</rdg>
          </app>
that?’ He says, sort of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1984"/>
pettish,

          <app from="pr1984" n="114.25 (334.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3688">
            <lem wit="MS1a">pettish,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">pettish,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1985"/>
“Tain’t

          <app from="pr1985" n="114.26 (334.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3689">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3690">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
“Tain’t

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ’Tain’t</rdg>
          </app>
nothing but an old empty bar’l.’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1986"/>
‘An

          <app from="pr1986" n="114.26 (334.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3691">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3692">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘An

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘An</rdg>
          </app>
empty bar’l!’ says I, ‘why,’ says I, ‘a spy-glass is a fool to

          <hi rend="italic">your</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1987"/>
eyes. How

          <app from="pr1987" n="114.27 (334.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la3693">
            <lem wit="LoM">eyes. How</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
eyes.—

              <lb/>
How

            </rdg>
          </app>
can you tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1988"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr1988" n="114.27 (334.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3694">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">it ’s</rdg>
          </app>
an empty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1989"/>
bar’l?

          <app from="pr1989" n="114.28 (334.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3695">
            <lem wit="LoM">bar’l?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">bar’l.</rdg>
          </app>
’ He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1990"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1990" n="114.28 (334.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3696">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2011"/>
‘I

          <app from="pr2011" n="114.28 (334.11)" type="hc" xml:id="lai721">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="ldt002">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘I

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘I</rdg>
          </app>
don’t know; I reckon it ain’t a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1992"/>
bar’l;

          <app from="pr1992" n="114.28 (334.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3699">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bar’l;</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">bar’l,</rdg>
          </app>
but I thought it might be,’ says he.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1993"/>
‘Yes

          <app from="pr1993" n="114.29 (334.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3700">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3701">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Yes

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Yes</rdg>
          </app>
,’ I says, ‘so it might

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1994"/>
be;

          <app from="pr1994" n="114.29 (334.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3702">
            <lem wit="MS1a">be;</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">be,</rdg>
          </app>
and it might be anything else,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1309"/>
too;

          <ptr target="#l10618" type="alt" xml:id="te1309"/>
a body can’t tell nothing about it, such a distance as that,’ I says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27415">
“We

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1995"/>
hadn’t

          <app from="pr1995" n="114.32 (334.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3703">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hadn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">had n’t</rdg>
          </app>
nothing else to do, so we kept on watching it. By and by I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1996"/>
says,

          <app from="pr1996" n="114.33 (335.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3704">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1997"/>
‘Why

          <app from="pr1997" n="114.33 (335.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3705">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3706">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Why

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Why</rdg>
          </app>
looky-here, Dick Allbright, that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1998"/>
thing’s

          <app from="pr1998" n="114.33 (335.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3707">
            <lem wit="MS1a">thing’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">thing ’s</rdg>
          </app>
a-gaining on us,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr1999"/>
I

          <app from="pr1999" n="114.34 (335.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3708">
            <lem wit="LoM">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
believe.’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2000"/>
He

          <app from="pr2000" n="114.34 (335.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3709">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3710">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
He

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “He</rdg>
          </app>
never said nothing. The thing gained and gained, and I judged it must be a dog that was about tired out. Well, we swung down into the crossing, and the thing floated across the bright streak of the moonshine,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2001"/>
and by George

          <app from="pr2001" n="114.37 (335.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3711">
            <lem wit="MS1a">and by George</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">and, by George,</rdg>
          </app>
it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
a bar’l.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27486">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2002"/>
“Says

          <app from="pr2002" n="114.38 (335.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3712">
            <lem wit="MS1a">[¶] “Says</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3713">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Says

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2003"/>
I,

          <app from="pr2003" n="114.38 (335.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3714">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2004"/>
‘Dick

          <app from="pr2004" n="114.38 (335.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3715">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3716">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Dick

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Dick</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1310"/>
Allbright

          <ptr target="#l10620" type="alt" xml:id="te1310"/>
, what made you think that thing was a

          <pb n="115" xml:id="pb0115"/>
bar’l, when it was a half a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pri005"/>
mile

          <app from="pri005" n="115.1 (335.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3717">
            <lem wit="LoM">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">mild</rdg>
          </app>
off,’ says I. Says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2006"/>
he,

          <app from="pr2006" n="115.1 (335.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3718">
            <lem wit="MS1a">he,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">he,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="prt007"/>
‘I

          <app from="prt007" n="115.1 (335.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3719">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3720">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘I

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘I</rdg>
          </app>
don’t know.’ Says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pry008"/>
I,

          <app from="pry008" n="115.2 (335.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3721">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pru009"/>
‘You

          <app from="pru009" n="115.2 (335.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3722">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3723">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘You

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘You</rdg>
          </app>
tell me, Dick

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pre010"/>
Allbright.’

          <app from="pre010" n="115.2 (335.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3724">
            <lem wit="LoM">Allbright.’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Allbright.

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="prq011"/>
says,

          <app from="prq011" n="115.2 (335.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3725">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2012"/>
‘Well

          <app from="pr2012" n="115.2 (335.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3726">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3727">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Well

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Well</rdg>
          </app>
, I knowed it was a bar’l;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2013"/>
I’ve

          <app from="pr2013" n="115.3 (336.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3728">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’ve</rdg>
          </app>
seen it before; lots has seen it; they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2014"/>
says

          <app from="pr2014" n="115.3 (336.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3729">
            <lem wit="LoM">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">say</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2015"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr2015" n="115.3 (336.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3730">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">it ’s</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2016"/>
ha’nted

          <app from="pr2016" n="115.3 (336.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3731">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ha’nted</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">hanted</rdg>
          </app>
bar’l.’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2017"/>
I

          <app from="pr2017" n="115.4 (336.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3732">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3733">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
I

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “I</rdg>
          </app>
called the rest of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2018"/>
watch

          <app from="pr2018" n="115.4 (336.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3734">
            <lem wit="MS1a">watch</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">watch,</rdg>
          </app>
and they come and stood there, and I told them what Dick said. It floated right along abreast, now, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2019"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2019" n="115.6 (336.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3735">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
gain any more. It was about twenty foot off. Some was for having it aboard, but the rest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2020"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2020" n="115.7 (336.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3736">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
want to. Dick Allbright said rafts that had fooled with it had got bad luck by it. The captain of the watch said he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2021"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2021" n="115.11 (336.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3737">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
believe in it. He said he reckoned the bar’l gained on us because it was in a little better current than what we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2022"/>
was; he

          <app from="pr2022" n="115.15 (336.22–337.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3738">
            <lem wit="MS1a">was; he</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">was. He</rdg>
          </app>
said it would leave by and by.

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y11501">
          <graphic url="y11501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the mysterious barrel</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27690">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2023"/>
“So

          <app from="pr2023" n="115.17 (337.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3739">
            <lem wit="LoM">“So</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
So

            </rdg>
          </app>
then we went to talking about other things, and we had a song, and then a breakdown; and after that the captain of the watch called for another song; but it was clouding up, now, and the bar’l stuck right thar in the same place, and the song

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2024"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2024" n="115.26 (337.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3740">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
seem to have much warm-up to it, somehow, and so they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2025"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2025" n="115.27 (337.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3741">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
finish it, and there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2026"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2026" n="115.27 (337.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3742">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
any cheers, but it sort of dropped flat, and nobody said anything for a minute. Then everybody tried to talk at once, and one chap got off a joke, but it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2027"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2027" n="115.29 (338.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3743">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
no use, they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2028"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2028" n="115.30 (338.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3744">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
laugh, and even the chap that made the joke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2029"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2029" n="115.30 (338.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3745">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
laugh at it, which ain’t usual. We all just settled down glum, and watched the bar’l, and was oneasy and oncomfortable.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2030"/>
Well

          <app from="pr2030" n="115.32 (338.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3746">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
sir, it shut down black and still, and then the wind begin to moan around, and next the lightning begin to play and the thunder to grumble. And pretty soon there was a regular storm, and in the middle of it a man that was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2031"/>
running

          <app from="pr2031" n="115.36 (338.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3747">
            <lem wit="LoM">running</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">runing</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1311"/>
aft

          <ptr target="#l10622" type="alt" xml:id="te1311"/>
stumbled and fell and

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0051"/>
sprained his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2032"/>
ancle

          <app from="pr2032" n="115.36 (338.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3748">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ancle</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">ankle</rdg>
          </app>
so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2033"/>
bad

          <app from="pr2033" n="✱115.36 (339.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3749">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bad</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">that</rdg>
          </app>
he had to lay up

          <ptr target="#tb0051" type="te" xml:id="tv0051"/>
. This made the boys shake their heads. And every time the lightning come, there was that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2034"/>
bar’l,

          <app from="pr2034" n="115.38 (339.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3750">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bar’l,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
bar’l

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with the blue lights

          <pb n="116" xml:id="pb0116"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1312"/>
winking

          <ptr target="#l10624" type="alt" xml:id="te1312"/>
around it. We was always on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2035"/>
lookout

          <app from="pr2035" n="116.1 (339.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3751">
            <lem wit="MS1a">lookout</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">look-out</rdg>
          </app>
for it. But by and by, towards dawn, she was gone. When the day come we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2036"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr2036" n="116.2 (339.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3752">
            <lem wit="MS1a">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">could n’t</rdg>
          </app>
see her anywhere, and we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2037"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1313"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l10626" type="alt" xml:id="te1313"/>
          <app from="pr2037" n="116.3 (339.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3753">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
sorry, neither.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27831">
“But next night about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2038"/>
half past

          <app from="pr2038" n="116.4 (339.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3754">
            <lem wit="MS1a">half past</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">half-past</rdg>
          </app>
nine, when there was songs and high jinks going on, here she comes again, and took her old roost on the stabboard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2039"/>
side. There

          <app from="pr2039" n="116.6 (339.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la3755">
            <lem wit="LoM">side. There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
side.—

              <lb/>
There

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2040"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2040" n="116.6 (339.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3756">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
no more high jinks. Everybody got solemn; nobody talked; you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2041"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr2041" n="116.7 (340.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3757">
            <lem wit="MS1a">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">could n’t</rdg>
          </app>
get anybody to do anything but set around moody and look at the bar’l. It begun to cloud up again. When the watch changed, the off watch stayed up, ’stead of turning in. The storm ripped and roared around all night, and in the middle of it another man tripped and sprained

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0022"/>
his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2042"/>
ancle

          <app from="pr2042" n="116.11 (340.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3758">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ancle</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">ankle,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#mt0022" type="alt" xml:id="wn0022"/>
and had to knock off. The bar’l

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2043"/>
left,

          <app from="pr2043" n="116.12 (340.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3759">
            <lem wit="MS1a">left,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
left

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
towards day, and nobody see it go.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27887">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y11601">
            <graphic url="y11601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">soon there was a regular storm.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27894">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1314"/>
“Everybody

          <ptr target="#l10628" type="alt" xml:id="te1314"/>
was sober and down in the mouth all day. I don’t mean the kind of sober that comes of leaving liquor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2044"/>
alone. Not

          <app from="pr2044" n="116.14 (341.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3760">
            <lem wit="MS1a">alone. Not</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">alone,—not</rdg>
          </app>
that. They was quiet, but they all drunk more than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2045"/>
usual

          <app from="pr2045" n="116.15 (341.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3761">
            <lem wit="MS1a">usual</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">usual,</rdg>
          </app>
—not

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2046"/>
together,

          <app from="pr2046" n="116.15 (341.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3762">
            <lem wit="MS1a">together,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">together,—</rdg>
          </app>
but each man sidled off and took it private, by himself.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e27925">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1315"/>
“After

          <ptr target="#l10630" type="alt" xml:id="te1315"/>
dark the off watch

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2047"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2047" n="116.17 (341.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3763">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
turn in;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1316"/>
nobody sung,

          <ptr target="#l10632" type="alt" xml:id="te1316"/>
nobody talked; the boys

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2048"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2048" n="116.18 (341.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3764">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
scatter around, neither; they sort of huddled

          <pb n="117" xml:id="pb0117"/>
together,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2049"/>
forrard,

          <app from="pr2049" n="117.1 (341.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3765">
            <lem wit="MS1a">forrard,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">forrard;</rdg>
          </app>
and for two hours they set there, perfectly still, looking steady in the one direction, and heaving a sigh once in a while. And then, here comes the bar’l again. She took up her old place. She staid there all night; nobody turned in. The storm come on again, after midnight. It got awful dark; the rain poured down; hail, too; the thunder boomed and roared and bellowed;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1317"/>
the wind blowed a hurricane;

          <ptr target="#l10634" type="alt" xml:id="te1317"/>
and the lightning spread over everything in big sheets of glare, and showed the whole raft as plain as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2050"/>
day,

          <app from="pr2050" n="117.8 (342.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3766">
            <lem wit="MS1a">day,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">day;</rdg>
          </app>
and the river lashed up white as milk as far as you could see for miles, and there was that bar’l jiggering along, same as ever. The captain ordered the watch to man the after sweeps for a crossing, and nobody would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2051"/>
go

          <app from="pr2051" n="117.12 (343.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3767">
            <lem wit="MS1a">go</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">go,</rdg>
          </app>
—no more sprained

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2052"/>
ancles

          <app from="pr2052" n="117.12 (343.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3768">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ancles</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">ankles</rdg>
          </app>
for them, they said. They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2053"/>
wouldn’t

          <app from="pr2053" n="117.13 (343.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3769">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">would n’t</rdg>
          </app>
even

          <hi rend="italic">walk</hi>
aft. Well then, just then the sky split wide open, with a crash, and the lightning killed two men of the after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2054"/>
watch

          <app from="pr2054" n="117.15 (343.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3770">
            <lem wit="MS1a">watch</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">watch,</rdg>
          </app>
and crippled two more. Crippled them how, says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2055"/>
you? Why

          <app from="pr2055" n="117.15 (343.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3771">
            <lem wit="LoM">you? Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
you?—

              <lb/>
Why

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2056"/>
          <hi rend="italic">sprained their ancles!</hi>
          <app from="pr2056" n="117.16 (343.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3772">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="italic">sprained their ancles!</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sprained their ancles!</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <hi rend="italic">sprained their ankles!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y11701">
          <graphic url="y11701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">the lightning killed two men.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28039">
“The bar’l

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2057"/>
left,

          <app from="pr2057" n="117.17 (343.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3773">
            <lem wit="MS1a">left,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
left

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the dark

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2058"/>
betwixt

          <app from="pr2058" n="117.17–18 (343.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3774">
            <lem wit="LoM">betwixt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">between</rdg>
          </app>
lightnings, towards dawn.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2059"/>
Well

          <app from="pr2059" n="117.19 (343.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3775">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
not a body eat a bite at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2060"/>
breakfast

          <app from="pr2060" n="117.19–20 (343.21–344.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3776">
            <lem wit="LoM">breakfast</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
break-

              <lb/>
fast

            </rdg>
          </app>
that morning. After that the men loafed around, in twos and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2061"/>
threes,

          <app from="pr2061" n="117.22 (344.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3777">
            <lem wit="LoM">threes,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
threes

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and talked low together. But none of them herded with Dick All bright. They

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1318"/>
all

          <ptr target="#l10636" type="alt" xml:id="te1318"/>
give him the cold shake. If he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1319"/>
come

          <ptr target="#l10638" type="alt" xml:id="te1319"/>
around where any of the men was, they split up and sidled away. They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2062"/>
wouldn’t

          <app from="pr2062" n="117.28 (344.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3778">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">would n’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0052"/>
man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2063"/>
a sweep

          <app from="pr2063" n="✱117.28 (344.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3779">
            <lem wit="MS1a">a sweep</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM Pr">sweep</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">the sweeps</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tv0052" type="te" xml:id="tb0052"/>
with him. The captain had all the skiffs hauled up on the raft, alongside of his wigwam, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2064"/>
wouldn’t

          <app from="pr2064" n="117.31 (344.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3780">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">would n’t</rdg>
          </app>
let the dead men be took ashore to be planted; he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2065"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2065" n="117.33 (344.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3781">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
believe a man that got ashore would come back; and he was right.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28131">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1320"/>
“After

          <ptr target="#l10640" type="alt" xml:id="te1320"/>
night

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1321"/>
come,

          <ptr target="#l10642" type="alt" xml:id="te1321"/>
you could see pretty plain that there was going to be trouble if that bar’l come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2066"/>
again,

          <app from="pr2066" n="117.39 (345.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3782">
            <lem wit="MS1a">again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">again;</rdg>
          </app>
there was such a muttering

          <pb n="118" xml:id="pb0118"/>
going on. A good many wanted to kill Dick Allbright, because he’d seen the bar’l on other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2067"/>
trips

          <app from="pr2067" n="118.2 (345.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3783">
            <lem wit="MS1a">trips</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">trips,</rdg>
          </app>
and that had an ugly look. Some wanted to put him ashore. Some said,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2068"/>
let’s

          <app from="pr2068" n="118.3 (345.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3784">
            <lem wit="MS1a">let’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">let ’s</rdg>
          </app>
all go ashore in a pile, if the bar’l comes again.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28167">
“This kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1322"/>
whispers

          <ptr target="#l10644" type="alt" xml:id="te1322"/>
was still going on, the men being bunched together forrard watching for the bar’l,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2069"/>
when

          <app from="pr2069" n="118.6 (345.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3785">
            <lem wit="MS1a">when</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">when,</rdg>
          </app>
lo and behold you, here she comes again. Down she comes, slow and steady, and settles into her old tracks. You could a heard a pin drop. Then up comes the captain, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2070"/>
says:

          <app from="pr2070" n="118.9 (346.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3786">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2071"/>
‘Boys

          <app from="pr2071" n="118.9 (346.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3787">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3788">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Boys

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Boys</rdg>
          </app>
, don’t be a pack of children and fools; I don’t want this bar’l to be dogging us all the way to Orleans, and

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
don’t; well, then,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2072"/>
how’s

          <app from="pr2072" n="118.11 (346.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3789">
            <lem wit="MS1a">how’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">how ’s</rdg>
          </app>
the best way to stop it? Burn it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2073"/>
up—that’s

          <app from="pr2073" n="118.11 (346.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3790">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up—that’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">up,—that’s</rdg>
          </app>
the way.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2074"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr2074" n="118.12 (346.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3791">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
going to fetch it aboard,’ he says. And before anybody could say a word, in he went.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28229">
“He swum to it, and as he come pushing it to the raft, the men spread to one side. But the old man got it aboard and busted in the head, and there was a baby in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2075"/>
it!

          <app from="pr2075" n="118.16 (347.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3792">
            <lem wit="LoM">it!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it.</rdg>
          </app>
Yes sir, a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1323"/>
stark

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2076"/>
naked

          <app from="pr2076" n="118.16 (347.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3793">
            <lem wit="LoM">naked</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">naked dead</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10646" type="alt" xml:id="te1323"/>
baby. It was Dick Allbright’s baby; he owned up and said so.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2077"/>
‘Yes

          <app from="pr2077" n="118.17 (347.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3794">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3795">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
‘Yes

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">[¶] “ ‘Yes</rdg>
          </app>
,’ he says,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2078"/>
a leaning

          <app from="pr2078" n="118.17–18 (347.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3796">
            <lem wit="MS1a">a leaning</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">a-leaning</rdg>
          </app>
over it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1324"/>
‘

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2079"/>
Yes

          <ptr target="#l10648" type="alt" xml:id="te1324"/>
          <app from="pr2079" n="118.18 (347.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3797">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Yes</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">yes</rdg>
          </app>
, it is my own lamented darling, my poor lost Charles William Allbright deceased,’ says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2080"/>
he—for

          <app from="pr2080" n="118.19 (347.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3798">
            <lem wit="MS1a">he—for</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">he,—for</rdg>
          </app>
he could curl his tongue around the bulliest words in the language when he was a mind to, and lay them before you without a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2081"/>
j’int

          <app from="pr2081" n="118.21 (347.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3799">
            <lem wit="MS1a">j’int</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">jint</rdg>
          </app>
started, anywheres. Yes, he said he used to live up at the head of this bend, and one night he choked his child, which was crying, not intending to kill

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2082"/>
it,

          <app from="pr2082" n="118.24 (347.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3800">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">it,—</rdg>
          </app>
which was prob’ly a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2083"/>
lie,

          <app from="pr2083" n="118.24 (348.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3801">
            <lem wit="MS1a">lie,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">lie,—</rdg>
          </app>
and then he was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1325"/>
scared

          <ptr target="#l10650" type="alt" xml:id="te1325"/>
, and buried it in a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1326"/>
bar’l

          <ptr target="#l10652" type="alt" xml:id="te1326"/>
, before his wife got home, and off he went, and struck the northern trail and went to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2084"/>
rafting,

          <app from="pr2084" n="118.26 (348.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3802">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rafting,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">rafting;</rdg>
          </app>
and this was the third year that the bar’l had chased him. He said the bad luck

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1327"/>
always

          <ptr target="#l10654" type="alt" xml:id="te1327"/>
begun light, and lasted till four men was killed, and then the bar’l

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2085"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2085" n="118.28 (348.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3803">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
come any more after that. He said if the men would stand it one more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2086"/>
night—

          <app from="pr2086" n="118.30 (348.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3804">
            <lem wit="MS1a">night—</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">night,—</rdg>
          </app>
and was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2087"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1328"/>
agoing

          <ptr target="#l10656" type="alt" xml:id="te1328"/>
          <app from="pr2087" n="118.30 (348.19)" type="e" xml:id="la3805">
            <lem wit="C">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a LoM">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
on like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2088"/>
that,

          <app from="pr2088" n="118.30 (348.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3806">
            <lem wit="MS1a">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">that,—</rdg>
          </app>
but the men had got enough. They started to get out a boat to take him ashore and lynch him, but he grabbed the little child all of a sudden and jumped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2089"/>
overboard

          <app from="pr2089" n="118.32–33 (349.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3807">
            <lem wit="MS1a">overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
over-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
          </app>
with it hugged up to his breast and shedding tears, and we never see him again in this life,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1329"/>
poor

          <ptr target="#l10658" type="alt" xml:id="te1329"/>
old suffering soul, nor Charles William neither.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28388">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Who</hi>
was shedding tears?” says Bob; “was it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2090"/>
Allbright,

          <app from="pr2090" n="118.36 (349.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3808">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Allbright,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
Allbright

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
or the baby?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28401">“Why, Allbright, of course; didn’t I tell you the baby was dead? Been dead three years—how could it cry?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28403">
          <pb n="119" xml:id="pb0119"/>
“Well, never mind how it could cry—how could it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2091"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1330"/>
          <hi rend="italic">keep</hi>
          <ptr target="#l10660" type="alt" xml:id="te1330"/>
,

          <app from="pr2091" n="119.1 (349.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3809">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">keep</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
keep

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all that time?” says

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1331"/>
Davy.

          <ptr target="#l10662" type="alt" xml:id="te1331"/>
“You answer me that.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28425">
“I don’t know how it done it,” says Ed. “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2092"/>
It done it,

          <app from="pr2092" n="119.3 (350.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3810">
            <lem wit="MS1a">It done it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
It done it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1332"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2093"/>
though,

          <app from="pr2093" n="119.3 (350.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3811">
            <lem wit="MS1a">though,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
though

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2094"/>
that’s

          <ptr target="#l10664" type="alt" xml:id="te1332"/>
          <app from="pr2094" n="119.4 (350.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3812">
            <lem wit="MS1a">that’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">that ’s</rdg>
          </app>
all I know about it.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y11901">
          <graphic url="y11901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">grabbed the little child.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28460">“Say—what did they do with the bar’l?” says the Child of Calamity.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28462">
“Why, they hove it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2095"/>
overboard

          <app from="pr2095" n="119.8–9 (350.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la3813">
            <lem wit="C">overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
over-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">overboard,</rdg>
          </app>
and it sunk like a chunk of lead.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28476">
“Edward,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1333"/>
did

          <ptr target="#l10666" type="alt" xml:id="te1333"/>
the child look

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1334"/>
like

          <ptr target="#l10668" type="alt" xml:id="te1334"/>
it was choked?” says one.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28486">“Did it have its hair parted?” says another.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28488">“What was the brand on that bar’l, Eddy?” says a fellow they called Bill.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28490">
“Have you got the papers for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2096"/>
them statistics

          <app from="pr2096" n="119.19 (350.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3814">
            <lem wit="LoM">them statistics</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that yarn</rdg>
          </app>
, Edmund?” says Jimmy.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28500">“Say, Edwin, was you one of the men that was killed by the lightning?” says Davy.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28502">
“Him? O, no, he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2097"/>
both

          <app from="pr2097" n="119.24 (351.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3815">
            <lem wit="LoM">both</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">both</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of ’em,” says Bob.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1335"/>
Then they all haw-hawed.

          <ptr target="#l10670" type="alt" xml:id="te1335"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28516">
“Say, Edward, don’t you reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2098"/>
you’d

          <app from="pr2098" n="119.27 (351.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3816">
            <lem wit="C">you’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">you ’d</rdg>
          </app>
better take a pill? You look bad—don’t you feel

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2099"/>
pale?

          <app from="pr2099" n="119.28 (351.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3817">
            <lem wit="LoM">pale?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">pale,</rdg>
          </app>
” says the Child of Calamity.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28536">
“O, come, now, Eddy,” says Jimmy, “show up; you must a kept part of that bar’l to prove the thing by. Show us the bunghole—

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
—and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2100"/>
we’ll

          <app from="pr2100" n="119.31 (351.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3818">
            <lem wit="MS1a">we’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">we ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
all believe you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28549">
“Say, boys,” says Bill, “less divide it up.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2101"/>
Thar’s

          <app from="pr2101" n="119.32 (351.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3819">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Thar’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Thar ’s</rdg>
          </app>
thirteen of us. I can swaller a thirteenth of the yarn, if you can worry down the rest.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28560">
Ed got up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1336"/>
mad

          <ptr target="#l10672" type="alt" xml:id="te1336"/>
and said they could all go to some place which he ripped out pretty savage, and then walked off aft cussing to himself, and they yelling and jeering at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2102"/>
him

          <app from="pr2102" n="119.36 (352.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3820">
            <lem wit="MS1a">him</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">him,</rdg>
          </app>
and roaring and laughing so you could hear them a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2103"/>
mile.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28576">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0023"/>
“Boys

          <app from="pr2103" n="119.37–38 (352.14–353.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3821">
            <lem wit="LoM">mile. [¶] “Boys</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
mile.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] “Boys

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2104"/>
we’ll

          <app from="pr2104" n="119.38 (353.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la3822">
            <lem wit="MS1a">we’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">we ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
split a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2105"/>
watermelon

          <app from="pr2105" n="119.38 (353.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3823">
            <lem wit="LoM">watermelon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">water melon</rdg>
          </app>
on that,” says the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1337"/>
Child

          <ptr target="#l10674" type="alt" xml:id="te1337"/>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2106"/>
Calamity,

          <app from="pr2106" n="119.38–39 (353.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3824">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Calamity,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Calamity;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1338"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l10676" type="alt" xml:id="te1338"/>
he come rummaging around in the dark amongst the

          <pb n="120" xml:id="pb0120"/>
shingle bundles where I was, and put his hand on me. I was warm and soft and naked; so he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1339"/>
says

          <ptr target="#l10678" type="alt" xml:id="te1339"/>
“Ouch!” and jumped

          <ptr target="#mt0023" type="alt" xml:id="wn0023"/>
back.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28628">
“Fetch a lantern or a chunk of fire here,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1340"/>
boys—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2107"/>
there’s

          <app from="pr2107" n="120.3 (354.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3825">
            <lem wit="MS1a">there’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">there ’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10680" type="alt" xml:id="te1340"/>
a snake here as big as a cow!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28641">So they run there with a lantern and crowded up and looked in on me.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28643">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y12001">
            <graphic url="y12001.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">ed got up mad.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28650">“Come out of that, you beggar!” says one.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28652">“Who are you?” says another.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28654">
“What

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2108"/>
are

          <app from="pr2108" n="120.10 (354.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3826">
            <lem wit="LoM">are</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3827">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you after here? Speak up prompt, or overboard you go.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28665">“Snake him out, boys. Snatch him out by the heels.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28667">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2109"/>
began

          <app from="pr2109" n="120.14 (354.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3828">
            <lem wit="LoM">began</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">begun</rdg>
          </app>
to beg, and crept out amongst them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2110"/>
trembling. They

          <app from="pr2110" n="120.14 (355.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la3829">
            <lem wit="LoM">trembling. They</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
trembling.—

              <lb/>
They

            </rdg>
          </app>
looked me over, wondering, and the Child of Calamity

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2111"/>
says:

          <app from="pr2111" n="120.15 (355.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3830">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28695">“A cussed thief! Lend a hand and less heave him overboard!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28698">
“No,” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2112"/>
Big Bob

          <app from="pr2112" n="120.17 (355.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3831">
            <lem wit="LoM">Big Bob</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">big Bob</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1341"/>
“less

          <ptr target="#l10682" type="alt" xml:id="te1341"/>
get out the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2113"/>
paint pot

          <app from="pr2113" n="120.17 (355.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3832">
            <lem wit="MS1a">paint pot</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">paint-pot</rdg>
          </app>
and paint him a sky blue all over from head to heel, and

          <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
heave him over!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28724">
“Good!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2114"/>
That’s

          <app from="pr2114" n="120.19 (355.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3833">
            <lem wit="MS1a">That’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">that’s</rdg>
          </app>
it. Go for the paint,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1342"/>
Jimmy.”

          <ptr target="#l10684" type="alt" xml:id="te1342"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28737">
When the paint come, and Bob took the brush and was just going to begin, the others laughing and rubbing their hands, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1343"/>
begun

          <ptr target="#l10686" type="alt" xml:id="te1343"/>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1344"/>
cry,

          <ptr target="#l10688" type="alt" xml:id="te1344"/>
and that sort of worked on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2115"/>
Davy

          <app from="pr2115" n="120.22 (356.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3834">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Davy</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Davy,</rdg>
          </app>
and he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2116"/>
says:

          <app from="pr2116" n="120.22 (356.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3835">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28763">
          <pb n="121" xml:id="pb0121"/>
“ ’Vast there!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2117"/>
He’s

          <app from="pr2117" n="121.1 (356.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3836">
            <lem wit="MS1a">He’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">He ’s</rdg>
          </app>
nothing but a cub.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2118"/>
I’ll

          <app from="pr2118" n="121.1 (356.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3837">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
paint the man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1345"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2119"/>
that

          <app from="pr2119" n="121.1 (356.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la3838">
            <lem wit="LoM">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">that that</rdg>
          </app>
tetches

          <ptr target="#l10690" type="alt" xml:id="te1345"/>
him!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28794">
So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2120"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0053"/>
he

          <ptr target="#tb0053" type="te" xml:id="tv0053"/>
          <app from="pr2120" n="✱121.3 (356.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3839">
            <lem wit="MS1a">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I</rdg>
          </app>
looked around on them, and some of them grumbled and growled,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2121"/>
and

          <app from="pr2121" n="121.4 (356.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3840">
            <lem wit="LoM">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">but</rdg>
          </app>
Bob put down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2122"/>
paint

          <app from="pr2122" n="121.4 (356.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3841">
            <lem wit="MS1a">paint</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">paint,</rdg>
          </app>
and the others

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2123"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2123" n="121.4 (356.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3842">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
take it up.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y12101">
          <graphic url="y12101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">who are you?</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28837">
“Come here to the fire, and less see what

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2124"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr2124" n="121.7 (356.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3843">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">you ’re</rdg>
          </app>
up to here,” says Davy. “Now set down there and give an account of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1346"/>
yourself.

          <ptr target="#l10692" type="alt" xml:id="te1346"/>
How long

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2125"/>
have you been

          <app from="pr2125" n="121.12 (357.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3844">
            <lem wit="LoM">have you been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">you ben</rdg>
          </app>
aboard

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1347"/>
here?

          <ptr target="#l10694" type="alt" xml:id="te1347"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28864">“Not over a quarter of a minute, sir,” says I.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28866">
“How did you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2126"/>
get

          <app from="pr2126" n="121.15 (357.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3845">
            <lem wit="LoM">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">git</rdg>
          </app>
dry so quick?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28876">
“I don’t know, sir.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2127"/>
I’m

          <app from="pr2127" n="121.16 (357.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3846">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">I ’m</rdg>
          </app>
always that way, mostly.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28886">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2128"/>
O

          <app from="pr2128" n="121.18 (357.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3847">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, you are, are

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1348"/>
you?

          <ptr target="#l10696" type="alt" xml:id="te1348"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2129"/>
What’s

          <app from="pr2129" n="121.18 (357.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3848">
            <lem wit="MS1a">What’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">What ’s</rdg>
          </app>
your name?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28908">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2130"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2130" n="121.19 (357.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3849">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
going to tell my name. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2131"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2131" n="121.19 (357.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3850">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
know what to say, so I just says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28926">“Charles William Allbright, sir.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28928">Then they roared—the whole crowd; and I was mighty glad I said that, because maybe laughing would get them in a better humor.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28930">
When they got done laughing, Davy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2132"/>
says:

          <app from="pr2132" n="121.24 (358.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3851">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">says:—</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28939">
“It won’t hardly do, Charles William. You

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2133"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr2133" n="121.25 (358.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3852">
            <lem wit="MS1a">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">could n’t</rdg>
          </app>
have growed this much in five year, and you was a baby when you come out of the bar’l, you know, and dead at that. Come, now, tell a straight story, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1349"/>
nobody

          <ptr target="#l10698" type="alt" xml:id="te1349"/>
’ll hurt you, if you ain’t up to anything wrong. What

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
your name?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28956">
          <pb n="122" xml:id="pb0122"/>
“Aleck Hopkins, sir. Aleck James Hopkins.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28959">“Well, Aleck, where did you come from, here?”</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y12201">
          <graphic url="y12201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">charles william allbright, sir.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28967">“From a trading scow. She lays up the bend yonder. I was born on her. Pap has traded up and down here all his life; and he told me to swim off here, because when you went by he said he would like to get some of you to speak to a Mr. Jonas Turner, in Cairo, and tell him—”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28969">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2134"/>
O

          <app from="pr2134" n="122.8 (359.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la3853">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, come!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28979">
“Yes, sir,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2135"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr2135" n="122.9 (359.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3854">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">it ’s</rdg>
          </app>
as true as the world; Pap he says—”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e28990">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2136"/>
O

          <app from="pr2136" n="122.10 (359.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3855">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, your grandmother!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29000">They all laughed, and I tried again to talk, but they broke in on me and stopped me.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29002">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2137"/>
Now

          <app from="pr2137" n="122.13 (359.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3856">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">Now,</rdg>
          </app>
looky-here,” says Davy; “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2138"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr2138" n="122.13 (359.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3857">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">you ’re</rdg>
          </app>
scared, and so you talk

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2139"/>
wild. Honest

          <app from="pr2139" n="122.14 (359.22–360.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3858">
            <lem wit="LoM">wild. Honest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
wild.—

              <milestone unit="page"/>
Honest

            </rdg>
          </app>
, now, do you live in a scow, or is it a lie?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29031">
“Yes, sir, in a trading scow. She lays up at the head of the bend. But I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2140"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2140" n="122.16 (360.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3859">
            <lem wit="MS1a">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">war n’t</rdg>
          </app>
born in her.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2141"/>
It’s

          <app from="pr2141" n="122.16 (360.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3860">
            <lem wit="MS1a">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">It ’s</rdg>
          </app>
our first trip.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29049">
          <pb n="123" xml:id="pb0123"/>
“Now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2142"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr2142" n="123.1 (360.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3861">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">you ’re</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2143"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1350"/>
talking

          <ptr target="#l10700" type="alt" xml:id="te1350"/>
!

          <app from="pr2143" n="123.1 (360.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3862">
            <lem wit="LoM">talking!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">talking!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
What did you come aboard here, for? To steal?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29071">
“No, sir, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2144"/>
didn’t. It

          <app from="pr2144" n="123.3 (360.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la3863">
            <lem wit="C">didn’t. It</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
did n’t.—

              <lb/>
It

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">didn’t.—It</rdg>
          </app>
was only to get a ride on the raft. All boys does that.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29085">
“Well, I know that. But what did you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2145"/>
hide,

          <app from="pr2145" n="123.5 (360.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3864">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hide,</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
hide

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29095">“Sometimes they drive the boys off.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29097">
“So they do. They might steal. Looky-here; if we let you off this time, will you keep out of these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2146"/>
kind

          <app from="pr2146" n="123.8 (361.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3865">
            <lem wit="LoM">kind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">kinds</rdg>
          </app>
of scrapes hereafter?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29107">“ ’Deed I will, boss. You try me.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29109">
“All right, then. You ain’t but little ways from shore.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2147"/>
Overboard

          <app from="pr2147" n="123.11 (361.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3866">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
Over-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
          </app>
with you, and don’t you make a fool of yourself another time this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2148"/>
way. Blast

          <app from="pr2148" n="123.13 (361.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la3867">
            <lem wit="C">way. Blast</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
way.—

              <lb/>
Blast

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">way.—Blast</rdg>
          </app>
it, boy, some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2149"/>
raftsmen

          <app from="pr2149" n="123.14 (361.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3868">
            <lem wit="LoM">raftsmen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
rafts-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
would rawhide you till you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2150"/>
were

          <app from="pr2150" n="123.15 (361.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3869">
            <lem wit="LoM">were</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
black and blue!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y12301">
          <graphic url="y12301.jpg"/>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29154">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2151"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr2151" n="123.16 (361.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3870">
            <lem wit="MS1a">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="LoM">did n’t</rdg>
          </app>
wait to kiss good-bye, but went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2152"/>
overboard

          <app from="pr2152" n="123.17 (361.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3871">
            <lem wit="LoM">overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
over-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
          </app>
and broke for shore.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1351"/>
When

          <ptr target="#l10702" type="alt" xml:id="te1351"/>
Jim come along by and by,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1352"/>
the big

          <ptr target="#l10704" type="alt" xml:id="te1352"/>
raft was away out of sight around the point. I swum out and got aboard,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0024"/>
and was mighty glad to see home

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2153"/>
again.

          <app from="pr1844" n="✱107.1–123.20 (309.6–362.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3532">
            <lem wit="MS1a LoM">But . . . again.</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3533">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0115" type="an" xml:id="gs0002"/>
          <ptr target="#mt0024" type="alt" xml:id="wn0024"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29196">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0025"/>
I had to tell Jim I didn’t find out how far it was to Cairo. He was pretty sorry.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="rp2153"/>
There

          <app from="pr2153" n="123.20–22 (362.2–363.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3872">
            <lem wit="C">again. [¶] I . . . sorry. There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
again.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] I . . . sorry. There

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">[¶] There</rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">again.</rdg>
          </app>
warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2155"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr2155" n="123.22 (363.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3875">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2156"/>
do now

          <app from="pr2156" n="123.22 (363.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3876">
            <lem wit="MS1a">do now</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">do, now,</rdg>
          </app>
but to look out sharp for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2157"/>
town

          <app from="pr2157" n="123.23 (363.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3877">
            <lem wit="MS1a">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">town,</rdg>
          </app>
and not pass it without seeing it. He said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2158"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr2158" n="123.23 (363.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3878">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he would</rdg>
          </app>
be mighty sure to see it, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2159"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr2159" n="123.24 (363.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3879">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he would</rdg>
          </app>
be a free man the minute he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2160"/>
seen

          <app from="pr2160" n="123.24 (363.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3880">
            <lem wit="A">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
it, but if he missed

          <ptr target="#mt0025" type="alt" xml:id="wn0025"/>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2161"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr2161" n="123.25 (364.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3881">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he would</rdg>
          </app>
be in the slave country again and no more show for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1353"/>
freedom. Every

          <ptr target="#l10706" type="alt" xml:id="te1353"/>
little while he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2162"/>
jumps

          <app from="pr2162" n="123.26 (364.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3882">
            <lem wit="A">jumps</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">jumped</rdg>
          </app>
up and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29286">“Dah she is!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29288">
But it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2163"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2163" n="123.28 (364.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3883">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
. It was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2164"/>
jack-o’-lanterns

          <app from="pr2164" n="123.28 (364.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3884">
            <lem wit="MS1a">jack-o’-lanterns</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jack-o-lanterns</rdg>
          </app>
, or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2165"/>
lightning bugs

          <app from="pr2165" n="123.28 (364.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3885">
            <lem wit="MS1a">lightning bugs</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-bugs</rdg>
          </app>
; so he set down

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1354"/>
again,

          <ptr target="#l10708" type="alt" xml:id="te1354"/>
and went to watching, same as before. Jim said it made him all over trembly and feverish to be so close to freedom. Well, I can tell you it made me all over trembly and feverish, too, to hear him, because I begun to get it through my head that he

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
most free—and who was to blame for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2166"/>
it? Why

          <app from="pr2166" n="123.33 (365.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la3886">
            <lem wit="A">it? Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
it?—

              <lb/>
Why

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <hi rend="italic">me.</hi>
I couldn’t get that out of my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2167"/>
conscience, no how nor no way

          <app from="pr2167" n="123.34 (365.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3887">
            <lem wit="A">conscience, no how nor no way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">conscience</rdg>
          </app>
. It got to troubling me so I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1355"/>
couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2168"/>
rest

          <ptr target="#l10710" type="alt" xml:id="te1355"/>
,

          <app from="pr2168" n="123.35 (365.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3888">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rest,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rest;</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1356"/>
couldn’t stay

          <ptr target="#l10712" type="alt" xml:id="te1356"/>
still in one place. It hadn’t ever come home to me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2169"/>
before

          <app from="pr2169" n="123.36 (365.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3889">
            <lem wit="MS1a">before</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">before,</rdg>
          </app>
what this thing was that I was doing. But now it did; and it staid with me, and scorched me more and more. I tried to make out to myself that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2170"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2170" n="123.38 (365.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3890">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
warn’t

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I warn’t</rdg>
          </app>
to blame, because

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2171"/>
didn’t run

          <app from="pr2171" n="123.38 (365.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3891">
            <lem wit="A">didn’t run</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">warn’t running</rdg>
          </app>
Jim

          <pb n="124" xml:id="pb0124"/>
off from his rightful owner; but it warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2172"/>
no

          <app from="pr2172" n="124.1 (365.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3892">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
use, conscience up and says, every time,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2173"/>
‘But

          <app from="pr2173" n="124.2 (365.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3893">
            <lem wit="MS1a">‘But</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“But</rdg>
          </app>
you knowed he was running for his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2174"/>
freedom

          <app from="pr2174" n="124.2 (366.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3894">
            <lem wit="MS1a">freedom</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">freedom,</rdg>
          </app>
and you could a paddled ashore and told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2175"/>
somebody.’

          <app from="pr2175" n="124.3 (366.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la3895">
            <lem wit="MS1a">somebody.’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">somebody.”</rdg>
          </app>
That was so—I couldn’t get around that,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2176"/>
no way

          <app from="pr2176" n="124.4 (366.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3896">
            <lem wit="MS1a">no way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">noway</rdg>
          </app>
. That was where it pinched. Conscience says to me,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2177"/>
‘What

          <app from="pr2177" n="124.5 (366.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3897">
            <lem wit="MS1a">‘What</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“What</rdg>
          </app>
had poor Miss Watson done to you, that you could see her nigger go off right under your eyes and never say one single word? What did that poor old woman do to you, that you could treat her so mean?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2178"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2178" n="124.8 (366.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3898">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
she tried to learn you your book, she tried to learn you your manners, she tried to be good to you every way she knowed how.

          <hi rend="italic">That’s</hi>
what she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2179"/>
done.’

          <app from="pr2179" n="124.10 (367.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3899">
            <lem wit="MS1a">done.’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">done.”</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29463">
I got to feeling so mean and so miserable I most wished I was dead. I fidgeted up and down the raft, abusing myself to myself, and Jim was fidgeting up and down past me. We neither of us could keep still. Every time he danced around and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2180"/>
says

          <app from="pr2180" n="124.14 (367.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3900">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2181"/>
‘Dah’s Cairo!’

          <app from="pr2181" n="124.14 (367.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3901">
            <lem wit="MS1a">‘Dah’s Cairo!’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“Dah’s Cairo!”</rdg>
          </app>
it went through me like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2182"/>
a

          <app from="pr2182" n="124.15 (367.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la3902">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I was</rdg>
          </app>
shot, and I thought if it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
Cairo I reckoned I would die of miserableness.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29492">
Jim talked out loud all the time while I was talking to myself. He was saying how the first thing he would do when he got to a free State he would go to saving up money and never spend a single cent, and when he got enough he would buy his wife, which was owned on a farm close to where Miss Watson lived; and then they would both work

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2183"/>
to buy

          <app from="pr2183" n="124.22 (368.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3903">
            <lem wit="A">to buy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and buy</rdg>
          </app>
the two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2184"/>
children;

          <app from="pr2184" n="124.22 (368.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3904">
            <lem wit="MS1a">children;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">children,</rdg>
          </app>
and if their master wouldn’t sell them,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2185"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr2185" n="124.23 (368.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3905">
            <lem wit="A">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they would</rdg>
          </app>
get an

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2186"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1357"/>
ab’litionist

          <ptr target="#l10714" type="alt" xml:id="te1357"/>
          <app from="pr2186" n="124.23 (368.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3906">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ab’litionist</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Ab’litionist</rdg>
          </app>
to go and steal them.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29529">
It most froze me to hear such talk. He wouldn’t ever dared to talk such talk in his life before. Just see what a difference it made in him the minute he judged he was about free. It was according to

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0021"/>
the old saying,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2187"/>
‘Give

          <app from="pr2187" n="124.27 (369.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la3907">
            <lem wit="MS1a">‘Give</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“give</rdg>
          </app>
a nigger an inch and he’ll take an

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2188"/>
ell.’

          <app from="pr2188" n="124.27 (369.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3908">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ell.’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ell.”</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0125" type="an" xml:id="gs0022"/>
Thinks I, this is what comes of my not thinking. Here was this nigger which I had as good as helped to run away, coming right out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2189"/>
flat-footed

          <app from="pr2189" n="124.29 (369.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3909">
            <lem wit="A">flat-footed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
flat-

              <lb/>
footed

            </rdg>
          </app>
and saying he would steal his children—children that belonged to a man I didn’t even

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2190"/>
know;

          <app from="pr2190" n="124.31 (369.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3910">
            <lem wit="A">know;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">know—</rdg>
          </app>
a man that hadn’t ever done me no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1358"/>
harm.

          <ptr target="#l10716" type="alt" xml:id="te1358"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29572">
I was sorry to hear Jim say that, it was such a lowering of him.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1359"/>
My

          <ptr target="#l10718" type="alt" xml:id="te1359"/>
conscience got to stirring me up hotter than ever,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2191"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1360"/>
until

          <ptr target="#l10720" type="alt" xml:id="te1360"/>
          <app from="pr2191" n="124.33 (370.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3911">
            <lem wit="A">until</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">till</rdg>
          </app>
at last I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2192"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1361"/>
says to it,

          <ptr target="#l10722" type="alt" xml:id="te1361"/>
          <app from="pr2192" n="124.33–34 (370.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3912">
            <lem wit="A">says to it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">says, to it</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2193"/>
‘Let

          <app from="pr2193" n="124.34 (370.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3913">
            <lem wit="MS1a">‘Let</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“Let</rdg>
          </app>
up on me—it ain’t too late, yet—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1362"/>
I’ll

          <ptr target="#l10724" type="alt" xml:id="te1362"/>
paddle ashore at the first

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2194"/>
light

          <app from="pr2194" n="124.35 (370.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3914">
            <lem wit="MS1a">light</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">light,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2195"/>
tell.’

          <app from="pr2195" n="124.35 (370.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3915">
            <lem wit="MS1a">tell.’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tell.”</rdg>
          </app>
I felt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2196"/>
easy

          <app from="pr2196" n="124.35 (370.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3916">
            <lem wit="MS1a">easy</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">easy,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2197"/>
happy

          <app from="pr2197" n="124.35 (370.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3917">
            <lem wit="MS1a">happy</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">happy,</rdg>
          </app>
and light as a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2198"/>
feather

          <app from="pr2198" n="124.35 (370.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3918">
            <lem wit="MS1a">feather</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">feather,</rdg>
          </app>
right off. All my troubles was gone. I went to looking out sharp for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2199"/>
light

          <app from="pr2199" n="124.36 (370.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3919">
            <lem wit="MS1a">light</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">light,</rdg>
          </app>
and sort of singing to myself.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2200"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr2200" n="124.37 (370.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la3920">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
one showed. Jim

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1363"/>
sings

          <ptr target="#l10726" type="alt" xml:id="te1363"/>
out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29673">
“We’s safe, Huck, we’s safe! Jump up and crack yo’ heels, dat’s de good ole Cairo at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2201"/>
las’

          <app from="pr2201" n="124.39 (371.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la3921">
            <lem wit="MS1a">las’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">las’,</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2202"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1364"/>
jis’

          <ptr target="#l10728" type="alt" xml:id="te1364"/>
          <app from="pr2202" n="124.39 (371.5)" type="e" xml:id="la3922">
            <lem wit="C">jis’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">jes’</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">jis</rdg>
          </app>
knows it!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29695">
          <pb n="125" xml:id="pb0125"/>
I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29699">
“I’ll take the canoe and go see, Jim. It

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1365"/>
mightn’t

          <ptr target="#l10730" type="alt" xml:id="te1365"/>
be, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2203"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1366"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0054"/>
know.”

          <ptr target="#tb0054" type="te" xml:id="tv0054"/>
          <ptr target="#l10732" type="alt" xml:id="te1366"/>
          <app from="pr2203" n="✱125.2 (371.10–15)" type="e" xml:id="la3923">
            <lem wit="A">know.”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">know.” [¶] “Dat’s so, Huck. A body can’t be too keerful. I’ll float along en wait. But it’s Cairo, I jes’ knows it is.”</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29717">
He jumped and got the canoe ready, and put his old coat in the bottom for me to set on, and give me the paddle; and as I shoved

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2204"/>
off

          <app from="pr2204" n="125.4 (371.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3924">
            <lem wit="MS1a">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">off,</rdg>
          </app>
he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29727">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2205"/>
Pooty

          <app from="pr2205" n="125.6 (372.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3925">
            <lem wit="A">Pooty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Putty</rdg>
          </app>
soon I’ll be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2206"/>
a-shout’n

          <app from="pr2206" n="125.6 (372.2)" type="e" xml:id="la3926">
            <lem wit="A">a-shout’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a-shoutin’</rdg>
          </app>
for joy,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1367"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10734" type="alt" xml:id="te1367"/>
I’ll say, it’s all on accounts

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2207"/>
o’

          <app from="pr2207" n="125.7 (372.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3927">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
Huck; I’s a free man,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1368"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10736" type="alt" xml:id="te1368"/>
I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2208"/>
ever

          <app from="pr2208" n="125.7 (372.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3928">
            <lem wit="A">ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">never</rdg>
          </app>
ben free

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2209"/>
ef

          <app from="pr2209" n="125.7 (372.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3929">
            <lem wit="A">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">if</rdg>
          </app>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2210"/>
hadn’

          <app from="pr2210" n="125.7 (372.7)" type="e" xml:id="la3930">
            <lem wit="A">hadn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hadn’t</rdg>
          </app>
ben for Huck; Huck done it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2211"/>
Jim won’t ever

          <app from="pr2211" n="125.8 (372.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3931">
            <lem wit="A">Jim won’t ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I shan’t nuvver</rdg>
          </app>
forgit you, Huck; you’s de bes’ fren’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1369"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2212"/>
Jim’s

          <app from="pr2212" n="125.9 (372.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3932">
            <lem wit="A">Jim’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I’s</rdg>
          </app>
ever

          <ptr target="#l10738" type="alt" xml:id="te1369"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1370"/>
had

          <ptr target="#l10740" type="alt" xml:id="te1370"/>
;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1371"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l10742" type="alt" xml:id="te1371"/>
you’s de

          <hi rend="italic">only</hi>
fren’ ole Jim’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2213"/>
got,

          <app from="pr2213" n="125.9 (372.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3933">
            <lem wit="MS1a">got,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
got

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29826">
I was paddling off, all in a sweat to tell on him; but when he says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2214"/>
this

          <app from="pr2214" n="125.11 (372.17)" type="e" xml:id="la3934">
            <lem wit="MS1a">this</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">this,</rdg>
          </app>
it seemed to kind of take the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1372"/>
tuck

          <ptr target="#l10744" type="alt" xml:id="te1372"/>
all out of me. I went along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2215"/>
slow,

          <app from="pr2215" n="125.12 (372.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3935">
            <lem wit="MS1a">slow,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
slow

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then, and I warn’t right down certain whether I was glad I started or whether I warn’t. When I was fifty yards off, Jim says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29849">
“Dah you goes, de ole true Huck; de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2216"/>
on’y

          <app from="pr2216" n="125.14 (373.6)" type="e" xml:id="la3936">
            <lem wit="A">on’y</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">only</rdg>
          </app>
white genlman dat ever kep’ his promise to ole

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1373"/>
Jim.”

          <ptr target="#l10746" type="alt" xml:id="te1373"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29862">
Well, I just felt sick. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2217"/>
I says

          <app from="pr2217" n="125.16 (373.14)" type="e" xml:id="la3937">
            <lem wit="A">I says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">says I</rdg>
          </app>
, I

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to do it—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2218"/>
I can’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1374"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l10748" type="alt" xml:id="te1374"/>
          <hi rend="italic">out</hi>
          <app from="pr2218" n="125.16 (373.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3938">
            <lem wit="A">
I can’t get

              <hi rend="italic">out</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">how can I git out</rdg>
          </app>
of it. Right then, along comes a skiff with two men in it, with guns, and they stopped and I stopped. One of them says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29891">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2219"/>
What’s

          <app from="pr2219" n="125.19 (373.21)" type="e" xml:id="la3939">
            <lem wit="A">What’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">What is</rdg>
          </app>
that, yonder?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29901">“A piece of a raft,” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29903">“Do you belong on it?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29905">“Yes, sir.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29907">“Any men on it?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29910">“Only one, sir.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29912">
“Well, there’s five niggers run

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2220"/>
off,

          <app from="pr2220" n="125.25 (374.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la3940">
            <lem wit="MS1a">off,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
off

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to-night, up yonder above the head of the bend. Is your man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2221"/>
white,

          <app from="pr2221" n="125.26 (374.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3941">
            <lem wit="MS1a">white,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
white

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
or black?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29930">
I didn’t answer up prompt.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1375"/>
I tried to, but the words wouldn’t come. I tried,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1376"/>
for a second or two,

          <ptr target="#l10752" type="alt" xml:id="te1376"/>
to brace

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2222"/>
up,

          <app from="pr2222" n="125.28 (374verso.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la3942">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and out with it, but I warn’t man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1377"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2223"/>
enough—hadn’t the spunk of a rabbit

          <app from="pr2223" n="125.29 (374verso.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3943">
            <lem wit="A">enough—hadn’t the spunk of a rabbit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">enough; I couldn’t bear it, I hadn’t the heart to do it</rdg>
          </app>
. I see I was weakening; so I just give up trying, and up and says—

          <ptr target="#l10754" type="alt" xml:id="te1377"/>
          <ptr target="#l10750" type="alt" xml:id="te1375"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29958">“He’s white.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29960">“I reckon we’ll go and see for ourselves.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29962">
“I wish you would,” says I, “

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1378"/>
because

          <ptr target="#l10756" type="alt" xml:id="te1378"/>
it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2224"/>
pap

          <app from="pr2224" n="125.33 (374.18)" type="e" xml:id="la3944">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
that’s there, and maybe you’d help me tow the raft ashore where the light is. He’s sick—and so is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2225"/>
mam

          <app from="pr2225" n="125.35 (375.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3945">
            <lem wit="A">mam</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Mam</rdg>
          </app>
and Mary Ann.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29985">
“Oh, the devil!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2226"/>
We’re

          <app from="pr2226" n="125.36 (375.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la3946">
            <lem wit="MS1a">We’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">we’re</rdg>
          </app>
in a hurry, boy. But I s’pose we’ve got to. Come—buckle to your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1379"/>
paddle,

          <ptr target="#l10758" type="alt" xml:id="te1379"/>
and let’s get along.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e29999">
I buckled to my paddle and they laid to their oars. When we had made a stroke or

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1380"/>
two,

          <ptr target="#l10760" type="alt" xml:id="te1380"/>
I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30005">
          <pb n="126" xml:id="pb0126"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2227"/>
Pap ’ll

          <app from="pr2227" n="126.1 (375.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3947">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Pap ’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Pap’ll</rdg>
          </app>
be mighty much

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2228"/>
obleeged

          <app from="pr2228" n="126.1 (375.15)" type="e" xml:id="la3948">
            <lem wit="A">obleeged</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">obliged</rdg>
          </app>
to you, I can tell you. Everybody goes away when I want them to help me tow the raft

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2229"/>
ashore

          <app from="pr2229" n="126.2 (375.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3949">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ashore</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ashore,</rdg>
          </app>
and I can’t do it by myself.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30033">
“Well, that’s infernal

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1381"/>
mean

          <ptr target="#l10762" type="alt" xml:id="te1381"/>
. Odd, too. Say, boy, what’s the matter with your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1382"/>
father?”

          <ptr target="#l10764" type="alt" xml:id="te1382"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30042">“It’s the—a—the—well, it ain’t anything, much.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30045">They stopped pulling. It warn’t but a mighty little ways to the raft, now. One says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30047">
“Boy, that’s a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2230"/>
lie. What

          <app from="pr2230" n="126.9 (376.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la3950">
            <lem wit="A">lie. What</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
lie.—

              <lb/>
What

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
the matter with your pap? Answer up square, now, and it’ll be the better for you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30061">
“I will, sir, I will, honest—but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2231"/>
don’t

          <app from="pr2231" n="126.11 (376.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3951">
            <lem wit="A">don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
leave us, please. It’s the—the—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2232"/>
gentlemen

          <app from="pr2232" n="126.12 (376.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la3952">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gentlemen</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
gentle-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
, if you’ll only pull ahead, and let me heave you the head-line, you won’t have to come a-near the raft—please do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30082">
“Set her back, John, set her back!” says one. They backed water. “Keep away, boy—keep to looard. Confound it, I just expect the wind has blowed it to us. Your pap’s got the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1383"/>
small-pox,

          <ptr target="#l10766" type="alt" xml:id="te1383"/>
and you know it precious well. Why didn’t you come out and say so? Do you want to spread it all over?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30088">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2233"/>
Well,” says I, a-blubbering, “I’ve

          <app from="pr2233" n="126.19 (377.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3953">
            <lem wit="A">Well,” says I, a-blubbering, “I’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Well, I’ve</rdg>
          </app>
told everybody before, and then they just went away and left us.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y12601">
          <graphic url="y12601.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">boy, that’s a lie.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30104">
“Poor devil, there’s something in that. We are right down sorry for you, but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1384"/>
we

          <ptr target="#l10768" type="alt" xml:id="te1384"/>
—well, hang it, we don’t want the small-pox, you see.

          <pb n="127" xml:id="pb0127"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2234"/>
Look here

          <app from="pr2234" n="127.1 (378.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3954">
            <lem wit="A">Look here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Looky-here</rdg>
          </app>
, I’ll tell you what to do. Don’t you try to land by yourself, or you’ll smash everything to pieces. You float along down about twenty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2235"/>
miles

          <app from="pr2235" n="127.3 (378.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3955">
            <lem wit="A">miles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">mile</rdg>
          </app>
and you’ll come to a town on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2236"/>
left hand

          <app from="pr2236" n="127.3 (378.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la3956">
            <lem wit="MS1a">left hand</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">left-hand</rdg>
          </app>
side of the river. It will be long after sun-up, then, and when you ask for help, you tell them your folks are all down with chills and fever. Don’t be a fool

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2237"/>
again

          <app from="pr2237" n="127.6 (378.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la3957">
            <lem wit="MS1a">again</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">again,</rdg>
          </app>
and let people guess what is the matter. Now we’re trying to do you a kindness; so you just put twenty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2238"/>
miles

          <app from="pr2238" n="127.7 (379.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3958">
            <lem wit="A">miles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">mile</rdg>
          </app>
between us, that’s a good boy. It wouldn’t do any good to land yonder where the light is—it’s only a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2239"/>
wood yard

          <app from="pr2239" n="127.9 (379.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la3959">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wood yard</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wood-yard</rdg>
          </app>
. Say—I reckon your father’s poor, and I’m bound to say he’s in pretty hard luck. Here—I’ll put

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0023"/>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2240"/>
twenty-dollar

          <app from="pr2240" n="127.11 (379.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3960">
            <lem wit="MS1a">twenty-dollar</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">twenty dollar</rdg>
          </app>
gold piece

          <ptr target="#as0126" type="an" xml:id="gs0024"/>
on this board, and you get it when it floats

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2241"/>
by. I

          <app from="pr2241" n="127.12 (379.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la3961">
            <lem wit="A">by. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
by.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
feel mighty mean to leave you, but my kingdom! it won’t do to fool with small-pox, don’t you see?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30184">
“Hold on, Parker,” says the other man, “here’s a twenty to put on the board for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1385"/>
me.

          <ptr target="#l10770" type="alt" xml:id="te1385"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2242"/>
Good-bye

          <app from="pr2242" n="127.15 (380.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la3962">
            <lem wit="A">Good-bye</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Good-

              <lb/>
bye

            </rdg>
          </app>
, boy, you do as Mr. Parker

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2243"/>
told you

          <app from="pr2243" n="127.15 (380.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la3963">
            <lem wit="MS1a">told you</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">told you,</rdg>
          </app>
and you’ll be all right.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30207">
“That’s so, my boy—good-bye, good-bye. If you see any runaway niggers, you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1386"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l10772" type="alt" xml:id="te1386"/>
help and nab them, and you can make some money by it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30213">“Good-bye, sir,” says I, “I won’t let no runaway niggers get by me if I can help it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30215">
They went off, and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2244"/>
got

          <app from="pr2244" n="127.22 (380.20)" type="e" xml:id="la3964">
            <lem wit="A">got</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">hopped</rdg>
          </app>
aboard the raft,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2245"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1387"/>
feeling bad and low, because I knowed very well I had done wrong, and I see it warn’t no use for me to try to learn to do right;

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0025"/>
a body that don’t get

          <hi rend="italic">started</hi>
right when he’s little, ain’t got no show

          <ptr target="#as0127" type="an" xml:id="gs0026"/>
—when the pinch comes there ain’t nothing to back him up and keep him to his work, and so he gets beat. Then I thought a minute, and says to myself, hold on,—s’pose you’d a done right and give Jim up; would you felt better than what you do now? No, says I, I’d feel bad—I’d feel just the same way I do now. Well, then, says I, what’s the use you learning to do right, when it’s troublesome to do right and ain’t no trouble to do wrong, and the wages is just the same? I was stuck. I couldn’t answer that. So I reckoned I wouldn’t bother no more about it, but after this always do whichever come handiest at the time.

          <ptr target="#l10774" type="alt" xml:id="te1387"/>
          <app from="pr2245" n="127.22–34 (380.21–382.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3965">
            <lem wit="A">feeling . . . time.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saying to myself, I’ve done wrong again, and was trying as hard as I could to do right, too; but when it come right down to telling them it was a nigger on the raft, and I opened my mouth a-purpose to do it, I couldn’t. I am a mean, low coward, and it’s the fault of them that brung me up. If I had been raised right, I wouldn’t said anything about anybody being sick, but the more I try to do right, the more I can’t. I reckon I won’t ever try again, because it ain’t no sort of use and only makes me feel bad. From this out I mean to do everything as wrong as I can do it, and just go straight to the dogs and done with it. I don’t see why people’s put here, anyway.</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30243">
I went into the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2246"/>
wigwam

          <app from="pr2246" n="127.35 (382.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la3966">
            <lem wit="A">wigwam</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
wig-

              <lb/>
wam

            </rdg>
          </app>
; Jim warn’t there. I looked all around; he warn’t anywhere. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30255">“Jim!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30257">
“Here I is, Huck. Is dey out o’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2247"/>
sight,

          <app from="pr2247" n="127.38 (382.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la3967">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sight,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
sight

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yit? Don’t talk loud.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30267">
          <pb n="128" xml:id="pb0128"/>
He was in the river, under the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2248"/>
stern-oar

          <app from="pr2248" n="128.1 (382.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la3968">
            <lem wit="MS1a">stern-oar</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stern oar</rdg>
          </app>
, with just his nose out. I told him they was out of sight, so he come aboard. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30278">
“I was a-listenin’ to all de talk,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1388"/>
en I

          <ptr target="#l10776" type="alt" xml:id="te1388"/>
slips into de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2249"/>
river

          <app from="pr2249" n="128.3 (383.4)" type="e" xml:id="la3969">
            <lem wit="A">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">riber</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1389"/>
en was

          <ptr target="#l10778" type="alt" xml:id="te1389"/>
gwyne to shove for sho’ if dey come aboard. Den I was gwyne to swim to de raf’ agin when dey was gone. But lawsy, how you did fool ’em,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2250"/>
Huck!

          <app from="pr2250" n="128.6 (383.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3970">
            <lem wit="A">Huck!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Huck.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0027"/>
Dat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2251"/>
          <hi rend="italic">wuz</hi>
          <app from="pr2251" n="128.6 (383.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3971">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">wuz</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2252"/>
smartes’

          <app from="pr2252" n="128.6 (383.12)" type="e" xml:id="la3972">
            <lem wit="A">smartes’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">smartest</rdg>
          </app>
dodge

          <ptr target="#as0128" type="an" xml:id="gs0028"/>
! I tell you, chile, I ’speck it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1390"/>
save’

          <ptr target="#l10780" type="alt" xml:id="te1390"/>
ole Jim—ole Jim ain’t gwyne to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2253"/>
forgit

          <app from="pr2253" n="128.7 (383.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3973">
            <lem wit="A">forgit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">fogit</rdg>
          </app>
you for dat, honey.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30339">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y12801">
            <graphic url="y12801.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2254"/>
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">here</hi>
              <app from="pr2254" n="128 caption" type="e" xml:id="la3974">
                <lem wit="C">
“

                  <hi rend="smallcaps">here</hi>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de3975">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
‘

                  <hi rend="smallcaps">here</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">i is, huck.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30361">
Then we talked about the money. It was a pretty good raise,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1391"/>
twenty

          <ptr target="#l10782" type="alt" xml:id="te1391"/>
dollars apiece. Jim said we could take deck passage on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2255"/>
steamboat,

          <app from="pr2255" n="128.10 (384.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3976">
            <lem wit="MS1a">steamboat,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
steamboat

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1392"/>
now,

          <ptr target="#l10784" type="alt" xml:id="te1392"/>
and the money would last us as far as we wanted to go in the free States. He said twenty mile more warn’t far for the raft to go, but he wished we was already there.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30378">
Towards daybreak we tied up, and Jim was mighty particular about hiding the raft good. Then he worked all day fixing things in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2256"/>
bundles

          <app from="pr2256" n="128.14 (384.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3977">
            <lem wit="MS1a">bundles</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">bundles,</rdg>
          </app>
and getting all ready to quit rafting.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30388">
That night about ten we hove in sight of the lights of a town away down in a left-hand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2257"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1393"/>
bend.

          <ptr target="#l10786" type="alt" xml:id="te1393"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30394">
I

          <app from="pr2257" n="128.17–18 (384.22–385.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3978">
            <lem wit="A">bend. [¶] I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
bend.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] I

            </rdg>
          </app>
went off in the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1394"/>
canoe,

          <ptr target="#l10788" type="alt" xml:id="te1394"/>
to ask about it. Pretty soon I found a man out in the river with a skiff, setting a trot-line. I ranged up and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30408">
          <pb n="129" xml:id="pb0129"/>
“Mister, is that town Cairo?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30412">
“Cairo?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2258"/>
No

          <app from="pr2258" n="129.2 (385.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3979">
            <lem wit="MS1a">No</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">no</rdg>
          </app>
. You must be a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2259"/>
blame’

          <app from="pr2259" n="129.2 (385.11)" type="e" xml:id="la3980">
            <lem wit="A">blame’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">blamed</rdg>
          </app>
fool.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30430">“What town is it, mister?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30432">
“If you want to know, go and find out. If you stay here

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2260"/>
botherin’

          <app from="pr2260" n="129.4 (386.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3981">
            <lem wit="A">botherin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">bothering</rdg>
          </app>
around me for about a half a minute longer, you’ll get something you won’t want.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30442">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2261"/>
paddled

          <app from="pr2261" n="129.7 (386.8)" type="e" xml:id="la3982">
            <lem wit="A">paddled</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">paddled back</rdg>
          </app>
to the raft. Jim was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2262"/>
awful

          <app from="pr2262" n="129.7 (386.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la3983">
            <lem wit="A">awful</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dreadful</rdg>
          </app>
disappointed, but I said never mind, Cairo would be the next place, I reckoned.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30460">
We passed another town before

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2263"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr2263" n="129.9 (386.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3984">
            <lem wit="MS1a">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">daylight,</rdg>
          </app>
and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1395"/>
was going

          <ptr target="#l10790" type="alt" xml:id="te1395"/>
out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2264"/>
again; but

          <app from="pr2264" n="129.10 (386.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3985">
            <lem wit="A">again; but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">again. But</rdg>
          </app>
it was high ground, so I didn’t go. No high ground about Cairo, Jim said. I had forgot it. We laid up for the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1396"/>
day,

          <ptr target="#l10792" type="alt" xml:id="te1396"/>
on a tow-head tolerable close to the left-hand bank. I begun to suspicion something. So did Jim. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30487">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0029"/>
“Maybe we went by Cairo in the fog that night.”

          <ptr target="#as0129" type="an" xml:id="gs0030"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30491">He says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30493">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2265"/>
Doan’

          <app from="pr2265" n="129.16 (387.10)" type="e" xml:id="la3986">
            <lem wit="A">Doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Don’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2266"/>
less

          <app from="pr2266" n="129.16 (387.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la3987">
            <lem wit="MS1a">less</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">less’</rdg>
          </app>
talk about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1397"/>
it,

          <ptr target="#l10794" type="alt" xml:id="te1397"/>
Huck. Po’ niggers can’t have no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2267"/>
luck. I

          <app from="pr2267" n="129.16 (387.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la3988">
            <lem wit="A">luck. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
luck.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2268"/>
awluz

          <app from="pr2268" n="129.17 (387.13)" type="e" xml:id="la3989">
            <lem wit="A">awluz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">always</rdg>
          </app>
’spected dat rattle-snake skin warn’t done wid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2269"/>
its

          <app from="pr2269" n="129.17 (387.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la3990">
            <lem wit="MS1a">its</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it’s</rdg>
          </app>
work.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30540">
“I wish I’d never seen that snake-skin, Jim—I do wish I’d never

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1398"/>
laid

          <ptr target="#l10796" type="alt" xml:id="te1398"/>
eyes on it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30546">
“It ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1399"/>
yo’

          <ptr target="#l10798" type="alt" xml:id="te1399"/>
fault, Huck; you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2270"/>
didn’

          <app from="pr2270" n="129.20 (388.1)" type="e" xml:id="la3991">
            <lem wit="A">didn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
know. Don’t you blame

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2271"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1400"/>
yo’self

          <ptr target="#l10800" type="alt" xml:id="te1400"/>
          <app from="pr2271" n="129.20 (388.3)" type="e" xml:id="la3992">
            <lem wit="A">yo’self</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">yousef</rdg>
          </app>
’bout it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30571">
When it was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2272"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr2272" n="129.22 (388.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la3993">
            <lem wit="A">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
day-

              <lb/>
light

            </rdg>
          </app>
, here was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0031"/>
the clear Ohio water in shore, sure enough, and outside was the old regular

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2273"/>
Muddy!

          <app from="pr2273" n="129.23 (388.9)" type="e" xml:id="la3994">
            <lem wit="A">Muddy!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">muddy.</rdg>
          </app>
So it was all up with Cairo

          <ptr target="#as0130" type="an" xml:id="gs0032"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30597">
We talked it all over. It wouldn’t do to take to the shore; we couldn’t take

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1401"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l10802" type="alt" xml:id="te1401"/>
raft

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0055"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2274"/>
up stream

          <ptr target="#tb0055" type="te" xml:id="tv0055"/>
          <app from="pr2274" n="✱129.26 (388.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la3995">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up stream</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">up the stream</rdg>
          </app>
, of course. There warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2275"/>
no

          <app from="pr2275" n="129.26 (388.16)" type="e" xml:id="la3996">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
way but to wait for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2276"/>
dark

          <app from="pr2276" n="129.27 (388.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la3997">
            <lem wit="MS1a">dark</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dark,</rdg>
          </app>
and start back in the canoe and take the chances. So we slept all day amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2277"/>
cottonwood

          <app from="pr2277" n="129.28 (388.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la3998">
            <lem wit="MS1a">cottonwood</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cotton-wood</rdg>
          </app>
thicket, so as to be fresh for the work, and when we went back to the raft about dark the canoe was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1402"/>
gone!

          <ptr target="#l10804" type="alt" xml:id="te1402"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30642">
We didn’t say a word for a good while. There warn’t anything to say. We both knowed well enough it was some more work of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2278"/>
rattlesnake

          <app from="pr2278" n="129.33 (389.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la3999">
            <lem wit="MS1a">rattlesnake</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rattle-snake</rdg>
          </app>
skin; so what was the use to talk about it? It would only

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2279"/>
look

          <app from="pr2279" n="129.34 (389.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4000">
            <lem wit="A">look</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">seem</rdg>
          </app>
like we was finding fault, and that would be bound to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1403"/>
fetch

          <ptr target="#l10806" type="alt" xml:id="te1403"/>
more bad luck—and keep on fetching it, too, till we knowed enough to keep still.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30665">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2280"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr2280" n="129.37 (389.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la4001">
            <lem wit="MS1a">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
we talked about what we better do, and found there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2281"/>
no

          <app from="pr2281" n="129.38 (390.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4002">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
way but just to go along down with the raft till we got a chance to buy a canoe to go back in. We warn’t going to borrow it

          <pb n="130" xml:id="pb0130"/>
when there warn’t anybody around, the way

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2282"/>
pap

          <app from="pr2282" n="130.1 (390.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4003">
            <lem wit="A">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
would do, for that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2283"/>
might

          <app from="pr2283" n="130.2 (390.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4004">
            <lem wit="A">might</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">would</rdg>
          </app>
set people after us.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30701">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2284"/>
So we

          <app from="pr2284" n="130.3 (390.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4005">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">So we</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">We</rdg>
          </app>
shoved out, after dark,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1404"/>
on

          <ptr target="#l10808" type="alt" xml:id="te1404"/>
the raft.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30714">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2285"/>
Anybody that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1405"/>
don’t

          <ptr target="#l10810" type="alt" xml:id="te1405"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2286"/>
believe,

          <app from="pr2286" n="130.4 (390.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4008">
            <lem wit="MS1a">believe,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
believe

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet, that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2287"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr2287" n="130.4 (390.18)" type="e" xml:id="la4009">
            <lem wit="A">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">it is</rdg>
          </app>
foolishness to handle a snake-skin,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1406"/>
after

          <ptr target="#l10812" type="alt" xml:id="te1406"/>
all that that snake-skin done for us, will believe it now, if they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2288"/>
read

          <app from="pr2288" n="130.6 (391.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4010">
            <lem wit="A">read</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">will read</rdg>
          </app>
on and see what more it done for us.

          <app from="pr2285" n="130.4–6 (390.17–391.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4006">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Anybody . . . us.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4007">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30755">
The place to buy canoes is off of rafts laying up at shore. But we didn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2289"/>
no

          <app from="pr2289" n="130.8 (391.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4011">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
rafts laying

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2290"/>
up; so

          <app from="pr2290" n="130.8 (391.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4012">
            <lem wit="A Cent">up; so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">up as</rdg>
          </app>
we went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2291"/>
along,

          <app from="pr2291" n="130.8 (391.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4013">
            <lem wit="MS1a">along,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
along

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
during three hours and more. Well, the night got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2292"/>
gray

          <app from="pr2292" n="130.9 (391.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4014">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gray</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">gray,</rdg>
          </app>
and ruther thick, which is the next meanest thing to fog. You can’t tell the shape of the river, and you can’t see no distance. It got to be very late and still, and then along comes a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2293"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr2293" n="130.12 (391.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4015">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">steam-boat</rdg>
          </app>
up the river. We lit the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2294"/>
lantern,

          <app from="pr2294" n="130.12 (391.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la4016">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">lantern,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
lantern

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and judged she would see it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2295"/>
Up-stream

          <app from="pr2295" n="130.13 (392.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la4017">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Up-stream</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Up-

              <lb/>
stream

            </rdg>
          </app>
boats didn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2296"/>
generly

          <app from="pr2296" n="130.13 (392.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4018">
            <lem wit="A Cent">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">generally</rdg>
          </app>
come close to us; they go out and follow the bars and hunt for easy water under the reefs; but nights like this they bull right up the channel against the whole river.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30825">
We could hear her pounding along, but we didn’t see her good till she was close.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0033"/>
She aimed right for us. Often they do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2297"/>
that

          <app from="pr2297" n="130.18 (392.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4019">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">that,</rdg>
          </app>
and try to see how close they can come without touching; sometimes the wheel bites off a sweep, and then the pilot sticks his head out and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2298"/>
laughs

          <app from="pr2298" n="130.21 (392.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la4020">
            <lem wit="MS1a">laughs</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">laughs,</rdg>
          </app>
and thinks

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2299"/>
he’s

          <app from="pr2299" n="130.21 (393.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4021">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">he is</rdg>
          </app>
mighty smart. Well, here she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2300"/>
comes

          <app from="pr2300" n="130.21 (393.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4022">
            <lem wit="MS1a">comes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">comes,</rdg>
          </app>
and we said she was going to try to shave

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1407"/>
us

          <ptr target="#as0131" type="an" xml:id="gs0034"/>
;

          <ptr target="#l10814" type="alt" xml:id="te1407"/>
but she didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1408"/>
seem

          <ptr target="#l10816" type="alt" xml:id="te1408"/>
to be sheering off a bit. She was a big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2301"/>
one

          <app from="pr2301" n="130.23 (393.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4023">
            <lem wit="MS1a">one</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">one,</rdg>
          </app>
and she was coming in a hurry,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2302"/>
too—

          <app from="pr2302" n="130.24 (393.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4024">
            <lem wit="MS1a">too—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">too,</rdg>
          </app>
looking like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2303"/>
black

          <app from="pr2303" n="130.24 (393.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4025">
            <lem wit="A Cent">black</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dull</rdg>
          </app>
cloud with rows of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2304"/>
glow-worms

          <app from="pr2304" n="130.24 (393.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4026">
            <lem wit="A Cent">glow-worms</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">dim glow-worms</rdg>
          </app>
around it; but all of a sudden she bulged out, big and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2305"/>
scary

          <app from="pr2305" n="130.25 (393.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4027">
            <lem wit="A Cent">scary</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">black</rdg>
          </app>
, with a long row of wide-open

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2306"/>
furnace-doors

          <app from="pr2306" n="130.26 (393.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4028">
            <lem wit="MS1a">furnace-doors</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">furnace doors</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1409"/>
shining

          <ptr target="#l10818" type="alt" xml:id="te1409"/>
like red-hot teeth, and her monstrous bows and guards hanging right over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2307"/>
us. There

          <app from="pr2307" n="130.27 (393.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la4029">
            <lem wit="A Cent">us. There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
us.—

              <lb/>
There

            </rdg>
          </app>
was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1410"/>
yell at us,

          <ptr target="#l10820" type="alt" xml:id="te1410"/>
and a jingling of bells to stop the engines, a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2308"/>
pow-wow

          <app from="pr2308" n="130.28 (394.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la4030">
            <lem wit="A Cent">pow-wow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
pow-

              <lb/>
wow

            </rdg>
          </app>
of cussing, and whistling of steam—and as Jim went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2309"/>
overboard

          <app from="pr2309" n="130.29 (394.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la4031">
            <lem wit="A Cent">overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
over-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
          </app>
on one side and I on the other, she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1411"/>
come

          <ptr target="#l10822" type="alt" xml:id="te1411"/>
smashing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2310"/>
straight

          <app from="pr2310" n="130.30 (394.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4032">
            <lem wit="A Cent">straight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4033">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2311"/>
raft

          <app from="pr2311" n="130.30 (394.8–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4034">
            <lem wit="A Cent">raft</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">raft and tore it to tooth-picks and splinters</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e30984">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0035"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2312"/>
I

          <app from="pr2312" n="130.31 (394.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4035">
            <lem wit="A Cent">[¶] I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4036">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
dived—and I aimed to find the bottom

          <ptr target="#as0132" type="an" xml:id="gs0036"/>
, too, for a thirty-foot wheel had got to go over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2313"/>
me

          <app from="pr2313" n="130.32 (394.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4037">
            <lem wit="MS1a">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">me,</rdg>
          </app>
and I wanted it to have plenty of room. I could always stay under

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2314"/>
water

          <app from="pr2314" n="130.34 (394.19)" type="e" xml:id="la4038">
            <lem wit="A Cent">water</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4039">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a minute; this time I reckon I staid under water a minute and a half. Then I bounced for the top in a hurry, for I was nearly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2315"/>
busting. I

          <app from="pr2315" n="130.35 (395.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la4040">
            <lem wit="A Cent">busting. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
bursting.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
popped out to my arm-pits and blowed the water out of my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2316"/>
nose

          <app from="pr2316" n="130.36 (395.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4041">
            <lem wit="MS1a">nose</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">nose,</rdg>
          </app>
and puffed a bit. Of course there was a booming current; and of course that boat started her engines again ten seconds after she stopped them, for they never cared much

          <pb n="131" xml:id="pb0131"/>
for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2317"/>
raftsmen

          <app from="pr2317" n="131.1 (395.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4042">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">raftsmen</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rafts-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
; so now she was churning along up the river, out of sight in the thick

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2318"/>
weather

          <app from="pr2318" n="131.2 (395.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4043">
            <lem wit="A Cent">weather</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4044">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, though I could hear her.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31058">
I sung out for Jim about a dozen times, but I didn’t get any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2319"/>
answer,

          <app from="pr2319" n="131.3 (395.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4045">
            <lem wit="MS1a">answer,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">answer;</rdg>
          </app>
so I grabbed a plank that touched me while I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2320"/>
“treading water,”

          <app from="pr2320" n="131.4 (396.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la4046">
            <lem wit="A">“treading water,”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
“treading water

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
”

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
treading water,

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and struck

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1412"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l10824" type="alt" xml:id="te1412"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1413"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l10826" type="alt" xml:id="te1413"/>
shore, shoving it ahead of me. But I made out to see that the drift of the current was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0037"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2321"/>
towards

          <app from="pr2321" n="131.6 (396.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4047">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">toward</rdg>
          </app>
the left-hand shore,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1414"/>
which

          <ptr target="#l10828" type="alt" xml:id="te1414"/>
meant that I was in a crossing; so I changed off and went that way.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31100">
It was one of these long, slanting, two-mile crossings; so I was a good long time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2322"/>
in

          <app from="pr2322" n="131.10 (396.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4048">
            <lem wit="A Cent">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4049">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
getting

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2323"/>
over. I

          <app from="pr2323" n="131.10 (396.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la4050">
            <lem wit="A Cent">over. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
over.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
made a safe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2324"/>
landing

          <app from="pr2324" n="131.10 (396.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4051">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">landing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">landing,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0133" type="an" xml:id="gs0038"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2325"/>
clumb

          <app from="pr2325" n="131.10 (396.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4052">
            <lem wit="MS1a">clumb</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">clum</rdg>
          </app>
up the bank. I couldn’t see but a little ways, but I went poking along over rough ground for a quarter of a mile or more, and then I run across a big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2326"/>
old-fashioned

          <app from="pr2326" n="131.13 (397.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la4053">
            <lem wit="A Cent">old-fashioned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">old fashioned</rdg>
          </app>
double log house before I noticed it. I was going to rush by and get away, but a lot of dogs jumped out and went to howling and barking at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2327"/>
me

          <app from="pr2327" n="131.15 (397.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4054">
            <lem wit="MS1a">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">me,</rdg>
          </app>
and I knowed better than to move another peg.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31156">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y13101">
            <graphic url="y13101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">climbing up the bank</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0328">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XVII.</head>
        <pb n="132" xml:id="pb0132"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31166">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y13201">
            <graphic url="y13201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2328"/>
Chapter XVII.

              <app from="pr2328" n="132 title (397.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4055">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XVII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4056">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">In</ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1321">
            <graphic url="hf1321.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">who’s there?</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e31185">
          <hi rend="smallcaps">about</hi>
half a minute somebody spoke out of a window, without putting his head out, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31189">“Be done, boys! Who’s there?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31191">I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31193">“It’s me.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31195">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2329"/>
Who’s me?

          <app from="pr2329" n="132.8 (398.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4057">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Who’s me?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
Who is

              <hi rend="italic">me?</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31207">“George Jackson, sir.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31209">“What do you want?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31211">
“I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1415"/>
don’t

          <ptr target="#l10830" type="alt" xml:id="te1415"/>
want nothing, sir. I only want to go along by, but the dogs

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2330"/>
won’t

          <app from="pr2330" n="132.13 (398.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4058">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">won’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">wont</rdg>
          </app>
let me.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31226">
“What are you prowling around here this time of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2331"/>
night

          <app from="pr2331" n="132.15 (398.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4059">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">night</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">night,</rdg>
          </app>
for—hey?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31236">
“I warn’t prowling around, sir; I fell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2332"/>
overboard

          <app from="pr2332" n="132.17 (398.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4060">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
over-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
          </app>
off of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2333"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr2333" n="132.17–18 (398.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4061">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">steam-boat</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31256">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2334"/>
O

          <app from="pr2334" n="132.19 (398.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4062">
            <lem wit="MS1a">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, you did, did you? Strike a light there,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2335"/>
somebody

          <app from="pr2335" n="132.19 (398.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la4063">
            <lem wit="A Cent">somebody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">old woman</rdg>
          </app>
. What did you say your name was?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31274">“George Jackson, sir. I’m only a boy.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31276">
“Look here; if you’re telling the truth, you needn’t be afraid—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2336"/>
nobody’ll

          <app from="pr2336" n="132.23 (399.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4064">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">nobody’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">nobody ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
hurt you. But don’t try to budge; stand right where you are.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2337"/>
Rouse

          <app from="pr2337" n="132.24 (399.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4065">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Rouse</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Roust</rdg>
          </app>
out Bob and Tom,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1416"/>
some of you,

          <ptr target="#l10832" type="alt" xml:id="te1416"/>
and fetch the guns. George Jackson, is there anybody with you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31299">
“No,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2338"/>
sir,

          <app from="pr2338" n="132.26 (399.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4066">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">sir,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sir;</rdg>
          </app>
nobody.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31309">
I heard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2339"/>
the people

          <app from="pr2339" n="132.27 (399.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4067">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the people</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">people</rdg>
          </app>
stirring around in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2340"/>
house,

          <app from="pr2340" n="132.27 (399.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4068">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">house,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
house

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2341"/>
see

          <app from="pr2341" n="132.27 (399.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4069">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
a light. The man sung out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31336">
“Snatch that light away,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1417"/>
Betsy,

          <ptr target="#l10834" type="alt" xml:id="te1417"/>
you old fool—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2342"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2342" n="132.29 (399.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4070">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
you got any sense? Put it on the floor behind the front door. Bob, if you and Tom are ready, take your places.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31350">“All ready.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31352">
          <pb n="133" xml:id="pb0133"/>
“Now, George Jackson, do you know the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1418"/>
Shepherdsons?”

          <ptr target="#l10836" type="alt" xml:id="te1418"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31358">“No, sir—I never heard of them.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31361">
“Well, that may be so, and it mayn’t.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1419"/>
Now,

          <ptr target="#l10838" type="alt" xml:id="te1419"/>
all ready. Step forward, George Jackson. And mind, don’t you hurry—come mighty slow. If there’s anybody with you, let him keep

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2343"/>
back—

          <app from="pr2343" n="133.5 (400.20–21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4071">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">back—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">back;</rdg>
          </app>
if he shows himself he’ll be shot. Come along, now. Come slow; push the door

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2344"/>
open,

          <app from="pr2344" n="133.6 (401.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4072">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">open,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
open

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yourself—just enough to squeeze in,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2345"/>
d’you

          <app from="pr2345" n="133.7 (401.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4073">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">d’you</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">d’ you</rdg>
          </app>
hear?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31392">
I didn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2346"/>
hurry. I

          <app from="pr2346" n="133.8 (401.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la4074">
            <lem wit="C">hurry. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
hurry.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">hurry, I</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hurry; I</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2347"/>
couldn’t,

          <app from="pr2347" n="133.8 (401.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4075">
            <lem wit="MS1a">couldn’t,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">couldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2348"/>
I’d a

          <app from="pr2348" n="133.8 (401.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4076">
            <lem wit="A">I’d a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I had</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">I’d ’a’</rdg>
          </app>
wanted to. I took one slow step at a time, and there warn’t a sound, only I thought I could hear my heart. The dogs

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2349"/>
were

          <app from="pr2349" n="133.10 (401.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4077">
            <lem wit="A Cent">were</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">was</rdg>
          </app>
as still as the humans, but they followed a little behind me. When I got to the three log

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2350"/>
door-steps

          <app from="pr2350" n="133.11 (401.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4078">
            <lem wit="MS1a">door-steps</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">door-steps,</rdg>
          </app>
I heard them unlocking and unbarring and unbolting. I put my hand on the door and pushed it a little and a little more, till somebody said, “There, that’s enough—put your head in.” I done it, but I judged they would take it off.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31442">
The candle was on the floor, and there they all was, looking at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2351"/>
me and

          <app from="pr2351" n="133.17 (402.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4079">
            <lem wit="MS1a">me and</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">me, and</rdg>
          </app>
me at them, for about a quarter of a minute. Three big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2352"/>
men,

          <app from="pr2352" n="133.17 (402.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4080">
            <lem wit="MS1a">men,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
men

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with guns pointed at me, which made me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2353"/>
wince

          <app from="pr2353" n="133.18 (402.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4081">
            <lem wit="MS1a">wince</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wince,</rdg>
          </app>
I tell

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1420"/>
you;

          <ptr target="#l10840" type="alt" xml:id="te1420"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2354"/>
oldest

          <app from="pr2354" n="133.18–19 (402.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4082">
            <lem wit="MS1a">oldest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">oldest,</rdg>
          </app>
gray and about sixty, the other two thirty or more—all of them fine and handsome—and the sweetest old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2355"/>
gray-headed

          <app from="pr2355" n="133.20 (402.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la4083">
            <lem wit="A Cent">gray-headed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
gray-

              <lb/>
headed

            </rdg>
          </app>
lady, and back of her two young

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2356"/>
women

          <app from="pr2356" n="133.21 (402.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4084">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">women</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">women,</rdg>
          </app>
which I couldn’t see right well. The old gentleman says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31500">“There—I reckon it’s all right. Come in.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31502">
As soon as I was in, the old gentleman

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2357"/>
he

          <app from="pr2357" n="133.24 (403.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4085">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4086">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
locked the door and barred it and bolted it, and told the young men to come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2358"/>
in

          <app from="pr2358" n="133.25 (403.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4087">
            <lem wit="A Cent">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4088">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with their guns, and they all went in a big

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1421"/>
parlor

          <ptr target="#l10842" type="alt" xml:id="te1421"/>
that had a new rag carpet on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2359"/>
floor

          <app from="pr2359" n="133.27 (403.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4089">
            <lem wit="MS1a">floor</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">floor,</rdg>
          </app>
and got together in a corner that was out of range of the front windows—there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2360"/>
none

          <app from="pr2360" n="133.28 (403.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4090">
            <lem wit="A Cent">none</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
on the side. They held the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2361"/>
candle

          <app from="pr2361" n="133.28–29 (403.17–18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4091">
            <lem wit="MS1a">candle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">candle,</rdg>
          </app>
and took a good look at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2362"/>
me

          <app from="pr2362" n="133.29 (403.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4092">
            <lem wit="MS1a">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">me,</rdg>
          </app>
and all said, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2363"/>
Why,

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
          <app from="pr2363" n="133.29 (403.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la4093">
            <lem wit="Cent">
Why,

              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Why, he</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
Why

              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2364"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2364" n="133.29 (403.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4094">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
a Shepherdson—no, there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2365"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2365" n="133.30 (403.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4095">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
any Shepherdson about him.” Then the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1422"/>
old

          <ptr target="#l10844" type="alt" xml:id="te1422"/>
man said he hoped I wouldn’t mind being searched for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2366"/>
arms

          <app from="pr2366" n="133.31 (404.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4096">
            <lem wit="MS1a">arms</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">arms,</rdg>
          </app>
because he didn’t mean no harm by it—it was only to make sure. So he didn’t pry into my pockets, but only felt outside with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2367"/>
hands

          <app from="pr2367" n="133.33 (404.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4097">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hands</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hands,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hand,</rdg>
          </app>
and said it was all right. He told me to make myself easy and at home, and tell all about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2368"/>
myself,

          <app from="pr2368" n="133.35 (404.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4098">
            <lem wit="MS1a">myself,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">myself;</rdg>
          </app>
but the old lady says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31623">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2369"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2369" n="133.36 (404.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4099">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
bless you, Saul, the poor thing’s as wet as he can be; and don’t you reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2370"/>
it may be

          <app from="pr2370" n="133.37 (404.20)" type="e" xml:id="la4100">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it may be</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">maybe</rdg>
          </app>
he’s hungry?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31641">“True for you, Rachel—I forgot.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31643">
          <pb n="134" xml:id="pb0134"/>
So the old lady says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31646">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1423"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2371"/>
Betsy,

          <app from="pr2371" n="134.2 (405.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4101">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Betsy,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
Betsy

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#l10846" type="alt" xml:id="te1423"/>
(this was a nigger

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2372"/>
woman,)

          <app from="pr2372" n="134.2 (405.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4102">
            <lem wit="MS1a">woman,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">woman),</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1424"/>
“you

          <ptr target="#l10848" type="alt" xml:id="te1424"/>
fly around and get him something to eat, as quick as you can, poor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2373"/>
thing,

          <app from="pr2373" n="134.3 (405.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4103">
            <lem wit="MS1a">thing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">thing;</rdg>
          </app>
and one of you girls go and wake up Buck and tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2374"/>
him—O

          <app from="pr2374" n="134.4 (405.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4104">
            <lem wit="C">him—O</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">him—O</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">him—Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, here he is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2375"/>
himself. Buck

          <app from="pr2375" n="134.4–5 (405.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la4105">
            <lem wit="A Cent">himself. Buck</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
himself.—

              <lb/>
Buck

            </rdg>
          </app>
, take this little stranger and get the wet clothes off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2376"/>
from him

          <app from="pr2376" n="134.7 (405.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4106">
            <lem wit="A">from him</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of him</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">from him,</rdg>
          </app>
and dress him up in some of yours that’s dry.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="left" xml:id="y13401">
          <graphic url="y13401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">buck.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31716">
Buck looked

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0039"/>
about as old as me—thirteen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2377"/>
or fourteen

          <app from="pr2377" n="134.11–12 (405.18)" type="e" xml:id="la4107">
            <lem wit="A Cent">or fourteen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4108">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
or along there

          <ptr target="#as0134" type="an" xml:id="gs0040"/>
, though he was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1425"/>
a little

          <ptr target="#l10850" type="alt" xml:id="te1425"/>
bigger than me. He hadn’t on anything but a shirt, and he was very frowsy-headed. He come in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2378"/>
gaping

          <app from="pr2378" n="134.17 (406.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4109">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">gaping</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gaping,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2379"/>
and

          <app from="pr2379" n="134.18 (406.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4110">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and and</rdg>
          </app>
digging one fist into his eyes, and he was dragging a gun along with the other

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1426"/>
one. He

          <ptr target="#l10852" type="alt" xml:id="te1426"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31757">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2380"/>
Ain’t

          <app from="pr2380" n="134.21 (406.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4111">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Aint</rdg>
          </app>
they no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1427"/>
Shepherdsons

          <ptr target="#l10854" type="alt" xml:id="te1427"/>
around?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31771">They said, no, ’twas a false alarm.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31773">
“Well,” he says, “if they’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2381"/>
a ben

          <app from="pr2381" n="134.26 (406.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4112">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">a ben</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ be’n</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2382"/>
some

          <app from="pr2382" n="134.26 (406.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4113">
            <lem wit="MS1a">some</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">some,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1428"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l10856" type="alt" xml:id="te1428"/>
reckon I’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2383"/>
a got

          <app from="pr2383" n="134.26 (406.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4114">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">a got</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ got</rdg>
          </app>
one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31802">They all laughed, and Bob says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31804">
“Why, Buck, they might have scalped us all, you’ve been so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2384"/>
slow in

          <app from="pr2384" n="134.30–31 (406.21)" type="e" xml:id="la4115">
            <lem wit="A Cent">slow in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">long</rdg>
          </app>
coming.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31814">
“Well, nobody come after me, and it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2385"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2385" n="134.32 (407.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4116">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
right. I’m always kep’ down; I don’t get no show.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31824">
“Never mind, Buck, my boy,” says the old man, “you’ll have show enough, all in good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2386"/>
time,

          <app from="pr2386" n="134.35 (407.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4117">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">time,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">time;</rdg>
          </app>
don’t you fret about that. Go ’long with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2387"/>
you,

          <app from="pr2387" n="134.36 (407.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4118">
            <lem wit="MS1a">you,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
you

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1429"/>
now

          <ptr target="#l10858" type="alt" xml:id="te1429"/>
, and do as your mother told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2388"/>
you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31848">
When

          <app from="pr2388" n="134.36–37 (407.13–408.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4119">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you.” [¶] When</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
you.”

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] When

            </rdg>
          </app>
we got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2389"/>
up stairs

          <app from="pr2389" n="134.37 (408.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4120">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">up stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">upstairs</rdg>
          </app>
to his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2390"/>
room,

          <app from="pr2390" n="134.37 (408.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4121">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">room,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
room

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he got me a coarse shirt and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1430"/>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2391"/>
roundabout

          <app from="pr2391" n="134.38 (408.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4122">
            <lem wit="Cent">roundabout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">yellow nankeen roundabout</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
round-

              <lb/>
about

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10860" type="alt" xml:id="te1430"/>
and pants of his, and I put them on. While I was at it he asked me what my name was, but before I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1431"/>
could

          <ptr target="#l10862" type="alt" xml:id="te1431"/>
tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2392"/>
him

          <app from="pr2392" n="134.39 (408.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4123">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">him</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">him,</rdg>
          </app>
he started

          <pb n="135" xml:id="pb0135"/>
to telling me about a blue jay and a young rabbit he had

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1432"/>
catched

          <ptr target="#l10864" type="alt" xml:id="te1432"/>
in the woods day before yesterday, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0041"/>
he asked me where Moses was when the candle went out

          <ptr target="#as0135" type="an" xml:id="gs0042"/>
. I said I didn’t know; I hadn’t heard about it before,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2393"/>
no way

          <app from="pr2393" n="135.4 (409.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4124">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">no way</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">noway</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31922">“Well, guess,” he says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31924">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2394"/>
How’m

          <app from="pr2394" n="135.6 (409.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4125">
            <lem wit="A Cent">How’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">How am</rdg>
          </app>
I going to guess,” says I, “when I never heard tell about it before?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31934">“But you can guess, can’t you? It’s just as easy.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31937">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Which</hi>
candle?” I says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31942">
“Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2395"/>
any

          <app from="pr2395" n="135.10 (409.19)" type="e" xml:id="la4126">
            <lem wit="A Cent">any</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
candle,” he says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31953">
“I don’t know where he was,” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2396"/>
I,

          <app from="pr2396" n="135.11 (410.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4127">
            <lem wit="MS1a">I,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">I;</rdg>
          </app>
“where

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2397"/>
was he

          <app from="pr2397" n="135.11 (410.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4128">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
he

            </rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31973">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2398"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2398" n="135.12 (410.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4129">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
he was in the

          <hi rend="italic">dark!</hi>
That’s where he was!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e31986">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2399"/>
Well

          <app from="pr2399" n="135.13 (410.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4130">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
if you knowed where he was, what did you ask

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2400"/>
me

          <app from="pr2400" n="135.13 (410.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4131">
            <lem wit="A Cent">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">me about it</rdg>
          </app>
for?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32004">
“Why, blame it, it’s a riddle, don’t you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2401"/>
see? Say—

          <app from="pr2401" n="135.14 (410.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la4132">
            <lem wit="C">see? Say—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
see?—

              <lb/>
Say—

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">see? Say,</rdg>
          </app>
how long

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2402"/>
are

          <app from="pr2402" n="135.14 (410.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4133">
            <lem wit="A Cent">are</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4134">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you going to stay here? You got to stay always. We can just have booming times—they don’t have no school now. Do you own a dog? I’ve got a dog—and he’ll go in the river and bring out chips that you throw in. Do you like to comb

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2403"/>
up,

          <app from="pr2403" n="135.18 (411.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4135">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Sundays, and all that kind of foolishness? You bet I don’t, but ma

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1433"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l10866" type="alt" xml:id="te1433"/>
makes me.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2404"/>
Confound

          <app from="pr2404" n="135.19 (411.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4136">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Confound</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Consound</rdg>
          </app>
these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2405"/>
ole

          <app from="pr2405" n="135.20 (411.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4137">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ole</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">old</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2406"/>
britches,

          <app from="pr2406" n="135.20 (411.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4138">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">britches,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">britches!</rdg>
          </app>
I reckon I’d better put ’em on, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2407"/>
I’d ruther

          <app from="pr2407" n="135.20 (411.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4139">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d ruther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I’d druther</rdg>
          </app>
not, it’s so warm.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1434"/>
Are

          <ptr target="#l10868" type="alt" xml:id="te1434"/>
you all ready? All right—come along, old hoss.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32077">
Cold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2408"/>
corn-pone

          <app from="pr2408" n="135.22 (411.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4140">
            <lem wit="A Cent">corn-pone</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">corn pone</rdg>
          </app>
, cold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2409"/>
corn beef

          <app from="pr2409" n="135.22 (411.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4141">
            <lem wit="MS1a">corn beef</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">corn-beef</rdg>
          </app>
, butter and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2410"/>
buttermilk

          <app from="pr2410" n="135.22 (411.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4142">
            <lem wit="MS1a">buttermilk</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">butter-milk</rdg>
          </app>
—that is what they had for me down there, and there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2411"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2411" n="135.23 (411.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4143">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2412"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr2412" n="135.23 (411.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4144">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
better that ever I’ve come across yet. Buck and his ma and all of them smoked cob pipes, except the nigger woman, which was gone, and the two young women. They all smoked and talked, and I eat and talked. The young women had quilts around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2413"/>
them

          <app from="pr2413" n="135.27 (412.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4145">
            <lem wit="MS1a">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">them,</rdg>
          </app>
and their hair down their backs. They

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1435"/>
all

          <ptr target="#l10870" type="alt" xml:id="te1435"/>
asked me questions, and I told them how pap and me and all the family was living on a little farm down at the bottom of Arkansaw, and my sister Mary Ann run off and got married and never was heard of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1436"/>
no

          <ptr target="#l10872" type="alt" xml:id="te1436"/>
more, and Bill went to hunt them and he warn’t heard of no more,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0056"/>
and Tom and Mort died,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2414"/>
and by and by mam died,

          <ptr target="#tb0056" type="te" xml:id="tv0056"/>
          <app from="pr2414" n="✱135.32–33 (412.19–20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4146">
            <lem wit="MS1a">and by and by mam died,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4147">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and then there warn’t nobody but just me and pap

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1437"/>
left,

          <ptr target="#l10874" type="alt" xml:id="te1437"/>
and he was just trimmed down to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2415"/>
nothing,

          <app from="pr2415" n="135.34 (413.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4148">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">nothing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
nothing

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
on account of his troubles; so when he died I took what there was left, because the farm didn’t belong to us, and started up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2416"/>
river

          <app from="pr2416" n="135.36 (413.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4149">
            <lem wit="MS1a">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">river,</rdg>
          </app>
deck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2417"/>
passage

          <app from="pr2417" n="135.36 (413.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4150">
            <lem wit="MS1a">passage</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">passage,</rdg>
          </app>
and fell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2418"/>
overboard

          <app from="pr2418" n="135.37 (413.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4151">
            <lem wit="MS1a">overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">overboard;</rdg>
          </app>
and that was how I come to be here. So they said I could have a home there as long as I wanted it. Then it was most daylight, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1438"/>
everybody

          <ptr target="#l10876" type="alt" xml:id="te1438"/>
went to bed, and I went to bed with Buck,

          <pb n="136" xml:id="pb0136"/>
and when I waked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2419"/>
up,

          <app from="pr2419" n="136.1 (413.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4152">
            <lem wit="MS1a">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1439"/>
in the morning,

          <ptr target="#l10878" type="alt" xml:id="te1439"/>
drat it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2420"/>
all

          <app from="pr2420" n="136.1 (413.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4153">
            <lem wit="MS1a">all</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">all,</rdg>
          </app>
I had forgot what my name was. So I laid there about an hour trying to think, and when Buck waked up, I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32213">“Can you spell, Buck?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32215">“Yes,” he says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32217">
“I bet you can’t spell my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1440"/>
name,

          <ptr target="#l10880" type="alt" xml:id="te1440"/>
” says I.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32223">“I bet you what you dare I can,” says he.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32226">
“All

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1441"/>
right,” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2421"/>
I,

          <app from="pr2421" n="136.8 (414.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4154">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">I,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">I;</rdg>
          </app>
“go

          <ptr target="#l10882" type="alt" xml:id="te1441"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1442"/>
ahead.”

          <ptr target="#l10884" type="alt" xml:id="te1442"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32242">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1443"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2422"/>
G-o-r-g-e

          <app from="pr2422" n="136.9 (414.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4155">
            <lem wit="A Cent">G-o-r-g-e</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">G-o-r-g-e,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l10886" type="alt" xml:id="te1443"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1444"/>
J-a-x-o-n

          <ptr target="#l10888" type="alt" xml:id="te1444"/>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2423"/>
there,

          <app from="pr2423" n="136.9 (414.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4156">
            <lem wit="MS1a">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now,” he says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32266">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1445"/>
“Well,” says I, “you

          <ptr target="#l10890" type="alt" xml:id="te1445"/>
done it, but I didn’t think you could. It

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2424"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2424" n="136.10 (414.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4157">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
no slouch of a name to spell—right off without studying.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32279">
I set it down, private, because somebody might want

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
to spell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2425"/>
it,

          <app from="pr2425" n="136.13 (414.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4158">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
next, and so I wanted to be handy with it and rattle it off like I was used to it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32292">
It was a mighty nice family, and a mighty nice house, too. I

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0043"/>
hadn’t seen no house out in the country before that was so nice and had so much style

          <ptr target="#as0136" type="an" xml:id="gs0044"/>
. It didn’t have an iron latch

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1446"/>
on

          <ptr target="#l10892" type="alt" xml:id="te1446"/>
the front door, nor a wooden one with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2426"/>
buckskin

          <app from="pr2426" n="136.18 (415.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la4159">
            <lem wit="A Cent">buckskin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
buck-

              <lb/>
skin

            </rdg>
          </app>
string, but a brass knob to turn, the same as houses in a town. There warn’t no bed in the parlor, not a sign of a bed; but heaps of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1447"/>
parlors

          <ptr target="#l10894" type="alt" xml:id="te1447"/>
in towns has beds in them. There was a big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2427"/>
fire place

          <app from="pr2427" n="136.21 (415.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4160">
            <lem wit="MS1a">fire place</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fireplace</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">fire-place</rdg>
          </app>
that was bricked on the bottom, and the bricks was kept clean and red by

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1448"/>
pouring

          <ptr target="#l10896" type="alt" xml:id="te1448"/>
water on them and scrubbing them with another brick; sometimes they washed them over with red water-paint that they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1449"/>
call

          <ptr target="#l10898" type="alt" xml:id="te1449"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2428"/>
Spanish brown

          <app from="pr2428" n="136.24 (416.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4161">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Spanish brown</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Spanish-brown</rdg>
          </app>
, same as they do in town. They had big brass dog-irons that could hold up a saw-log.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0045"/>
There was a clock on the middle of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2429"/>
mantel piece

          <app from="pr2429" n="136.26 (416.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4162">
            <lem wit="MS1a">mantel piece</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">mantel-piece,</rdg>
          </app>
with a picture of a town painted on the bottom half of the glass front, and a round place in the middle of it for the sun, and you could see the pendulum swing behind it. It was beautiful to hear that clock tick; and sometimes when one of these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2430"/>
pedlers

          <app from="pr2430" n="136.30 (416.22–417.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4163">
            <lem wit="MS1a">pedlers</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">peddlers</rdg>
          </app>
had been along and scoured her up and got her in good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2431"/>
shape

          <app from="pr2431" n="136.31 (417.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4164">
            <lem wit="MS1a">shape</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">shape,</rdg>
          </app>
she would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1450"/>
start in

          <ptr target="#l10900" type="alt" xml:id="te1450"/>
and strike a hundred and fifty before she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2432"/>
got tuckered out

          <app from="pr2432" n="136.32 (417.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4165">
            <lem wit="A Cent">got tuckered out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">stopped</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0137" type="an" xml:id="gs0046"/>
. They wouldn’t took any money for her.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32384">
Well, there was a big outlandish parrot on each side of the clock, made out of something like

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1451"/>
chalk,

          <ptr target="#l10902" type="alt" xml:id="te1451"/>
and painted up gaudy. By one of the parrots was a cat made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2433"/>
of crockery

          <app from="pr2433" n="136.36 (417.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4166">
            <lem wit="MS1a">of crockery</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">of crockery,</rdg>
          </app>
and a crockery dog by the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1452"/>
other;

          <ptr target="#l10904" type="alt" xml:id="te1452"/>
and when you pressed down on them they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2434"/>
squeaked

          <app from="pr2434" n="136.37 (417.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4167">
            <lem wit="MS1a">squeaked</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">squeaked,</rdg>
          </app>
but didn’t open their mouths nor look different

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2435"/>
nor interested

          <app from="pr2435" n="136.38 (417.21)" type="e" xml:id="la4168">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nor interested</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4169">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. They

          <pb n="137" xml:id="pb0137"/>
squeaked through

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2436"/>
underneath

          <app from="pr2436" n="137.1 (417.22–418.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4170">
            <lem wit="A Cent">underneath</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">a hole underneath</rdg>
          </app>
. There was a couple of big

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1453"/>
wild-turkey-wing

          <ptr target="#l10906" type="alt" xml:id="te1453"/>
fans spread out behind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2437"/>
those

          <app from="pr2437" n="137.2 (418.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4171">
            <lem wit="A Cent">those</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">these</rdg>
          </app>
things. On a table in the middle of the room was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1454"/>
kind

          <ptr target="#l10908" type="alt" xml:id="te1454"/>
of a lovely crockery basket that had apples and oranges and peaches and grapes piled up in it which was much

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1455"/>
redder

          <ptr target="#l10910" type="alt" xml:id="te1455"/>
and yellower and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0047"/>
prettier than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2438"/>
real ones is

          <app from="pr2438" n="137.5 (418.14–16)" type="e" xml:id="la4172">
            <lem wit="A Cent">real ones is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">such things generally is, and looked ever so natural</rdg>
          </app>
, but they warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2439"/>
real,

          <app from="pr2439" n="137.6 (418.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4173">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">real,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
real

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
because you could see where pieces had got chipped off and showed the white chalk or whatever it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2440"/>
was,

          <app from="pr2440" n="137.7 (418.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4174">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
underneath

          <ptr target="#as0138" type="an" xml:id="gs0048"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32481">
This table had a cover made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2441"/>
out

          <app from="pr2441" n="137.8 (419.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4175">
            <lem wit="A Cent">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4176">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of beautiful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2442"/>
oil cloth

          <app from="pr2442" n="137.8 (419.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4177">
            <lem wit="MS1a">oil cloth</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">oil-cloth</rdg>
          </app>
, with a red and blue

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1456"/>
spread-eagle

          <ptr target="#l10912" type="alt" xml:id="te1456"/>
painted on it, and a painted border all around. It come all the way from Philadelphia, they said. There was some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2443"/>
books,

          <app from="pr2443" n="137.11 (419.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4178">
            <lem wit="MS1a">books,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
books

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too, piled up perfectly exact, on each corner of the table. One was a big family Bible, full of pictures. One was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0049"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2444"/>
“Pilgrim’s Progress,”

          <app from="pr2444" n="137.12–13 (419.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4179">
            <lem wit="A Cent">“Pilgrim’s Progress,”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <add>Pilgrim’s Progress,</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
about a man that left his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2445"/>
family,

          <app from="pr2445" n="137.13 (419.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4180">
            <lem wit="MS1a">family,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
family

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
it didn’t say why

          <ptr target="#as0139" type="an" xml:id="gs0050"/>
. I read considerable in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2446"/>
it,

          <app from="pr2446" n="137.14 (419.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4181">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now and then.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2447"/>
The statements was interesting, but tough.

          <app from="pr2447" n="137.14–15 (419.18)" type="e" xml:id="la4182">
            <lem wit="A Cent">The . . . tough.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4183">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2448"/>
Another

          <app from="pr2448" n="137.15 (419.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la4184">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Another</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Another one</rdg>
          </app>
was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0051"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2449"/>
“Friendship’s Offering,”

          <app from="pr2449" n="137.15 (419.19–20)" type="e" xml:id="la4185">
            <lem wit="A Cent">“Friendship’s Offering,”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <add>Friendship’s Offering,</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
full of beautiful stuff and poetry; but I didn’t read the poetry

          <ptr target="#as0140" type="an" xml:id="gs0052"/>
. Another was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0053"/>
Henry Clay’s Speeches

          <ptr target="#as0141" type="an" xml:id="gs0054"/>
, and another was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0055"/>
Dr. Gunn’s Family Medicine, which told you all about what to do if a body was sick

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2450"/>
or dead

          <app from="pr2450" n="137.18 (420.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4186">
            <lem wit="A Cent">or dead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4187">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0142" type="an" xml:id="gs0056"/>
. There was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2451"/>
hymn book

          <app from="pr2451" n="137.19 (420.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4188">
            <lem wit="MS1a">hymn book</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Hymn Book</rdg>
          </app>
, and a lot of other books.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2452"/>
And there

          <app from="pr2452" n="137.19 (420.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4189">
            <lem wit="A Cent">And there</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">There</rdg>
          </app>
was nice split-bottom chairs, and perfectly sound, too—not bagged down in the middle and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2453"/>
busted

          <app from="pr2453" n="137.21 (420.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4190">
            <lem wit="A Cent">busted</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">broke</rdg>
          </app>
, like an old basket.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32613">
They had pictures hung on the walls—mainly

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0057"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2454"/>
Washingtons,

          <app from="pr2454" n="137.22 (420.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4191">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Washingtons,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
Washingtons

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and Lafayettes, and battles, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0059"/>
Highland Marys

          <ptr target="#as0144" type="an" xml:id="gs0060"/>
, and one called “Signing the Declaration.”

          <ptr target="#as0143" type="an" xml:id="gs0058"/>
There was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0061"/>
some that they called crayons, which one of the daughters which was dead made her own self when she was only fifteen years old. They was different from any pictures I ever see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2455"/>
before;

          <app from="pr2455" n="137.27 (421.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4192">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">before;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">before—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2456"/>
blacker, mostly

          <app from="pr2456" n="137.27 (421.7–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4193">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blacker, mostly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">blacker in places, and whiter in other places</rdg>
          </app>
, than is common

          <ptr target="#as0145" type="an" xml:id="gs0062"/>
. One was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0063"/>
a woman in a slim black dress, belted small under the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2457"/>
arm-pits

          <app from="pr2457" n="137.28 (421.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4194">
            <lem wit="A Cent">arm-pits</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
arm-

              <lb/>
pits

            </rdg>
          </app>
, with bulges like a cabbage in the middle of the sleeves, and a large black scoop-shovel bonnet with a black veil, and white slim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2458"/>
ancles

          <app from="pr2458" n="137.30 (421.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4195">
            <lem wit="MS1a">ancles</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">ankles</rdg>
          </app>
crossed about with black tape, and very wee black slippers,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2459"/>
like a chisel,

          <app from="pr2459" n="137.31–32 (421.20)" type="e" xml:id="la4196">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like a chisel,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4197">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and she was leaning pensive on a tombstone on her right elbow, under a weeping willow, and her other hand hanging down her side holding a white

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2460"/>
handkerchief

          <app from="pr2460" n="137.34 (422.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la4198">
            <lem wit="A Cent">handkerchief</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
hander-

              <lb/>
chief,

            </rdg>
          </app>
and a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1457"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2461"/>
reticule,

          <app from="pr2461" n="137.34 (422.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4199">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">reticule,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">reticule;</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <ptr target="#l10914" type="alt" xml:id="te1457"/>
underneath the picture it said “Shall I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2462"/>
Never See Thee More Alas

          <app from="pr2462" n="137.35 (422.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4200">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Never See Thee More Alas</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">never see thee more alas</rdg>
          </app>
.”

          <ptr target="#as0146" type="an" xml:id="gs0064"/>
Another one was a young lady with her hair all combed up straight to the top of her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2463"/>
head

          <app from="pr2463" n="137.37 (422.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4201">
            <lem wit="MS1a">head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">head,</rdg>
          </app>
and knotted there in front of a comb like a chair-back, and she was crying into a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2464"/>
handkerchief

          <app from="pr2464" n="137.38 (422.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4202">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">handkerchief</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">handkerchief,</rdg>
          </app>
and had a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0065"/>
dead

          <pb n="138" xml:id="pb0138"/>
bird

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1458"/>
laying

          <ptr target="#l10916" type="alt" xml:id="te1458"/>
on its back in her other hand with its heels up, and underneath the picture it said “I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2465"/>
Shall Never Hear Thy Sweet Chirrup More Alas

          <app from="pr2465" n="138.2–3 (422.21–423.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4203">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Shall Never Hear Thy Sweet Chirrup More Alas</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">shall never hear thy sweet chirrup more alas</rdg>
          </app>
.” There was one where a young lady was at a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2466"/>
window,

          <app from="pr2466" n="138.3 (423.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4204">
            <lem wit="MS1a">window,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
window

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
looking up at the moon, and tears running down her cheeks

          <ptr target="#as0147" type="an" xml:id="gs0066"/>
; and she had an open letter in one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2467"/>
hand

          <app from="pr2467" n="138.5 (423.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4205">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">hand</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hand,</rdg>
          </app>
with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1459"/>
black

          <ptr target="#l10918" type="alt" xml:id="te1459"/>
sealing-wax showing on one edge of it, and she was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2468"/>
mashing

          <app from="pr2468" n="138.6 (423.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4206">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mashing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">squeezing</rdg>
          </app>
a locket with a chain to it against her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2469"/>
mouth,

          <app from="pr2469" n="138.7 (423.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4207">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">mouth,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">mouth;</rdg>
          </app>
and underneath the picture it said “And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2470"/>
Art Thou Gone Yes Thou Art Gone Alas

          <app from="pr2470" n="138.7–8 (423.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la4208">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Art Thou Gone Yes Thou Art Gone Alas</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">art thou gone, yes thou art gone alas</rdg>
          </app>
.” These was all nice pictures, I reckon, but I didn’t somehow seem to take to them, because if ever I was down a little, they always give me the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1460"/>
fan-tods. Everybody

          <ptr target="#l10920" type="alt" xml:id="te1460"/>
was sorry she died,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1461"/>
because

          <ptr target="#l10922" type="alt" xml:id="te1461"/>
she had laid out a lot more of these pictures to do, and a body could see by what she had done what they had lost. But I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2471"/>
reckoned, that

          <app from="pr2471" n="138.13 (424.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4209">
            <lem wit="A">reckoned, that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">reckoned,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">reckoned that,</rdg>
          </app>
with her disposition, she was having a better time in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2472"/>
graveyard

          <app from="pr2472" n="138.14 (424.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la4210">
            <lem wit="Cent">graveyard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a A">
grave-

              <lb/>
yard

            </rdg>
          </app>
. She was at work on what they said was her greatest picture when she took sick, and every day and every night it was her prayer to be allowed to live till she got it done, but she never got the chance. It was a picture of a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0067"/>
young woman in a long white gown, standing on the rail of a bridge

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1462"/>
all

          <ptr target="#l10924" type="alt" xml:id="te1462"/>
ready to jump off

          <ptr target="#as0148" type="an" xml:id="gs0068"/>
, with her hair all down her back, and looking up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2473"/>
to

          <app from="pr2473" n="138.24 (425.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4211">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">at</rdg>
          </app>
the moon, with the tears running down her face, and she had two arms folded across her breast, and two arms stretched out in front, and two more reaching up towards the moon—and the idea

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2474"/>
was,

          <app from="pr2474" n="138.32 (425.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4212">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to see which pair would look best and then scratch out all the other arms;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2475"/>
but

          <app from="pr2475" n="138.35 (425.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4213">
            <lem wit="MS1a">but</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">but,</rdg>
          </app>
as I was saying, she died before she got her mind made

          <pb n="139" xml:id="pb0139"/>
up, and now they kept this picture over the head of the bed in her room, and every time her birthday come they hung flowers on it. Other times it was hid with a little curtain. The young woman in the picture had a kind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1463"/>
of a

          <ptr target="#l10926" type="alt" xml:id="te1463"/>
nice sweet face, but there was so many arms it made her look too

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2477"/>
spidery, seemed to me

          <app from="pr2477" n="139.5 (426.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4216">
            <lem wit="A Cent">spidery, seemed to me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">spidery</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <figure rend="left" xml:id="y13801">
          <graphic url="y13801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2476"/>
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">it made her look too spidery</hi>
.”

            <app from="pr2476" n="138 caption" type="e" xml:id="la4214">
              <lem wit="C">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">it made her look too spidery</hi>
.”

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1a Cent">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4215">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">it made her look spidery</hi>
.”

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e32894">
This young girl kept a scrap-book when she was alive, and used to paste obituaries

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1464"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2478"/>
accidents,

          <app from="pr2478" n="139.7 (426.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4217">
            <lem wit="MS1a">accidents,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
accidents

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and cases of patient suffering

          <ptr target="#l10928" type="alt" xml:id="te1464"/>
in it out of

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0069"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2479"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Presbyterian Observer</hi>
          <app from="pr2479" n="139.8 (426.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4218">
            <lem wit="MS1a">
              <hi rend="italic">Presbyterian Observer</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Presbyterian Observer</hi>
,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">“Presbyterian Observer,”</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0149" type="an" xml:id="gs0070"/>
and write poetry after them out of her own head. It was very good poetry.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2480"/>
This is what she wrote about a boy by the name of Stephen Dowling Bots that fell down a well and was drownded:

        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <lg>
            <l rend="center">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2481"/>
              <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0071"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">Ode to Stephen Dowling Bots</hi>
,

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1465"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">Dec’d</hi>
              <ptr target="#as0150" type="an" xml:id="gs0072"/>
.

              <ptr target="#l10930" type="alt" xml:id="te1465"/>
              <app from="pr2481" n="139.12 (427.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la4221">
                <lem wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">Ode to Stephen Dowling Bots, Dec’d</hi>
.

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
Ode to Stephen Dowling Bots, Dec’d.

                  <lb/>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4222">centered rule</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">And did young Stephen sicken,</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">And did young Stephen die?</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">And did the sad hearts thicken,</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">And did the mourners cry?</l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">No; such was not the fate of</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">Young Stephen Dowling Bots;</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">
Though sad hearts round him

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1466"/>
thickened,

              <ptr target="#l10932" type="alt" xml:id="te1466"/>
            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
’Twas not from

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2482"/>
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1467"/>
sickness’

              <ptr target="#l10934" type="alt" xml:id="te1467"/>
              <app from="pr2482" n="139.20 (427.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4223">
                <lem wit="A">sickness’</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">sickness’s</rdg>
              </app>
shots.

            </l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">No whooping-cough did rack his frame,</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
Nor measles

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2483"/>
drear,

              <app from="pr2483" n="139.22 (427.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4224">
                <lem wit="A">drear,</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">mar</rdg>
              </app>
with spots;

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">Not these impaired the sacred name</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">Of Stephen Dowling Bots.</l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2484"/>
Despisèd

              <app from="pr2484" n="139.25 (427½.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4225">
                <lem wit="MS1a">Despisèd</lem>
                <rdg wit="A">Despised</rdg>
              </app>
love struck not with woe

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
That

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1468"/>
head

              <ptr target="#l10936" type="alt" xml:id="te1468"/>
of curly knots,

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">
Nor

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2485"/>
stomach troubles laid him low,

              <app from="pr2485" n="139.27 (427½.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4226">
                <lem wit="A">stomach troubles laid him low,</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">bowel trouble laid full low</rdg>
              </app>
            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">Young Stephen Dowling Bots.</l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">
O

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2486"/>
no.

              <app from="pr2486" n="139.29 (427½.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4227">
                <lem wit="A">no.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">no!</rdg>
              </app>
Then list with tearful eye,

            </l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">Whilst I his fate do tell.</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">His soul did from this cold world fly,</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
By

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1469"/>
falling

              <ptr target="#l10938" type="alt" xml:id="te1469"/>
down a well.

            </l>
            <lb/>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">They got him out and emptied him;</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">Alas it was too late;</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:8">His spirit was gone for to sport aloft</l>
            <l rend="text-indent:9">
In the realms of the good and

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2487"/>
great.

              <lb/>
              <app from="pr2487" n="139.36 (427½.12–16)" type="e" xml:id="la4228">
                <lem wit="A">great.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
great.

                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4229">extra line space</note>
Now all young people, come listen unto me:

                  <lb/>
So shape ye your varigated lots,

                  <lb/>
That you can all die, when you come for to die,

                  <lb/>
Like the late sweet Stephen D. Bots.

                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4230">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <app from="pr2480" n="139.9–36 (427.1–427½.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4219">
                <lem wit="MS1a A">This . . . great.</lem>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4220">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </l>
          </lg>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33086">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y14001">
            <graphic url="y14001.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">they got him out and emptied him.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33093">
          <pb n="140" xml:id="pb0140"/>
If

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0073"/>
Emmeline Grangerford

          <ptr target="#as0151" type="an" xml:id="gs0074"/>
could make poetry like that before she was fourteen, there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2488"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2488" n="140.2 (428.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4231">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2489"/>
no

          <app from="pr2489" n="140.2 (428.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4232">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">any</rdg>
          </app>
telling what she could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2490"/>
a

          <app from="pr2490" n="140.2 (428.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4233">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">have</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’</rdg>
          </app>
done

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2491"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr2491" n="140.2 (428.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4234">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
. Buck said she could rattle off poetry like nothing. She didn’t ever have

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2492"/>
to stop

          <app from="pr2492" n="140.4 (428.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4235">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to stop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">and stop</rdg>
          </app>
to think. He said she would slap down a line, and if she couldn’t find anything to rhyme with it she would just scratch it out and slap down another one, and go ahead. She warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2493"/>
particular,

          <app from="pr2493" n="140.6 (428.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4236">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">particular,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">particular;</rdg>
          </app>
she could write about anything you choose to give her to write about, just so it was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2494"/>
sadful

          <app from="pr2494" n="140.8 (428.20)" type="e" xml:id="la4237">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sadful</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sad-like</rdg>
          </app>
. Every time a man died, or a woman died, or a child died, she would be on hand with her “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2495"/>
Tribute

          <app from="pr2495" n="140.9 (429.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4238">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Tribute</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tribute</rdg>
          </app>
” before he was cold. She called them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2496"/>
Tributes

          <app from="pr2496" n="140.10 (429.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4239">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Tributes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tributes</rdg>
          </app>
. The neighbors said it was the doctor first, then Emmeline, then the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2497"/>
undertaker—the undertaker

          <app from="pr2497" n="140.11 (429.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4240">
            <lem wit="MS1a">undertaker—the undertaker</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
undertaker—the under-

              <lb/>
taker

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">undertaker. The undertaker</rdg>
          </app>
never got in ahead of Emmeline but once, and then she hung fire on a rhyme for the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1470"/>
dead person’s name, which was Whistler. She warn’t ever the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2498"/>
same,

          <app from="pr2498" n="140.14 (429.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4241">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">same,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
same

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
after that; she never complained, but she kind of pined away and did not live long. Poor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2499"/>
thing,

          <app from="pr2499" n="140.15 (429.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4242">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">thing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">thing!</rdg>
          </app>
many’s the time I made

          <pb n="141" xml:id="pb0141"/>
myself go up to the little room that used to be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2500"/>
hers

          <app from="pr2500" n="141.1 (429.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4243">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">hers</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hers,</rdg>
          </app>
and get out her poor old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2501"/>
scrap book

          <app from="pr2501" n="141.2 (430.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4244">
            <lem wit="MS1a">scrap book</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
scrap-

              <lb/>
book

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">scrap-book</rdg>
          </app>
and read in it when her pictures had been aggravating me and I had soured on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2502"/>
her

          <app from="pr2502" n="141.3 (430.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4245">
            <lem wit="A Cent">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">her memory</rdg>
          </app>
a little. I liked all

          <ptr target="#l10940" type="alt" xml:id="te1470"/>
that family, dead ones and all, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2503"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2503" n="141.4 (430.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4246">
            <lem wit="A Cent">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">I warn’t</rdg>
          </app>
going to let anything come between us. Poor Emmeline made poetry about all the dead people when she was alive, and it didn’t seem right that there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2504"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr2504" n="141.6 (430.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4247">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
to make some about her, now she was gone; so I tried to sweat out a verse or two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2505"/>
myself

          <app from="pr2505" n="141.8 (430.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4248">
            <lem wit="MS1a">myself</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">myself,</rdg>
          </app>
but I couldn’t seem to make it go, somehow.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0075"/>
They kept Emmeline’s room trim and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2506"/>
nice,

          <app from="pr2506" n="141.9 (430.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4249">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">nice,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
nice

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and all the things fixed in it just the way she liked

          <ptr target="#as0152" type="an" xml:id="gs0076"/>
to have them when she was alive, and nobody ever slept there. The old lady took care of the room herself, though there was plenty of niggers, and she sewed there a good deal and read her Bible there, mostly.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33278">
Well, as I was saying about the parlor, there was beautiful curtains on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2507"/>
windows,

          <app from="pr2507" n="141.15 (431.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4250">
            <lem wit="MS1a">windows,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">windows:</rdg>
          </app>
white, with pictures painted on them, of castles with vines all down the walls, and cattle coming down to drink. There was a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0077"/>
little old piano, too, that had tin pans in it

          <ptr target="#as0153" type="an" xml:id="gs0078"/>
, I reckon, and nothing was ever so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2508"/>
lovely

          <app from="pr2508" n="141.18 (431.21)" type="e" xml:id="la4251">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lovely</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">sweet</rdg>
          </app>
as to hear the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0026"/>
young ladies

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2509"/>
sing

          <app from="pr2509" n="141.18 (432.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4252">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">sing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sing,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0079"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2510"/>
“The Last Link is Broken”

          <app from="pr2510" n="141.18–19 (432.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4253">
            <lem wit="A">“The . . . Broken”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <add>The . . . Broken</add>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">“The . . . Broken,”</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0154" type="an" xml:id="gs0080"/>
and play

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0081"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2511"/>
“The Battle of Prague”

          <app from="pr2511" n="141.19 (432.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4254">
            <lem wit="A Cent">“The . . . Prague”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <add>The . . . Prague</add>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0155" type="an" xml:id="gs0082"/>
on it.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0083"/>
The walls of all the rooms was plastered

          <ptr target="#as0156" type="an" xml:id="gs0084"/>
, and most had carpets on the floors, and the whole

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2512"/>
house

          <app from="pr2512" n="141.22 (432.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4255">
            <lem wit="MS1a">house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">house,</rdg>
          </app>
was whitewashed on the outside.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33348">
It was a double house and the big open place betwixt them was roofed and floored, and sometimes the table was set there in the middle of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2513"/>
day

          <app from="pr2513" n="141.24 (432.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4256">
            <lem wit="MS1a">day</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">day,</rdg>
          </app>
and it was a cool, comfortable place. Nothing couldn’t be better. And warn’t the cooking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2514"/>
good

          <app from="pr2514" n="141.25 (432.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4257">
            <lem wit="MS1a">good</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">good,</rdg>
          </app>
and just bushels of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2515"/>
it,

          <app from="pr2515" n="141.26 (432.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4258">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2516"/>
too!

          <app from="pr2516" n="141.26 (432.19)" type="e" xml:id="la4259">
            <lem wit="A Cent">too!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">too?</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#mt0026" type="alt" xml:id="wn0026"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33382">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y14101">
            <graphic url="y14101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">the house</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0334">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XVIII.</head>
        <pb n="142" xml:id="pb0142"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33392">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y14201">
            <graphic url="y14201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2517"/>
Chapter XVIII.

              <app from="pr2517" n="142 title (433 title)" type="e" xml:id="la4260">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XVIII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">CHAP.</rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4261">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0085"/>
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2518"/>
Col.

              <app from="pr2518" n="142.1 (433.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4262">
                <lem wit="MS1a Ab">Col.</lem>
                <rdg wit="Pfs1 Can">Col</rdg>
                <rdg wit="Aa">Co</rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">Colonel</rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1421">
            <graphic url="hf1421.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2532"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">col.</hi>
              <app from="pr2532" n="142 caption" type="e" xml:id="la4277">
                <lem wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">col</hi>
.

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1a">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4278">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">colonel</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">grangerford.</hi>
            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e33436">
Grangerford was a gentleman, you see. He was a gentleman all over; and so was his family. He was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2519"/>
well born

          <app from="pr2519" n="142.4 (433.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4263">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">well born</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">well-born</rdg>
          </app>
, as the saying is, and that’s worth as much in a man as it is in a horse, so the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2520"/>
widow

          <app from="pr2520" n="142.7 (433.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4264">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">widow</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Widow</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2521"/>
Douglas

          <app from="pr2521" n="142.7 (433.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4265">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Douglas</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Douglass</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2522"/>
said

          <app from="pr2522" n="142.7 (433.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4266">
            <lem wit="A Cent">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">always said</rdg>
          </app>
, and nobody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2523"/>
ever

          <app from="pr2523" n="142.8 (433.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4267">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">never</rdg>
          </app>
denied that she was of the first aristocracy in our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2524"/>
town

          <app from="pr2524" n="142.10 (433.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4268">
            <lem wit="A Cent">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">village</rdg>
          </app>
; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2525"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1471"/>
pap

          <ptr target="#l10942" type="alt" xml:id="te1471"/>
          <app from="pr2525" n="142.10 (433.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4269">
            <lem wit="A Cent">pap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Pap</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2526"/>
he

          <app from="pr2526" n="142.10 (433.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4270">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4271">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
always said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2527"/>
it

          <app from="pr2527" n="142.11 (434.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4272">
            <lem wit="MS1a">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">it,</rdg>
          </app>
too, though he warn’t no more quality than a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2528"/>
mud-cat

          <app from="pr2528" n="142.12 (434.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4273">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">mud-cat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
mud-

              <lb/>
cat

            </rdg>
          </app>
, himself.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2529"/>
Col.

          <app from="pr2529" n="142.13 (434.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4274">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Col.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Colonel</rdg>
          </app>
Grangerford was very tall and very slim, and had a darkish-paly complexion, not a sign of red in it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1472"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2530"/>
anywheres

          <app from="pr2530" n="142.16–17 (434.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4275">
            <lem wit="A Cent">anywheres</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anywhere</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <ptr target="#l10944" type="alt" xml:id="te1472"/>
he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2531"/>
clean-shaved

          <app from="pr2531" n="142.17 (434.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4276">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">clean-shaved</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
clean-

              <lb/>
shaved

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1473"/>
every

          <ptr target="#l10946" type="alt" xml:id="te1473"/>
morning, all over his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1474"/>
thin

          <ptr target="#l10948" type="alt" xml:id="te1474"/>
face, and he had the thinnest kind of lips, and the thinnest kind of nostrils, and a high nose, and heavy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2533"/>
eyebrows

          <app from="pr2533" n="142.20 (434.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la4279">
            <lem wit="A Cent">eyebrows</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
eye-

              <lb/>
brows

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and the blackest kind of eyes, sunk so deep back that they seemed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2534"/>
like they was

          <app from="pr2534" n="142.21 (434.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4280">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like they was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">to be</rdg>
          </app>
looking out of caverns at you, as you may say. His forehead was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2535"/>
high

          <app from="pr2535" n="142.22 (434.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4281">
            <lem wit="MS1a">high</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">high,</rdg>
          </app>
and his hair

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2536"/>
was black

          <app from="pr2536" n="142.22 (434.20)" type="e" xml:id="la4282">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was black</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">black</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2537"/>
straight

          <app from="pr2537" n="142.22 (434.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4283">
            <lem wit="MS1a">straight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">straight,</rdg>
          </app>
and hung to his shoulders. His hands was long and thin, and every day of his life he put on a clean shirt and a full suit from head to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2538"/>
foot

          <app from="pr2538" n="142.24 (435.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4284">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">foot</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">foot,</rdg>
          </app>
made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2539"/>
out

          <app from="pr2539" n="142.24 (435.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4285">
            <lem wit="A Cent">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4286">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of linen so white it hurt your eyes to look at it; and on Sundays he wore a blue tail-coat with brass buttons on it. He carried a mahogany cane with a silver head to it. There warn’t no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2540"/>
frivolishness

          <app from="pr2540" n="142.27 (435.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4287">
            <lem wit="A Cent">frivolishness</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">frivolousness</rdg>
          </app>
about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2541"/>
him

          <app from="pr2541" n="142.28 (435.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4288">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">him</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it</rdg>
          </app>
, not a bit, and he warn’t ever loud. He was as kind as he could be—you could feel that, you know, and so you had confidence. Sometimes he smiled, and it was good to see; but when he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2542"/>
straightened

          <app from="pr2542" n="142.30–31 (435.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la4289">
            <lem wit="A Cent">straightened</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">straightend</rdg>
          </app>
himself up like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2543"/>
liberty-pole

          <app from="pr2543" n="142.31 (435.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la4290">
            <lem wit="MS1a">liberty-pole</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">liberty-pole,</rdg>
          </app>
and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0027"/>
lightning begun to flicker

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1475"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l10950" type="alt" xml:id="te1475"/>
from under his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2544"/>
eyebrows,

          <app from="pr2544" n="142.32 (436.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4291">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">eyebrows,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
eyebrows

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you wanted to climb a tree

          <pb n="143" xml:id="pb0143"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2545"/>
first,

          <app from="pr2545" n="143.1 (436.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4292">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">first,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
first

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and find out what the matter was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2546"/>
afterwards

          <app from="pr2546" n="143.1 (436.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4293">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">afterwards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">afterward</rdg>
          </app>
. He didn’t ever have to tell anybody to mind their manners—everybody was always

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2547"/>
good mannered

          <app from="pr2547" n="143.3 (436.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4294">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">good mannered</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">good-mannered</rdg>
          </app>
where he was.

          <ptr target="#as0157" type="an" xml:id="gs0086"/>
Everybody loved to have him around, too; he was sunshine most always—I mean he made it seem like good weather. When he turned into a cloud-bank it was awful dark for a half a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2548"/>
minute,

          <app from="pr2548" n="143.6 (436.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4295">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">minute,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
minute

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and that was enough; there wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2549"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr2549" n="143.7 (436.20)" type="e" xml:id="la4296">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
go wrong again for a week.

          <ptr target="#mt0027" type="alt" xml:id="wn0027"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33717">
When him and the old lady come down in the morning, all the family got up out of their chairs and give them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2550"/>
good day

          <app from="pr2550" n="143.9 (437.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4297">
            <lem wit="MS1a">good day</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">good-day,</rdg>
          </app>
and didn’t set down again till they had set down. Then Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2551"/>
and

          <app from="pr2551" n="143.10 (437.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4298">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">or</rdg>
          </app>
Bob went to the sideboard where the decanters was, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0087"/>
mixed a glass of bitters and handed it to him, and he held it in his hand and waited till Tom’s and Bob’s was mixed, and then they bowed and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2552"/>
said

          <app from="pr2552" n="143.13 (437.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4299">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">said,</rdg>
          </app>
“Our duty to you, sir, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2553"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0057"/>
madam;”

          <app from="pr2553" n="✱143.14 (437.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4300">
            <lem wit="A">madam;”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">madam,”</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">madam”;</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2554"/>
          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
          <app from="pr2554" n="✱143.14 (437.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4301">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">they</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0057" type="te" xml:id="tv0057"/>
bowed the least bit in the world and said thank you, and so they drank, all three, and Bob and Tom poured a spoonful of water on the sugar and the mite of whisky or apple brandy

          <ptr target="#as0158" type="an" xml:id="gs0088"/>
in the bottom of their tumblers, and give it to me and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2555"/>
Buck

          <app from="pr2555" n="143.17 (438.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4302">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Buck</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Buck,</rdg>
          </app>
and we drank to the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2556"/>
people

          <app from="pr2556" n="143.18 (438.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4303">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">people</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">people,</rdg>
          </app>
too.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33788">
Bob was the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2557"/>
oldest

          <app from="pr2557" n="143.19 (438.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4304">
            <lem wit="MS1a">oldest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">oldest,</rdg>
          </app>
and Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2558"/>
next. Tall

          <app from="pr2558" n="143.19 (438.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4305">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">next. Tall</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">next—tall</rdg>
          </app>
, beautiful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2559"/>
men

          <app from="pr2559" n="143.19 (438.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4306">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">men</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">men,</rdg>
          </app>
with very broad

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2560"/>
shoulders,

          <app from="pr2560" n="143.20 (438.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4307">
            <lem wit="MS1a">shoulders,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
shoulders

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and brown

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2561"/>
faces

          <app from="pr2561" n="143.20 (438.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4308">
            <lem wit="MS1a">faces</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">faces,</rdg>
          </app>
and long black hair and black eyes. They dressed in white linen from head to foot, like the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2562"/>
gentleman

          <app from="pr2562" n="143.21–22 (438.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4309">
            <lem wit="A Cent">gentleman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
gentle-

              <lb/>
man

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and wore broad Panama hats.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33842">
Then there was Miss

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2563"/>
Charlotte,

          <app from="pr2563" n="143.23 (438.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la4310">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Charlotte,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Charlotte;</rdg>
          </app>
she was twenty-five, and tall and proud and grand, but as good as she could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2564"/>
be,

          <app from="pr2564" n="143.24 (438.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la4311">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">be,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
be

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
when she warn’t stirred

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0028"/>
up; but when she was, she had a look that would make you wilt in your tracks, like her father. She was beautiful.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33862">
So was her sister, Miss Sophia, but it was a different kind. She was gentle and sweet, like a dove, and she was only

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2565"/>
twenty.

          <app from="pr2565" n="143.28 (439.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4312">
            <lem wit="MS1a Cent">twenty.</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
twenty

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33871">Each person had their own nigger to wait on them—Buck, too. My nigger had a monstrous easy time, because I warn’t used to having anybody do anything for me, but Buck’s was on the jump most of the time.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33873">
This

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2566"/>
was all

          <app from="pr2566" n="143.33 (439.21)" type="hc" xml:id="la4313">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">was all</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">is all</rdg>
          </app>
there was of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2567"/>
family,

          <app from="pr2567" n="143.33 (439.22)" type="hc" xml:id="la4314">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">family,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
family

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now;

          <ptr target="#mt0028" type="alt" xml:id="wn0028"/>
but there used to be more—three

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2568"/>
sons—

          <app from="pr2568" n="143.34 (440.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4315">
            <lem wit="MS1a">sons—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">sons;</rdg>
          </app>
they got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1476"/>
killed

          <ptr target="#l10952" type="alt" xml:id="te1476"/>
; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2569"/>
Emmeline,

          <app from="pr2569" n="143.34 (440.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4316">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Emmeline,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
Emmeline

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that died.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33914">
The old gentleman owned a lot of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2570"/>
farms

          <app from="pr2570" n="143.35 (440.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4317">
            <lem wit="MS1a">farms</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">farms,</rdg>
          </app>
and over a hundred niggers. Sometimes a stack of people would come there, horseback, from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2571"/>
ten or

          <app from="pr2571" n="143.37 (440.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4318">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ten or</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">ten and</rdg>
          </app>
fifteen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2572"/>
mile

          <app from="pr2572" n="143.37 (440.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4319">
            <lem wit="A">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a Cent">miles</rdg>
          </app>
around, and stay five or six days, and have such junketings

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1477"/>
round

          <ptr target="#l10954" type="alt" xml:id="te1477"/>
about and on the river, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1478"/>
dances and

          <ptr target="#l10956" type="alt" xml:id="te1478"/>
          <pb n="144" xml:id="pb0144"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2573"/>
picnics

          <app from="pr2573" n="144.1 (440.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la4320">
            <lem wit="A Cent">picnics</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
pic-

              <lb/>
nics

            </rdg>
          </app>
in the woods,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2574"/>
daytimes

          <app from="pr2574" n="144.1 (440.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la4321">
            <lem wit="C">daytimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
day-

              <lb/>
times

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">day-times</rdg>
          </app>
, and balls at the house, nights. These people was mostly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2575"/>
kin-folks

          <app from="pr2575" n="144.2 (440.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la4322">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kin-folks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
kin-

              <lb/>
folks

            </rdg>
          </app>
of the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1479"/>
family.

          <ptr target="#l10958" type="alt" xml:id="te1479"/>
The men brought their guns with them. It was a handsome lot of quality, I tell you.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e33988">
There was another clan of aristocracy around there—five or six families—mostly of the name of Shepherdson. They was as high-toned, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2576"/>
well born

          <app from="pr2576" n="144.6 (441.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4323">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">well born</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">well-born</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2577"/>
rich

          <app from="pr2577" n="144.6 (441.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4324">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">rich</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">rich,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2578"/>
grand

          <app from="pr2578" n="144.6 (441.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4325">
            <lem wit="MS1a">grand</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">grand,</rdg>
          </app>
as the tribe of Grangerfords. The Shepherdsons and the Grangerfords used the same

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2580"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr2580" n="144.8 (441.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4328">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">steam-boat</rdg>
          </app>
landing, which was about two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2581"/>
mile

          <app from="pr2581" n="144.8 (441.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4329">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">miles</rdg>
          </app>
above our house; so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2582"/>
sometimes

          <app from="pr2582" n="144.9 (441.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4330">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">sometimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sometimes,</rdg>
          </app>
when I went up there with a lot of our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2583"/>
folks

          <app from="pr2583" n="144.9 (441.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4331">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">folks</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">folks,</rdg>
          </app>
I used to see a lot of the Shepherdsons there, on their fine horses.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y14401">
          <graphic url="y14401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2579"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">young harney shepherdson</hi>
.

            <app from="pr2579" n="144 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la4326">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">young harney shepherdson</hi>
.

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1a">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4327">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">harney shepherdson</hi>
.

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34066">
One day Buck and me was away

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2584"/>
out

          <app from="pr2584" n="144.11 (442.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4332">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4333">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2585"/>
woods

          <app from="pr2585" n="144.11 (442.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4334">
            <lem wit="MS1a">woods</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">woods,</rdg>
          </app>
hunting, and heard a horse coming.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1480"/>
We

          <ptr target="#l10960" type="alt" xml:id="te1480"/>
was crossing the road. Buck says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34090">“Quick! Jump for the woods!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34092">
We done it, and then peeped down the woods through the leaves. Pretty soon a splendid young man come galloping down the road, setting his horse easy and looking like a soldier. He had his gun across his pommel. I had seen him before. It was young

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1481"/>
Harney

          <ptr target="#l10962" type="alt" xml:id="te1481"/>
          <pb n="145" xml:id="pb0145"/>
Shepherdson. I heard Buck’s gun go off at my ear, and Harney’s hat tumbled off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2586"/>
from

          <app from="pr2586" n="145.2 (443.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4335">
            <lem wit="A Cent">from</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">of</rdg>
          </app>
his head. He grabbed his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2587"/>
gun

          <app from="pr2587" n="145.2 (443.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4336">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">gun</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gun,</rdg>
          </app>
and rode straight

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2588"/>
to

          <app from="pr2588" n="145.2 (443.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4337">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">at</rdg>
          </app>
the place where we was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2589"/>
hid. But

          <app from="pr2589" n="145.3 (443.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4338">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hid. But</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
hid.—

              <lb/>
But

            </rdg>
          </app>
we didn’t wait. We started through the woods on a run. The woods warn’t thick, so I looked over my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2590"/>
shoulder,

          <app from="pr2590" n="145.5 (443.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4339">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">shoulder,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
shoulder

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to dodge the bullet, and twice I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2591"/>
seen

          <app from="pr2591" n="145.5 (443.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4340">
            <lem wit="A Cent">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">saw</rdg>
          </app>
Harney cover Buck with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2592"/>
gun,

          <app from="pr2592" n="145.6 (443.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la4341">
            <lem wit="MS1a">gun,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">gun;</rdg>
          </app>
and then he rode away the way he come—to get his hat, I reckon, but I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2593"/>
see. We

          <app from="pr2593" n="145.7 (443.20–21)" type="e" xml:id="la4342">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see. We</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
see.—

              <lb/>
We

            </rdg>
          </app>
never stopped running till we got home. The old gentleman’s eyes blazed a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2594"/>
minute—

          <app from="pr2594" n="145.8 (444.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4343">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">minute—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">minute,—</rdg>
          </app>
’twas pleasure,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1482"/>
mainly

          <ptr target="#l10964" type="alt" xml:id="te1482"/>
, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2595"/>
judged—

          <app from="pr2595" n="145.9 (444.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4344">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">judged—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">judged,—</rdg>
          </app>
then his face sort of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2596"/>
smoothed

          <app from="pr2596" n="145.9 (444.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4345">
            <lem wit="A Cent">smoothed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">soothed</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2597"/>
down

          <app from="pr2597" n="145.9 (444.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4346">
            <lem wit="MS1a">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">down,</rdg>
          </app>
and he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2598"/>
says

          <app from="pr2598" n="145.10 (444.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4347">
            <lem wit="MS1a">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">says,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2599"/>
kind of gentle

          <app from="pr2599" n="145.10 (444.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4348">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kind of gentle</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">gently</rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34222">“I don’t like that shooting from behind a bush. Why didn’t you step into the road, my boy?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34224">
“The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2600"/>
Shepherdsons

          <app from="pr2600" n="145.13 (444.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4349">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Shepherdsons</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">Shepherdson’s</rdg>
          </app>
don’t, father. They always take

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1483"/>
advantage

          <ptr target="#l10966" type="alt" xml:id="te1483"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34238">
Miss Charlotte

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2601"/>
she

          <app from="pr2601" n="145.14 (444.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4350">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4351">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
held her head up like a queen while Buck was telling his tale, and her nostrils spread and her eyes snapped. The two young men looked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2602"/>
dark

          <app from="pr2602" n="145.16 (445.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4352">
            <lem wit="MS1a">dark</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">dark,</rdg>
          </app>
but never said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2603"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr2603" n="145.16 (445.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4353">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
. Miss Sophia

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2604"/>
she turned

          <app from="pr2604" n="145.17 (445.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4354">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she turned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">turned</rdg>
          </app>
pale, but the color come back when she found the man warn’t hurt.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34274">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y14501">
            <graphic url="y14501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">miss charlotte</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34280">
          <pb n="146" xml:id="pb00146"/>
Soon as I could

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1484"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l10968" type="alt" xml:id="te1484"/>
Buck down by the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2605"/>
corn-cribs

          <app from="pr2605" n="146.1 (445.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4355">
            <lem wit="A Cent">corn-cribs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
corn-

              <lb/>
cribs

            </rdg>
          </app>
under the trees by ourselves, I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34297">“Did you want to kill him, Buck?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34300">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2606"/>
Well

          <app from="pr2606" n="146.4 (445.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4356">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
I bet I did.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34310">
“What did he do

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1485"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l10970" type="alt" xml:id="te1485"/>
you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34316">
“Him? He never done

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2607"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr2607" n="146.6 (445.17)" type="e" xml:id="la4357">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">anything</rdg>
          </app>
to me.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34326">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2608"/>
Well

          <app from="pr2608" n="146.7 (445.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la4358">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
then, what did you want to kill him for?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34336">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2609"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2609" n="146.8 (445.20)" type="hc" xml:id="la4359">
            <lem wit="MS1a A">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
nothing—only it’s on account of the feud.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34346">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0029"/>
“What’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2610"/>
a

          <app from="pr2610" n="146.9 (446.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4360">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">the</rdg>
          </app>
feud?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34357">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2611"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2611" n="146.10 (446.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4361">
            <lem wit="MS1a">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
where was you raised? Don’t you know what a feud is?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34367">
“Never heard of it before—tell me about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2612"/>
it.”

          <ptr target="#mt0029" type="alt" xml:id="wn0029"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34372">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0030"/>
“Well

          <app from="pr2612" n="146.11–12 (446.6–447.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4362">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it.” [¶] “Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a–MS1b">
it.”

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] “Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
,” says Buck, “

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0089"/>
a feud is this way. A man has a quarrel with another man, and kills him; then that other man’s brother kills

          <hi rend="italic">him;</hi>
then the other brothers, on both sides, goes for one another; then the

          <hi rend="italic">cousins</hi>
chip in—and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2613"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr2613" n="146.15 (447.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4363">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
everybody’s killed off, and there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2614"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2614" n="146.16 (447.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4364">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
no more

          <ptr target="#mt0030" type="alt" xml:id="wn0030"/>
feud. But it’s kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2615"/>
slow

          <app from="pr2615" n="146.16 (448.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4365">
            <lem wit="MS1b">slow</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">slow,</rdg>
          </app>
and takes a long time

          <ptr target="#as0159" type="an" xml:id="gs0090"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34421">
“Has this one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2616"/>
been

          <app from="pr2616" n="146.18 (448.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4366">
            <lem wit="A Cent">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">ben</rdg>
          </app>
going on long, Buck?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34431">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2617"/>
Well

          <app from="pr2617" n="146.19 (448.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4367">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
I should

          <hi rend="italic">reckon!</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2618"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1486"/>
It

          <ptr target="#l10972" type="alt" xml:id="te1486"/>
          <app from="pr2618" n="146.19 (448.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4368">
            <lem wit="MS1b">It</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">it</rdg>
          </app>
started thirty year ago,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1487"/>
or

          <ptr target="#l10974" type="alt" xml:id="te1487"/>
som’ers along there. There was trouble ’bout

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2619"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1488"/>
something

          <ptr target="#l10976" type="alt" xml:id="te1488"/>
,

          <app from="pr2619" n="146.20 (448.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4369">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">something,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
something

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and then a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2620"/>
lawsuit

          <app from="pr2620" n="146.20 (448.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la4370">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lawsuit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
law-

              <lb/>
suit

            </rdg>
          </app>
to settle it; and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1489"/>
suit

          <ptr target="#l10978" type="alt" xml:id="te1489"/>
went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2621"/>
agin

          <app from="pr2621" n="146.21 (448.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4371">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ag’in’</rdg>
          </app>
one of the men, and so he up and shot the man that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2622"/>
won

          <app from="pr2622" n="146.22 (448.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4372">
            <lem wit="A Cent">won</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">win</rdg>
          </app>
the suit—which he would naturally do, of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1490"/>
course.

          <ptr target="#l10980" type="alt" xml:id="te1490"/>
Anybody would.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34506">“What was the trouble about, Buck?—land?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34508">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2623"/>
reckon maybe

          <app from="pr2623" n="146.25 (449.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4373">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">reckon maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">reckon, may be</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2624"/>
—I

          <app from="pr2624" n="146.25 (449.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4374">
            <lem wit="A Cent">—I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
—

              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
don’t know.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34527">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2625"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1491"/>
Well

          <ptr target="#l10982" type="alt" xml:id="te1491"/>
          <app from="pr2625" n="146.26 (449.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4375">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
who done the shooting?—was it a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2626"/>
Grangerford,

          <app from="pr2626" n="146.26 (449.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4376">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Grangerford,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
Grangerford

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
or a Shepherdson?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34547">
“Laws, how do

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2627"/>
It

          <app from="pr2627" n="146.28 (449.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4377">
            <lem wit="MS1b">It</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">it</rdg>
          </app>
was so long ago.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34560">“Don’t anybody know?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34562">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2628"/>
O

          <app from="pr2628" n="146.30 (449.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4378">
            <lem wit="MS1b">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes, pa knows, I reckon, and some of the other old folks; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2629"/>
they

          <app from="pr2629" n="146.31 (449.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4379">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
don’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2630"/>
know,

          <app from="pr2630" n="146.31 (450.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4380">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">know,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
know

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2631"/>
now,

          <app from="pr2631" n="146.31 (450.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4381">
            <lem wit="A">now,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">now</rdg>
          </app>
what the row was about in the first place.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34601">
“Has there been many

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1492"/>
killed,

          <ptr target="#l10984" type="alt" xml:id="te1492"/>
Buck?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34607">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1493"/>
Yes—right

          <ptr target="#l10986" type="alt" xml:id="te1493"/>
smart chance of funerals. But they don’t always kill. Pa’s got a few buck-shot in him; but he don’t mind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2632"/>
it,

          <app from="pr2632" n="146.34 (450.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4382">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
’cuz he don’t weigh

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2633"/>
much

          <app from="pr2633" n="146.35 (450.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4383">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">much</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">much,</rdg>
          </app>
anyway. Bob’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2634"/>
been

          <app from="pr2634" n="146.35 (450.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4384">
            <lem wit="A Cent">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">ben</rdg>
          </app>
carved up some with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2635"/>
Bowie

          <app from="pr2635" n="146.35 (450.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4385">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Bowie</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">bowie</rdg>
          </app>
, and Tom’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2636"/>
been

          <app from="pr2636" n="146.36 (450.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4386">
            <lem wit="A Cent">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">ben</rdg>
          </app>
hurt once or twice.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34655">
“Has anybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2637"/>
been

          <app from="pr2637" n="146.37 (451.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4387">
            <lem wit="A Cent">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">ben</rdg>
          </app>
killed this year, Buck?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34665">
“Yes,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1494"/>
we

          <ptr target="#l10988" type="alt" xml:id="te1494"/>
got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2638"/>
one,

          <app from="pr2638" n="146.38 (451.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4388">
            <lem wit="MS1b">one,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
one

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1495"/>
they

          <ptr target="#l10990" type="alt" xml:id="te1495"/>
got one. ’Bout three months ago, my

          <pb n="147" xml:id="pb0147"/>
cousin Bud, fourteen year old, was riding through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2639"/>
woods,

          <app from="pr2639" n="147.1 (451.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4389">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">woods,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
woods

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
on t’other side of the river, and didn’t have no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2640"/>
weapon

          <app from="pr2640" n="147.2 (451.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4390">
            <lem wit="A Cent">weapon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">weepon</rdg>
          </app>
with him, which was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2641"/>
blame’

          <app from="pr2641" n="147.3 (451.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4391">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blame’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">blame</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2642"/>
foolishness,

          <app from="pr2642" n="147.3 (451.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4392">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">foolishness,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">foolishness;</rdg>
          </app>
and in a lonesome place he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1496"/>
hears

          <ptr target="#l10992" type="alt" xml:id="te1496"/>
a horse

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2643"/>
a-coming,

          <app from="pr2643" n="147.3–4 (451.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4393">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a-coming,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">a-coming</rdg>
          </app>
behind him,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1497"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l10994" type="alt" xml:id="te1497"/>
sees old Baldy Shepherdson a-linkin’ after him with his gun in his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2644"/>
hand

          <app from="pr2644" n="147.5 (452.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4394">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">hand</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hand,</rdg>
          </app>
and his white hair a-flying in the wind; and ’stead of jumping off and taking to the brush, Bud ’lowed he could outrun him; so they had it, nip and tuck, for five mile or more, the old man a-gaining all the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2645"/>
time; so

          <app from="pr2645" n="147.8 (452.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4395">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">time; so</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">time. So</rdg>
          </app>
at last Bud seen it warn’t any use, so he stopped and faced

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2646"/>
around,

          <app from="pr2646" n="147.9 (452.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4396">
            <lem wit="MS1b">around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
around

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
so as to have the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2647"/>
bullet holes

          <app from="pr2647" n="147.9 (452.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4397">
            <lem wit="A">bullet holes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">bullet hole</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">bullet-holes</rdg>
          </app>
in front, you know, and the old man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2648"/>
he

          <app from="pr2648" n="147.10 (453.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4398">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1a">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4399">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
rode up and shot him down. But he didn’t git much chance to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2649"/>
enjoy

          <app from="pr2649" n="147.11 (453.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4400">
            <lem wit="A Cent">enjoy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">injoy</rdg>
          </app>
his luck, for inside of a week our folks laid

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
out.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34791">“I reckon that old man was a coward, Buck.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34794">
“I reckon he

          <hi rend="italic">warn’t</hi>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2650"/>
coward. Not

          <app from="pr2650" n="147.14 (453.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4401">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">coward. Not</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">coward—not</rdg>
          </app>
by a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2651"/>
blame’

          <app from="pr2651" n="147.14 (453.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4402">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blame’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">blame</rdg>
          </app>
sight. There

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2652"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2652" n="147.14 (453.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4403">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
a coward amongst them Shepherdsons—not a one. And there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2653"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2653" n="147.15 (454.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4404">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
no cowards amongst the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1498"/>
Grangerfords

          <ptr target="#l10996" type="alt" xml:id="te1498"/>
, either.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2654"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2654" n="147.16 (454.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4405">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
that old man kep’ up his end in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2655"/>
fight,

          <app from="pr2655" n="147.17 (454.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4406">
            <lem wit="MS1b">fight,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
fight

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
one day, for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2656"/>
a half

          <app from="pr2656" n="147.17 (454.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4407">
            <lem wit="A">a half</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">half</rdg>
          </app>
an hour,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2657"/>
against

          <app from="pr2657" n="147.17 (454.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4408">
            <lem wit="A Cent">against</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">agin</rdg>
          </app>
three Grangerfords, and come out winner.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1499"/>
They

          <ptr target="#l10998" type="alt" xml:id="te1499"/>
was all a-horseback; he lit

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2658"/>
off of

          <app from="pr2658" n="147.19 (454.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4409">
            <lem wit="A">off of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">off’n</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">off</rdg>
          </app>
his horse and got behind a little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2659"/>
woodpile

          <app from="pr2659" n="147.19 (454.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4410">
            <lem wit="MS1b">woodpile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wood-pile</rdg>
          </app>
, and kep’ his horse before him to stop the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1500"/>
bullets;

          <ptr target="#l11000" type="alt" xml:id="te1500"/>
but the Grangerfords staid on their horses and capered around the old man, and peppered away at him, and he peppered away at them. Him and his horse both went home pretty leaky and crippled, but the Grangerfords had to be

          <hi rend="italic">fetched</hi>
home—and one of ’em was dead, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2660"/>
another died the

          <app from="pr2660" n="147.24 (455.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la4411">
            <lem wit="A Cent">another died the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">another one died</rdg>
          </app>
next day. No,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2661"/>
sir,

          <app from="pr2661" n="147.25 (455.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4412">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">sir,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sir;</rdg>
          </app>
if a body’s out hunting for cowards, he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1501"/>
don’t

          <ptr target="#l11002" type="alt" xml:id="te1501"/>
want to fool away any time amongst them Shepherdsons, becuz they don’t breed any of that

          <hi rend="italic">kind.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34924">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0091"/>
Next Sunday we all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1502"/>
went

          <ptr target="#l11004" type="alt" xml:id="te1502"/>
to church, about three mile, everybody a-horseback. The men took their guns along, so did Buck, and kept them between their knees or stood them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1503"/>
handy

          <ptr target="#l11006" type="alt" xml:id="te1503"/>
against the wall. The Shepherdsons done the same.

          <ptr target="#as0160" type="an" xml:id="gs0092"/>
It was pretty ornery

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2662"/>
preaching

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1504"/>
—

          <app from="pr2662" n="147.31 (456.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la4413">
            <lem wit="A Cent">preaching—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">preaching,—</rdg>
          </app>
all

          <ptr target="#l11008" type="alt" xml:id="te1504"/>
about brotherly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2663"/>
love

          <app from="pr2663" n="147.32 (456.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4414">
            <lem wit="MS1b">love</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">love,</rdg>
          </app>
and such-like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2664"/>
tiresomeness,

          <app from="pr2664" n="147.32 (457.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4415">
            <lem wit="MS1b">tiresomeness,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tiresomeness;</rdg>
          </app>
but everybody said it was a good sermon, and they all talked it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2665"/>
over,

          <app from="pr2665" n="147.33 (457.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4416">
            <lem wit="MS1b">over,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
over

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
going home, and had such a powerful lot to say about faith, and good works, and free grace, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0093"/>
preforeordestination

          <ptr target="#as0161" type="an" xml:id="gs0094"/>
, and I don’t know what all, that it did seem to me to be one of the roughest Sundays I had run

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2666"/>
across

          <app from="pr2666" n="147.36 (457.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4417">
            <lem wit="A Cent">across</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">acrost</rdg>
          </app>
yet.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y14801">
          <graphic url="y14801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">and asked me if i liked her.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e34994">
About an hour after dinner everybody was dozing around, some

          <pb n="148" xml:id="pb0148"/>
in their chairs and some in their rooms, and it got to be pretty dull. Buck and a dog was stretched out on the grass in the sun, sound asleep. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1505"/>
went

          <ptr target="#l11010" type="alt" xml:id="te1505"/>
up to our room, and judged I would take a nap myself. I found that sweet Miss Sophia standing in her door, which was next to ours, and she took me in her room and shut the door very soft, and asked me if I liked her, and I said I did; and she asked me if I would do something for her and not tell anybody, and I said I would. Then she said she’d forgot her Testament, and left

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1506"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l11012" type="alt" xml:id="te1506"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2667"/>
in the seat at

          <app from="pr2667" n="148.8 (459.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4418">
            <lem wit="A Cent">in the seat at</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">on the seat in</rdg>
          </app>
church, between two other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2668"/>
books,

          <app from="pr2668" n="148.9 (459.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4419">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">books,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
books

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and would I slip out quiet and go there and fetch it to her, and not say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2669"/>
nothing to nobody.

          <app from="pr2669" n="148.10 (459.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la4420">
            <lem wit="A">nothing to nobody.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anything to anybody.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">nothing to nobody?</rdg>
          </app>
I said I would. So I slid out and slipped off up the road, and there warn’t anybody at the church, except

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2670"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr2670" n="148.12 (460.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4421">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
a hog or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2671"/>
two,

          <app from="pr2671" n="148.12 (460.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4422">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">two,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">two;</rdg>
          </app>
for there warn’t any lock on the door, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0095"/>
hogs likes a puncheon floor

          <ptr target="#as0162" type="an" xml:id="gs0096"/>
in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2672"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1507"/>
summer

          <ptr target="#l11014" type="alt" xml:id="te1507"/>
time

          <app from="pr2672" n="148.13–14 (460.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4423">
            <lem wit="MS1b">summer time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">summer-time</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">summer-time,</rdg>
          </app>
because it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2673"/>
cool. If you notice, most folks don’t go to church only when they’ve got to; but a hog is different

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35069">
Says

          <app from="pr2673" n="148.14–16 (460.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4424">
            <lem wit="A Cent">cool. If . . . different. [¶] Says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
cool.—

              <lb/>
[¶] Says

            </rdg>
          </app>
I to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2674"/>
myself,

          <app from="pr2674" n="148.16 (460.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4425">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">myself,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
myself

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
something’s up—it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2675"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2675" n="148.16 (460.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4426">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
natural for a girl to be in such a sweat about a Testament; so I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2676"/>
give

          <app from="pr2676" n="148.17 (460.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4427">
            <lem wit="A Cent">give</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">gives</rdg>
          </app>
it a shake, and out drops

          <pb n="149" xml:id="pb0149"/>
a little piece of paper with “

          <hi rend="italic">Half-past two</hi>
” wrote on it with a pencil. I ransacked it,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2677"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1508"/>
but

          <ptr target="#l11016" type="alt" xml:id="te1508"/>
          <app from="pr2677" n="149.2 (461.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4428">
            <lem wit="A Cent">but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">but I</rdg>
          </app>
couldn’t find anything else. I couldn’t make anything out of that, so I put the paper in the book again, and when I got home and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2678"/>
up stairs

          <app from="pr2678" n="149.4 (461.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4429">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">up stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">upstairs</rdg>
          </app>
, there was Miss Sophia in her door waiting for me. She pulled me in and shut the door; then she looked in the Testament till she found the paper, and as soon as she read it she looked glad; and before a body could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2679"/>
think,

          <app from="pr2679" n="149.7 (462.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4430">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">think,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
think

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
she grabbed me and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2680"/>
give me a squeeze

          <app from="pr2680" n="149.7–8 (462.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la4431">
            <lem wit="A Cent">give me a squeeze</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">kissed me right on the mouth</rdg>
          </app>
, and said I was the best boy in the world, and not to tell anybody. She was mighty red in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2681"/>
face,

          <app from="pr2681" n="149.9 (462.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4432">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">face,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
face

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for a minute, and her eyes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2682"/>
lighted up,

          <app from="pr2682" n="149.10 (462.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4433">
            <lem wit="Cent">lighted up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">mighty bright,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">lighted up</rdg>
          </app>
and it made her powerful pretty. I was a good deal astonished, but when I got my breath I asked her what the paper was about, and she asked me if I had read it, and I said no, and she asked me if I could read writing, and I told her “no, only coarse-hand,” and then she said the paper

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2683"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2683" n="149.14 (463.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4434">
            <lem wit="A Cent">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
anything but a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2684"/>
book-mark

          <app from="pr2684" n="149.14 (463.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4435">
            <lem wit="A Cent">book-mark</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
book-

              <lb/>
mark

            </rdg>
          </app>
to keep her place, and I might go and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2685"/>
play,

          <app from="pr2685" n="149.15 (463.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4436">
            <lem wit="MS1b">play,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
play

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35190">
I went off down to the river, studying over this thing, and pretty soon I noticed that my nigger was following along behind. When we was out of sight of the house, he looked back and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2686"/>
around,

          <app from="pr2686" n="149.18 (464.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4437">
            <lem wit="MS1b">around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
around

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a second, and then comes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2687"/>
a-running

          <app from="pr2687" n="149.19 (464.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4438">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a-running</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">a-running,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2688"/>
says—

          <app from="pr2688" n="149.19 (464.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4439">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35216">
“Mars

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2689"/>
Jawge

          <app from="pr2689" n="149.20 (464.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4440">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Jawge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">George</rdg>
          </app>
, if you’ll come down into de swamp, I’ll show you a whole stack o’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1509"/>
water-moccasins

          <ptr target="#l11018" type="alt" xml:id="te1509"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35230">
Thinks I,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2690"/>
that’s

          <app from="pr2690" n="149.22 (464.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4441">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">thats</rdg>
          </app>
mighty curious; he said that yesterday.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2691"/>
He oughter know

          <app from="pr2691" n="149.22–23 (464.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4442">
            <lem wit="A Cent">He oughter know</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">He</hi>
knows

            </rdg>
          </app>
a body don’t love

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2692"/>
water-moccasins

          <app from="pr2692" n="149.23 (464.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la4443">
            <lem wit="A Cent">water-moccasins</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
water-

              <lb/>
moccasins

            </rdg>
          </app>
enough to go around hunting for them. What is he up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2693"/>
to,

          <app from="pr2693" n="149.24 (465.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4444">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">to,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
to

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
anyway? So I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2694"/>
says—

          <app from="pr2694" n="149.24 (465.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4445">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35276">
“All

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2695"/>
right—

          <app from="pr2695" n="149.25 (465.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4446">
            <lem wit="MS1b">right—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">right,</rdg>
          </app>
trot ahead.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35286">
I followed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2696"/>
a half

          <app from="pr2696" n="149.26 (465.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4447">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a half</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">him half</rdg>
          </app>
a mile, then he struck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2697"/>
out over

          <app from="pr2697" n="149.26 (465.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4448">
            <lem wit="A Cent">out over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">into</rdg>
          </app>
the swamp and waded

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2698"/>
ancle deep

          <app from="pr2698" n="149.27 (465.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4449">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ancle deep</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ankle deep</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ankle-deep</rdg>
          </app>
as much as another

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2699"/>
half mile

          <app from="pr2699" n="149.27 (465.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4450">
            <lem wit="A">half mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">half a mile</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">half-mile</rdg>
          </app>
. We come to a little flat piece of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2700"/>
land

          <app from="pr2700" n="149.28 (465.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4451">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">land</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">land,</rdg>
          </app>
which was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2701"/>
dry,

          <app from="pr2701" n="149.28 (465.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4452">
            <lem wit="MS1b">dry,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
dry

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and very thick with trees and bushes and vines, and he says—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35342">
“You shove right in dah, jist a few steps,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0058"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2702"/>
mars

          <app from="pr2702" n="✱149.30 (466.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4453">
            <lem wit="C">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A Cent">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2703"/>
Jawge

          <ptr target="#tb0058" type="te" xml:id="tv0058"/>
          <app from="pr2703" n="149.30 (466.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4454">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Jawge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">George</rdg>
          </app>
, dah’s whah dey is. I’s seed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2704"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1510"/>
’m

          <ptr target="#l11020" type="alt" xml:id="te1510"/>
          <app from="pr2704" n="149.31 (466.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la0535">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’em</rdg>
          </app>
befo’,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1511"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l11022" type="alt" xml:id="te1511"/>
don’t k’yer to see ’em no mo’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35377">
Then he slopped right along and went away, and pretty soon the trees hid him. I poked into the place

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2705"/>
a ways

          <app from="pr2705" n="149.33 (466.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4456">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a ways</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">a-ways</rdg>
          </app>
, and come to a little open patch as big as a bedroom, all hung around with vines, and found a man laying there asleep—and by jings it was my old Jim!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35387">
I waked him up, and I reckoned

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1512"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l11024" type="alt" xml:id="te1512"/>
was going to be a grand surprise to him to see me again, but it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2706"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2706" n="149.37 (467.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4457">
            <lem wit="A Cent">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
. He nearly cried, he was so glad, but he warn’t surprised. Said he swum along behind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2707"/>
me,

          <app from="pr2707" n="149.38 (467.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4458">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">me,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that night,

          <pb n="150" xml:id="pb0150"/>
and heard me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2708"/>
yell,

          <app from="pr2708" n="150.1 (467.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4459">
            <lem wit="MS1b">yell,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
yell

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
every time, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2709"/>
dasn’t

          <app from="pr2709" n="150.1 (467.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4460">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dasn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">darsn’t</rdg>
          </app>
answer, because he didn’t want

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2710"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr2710" n="150.2 (467.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4461">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
to pick

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
up, and take him into slavery again.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1513"/>
Says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2711"/>
he—

          <app from="pr2711" n="150.3 (467.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4462">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">he—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">he:</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11026" type="alt" xml:id="te1513"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35451">
“I got hurt a little,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1514"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11028" type="alt" xml:id="te1514"/>
couldn’t swim

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1515"/>
fas’

          <ptr target="#l11030" type="alt" xml:id="te1515"/>
, so I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2712"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr2712" n="150.4 (468.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4463">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1516"/>
considable

          <ptr target="#l11032" type="alt" xml:id="te1516"/>
ways behine

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2713"/>
you,

          <app from="pr2713" n="150.5 (468.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4464">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">you,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
you

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2714"/>
towards

          <app from="pr2714" n="150.5 (468.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4465">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">toward</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2715"/>
de

          <app from="pr2715" n="150.5 (468.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4466">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">de</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">the</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2716"/>
las’;

          <app from="pr2716" n="150.5 (468.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4467">
            <lem wit="A Cent">las’;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">las’,</rdg>
          </app>
when you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2717"/>
landed

          <app from="pr2717" n="150.5 (468.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4468">
            <lem wit="A Cent">landed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">landed.</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2718"/>
reck’ned

          <app from="pr2718" n="150.5 (468.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4469">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’ned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reckoned</rdg>
          </app>
I could ketch up wid you on de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2719"/>
lan’

          <app from="pr2719" n="150.6 (468.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4470">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">lan’,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1517"/>
’dout

          <ptr target="#l11034" type="alt" xml:id="te1517"/>
havin’ to shout at you, but when I see dat house I begin to go slow. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2720"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr2720" n="150.7 (468.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4471">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
off too fur to hear what dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2721"/>
say

          <app from="pr2721" n="150.7 (468.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4472">
            <lem wit="A Cent">say</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">said</rdg>
          </app>
to you—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2722"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr2722" n="150.8 (468.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4473">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2723"/>
’fraid

          <app from="pr2723" n="150.8 (468.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4474">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">’fraid</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">afraid</rdg>
          </app>
o’ de dogs—but when it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2724"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr2724" n="150.8 (468.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4475">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
all quiet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2725"/>
agin

          <app from="pr2725" n="150.8 (468.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4476">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ag’in</rdg>
          </app>
, I knowed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2726"/>
you’s

          <app from="pr2726" n="150.9 (469.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4477">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">you was</rdg>
          </app>
in de house, so I struck out for de woods to wait for day. Early in de mawnin’

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0059"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1518"/>
some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2727"/>
er

          <app from="pr2727" n="✱150.10 (469.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4478">
            <lem wit="A Cent">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4479">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
de

          <ptr target="#l11036" type="alt" xml:id="te1518"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0059" type="te" xml:id="tv0059"/>
niggers come along,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2728"/>
gwyne

          <app from="pr2728" n="150.10 (469.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4480">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">gwyne</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gwine</rdg>
          </app>
to de fields,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1519"/>
en dey

          <ptr target="#l11038" type="alt" xml:id="te1519"/>
tuck

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1520"/>
me en

          <ptr target="#l11040" type="alt" xml:id="te1520"/>
showed me dis place, whah de dogs can’t track me on accounts o’ de water,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1521"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11042" type="alt" xml:id="te1521"/>
dey brings me truck to eat every night,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1522"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11044" type="alt" xml:id="te1522"/>
tells me how you’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2729"/>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1523"/>
gitt’n

          <ptr target="#l11046" type="alt" xml:id="te1523"/>
          <app from="pr2729" n="150.13 (469.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4481">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">a gitt’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-gitt’n</rdg>
          </app>
along.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35643">“Why didn’t you tell my Jack to fetch me here sooner, Jim?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35645">
“Well, ’twarn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2730"/>
no

          <app from="pr2730" n="150.15 (470.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4482">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any</rdg>
          </app>
use to ’sturb you, Huck, tell we could do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2731"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1524"/>
sumfn

          <ptr target="#l11048" type="alt" xml:id="te1524"/>
          <app from="pr2731" n="150.16 (470.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4483">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sumfn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sumfin</rdg>
          </app>
—but we’s all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2732"/>
right,

          <app from="pr2732" n="150.16 (470.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4484">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2733"/>
ben

          <app from="pr2733" n="150.16 (470.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4485">
            <lem wit="A">ben</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">been</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">b’en</rdg>
          </app>
a-buyin’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1525"/>
pots en

          <ptr target="#l11050" type="alt" xml:id="te1525"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1526"/>
pans en

          <ptr target="#l11052" type="alt" xml:id="te1526"/>
vittles, as I got a chanst,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1527"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11054" type="alt" xml:id="te1527"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2734"/>
a-patchin’

          <app from="pr2734" n="150.17 (470.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4486">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">a-patchin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a patchin’</rdg>
          </app>
up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1528"/>
de

          <ptr target="#l11056" type="alt" xml:id="te1528"/>
raf’,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2735"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1529"/>
nights

          <ptr target="#l11058" type="alt" xml:id="te1529"/>
          <app from="pr2735" n="150.17 (470.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4487">
            <lem wit="MS1b">nights</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">nights,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2736"/>
when—

          <app from="pr2736" n="150.17 (470.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4488">
            <lem wit="MS1b">when—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">when——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35726">
“

          <hi rend="italic">What</hi>
raft, Jim?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35731">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2737"/>
Our

          <app from="pr2737" n="150.19 (470.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4489">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Our</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">Our</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
ole raf’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35742">
“You mean to say our old raft

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1530"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l11060" type="alt" xml:id="te1530"/>
smashed all to flinders?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35748">
“No, she warn’t. She was tore up a good deal—one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1531"/>
en’

          <ptr target="#l11062" type="alt" xml:id="te1531"/>
of her was—but dey warn’t no great harm done, on’y our traps was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1532"/>
mos’

          <ptr target="#l11064" type="alt" xml:id="te1532"/>
all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1533"/>
los’

          <ptr target="#l11066" type="alt" xml:id="te1533"/>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2738"/>
Ef we hadn’

          <app from="pr2738" n="150.23 (471.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4490">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Ef we hadn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">If we hadn’t</rdg>
          </app>
dive’ so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1534"/>
deep en

          <ptr target="#l11068" type="alt" xml:id="te1534"/>
swum so fur under

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1535"/>
water, en

          <ptr target="#l11070" type="alt" xml:id="te1535"/>
de night

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2739"/>
hadn’

          <app from="pr2739" n="150.24 (471.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4491">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hadn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">hadn’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2740"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1536"/>
ben so

          <ptr target="#l11072" type="alt" xml:id="te1536"/>
dark,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1537"/>
en we

          <ptr target="#l11074" type="alt" xml:id="te1537"/>
warn’t so sk’yerd,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1538"/>
en ben

          <ptr target="#l11076" type="alt" xml:id="te1538"/>
          <app from="pr2740" n="150.24 (471.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4492">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ben . . . ben</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">b’en . . . b’en</rdg>
          </app>
sich punkin-heads,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1539"/>
as de

          <ptr target="#l11078" type="alt" xml:id="te1539"/>
sayin’ is,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1540"/>
we’d

          <ptr target="#l11080" type="alt" xml:id="te1540"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2741"/>
a seed

          <app from="pr2741" n="150.25 (471.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4493">
            <lem wit="A">a seed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a seen</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ seed</rdg>
          </app>
de raf’. But it’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1541"/>
jis’

          <ptr target="#l11082" type="alt" xml:id="te1541"/>
as well we didn’t,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2742"/>
’kase

          <app from="pr2742" n="150.26 (472.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4494">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’kase</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">’case</rdg>
          </app>
now she’s all fixed up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2743"/>
agin

          <app from="pr2743" n="150.26 (472.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4495">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ag’in</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1542"/>
mos’

          <ptr target="#l11084" type="alt" xml:id="te1542"/>
as good as new,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1543"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11086" type="alt" xml:id="te1543"/>
we’s got a new lot o’ stuff, too, in de place

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1544"/>
o’ what

          <ptr target="#l11088" type="alt" xml:id="te1544"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2744"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr2744" n="150.27 (472.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4496">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1545"/>
los’

          <ptr target="#l11090" type="alt" xml:id="te1545"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35868">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2745"/>
Why

          <app from="pr2745" n="150.28 (472.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4497">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
how did you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1546"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l11092" type="alt" xml:id="te1546"/>
hold of the raft again, Jim—did you catch her?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e35882">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1547"/>
How

          <ptr target="#l11094" type="alt" xml:id="te1547"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2746"/>
I gwyne

          <app from="pr2746" n="150.30 (472.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4498">
            <lem wit="A">I gwyne</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
gwyne

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">I gwine</rdg>
          </app>
to ketch

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1548"/>
her,

          <ptr target="#l11096" type="alt" xml:id="te1548"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1549"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11098" type="alt" xml:id="te1549"/>
I out in de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1550"/>
woods?

          <ptr target="#l11100" type="alt" xml:id="te1550"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2747"/>
No,

          <app from="pr2747" n="150.30 (472.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4499">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">No,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">No;</rdg>
          </app>
some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2748"/>
er

          <app from="pr2748" n="150.30 (472.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4500">
            <lem wit="A Cent">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">o’</rdg>
          </app>
de niggers foun’ her ketched on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2749"/>
snag

          <app from="pr2749" n="150.31 (472.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4501">
            <lem wit="MS1b">snag</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">snag,</rdg>
          </app>
along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2750"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1551"/>
heah

          <ptr target="#l11102" type="alt" xml:id="te1551"/>
          <app from="pr2750" n="150.31 (472.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4502">
            <lem wit="A Cent">heah</lem>
