reck’n

          <app from="pr2805" n="151.32 (479.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4561">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
he

          <hi rend="italic">did!</hi>
Dey warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2806"/>
gwyne

          <app from="pr2806" n="151.32 (480.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4562">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">gwyne</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gwine</rdg>
          </app>
to mix

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2807"/>
you

          <app from="pr2807" n="151.32 (480.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4563">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
up in it. Mars Buck he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2808"/>
loaded

          <app from="pr2808" n="151.33 (480.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4564">
            <lem wit="A Cent">loaded</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">loadened</rdg>
          </app>
up his gun

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1584"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11168" type="alt" xml:id="te1584"/>
’lowed he’s gwyne to fetch home a Shepherdson or bust. Well, dey’ll be plenty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2809"/>
un

          <app from="pr2809" n="151.34 (480.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4565">
            <lem wit="A Cent">un</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1585"/>
’m

          <ptr target="#l11170" type="alt" xml:id="te1585"/>
dah, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2810"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr2810" n="151.34 (480.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4566">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1586"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11172" type="alt" xml:id="te1586"/>
you bet you he’ll fetch one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2811"/>
ef

          <app from="pr2811" n="151.35 (480.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4567">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">if</rdg>
          </app>
he gits a chanst.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e36647">
I took

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2812"/>
up

          <app from="pr2812" n="151.36 (480.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4568">
            <lem wit="A Cent">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">out up</rdg>
          </app>
the river road as hard as I could put.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2813"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr2813" n="151.36 (480.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4569">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2814"/>
begin

          <app from="pr2814" n="151.36 (480.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4570">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">begin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">began</rdg>
          </app>
to hear guns a good ways off. When I come in sight of the log store and

          <pb n="152" xml:id="pb0152"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2815"/>
woodpile

          <app from="pr2815" n="152.1 (480.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la4571">
            <lem wit="C">woodpile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
wood-

              <lb/>
pile

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wood-pile</rdg>
          </app>
where the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2816"/>
steamboats

          <app from="pr2816" n="152.1 (480.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4572">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">steamboats</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">steam-boats</rdg>
          </app>
lands, I worked along under the trees and brush till I got to a good place, and then I clumb up into the forks of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2817"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1587"/>
cottonwood

          <ptr target="#l11174" type="alt" xml:id="te1587"/>
          <app from="pr2817" n="152.3 (481.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la4573">
            <lem wit="C">cottonwood</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
cotton-

              <lb/>
wood

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">cotton-wood</rdg>
          </app>
that was out of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2818"/>
reach

          <app from="pr2818" n="152.3 (481.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4574">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reach</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">range</rdg>
          </app>
, and watched. There was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2819"/>
wood-rank,

          <app from="pr2819" n="152.4 (481.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4575">
            <lem wit="MS1b">wood-rank,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wood-rank</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1588"/>
four

          <ptr target="#l11176" type="alt" xml:id="te1588"/>
foot high, a little ways in front of the tree, and first I was going to hide behind that; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2820"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr2820" n="152.5 (481.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4576">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
it was luckier I didn’t.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e36739">
There was four or five men cavorting around on their horses

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1589"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l11178" type="alt" xml:id="te1589"/>
the open place before the log store, cussing and yelling, and trying to get at

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="gs0099"/>
a couple of young chaps that was behind the wood-rank

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2821"/>
alongside

          <app from="pr2821" n="152.10 (482.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la4577">
            <lem wit="A Cent">alongside</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
along-

              <lb/>
side

            </rdg>
          </app>
of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2822"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr2822" n="152.10 (482.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4578">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
landing—but they couldn’t come it. Every time

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1590"/>
one

          <ptr target="#l11180" type="alt" xml:id="te1590"/>
of them showed himself on the river side of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2824"/>
wood pile

          <app from="pr2824" n="152.12 (482.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4581">
            <lem wit="MS1b">wood pile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wood-pile</rdg>
          </app>
he got shot at. The two boys was squatting back to back behind the pile, so they could watch both ways.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y15201">
          <graphic url="y15201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2823"/>
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">behind the wood-rank.</hi>
”

            <app from="pr2823" n="152 caption" type="e" xml:id="la4579">
              <lem wit="C">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">behind the wood-rank</hi>
.”

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1b">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4580">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">behind the wood-pile</hi>
.”

              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">behind the wood-pile</hi>
.

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e36806">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2825"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr2825" n="152.14 (482.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4582">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
the men stopped cavorting

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2826"/>
around,

          <app from="pr2826" n="152.14 (483.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4583">
            <lem wit="MS1b">around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
around

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and yelling. They started riding

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2827"/>
towards

          <app from="pr2827" n="152.15 (483.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4584">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">toward</rdg>
          </app>
the store; then up gets one of the boys, draws a steady bead

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1591"/>
over

          <ptr target="#l11182" type="alt" xml:id="te1591"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2828"/>
wood-rank

          <app from="pr2828" n="152.16 (483.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la4585">
            <lem wit="A">wood-rank</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
wood-

              <lb/>
rank

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and drops one of them out of his saddle. All the men jumped off of their

          <pb n="153" xml:id="pb0153"/>
horses and grabbed the hurt one and started to carry him to the store; and that minute the two boys started on the run. They got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2829"/>
half way

          <app from="pr2829" n="152.19 (483.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4586">
            <lem wit="MS1b">half way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">half-way</rdg>
          </app>
to the tree I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2830"/>
in,

          <app from="pr2830" n="152.19 (483.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4587">
            <lem wit="MS1b">in,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
in

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before the men noticed. Then the men

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2831"/>
see

          <app from="pr2831" n="152.20 (484.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4588">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saw</rdg>
          </app>
them, and jumped on their horses and took out after them. They gained on the boys, but it didn’t do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2832"/>
no

          <app from="pr2832" n="153.2 (484.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4589">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any</rdg>
          </app>
good, the boys had too good a start; they got to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2833"/>
wood pile

          <app from="pr2833" n="153.2–3 (484.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4590">
            <lem wit="MS1b">wood pile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wood-pile</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
wood-

              <lb/>
pile

            </rdg>
          </app>
that was in front of my tree, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2834"/>
slipped

          <app from="pr2834" n="153.3 (484.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4591">
            <lem wit="A Cent">slipped</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">skipped</rdg>
          </app>
in behind it, and so they had the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2835"/>
bulge on

          <app from="pr2835" n="153.4 (484.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4592">
            <lem wit="A Cent">bulge on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">advantage of</rdg>
          </app>
the men again. One of the boys was Buck, and the other was a slim young

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1592"/>
chap

          <ptr target="#l11184" type="alt" xml:id="te1592"/>
about nineteen years old.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e36915">
The men ripped around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2836"/>
a while

          <app from="pr2836" n="153.6 (485.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4593">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
, and then rode away. As soon as they was out of sight, I sung out to Buck and told him. He didn’t know what to make of my voice coming out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2837"/>
tree,

          <app from="pr2837" n="153.8 (485.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4594">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">tree,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
tree

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at first. He was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2838"/>
awful

          <app from="pr2838" n="153.9 (485.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4595">
            <lem wit="A Cent">awful</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">awfully</rdg>
          </app>
surprised. He told me to watch out sharp and let him know when the men come in sight again; said they was up to some devilment or other—wouldn’t be gone long. I wished I was out of that tree, but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2839"/>
dasn’t

          <app from="pr2839" n="153.12 (486.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4596">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dasn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">darsn’t</rdg>
          </app>
come down. Buck begun to cry and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1593"/>
rip,

          <ptr target="#l11186" type="alt" xml:id="te1593"/>
and ’lowed that him and his cousin Joe (that was the other young chap) would make up for this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2840"/>
day,

          <app from="pr2840" n="153.14 (486.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4597">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">day,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
day

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet. He said his father and his two brothers was killed, and two or three of the enemy. Said the Shepherdsons laid for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2841"/>
them,

          <app from="pr2841" n="153.16 (486.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4598">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">them,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
them

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in ambush. Buck said his father and brothers ought to waited for their relations—the Shepherdsons was too strong for them. I asked him what was become of young Harney and Miss Sophia. He said they’d got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2842"/>
across

          <app from="pr2842" n="153.19 (487.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4599">
            <lem wit="A Cent">across</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">acrost</rdg>
          </app>
the river and was safe. I was glad of that; but the way Buck did take on because he didn’t manage to kill Harney that day he shot at him—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2843"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr2843" n="153.21 (487.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4600">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">ain’t</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">haint</rdg>
          </app>
ever heard anything like it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e36990">
All of a sudden, bang! bang! bang! goes three or four guns—the men had slipped around through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2844"/>
woods,

          <app from="pr2844" n="153.24 (488.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4601">
            <lem wit="MS1b">woods,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
woods

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and come in from behind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1594"/>
without their horses

          <ptr target="#l11188" type="alt" xml:id="te1594"/>
!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1595"/>
The boys

          <ptr target="#l11190" type="alt" xml:id="te1595"/>
jumped for the river—both of them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2845"/>
hurt

          <app from="pr2845" n="153.26 (488.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4602">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hurt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was hurt</rdg>
          </app>
—and as they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2846"/>
swum

          <app from="pr2846" n="153.26 (488.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4603">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">swum</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">swam</rdg>
          </app>
down the current the men run along the bank shooting at them and singing out, “Kill them, kill them!” It made me so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2847"/>
sick,

          <app from="pr2847" n="153.28 (488.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4604">
            <lem wit="MS1b">sick,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
sick

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I most fell out of the tree. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2848"/>
ain’t agoing

          <app from="pr2848" n="153.28 (488.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4605">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint a-going</rdg>
          </app>
to tell

          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
that happened—it would make me sick again if I was to do that. I wished I hadn’t ever come ashore that night,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1596"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l11192" type="alt" xml:id="te1596"/>
see such things. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2849"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2849" n="153.31 (489.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4606">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
ever going to get shut of them—lots of times I dream about them.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37058">
I staid in the tree till

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1597"/>
it begun to get dark,

          <ptr target="#l11194" type="alt" xml:id="te1597"/>
afraid to come down. Sometimes I heard guns away off in the woods; and twice I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2850"/>
seen

          <app from="pr2850" n="153.34 (489.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4607">
            <lem wit="A Cent">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saw</rdg>
          </app>
little gangs of men gallop

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1598"/>
past

          <ptr target="#l11196" type="alt" xml:id="te1598"/>
the log store with guns; so I reckoned the trouble was still

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pro851"/>
agoing

          <app from="pro851" n="153.36 (490.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4608">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
on. I was mighty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2852"/>
down-hearted;

          <app from="pr2852" n="153.36 (490.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4609">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">down-hearted;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">downhearted,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2853"/>
so

          <app from="pr2853" n="153.36 (490.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4610">
            <lem wit="A Cent">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and</rdg>
          </app>
I made up my mind I wouldn’t ever go anear that house again, because I reckoned I was to blame, somehow. I judged that that piece of paper

          <pb n="154" xml:id="pb0154"/>
meant that Miss Sophia was to meet Harney somewheres at half-past two and run off; and I judged I ought to told her father about that paper and the curious way she acted, and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2854"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr2854" n="154.3 (491.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4611">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
he would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2855"/>
a

          <app from="pr2855" n="154.4 (491.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4612">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">have</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’</rdg>
          </app>
locked her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2856"/>
up

          <app from="pr2856" n="154.4 (491.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4613">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">up,</rdg>
          </app>
and this awful mess wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2857"/>
ever

          <app from="pr2857" n="154.4 (491.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4614">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">ever have</rdg>
          </app>
happened.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37138">
When I got down out of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1599"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2858"/>
tree

          <app from="pr2858" n="154.5 (491.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4615">
            <lem wit="MS1b">tree</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tree,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11198" type="alt" xml:id="te1599"/>
I crept along down the river bank a piece, and found the two bodies laying in the edge of the water

          <ptr target="#as0164" type="an" xml:id="gs0100"/>
, and tugged at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1600"/>
them

          <ptr target="#l11200" type="alt" xml:id="te1600"/>
till I got them ashore; then I covered up their faces, and got away as quick as I could. I cried a little when I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1601"/>
covering up Buck’s face, for he was mighty good to me.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37160">
It was just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2859"/>
dark,

          <app from="pr2859" n="154.10 (492.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4616">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">dark,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
dark

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now. I never went near the house, but struck through the woods and made for the swamp. Jim warn’t on his island, so I tramped off in a hurry for the crick, and crowded through the willows, red-hot to jump aboard and get out of that awful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2860"/>
country—the

          <app from="pr2860" n="154.14 (492.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4617">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">country—the</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">country. The</rdg>
          </app>
raft was gone! My souls, but I was scared!

          <ptr target="#l11202" type="alt" xml:id="te1601"/>
I couldn’t get my breath for most a minute. Then I raised a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2861"/>
yell.

          <app from="pr2861" n="154.15 (493.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4618">
            <lem wit="A Cent">yell.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">yell!</rdg>
          </app>
A voice not twenty-five foot from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2862"/>
me

          <app from="pr2862" n="154.16 (493.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4619">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">me,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2863"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1602"/>
says—

          <ptr target="#l11204" type="alt" xml:id="te1602"/>
          <app from="pr2863" n="154.16 (493.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4620">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37206">
“Good lan’! is

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1603"/>
dat

          <ptr target="#l11206" type="alt" xml:id="te1603"/>
you,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2864"/>
honey? Doan’

          <app from="pr2864" n="154.17 (493.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la4621">
            <lem wit="A Cent">honey? Doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
honey?—

              <lb/>
don’t

            </rdg>
          </app>
make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2865"/>
no

          <app from="pr2865" n="154.17 (493.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4622">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a</rdg>
          </app>
noise.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37231">
It was Jim’s voice—nothing ever sounded so good before. I run along the bank a piece and got aboard, and Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2866"/>
he

          <app from="pr2866" n="154.19 (493.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4623">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">just</rdg>
          </app>
grabbed me and hugged me, he was so glad to see me. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2867"/>
says—

          <app from="pr2867" n="154.20 (493.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4624">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37248">
“Laws bless you, chile, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2868"/>
’uz

          <app from="pr2868" n="154.21 (494.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4625">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’uz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
right down sho’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2869"/>
you’s

          <app from="pr2869" n="154.21 (494.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la4626">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">you was</rdg>
          </app>
dead

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2870"/>
agin

          <app from="pr2870" n="154.21 (494.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4627">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ag’in</rdg>
          </app>
. Jack’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2871"/>
ben

          <app from="pr2871" n="154.22 (494.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4628">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ben</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">been</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2872"/>
heah,

          <app from="pr2872" n="154.22 (494.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4629">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">heah,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">heah;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0060"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1604"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ar0001"/>
en

          <app from="ar0001" n="✱154.22 (494.4)" type="hc" xml:id="dz0001">
            <lem wit="MS1b">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="um0001">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11208" type="alt" xml:id="te1604"/>
          <ptr target="#tb0060" type="te" xml:id="tv0060"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1605"/>
he say

          <ptr target="#l11210" type="alt" xml:id="te1605"/>
he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2874"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1606"/>
reck’n

          <ptr target="#l11212" type="alt" xml:id="te1606"/>
          <app from="pr2874" n="154.22 (494.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4632">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2875"/>
you’s ben

          <app from="pr2875" n="154.22 (494.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4633">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">you’s ben</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">you’s be’n</rdg>
          </app>
shot,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2876"/>
kase you didn’

          <app from="pr2876" n="154.22 (494.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4634">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kase you didn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">’case you didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
come home no mo’; so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2877"/>
I’s

          <app from="pr2877" n="154.23 (494.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4635">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">I was</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1607"/>
jes’

          <ptr target="#l11214" type="alt" xml:id="te1607"/>
dis minute

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2878"/>
a startin’

          <app from="pr2878" n="154.23 (494.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4636">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">a startin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-startin’</rdg>
          </app>
de raf’ down towards de mouf

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1608"/>
er

          <ptr target="#l11216" type="alt" xml:id="te1608"/>
de crick,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2879"/>
so’s

          <app from="pr2879" n="154.24 (494.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4637">
            <lem wit="A Cent">so’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">so as</rdg>
          </app>
to be all ready for to shove out

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1609"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11218" type="alt" xml:id="te1609"/>
leave soon as Jack comes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2880"/>
agin

          <app from="pr2880" n="154.25 (494.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4638">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ag’in</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1610"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11220" type="alt" xml:id="te1610"/>
tells me for certain you

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
dead. Lawsy, I’s mighty glad to git you back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2881"/>
agin

          <app from="pr2881" n="154.26 (495.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4639">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ag’in</rdg>
          </app>
, honey.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37392">
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2882"/>
says—

          <app from="pr2882" n="154.27 (495.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4640">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37402">
“All right—that’s mighty good; they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2883"/>
won’t

          <app from="pr2883" n="154.28 (495.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4641">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">won’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">wont</rdg>
          </app>
find me, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2884"/>
they’ll

          <app from="pr2884" n="154.28 (495.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4642">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
they

              <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
think I’ve been killed, and floated down the river—there’s something up there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2885"/>
that’ll

          <app from="pr2885" n="154.30 (495.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4643">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that will</rdg>
          </app>
help them to think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2886"/>
so—

          <app from="pr2886" n="154.30 (495.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4644">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">so—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">so;</rdg>
          </app>
so don’t you lose no time, Jim, but just shove

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2887"/>
off

          <app from="pr2887" n="154.31 (495.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4645">
            <lem wit="A Cent">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4646">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for the big water as fast as ever you can.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37448">
I never felt easy till the raft was two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2888"/>
mile

          <app from="pr2888" n="154.32 (496.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4647">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">miles</rdg>
          </app>
below there and out in the middle of the Mississippi. Then we hung up our signal lantern, and judged that we was free and safe once more. I hadn’t had a bite to eat since yesterday; so Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2889"/>
he

          <app from="pr2889" n="154.35 (496.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4648">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4649">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
got out some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2890"/>
corn-dodgers,

          <app from="pr2890" n="154.35 (496.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4650">
            <lem wit="MS1b">corn-dodgers,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">corn-dodgers</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1611"/>
and buttermilk,

          <ptr target="#l11222" type="alt" xml:id="te1611"/>
and pork and cabbage, and greens—there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2891"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr2891" n="154.36 (496.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4651">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">aint</rdg>
          </app>
nothing in the world

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2892"/>
so

          <app from="pr2892" n="154.37 (496.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4652">
            <lem wit="A Cent">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">as</rdg>
          </app>
good, when it’s cooked right—and whilst I eat my

          <pb n="155" xml:id="pb0155"/>
supper we talked, and had a good time. I was powerful glad to get away from the feuds, and so was Jim to get away from the swamp. We said there warn’t no home like a raft, after all. Other places do seem so cramped up and smothery, but a raft don’t. You feel mighty free and easy and comfortable on a raft.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0340">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XIX.</head>
        <pb n="156" xml:id="pb0156"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37502">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y15601">
            <graphic url="y15601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2893"/>
Chapter XIX.

              <app from="pr2893" n="156 title (498 title)" type="e" xml:id="la4653">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XIX.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">CHAP.</rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4654">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1561">
            <graphic url="hf1561.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">hiding</hi>
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2905"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">daytimes</hi>
              <app from="pr2905" n="156 caption" type="e" xml:id="la4668">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">daytimes</hi>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4669">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">day-times</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e37533">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2894"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">
            <sic>wo</sic>
or three

          </hi>
days and nights went by; I reckon I might say they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2895"/>
swum

          <app from="pr2895" n="156.3 (498.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4657">
            <lem wit="A">swum</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">swum</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
by, they slid along so quiet and smooth and lovely

          <app from="pr2894" n="156.1–4 (498.1–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4655">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Two . . . lovely.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4656">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1612"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2896"/>
Here

          <app from="pr2896" n="156.5 (498.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4658">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4659">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Here

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">[¶] Here</rdg>
          </app>
is the way we put in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2897"/>
time.

          <ptr target="#l11224" type="alt" xml:id="te1612"/>
It

          <app from="pr2897" n="156.6 (498.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4660">
            <lem wit="A Cent">time. It</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
time.—

              <lb/>
It

            </rdg>
          </app>
was a monstrous big river down there—sometimes a mile and a half

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2898"/>
wide; we

          <app from="pr2898" n="156.8 (498.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4661">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">wide; we</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">wide. We</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2899"/>
run,

          <app from="pr2899" n="156.8 (498.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4662">
            <lem wit="MS1b">run,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
run

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
nights, and laid up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2900"/>
hid,

          <app from="pr2900" n="156.9 (499.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4663">
            <lem wit="MS1b">hid,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
hid

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1613"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2901"/>
daytimes

          <app from="pr2901" n="156.10 (499.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4664">
            <lem wit="MS1b">daytimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">day-times</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <ptr target="#l11226" type="alt" xml:id="te1613"/>
soon as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1614"/>
night

          <ptr target="#l11228" type="alt" xml:id="te1614"/>
was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1615"/>
most

          <ptr target="#l11230" type="alt" xml:id="te1615"/>
gone, we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1616"/>
stopped

          <ptr target="#l11232" type="alt" xml:id="te1616"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2902"/>
navigating,

          <app from="pr2902" n="156.11–12 (499.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4665">
            <lem wit="MS1b">navigating,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
navigating

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1617"/>
tied

          <ptr target="#l11234" type="alt" xml:id="te1617"/>
up—nearly always in the dead water under a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1618"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2903"/>
tow-head

          <app from="pr2903" n="156.14 (499.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4666">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">tow-head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
tow-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
;

          <ptr target="#l11236" type="alt" xml:id="te1618"/>
and then cut young

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2904"/>
cottonwoods

          <app from="pr2904" n="156.15 (499.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4667">
            <lem wit="MS1b">cottonwoods</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
cotton-

              <lb/>
woods

            </rdg>
          </app>
and willows and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1619"/>
hid

          <ptr target="#l11238" type="alt" xml:id="te1619"/>
the raft with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1620"/>
them.

          <ptr target="#l11240" type="alt" xml:id="te1620"/>
Then we set out the lines.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1621"/>
Next

          <ptr target="#l11242" type="alt" xml:id="te1621"/>
we slid into the river and had a swim, so as to freshen up and cool off; then we set down on the sandy bottom where the water was about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2906"/>
knee deep

          <app from="pr2906" n="156.20 (500.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4670">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">knee deep</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">knee-deep</rdg>
          </app>
, and watched the daylight come. Not a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2907"/>
sound,

          <app from="pr2907" n="156.20 (500.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4671">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">sound,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
sound

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
anywheres—perfectly still—just

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1622"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2908"/>
like

          <app from="pr2908" n="156.21 (500.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la4672">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">as if</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11244" type="alt" xml:id="te1622"/>
the whole world was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2909"/>
asleep, only sometimes the bull-frogs a-cluttering, maybe

          <app from="pr2909" n="156.21–22 (500.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4673">
            <lem wit="A">asleep . . . maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">dead asleep</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">asleep . . . may be</rdg>
          </app>
. The first thing to see, looking away

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2910"/>
over

          <app from="pr2910" n="156.23 (500.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4674">
            <lem wit="A Cent">over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">across</rdg>
          </app>
the water, was a kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2911"/>
dull

          <app from="pr2911" n="156.23 (500.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4675">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dull</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a dim, dull</rdg>
          </app>
line—that was the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2912"/>
woods

          <app from="pr2912" n="156.24 (500.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4676">
            <lem wit="A Cent">woods</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">forest</rdg>
          </app>
on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1623"/>
t’other

          <ptr target="#l11246" type="alt" xml:id="te1623"/>
side—you couldn’t make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2913"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr2913" n="156.24 (500.18)" type="e" xml:id="la4677">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anything</rdg>
          </app>
else out; then a pale place in the sky; then more paleness, spreading around; then the river softened up, away off, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2914"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr2914" n="156.26 (501.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4678">
            <lem wit="A Cent">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1624"/>
black

          <ptr target="#l11248" type="alt" xml:id="te1624"/>
any more, but gray; you could see little dark spots drifting along, ever so far away—trading scows, and such

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1625"/>
things;

          <ptr target="#l11250" type="alt" xml:id="te1625"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2915"/>
long,

          <app from="pr2915" n="156.28 (501.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4679">
            <lem wit="MS1b">long,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
long

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
black streaks—rafts; sometimes you could hear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2916"/>
a sweep screaking;

          <app from="pr2916" n="156.29 (501.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la4680">
            <lem wit="A">a sweep screaking;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the screak of a sweep,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a sweep screaking,</rdg>
          </app>
or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2917"/>
jumbled up

          <app from="pr2917" n="156.29 (501.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4681">
            <lem wit="A">jumbled up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">jumbled sounds of</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">jumbled-up</rdg>
          </app>
voices, it was so still, and sounds

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2918"/>
come

          <app from="pr2918" n="156.30 (502.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4682">
            <lem wit="A Cent">come</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">traveled</rdg>
          </app>
so far;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2919"/>
and by and by

          <app from="pr2919" n="156.30 (502.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4683">
            <lem wit="Cent">and by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">now</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">and by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
you could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2920"/>
see a

          <app from="pr2920" n="156.30–31 (502.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la4684">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">begin to see the ruffled</rdg>
          </app>
streak on the water

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1626"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2921"/>
which you know by the look of the streak that there’s a snag there in a swift current which breaks on it and makes

          <pb n="157" xml:id="pb0157"/>
that streak look that way

          <app from="pr2921" n="156.31–157.1 (502.4–6)" type="e" xml:id="la4685">
            <lem wit="A Cent">which . . . way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that the current breaking past a snag makes</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11252" type="alt" xml:id="te1626"/>
;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2922"/>
and you see the mist curl

          <app from="pr2922" n="157.1 (502.6–8)" type="e" xml:id="la4686">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and . . . curl</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">next, you would see the lightest and whitest mist curling</rdg>
          </app>
up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2923"/>
off of the water, and the

          <app from="pr2923" n="157.1–2 (502.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4687">
            <lem wit="A Cent">off of the water, and the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">from the water; pretty soon</rdg>
          </app>
east reddens up,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2924"/>
and the river, and

          <app from="pr2924" n="157.2 (502.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la4688">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and the river, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">then the river reddens, and maybe</rdg>
          </app>
you make out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2925"/>
a

          <app from="pr2925" n="157.2 (502.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4689">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a little</rdg>
          </app>
log cabin in the edge of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2926"/>
woods

          <app from="pr2926" n="157.3 (502.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4690">
            <lem wit="A Cent">woods</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">forest</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2927"/>
away

          <app from="pr2927" n="157.3 (502.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la4691">
            <lem wit="A Cent">away</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">away yonder</rdg>
          </app>
on the bank on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1627"/>
t’other

          <ptr target="#l11254" type="alt" xml:id="te1627"/>
side of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2928"/>
river, being a wood-yard, likely, and piled by them cheats so you can throw a dog through it anywheres

          <app from="pr2928" n="157.4–5 (502.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4692">
            <lem wit="A Cent">river, being . . . anywheres</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">river</rdg>
          </app>
; then the nice breeze

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2929"/>
springs up, and comes

          <app from="pr2929" n="157.6 (503.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la4693">
            <lem wit="A Cent">springs up, and comes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">would spring up, and come</rdg>
          </app>
fanning you from over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2930"/>
there

          <app from="pr2930" n="157.6 (503.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4694">
            <lem wit="A Cent">there</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the water</rdg>
          </app>
, so cool and fresh, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2931"/>
sweet

          <app from="pr2931" n="157.7 (503.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4695">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sweet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">so sweet</rdg>
          </app>
to smell, on account of the woods and the flowers;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2932"/>
but sometimes not that way, because they’ve left dead fish laying around, gars, and such, and they do get pretty rank; and

          <app from="pr2932" n="157.8–9 (503.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4696">
            <lem wit="A Cent">but . . . rank; and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4697">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2933"/>
you’ve got

          <app from="pr2933" n="157.9–10 (503.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4698">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’ve got</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">you’d have</rdg>
          </app>
the full day, and everything

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2934"/>
smiling

          <app from="pr2934" n="157.10 (503.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4699">
            <lem wit="A Cent">smiling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">shining</rdg>
          </app>
in the sun, and the song-birds just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2935"/>
going

          <app from="pr2935" n="157.11 (503.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4700">
            <lem wit="A Cent">going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">agoing</rdg>
          </app>
it!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e37960">
A little smoke couldn’t be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2936"/>
noticed,

          <app from="pr2936" n="157.12 (503.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4701">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">noticed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
noticed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, so we would take some fish off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2937"/>
of

          <app from="pr2937" n="157.13 (503.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4702">
            <lem wit="A Cent">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4703">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2938"/>
lines,

          <app from="pr2938" n="157.13 (503.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4704">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">lines,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
lines

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and cook up a hot breakfast.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2939"/>
And afterwards

          <app from="pr2939" n="157.13 (504.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la4705">
            <lem wit="A">And afterwards</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">After we had had a smoke,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">And afterward</rdg>
          </app>
we would watch the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2940"/>
lonesomeness

          <app from="pr2940" n="157.14 (504.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4706">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lonesomeness</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">awful lonesomeness</rdg>
          </app>
of the river, and kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2941"/>
lazy along

          <app from="pr2941" n="157.14 (504.6–8)" type="e" xml:id="la4707">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lazy along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">dream along, and be happy, not talking much</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2942"/>
and by and by

          <app from="pr2942" n="157.15 (504.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4708">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">and by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2943"/>
lazy

          <app from="pr2943" n="157.15 (504.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4709">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lazy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">nod</rdg>
          </app>
off to sleep. Wake

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2944"/>
up, by and by

          <app from="pr2944" n="157.15 (504.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4710">
            <lem wit="MS1b">up, by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">up, by-and-by</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">up by and by</rdg>
          </app>
, and look to see what done it, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2945"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr2945" n="157.16 (504.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4711">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
see a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2946"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr2946" n="157.16 (504.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4712">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
, coughing along up stream, so far off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2947"/>
towards

          <app from="pr2947" n="157.17 (504.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4713">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">toward</rdg>
          </app>
the other side

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2948"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1628"/>
you couldn’t tell nothing about her only whether she was stern-wheel or side-wheel

          <app from="pr2948" n="157.17–18 (504.15–505.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4714">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you . . . side-wheel</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that she didn’t seem to belong to this world at all, hardly</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11256" type="alt" xml:id="te1628"/>
; then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1629"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l11258" type="alt" xml:id="te1629"/>
about an hour there wouldn’t be

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1630"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2949"/>
nothing to hear nor nothing to

          <app from="pr2949" n="157.19 (505.4–7)" type="e" xml:id="la4715">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing to hear nor nothing to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a sound on the water, nor a solitary moving thing, as far as you could</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11260" type="alt" xml:id="te1630"/>
see—just solid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2950"/>
lonesomeness

          <app from="pr2950" n="157.20 (505.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4716">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lonesomeness</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Sunday and lonesomeness</rdg>
          </app>
. Next you’d see a raft sliding by, away off yonder, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2951"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr2951" n="157.21 (505.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4717">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2952"/>
galoot on it chopping, because they’re most always doing it on a raft

          <app from="pr2952" n="157.21–22 (505.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4718">
            <lem wit="A Cent">galoot . . . raft</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">man on it, chopping</rdg>
          </app>
; you’d see the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1631"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2953"/>
axe

          <app from="pr2953" n="157.22 (505.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4719">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">axe</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ax</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11262" type="alt" xml:id="te1631"/>
flash, and come down—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2954"/>
you don’t hear nothing; you

          <app from="pr2954" n="157.22–23 (505.14–506.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4720">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you don’t hear nothing; you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">nary a sound, any more than if it had sunk into butter; you’d</rdg>
          </app>
see that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2955"/>
axe

          <app from="pr2955" n="157.23 (506.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4721">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">axe</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ax</rdg>
          </app>
go up again, and by the time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2956"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr2956" n="157.23 (506.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4722">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">it was</rdg>
          </app>
above the man’s head,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2957"/>
then you

          <app from="pr2957" n="157.24 (506.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4723">
            <lem wit="A Cent">then you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
you’d

            </rdg>
          </app>
hear the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2958"/>
          <hi rend="italic">k’chunk!</hi>
          <app from="pr2958" n="157.24 (506.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4724">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">k’chunk!</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sound, sharp and clean</rdg>
          </app>
—it had took all that time to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2959"/>
come

          <app from="pr2959" n="157.25 (506.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4725">
            <lem wit="A Cent">come</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">travel</rdg>
          </app>
over the water. So we would put in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2960"/>
day, lazying around,

          <app from="pr2960" n="157.25–26 (506.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4726">
            <lem wit="A Cent">day, lazying around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">day; dozing, dreaming, and</rdg>
          </app>
listening to the stillness. Once there was a thick fog, and the rafts and things that went by

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1632"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l11264" type="alt" xml:id="te1632"/>
beating tin pans

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2961"/>
so the steamboats wouldn’t

          <app from="pr2961" n="157.27–28 (506.14–16)" type="e" xml:id="la4727">
            <lem wit="A">so the steamboats wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">to warn steamboats to keep off and not</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">so the steam-boats wouldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
run over them.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1633"/>
A

          <ptr target="#l11266" type="alt" xml:id="te1633"/>
scow or a raft went by so close

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2962"/>
we could hear

          <app from="pr2962" n="157.29 (507.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la4728">
            <lem wit="A Cent">we could hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">to us that we heard</rdg>
          </app>
them talking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2963"/>
and cussing

          <app from="pr2963" n="157.29 (507.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4729">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and cussing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4730">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and laughing—heard them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1634"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2964"/>
plain

          <app from="pr2964" n="157.30 (507.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la4731">
            <lem wit="A Cent">plain</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">just as plain as if they had been only five steps off</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <ptr target="#l11268" type="alt" xml:id="te1634"/>
but we couldn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="aru001"/>
no

          <app from="aru001" n="157.30 (507.8)" type="e" xml:id="mua001">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the faintest</rdg>
          </app>
sign of them; it made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="aru002"/>
you

          <app from="aru002" n="157.30 (507.9)" type="e" xml:id="mua002">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">me</rdg>
          </app>
feel crawly, it was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1635"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="aru003"/>
like spirits carrying on that way in the air

          <app from="aru003" n="157.31 (507.10–508.1)" type="e" xml:id="mua003">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like . . . air</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">so like ghosts or spirits talking and laughing in the air; and the voices drifted off and faded out, just the same as if they had been on the wing</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11270" type="alt" xml:id="te1635"/>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2968"/>
Jim said he believed it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2969"/>
was

          <app from="pr2969" n="157.32 (508.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4737">
            <lem wit="A">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
spirits; but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2970"/>
says:

          <app from="pr2970" n="157.32 (508.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4738">
            <lem wit="A">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">says,</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38285">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1636"/>
“No

          <ptr target="#l11272" type="alt" xml:id="te1636"/>
, spirits wouldn’t say,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2971"/>
‘Dern

          <app from="pr2971" n="157.33 (508.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4739">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Dern</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dern</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2972"/>
dern

          <app from="pr2972" n="157.33 (508.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4740">
            <lem wit="A">dern</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">derned</rdg>
          </app>
fog.’ ”

          <app from="pr2968" n="157.31–33 (508.1–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4735">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Jim . . . fog.’ ”</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4736">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38313">
Soon as it was night, out we shoved; when we got her out to about the middle, we let her alone, and let her float wherever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1637"/>
the current

          <ptr target="#l11274" type="alt" xml:id="te1637"/>
wanted her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2973"/>
to; then

          <app from="pr2973" n="157.36 (508.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4741">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">to; then</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">to. Then</rdg>
          </app>
we lit the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2974"/>
pipes

          <app from="pr2974" n="157.36 (508.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4742">
            <lem wit="MS1b">pipes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">pipes,</rdg>
          </app>
and dangled our legs in the water

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1638"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l11276" type="alt" xml:id="te1638"/>
talked

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1639"/>
about

          <ptr target="#l11278" type="alt" xml:id="te1639"/>
all kinds of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2975"/>
things—we was always naked, day and night, whenever the mosquitoes would let us—the new

          <pb n="158" xml:id="pb0158"/>
clothes Buck’s folks made for me was too good to be comfortable, and besides I didn’t go much on clothes, nohow

          <app from="pr2975" n="157.37–158.2 (509.1–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4743">
            <lem wit="C">things—we . . . clothes, nohow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">things—we . . . clothes anyway</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
things—we . . . no-

              <lb/>
how

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">things</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38361">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2976"/>
Sometimes

          <app from="pr2976" n="158.3 (509.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4744">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Sometimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Well, sometimes</rdg>
          </app>
we’d have that whole

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2977"/>
river

          <app from="pr2977" n="158.3 (509.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4745">
            <lem wit="A Cent">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">monstrous river</rdg>
          </app>
all to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2978"/>
ourselves,

          <app from="pr2978" n="158.3 (509.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4746">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ourselves,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
ourselves

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2979"/>
the longest time

          <app from="pr2979" n="158.3–4 (509.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4747">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the longest time</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">hours</rdg>
          </app>
. Yonder was the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2980"/>
banks

          <app from="pr2980" n="158.4 (509.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4748">
            <lem wit="A Cent">banks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">dim banks</rdg>
          </app>
and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2981"/>
islands,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1640"/>
across

          <ptr target="#l11280" type="alt" xml:id="te1640"/>
          <app from="pr2981" n="158.4 (509.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la4749">
            <lem wit="A Cent">islands, across</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">islands away off acrost</rdg>
          </app>
the water; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2982"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr2982" n="158.5 (509.17–510.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4750">
            <lem wit="A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">now and then</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2983"/>
spark—

          <app from="pr2983" n="158.5 (510.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4751">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">spark—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">spark,—</rdg>
          </app>
which was a candle in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2984"/>
a cabin

          <app from="pr2984" n="158.5 (510.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4752">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a cabin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">some cabin</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2985"/>
window—

          <app from="pr2985" n="158.5 (510.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4753">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">window—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">window,—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2986"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1641"/>
sometimes

          <ptr target="#l11282" type="alt" xml:id="te1641"/>
on the water you

          <app from="pr2986" n="158.6 (510.3–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4754">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and . . . you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">some family was at home, there, and they could see our lantern, of course, and so it was kind of sociable-like, and friendly; and sometimes, away down the river, or away up it, we</rdg>
          </app>
could see a spark or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2987"/>
two—

          <app from="pr2987" n="158.6 (510.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4755">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">two—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">two,</rdg>
          </app>
on a raft or a scow, you know; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2988"/>
maybe you could

          <app from="pr2988" n="158.7 (510.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la4756">
            <lem wit="A">maybe you could</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">maybe we would just</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be you could</rdg>
          </app>
hear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2989"/>
a fiddle

          <app from="pr2989" n="158.7 (510.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la4757">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a fiddle</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the faintest scraping of a fiddle</rdg>
          </app>
or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2990"/>
a song

          <app from="pr2990" n="158.7 (510.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4758">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a song</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sound of a song</rdg>
          </app>
coming

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2991"/>
over

          <app from="pr2991" n="158.8 (511.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4759">
            <lem wit="A Cent">over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">over the water</rdg>
          </app>
from one of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2992"/>
them

          <app from="pr2992" n="158.8 (511.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4760">
            <lem wit="A Cent">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">those</rdg>
          </app>
crafts.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1642"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2993"/>
It’s

          <app from="pr2993" n="158.8 (511.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4761">
            <lem wit="A Cent">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
Lordy, it

              <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11284" type="alt" xml:id="te1642"/>
lovely to live on a raft. We had the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2994"/>
sky,

          <app from="pr2994" n="158.9 (511.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4762">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">sky,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
sky

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2995"/>
there,

          <app from="pr2995" n="158.9 (511.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4763">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2996"/>
speckled

          <app from="pr2996" n="158.9 (511.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4764">
            <lem wit="A Cent">speckled</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sprinkled thick</rdg>
          </app>
with stars, and we used to lay on our backs and look up at them, and discuss about whether they was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1643"/>
made, or

          <ptr target="#l11286" type="alt" xml:id="te1643"/>
only just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2997"/>
happened—Jim

          <app from="pr2997" n="158.11 (511.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4765">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">happened—Jim</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">happened. Jim</rdg>
          </app>
he allowed they was made, but I allowed they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2998"/>
happened; I

          <app from="pr2998" n="158.12 (511.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4766">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">happened; I</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">happened. I</rdg>
          </app>
judged it would have took too long to

          <hi rend="italic">make</hi>
so many. Jim said the moon could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr2999"/>
a

          <app from="pr2999" n="158.13 (512.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4767">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">have</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">laid</hi>
them; well, that looked kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3000"/>
reasonable

          <app from="pr3000" n="158.14 (512.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la4768">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reasonable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reasonable and natural</rdg>
          </app>
, so I didn’t say nothing against it, because I’ve seen a frog lay most as many, so of course it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3001"/>
could

          <app from="pr3001" n="158.15 (512.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4769">
            <lem wit="A Cent">could</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was plain enough it could</rdg>
          </app>
be done.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3002"/>
We used to watch the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3003"/>
stars that fell

          <app from="pr3003" n="158.16 (512.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la4772">
            <lem wit="A">stars that fell</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">falling stars</rdg>
          </app>
, too, and see them streak

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3004"/>
down. Jim

          <app from="pr3004" n="158.16 (513.1–4)" type="e" xml:id="la4773">
            <lem wit="A">down. Jim</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
down the sky and trail their sparky tails behind them.—

              <lb/>
Jim

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3005"/>
allowed they’d

          <app from="pr3005" n="158.17 (513.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4774">
            <lem wit="A">allowed they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reckoned they had</rdg>
          </app>
got spoiled and was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3006"/>
hove

          <app from="pr3006" n="158.17 (513.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4775">
            <lem wit="A">hove</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">flung</rdg>
          </app>
out of the nest.

          <app from="pr3002" n="158.15–17 (512.13–513.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4770">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">We . . . nest.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4771">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38646">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3007"/>
Once

          <app from="pr3007" n="158.18 (513.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4776">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Once</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">About once</rdg>
          </app>
or twice

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3008"/>
of

          <app from="pr3008" n="158.18 (513.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4777">
            <lem wit="A Cent">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4778">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a night we would see a steamboat slipping along in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3009"/>
dark

          <app from="pr3009" n="158.19 (513.10–12)" type="e" xml:id="la4779">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dark</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">dark, away over on t’other side, like a long string of glow-worms</rdg>
          </app>
, and now and then she would belch a whole world of sparks up out of her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3010"/>
chimbleys,

          <app from="pr3010" n="158.20 (513.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4780">
            <lem wit="A Cent">chimbleys</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">chimneys</rdg>
          </app>
and they would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3011"/>
rain

          <app from="pr3011" n="158.20 (514.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la4781">
            <lem wit="A Cent">rain</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">trail off and rain</rdg>
          </app>
down in the river and look awful pretty; then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3012"/>
she

          <app from="pr3012" n="158.21 (514.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4782">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the boat</rdg>
          </app>
would turn a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3013"/>
corner

          <app from="pr3013" n="158.21 (514.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4783">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">corner</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">corner,</rdg>
          </app>
and her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3014"/>
lights

          <app from="pr3014" n="158.22 (514.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4784">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lights</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">light</rdg>
          </app>
would wink out and her pow-wow

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3015"/>
shut off

          <app from="pr3015" n="158.22 (514.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4785">
            <lem wit="A Cent">shut off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">die down</rdg>
          </app>
and leave the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3016"/>
river still

          <app from="pr3016" n="158.22–23 (514.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4786">
            <lem wit="A Cent">river still</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">big river all to us</rdg>
          </app>
again; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3017"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr3017" n="158.23 (514.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4787">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3018"/>
her

          <app from="pr3018" n="158.23 (514.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la4788">
            <lem wit="A Cent">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the wash of her</rdg>
          </app>
waves would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3019"/>
get

          <app from="pr3019" n="158.23 (514.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4789">
            <lem wit="A Cent">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">travel</rdg>
          </app>
to us,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3020"/>
a long time

          <app from="pr3020" n="158.23 (514.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4790">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a long time</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">long</rdg>
          </app>
after she was gone, and joggle

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3021"/>
the

          <app from="pr3021" n="158.24 (514.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4791">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">our</rdg>
          </app>
raft a bit, and after that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1645"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3022"/>
you wouldn’t hear nothing for you couldn’t tell how long, except maybe frogs or something

          <app from="pr3022" n="158.24–26 (514.14–16)" type="e" xml:id="la4792">
            <lem wit="A">you . . . maybe . . . something</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">we would have the dead quiet once more</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">you . . . may be . . . something</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11290" type="alt" xml:id="te1645"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38784">
After midnight the people on shore went to bed, and then for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1646"/>
two or

          <ptr target="#l11292" type="alt" xml:id="te1646"/>
three hours the shores was black—no more sparks in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3023"/>
the cabin

          <app from="pr3023" n="158.28 (515.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4793">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the cabin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">cabin</rdg>
          </app>
windows. These sparks was our clock—the first one that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3024"/>
showed, again,

          <app from="pr3024" n="158.29–30 (515.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4794">
            <lem wit="MS1b">showed, again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
showed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
again

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
meant

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3025"/>
morning

          <app from="pr3025" n="158.30 (515.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4795">
            <lem wit="A Cent">morning</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that morning</rdg>
          </app>
was coming, so we hunted a place to hide and tie

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3026"/>
up,

          <app from="pr3026" n="158.31 (515.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4796">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
right away.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y15901">
          <graphic url="y15901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">and dogs a-coming.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38830">
One

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3027"/>
morning

          <app from="pr3027" n="158.32 (515.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4797">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">morning</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">morning,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1647"/>
about

          <ptr target="#l11294" type="alt" xml:id="te1647"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3028"/>
daybreak

          <app from="pr3028" n="158.32 (515.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4798">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">daybreak</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-break</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sm0001"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3029"/>
found a

          <app from="pr3029" n="158.32 (515.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4799">
            <lem wit="A Cent">found a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Pfs1">took the</rdg>
            <rdg>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="deg814">
see

                <ref corresp="#bm0010" type="chapterref">explanatory note</ref>
              </note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
canoe

          <ptr target="#as0165" type="an" xml:id="vs0001"/>
and crossed over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3030"/>
a chute

          <app from="pr3030" n="158.32–33 (515.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4800">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a chute</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="dec814">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1648"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l11296" type="alt" xml:id="te1648"/>
the main

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3031"/>
shore—it was only two hundred yards—

          <app from="pr3031" n="158.33 (516.1–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4801">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">shore— . . . yards—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">shore,— . . . yards,—</rdg>
          </app>
and paddled about a mile up a crick amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3032"/>
cypress

          <app from="pr3032" n="158.34 (516.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la4802">
            <lem wit="A Cent">cypress</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">thick cypress</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3033"/>
woods,

          <app from="pr3033" n="158.34 (516.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4803">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">woods,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
woods

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to see if I couldn’t get some berries. Just as I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1649"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l11298" type="alt" xml:id="te1649"/>
passing a place where a kind of a cow-path crossed the crick, here comes a couple of men tearing up the path as tight as they could foot it. I thought I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1650"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l11300" type="alt" xml:id="te1650"/>
goner, for whenever anybody was after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3034"/>
anybody,

          <app from="pr3034" n="158.38 (517.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4804">
            <lem wit="MS1b">anybody,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
anybody

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I judged it was

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
—or

          <pb n="159" xml:id="pb0159"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3035"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr3035" n="159.1 (517.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4805">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
Jim. I was about to dig out from there in a hurry, but they was pretty close to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3036"/>
me,

          <app from="pr3036" n="159.2 (517.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4806">
            <lem wit="MS1b">me,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then, and sung out and begged me to save their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3037"/>
lives—said they hadn’t been doing nothing, and was being chased for it—

          <app from="pr3037" n="159.3–4 (517.8–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4807">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">lives— . . . it—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">lives; . . . it;</rdg>
          </app>
said there was men and dogs a-coming.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1651"/>
They

          <ptr target="#l11302" type="alt" xml:id="te1651"/>
wanted to jump right in, but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3038"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3038" n="159.5 (517.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4808">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38963">
“Don’t you do it. I don’t hear the dogs and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3039"/>
horses,

          <app from="pr3039" n="159.6 (518.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4809">
            <lem wit="MS1b">horses,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
horses

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3040"/>
yet; you’ve

          <app from="pr3040" n="159.6 (518.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4810">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">yet; you’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">yet. You’ve</rdg>
          </app>
got time to crowd through the brush and get up the crick a little ways; then you take to the water and wade down to me and get in—that’ll throw the dogs

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3041"/>
off

          <app from="pr3041" n="159.9 (518.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4811">
            <lem wit="A Cent">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">off of</rdg>
          </app>
the scent.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e38988">
They done it, and soon as they was aboard I lit out for our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3042"/>
towhead

          <app from="pr3042" n="159.10–11 (518.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4812">
            <lem wit="MS1b">towhead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tow-head</rdg>
          </app>
, and in about five or ten

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1652"/>
minutes

          <ptr target="#l11304" type="alt" xml:id="te1652"/>
we heard the dogs

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3043"/>
and the men

          <app from="pr3043" n="159.11–12 (519.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4813">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and the men</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4814">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
away

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3044"/>
off

          <app from="pr3044" n="159.12 (519.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4815">
            <lem wit="A Cent">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">off, and then the men</rdg>
          </app>
, shouting. We heard them come along

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1653"/>
towards the crick,

          <ptr target="#l11306" type="alt" xml:id="te1653"/>
but couldn’t see them; they seemed to stop and fool around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3045"/>
a while; then

          <app from="pr3045" n="159.13–14 (519.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4816">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">a while; then</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile. Then</rdg>
          </app>
, as we got further and further away all the time, we couldn’t hardly hear them at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3046"/>
all; by

          <app from="pr3046" n="159.15 (519.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4817">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">all; by</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">all. By</rdg>
          </app>
the time we had left a mile of

          <pb n="160" xml:id="pb0160"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3047"/>
woods

          <app from="pr3047" n="160.1 (520.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4818">
            <lem wit="A Cent">woods</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">forest</rdg>
          </app>
behind us and struck the river, everything was quiet, and we paddled over to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3048"/>
towhead

          <app from="pr3048" n="160.2 (520.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4819">
            <lem wit="MS1b">towhead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tow-head</rdg>
          </app>
and hid in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3049"/>
cottonwoods

          <app from="pr3049" n="160.2 (520.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4820">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">cottonwoods</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cotton-woods</rdg>
          </app>
and was safe.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39067">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="smm001"/>
One of these fellows was about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1654"/>
seventy,

          <ptr target="#l11308" type="alt" xml:id="te1654"/>
or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3050"/>
upwards

          <app from="pr3050" n="160.4 (520.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4821">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">upwards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">upward</rdg>
          </app>
, and had a bald head and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1655"/>
very

          <ptr target="#l11310" type="alt" xml:id="te1655"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1656"/>
gray

          <ptr target="#l11312" type="alt" xml:id="te1656"/>
whiskers. He had an old battered-up slouch hat on, and a greasy blue woolen shirt, and ragged old blue jeans britches stuffed into his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3051"/>
boot tops

          <app from="pr3051" n="160.7 (521.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4822">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">boot tops</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">boot-tops</rdg>
          </app>
, and home-knit galluses—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3052"/>
no

          <app from="pr3052" n="160.7 (521.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4823">
            <lem wit="MS1b">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">no,</rdg>
          </app>
he only had one. He had an old long-tailed blue jeans coat with slick brass

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3053"/>
buttons

          <ptr target="#as0166" type="an" xml:id="vim001"/>
,

          <app from="pr3053" n="160.9 (521.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4824">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">buttons,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
buttons

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
flung over his arm,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1657"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l11314" type="alt" xml:id="te1657"/>
both of them had big fat ratty-looking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3054"/>
carpet-bags

          <app from="pr3054" n="160.10 (521.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4825">
            <lem wit="A Cent">carpet-bags</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">old carpet-bags</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39130">
The other fellow was about thirty and dressed about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3055"/>
as ornery

          <app from="pr3055" n="160.11 (521.15–522.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4826">
            <lem wit="A Cent">as ornery</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the same</rdg>
          </app>
. After breakfast we all laid off and talked, and the first thing that come out was that these chaps didn’t know

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1658"/>
one another

          <ptr target="#l11316" type="alt" xml:id="te1658"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39144">
“What got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3056"/>
you

          <app from="pr3056" n="160.14 (522.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4827">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
into trouble?” says the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3057"/>
bald-head

          <app from="pr3057" n="160.14 (522.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la4828">
            <lem wit="C">bald-head</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
bald-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">baldhead</rdg>
          </app>
to t’other chap.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39167">
“Well,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1659"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3058"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr3058" n="160.15 (522.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4829">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">I had</rdg>
          </app>
been

          <ptr target="#l11318" type="alt" xml:id="te1659"/>
selling an article to

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0003"/>
take the tartar

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1660"/>
off the

          <ptr target="#l11320" type="alt" xml:id="te1660"/>
teeth—and it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3059"/>
does

          <app from="pr3059" n="160.16 (522.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4830">
            <lem wit="A Cent">does</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">does</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
take it off, too, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1661"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3060"/>
generly

          <app from="pr3060" n="160.16 (522.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4831">
            <lem wit="A Cent">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">generally</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11322" type="alt" xml:id="te1661"/>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1662"/>
enamel

          <ptr target="#l11324" type="alt" xml:id="te1662"/>
along with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3061"/>
it

          <ptr target="#as0167" type="an" xml:id="vs0003"/>
—

          <app from="pr3061" n="160.16 (522.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4832">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">it—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it;</rdg>
          </app>
but I staid

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1663"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3062"/>
about

          <app from="pr3062" n="160.17 (522.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4833">
            <lem wit="A Cent">about</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">just about</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11326" type="alt" xml:id="te1663"/>
one night

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1664"/>
longer than

          <ptr target="#l11328" type="alt" xml:id="te1664"/>
I ought to, and was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1665"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l11330" type="alt" xml:id="te1665"/>
in the act of sliding out when I ran

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1666"/>
across

          <ptr target="#l11332" type="alt" xml:id="te1666"/>
you on the trail this side of town, and you told me they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1667"/>
were

          <ptr target="#l11334" type="alt" xml:id="te1667"/>
coming, and begged me to help you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3063"/>
to

          <app from="pr3063" n="160.20 (523.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4834">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4835">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
get off. So I told you I was expecting trouble myself and would scatter out

          <hi rend="italic">with</hi>
you. That’s the whole yarn—what’s yourn?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39262">
“Well, I’d ben

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3064"/>
a-runnin’

          <app from="pr3064" n="160.22 (523.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4836">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a-runnin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a-running</rdg>
          </app>
a little temperance revival thar, ’bout a week, and was the pet of the women-folks, big and little, for I was makin’ it mighty warm for the rummies, I

          <hi rend="italic">tell</hi>
you, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3065"/>
takin’

          <app from="pr3065" n="160.24 (524.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4837">
            <lem wit="A Cent">takin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">takin’ in</rdg>
          </app>
as much as five

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3066"/>
or

          <app from="pr3066" n="160.25 (524.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4838">
            <lem wit="A Cent">or</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and</rdg>
          </app>
six dollars a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3067"/>
night,—

          <app from="pr3067" n="160.25 (524.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4839">
            <lem wit="MS1b">night,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
night

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
—

            </rdg>
          </app>
ten cents a head, children and niggers free—and business

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3068"/>
a growin’,

          <app from="pr3068" n="160.26 (524.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4840">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a growin’,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a growin’</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-growin’</rdg>
          </app>
all the time; when somehow or another a little report got around, last night, that I had a way of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3069"/>
puttin’

          <app from="pr3069" n="160.28 (524.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4841">
            <lem wit="A Cent">puttin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">putting</rdg>
          </app>
in my time with a private jug, on the sly. A nigger rousted me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3070"/>
out,

          <app from="pr3070" n="160.29 (524.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la4842">
            <lem wit="MS1b">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3071"/>
mornin’

          <app from="pr3071" n="160.29 (524.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4843">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mornin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">morning</rdg>
          </app>
, and told me the people was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3072"/>
getherin’

          <app from="pr3072" n="160.29 (525.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4844">
            <lem wit="A Cent">getherin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">gathering</rdg>
          </app>
on the quiet, with their dogs and horses, and they’d be along pretty soon and give me ’bout

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3073"/>
half an

          <app from="pr3073" n="160.31 (525.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4845">
            <lem wit="A Cent">half an</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a half</rdg>
          </app>
hour’s start, and then run me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3074"/>
down,

          <app from="pr3074" n="160.31 (525.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4846">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">down,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
down

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
if they could; and if they got me

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0004"/>
they’d tar and feather me and ride me on a rail

          <ptr target="#as0168" type="an" xml:id="vs0004"/>
, sure. I didn’t wait for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3075"/>
no

          <app from="pr3075" n="160.33 (525.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4847">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4848">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
breakfast—I warn’t hungry.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39374">
“Old man,” says the young one, “I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3076"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1668"/>
reckon

          <ptr target="#l11336" type="alt" xml:id="te1668"/>
          <app from="pr3076" n="160.34 (525.15)" type="e" xml:id="la4849">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reckon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">fancy</rdg>
          </app>
we might double-team it together; what do you think?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39386">“I ain’t undisposed. What’s your line—mainly?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39388">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0005"/>
Jour

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3077"/>
printer,

          <app from="pr3077" n="160.37 (526.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4850">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">printer,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
printer

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
by trade

          <ptr target="#as0169" type="an" xml:id="vs0005"/>
;

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0006"/>
do a little in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1669"/>
patent

          <ptr target="#l11338" type="alt" xml:id="te1669"/>
medicines

          <ptr target="#as0170" type="an" xml:id="vs0006"/>
;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3078"/>
theatre-actor

          <app from="pr3078" n="160.37–38 (526.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4851">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">theatre-actor</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">theater-actor</rdg>
          </app>
—tragedy, you know; take a turn at

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0007"/>
mesmerism and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1670"/>
phrenology

          <ptr target="#l11340" type="alt" xml:id="te1670"/>
          <ptr target="#as0171" type="an" xml:id="vs0007"/>
when there’s a chance; teach

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0008"/>
singing-geography school

          <ptr target="#as0172" type="an" xml:id="vs0008"/>
for a

          <pb n="161" xml:id="pb0161"/>
change; sling a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3079"/>
lecture,

          <app from="pr3079" n="161.1 (526.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4852">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">lecture,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
lecture

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3080"/>
sometimes—O

          <app from="pr3080" n="161.1 (526.15–527.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4853">
            <lem wit="MS1b">sometimes—O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sometimes—oh</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sometimes. Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, I do lots of things—most anything that comes handy, so it ain’t work. What’s your lay?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39452">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1671"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3081"/>
I’ve

          <app from="pr3081" n="161.3 (527.6–529.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4854">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Gospil-work, mainly—most any kind of gospil work: boosting revivals along, or getting ’em up; working camp meetings; ‘occupying’ for a preacher that wants to take a week’s rest; and missionarying. Thar’s more money in missionarying than the others; folks will plank out cash for the heathen mighty free, if you only locate your heathen fur enough off. I’ve took in as much as seventeen dollars at one grist for the pore benighted Goojoos—invented ’em myself—located ’em away up jest back of the north pole. Seeing that that worked so good, I kind of strained myself, next time, and located some in a comet, expecting to jest simply bust the community—but it warn’t a go. They wouldn’t ante a red—and I come mighty near getting ducked, too. I’ve</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11342" type="alt" xml:id="te1671"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1672"/>
done

          <ptr target="#l11344" type="alt" xml:id="te1672"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3082"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr3082" n="161.3 (529.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4855">
            <lem wit="A Cent">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
in the doctoring

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3083"/>
way,

          <app from="pr3083" n="161.3 (529.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4856">
            <lem wit="MS1b">way,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
way

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in my time.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3084"/>
Layin’ on o’

          <app from="pr3084" n="161.3–4 (529.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4857">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Layin’ on o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Laying on of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1673"/>
hands

          <ptr target="#l11346" type="alt" xml:id="te1673"/>
is my best holt—for cancer, and paralysis, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3085"/>
sich

          <app from="pr3085" n="161.4 (529.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4858">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sich</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">such</rdg>
          </app>
things; and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3086"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr3086" n="161.5 (529.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4859">
            <lem wit="A Cent">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">can</rdg>
          </app>
tell a fortune pretty good, when I’ve got somebody along to find out the facts for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3087"/>
me. Preachin’s my line, too; and workin’ camp-meetin’s; and missionaryin’ around.

          <app from="pr3087" n="161.6–7 (530.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4860">
            <lem wit="A Cent">me. Preachin’s . . . around.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">me.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39520">
Nobody never said anything for a while; then the young man hove a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3088"/>
sigh

          <app from="pr3088" n="161.9 (530.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4861">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sigh</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">deep sigh</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3089"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3089" n="161.9 (530.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4862">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39537">“Alas!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39539">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3090"/>
What ’re

          <app from="pr3090" n="161.11 (530.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4863">
            <lem wit="A">What ’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">What are</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">What’re</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3091"/>
alassin’

          <app from="pr3091" n="161.11 (530.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4864">
            <lem wit="A Cent">alassin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">alassing</rdg>
          </app>
about?” says the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3092"/>
bald-head

          <app from="pr3092" n="161.11 (530.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4865">
            <lem wit="MS1b">bald-head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">baldhead</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39568">
“To

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3093"/>
think

          <app from="pr3093" n="161.12 (530.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4866">
            <lem wit="A Cent">think</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">think that</rdg>
          </app>
I should

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1674"/>
have

          <ptr target="#l11348" type="alt" xml:id="te1674"/>
lived to be leading such

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1675"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l11350" type="alt" xml:id="te1675"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3094"/>
life

          <app from="pr3094" n="161.12 (530.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4867">
            <lem wit="MS1b">life</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">life,</rdg>
          </app>
and be degraded down into such

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3095"/>
company.” And

          <app from="pr3095" n="161.13 (530.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la4868">
            <lem wit="A Cent">company.” And</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
company.”—

              <lb/>
And

            </rdg>
          </app>
he begun to wipe the corner of his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1676"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3096"/>
eye

          <app from="pr3096" n="161.14 (531.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4869">
            <lem wit="A Cent">eye</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">left eye</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11352" type="alt" xml:id="te1676"/>
with a rag.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39615">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3097"/>
Dern your skin, ain’t

          <app from="pr3097" n="161.15 (531.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4870">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Dern your skin, ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
the company good enough for you?” says the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3098"/>
bald-head,

          <app from="pr3098" n="161.16 (531.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4871">
            <lem wit="C">bald-head,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">bad-head</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
bald-

              <lb/>
head,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">baldhead,</rdg>
          </app>
pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3099"/>
pert

          <app from="pr3099" n="161.16 (531.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4872">
            <lem wit="A Cent">pert</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">peart</rdg>
          </app>
and uppish.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39648">
“Yes, it

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
good enough for me; it’s as good as I deserve; for who fetched me so low, when I was so high?

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1677"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3100"/>
did

          <app from="pr3100" n="161.18 (531.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la4873">
            <lem wit="A Cent">did</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">did it,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11354" type="alt" xml:id="te1677"/>
myself. I don’t blame

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
, gentlemen—far from it; I don’t blame

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1678"/>
anybody

          <ptr target="#l11356" type="alt" xml:id="te1678"/>
. I deserve it all. Let the cold world do its worst;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3101"/>
one thing

          <app from="pr3101" n="161.20 (532.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4874">
            <lem wit="A Cent">one thing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">one I thing</rdg>
          </app>
I know—there’s a grave

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1679"/>
somewhere

          <ptr target="#l11358" type="alt" xml:id="te1679"/>
for me. The world may go on just as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3102"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr3102" n="161.21 (532.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4875">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">its</rdg>
          </app>
always done, and take everything from me—loved ones, property, everything—but it can’t take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3103"/>
that

          <app from="pr3103" n="161.23 (532.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4876">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. Some day I’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1680"/>
lie

          <ptr target="#l11360" type="alt" xml:id="te1680"/>
down in it and forget it all, and my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1681"/>
poor

          <ptr target="#l11362" type="alt" xml:id="te1681"/>
broken heart will be at rest.”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1682"/>
He went on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3104"/>
a wiping

          <app from="pr3104" n="161.24 (532.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4877">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a wiping</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">a-wiping</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l11364" type="alt" xml:id="te1682"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39723">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3105"/>
Drot

          <app from="pr3105" n="161.25 (533.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4878">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Drot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">Dang</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
your pore broken heart,” says the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3106"/>
bald-head

          <app from="pr3106" n="161.25 (533.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la4879">
            <lem wit="MS1b">bald-head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">baldhead</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
bald-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
; “what are you heaving your pore broken heart at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3107"/>
          <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
,

          <app from="pr3107" n="161.26 (533.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4880">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3108"/>
f’r

          <app from="pr3108" n="161.26 (533.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4881">
            <lem wit="A Cent">f’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">for</rdg>
          </app>
?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3109"/>
          <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
          <app from="pr3109" n="161.26 (533.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4882">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">We</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
hain’t done nothing.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39779">
“No, I know you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1683"/>
haven’t.

          <ptr target="#l11366" type="alt" xml:id="te1683"/>
I ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3110"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1684"/>
blaming

          <ptr target="#l11368" type="alt" xml:id="te1684"/>
you

          <app from="pr3110" n="161.27 (533.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4883">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blaming you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
blaming

              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, gentlemen. I brought myself down—yes, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1685"/>
did

          <ptr target="#l11370" type="alt" xml:id="te1685"/>
it myself. It’s right I should suffer—perfectly right—I don’t make

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1686"/>
any

          <ptr target="#l11372" type="alt" xml:id="te1686"/>
moan.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39807">
“Brought you down from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3111"/>
whar? Whar

          <app from="pr3111" n="161.30 (534.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4884">
            <lem wit="A Cent">whar? Whar</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">whar? Whar</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
was you brought down from?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39818">
“Ah, you would not believe me; the world never believes—let it pass—’tis no matter. The secret of my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3112"/>
birth—

          <app from="pr3112" n="161.33 (534.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4885">
            <lem wit="MS1b">birth—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">birth——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39829">
“The secret of your birth? Do you mean to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3113"/>
say—

          <app from="pr3113" n="161.34 (534.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4886">
            <lem wit="MS1b">say—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">say——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39839">
“Gentlemen,” says the young man, very solemn, “I will reveal it to you, for I feel I may have confidence in you. By rights

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0009"/>
I am a duke!

          <ptr target="#as0173" type="an" xml:id="vs0009"/>
”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y16201">
          <graphic url="y16201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3123"/>
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">by rights i am a duke!</hi>
”

            <app from="pr3123" n="162 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la4897">
              <lem wit="A">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">by rights i am a duke</hi>
!”

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1b">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4898">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">i am the rightful duke of bridgewater</hi>
.”

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39866">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3114"/>
Jim’s eyes bugged out when he heard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="re6138"/>
that;

          <app from="re6138" n="161.38" type="hc" xml:id="ra4890">
            <lem wit="A">that;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">that,</rdg>
          </app>
and I reckon mine did, too. Then the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3116"/>
bald-head

          <app from="pr3116" n="161.39" type="hc" xml:id="la4890">
            <lem wit="C">bald-head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
bald-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
says:

          <app from="pr3114" n="161.38–39 (535.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4887">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Jim’s . . . says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4888">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
“No!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3117"/>
You

          <app from="pr3117" n="161.39 (535.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4891">
            <lem wit="MS1b">You</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">you</rdg>
          </app>
can’t mean

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3118"/>
it?

          <app from="pr3118" n="161.39 (535.8)" type="e" xml:id="la4892">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">it.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39911">
          <pb n="162" xml:id="pb0162"/>
“Yes. My

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1687"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3119"/>
great-grandfather

          <app from="pr3119" n="162.1 (535.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4893">
            <lem wit="A Cent">great-grandfather</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
great-grand-

              <lb/>
father

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11374" type="alt" xml:id="te1687"/>
,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0010"/>
eldest son of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3120"/>
duke

          <app from="pr3120" n="162.1 (535.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4894">
            <lem wit="MS1b">duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Duke</rdg>
          </app>
of Bridgewater, fled to this country about the end of the last century, to breathe the pure air of freedom; married here, and died, leaving a son, his own father dying about the same time. The second son of the late duke seized the title and estates—the infant

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3121"/>
real

          <app from="pr3121" n="162.5 (536.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4895">
            <lem wit="A Cent">real</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">real</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
duke was ignored. I am the lineal descendant of that infant—I am the rightful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3122"/>
duke

          <app from="pr3122" n="162.6 (536.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4896">
            <lem wit="MS1b">duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Duke</rdg>
          </app>
of

          <ptr target="#as0174" type="an" xml:id="vs0010"/>
Bridgewater; and here am I,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1688"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3124"/>
forlorn

          <app from="pr3124" n="162.7 (536.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4899">
            <lem wit="A Cent">forlorn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">poor, forlorn</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11376" type="alt" xml:id="te1688"/>
, torn from my high estate, hunted of men,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1689"/>
despised

          <ptr target="#l11378" type="alt" xml:id="te1689"/>
by the cold world, ragged, worn, heart-broken, and degraded to the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1690"/>
companionship

          <ptr target="#l11380" type="alt" xml:id="te1690"/>
of felons on a raft!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e39976">
Jim pitied him ever so much, and so did I. We tried to comfort him, but he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3125"/>
said

          <app from="pr3125" n="162.11 (537.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la4900">
            <lem wit="MS1b,Pr,Aa Can,Cent">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="Ab">d</rdg>
          </app>
it warn’t much use, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3126"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr3126" n="162.11 (537.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4901">
            <lem wit="A Cent">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
be much comforted; said if we was a mind to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3127"/>
acknowledge

          <app from="pr3127" n="162.12 (537.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4902">
            <lem wit="A Cent">acknowledge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">acknowledge</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
him,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3128"/>
that

          <app from="pr3128" n="162.12 (537.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4903">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that that</rdg>
          </app>
would do him more good than most anything else; so we said we would, if he would tell us how. He said we ought to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3129"/>
bow,

          <app from="pr3129" n="162.14 (538.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4904">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">bow,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
bow

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
when we spoke to him, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3130"/>
say

          <app from="pr3130" n="162.14 (538.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4905">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">say</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">say,</rdg>
          </app>
“Your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3132"/>
Grace

          <app from="pr3132" n="162.15 (538.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4907">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Grace</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Grace,</rdg>
          </app>
” or “My Lord,” or “Your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3131"/>
Lordship

          <app from="pr3131" n="162.15 (538.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4906">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Lordship</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Lordship,</rdg>
          </app>
”—and he wouldn’t mind it if we called him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1691"/>
plain

          <ptr target="#l11382" type="alt" xml:id="te1691"/>
“Bridgewater,” which he said was a title, anyway, and not a name; and one of us ought to wait on him at dinner, and do any little thing for him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3133"/>
he

          <app from="pr3133" n="162.18 (539.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4908">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that he</rdg>
          </app>
wanted done.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40059">
          <pb n="163" xml:id="pb0163"/>
Well, that was all easy, so we done it. All through dinner Jim stood around and waited on him, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3134"/>
says

          <app from="pr3134" n="163.2 (539.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4909">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">says,</rdg>
          </app>
“Will

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1692"/>
yo’

          <ptr target="#l11384" type="alt" xml:id="te1692"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3135"/>
grace

          <app from="pr3135" n="163.2 (539.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4910">
            <lem wit="MS1b">grace</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Grace</rdg>
          </app>
have some o’ dis, or some o’ dat?” and so on, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1693"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l11386" type="alt" xml:id="te1693"/>
body could see it was mighty pleasing to him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40086">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1694"/>
But

          <ptr target="#l11388" type="alt" xml:id="te1694"/>
the old man got pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3136"/>
silent,

          <app from="pr3136" n="163.5 (540.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4911">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">silent,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
silent

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3137"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr3137" n="163.5 (540.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4912">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
—didn’t have much to say, and didn’t look pretty comfortable over all that petting that was going on around that duke. He seemed to have something on his mind. So, along in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3138"/>
afternoon

          <app from="pr3138" n="163.8 (540.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la4913">
            <lem wit="Cent">afternoon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A">
after-

              <lb/>
noon

            </rdg>
          </app>
, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3139"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3139" n="163.8 (540.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4914">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40124">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3140"/>
Looky here

          <app from="pr3140" n="163.9 (540.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4915">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Looky here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Look-a-here</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0011"/>
Bilgewater,

          <ptr target="#as0175" type="an" xml:id="vs0011"/>
” he says, “I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3141"/>
nation

          <app from="pr3141" n="163.9 (540.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4916">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">nation</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’nation</rdg>
          </app>
sorry for you, but you ain’t the only person that’s had troubles like that.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40147">“No?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40149">
“No,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3142"/>
you ain’t

          <app from="pr3142" n="163.12 (541.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4917">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
you

              <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. You ain’t the only person that’s ben snaked down wrongfully out’n a high place.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40162">“Alas!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40164">
“No, you ain’t the only person that’s had a secret of his birth.”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3143"/>
And

          <app from="pr3143" n="163.16 (541.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4918">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4919">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
And

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">[¶] And</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3144"/>
by jings,

          <app from="pr3144" n="163.16 (541.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4920">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">by jings,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4921">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
begins to cry.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40188">“Hold! What do you mean?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40190">
“Bilgewater,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3145"/>
kin

          <app from="pr3145" n="163.18 (542.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4922">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">can</rdg>
          </app>
I trust you?” says the old man, still sort of sobbing.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40200">
“To the bitter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3146"/>
death!

          <app from="pr3146" n="163.20 (542.6–10)" type="e" xml:id="la4923">
            <lem wit="A Cent">death!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">death! Pour your secret into this breast—I will die ere it shall be torn from me.</rdg>
          </app>
” He took the old man by the hand and squeezed it, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3147"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1695"/>
says,

          <ptr target="#l11390" type="alt" xml:id="te1695"/>
—

          <app from="pr3147" n="163.21 (542.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4924">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3148"/>
The

          <app from="pr3148" n="163.21 (542.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4925">
            <lem wit="A Cent">The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the</rdg>
          </app>
secret of your being: speak!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40232">“Bilgewater, I am the late Dauphin!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40234">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3149"/>
You bet you Jim and me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3150"/>
stared,

          <app from="pr3150" n="163.23 (544.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4928">
            <lem wit="A">stared,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
stared

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
this time. Then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3151"/>
the duke

          <app from="pr3151" n="163.23 (544.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4929">
            <lem wit="Pr, A, Cent">the duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="Pfs1">Baldy</rdg>
          </app>
says:

          <app from="pr3149" n="163.23 (544.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4926">
            <lem wit="A Cent">You . . . says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4927">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40259">
“You are

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3152"/>
what

          <app from="pr3152" n="163.24 (544.2)" type="e" xml:id="la4930">
            <lem wit="A Cent">what</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">what</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40270">
“Yes, my friend, it is too true—your eyes is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3153"/>
lookin’

          <app from="pr3153" n="163.25 (544.5)" type="e" xml:id="la4931">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lookin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">looking</rdg>
          </app>
at this very moment on the pore disappeared Dauphin, Looy the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1696"/>
Seventeen

          <ptr target="#l11392" type="alt" xml:id="te1696"/>
, son of Looy the Sixteen and Marry Antonette.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40284">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3154"/>
You!

          <app from="pr3154" n="163.28 (544.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4932">
            <lem wit="A Cent">You!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">You!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
At your age! No!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3155"/>
you

          <app from="pr3155" n="163.28 (544.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4933">
            <lem wit="MS1b">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">You</rdg>
          </app>
mean you’re the late Charlemagne; you must be six or seven hundred years old, at the very least.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40303">
“Trouble has done it, Bilgewater, trouble has done it; trouble has brung these gray hairs and this

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1697"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3156"/>
premature

          <app from="pr3156" n="163.31 (545.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la4934">
            <lem wit="A Cent">premature</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">primmature</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11393" type="alt" xml:id="te1697"/>
balditude. Yes, gentlemen, you see before you, in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1698"/>
blue

          <ptr target="#l11394" type="alt" xml:id="te1698"/>
jeans and misery, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3157"/>
wanderin’

          <app from="pr3157" n="163.32 (545.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4935">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wanderin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wandering</rdg>
          </app>
, exiled,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3158"/>
trampled-on

          <app from="pr3158" n="163.33 (545.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la4936">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">trampled-on</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">trampled-on,</rdg>
          </app>
and sufferin’ rightful King of France.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y16401">
          <graphic url="y16401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">
i am the late

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3165"/>
dauphin!

            </hi>
            <app from="pr3165" n="164 caption" type="e" xml:id="la4943">
              <lem wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">dauphin</hi>
!

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS1b">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4944">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">dauphin</hi>
.

              </rdg>
            </app>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40357">
Well, he cried and took on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3159"/>
so,

          <app from="pr3159" n="163.34 (546.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la4937">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that me and Jim didn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3160"/>
know hardly

          <app from="pr3160" n="163.34 (546.3)" type="e" xml:id="la4938">
            <lem wit="A Cent">know hardly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">hardly know</rdg>
          </app>
what to do, we was so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3161"/>
sorry—and so glad and proud we’d got him with us, too

          <app from="pr3161" n="163.35–36 (546.4)" type="e" xml:id="la4939">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sorry—and . . . too</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sorry</rdg>
          </app>
. So we set in, like we done before

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1699"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3162"/>
with the duke

          <app from="pr3162" n="163.36 (546.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4940">
            <lem wit="A Cent">with the duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">for the duke</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l11395" type="alt" xml:id="te1699"/>
and tried to comfort

          <hi rend="italic">him.</hi>
But he said it warn’t no use, nothing but to be dead and done with it all could do him any good; though he said it often made him feel easier and better for a while if people treated

          <pb n="164" xml:id="pb0164"/>
him according to his rights, and got down on one knee to speak to him, and always called him “Your Majesty,”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1700"/>
and waited

          <ptr target="#l11396" type="alt" xml:id="te1700"/>
on him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1701"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3163"/>
first

          <ptr target="#l11397" type="alt" xml:id="te1701"/>
,

          <app from="pr3163" n="164.2 (547.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4941">
            <lem wit="MS1b">first,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
first

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at meals, and didn’t set down in his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1702"/>
presence

          <ptr target="#l11398" type="alt" xml:id="te1702"/>
till he asked them. So Jim and me set to majestying him, and doing this and that and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3164"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr3164" n="164.5 (547.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4942">
            <lem wit="A Cent">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">t’other thing</rdg>
          </app>
for him, and standing up till he told us we might set down. This done him heaps of good, and so he got cheerful and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3166"/>
comfortable.

          <app from="pr3166" n="164.6 (548.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4945">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">comfortable.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
comfortable

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1703"/>
But the

          <ptr target="#l11399" type="alt" xml:id="te1703"/>
duke kind of soured on him, and didn’t look a bit satisfied with the way things was going;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1704"/>
still,

          <ptr target="#l11400" type="alt" xml:id="te1704"/>
the king acted real friendly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3167"/>
towards

          <app from="pr3167" n="164.9 (548.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4946">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">toward</rdg>
          </app>
him, and said the duke’s great-grandfather

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1705"/>
and all

          <ptr target="#l11401" type="alt" xml:id="te1705"/>
the other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3168"/>
dukes

          <app from="pr3168" n="164.10 (548.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la4947">
            <lem wit="MS1b">dukes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Dukes</rdg>
          </app>
of Bilgewater was a good deal thought of by

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1706"/>
          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11402" type="alt" xml:id="te1706"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3169"/>
father

          <app from="pr3169" n="164.10 (548.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la4948">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">father</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">father,</rdg>
          </app>
and was allowed to come to the palace considerable; but the duke staid huffy a good while, till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3170"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr3170" n="164.12 (549.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4949">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3171"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3171" n="164.12 (549.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la4950">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40494">
“Like as not we got to be together a blamed long time, on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3172"/>
thish-yer

          <app from="pr3172" n="164.13–14 (549.7)" type="e" xml:id="la4951">
            <lem wit="C">thish-yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">this</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">this h-yer</rdg>
          </app>
raft, Bilgewater, and so what’s the use

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3173"/>
o’ your bein’

          <app from="pr3173" n="164.14 (549.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4952">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’ your bein’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of our being</rdg>
          </app>
sour?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3174"/>
it’ll

          <app from="pr3174" n="164.14 (549.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4953">
            <lem wit="MS1b">it’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">It’ll</rdg>
          </app>
only make things

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3175"/>
oncomfortable

          <app from="pr3175" n="164.15 (549.11)" type="e" xml:id="la4954">
            <lem wit="A Cent">oncomfortable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">uncomfortable</rdg>
          </app>
. It ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3176"/>
my

          <app from="pr3176" n="164.15 (549.12)" type="e" xml:id="la4955">
            <lem wit="A Cent">my</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">my</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
fault I warn’t born a duke, it ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3177"/>
your

          <app from="pr3177" n="164.16 (549.14)" type="e" xml:id="la4956">
            <lem wit="A Cent">your</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">your</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
fault you warn’t born a king—so what’s the use to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3178"/>
worry?

          <app from="pr3178" n="164.17 (549.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4957">
            <lem wit="A Cent">worry?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">worry.</rdg>
          </app>
Make the best

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3179"/>
o’

          <app from="pr3179" n="164.17 (550.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4958">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of</rdg>
          </app>
things the way you find ’em, says I—

          <pb n="165" xml:id="pb0165"/>
that’s my motto. This ain’t no bad thing that we’ve struck here—plenty grub and an easy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3180"/>
life—come

          <app from="pr3180" n="165.2 (550.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4959">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">life—come</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">life. Come</rdg>
          </app>
, give us your hand,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3181"/>
duke

          <app from="pr3181" n="165.2 (550.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4960">
            <lem wit="MS1b">duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Duke</rdg>
          </app>
, and less all be friends.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40585">
The duke done it, and Jim and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1707"/>
me

          <ptr target="#l11403" type="alt" xml:id="te1707"/>
was pretty glad to see it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3182"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1708"/>
It

          <ptr target="#l11404" type="alt" xml:id="te1708"/>
took away all the uncomfortableness, and we felt mighty good over it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1709"/>
because

          <ptr target="#l11405" type="alt" xml:id="te1709"/>
it would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3183"/>
a

          <app from="pr3183" n="165.6 (551.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4963">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">have</rdg>
          </app>
been a miserable business to have any unfriendliness on the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1710"/>
raft;

          <ptr target="#l11406" type="alt" xml:id="te1710"/>
for what you want, above all things, on a raft, is for everybody to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1711"/>
be

          <ptr target="#l11407" type="alt" xml:id="te1711"/>
satisfied, and feel right and kind towards the others.

          <app from="pr3182" n="165.4–8 (550.12–551.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4961">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">It . . . others.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4962">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40624">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3184"/>
It didn’t take me long to make up my mind that these liars warn’t no kings nor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3185"/>
dukes,

          <app from="pr3185" n="165.10" type="hc" xml:id="la4966">
            <lem wit="A">dukes,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
dukes

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at all, but just low-down humbugs and frauds. But I never said nothing, never let on; kept it to myself; it’s the best way; then you don’t have no quarrels, and don’t get into no trouble. If they wanted us to call them kings and dukes, I hadn’t no objections,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3186"/>
long

          <app from="pr3186" n="165.14" type="hc" xml:id="la4967">
            <lem wit="C">long</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">’long</rdg>
          </app>
as it would keep peace in the family; and it warn’t no use to tell Jim, so I didn’t tell him.

          <app from="pr3184" n="165.9–15 (551.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4964">
            <lem wit="A Cent">It . . . him.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4965">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3187"/>
If I never learnt nothing else out of pap, I learnt that the best way to get along with his kind of people is to let them have their own way.

          <app from="pr3187" n="165.15–17" type="e" xml:id="la4968">
            <lem wit="A">If . . . way.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4969">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40658">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y16501">
            <graphic url="y16501.jpg"/>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0346">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XX.</head>
        <pb n="166" xml:id="pb0166"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40664">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y16601">
            <graphic url="y16601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3188"/>
Chapter XX

              <app from="pr3188" n="166 title (552 title)" type="e" xml:id="la4970">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XX</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">CHAP.</rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4971">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1661">
            <graphic url="hf1661.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3198"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">on the raft</hi>
              <app from="pr3198" n="166 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la4981">
                <lem wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">on the raft</hi>
.

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de4982">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">the raft</hi>
.

                </rdg>
              </app>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e40695">
          <hi rend="smallcaps"> asked us</hi>
considerable many questions; wanted to know

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1712"/>
what

          <ptr target="#l11408" type="alt" xml:id="te1712"/>
we covered up the raft that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3189"/>
way,

          <app from="pr3189" n="166.4 (552.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4972">
            <lem wit="MS1b">way,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
way

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for, and laid by in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3190"/>
daytime

          <app from="pr3190" n="166.4–5 (552.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4973">
            <lem wit="MS1b">daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-time</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
day-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3191"/>
instead

          <app from="pr3191" n="166.5 (552.6)" type="e" xml:id="la4974">
            <lem wit="A Cent">instead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">’stead</rdg>
          </app>
of running—was Jim a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3192"/>
runaway

          <app from="pr3192" n="166.6 (552.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la4975">
            <lem wit="A Cent">runaway</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
run-

              <lb/>
away

            </rdg>
          </app>
nigger? Says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3193"/>
I—

          <app from="pr3193" n="166.6 (552.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4976">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">I—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">I:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40749">
“Goodness sakes, would a runaway nigger run

          <hi rend="italic">south?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40754">
No, they allowed he wouldn’t. I had to account for things some

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1713"/>
way, so

          <ptr target="#l11409" type="alt" xml:id="te1713"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3194"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3194" n="166.11 (553.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la4977">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40767">
“My folks was living in

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0012"/>
Pike

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3195"/>
county

          <app from="pr3195" n="166.13 (553.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4978">
            <lem wit="MS1b">county</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">County</rdg>
          </app>
, in Missouri,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3196"/>
where

          <app from="pr3196" n="166.13 (553.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4979">
            <lem wit="A Cent">where</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wher’</rdg>
          </app>
I was born, and they all died off but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3197"/>
me, and pa,

          <app from="pr3197" n="166.15 (553.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la4980">
            <lem wit="MS1b">me, and pa,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
and pa

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and my brother Ike

          <ptr target="#as0176" type="an" xml:id="vs0012"/>
. Pa, he ’lowed he’d break up and go down and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1714"/>
live

          <ptr target="#l11410" type="alt" xml:id="te1714"/>
with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3199"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr3199" n="166.17 (553.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4983">
            <lem wit="MS1b">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Ben, who’s got a little one-horse

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1715"/>
place

          <ptr target="#l11411" type="alt" xml:id="te1715"/>
on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3200"/>
river

          <app from="pr3200" n="166.18 (554.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la4984">
            <lem wit="MS1b">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">river,</rdg>
          </app>
forty-four mile below Orleans. Pa was pretty poor, and had some debts; so when he’d squared up there warn’t nothing left but sixteen dollars and our nigger, Jim. That warn’t enough to take us fourteen hundred mile, deck passage nor no other way. Well, when the river rose, pa had a streak of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3201"/>
luck,

          <app from="pr3201" n="166.22 (554.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la4985">
            <lem wit="MS1b">luck,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
luck

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
one day; he ketched this piece of a raft; so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3202"/>
we

          <app from="pr3202" n="166.23 (555.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4986">
            <lem wit="A Cent">we</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">he</rdg>
          </app>
reckoned we’d go down to Orleans on it. Pa’s luck didn’t hold out; a steamboat run over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1716"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3203"/>
forrard

          <app from="pr3203" n="166.24 (555.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4987">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">forrard</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">forward</rdg>
          </app>
corner of

          <ptr target="#l11412" type="alt" xml:id="te1716"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3204"/>
raft

          <app from="pr3204" n="166.25 (555.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4988">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">raft</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">raft,</rdg>
          </app>
one night,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1717"/>
and we

          <ptr target="#l11413" type="alt" xml:id="te1717"/>
all went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1718"/>
overboard and dove

          <ptr target="#l11414" type="alt" xml:id="te1718"/>
under the wheel; Jim and me come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3205"/>
up,

          <app from="pr3205" n="166.26 (555.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la4989">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all right, but pa was drunk, and Ike was only four

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3206"/>
years

          <app from="pr3206" n="166.27 (555.10)" type="e" xml:id="la4990">
            <lem wit="A Cent">years</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">year</rdg>
          </app>
old, so they never come up no more. Well, for the next day or two we had considerable trouble, because people was always coming out in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3207"/>
skiffs

          <app from="pr3207" n="166.29 (555.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4991">
            <lem wit="A Cent">skiffs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">skifts</rdg>
          </app>
and trying to take Jim away from me, saying they believed he was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3208"/>
runaway

          <app from="pr3208" n="166.30 (556.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la4992">
            <lem wit="A Cent">runaway</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
runa-

              <lb/>
way

            </rdg>
          </app>
nigger. We don’t run

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3209"/>
daytimes

          <app from="pr3209" n="166.30 (556.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la4993">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">daytimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-times</rdg>
          </app>
no more, now; nights they don’t bother us.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40913">
The duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3210"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3210" n="166.32 (556.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la4994">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40922">
          <pb n="167" xml:id="pb0167"/>
“Leave me alone to cipher out a way

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3211"/>
so

          <app from="pr3211" n="167.1 (556.9)" type="e" xml:id="la4995">
            <lem wit="A Cent">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">so that</rdg>
          </app>
we can run in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3212"/>
day time

          <app from="pr3212" n="167.1–2 (556.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la4996">
            <lem wit="MS1b">day time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-time</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">daytime</rdg>
          </app>
if we want to. I’ll think the thing over—I’ll invent a plan

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3213"/>
that’ll

          <app from="pr3213" n="167.2 (556.13)" type="e" xml:id="la4997">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that will</rdg>
          </app>
fix

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1719"/>
it.

          <ptr target="#l11415" type="alt" xml:id="te1719"/>
We’ll let it alone for to-day, because of course we don’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3214"/>
want

          <app from="pr3214" n="167.3 (556.16)" type="e" xml:id="la4998">
            <lem wit="A Cent">want</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to go by that town

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3215"/>
yonder

          <app from="pr3215" n="167.4 (557.1)" type="e" xml:id="la4999">
            <lem wit="A Cent">yonder</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">down yonder</rdg>
          </app>
in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3216"/>
daylight

          <app from="pr3216" n="167.4 (557.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la5000">
            <lem wit="Cent">daylight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A">
day-

              <lb/>
light

            </rdg>
          </app>
—it mightn’t be healthy.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e40984">
Towards night it begun to darken up and look like rain; the heat lightning was squirting around, low down in the sky, and the leaves was beginning to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3217"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1720"/>
shiver

          <ptr target="#l11416" type="alt" xml:id="te1720"/>
—

          <app from="pr3217" n="167.7 (557.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5001">
            <lem wit="A">shiver—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">shiver and moan—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">shiver;</rdg>
          </app>
it was going to be pretty ugly, it was easy to see that. So the duke and the king went to overhauling our wigwam, to see what the beds was like. My bed was a straw tick—better than Jim’s, which was a corn-shuck tick; there’s always cobs around about in a shuck tick, and they poke into you and hurt; and when you roll over, the dry shucks sound like you was rolling over in a pile of dead

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3218"/>
leaves

          <app from="pr3218" n="167.13 (558.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5002">
            <lem wit="A Cent">leaves</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">autumn leaves</rdg>
          </app>
; it makes such a rustling that you wake up. Well, the duke allowed he would take my bed; but the king allowed he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3219"/>
wouldn’t

          <app from="pr3219" n="167.15 (559.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5003">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">wouldn’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3220"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3220" n="167.15 (559.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5004">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41024">
“I should

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3221"/>
a reckoned the difference in rank would a sejested

          <app from="pr3221" n="167.16 (559.3–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5005">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">a reckoned . . . a sejested</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ reckoned . . . ’a’ sejested</rdg>
          </app>
to you that a corn-shuck bed warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3222"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1721"/>
jest

          <ptr target="#l11417" type="alt" xml:id="te1721"/>
          <app from="pr3222" n="167.17 (559.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5006">
            <lem wit="MS1b">jest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">just</rdg>
          </app>
fitten for me to sleep on. Your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3223"/>
grace’ll

          <app from="pr3223" n="167.18 (559.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5007">
            <lem wit="MS1b">grace’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Grace’ll</rdg>
          </app>
take the shuck bed yourself.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41054">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1722"/>
Jim

          <ptr target="#l11418" type="alt" xml:id="te1722"/>
and me was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3224"/>
in a sweat again, for a minute, being

          <app from="pr3224" n="167.19 (559.11–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5008">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">in . . . being</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5009">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
afraid there was going to be some more trouble amongst them; so we was pretty glad when the duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3225"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3225" n="167.21 (560.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5010">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41075">
“ ’Tis my fate to be always ground into the mire under the iron heel of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3226"/>
oppression. Misfortune

          <app from="pr3226" n="167.23 (560.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5011">
            <lem wit="A Cent">oppression. Misfortune</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
oppression.—

              <lb/>
Misfortune

            </rdg>
          </app>
has broken my once haughty spirit; I yield, I submit; ’tis my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3227"/>
fate.

          <app from="pr3227" n="167.24 (560.9–14)" type="e" xml:id="la5012">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fate.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">fate. I accept the bitter draught, and make no moan. They that would have pitied me, alas, are long since gone down into the silent tomb.</rdg>
          </app>
I am alone in the world—let me suffer; I can bear it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41095">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0031"/>
We got away as soon as it was good and dark. The king told us to stand well out towards the middle of the river, and not show a light till we got a long ways below the town.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1723"/>
We

          <ptr target="#l11419" type="alt" xml:id="te1723"/>
come in sight of the little bunch of lights

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3228"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr3228" n="167.29 (561.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5013">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
—that was the town, you know—and slid by, about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3229"/>
a half

          <app from="pr3229" n="167.30 (561.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5014">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a half</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">half</rdg>
          </app>
a mile out, all right. When we was three-quarters of a mile below, we hoisted up our signal lantern; and about

          <ptr target="#mt0031" type="alt" xml:id="wn0031"/>
ten o’clock it come on to rain and blow and thunder and lighten like everything; so the king told us to both stay on watch till the weather got better; then him and the duke crawled into the wigwam and turned in for the night. It was my watch

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3230"/>
below,

          <app from="pr3230" n="167.35 (562.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5015">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">below,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
below

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
till twelve, but I wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3231"/>
a turned

          <app from="pr3231" n="167.35–36 (562.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5016">
            <lem wit="A">a turned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">have turned</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ turned</rdg>
          </app>
in, anyway, if I’d had a bed; because a body don’t see such a storm as that every day in the week, not by a long sight. My souls, how the wind did

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3232"/>
scream

          <app from="pr3232" n="167.38 (563.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5017">
            <lem wit="A Cent">scream</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">whistle and scream</rdg>
          </app>
along!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3233"/>
and

          <app from="pr3233" n="167.38 (563.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5018">
            <lem wit="MS1b">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">And</rdg>
          </app>
every second or two there’d

          <pb n="168" xml:id="pb0168"/>
come a glare that lit up the white-caps for a half a mile

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1724"/>
around, and

          <ptr target="#l11420" type="alt" xml:id="te1724"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3234"/>
you’d see the islands looking dusty

          <app from="pr3234" n="168.2 (563.6–12)" type="e" xml:id="la5019">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’d see the islands looking dusty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">made them look like whole armies of white worms squirming along on a march; and away beyond, you would see the dimmest kind of islands</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1725"/>
through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3235"/>
rain

          <app from="pr3235" n="168.2 (563.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5020">
            <lem wit="A Cent">rain</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sheets of rain</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11421" type="alt" xml:id="te1725"/>
, and the trees

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3236"/>
thrashing around

          <app from="pr3236" n="168.3 (563.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5021">
            <lem wit="A Cent">thrashing around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">waving and thrashing</rdg>
          </app>
in the wind; then comes a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3237"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">h-wack</hi>
!

          <app from="pr3237" n="168.3 (563.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5022">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">h-wack</hi>
!

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">h-wack!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3238"/>
bum! bum!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1726"/>
bumble-umble-um-bum-bum-bum-bum

          <ptr target="#l11422" type="alt" xml:id="te1726"/>
          <app from="pr3238" n="168.3–4 (563.17–564.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5023">
            <lem wit="C">bum! bum! bumble-umble-um-bum-bum-bum-bum</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">
bum! bum! bumble-

                <milestone unit="page"/>
umble-um-bum-bum-

                <lb/>
bum-bum

              </hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
bum! bum! bumble-umble-um-

              <lb/>
bum-bum-bum-bum

            </rdg>
          </app>
—and the thunder would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3239"/>
go

          <app from="pr3239" n="168.5 (564.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5024">
            <lem wit="A Cent">go</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">slow down and go</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3240"/>
rumbling

          <app from="pr3240" n="168.5 (564.4–7)" type="e" xml:id="la5025">
            <lem wit="A Cent">rumbling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">rumbling and tumbling down the sky, and taper off with a kind of muttering</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3241"/>
grumbling away

          <app from="pr3241" n="168.5 (564.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la5026">
            <lem wit="A Cent">grumbling away</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">grumbling, away yonder</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3242"/>
quit—

          <app from="pr3242" n="168.5 (564.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5027">
            <lem wit="A">quit—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">then die out—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">quit;</rdg>
          </app>
and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3243"/>
          <hi rend="italic">rip</hi>
          <app from="pr3243" n="168.5 (564.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5028">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">rip</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">rip</rdg>
          </app>
comes another flash and another

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3244"/>
sockdolager

          <app from="pr3244" n="168.6 (564.10–12)" type="e" xml:id="la5029">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sockdolager</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">jolting sockdolager. It was just beautiful</rdg>
          </app>
. The waves most washed me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3245"/>
off

          <app from="pr3245" n="168.7 (564.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5030">
            <lem wit="A Cent">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">off of</rdg>
          </app>
the raft, sometimes, but I hadn’t any clothes on, and didn’t mind. We didn’t have

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3246"/>
no

          <app from="pr3246" n="168.8 (564.17)" type="e" xml:id="la5031">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any</rdg>
          </app>
trouble about snags; the lightning was glaring and flittering around so constant that we could see them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1727"/>
plenty

          <ptr target="#l11423" type="alt" xml:id="te1727"/>
soon enough to throw her head this way or that and miss them.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41297">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3247"/>
I had

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0013"/>
the middle watch

          <ptr target="#as0177" type="an" xml:id="vs0013"/>
, you know, but I was pretty sleepy by that time, so Jim he said he would stand the first half of it for me; he was always mighty good, that way, Jim was. I crawled into the wigwam, but the king and the duke had their legs sprawled around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3248"/>
so

          <app from="pr3248" n="168.14 (566.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5034">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">so that</rdg>
          </app>
there warn’t no show for me; so I laid outside—I didn’t mind the rain, because it was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1728"/>
warm,

          <ptr target="#l11424" type="alt" xml:id="te1728"/>
and the waves

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3249"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr3249" n="168.16 (566.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5035">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
running so high, now. About two they come up again, though, and Jim was going to call me,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3250"/>
but he

          <app from="pr3250" n="168.18 (566.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5036">
            <lem wit="A">but he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">but</rdg>
          </app>
changed his mind because he reckoned they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3251"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr3251" n="168.18 (566.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5037">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
high enough yet to do any

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1729"/>
harm;

          <ptr target="#l11425" type="alt" xml:id="te1729"/>
but he was mistaken about that, for pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3252"/>
soon,

          <app from="pr3252" n="168.20 (567.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la5038">
            <lem wit="MS1b">soon,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
soon

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all of a sudden along comes a regular ripper, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3253"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1730"/>
washed me overboard

          <app from="pr3253" n="168.20–21 (567.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la5039">
            <lem wit="A">washed me overboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">overboard I washed</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l11426" type="alt" xml:id="te1730"/>
It most killed Jim a-laughing. He was the easiest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3254"/>
nigger

          <app from="pr3254" n="168.22 (567.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5040">
            <lem wit="A">nigger</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">fellow</rdg>
          </app>
to laugh that ever was, anyway.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41374">
I took the watch, and Jim he laid down and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3255"/>
snored

          <app from="pr3255" n="168.23 (567.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5041">
            <lem wit="A">snored</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">snoozed</rdg>
          </app>
away;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3256"/>
and

          <app from="pr3247" n="168.11–23 (565.9–567.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la5032">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">I had . . . away; and</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5033">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
by and by

          <app from="pr3256" n="168.23–24 (567.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la5042">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5043">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
and by and by

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5044">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
and by-and-by

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
[

              <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
] By and by

            </rdg>
          </app>
the storm let up for good and all; and the first

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3257"/>
cabin-light

          <app from="pr3257" n="168.24 (567.16–568.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5045">
            <lem wit="A Cent">cabin-light</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
cabin-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
light

            </rdg>
          </app>
that showed, I rousted

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3258"/>
him

          <app from="pr3258" n="168.25 (568.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5046">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">him</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Jim</rdg>
          </app>
out and we slid the raft into hiding-quarters for the day.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41431">
The king got out an old ratty deck of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3259"/>
cards,

          <app from="pr3259" n="168.27 (568.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5047">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">cards,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
cards

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1731"/>
after

          <ptr target="#l11427" type="alt" xml:id="te1731"/>
breakfast, and him and the duke played seven-up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3260"/>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1732"/>
while

          <app from="pr3260" n="168.28 (568.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5048">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l11428" type="alt" xml:id="te1732"/>
five cents a game. Then they got tired of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3261"/>
it

          <app from="pr3261" n="168.29 (568.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5049">
            <lem wit="MS1b">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">it,</rdg>
          </app>
and allowed they would “lay out a campaign,” as they called it. The duke went down into his carpet-bag and fetched up a lot of little printed bills, and read them out loud. One bill

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3262"/>
said

          <app from="pr3262" n="168.31 (569.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5050">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">said,</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3263"/>
the

          <app from="pr3263" n="168.32 (569.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5051">
            <lem wit="MS1b">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">The</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1733"/>
celebrated

          <ptr target="#l11429" type="alt" xml:id="te1733"/>
Dr. Armand de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3264"/>
Montalban,

          <app from="pr3264" n="168.32 (569.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la5052">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">Montalban,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Montalban

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1734"/>
of Paris,

          <ptr target="#l11430" type="alt" xml:id="te1734"/>
” would “lecture on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3265"/>
science of phrenology

          <app from="pr3265" n="168.33 (569.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5053">
            <lem wit="MS1b">science of phrenology</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Science of Phrenology</rdg>
          </app>
” at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3266"/>
such-and-such

          <app from="pr3266" n="168.33 (569.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5054">
            <lem wit="MS1b">such-and-such</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">such and such</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1735"/>
place, on

          <ptr target="#l11431" type="alt" xml:id="te1735"/>
the blank day of blank, at ten cents admission, and “furnish charts of character at twenty-five cents

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3267"/>
apiece.” The

          <app from="pr3267" n="168.35 (569.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5055">
            <lem wit="A Cent">apiece.” The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
apiece.”—

              <lb/>
The

            </rdg>
          </app>
duke said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3268"/>
that

          <app from="pr3268" n="168.35 (569.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5056">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that that</rdg>
          </app>
was

          <hi rend="italic">him.</hi>
In another bill he was the “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3269"/>
world-renowned

          <app from="pr3269" n="168.36 (569.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5057">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">world-renowned</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">world renowned</rdg>
          </app>
Shaksperean tragedian,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0014"/>
Garrick the Younger

          <ptr target="#as0178" type="an" xml:id="vs0014"/>
, of Drury Lane, London.” In other bills he had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3270"/>
a lot of

          <app from="pr3270" n="168.38 (570.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5058">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a lot of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5059">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3271"/>
names,

          <app from="pr3271" n="168.38 (570.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5060">
            <lem wit="MS1b">names,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
names

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and done other wonderful things, like

          <pb n="169" xml:id="pb0169"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0015"/>
finding water and gold with a “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3272"/>
divining rod

          <app from="pr3272" n="169.1 (570.7–8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5061">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">divining rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">divining-rod</rdg>
          </app>
,”

          <ptr target="#as0179" type="an" xml:id="vs0015"/>
“dissipating

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3273"/>
witch-spells

          <app from="pr3273" n="169.1–2 (570.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5062">
            <lem wit="A Cent">witch-spells</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
witch-

              <lb/>
spells

            </rdg>
          </app>
,” and so on.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3274"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr3274" n="169.2 (570.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5063">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3275"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3275" n="169.2 (570.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5064">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41610">
“But the histrionic muse is the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3276"/>
darling

          <app from="pr3276" n="169.3 (570.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5065">
            <lem wit="A Cent">darling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">darling of my soul’s devotion</rdg>
          </app>
. Have you ever trod the boards, Royalty?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41620">“No,” says the king.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41622">
“You

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3277"/>
shall, then,

          <app from="pr3277" n="169.6 (570.16–571.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5066">
            <lem wit="A Cent">shall, then,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">shall revel in that divinest of intellectual intoxications</rdg>
          </app>
before

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3278"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr3278" n="169.6 (571.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5067">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">you are</rdg>
          </app>
three days older, Fallen Grandeur,” says the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3279"/>
duke. “The

          <app from="pr3279" n="169.7 (571.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5068">
            <lem wit="A Cent">duke. “The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
duke.—

              <lb/>
“The

            </rdg>
          </app>
first good town we come to, we’ll hire a hall and do the

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0016"/>
sword-fight in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3280"/>
Richard III

          <ptr target="#as0180" type="an" xml:id="vs0016"/>
,

          <app from="pr3280" n="169.8 (571.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5069">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Richard III,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Richard III.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">‘Richard III.’</rdg>
          </app>
and the balcony scene in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3281"/>
Romeo and Juliet.

          <app from="pr3281" n="169.9 (571.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5070">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Romeo and Juliet.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">‘Romeo and Juliet.’</rdg>
          </app>
How does that strike you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41674">
“I’m in, up to the hub, for anything

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3282"/>
that will

          <app from="pr3282" n="169.10 (571.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5071">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that will</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that’ll</rdg>
          </app>
pay,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3283"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1736"/>
Bilgewater,

          <ptr target="#l11432" type="alt" xml:id="te1736"/>
          <app from="pr3283" n="169.10 (571.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5072">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Bilgewater,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Bilgewater;</rdg>
          </app>
but you see I don’t know nothing about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3284"/>
play-actn’

          <app from="pr3284" n="169.11 (572.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5073">
            <lem wit="A">play-actn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">play-acting</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">play-act’n’</rdg>
          </app>
, and hain’t ever seen much of it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3285"/>
I was too small when pap used to have ’em at the palace.

          <app from="pr3285" n="169.12 (572.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5074">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I . . . palace.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5075">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Do you reckon you can learn me?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41714">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1737"/>
“Easy!”

          <ptr target="#l11433" type="alt" xml:id="te1737"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41719">
“All right. I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3286"/>
jest

          <app from="pr3286" n="169.15 (572.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5076">
            <lem wit="MS1b">jest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">jist</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3287"/>
a-freezn’

          <app from="pr3287" n="169.15 (572.7)" type="e" xml:id="la5077">
            <lem wit="C">a-freezn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a-freezing</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
a-

              <lb/>
freezn’

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-freez’n’</rdg>
          </app>
for something fresh, anyway. Less commence, right away.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y16901">
          <graphic url="y16901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the king as juliet</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41747">
So the duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3288"/>
he

          <app from="pr3288" n="169.17 (572.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5078">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5079">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
told him all about who Romeo was, and who Juliet was, and said he was used to being Romeo, so the king could be Juliet.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41758">
“But if Juliet’s such a young gal,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3289"/>
duke

          <app from="pr3289" n="169.24 (573.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5080">
            <lem wit="MS1b">duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Duke</rdg>
          </app>
, my peeled head and my white whiskers is goin’ to look

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3290"/>
oncommon

          <app from="pr3290" n="169.27 (573.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5081">
            <lem wit="A Cent">oncommon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">uncommon</rdg>
          </app>
odd on her,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3291"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr3291" n="169.28 (573.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5082">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41785">
“No, don’t you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3292"/>
worry—

          <app from="pr3292" n="169.30 (573.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5083">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">worry—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">worry;</rdg>
          </app>
these country jakes won’t ever think of that. Besides, you know, you’ll be in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1738"/>
costume,

          <ptr target="#l11434" type="alt" xml:id="te1738"/>
and that makes all the difference in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3293"/>
world;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1739"/>
Juliet’s

          <app from="pr3293" n="169.36 (573.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5084">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">world; Juliet’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">world. Juliet’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11435" type="alt" xml:id="te1739"/>
in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3294"/>
balcony,

          <app from="pr3294" n="169.36–37 (573.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5085">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">balcony,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
balcony

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
enjoying the moonlight before she

          <pb n="170" xml:id="pb0170"/>
goes to bed, and she’s got on her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3295"/>
night-gown

          <app from="pr3295" n="170.1 (573.16–574.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5086">
            <lem wit="A Cent">night-gown</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
night-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
gown

            </rdg>
          </app>
and her ruffled night-cap.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1740"/>
Here are

          <ptr target="#l11436" type="alt" xml:id="te1740"/>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1741"/>
costumes

          <ptr target="#l11437" type="alt" xml:id="te1741"/>
for the parts.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41840">
He got out two or three curtain-calico

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3296"/>
suits

          <app from="pr3296" n="170.3 (574.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5087">
            <lem wit="MS1b">suits</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">suits,</rdg>
          </app>
which he said was meedyevil

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3297"/>
armor,

          <app from="pr3297" n="170.4 (574.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5088">
            <lem wit="MS1b">armor,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
armor

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for Richard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3298"/>
III

          <app from="pr3298" n="170.4 (574.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5089">
            <lem wit="MS1b">III</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">III.</rdg>
          </app>
and t’other chap, and a long white cotton

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3299"/>
night shirt

          <app from="pr3299" n="170.5 (574.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5090">
            <lem wit="MS1b">night shirt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">night-shirt</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1742"/>
a ruffled

          <ptr target="#l11438" type="alt" xml:id="te1742"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3300"/>
night-cap

          <app from="pr3300" n="170.5 (574.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la5091">
            <lem wit="A">night-cap</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
night-

              <lb/>
cap

            </rdg>
          </app>
to match. The king was satisfied; so the duke got out his book and read the parts over in the most splendid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3301"/>
spread-eagle

          <app from="pr3301" n="170.7 (574.16–575.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5092">
            <lem wit="A Cent">spread-eagle</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
spread-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
eagle

            </rdg>
          </app>
way, prancing around and acting at the same time, to show how it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1743"/>
had got

          <ptr target="#l11439" type="alt" xml:id="te1743"/>
to be done; then he give the book to the king and told him to get his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3302"/>
part

          <app from="pr3302" n="170.9 (575.7)" type="e" xml:id="la5093">
            <lem wit="A Cent">part</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">parts</rdg>
          </app>
by heart.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41912">
There was a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0017"/>
little one-horse town about three mile down the bend, and after dinner the duke said he had ciphered out his idea about how to run in daylight without it being

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1744"/>
dangersome

          <ptr target="#l11440" type="alt" xml:id="te1744"/>
for Jim; so he allowed he would go down to the town and fix that thing. The king allowed he would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3303"/>
go,

          <app from="pr3303" n="170.14 (576.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5094">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">go,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
go

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too, and see if he couldn’t strike something. We was out of coffee, so Jim said I better go along with them in the canoe and get some.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41928">
When we got there, there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3304"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr3304" n="170.17 (576.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5095">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
stirring; streets empty, and perfectly dead and still, like Sunday. We found a sick nigger sunning himself in a back yard, and he said everybody that warn’t too

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3305"/>
young

          <app from="pr3305" n="170.20 (577.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5096">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">young</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">young,</rdg>
          </app>
or too

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3306"/>
sick

          <app from="pr3306" n="170.20 (577.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5097">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">sick</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sick,</rdg>
          </app>
or too old, was gone to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3307"/>
camp-meeting

          <app from="pr3307" n="170.20 (577.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la5098">
            <lem wit="A Cent">camp-meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
camp-

              <lb/>
meeting

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0181" type="an" xml:id="vs0017"/>
, about two mile back in the woods. The

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0018"/>
king got the directions, and allowed he’d go and work that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3308"/>
camp meeting

          <app from="pr3308" n="170.22 (577.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5099">
            <lem wit="MS1b">camp meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">camp-meeting</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0182" type="an" xml:id="vs0018"/>
for all it was worth, and I might go, too.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e41978">
The duke said what he was after was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3309"/>
printing office

          <app from="pr3309" n="170.24 (577.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5100">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">printing office</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">printing-office</rdg>
          </app>
. We found

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3310"/>
it;

          <app from="pr3310" n="170.25 (578.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5101">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">it;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it—</rdg>
          </app>
a little bit of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3311"/>
concern,

          <app from="pr3311" n="170.25 (578.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5102">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">concern,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
concern

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
up over a carpenter shop—carpenters and printers all gone to the meeting, and no doors locked.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3312"/>
It was a dirty, littered-up place, and had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3313"/>
ink-marks

          <app from="pr3313" n="170.27 (578.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5105">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ink-marks</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ink marks</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3314"/>
handbills

          <app from="pr3314" n="170.27 (578.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5106">
            <lem wit="A">handbills</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
hand-

              <lb/>
bills

            </rdg>
          </app>
with pictures of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1745"/>
horses and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3315"/>
runaway-niggers

          <app from="pr3315" n="170.28 (578.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5107">
            <lem wit="MS1b">runaway-niggers</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">runaway niggers</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11441" type="alt" xml:id="te1745"/>
on them, all over the walls.

          <app from="pr3312" n="170.26–28 (578.6–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5103">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">It . . . walls.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5104">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
The duke shed his coat and said he was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3316"/>
right,

          <app from="pr3316" n="170.29 (578.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5108">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now. So me and the king lit out for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3317"/>
camp meeting

          <app from="pr3317" n="170.30 (578.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5109">
            <lem wit="MS1b">camp meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">camp-meeting</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42061">
We got there in about a half an hour,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3318"/>
fairly dripping

          <app from="pr3318" n="170.31 (579.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5110">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fairly dripping</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sweating like sin</rdg>
          </app>
, for it was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1746"/>
a most

          <ptr target="#l11442" type="alt" xml:id="te1746"/>
awful hot

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3319"/>
day.

          <app from="pr3319" n="170.32 (579.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5111">
            <lem wit="A Cent">day.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
day. Everything was a-

              <lb/>
booming.

            </rdg>
          </app>
There was as much as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1747"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l11443" type="alt" xml:id="te1747"/>
thousand people there, from

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1748"/>
twenty

          <ptr target="#l11444" type="alt" xml:id="te1748"/>
mile around. The woods was full of teams and wagons, hitched

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1749"/>
everywheres

          <ptr target="#l11445" type="alt" xml:id="te1749"/>
, feeding out of the wagon troughs and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1750"/>
stomping

          <ptr target="#l11446" type="alt" xml:id="te1750"/>
to keep off the flies. There was sheds made out of poles and roofed over with branches, where they had lemonade and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3320"/>
ginger-bread

          <app from="pr3320" n="170.36–37 (580.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5112">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ginger-bread</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">gingerbread</rdg>
          </app>
to sell,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3321"/>
and piles

          <app from="pr3321" n="170.37 (580.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la5113">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and piles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and piles and piles</rdg>
          </app>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3322"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1751"/>
watermelons

          <app from="pr3322" n="170.37 (580.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5114">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">watermelons</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">water-melons</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11447" type="alt" xml:id="te1751"/>
and green corn and such-like truck.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42130">
          <pb n="171" xml:id="pb0171"/>
The preaching was going on under the same

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3323"/>
kinds

          <app from="pr3323" n="171.1 (580.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5115">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kinds</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">kind</rdg>
          </app>
of sheds, only they was bigger and held crowds of people. The benches was made out of outside slabs of logs, with holes bored in the round side to drive sticks into for legs. They didn’t have

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3324"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1752"/>
no

          <app from="pr3324" n="171.4 (581.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5116">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11448" type="alt" xml:id="te1752"/>
backs. The preachers had high platforms to stand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3325"/>
on,

          <app from="pr3325" n="171.5 (581.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5117">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at one end of the sheds. The women had on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3326"/>
sun-bonnets

          <app from="pr3326" n="171.6 (581.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5118">
            <lem wit="Cent">sun-bonnets</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A">
sun-

              <lb/>
bonnets

            </rdg>
          </app>
; and some had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3327"/>
linsey-woolsey

          <app from="pr3327" n="171.6 (581.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5119">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">linsey-woolsey</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
linsey-

              <lb/>
woolsey

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1753"/>
frocks

          <ptr target="#l11449" type="alt" xml:id="te1753"/>
, some gingham ones, and a few of the young ones had on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3328"/>
calico. Some

          <app from="pr3328" n="171.7 (581.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la5120">
            <lem wit="A Cent">calico. Some</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
calico.—

              <lb/>
Some

            </rdg>
          </app>
of the young men was barefooted, and some of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3329"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1754"/>
children

          <app from="pr3329" n="171.8 (581.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la5121">
            <lem wit="A Cent">children</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">children and good-sized boys</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11450" type="alt" xml:id="te1754"/>
didn’t have on any clothes but just a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3330"/>
tow-linen

          <app from="pr3330" n="171.9 (581.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5122">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">tow-linen</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
tow-

              <lb/>
linen

            </rdg>
          </app>
shirt. Some of the old women was knitting, and some of the young folks was courting on the sly.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y17101">
          <graphic url="y17101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">courting on the sly.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42222">
The first shed we come to,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1755"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l11451" type="alt" xml:id="te1755"/>
preacher was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3331"/>
lining-out

          <app from="pr3331" n="171.11 (582.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5123">
            <lem wit="MS1b">lining-out</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">lining out</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1756"/>
hymn.

          <ptr target="#l11452" type="alt" xml:id="te1756"/>
He lined out two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3332"/>
lines,

          <app from="pr3332" n="171.12 (582.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5124">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lines,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">lines;</rdg>
          </app>
everybody

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1757"/>
sung

          <ptr target="#l11453" type="alt" xml:id="te1757"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3333"/>
it, and it was kind of grand to hear it, there was so many of them and they done it in such a rousing way; then he lined out two more for them to sing—and so on.

          <app from="pr3333" n="171.12–15 (582.9–583.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5125">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it, and . . . sing—and so on.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
it—roared it out, they did, in a most rousing way:

              <floatingText>
                <body>
                  <lg>
                    <l rend="text-indent:3">“Am I a soldier of the cross,</l>
                    <l rend="text-indent:3">A follower of the Lamb,”—</l>
                  </lg>
                  <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42264">
—then the preacher lined-

                    <lb/>
out the next two:

                  </p>
                  <lg>
                    <l rend="text-indent:3">“And shall I fear to own his cause,</l>
                    <l rend="text-indent:3">Or blush to speak his name?”</l>
                  </lg>
                </body>
              </floatingText>
—and so on.

            </rdg>
          </app>
The people woke up more and more, and sung louder and louder; and towards the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3334"/>
end,

          <app from="pr3334" n="171.16 (583.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5126">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">end,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
end

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
some begun to groan, and some begun to shout.

          <pb n="172" xml:id="pb0172"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3335"/>
Then the

          <app from="pr3335" n="172.1 (583.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5127">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Then the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">The</rdg>
          </app>
preacher begun to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3336"/>
preach; and begun in earnest, too;

          <app from="pr3336" n="172.1 (583.10–12)" type="e" xml:id="la5128">
            <lem wit="A">preach; and begun in earnest, too;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">preach, and he warmed up, right away,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">preach, and begun in earnest, too;</rdg>
          </app>
and went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3337"/>
weaving

          <app from="pr3337" n="172.2 (583.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5129">
            <lem wit="A Cent">weaving</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a-weaving</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1758"/>
first

          <ptr target="#l11454" type="alt" xml:id="te1758"/>
to one side of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3338"/>
the platform

          <app from="pr3338" n="172.2 (583.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5130">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the platform</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">his platform</rdg>
          </app>
and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3339"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1759"/>
the other

          <ptr target="#l11455" type="alt" xml:id="te1759"/>
          <app from="pr3339" n="172.2 (583.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5131">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
to-

              <lb/>
t’other

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3340"/>
a-leaning

          <app from="pr3340" n="172.3 (583.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5132">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">a-leaning</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a leaning</rdg>
          </app>
down over the front of it, with his arms and his body

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3341"/>
going

          <app from="pr3341" n="172.4 (584.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5133">
            <lem wit="A Cent">going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a-going it</rdg>
          </app>
all the time, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3342"/>
shouting

          <app from="pr3342" n="172.4 (584.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5134">
            <lem wit="A Cent">shouting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sing-songing</rdg>
          </app>
his words out

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1760"/>
with

          <ptr target="#l11456" type="alt" xml:id="te1760"/>
all his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3343"/>
might;

          <app from="pr3343" n="172.5 (584.6–8)" type="e" xml:id="la5135">
            <lem wit="A">might;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">might and main, so you could a heard him a mile;</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">might.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3344"/>
and every now and then he would hold up his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3345"/>
Bible and spread it open

          <app from="pr3345" n="172.5–6 (584.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5138">
            <lem wit="A">Bible and spread it open</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">open Bible</rdg>
          </app>
, and kind of pass it around this way and that, shouting,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0019"/>
“It’s the brazen serpent in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3346"/>
wilderness!

          <app from="pr3346" n="172.7 (584.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5139">
            <lem wit="A">wilderness!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wilderness-ah!</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3347"/>
look

          <app from="pr3347" n="172.7 (584.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5140">
            <lem wit="MS1b">look</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Look</rdg>
          </app>
upon it and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3348"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1761"/>
live!

          <app from="pr3348" n="172.7 (584.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5141">
            <lem wit="A">live!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">live-ah!</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0183" type="an" xml:id="vs0019"/>
”

          <ptr target="#l11457" type="alt" xml:id="te1761"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3349"/>
and

          <app from="pr3349" n="172.8 (584.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5142">
            <lem wit="MS1b">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">And</rdg>
          </app>
people would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3350"/>
shout

          <app from="pr3350" n="172.8 (585.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5143">
            <lem wit="A">shout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sing</rdg>
          </app>
out,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1762"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3351"/>
Glory!

          <ptr target="#l11458" type="alt" xml:id="te1762"/>
          <app from="pr3351" n="172.8 (585.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5144">
            <lem wit="A">Glory!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
Glo-o-

              <hi rend="italic">ree!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1763"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3352"/>
A-a-

          <hi rend="italic">men!</hi>
”

          <ptr target="#l11459" type="alt" xml:id="te1763"/>
          <app from="pr3352" n="172.8 (585.2–11)" type="e" xml:id="la5145">
            <lem wit="A">
A-a-

              <hi rend="italic">men!</hi>
”

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
A-a-

              <hi rend="italic">men!</hi>
” and so on, and next he would lay the Bible down and and weave about the platform, and work back to the Bible again, pretty soon, and fetch it a bang with his fist and shout “

              <hi rend="italic">Here</hi>
it is! the rock of salvation-ah!”

            </rdg>
          </app>
And so he went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3353"/>
on

          <app from="pr3353" n="172.9 (585.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5146">
            <lem wit="A">on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">on a-raging</rdg>
          </app>
, and the people

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1764"/>
groaning and

          <ptr target="#l11460" type="alt" xml:id="te1764"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3354"/>
crying and saying amen:

          <app from="pr3354" n="172.9 (585.14–586.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5147">
            <lem wit="A">crying and saying amen:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
crying, and jumping up and hugging one another, and

              <hi rend="italic">Amens</hi>
was popping off everywheres. Every little while he would preach right

              <hi rend="italic">at</hi>
people that he saw was stirred up:

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42492">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3355"/>
O,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0020"/>
come

          <app from="pr3355" n="172.10 (586.5–587.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5148">
            <lem wit="C">O, come</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
The sperrit’s a workin’ in you brother—don’t shake him off-ah!—

              <lb/>
Now is the accepted time-ah! [

              <hi rend="italic">A-a-</hi>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">men!</hi>
] The devil’s holt is a weakenin’ on you, sister—shake him loose, shake him loose-ah! One more shake and the vict’ry’s won-ah! [

              <hi rend="italic">Come</hi>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">down</hi>
,

              <hi rend="bold">Lord!</hi>
] Hell’s a-

              <lb/>
burning, the kingdom’s a-coming-ah!—one more shake, sister, one more shake and your chains is broke-ah! [

              <hi rend="italic">Glory</hi>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">hal</hi>
              <hi rend="italic">-lelujah!</hi>
] O, come

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh, come</rdg>
          </app>
to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3356"/>
mourners’

          <app from="pr3356" n="172.10 (587.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5152">
            <lem wit="A">mourners’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">mourner’s</rdg>
          </app>
bench!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3357"/>
Come

          <app from="pr3357" n="172.10 (587.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5153">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Come</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">come</rdg>
          </app>
, black with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1765"/>
sin!

          <ptr target="#l11462" type="alt" xml:id="te1765"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3358"/>
[

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1766"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Amen!</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11463" type="alt" xml:id="te1766"/>
] come, sick and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1767"/>
sore! [

          <hi rend="italic">Amen!</hi>
          <app from="pr3358" n="172.11 (587.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5154">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
[

              <hi rend="italic">Amen!</hi>
] . . . [

              <hi rend="italic">Amen!</hi>
]

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
(

              <hi rend="italic">amen!</hi>
) . . . (

              <hi rend="italic">amen!</hi>
)

            </rdg>
          </app>
]

          <ptr target="#l11466" type="alt" xml:id="te1767"/>
come,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3359"/>
lame and halt, and blind

          <app from="pr3359" n="172.11–12 (587.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5157">
            <lem wit="A">lame and halt, and blind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">lame, and blind and halt</rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3360"/>
[

          <hi rend="italic">Amen!</hi>
] come, pore and needy, sunk in shame! [

          <hi rend="italic">A-a-</hi>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">men</hi>
!]

          <app from="pr3360" n="172.12 (587.10–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5158">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
[

              <hi rend="italic">Amen!</hi>
] . . . [

              <hi rend="italic">
                <hi rend="italic">A-a-</hi>
              </hi>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">men!</hi>
]

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
(

              <hi rend="italic">amen!</hi>
) . . . (

              <hi rend="italic">a-a-men!</hi>
)

            </rdg>
          </app>
come all that’s worn, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3361"/>
soiled, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1768"/>
suffering

          <ptr target="#l11469" type="alt" xml:id="te1768"/>
          <app from="pr3361" n="172.13 (587.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5161">
            <lem wit="A">soiled, and suffering</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">guilty and sufferin’</rdg>
          </app>
!—come with a broken spirit! come with a contrite

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1769"/>
heart!

          <ptr target="#l11470" type="alt" xml:id="te1769"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3362"/>
come,

          <app from="pr3362" n="172.14 (587.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5162">
            <lem wit="MS1b">come,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
come

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in your rags and sin and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1770"/>
dirt!

          <ptr target="#l11471" type="alt" xml:id="te1770"/>
the waters that cleanse is free, the door of heaven stands open—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="rp0364"/>
O

          <app from="rp0364" n="172.16 (588.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la0001">
            <lem wit="MS1b">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">oh</rdg>
          </app>
, enter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3364"/>
in and be at

          <app from="pr3364" n="172.16 (588.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5164">
            <lem wit="A">in and be at</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">into the everlasting</rdg>
          </app>
rest!”

          <ptr target="#as0184" type="an" xml:id="vs0020"/>
[

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3365"/>
          <hi rend="italic">A-a-</hi>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">men</hi>
!

          <app from="pr3365" n="172.16 (588.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5165">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
[

              <hi rend="italic">A-a-</hi>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">men!</hi>
]

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
(

              <hi rend="italic">a-a-men!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3366"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Glory, glory hallelujah!</hi>
]

          <app from="pr3366" n="172.16 (588.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la5167">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="italic">Glory, glory hallelujah!</hi>
]

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">Glo-o-ry-glory! Come</hi>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">down</hi>
,

              <hi rend="italic">Lord!</hi>
]

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">glory, glory hallelujah!</hi>
)

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42711">
And so on.

          <app from="pr3344" n="172.5–17 (584.8–588.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5136">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">and every . . . so on.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5137">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
You couldn’t make out what the preacher said,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0061"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3367"/>
any more

          <app from="pr3367" n="✱172.17–18 (588.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la5168">
            <lem wit="A Cent">any more</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
any-

              <lb/>
more

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0061" type="te" xml:id="tv0061"/>
, on account of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3368"/>
shouting

          <app from="pr3368" n="172.18 (588.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la5169">
            <lem wit="A Cent">shouting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">whooping and shouting</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3369"/>
crying

          <app from="pr3369" n="172.18 (588.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5170">
            <lem wit="A Cent">crying</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">crying that was going on</rdg>
          </app>
. Folks got up, everywheres in the crowd, and worked their way, just by main

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3370"/>
strength

          <app from="pr3370" n="172.19 (589.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5171">
            <lem wit="A Cent">strength</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">force</rdg>
          </app>
, to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3371"/>
mourners’

          <app from="pr3371" n="172.20 (589.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la5172">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mourners’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">mourner’s</rdg>
          </app>
bench, with the tears

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3372"/>
running

          <app from="pr3372" n="172.20 (589.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5173">
            <lem wit="A Cent">running</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a-pouring</rdg>
          </app>
down their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3373"/>
faces; and

          <app from="pr3373" n="172.20–21 (589.5–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5174">
            <lem wit="A Cent">faces; and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">faces, and folks hugging them and crying over them all the way. And it was worse than ever</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1771"/>
when

          <ptr target="#l11472" type="alt" xml:id="te1771"/>
all the mourners had got up there to the front benches in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3374"/>
crowd, they sung,

          <app from="pr3374" n="172.22 (589.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5175">
            <lem wit="A Cent">crowd, they sung,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">gang. They hugged one another,</rdg>
          </app>
and shouted, and flung themselves down on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3375"/>
straw

          <app from="pr3375" n="172.23 (589.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la5176">
            <lem wit="A Cent">straw</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">straw, and wallowed around</rdg>
          </app>
, just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3376"/>
crazy

          <app from="pr3376" n="172.23 (590.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5177">
            <lem wit="A Cent">crazy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">plum crazy</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3377"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1772"/>
wild.

          <ptr target="#l11473" type="alt" xml:id="te1772"/>
          <app from="pr3377" n="172.23 (590.1–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5178">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wild.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
wild. One fat nigger woman about forty, was the worst. The white mourners couldn’t fend her off, no way—fast as one would get loose, she’d tackle the next one, and smother

              <hi rend="italic">him.</hi>
Next, down she went in the straw, along with the rest, and wallowed around, clawing dirt and shouting glory hallelujah same as they did.

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e42823">
Well, the first I knowed, the king got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3378"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1773"/>
agoing; and you could hear him over everybody; and next

          <ptr target="#l11474" type="alt" xml:id="te1773"/>
          <app from="pr3378" n="172.24–25 (591.2–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5179">
            <lem wit="A">agoing; and . . . next</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a start. He begun to warm up, and by and by he laid over them all, for whooping and hugging and wallowing. And when everything was just at its boomingest,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-going; and . . . next</rdg>
          </app>
he went a-charging up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3379"/>
onto

          <app from="pr3379" n="172.25 (591.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5180">
            <lem wit="MS1b">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">on to</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3380"/>
platform and

          <app from="pr3380" n="172.25–26 (591.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la5181">
            <lem wit="A">platform and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b cent">platform and flung his arms around</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">platform, and</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pra382"/>
preacher

          <app from="pra382" n="172.26 (591.12–592.2)" type="e" xml:id="laa183">
            <lem wit="A Cent">preacher</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">preacher and went to hugging him and kissing him, and crying all over him, and thanking him for saving him. The preacher felt so good about it, that</rdg>
          </app>
he begged

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3382"/>
him

          <app from="pr3382" n="172.26 (592.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5183">
            <lem wit="A Cent">him</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the king</rdg>
          </app>
to speak to the people, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1774"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l11475" type="alt" xml:id="te1774"/>
done it. He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3383"/>
told

          <app from="pr3383" n="172.27 (592.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5184">
            <lem wit="A Cent">told</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">warmed them up, too—told</rdg>
          </app>
them he was a pirate—been a pirate for thirty years, out in the Indian

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3384"/>
ocean

          <app from="pr3384" n="172.28 (592.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5185">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ocean</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Ocean</rdg>
          </app>
, and his crew was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1775"/>
thinned

          <ptr target="#l11476" type="alt" xml:id="te1775"/>
out considerable, last

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3385"/>
spring

          <app from="pr3385" n="172.29 (592.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5186">
            <lem wit="MS1b">spring</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">spring,</rdg>
          </app>
in a fight, and he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3386"/>
home,

          <app from="pr3386" n="172.29 (592.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5187">
            <lem wit="MS1b">home,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
home

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, to take out some fresh

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3387"/>
men,

          <app from="pr3387" n="172.30 (592.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5188">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">men,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">men;</rdg>
          </app>
and thanks to goodness he’d been robbed last

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3388"/>
night

          <app from="pr3388" n="172.30 (593.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5189">
            <lem wit="MS1b">night</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">night,</rdg>
          </app>
and put ashore

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3389"/>
off of

          <app from="pr3389" n="172.31 (593.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5190">
            <lem wit="A Cent">off of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">from</rdg>
          </app>
a steamboat without a cent, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3390"/>
he

          <app from="pr3390" n="172.31 (593.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la5191">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">glory hallelujah he</rdg>
          </app>
was glad of it, it was the blessedest thing that ever happened to him,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3391"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1776"/>
because he

          <ptr target="#l11477" type="alt" xml:id="te1776"/>
          <app from="pr3391" n="172.32–33 (593.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5192">
            <lem wit="A Cent">because he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">because he’d got religion to-day, and</rdg>
          </app>
was a changed man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3392"/>
now,

          <app from="pr3392" n="172.33 (593.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5193">
            <lem wit="A Cent">now,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5194">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and happy for the first time in his life;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3393"/>
and, poor

          <app from="pr3393" n="172.33 (593.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5195">
            <lem wit="MS1b">and, poor</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
and

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
poor

            </rdg>
          </app>
as he was, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3394"/>
was going

          <app from="pr3394" n="172.34 (593.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5196">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">meant</rdg>
          </app>
to start right off and work his way back to the Indian

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3395"/>
ocean

          <app from="pr3395" n="172.35 (593.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5197">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ocean</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Ocean</rdg>
          </app>
and put in the rest of his life

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3396"/>
trying to turn the pirates

          <app from="pr3396" n="172.35–36 (594.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la5198">
            <lem wit="A Cent">trying to turn the pirates</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">converting pirates and turning them</rdg>
          </app>
into the true path; for he could do it better than anybody else, being acquainted with all the pirate crews in that ocean; and though it would take him a long time to get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3397"/>
there,

          <app from="pr3397" n="172.38 (594.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5199">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
without money,

          <pb n="173" xml:id="pb0173"/>
he would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3398"/>
get

          <app from="pr3398" n="173.1 (594.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5200">
            <lem wit="A Cent">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">get</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3399"/>
there,

          <app from="pr3399" n="173.1 (594.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5201">
            <lem wit="MS1b">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
anyway, and every time he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3400"/>
convinced

          <app from="pr3400" n="173.1 (594.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5202">
            <lem wit="A Cent">convinced</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">converted</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3401"/>
pirate,

          <app from="pr3401" n="173.1 (594.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5203">
            <lem wit="MS1b">pirate,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
pirate

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he would say to him, “Don’t you thank

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3402"/>
me, don’t you give me

          <app from="pr3402" n="173.2 (595.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5204">
            <lem wit="A Cent">me, . . . me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
, . . .

              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3403"/>
credit,

          <app from="pr3403" n="173.3 (595.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5205">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">credit,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">credit;</rdg>
          </app>
it all belongs to them dear people in Pokeville

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3404"/>
camp meeting

          <app from="pr3404" n="173.3–4 (595.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5206">
            <lem wit="MS1b">camp meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">camp-meeting</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3405"/>
natural brothers and benefactors of the race—

          <app from="pr3405" n="173.4 (595.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5207">
            <lem wit="Prb, A, Cent">natural . . . race—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Pfs1 Pra">natural . . . base—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5208">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and that dear preacher

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3406"/>
there, the truest friend a pirate ever had!

          <app from="pr3406" n="173.5 (595.7–12)" type="e" xml:id="la5209">
            <lem wit="A Cent">there, . . . had!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that spoke the words that set my soul afire and saved it from that other fire that burns foreverlasting—glory hallelujah!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43093">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y17301">
            <graphic url="y17301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">a pirate for thirty years.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43100">
And then he busted into tears, and so did

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3407"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1777"/>
everybody

          <ptr target="#l11478" type="alt" xml:id="te1777"/>
          <app from="pr3407" n="173.6 (595.14–596.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5210">
            <lem wit="A Cent">everybody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
everybody; and he hugged the preacher and cried on him again, and everybody hugged one another and sung out A-a-

              <hi rend="smallcaps">men</hi>
! and all that sort of thing

            </rdg>
          </app>
. Then somebody sings

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3408"/>
out

          <app from="pr3408" n="173.7 (596.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5211">
            <lem wit="MS1b">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">out,</rdg>
          </app>
“Take up a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3409"/>
collection for him

          <app from="pr3409" n="173.7 (596.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la5212">
            <lem wit="A Cent">collection for him</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">collection</rdg>
          </app>
, take up a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3410"/>
collection!

          <app from="pr3410" n="173.7 (596.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la5213">
            <lem wit="A Cent">collection!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">collection for the pore soul!</rdg>
          </app>
” Well, a half a dozen made a jump to do it, but somebody sings out, “Let

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
pass the hat around!” Then everybody said it, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3411"/>
preacher,

          <app from="pr3411" n="173.10 (596.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la5214">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">preacher,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
preacher

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43152">
So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3412"/>
the

          <app from="pr3412" n="173.11 (596.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5215">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that</rdg>
          </app>
king went all through the crowd with his hat,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3413"/>
swabbing

          <app from="pr3413" n="173.11 (597.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la5216">
            <lem wit="A Cent">swabbing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
a-crying, and a-

              <lb/>
swabbing

            </rdg>
          </app>
his eyes, and blessing the people and praising them and thanking

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1778"/>
them

          <ptr target="#l11479" type="alt" xml:id="te1778"/>
for being so good to the poor pirates away off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3414"/>
there

          <app from="pr3414" n="173.13 (597.7–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5217">
            <lem wit="A Cent">there</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">there with nobody to give them a lift and show them the way to the light</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3415"/>
and every little while the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1779"/>
prettiest

          <ptr target="#l11480" type="alt" xml:id="te1779"/>
kind of girls, with the tears

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3416"/>
running

          <app from="pr3416" n="173.14 (597.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5220">
            <lem wit="A">running</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a-running</rdg>
          </app>
down their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3417"/>
cheeks,

          <app from="pr3417" n="173.15 (597.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5221">
            <lem wit="A">cheeks,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
cheeks

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
would up and ask him

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0021"/>
would he let them kiss him, for to remember him by; and he always

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3418"/>
done it

          <app from="pr3418" n="173.16 (598.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5222">
            <lem wit="A">done it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">let them</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0185" type="an" xml:id="vs0021"/>
; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1780"/>
some

          <ptr target="#l11481" type="alt" xml:id="te1780"/>
of them he hugged and kissed as many as five or six times—

          <app from="pr3415" n="173.13–17 (597.10–598.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5218">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">and every . . . times—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5219">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and he was invited

          <pb n="174" xml:id="pb0174"/>
to stay a week; and everybody wanted him to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1781"/>
live

          <ptr target="#l11482" type="alt" xml:id="te1781"/>
in their

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1782"/>
houses,

          <ptr target="#l11483" type="alt" xml:id="te1782"/>
and said they’d think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3419"/>
it was

          <app from="pr3419" n="174.2 (598.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5223">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">it</rdg>
          </app>
an honor; but he said as this was the last day of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3420"/>
camp meeting

          <app from="pr3420" n="174.3 (598.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5224">
            <lem wit="MS1b">camp meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">camp-meeting</rdg>
          </app>
he couldn’t do no good, and besides he was in a sweat to get to the Indian

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3421"/>
ocean

          <app from="pr3421" n="174.4 (599.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5225">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ocean</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Ocean</rdg>
          </app>
right off and go to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3422"/>
work on the

          <app from="pr3422" n="174.4–5 (599.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5226">
            <lem wit="A Cent">work on the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saving</rdg>
          </app>
pirates.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43275">
When we got back to the raft and he come to count up, he found he had collected eighty-seven dollars and seventy-five cents. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3423"/>
then

          <app from="pr3423" n="174.8 (599.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5227">
            <lem wit="A Cent">then</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5228">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he had fetched away a three-gallon jug of whisky, too, that he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3424"/>
found

          <app from="pr3424" n="174.9 (599.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5229">
            <lem wit="A Cent">found</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">had found</rdg>
          </app>
under a wagon when we was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1783"/>
starting

          <ptr target="#l11484" type="alt" xml:id="te1783"/>
home through the woods. The king said, take it all around, it laid over any day he’d

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1784"/>
ever

          <ptr target="#l11485" type="alt" xml:id="te1784"/>
put in in the missionarying line. He said it warn’t no use talking,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0022"/>
heathens

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3425"/>
don’t

          <app from="pr3425" n="174.12 (600.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5230">
            <lem wit="A Cent">don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
amount to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3426"/>
shucks

          <app from="pr3426" n="174.12 (600.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5231">
            <lem wit="A Cent">shucks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a dern</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3427"/>
alongside

          <app from="pr3427" n="174.12 (600.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la5232">
            <lem wit="A">alongside</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
along-

              <lb/>
side

            </rdg>
          </app>
of pirates, to work a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3428"/>
camp meeting

          <app from="pr3428" n="174.13 (600.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5233">
            <lem wit="MS1b">camp meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
camp-

              <lb/>
meeting

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">camp-meeting</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3429"/>
with

          <ptr target="#as0186" type="an" xml:id="vs0022"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43348">
The

          <app from="pr3429" n="174.13–14 (600.8–601.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5234">
            <lem wit="A Cent">with. [¶] The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
with.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
CHAP. [¶] The

            </rdg>
          </app>
duke was thinking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3430"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he’d</hi>
been doing

          <app from="pr3430" n="174.14 (601.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5235">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">he’d</hi>
been doing

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
had done

            </rdg>
          </app>
pretty well, till the king come to show up, but after that he didn’t think so so much. He had set up and printed off two little jobs for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3431"/>
farmers,

          <app from="pr3431" n="174.16 (601.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5236">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">farmers,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
farmers

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3432"/>
printing office

          <app from="pr3432" n="174.16–17 (601.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5237">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">printing office</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">printing-office</rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3433"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1785"/>
horse-bills,

          <app from="pr3433" n="174.17 (601.9–602.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5238">
            <lem wit="C">horse-bills,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
horse-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
bills,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">horse bills</rdg>
          </app>
—

          <ptr target="#l11486" type="alt" xml:id="te1785"/>
and took the money, four dollars. And he had got in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1786"/>
ten

          <ptr target="#l11487" type="alt" xml:id="te1786"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3434"/>
dollars

          <app from="pr3434" n="174.18 (602.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5239">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">dollars</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">dollars’</rdg>
          </app>
worth of advertisements for the paper, which he said he would put in for four dollars if they would pay in advance—so they done it. The price of the paper was two dollars a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1787"/>
year,

          <ptr target="#l11488" type="alt" xml:id="te1787"/>
but he took in three subscriptions for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3435"/>
half

          <app from="pr3435" n="174.21 (602.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5240">
            <lem wit="A Cent">half</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a half</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1788"/>
dollar

          <ptr target="#l11489" type="alt" xml:id="te1788"/>
apiece

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1789"/>
on condition of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3436"/>
them paying him

          <ptr target="#l11490" type="alt" xml:id="te1789"/>
          <app from="pr3436" n="174.22 (602.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5241">
            <lem wit="A Cent">them paying him</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">pay</rdg>
          </app>
in advance;

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0023"/>
they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3437"/>
were

          <app from="pr3437" n="174.22 (602.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5242">
            <lem wit="A Cent">were</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">was</rdg>
          </app>
going to pay in cord-wood and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3438"/>
onions

          <app from="pr3438" n="174.23 (602.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5243">
            <lem wit="A Cent">onions</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sweet potatoes</rdg>
          </app>
, as usual

          <ptr target="#as0187" type="an" xml:id="vs0023"/>
, but he said he had just bought the concern and knocked down the price

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1790"/>
as low

          <ptr target="#l11491" type="alt" xml:id="te1790"/>
as he could afford it, and was going to run it for cash. He set up a little piece of poetry, which he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3439"/>
made, himself,

          <app from="pr3439" n="174.25–26 (603.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5244">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">made, himself,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
made

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
himself

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
out of his own

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3440"/>
head,

          <app from="pr3440" n="174.26 (603.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5245">
            <lem wit="MS1b">head,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
head

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—three verses—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3441"/>
kind of

          <app from="pr3441" n="174.26 (603.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5246">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kind of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">very</rdg>
          </app>
sweet and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3442"/>
saddish

          <app from="pr3442" n="174.27 (603.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5247">
            <lem wit="A Cent">saddish</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">melancholy</rdg>
          </app>
—the name of it was,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0024"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3443"/>
Yes, Crush, Cold World, this Breaking Heart

          <app from="pr3443" n="174.27–28 (603.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la5248">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Yes, Crush, Cold World, this Breaking Heart</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Yes, crush, cold world, this breaking heart</rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#as0188" type="an" xml:id="vs0024"/>
—and he left that all set up and ready to print in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3444"/>
paper

          <app from="pr3444" n="174.28–29 (604.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5249">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">paper</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">paper,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3445"/>
didn’t charge nothing

          <app from="pr3445" n="174.29 (604.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la5250">
            <lem wit="A Cent">didn’t charge nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">never charged anything</rdg>
          </app>
for it. Well, he took in nine dollars and a half, and said he’d done a pretty square day’s work for it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43533">
Then he showed us another little job

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3446"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr3446" n="174.31 (604.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5251">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">he had</rdg>
          </app>
printed and hadn’t charged for, because it was for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3447"/>
us

          <app from="pr3447" n="174.32 (604.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5252">
            <lem wit="A Cent">us</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. It had a

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0025"/>
picture of a runaway nigger, with a bundle on a stick, over his shoulder

          <ptr target="#as0189" type="an" xml:id="vs0025"/>
, and “

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1791"/>
$200

          <ptr target="#l11492" type="alt" xml:id="te1791"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3448"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">Reward</hi>
          <app from="pr3448" n="174.34 (604.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5253">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">Reward</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">Reward</hi>
!

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">reward</rdg>
          </app>
” under it. The reading was all about Jim, and just described him to a dot. It said he run away from St.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3449"/>
Jacques

          <app from="pr3449" n="174.35 (605.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la5254">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Jacques</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Jacques’</rdg>
          </app>
plantation, forty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3450"/>
mile

          <app from="pr3450" n="174.36 (605.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5255">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">miles</rdg>
          </app>
below New Orleans, last winter, and likely went north, and whoever would catch him and send him back,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3451"/>
he

          <app from="pr3451" n="174.37 (605.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5256">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5257">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
could have the reward and expenses.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43601">
          <pb n="175" xml:id="pb0175"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y17501">
            <graphic url="y17501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">another little job</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43608">
“Now,” says the duke, “after to-night we can run in the daytime if we want to. Whenever we see anybody coming, we can tie Jim hand and foot with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3452"/>
rope

          <app from="pr3452" n="175.3 (606.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5258">
            <lem wit="MS1b">rope</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">rope,</rdg>
          </app>
and lay him in the wigwam and show this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3453"/>
handbill

          <app from="pr3453" n="175.4 (606.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5259">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">handbill</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hand-bill</rdg>
          </app>
and say we captured him up the river, and were too poor to travel on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3454"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr3454" n="175.5 (606.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5260">
            <lem wit="A Cent">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
, so we got this little raft on credit from our friends and are going down to get the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1792"/>
reward.

          <ptr target="#l11493" type="alt" xml:id="te1792"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0032"/>
Handcuffs and chains would look still better on Jim, but it wouldn’t go well with the story of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3455"/>
us

          <app from="pr3455" n="175.8 (607.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5261">
            <lem wit="A Cent">us</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">our</rdg>
          </app>
being so poor. Too much like jewelry. Ropes are the correct thing—we must preserve the unities, as we say on the boards.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43650">
We all said the duke was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1793"/>
pretty

          <ptr target="#l11494" type="alt" xml:id="te1793"/>
smart, and there couldn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1794"/>
be

          <ptr target="#l11495" type="alt" xml:id="te1794"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3456"/>
no trouble

          <app from="pr3456" n="175.11–12 (607.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la5262">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no trouble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any trouble now</rdg>
          </app>
about running daytimes. We judged we could make miles

          <ptr target="#mt0032" type="alt" xml:id="wn0032"/>
enough that night to get out of the reach of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1795"/>
the pow-wow

          <ptr target="#l11496" type="alt" xml:id="te1795"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3457"/>
we reckoned

          <app from="pr3457" n="175.13–14 (608.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5263">
            <lem wit="A Cent">we reckoned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5264">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the duke’s work in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3458"/>
printing office

          <app from="pr3458" n="175.14 (608.4–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5265">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">printing office</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">printing-office</rdg>
          </app>
was going to make in that little town—then we could boom right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3459"/>
along, if we wanted to

          <app from="pr3459" n="175.15–16 (608.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5266">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">along, if we wanted to</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">along</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43699">
          <pb n="176" xml:id="pb0176"/>
We

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1796"/>
laid

          <ptr target="#l11497" type="alt" xml:id="te1796"/>
low and kept still, and never shoved out till nearly ten o’clock; then we slid by, pretty wide away from the town, and didn’t hoist our lantern till we was clear out of sight of it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43706">
When Jim called me to take the watch at four in the morning, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3460"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3460" n="176.5 (609.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la5267">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43715">
“Huck, does you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3461"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr3461" n="176.6 (609.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5268">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
we gwyne to run acrost any mo’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1797"/>
kings

          <ptr target="#l11498" type="alt" xml:id="te1797"/>
on dis trip?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43729">
“No,”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3462"/>
I says

          <app from="pr3462" n="176.8 (609.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5269">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">says I</rdg>
          </app>
, “I reckon not.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43739">
“Well,”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3463"/>
says he

          <app from="pr3463" n="176.9 (609.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5270">
            <lem wit="A Cent">says he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">he says</rdg>
          </app>
, “dat’s all right, den. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3464"/>
doan’

          <app from="pr3464" n="176.9 (609.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5271">
            <lem wit="A Cent">doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">don’t</rdg>
          </app>
mine one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3465"/>
er

          <app from="pr3465" n="176.9 (609.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5272">
            <lem wit="A Cent">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">or</rdg>
          </app>
two kings, but dat’s enough. Dis one’s powerful drunk,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1798"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l11499" type="alt" xml:id="te1798"/>
de duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3466"/>
ain’

          <app from="pr3466" n="176.10 (610.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5273">
            <lem wit="A">ain’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">ain’t</rdg>
          </app>
much better.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43778">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3467"/>
I found Jim had been trying to get him to talk French, so he could hear what it was like; but he said he had been in this country so long, and had so much trouble, he’d forgot it.

          <app from="pr3467" n="176.12–14 (610.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5274">
            <lem wit="A">I . . . it.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5275">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0357">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXI.</head>
        <pb n="177" xml:id="pb0177"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e43791">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y17701">
            <graphic url="y17701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3468"/>
Chapter XXI.

              <app from="pr3468" n="177 title (610.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5276">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XXI.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5277">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">It</hi>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1771">
            <graphic url="hf1771.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3476"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">practicing</hi>
.

              <app from="pr3476" n="177 caption" type="e" xml:id="la5286">
                <lem wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">practicing</hi>
.

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5287">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="Cent">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">the sword-fight from richard iii</hi>
.

                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e43823">
was after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3469"/>
sun-up,

          <app from="pr3469" n="177.1 (610.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5278">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">sun-up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sun-up</rdg>
          </app>
now, but we went right on, and didn’t tie up. The king and the duke turned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3470"/>
out,

          <app from="pr3470" n="177.4 (610.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5279">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3471"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr3471" n="177.4 (610.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5280">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, looking pretty rusty; but after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3472"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr3472" n="177.5 (610.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5281">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">they had</rdg>
          </app>
jumped overboard and took a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3473"/>
swim

          <app from="pr3473" n="177.6 (610.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5282">
            <lem wit="MS1b">swim</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">swim,</rdg>
          </app>
it chippered them up a good deal. After breakfast the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3474"/>
he

          <app from="pr3474" n="177.8 (610.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5283">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5284">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
took a seat on a corner of the raft, and pulled off his boots and rolled up his britches, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1799"/>
let

          <ptr target="#l11500" type="alt" xml:id="te1799"/>
his legs dangle in the water, so as to be comfortable,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1800"/>
and lit his pipe,

          <ptr target="#l11501" type="alt" xml:id="te1800"/>
and went to getting his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3475"/>
Romeo and Juliet

          <app from="pr3475" n="177.15 (611.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5285">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Romeo and Juliet</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">“Romeo and Juliet”</rdg>
          </app>
by heart. When he had got it pretty good, him and the duke begun to practice it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3477"/>
together

          <app from="pr3477" n="177.17 (611.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5288">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">together</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5289">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. The duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3478"/>
had to learn him over and over again, how to say every speech; and he

          <app from="pr3478" n="177.17–18 (611.8–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5290">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">had . . . he</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5291">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
made him sigh, and put his hand on his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3479"/>
heart;

          <app from="pr3479" n="177.19 (611.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5292">
            <lem wit="MS1b">heart;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">heart,</rdg>
          </app>
and after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3480"/>
a

          <app from="pr3480" n="177.19 (611.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5293">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5294">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
while he said he done it pretty well; “only,” he says, “you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3481"/>
          <hi rend="italic">mustn’t</hi>
          <app from="pr3481" n="177.20 (611.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5295">
            <lem wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">mustn’t</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">mustn’t</rdg>
          </app>
bellow out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3482"/>
ROMEO!

          <app from="pr3482" n="177.21 (611.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5296">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ROMEO!</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">Romeo!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that way, like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3483"/>
bull

          <app from="pr3483" n="177.21 (611.17)" type="e" xml:id="la5297">
            <lem wit="A Cent">bull</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">bull-frog</rdg>
          </app>
—you must say it soft, and sick, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3484"/>
languishy

          <app from="pr3484" n="177.22 (612.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5298">
            <lem wit="A Cent">languishy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">languishing</rdg>
          </app>
, so—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3485"/>
R–o–o–meo

          <app from="pr3485" n="177.22 (612.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la5299">
            <lem wit="A Cent">R–o–o–meo</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
R-o-o-

              <lb/>
meo

            </rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3486"/>
—that is

          <app from="pr3486" n="177.22 (612.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5300">
            <lem wit="C">—that is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">—that’s</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">that is</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3487"/>
idea—

          <app from="pr3487" n="177.22 (612.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5301">
            <lem wit="MS1b">idea—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">idea;</rdg>
          </app>
for Juliet’s a dear sweet mere child of a girl,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1801"/>
you know,

          <ptr target="#l11502" type="alt" xml:id="te1801"/>
and she don’t bray like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3488"/>
jackass

          <app from="pr3488" n="177.24 (612.7)" type="e" xml:id="la5302">
            <lem wit="A Cent">jackass</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">trombone</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44006">
Well, next they got out a couple of long swords that the duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3489"/>
made

          <app from="pr3489" n="177.26 (612.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5303">
            <lem wit="A Cent">made</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">had made</rdg>
          </app>
out of oak laths, and begun to practice the sword-fight—the duke called himself Richard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3490"/>
III

          <app from="pr3490" n="177.27 (612.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5304">
            <lem wit="MS1b">III</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">III.</rdg>
          </app>
; and the way they laid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3491"/>
on,

          <app from="pr3491" n="177.27 (612.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5305">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and pranced around the raft was grand to see. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3492"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr3492" n="177.28 (613.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5306">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
the king tripped and fell overboard, and after that they took a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3493"/>
rest, and had a talk about all kinds of adventures

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3494"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr3494" n="177.30 (613.7)" type="e" xml:id="la5308">
            <lem wit="A">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">they had</rdg>
          </app>
had in other times along the river.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44051">
After dinner, the duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3495"/>
says—

          <app from="pr3495" n="177.32 (613.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5309">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44060">
          <pb n="178" xml:id="pb0178"/>
“Well,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0026"/>
Capet

          <ptr target="#as0190" type="an" xml:id="vs0026"/>
, we’ll want to make this a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0001"/>
first class

          <app from="ch0001" n="178.1 (613.12)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0001">
            <lem wit="MS1b">first class</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">first-class</rdg>
          </app>
show, you know, so I guess we’ll add a little more to it. We want a little something to answer encores with, anyway.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44075">“What’s onkores, Bilgewater?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44077">
The duke told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0002"/>
him;

          <app from="ch0002" n="178.5 (614.3)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0002">
            <lem wit="MS1b">him;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">him,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0003"/>
and

          <app from="ch0003" n="178.5 (614.4)" type="e" xml:id="hc0003">
            <lem wit="A">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="um1001">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0004"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1802"/>
says

          <ptr target="#l11503" type="alt" xml:id="te1802"/>
—

          <app from="ch0004" n="178.5 (614.4)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0004">
            <lem wit="MS1b">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44106">
“I’ll answer by doing the Highland

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0005"/>
Fling

          <app from="ch0005" n="178.6 (614.6)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0005">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Fling</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fling</rdg>
          </app>
or the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0006"/>
Sailor’s Hornpipe

          <app from="ch0006" n="178.6–7 (614.7)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0006">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Sailor’s Hornpipe</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sailor’s hornpipe</rdg>
          </app>
; and you—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0007"/>
well

          <app from="ch0007" n="178.7 (614.8)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0007">
            <lem wit="MS1b">well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">well,</rdg>
          </app>
let me see—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0008"/>
O

          <app from="ch0008" n="178.7 (614.9)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0008">
            <lem wit="MS1b">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">oh</rdg>
          </app>
, I’ve got it—you can do Hamlet’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0009"/>
Soliloquy

          <app from="ch0009" n="178.8 (614.10)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0009">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Soliloquy</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">soliloquy</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44149">“Hamlet’s which?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44152">
“Hamlet’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0010"/>
Soliloquy

          <app from="ch0010" n="178.10 (614.12)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0010">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Soliloquy</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">soliloquy</rdg>
          </app>
, you know; the most celebrated thing in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0011"/>
Shakspeare

          <app from="ch0011" n="178.11 (614.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0011">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Shakspeare</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Shakespeare</rdg>
          </app>
. Ah,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0012"/>
it’s

          <app from="ch0012" n="178.11 (614.15)" type="e" xml:id="hc0012">
            <lem wit="A">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">it is</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0013"/>
sublime,

          <app from="ch0013" n="178.11 (614.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="hc0013">
            <lem wit="A">sublime,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a sublime, thing,</rdg>
          </app>
sublime! Always fetches the house. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0014"/>
haven’t

          <app from="ch0014" n="178.12 (615.1)" type="e" xml:id="hc0014">
            <lem wit="A">haven’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">havent</rdg>
          </app>
got it in the book—I’ve only got one volume—but I reckon I can piece it out from memory. I’ll just walk up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ch0015"/>
down,

          <app from="ch0015" n="178.13 (615.6)" type="hc" xml:id="hc0015">
            <lem wit="MS1b">down,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
down

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a minute, and see if I can call it back from recollection’s vaults.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y17801">
          <graphic url="y17801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">hamlet’s soliloquy</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44208">
So he went to marching up and down,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3511"/>
thinking—

          <app from="pr3511" n="178.15 (615.11–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5326">
            <lem wit="MS1b">thinking—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">thinking,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3512"/>
frowning, horrible,

          <app from="pr3512" n="178.15–16 (615.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5327">
            <lem wit="MS1b">frowning, horrible,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
frowning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
horrible

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
every now and then; then he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1803"/>
would

          <ptr target="#l11504" type="alt" xml:id="te1803"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3513"/>
hoist up

          <app from="pr3513" n="178.16 (615.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5328">
            <lem wit="A">hoist up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">lift</rdg>
          </app>
his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3514"/>
eyebrows

          <app from="pr3514" n="178.16 (615.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5329">
            <lem wit="C">eyebrows</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A">
eye-

              <lb/>
brows

            </rdg>
          </app>
; next he would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3515"/>
squeeze

          <app from="pr3515" n="178.17 (615.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5330">
            <lem wit="A">squeeze</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">press</rdg>
          </app>
his hand on his forehead and stagger back

          <pb n="179" xml:id="pb0179"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3516"/>
kind of moan

          <app from="pr3516" n="179.1 (616.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5331">
            <lem wit="A">kind of moan</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">groan</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1804"/>
next he

          <ptr target="#l11505" type="alt" xml:id="te1804"/>
would sigh, and next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3517"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr3517" n="179.1 (616.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la5332">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">he would</rdg>
          </app>
let on to drop a tear. It was beautiful to see him.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3518"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr3518" n="179.2 (616.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5333">
            <lem wit="MS1b">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he got it. He told us to give attention. Then he strikes a most noble attitude, with one leg

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3519"/>
shoved forwards

          <app from="pr3519" n="179.4 (616.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5334">
            <lem wit="A">shoved forwards</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">put forward</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1805"/>
and his arms

          <ptr target="#l11506" type="alt" xml:id="te1805"/>
stretched

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1806"/>
away

          <ptr target="#l11507" type="alt" xml:id="te1806"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1807"/>
up,

          <ptr target="#l11508" type="alt" xml:id="te1807"/>
and his head tilted back,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3520"/>
looking

          <app from="pr3520" n="179.5 (616.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5335">
            <lem wit="A">looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and looking</rdg>
          </app>
up at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3521"/>
sky—

          <app from="pr3521" n="179.5 (616.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la5336">
            <lem wit="MS1b">sky—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sky;</rdg>
          </app>
and then he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1808"/>
begins

          <ptr target="#l11509" type="alt" xml:id="te1808"/>
to rip and rave and grit his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3522"/>
teeth—

          <app from="pr3522" n="179.6 (616.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5337">
            <lem wit="MS1b">teeth—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">teeth;</rdg>
          </app>
and after that, all through his speech he howled, and spread around, and swelled up his chest, and just knocked the spots out of any acting ever

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
see before. This is the speech—I learned it, easy enough, while he was learning it to the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1809"/>
king:

          <ptr target="#l11510" type="alt" xml:id="te1809"/>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <lg>
            <l rend="noindent">
              <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0027"/>
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1810"/>
To be, or not to

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3523"/>
be:

              <app from="pr3523" n="179.10 (618.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5338">
                <lem wit="MS1b">be:</lem>
                <rdg wit="A">be;</rdg>
              </app>
that is the bare bodkin

            </l>
            <l>That makes calamity of so long life;</l>
            <l>
For who would fardels bear, till Birnam

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3524"/>
wood

              <app from="pr3524" n="179.12 (618.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la5339">
                <lem wit="MS1b">wood</lem>
                <rdg wit="A">Wood</rdg>
              </app>
do come to Dunsinane,

            </l>
            <l>But that the fear of something after death</l>
            <l>Murders the innocent sleep,</l>
            <l>Great nature’s second course,</l>
            <l>And makes us rather sling the arrows of outrageous fortune</l>
            <l>Than fly to others that we know not of.</l>
            <l>
There’s the respect must give us

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3525"/>
pause:

            </l>
            <l>
Wake

              <app from="pr3525" n="179.19–20 (619.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5340">
                <lem wit="A">
pause:

                  <lb/>
Wake

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">pause—wake</rdg>
              </app>
Duncan with thy

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1811"/>
knocking!

              <ptr target="#l11512" type="alt" xml:id="te1811"/>
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3526"/>
I would thou couldst;

              <app from="pr3526" n="179.20 (619.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5341">
                <lem wit="A">I would thou couldst;</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5342">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </l>
            <l>For who would bear the whips and scorns of time,</l>
            <l>The oppressor’s wrong, the proud man’s contumely,</l>
            <l>
The law’s delay, and the quietus which his pangs might

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3527"/>
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1812"/>
take

              <ptr target="#l11513" type="alt" xml:id="te1812"/>
              <app from="pr3527" n="179.23 (619.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5343">
                <lem wit="A">take</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
make/

                  <add>take</add>
                </rdg>
              </app>
,

            </l>
            <l>In the dead waste and middle of the night, when churchyards yawn</l>
            <l>In customary suits of solemn black,</l>
            <l>But that the undiscovered country from whose bourne no traveler returns,</l>
            <l>Breathes forth contagion on the world,</l>
            <l>And thus the native hue of resolution, like the poor cat i’ the adage,</l>
            <l>
Is sicklied

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3528"/>
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1813"/>
o’er

              <app from="pr3528" n="179.32 (620.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5344">
                <lem wit="A">o’er</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">oe’r</rdg>
              </app>
              <ptr target="#l11514" type="alt" xml:id="te1813"/>
with care,

            </l>
            <l>
And all the clouds that lowered o’er our

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3529"/>
housetops

              <app from="pr3529" n="179.33 (620.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5345">
                <lem wit="A">housetops</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
house-

                  <lb/>
tops

                </rdg>
              </app>
,

            </l>
            <l>With this regard their currents turn awry,</l>
            <l>And lose the name of action.</l>
            <l>
’Tis a consummation devoutly to be wished. But soft you, the

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1814"/>
fair

              <ptr target="#l11515" type="alt" xml:id="te1814"/>
Ophelia:

            </l>
            <l>Ope not thy ponderous and marble jaws,</l>
            <l>
But get thee to a nunnery—

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3530"/>
go!

              <ptr target="#l11511" type="alt" xml:id="te1810"/>
              <app from="pr3530" n="179.39 (621.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5346">
                <lem wit="A">go!</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">go.</rdg>
              </app>
              <ptr target="#as0191" type="an" xml:id="vs0027"/>
            </l>
          </lg>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44482">
Well, the old man he liked that speech, and he mighty soon got it so he could do it first rate. It seemed like he was just born for it; and

          <pb n="180" xml:id="pb0180"/>
when he had his hand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3531"/>
in,

          <app from="pr3531" n="180.1 (621.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5347">
            <lem wit="MS1b">in,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
in

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and was excited, it was perfectly lovely the way he would rip and tear and rair up behind when he was getting it off

          <app from="pr3493" n="177.29–180.3 (613.5–621.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la5307">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">rest, and . . . off.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">rest.</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44500">
The first chance we got, the duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3532"/>
he

          <app from="pr3532" n="180.4 (621.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5348">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5349">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
had some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3533"/>
show bills

          <app from="pr3533" n="180.4 (621.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la5350">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">show bills</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">show-bills</rdg>
          </app>
printed; and after that, for two or three

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3534"/>
days,

          <app from="pr3534" n="180.5 (622.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5351">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">days,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
days

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
as we floated along, the raft was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3535"/>
a most

          <app from="pr3535" n="180.6 (622.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5352">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">an</rdg>
          </app>
uncommon lively place, for there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3536"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr3536" n="180.6 (622.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5353">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anything</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1815"/>
but

          <ptr target="#l11516" type="alt" xml:id="te1815"/>
sword-fighting and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1816"/>
rehearsing

          <ptr target="#l11517" type="alt" xml:id="te1816"/>
—as the duke called it—going

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3537"/>
on,

          <app from="pr3537" n="180.7 (622.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5354">
            <lem wit="MS1b">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all the time. One morning, when we was

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0028"/>
pretty well down the State of Arkansaw, we come in sight of a little one-horse town in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3538"/>
a big bend

          <app from="pr3538" n="180.9 (622.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5355">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a big bend</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Council Bend</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0192" type="an" xml:id="vs0028"/>
; so we tied up about three-quarters of a mile above it, in the mouth of a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1817"/>
crick

          <ptr target="#l11518" type="alt" xml:id="te1817"/>
which was shut

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1818"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l11519" type="alt" xml:id="te1818"/>
like a tunnel by the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3539"/>
cypress trees

          <app from="pr3539" n="180.11 (623.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5356">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">cypress trees</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">cypress-trees</rdg>
          </app>
, and all of us but Jim took the canoe and went down there to see if there was any chance in that place for our show.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e44589">
We struck it mighty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3540"/>
lucky:

          <app from="pr3540" n="180.14 (623.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5357">
            <lem wit="MS1b">lucky:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">lucky;</rdg>
          </app>
there was going to be a circus there that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3541"/>
afternoon

          <app from="pr3541" n="180.15 (623.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la5358">
            <lem wit="Cent">afternoon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A">
after-

              <lb/>
noon

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and the country people was already beginning to come in, in all kinds of old shackly wagons, and on horses. The circus would leave before night, so our show would have a pretty good chance. The duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3542"/>
he

          <app from="pr3542" n="180.18 (624.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5359">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5360">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
hired the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3543"/>
court house

          <app from="pr3543" n="180.18 (624.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5361">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">court house</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">court-house</rdg>
          </app>
, and we went around and stuck up our bills. They read like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3544"/>
this:

          <app from="pr3544" n="180.19 (624.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5362">
            <lem wit="A">
this:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5363">extra line space</note>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b Cent">
this:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5364">no extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
