Engagements!

                  <lb/>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5398">centeredrule</note>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="A Cent">engagements!</rdg>
              </app>
            </l>
            <milestone rend="plainrule" unit="section"/>
            <l rend="center">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3569"/>
              <hi rend="italic">Admission 25 cents; children and servants 10 cents.</hi>
              <ptr target="#as0193" type="an" xml:id="vs0029"/>
              <milestone rend="plainrule" unit="section"/>
              <app from="pr3569" n="181.16–17 (626.11–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5399">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="italic">Admission 25 cents; children and servants 10 cents.</hi>
                  <lb/>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5400">centered rule</note>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5401">extra line space</note>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS1b">
                  <hi rend="italic">Admission 25 cents; children</hi>
                  <lb/>
                  <hi rend="italic">and servants 10 cents</hi>
.

                  <lb/>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5402">centered rule</note>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5404">no extra line space</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A Cent">
Admission 25 cents; children and servants, 10 cents.

                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5403">extra line space</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </l>
          </lg>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45085">
Then we went loafing around the town. The stores and houses was most all old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3570"/>
shackly

          <app from="pr3570" n="181.19 (626.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la5405">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">shackly</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">shackly,</rdg>
          </app>
dried-up frame concerns that hadn’t ever been painted; they was set up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1823"/>
three

          <ptr target="#l11524" type="alt" xml:id="te1823"/>
or four foot

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3571"/>
above

          <app from="pr3571" n="181.20 (627.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5406">
            <lem wit="A Cent">above</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">from the</rdg>
          </app>
ground on stilts, so as to be out of reach of the water when the river

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3572"/>
was

          <app from="pr3572" n="181.21 (627.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5407">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5408">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
overflowed.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3573"/>
The houses had little gardens around them, but they didn’t seem to raise hardly anything in them but jimpson weeds, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3574"/>
sunflowers

          <app from="pr3574" n="181.24 (627.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la5411">
            <lem wit="C">sunflowers</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b A">
sun-

              <lb/>
flowers

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and ash-piles, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1824"/>
old

          <ptr target="#l11525" type="alt" xml:id="te1824"/>
curled-up boots and shoes, and pieces of bottles, and rags, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1825"/>
played-out

          <ptr target="#l11526" type="alt" xml:id="te1825"/>
tin-ware. The fences was made of different kinds of boards, nailed on at different times; and they leaned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3575"/>
every-which-way

          <app from="pr3575" n="181.27 (628.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la5412">
            <lem wit="C">every-which-way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
every-

              <lb/>
which-way

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">every which-way</rdg>
          </app>
, and had gates that didn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3576"/>
generly

          <app from="pr3576" n="181.27 (628.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5413">
            <lem wit="A">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">generally</rdg>
          </app>
have but one hinge—a leather one. Some of the fences had been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3577"/>
whitewashed

          <app from="pr3577" n="181.29 (628.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la5414">
            <lem wit="A">whitewashed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
white-

              <lb/>
washed

            </rdg>
          </app>
, some time or another, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3578"/>
the duke said it was in Clumbus’s time, like enough. There was generly

          <app from="pr3578" n="181.29–30 (628.10–14)" type="e" xml:id="la5415">
            <lem wit="A">the duke . . . generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">there warn’t a fence in the lot old enough to remember about it. There was generally</rdg>
          </app>
hogs in the garden, and people driving them out.

          <app from="pr3573" n="181.22–31 (627.6–628.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5409">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">The . . . out.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5410">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45184">
All the stores was along one street. They had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3579"/>
white domestic

          <app from="pr3579" n="181.32 (629.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5416">
            <lem wit="MS1b Cent">white domestic</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">white-domestic</rdg>
          </app>
awnings in front, and the country people hitched their horses to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3580"/>
awning posts

          <app from="pr3580" n="181.34 (629.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5417">
            <lem wit="MS1b">awning posts</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">awning-posts</rdg>
          </app>
. There was empty dry-goods boxes under the awnings, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0031"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1826"/>
loafers

          <ptr target="#l11527" type="alt" xml:id="te1826"/>
roosting on them all day long, whittling them with their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3581"/>
Barlow

          <app from="pr3581" n="181.36 (629.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5418">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Barlow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">barlow</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3582"/>
knives;

          <app from="pr3582" n="181.36 (629.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5419">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">knives;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">knives,</rdg>
          </app>
and chawing tobacco, and gaping and yawning and stretching—a mighty ornery lot.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="prg584"/>
They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3584"/>
generly

          <app from="pr3584" n="181.37 (630.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la5422">
            <lem wit="A">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">generally</rdg>
          </app>
had on yellow straw hats most as wide as an umbrella,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3585"/>
but didn’t wear

          <app from="pr3585" n="181.38 (630.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5423">
            <lem wit="A">but didn’t wear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and</rdg>
          </app>
no coats

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3586"/>
nor

          <app from="pr3586" n="181.38 (630.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5424">
            <lem wit="A">nor</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">or</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1827"/>
waistcoats

          <ptr target="#l11528" type="alt" xml:id="te1827"/>
; they called one another Bill, and Buck, and Hank, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3587"/>
Jo

          <app from="pr3587" n="181.40 (630.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5425">
            <lem wit="MS1b">Jo</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Joe</rdg>
          </app>
, and Andy, and talked lazy and drawly, and used considerable many cuss-words. There was as many as one loafer leaning up

          <pb n="182" xml:id="pb0182"/>
against every

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0001"/>
awning

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1828"/>
post

          <ptr target="#l11529" type="alt" xml:id="te1828"/>
          <app from="ra0001" n="182.1 (630.15–631.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0001">
            <lem wit="MS1b">awning post</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">awning-post</rdg>
          </app>
, and he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0002"/>
most

          <app from="ra0002" n="182.1 (631.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0002">
            <lem wit="A">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de0801">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
always had his hands in his britches pockets, except when he fetched them out to lend a chaw of tobacco or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0003"/>
scratch

          <app from="ra0003" n="182.3 (631.6)" type="e" xml:id="da0003">
            <lem wit="A">scratch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">borrow one</rdg>
          </app>
. What a body was hearing amongst them, all the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0004"/>
time, was,

          <app from="ra0004" n="182.4 (631.9)" type="hc" xml:id="da0004">
            <lem wit="MS1b">time, was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
time

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45302">
“Gimme a chaw

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0005"/>
’v

          <app from="ra0005" n="182.5 (631.10)" type="e" xml:id="da0005">
            <lem wit="A">’v</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of</rdg>
          </app>
tobacker, Hank.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45313">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1829"/>
“Cain’t—

          <ptr target="#l11530" type="alt" xml:id="te1829"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0006"/>
hain’t

          <app from="ra0006" n="182.6 (631.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0006">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">haint</rdg>
          </app>
got but one chaw left. Ask Bill.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45326">
Maybe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0007"/>
Bill he

          <app from="ra0007" n="182.7 (632.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0007">
            <lem wit="A">Bill he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Bill</rdg>
          </app>
gives him a chaw; maybe he lies

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0008"/>
and says he ain’t got none

          <app from="ra0008" n="182.7–8 (632.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0008">
            <lem wit="A">and says . . . none</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">about it and gets off</rdg>
          </app>
. Some of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0009"/>
them

          <app from="ra0009" n="182.8 (632.4)" type="e" xml:id="da0009">
            <lem wit="A">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">those</rdg>
          </app>
kinds of loafers never has a cent in the world, nor a chaw of tobacco of their own. They get all their chawing by borrowing—they say to a fellow, “I wisht you’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0010"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1830"/>
len’

          <ptr target="#l11531" type="alt" xml:id="te1830"/>
          <app from="ra0010" n="182.10 (632.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0010">
            <lem wit="A">len’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">lend</rdg>
          </app>
me

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1831"/>
a chaw

          <ptr target="#l11532" type="alt" xml:id="te1831"/>
, Jack, I jist

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1832"/>
this

          <ptr target="#l11533" type="alt" xml:id="te1832"/>
minute give Ben Thompson the last chaw I had”—which

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1833"/>
is

          <ptr target="#l11534" type="alt" xml:id="te1833"/>
a lie,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0011"/>
pretty much every time

          <app from="ra0011" n="182.12 (633.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0011">
            <lem wit="A">pretty much every time</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">you see</rdg>
          </app>
; it don’t fool

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0012"/>
nobody

          <app from="ra0012" n="182.12 (633.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0012">
            <lem wit="A">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0013"/>
but

          <app from="ra0013" n="182.13 (633.4)" type="e" xml:id="da0013">
            <lem wit="A">but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">if</rdg>
          </app>
a stranger; but Jack ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0014"/>
no

          <app from="ra0014" n="182.13 (633.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0014">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a</rdg>
          </app>
stranger,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0015"/>
so

          <app from="ra0015" n="182.13 (633.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0015">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1002">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he says—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45418">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y18201">
            <graphic url="y18201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">gimme a chaw.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45425">
“

          <hi rend="italic">You</hi>
give him a chaw, did you?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0016"/>
So

          <app from="ra0016" n="182.14 (633.7)" type="hc" xml:id="da0016">
            <lem wit="MS1b">So</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">so</rdg>
          </app>
did your sister’s cat’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0017"/>
grandmother

          <app from="ra0017" n="182.14–15 (633.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="da0017">
            <lem wit="A">grandmother</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
grand-

              <lb/>
mother

            </rdg>
          </app>
. You pay me back the chaws you’ve

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0018"/>
awready

          <app from="ra0018" n="182.15 (633.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0018">
            <lem wit="A">awready</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">already</rdg>
          </app>
borry’d

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1834"/>
off’n

          <ptr target="#l11535" type="alt" xml:id="te1834"/>
me, Lafe Buckner, then I’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1835"/>
loan

          <ptr target="#l11536" type="alt" xml:id="te1835"/>
you one or two ton of it, and won’t charge you no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0019"/>
back-intrust

          <app from="ra0019" n="182.17 (634.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0019">
            <lem wit="C">back-intrust</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
back-

              <hi rend="italic">in</hi>
trust

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">back intrust</rdg>
          </app>
, nuther.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45479">
“Well, I

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
pay you back some of it wunst.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45484">
          <pb n="183" xml:id="pb0183"/>
“Yes, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0020"/>
did

          <app from="ra0020" n="183.1 (634.4)" type="e" xml:id="da0020">
            <lem wit="A">did</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—’bout six

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1836"/>
chaws

          <ptr target="#l11537" type="alt" xml:id="te1836"/>
. You borry’d store tobacker and paid back nigger-head.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45500">
Store tobacco is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0021"/>
flat,

          <app from="ra0021" n="183.3 (634.8)" type="hc" xml:id="da0021">
            <lem wit="MS1b">flat,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
flat

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
black plug, but these fellows mostly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0022"/>
chaws

          <app from="ra0022" n="183.3 (634.10)" type="e" xml:id="da0022">
            <lem wit="A">chaws</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">chaw</rdg>
          </app>
the natural leaf

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1837"/>
twisted

          <ptr target="#l11538" type="alt" xml:id="te1837"/>
. When they borrow a chaw, they don’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0023"/>
generly

          <app from="ra0023" n="183.5 (634.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0023">
            <lem wit="A">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">generally</rdg>
          </app>
cut it off with a knife, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0024"/>
they

          <app from="ra0024" n="183.5 (634.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0024">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1003">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
set the plug in between their teeth, and gnaw with their teeth and tug at the plug with their hands till they get it in two—then sometimes the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0025"/>
one that owns

          <app from="ra0025" n="183.7 (635.6)" type="e" xml:id="da0025">
            <lem wit="A">one that owns</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">owner of</rdg>
          </app>
the tobacco looks mournful at it when it’s handed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0026"/>
back

          <app from="ra0026" n="183.8 (635.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0026">
            <lem wit="A">back</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">back to him</rdg>
          </app>
, and says, sarcastic—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45557">
“Here,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0027"/>
gimme

          <app from="ra0027" n="183.10 (635.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0027">
            <lem wit="A">gimme</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
gim

              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the

          <hi rend="italic">chaw</hi>
, and you take the

          <hi rend="italic">plug</hi>
          <ptr target="#as0195" type="an" xml:id="vs0031"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45576">
All the streets and lanes was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1838"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l11539" type="alt" xml:id="te1838"/>
mud,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0028"/>
they warn’t

          <app from="ra0028" n="183.11 (635.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0028">
            <lem wit="A">they warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and</rdg>
          </app>
nothing else

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0029"/>
          <hi rend="italic">but</hi>
mud

          <app from="ra0029" n="183.12 (636.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0029">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">but</hi>
mud

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="la1004">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—mud as black as tar, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0030"/>
nigh

          <app from="ra0030" n="183.12 (636.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0030">
            <lem wit="A">nigh</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">near</rdg>
          </app>
about a foot

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0031"/>
deep,

          <app from="ra0031" n="183.12 (636.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0031">
            <lem wit="MS1b">deep,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
deep

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in some places; and two or three inches deep in

          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0032"/>
the

          <app from="ra0032" n="183.13 (636.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0032">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1005">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
places. The hogs loafed and grunted around, everywheres. You’d see a muddy sow and a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1839"/>
litter

          <ptr target="#l11540" type="alt" xml:id="te1839"/>
of pigs come lazying along the street and whollop herself right down in the way, where folks had to walk

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0033"/>
around

          <app from="ra0033" n="183.16 (636.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0033">
            <lem wit="A">around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">out around</rdg>
          </app>
her, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0034"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1840"/>
she’d

          <ptr target="#l11541" type="alt" xml:id="te1840"/>
          <app from="ra0034" n="183.17 (636.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0034">
            <lem wit="A">she’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">she would</rdg>
          </app>
stretch

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0035"/>
out

          <app from="ra0035" n="183.17 (636.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0035">
            <lem wit="C">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">and out</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">out,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1841"/>
shut

          <ptr target="#l11542" type="alt" xml:id="te1841"/>
her eyes, and wave her ears, whilst the pigs was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0036"/>
milking her

          <app from="ra0036" n="183.18 (637.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0036">
            <lem wit="A">milking her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">sucking</rdg>
          </app>
, and look as happy as if she was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0037"/>
on salary

          <app from="ra0037" n="183.18 (637.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0037">
            <lem wit="A">on salary</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">in the kingdom</rdg>
          </app>
. And pretty soon you’d hear a loafer sing out, “Hi!

          <hi rend="italic">so</hi>
boy! sick him, Tige!” and away

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0038"/>
the

          <app from="ra0038" n="183.20 (637.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0038">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">that</rdg>
          </app>
sow would go, squealing

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1842"/>
most

          <ptr target="#l11543" type="alt" xml:id="te1842"/>
horrible, with a dog or two swinging to each ear, and three or four dozen more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0039"/>
a-coming

          <app from="ra0039" n="183.21–22 (637.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="da0039">
            <lem wit="A">a-coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
a-

              <lb/>
coming

            </rdg>
          </app>
; and then you would see all the loafers get up and watch the thing out of sight, and laugh at the fun and look grateful for the noise. Then they’d settle back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0040"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1843"/>
again,

          <app from="ra0040" n="183.24 (638.5)" type="hc" xml:id="da0040">
            <lem wit="MS1b">again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
again

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11544" type="alt" xml:id="te1843"/>
till there was a dog-fight. There couldn’t anything wake them up all over, and make them happy all over, like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0041"/>
dog-fight

          <app from="ra0041" n="183.26 (638.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="da0041">
            <lem wit="A">dog-fight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
dog-

              <lb/>
fight

            </rdg>
          </app>
—unless it might be putting turpentine on a stray dog and setting fire to him, or tying a tin pan to his tail and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0042"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0062"/>
seeing

          <ptr target="#tb0062" type="te" xml:id="tv0062"/>
          <app from="ra0042" n="✱183.28 (639.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0042">
            <lem wit="MS1b">seeing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">see</rdg>
          </app>
him run himself to death.

          <app from="prg584" n="181.37–183.28 (630.2–639.2)" type="hc" xml:id="lag561">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">They . . . death.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="deg006">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45750">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1844"/>
On

          <ptr target="#l11545" type="alt" xml:id="te1844"/>
the river front some of the houses was sticking out over the bank, and they was bowed and bent, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0043"/>
about

          <app from="ra0043" n="183.30 (639.8)" type="e" xml:id="da0043">
            <lem wit="A Cent">about</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1006">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
ready to tumble in. The people had moved out of them.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1845"/>
The bank

          <ptr target="#l11546" type="alt" xml:id="te1845"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0044"/>
was

          <app from="ra0044" n="183.31 (639.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0044">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">had</rdg>
          </app>
caved away under

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0045"/>
one

          <app from="ra0045" n="183.32 (639.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0045">
            <lem wit="A Cent">one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">a</rdg>
          </app>
corner of some others, and that corner was hanging

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0046"/>
over. People

          <app from="ra0046" n="183.32 (639.15–640.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0046">
            <lem wit="A Cent">over. People</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
over.—

              <milestone unit="page"/>
Peopled

            </rdg>
          </app>
lived in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0047"/>
them,

          <app from="ra0047" n="183.33 (640.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0047">
            <lem wit="MS1b">them,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
them

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet, but it was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0048"/>
dangersome

          <app from="ra0048" n="183.33 (640.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="da0048">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dangersome</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
danger-

              <lb/>
some

            </rdg>
          </app>
, because sometimes a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1846"/>
strip

          <ptr target="#l11547" type="alt" xml:id="te1846"/>
of land as wide as a house caves in at a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0049"/>
time.

          <app from="ra0049" n="183.34 (640.6)" type="e" xml:id="da0049">
            <lem wit="A Cent">time.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
time.—

              <lb/>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0050"/>
Sometimes a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1847"/>
belt

          <ptr target="#l11548" type="alt" xml:id="te1847"/>
of land a quarter of a mile deep will

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0051"/>
start in and cave along and cave along till it all caves

          <app from="ra0051" n="183.35–36 (640.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0051">
            <lem wit="A">start . . . caves</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">cave</rdg>
          </app>
into the river in one summer.

          <app from="ra0050" n="183.34–36 (640.7–11)" type="hc" xml:id="da0050">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">Sometimes . . . summer.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1070">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Such a town as that has to be always moving back,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0052"/>
and back, and back,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0032"/>
because

          <app from="ra0052" n="183.37 (640.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0052">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and back, and back, because</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">to save itself;</rdg>
          </app>
the river’s always gnawing at it

          <ptr target="#as0196" type="an" xml:id="vs0032"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45860">
The nearer it got to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0053"/>
noon,

          <app from="ra0053" n="183.39 (641.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0053">
            <lem wit="MS1b">noon,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
noon

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that day, the thicker and thicker was

          <pb n="184" xml:id="pb0184"/>
the wagons and horses in the streets, and more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0054"/>
coming,

          <app from="ra0054" n="184.1 (641.4)" type="hc" xml:id="da0054">
            <lem wit="MS1b">coming,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
coming

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all the time. Families fetched their dinners with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0055"/>
them,

          <app from="ra0055" n="184.2 (641.6)" type="hc" xml:id="da0055">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">them,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
them

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
from the country, and eat them in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0056"/>
wagons. There

          <app from="ra0056" n="184.3 (641.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="da0056">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wagons. There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
wagons.—

              <lb/>
There

            </rdg>
          </app>
was considerable

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0057"/>
whisky drinking

          <app from="ra0057" n="184.3–4 (641.10)" type="hc" xml:id="da0057">
            <lem wit="MS1b">whisky drinking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">whiskey drinking</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">whisky-drinking</rdg>
          </app>
going on, and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0058"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1848"/>
seen

          <ptr target="#l11549" type="alt" xml:id="te1848"/>
          <app from="ra0058" n="184.4 (641.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0058">
            <lem wit="A Cent">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saw</rdg>
          </app>
three fights.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0059"/>
By and by somebody sings out,—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45923">“Here comes old Boggs!—in from the country for his little old monthly drunk—here he comes, boys!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45925">All the loafers looked glad—I reckoned they was used to having fun out of Boggs. One of them says—</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45927">
“Wonder who he’s a gwyne to chaw up this time. If he’d a chawed up all the men he’s ben a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0061"/>
gwyne

          <app from="ra0061" n="184.11 (642.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0061">
            <lem wit="A">gwyne</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">gwyne</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to chaw up in the last twenty year, he’d have

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1849"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0062"/>
considerble

          <app from="ra0062" n="184.12 (642.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="da0062">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">considable</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11550" type="alt" xml:id="te1849"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1850"/>
ruputation

          <ptr target="#l11551" type="alt" xml:id="te1850"/>
, now.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45952">
Another

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0144"/>
one

          <app from="ra0144" n="187.13 (659.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0144">
            <lem wit="A">one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1018">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
says, “I wisht old Boggs ’d threaten

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0064"/>
me—

          <app from="ra0064" n="184.13 (643.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0064">
            <lem wit="MS1b">me—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">me,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1851"/>
’cuz

          <ptr target="#l11552" type="alt" xml:id="te1851"/>
then I’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0065"/>
know

          <app from="ra0065" n="184.14 (643.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0065">
            <lem wit="A">know</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">know</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I warn’t gwyne to die for a thousan’ year.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45984">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1852"/>
Boggs

          <ptr target="#l11553" type="alt" xml:id="te1852"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0066"/>
comes

          <app from="ra0066" n="184.15 (643.6)" type="e" xml:id="da0066">
            <lem wit="A">comes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">come</rdg>
          </app>
a-tearing along on his horse, whooping and yelling like an Injun, and singing out—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e45996">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0067"/>
Cler

          <app from="ra0067" n="184.17 (643.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0067">
            <lem wit="A">Cler</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Clar</rdg>
          </app>
the track,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0068"/>
thar.

          <app from="ra0068" n="184.17 (643.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0068">
            <lem wit="A">thar.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">thar!</rdg>
          </app>
I’m on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0069"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1853"/>
waw

          <ptr target="#l11554" type="alt" xml:id="te1853"/>
path

          <app from="ra0069" n="184.17 (643.12)" type="hc" xml:id="da0069">
            <lem wit="MS1b">waw path</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">waw-path</rdg>
          </app>
, and the price

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0070"/>
uv

          <app from="ra0070" n="184.17 (643.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0070">
            <lem wit="A">uv</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of</rdg>
          </app>
coffins is a gwyne to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0071"/>
raise.

          <app from="ra0071" n="184.18 (643.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0071">
            <lem wit="A">raise.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">rise!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46042">
He was drunk, and weaving about in his saddle; he was over fifty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0072"/>
year

          <app from="ra0072" n="184.20 (644.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0072">
            <lem wit="A">year</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">years</rdg>
          </app>
old, and had a very red face. Everybody yelled at him, and laughed at him, and sassed him, and he sassed back, and said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0073"/>
he’d

          <app from="ra0073" n="184.21 (644.7)" type="e" xml:id="da0073">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">he would</rdg>
          </app>
attend to them and lay them out in their regular turns, but he couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0074"/>
wait,

          <app from="ra0074" n="184.23 (644.10)" type="hc" xml:id="da0074">
            <lem wit="MS1b">wait,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
wait

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, because he’d come to town to kill old Colonel Sherburn, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1854"/>
his

          <ptr target="#l11555" type="alt" xml:id="te1854"/>
motto was, “meat first, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0075"/>
spoon-vittles

          <app from="ra0075" n="184.24 (644.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="da0075">
            <lem wit="C">spoon-vittles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
spoon-

              <lb/>
vittles

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">spoon vittles</rdg>
          </app>
to top off on.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46085">
He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0076"/>
see

          <app from="ra0076" n="184.26 (645.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0076">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saw</rdg>
          </app>
me, and rode up and says—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46095">
“Whar’d you come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0077"/>
f’m

          <app from="ra0077" n="184.27 (645.4)" type="e" xml:id="da0077">
            <lem wit="A">f’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">from</rdg>
          </app>
, boy?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1855"/>
You

          <ptr target="#l11556" type="alt" xml:id="te1855"/>
prepared to die?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46109">
Then he rode

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0078"/>
on. I

          <app from="ra0078" n="184.28 (645.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="da0078">
            <lem wit="A">on. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
on.—

              <lb/>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0079"/>
scared

          <app from="ra0079" n="184.28 (645.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="da0079">
            <lem wit="A">scared</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">most scared to death</rdg>
          </app>
; but a man says—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46129">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0080"/>
He

          <app from="ra0080" n="184.29 (645.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0080">
            <lem wit="A">He</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">He</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
don’t mean nothing; he’s always a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0081"/>
carryin’

          <app from="ra0081" n="184.29 (645.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="da0081">
            <lem wit="A">carryin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">carrying</rdg>
          </app>
on like

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1856"/>
that, when he’s drunk.

          <ptr target="#l11557" type="alt" xml:id="te1856"/>
He’s the best-naturedest old fool in Arkansaw—never

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0082"/>
hurt nobody

          <app from="ra0082" n="184.31 (645.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="da0082">
            <lem wit="A">hurt nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">hurts anybody</rdg>
          </app>
, drunk

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0083"/>
nor

          <app from="ra0083" n="184.31 (645.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0083">
            <lem wit="A">nor</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">or</rdg>
          </app>
sober.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46170">Boggs rode up before the biggest store in town and bent his head down so he could see under the curtain of the awning, and yells—</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46172">
“Come out here, Sherburn!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0084"/>
—come

          <app from="ra0084" n="184.34 (646.8)" type="hc" xml:id="da0084">
            <lem wit="MS1b">—come</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Come</rdg>
          </app>
out and meet the man you’ve swindled. You’re the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1857"/>
houn’

          <ptr target="#l11558" type="alt" xml:id="te1857"/>
I’m after, and I’m a gwyne to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0085"/>
have

          <app from="ra0085" n="184.35 (646.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0085">
            <lem wit="A">have</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <hi rend="italic">have</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you, too!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y18501">
          <graphic url="y18501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">a little monthly drunk</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46201">
And so he went on, calling Sherburn everything he could lay his tongue to, and the whole street packed with people listening and

          <pb n="185" xml:id="pb0185"/>
laughing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0086"/>
and going on

          <app from="ra0086" n="185.1 (647.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0086">
            <lem wit="A">and going on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1001">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0087"/>
By and by

          <app from="ra0087" n="185.1 (647.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0087">
            <lem wit="MS1b">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0088"/>
proud looking

          <app from="ra0088" n="185.1 (647.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0088">
            <lem wit="MS1b">proud looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">proud-looking</rdg>
          </app>
man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0089"/>
about

          <app from="ra0089" n="185.1 (647.4)" type="e" xml:id="da0089">
            <lem wit="A">about</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of about</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0090"/>
fifty-five,

          <app from="ra0090" n="185.1–2 (647.4)" type="hc" xml:id="da0090">
            <lem wit="MS1b">fifty-five,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fifty-five</rdg>
          </app>
—and he was a heap the best dressed man in that town, too—steps out of the store, and the crowd drops back on each side to let him come. He says to Boggs, mighty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0091"/>
ca’m

          <app from="ra0091" n="185.4 (647.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0091">
            <lem wit="A">ca’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">calm</rdg>
          </app>
and slow—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0092"/>
he says:

          <app from="ra0092" n="185.4 (647.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0092">
            <lem wit="A">he says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1011">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46263">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0093"/>
I’m

          <app from="ra0093" n="185.5 (647.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0093">
            <lem wit="A">I’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">I am</rdg>
          </app>
tired of this; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0094"/>
I’ll

          <app from="ra0094" n="185.5 (647.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0094">
            <lem wit="A">I’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">I will</rdg>
          </app>
endure it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0095"/>
till

          <app from="ra0095" n="185.5 (647.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0095">
            <lem wit="A">till</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">until</rdg>
          </app>
one o’clock. Till one o’clock, mind—no longer. If you open your mouth against me only once, after that time, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0096"/>
can’t

          <app from="ra0096" n="185.7 (648.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0096">
            <lem wit="A">can’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">cannot</rdg>
          </app>
travel so far but I will find you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46298">
Then he turns and goes in. The crowd looked mighty sober; nobody stirred, and there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0097"/>
warn’t no

          <app from="ra0097" n="185.9 (648.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0097">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t any</rdg>
          </app>
more laughing. Boggs rode off blackguarding Sherburn as loud as he could yell, all down the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1858"/>
street;

          <ptr target="#l11559" type="alt" xml:id="te1858"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0098"/>
pretty soon

          <app from="ra0098" n="185.11 (648.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0098">
            <lem wit="A">pretty soon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">presently</rdg>
          </app>
back he comes and stops before the store, still keeping it up. Some men crowded around him and tried to get him to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1859"/>
shut

          <ptr target="#l11560" type="alt" xml:id="te1859"/>
up, but he wouldn’t; they told

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1860"/>
him

          <ptr target="#l11561" type="alt" xml:id="te1860"/>
it would be one o’clock in about fifteen minutes, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0099"/>
so

          <app from="ra0099" n="185.14 (649.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0099">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1012">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he

          <hi rend="italic">must</hi>
go home—he must go right away. But it didn’t do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0100"/>
no

          <app from="ra0100" n="185.15 (649.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0100">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any</rdg>
          </app>
good. He cussed away, with all his might,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0101"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1861"/>
throwed

          <app from="ra0101" n="185.16 (649.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0101">
            <lem wit="A">and throwed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">throwed</rdg>
          </app>
his hat down in the mud and rode over it,

          <ptr target="#l11562" type="alt" xml:id="te1861"/>
and pretty soon away he went a-raging down the street

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0102"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1862"/>
again

          <app from="ra0102" n="185.17 (650.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0102">
            <lem wit="MS1b">again</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">again,</rdg>
          </app>
with his gray hair

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0103"/>
a flying

          <app from="ra0103" n="185.18 (650.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0103">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a flying</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a-flying</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l11563" type="alt" xml:id="te1862"/>
Everybody that could get a chance at him tried

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0104"/>
their best

          <app from="ra0104" n="185.18 (650.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0104">
            <lem wit="A">their best</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1013">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to coax him off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0105"/>
of

          <app from="ra0105" n="185.19 (650.4)" type="e" xml:id="da0105">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1014">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
his horse

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1863"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l11564" type="alt" xml:id="te1863"/>
they could lock him up and get him sober; but it warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0106"/>
no

          <app from="ra0106" n="185.20 (650.8)" type="e" xml:id="da0106">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">any</rdg>
          </app>
use—up the street he would tear again, and give Sherburn another cussing.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0107"/>
By and by,

          <app from="ra0107" n="185.21 (650.11)" type="hc" xml:id="da0107">
            <lem wit="MS1b">By and by,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
somebody says—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46422">“Go for his daughter!—quick, go for his daughter; sometimes he’ll listen to her. If anybody can persuade him, she can.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46424">
          <pb n="186" xml:id="pb0186"/>
So somebody started on a run. I walked down street

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1864"/>
a ways

          <ptr target="#l11565" type="alt" xml:id="te1864"/>
, and stopped. In about five or

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1865"/>
ten

          <ptr target="#l11566" type="alt" xml:id="te1865"/>
minutes, here comes Boggs again—but not on his horse. He was a-reeling across the street towards me,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1866"/>
bareheaded,

          <ptr target="#l11567" type="alt" xml:id="te1866"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1867"/>
with

          <ptr target="#l11568" type="alt" xml:id="te1867"/>
a friend on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0108"/>
both sides

          <app from="ra0108" n="186.4 (651.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="da0108">
            <lem wit="A">both sides</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">each side</rdg>
          </app>
of him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0109"/>
a-holt

          <app from="ra0109" n="186.4 (651.15)" type="hc" xml:id="da0109">
            <lem wit="MS1b">a-holt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">aholt</rdg>
          </app>
of his arms and hurrying him along. He was quiet,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1868"/>
and looked uneasy

          <ptr target="#l11569" type="alt" xml:id="te1868"/>
; and he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0110"/>
warn’t

          <app from="ra0110" n="186.6 (652.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0110">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
hanging

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0111"/>
back,

          <app from="ra0111" n="186.6 (652.4)" type="hc" xml:id="da0111">
            <lem wit="MS1b">back,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
back

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
any, but was doing some of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0112"/>
hurrying,

          <app from="ra0112" n="186.6 (652.6)" type="hc" xml:id="da0112">
            <lem wit="MS1b">hurrying,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
hurrying

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
himself.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0113"/>
Somebody sings

          <app from="ra0113" n="186.7 (652.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="da0113">
            <lem wit="A">Somebody sings</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">I heard somebody sing</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0060"/>
out—

          <app from="ra0060" n="184.5 (641.13)" type="hc" xml:id="da0060">
            <lem wit="MS1b">out,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
—

            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46504">“Boggs!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46506">
I looked over there to see who

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0114"/>
said

          <app from="ra0114" n="186.9 (652.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0114">
            <lem wit="A">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">it was that said</rdg>
          </app>
it, and it was that Colonel Sherburn. He was standing perfectly still, in the street, and had a pistol

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0115"/>
raised,

          <app from="ra0115" n="186.11 (653.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0115">
            <lem wit="MS1b">raised,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
raised

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in his right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0116"/>
hand,

          <app from="ra0116" n="186.11 (653.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0116">
            <lem wit="MS1b">hand,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
hand

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—not aiming it, but holding it out with the barrel tilted up towards the sky. The same

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0117"/>
second,

          <app from="ra0117" n="186.12 (653.5)" type="hc" xml:id="da0117">
            <lem wit="MS1b">second,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
second

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0118"/>
see

          <app from="ra0118" n="186.12 (653.6)" type="e" xml:id="da0118">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saw</rdg>
          </app>
a young girl coming on the run, and two men with her. Boggs and the men turned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0119"/>
round

          <app from="ra0119" n="186.14 (653.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0119">
            <lem wit="A">round</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">around</rdg>
          </app>
, to see who called him, and when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0120"/>
they see

          <app from="ra0120" n="186.14 (653.11)" type="e" xml:id="da0120">
            <lem wit="A">they see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">they saw</rdg>
          </app>
the pistol the men jumped

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1869"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l11570" type="alt" xml:id="te1869"/>
one side, and the pistol barrel come down slow and steady to a level—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0121"/>
both

          <app from="ra0121" n="186.16 (654.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0121">
            <lem wit="A">both</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">it had both</rdg>
          </app>
barrels

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0122"/>
cocked.

          <app from="ra0122" n="186.16 (654.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0122">
            <lem wit="A">cocked.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">cocked—</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0033"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1870"/>
Boggs

          <ptr target="#l11571" type="alt" xml:id="te1870"/>
throws up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0123"/>
both of

          <app from="ra0123" n="186.17 (654.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0123">
            <lem wit="A">both of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1015">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0124"/>
hands

          <app from="ra0124" n="186.17 (654.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0124">
            <lem wit="MS1b">hands</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hands,</rdg>
          </app>
and says, “O Lord, don’t shoot!”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0125"/>
Bang!

          <app from="ra0125" n="186.17 (654.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0125">
            <lem wit="A">Bang!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">—bang</rdg>
          </app>
goes the first shot

          <ptr target="#as0197" type="an" xml:id="vs0033"/>
, and he staggers

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0126"/>
back,

          <app from="ra0126" n="186.18 (654.6)" type="hc" xml:id="da0126">
            <lem wit="MS1b">back,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
back

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
clawing at the air—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0127"/>
bang!

          <app from="ra0127" n="186.18 (654.8)" type="e" xml:id="da0127">
            <lem wit="A">bang!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
bang

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
goes the second

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0128"/>
one

          <app from="ra0128" n="186.19 (654.8)" type="e" xml:id="da0128">
            <lem wit="A">one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1016">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, and he tumbles backwards

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0129"/>
onto

          <app from="ra0129" n="186.19 (654.10)" type="e" xml:id="da0129">
            <lem wit="A">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">to</rdg>
          </app>
the ground, heavy and solid, with his arms spread out. That young girl screamed out, and comes rushing, and down she throws herself on her father, crying, and saying, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0130"/>
O

          <app from="ra0130" n="186.22 (655.2)" type="hc" xml:id="da0130">
            <lem wit="MS1b">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, he’s killed him, he’s killed him!” The crowd closed up around them, and shouldered and jammed one another, with their necks stretched, trying to see, and people on the inside

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1871"/>
trying to

          <ptr target="#l11572" type="alt" xml:id="te1871"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1872"/>
shove

          <ptr target="#l11573" type="alt" xml:id="te1872"/>
them back, and shouting, “Back, back! give him air, give him air!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46670">
Colonel Sherburn he tossed his pistol onto the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0131"/>
ground

          <app from="ra0131" n="186.27 (655.15)" type="hc" xml:id="da0131">
            <lem wit="MS1b">ground</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ground,</rdg>
          </app>
and turned around on his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0132"/>
heel

          <app from="ra0132" n="186.28 (656.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0132">
            <lem wit="MS1b">heel</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">heels</rdg>
          </app>
and walked off.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y18701">
          <graphic url="y18701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the death of boggs</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46694">
They took Boggs to a little drug

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0133"/>
store—

          <app from="ra0133" n="186.29 (656.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0133">
            <lem wit="MS1b">store—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">store,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1873"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l11574" type="alt" xml:id="te1873"/>
crowd pressing around, just the same, and the whole town following, and I rushed and got a good place at the window, where I was close to him and could see in. They laid him on the floor, and put one large Bible under his head, and opened another one and spread it on his breast—but they tore open his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0134"/>
shirt,

          <app from="ra0134" n="186.34 (656.16)" type="hc" xml:id="da0134">
            <lem wit="MS1b">shirt,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
shirt

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
first, and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0135"/>
seen

          <app from="ra0135" n="186.34 (656.16)" type="e" xml:id="da0135">
            <lem wit="A">seen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">saw</rdg>
          </app>
where one of the bullets went in. He made about a dozen long gasps, his breast lifting the Bible up when he drawed in his breath, and letting it down again when he breathed it out—and after that he laid still; he was dead. Then they pulled his daughter away from him,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1874"/>
screaming

          <ptr target="#l11575" type="alt" xml:id="te1874"/>
and

          <pb n="187" xml:id="pb0187"/>
crying, and took her off. She was about sixteen, and very sweet and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0136"/>
gentle-looking

          <app from="ra0136" n="187.2 (657.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="da0136">
            <lem wit="A">gentle-looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">gentle-looking and pretty</rdg>
          </app>
, but awful pale and scared.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46739">
Well, pretty soon the whole town was there, squirming and scrouging and pushing and shoving to get at the window and have a look, but people that had the places wouldn’t give them up, and folks behind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0137"/>
them

          <app from="ra0137" n="187.6 (658.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0137">
            <lem wit="A">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1017">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
was saying all the time, “Say, now, you’ve looked enough, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0138"/>
fellows; ’tain’t

          <app from="ra0138" n="187.7 (658.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0138">
            <lem wit="C">fellows; ’tain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">fellows; t’ain’t</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">fellows; ’taint</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0139"/>
right,

          <app from="ra0139" n="187.7 (658.12)" type="hc" xml:id="da0139">
            <lem wit="MS1b">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0140"/>
’tain’t fair

          <app from="ra0140" n="187.7 (658.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0140">
            <lem wit="C">’tain’t fair</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">t’ain’t fair</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">’taint fair</rdg>
          </app>
, for you to stay thar all the time, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1875"/>
never

          <ptr target="#l11576" type="alt" xml:id="te1875"/>
give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0141"/>
nobody

          <app from="ra0141" n="187.8 (658.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="da0141">
            <lem wit="A">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">anybody else</rdg>
          </app>
a chance; other folks has their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0142"/>
rights,

          <app from="ra0142" n="187.9 (659.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0142">
            <lem wit="MS1b">rights,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rights

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
as well as you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46799">
There was considerable jawing back, so I slid out, thinking maybe there was going to be trouble. The streets was full, and everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0143"/>
was excited

          <app from="ra0143" n="187.12 (659.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0143">
            <lem wit="A">was excited</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">excited</rdg>
          </app>
. Everybody that seen the shooting was telling how it happened, and there was a big crowd packed around each

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0063"/>
one

          <app from="ra0063" n="184.13 (643.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0063">
            <lem wit="A">one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1009">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of these fellows, stretching their necks and listening. One long lanky

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0145"/>
man

          <app from="ra0145" n="187.15 (660.4)" type="hc" xml:id="da0145">
            <lem wit="MS1b">man</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">man,</rdg>
          </app>
with long hair and a big white fur

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0146"/>
stove-pipe

          <app from="ra0146" n="187.15 (660.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="da0146">
            <lem wit="A">stove-pipe</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">
stove-

              <lb/>
pipe

            </rdg>
          </app>
hat on the back of his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0147"/>
head

          <app from="ra0147" n="187.16 (660.7)" type="hc" xml:id="da0147">
            <lem wit="MS1b">head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">head,</rdg>
          </app>
and a crooked-handled cane, marked out the places on the

          <pb n="188" xml:id="pb0188"/>
ground where Boggs stood, and where Sherburn

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0148"/>
stood—

          <app from="ra0148" n="188.1 (660.12)" type="hc" xml:id="da0148">
            <lem wit="MS1b">stood—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stood,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0149"/>
and the

          <app from="ra0149" n="188.1 (660.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0149">
            <lem wit="A">and the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">the</rdg>
          </app>
people following him around from one place to t’other and watching everything he done, and bobbing their heads to show they understood, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0150"/>
stooping

          <app from="ra0150" n="188.4 (661.4)" type="hc" xml:id="da0150">
            <lem wit="MS1b,A">stooping</lem>
            <rdg wit="Pfs1">stopping</rdg>
          </app>
a little and resting their hands on their thighs to watch him mark the places on the ground with his cane; and then he stood

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1876"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l11577" type="alt" xml:id="te1876"/>
straight and stiff where

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0151"/>
Sherburn

          <app from="ra0151" n="188.6 (661.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0151">
            <lem wit="A">Sherburn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Sherburne</rdg>
          </app>
had stood,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0152"/>
frowning,

          <app from="ra0152" n="188.6 (661.13)" type="hc" xml:id="da0152">
            <lem wit="MS1b">frowning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
frowning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and having his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0153"/>
hat brim

          <app from="ra0153" n="188.7 (661.14)" type="hc" xml:id="da0153">
            <lem wit="MS1b">hat brim</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hat-brim</rdg>
          </app>
down over his eyes, and sung out, “Boggs!” and then fetched his cane down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0154"/>
slow,

          <app from="ra0154" n="188.8 (662.2)" type="hc" xml:id="da0154">
            <lem wit="MS1b">slow,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
slow

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to a level, and says

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1877"/>
“Bang!”

          <ptr target="#l11578" type="alt" xml:id="te1877"/>
staggered backwards, says “Bang!” again, and fell down flat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0155"/>
on

          <app from="ra0155" n="188.9 (662.8)" type="e" xml:id="da0155">
            <lem wit="A">on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">of</rdg>
          </app>
his back.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0034"/>
The people that had seen the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0156"/>
thing

          <app from="ra0156" n="188.10 (662.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="da0156">
            <lem wit="A">thing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">thing all</rdg>
          </app>
said he done it perfect

          <ptr target="#as0198" type="an" xml:id="vs0034"/>
; said it was just exactly the way it all happened. Then as much as a dozen people got out their bottles and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0033"/>
treated him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46937">
Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0157"/>
by and by

          <app from="ra0157" n="188.13 (663.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0157">
            <lem wit="MS1b">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0035"/>
somebody said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0158"/>
Sherburn

          <app from="ra0158" n="188.13 (663.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0158">
            <lem wit="A">Sherburn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">Sherburne</rdg>
          </app>
ought to be lynched. In about a minute everybody was saying it; so away they went, mad and yelling, and snatching down every

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0159"/>
clothes line

          <app from="ra0159" n="188.15 (663.9)" type="hc" xml:id="da0159">
            <lem wit="MS1b">clothes line</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">clothes-line</rdg>
          </app>
they come to, to do the hanging

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0160"/>
with.

          <app from="ra0160" n="188.16 (663.10–13)" type="e" xml:id="da0160">
            <lem wit="A">with.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b">with. But they was too late. Sherburn’s friends had got him away, long ago.</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0199" type="an" xml:id="vs0035"/>
          <ptr target="#mt0033" type="alt" xml:id="wn0033"/>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0363">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXII.</head>
        <pb n="189" xml:id="pb0189"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e46978">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y18901">
            <graphic url="y18901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0161"/>
Chapter XXII. They

            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1891">
            <graphic url="hf1891.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">sherburn steps out</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e46988">
          <app from="ra0161" n="189 title–1 (160.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0161">
            <lem wit="A">Chapter XXII. [¶] They</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1019">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
They

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0036"/>
swarmed up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0162"/>
street,

          <app from="ra0162" n="189.1 (160.1)" type="hc" xml:id="da0162">
            <lem wit="MS2">street,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
street

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
towards Sherburn’s house, a-whooping and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1878"/>
yelling

          <ptr target="#l11579" type="alt" xml:id="te1878"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1879"/>
and raging

          <ptr target="#l11580" type="alt" xml:id="te1879"/>
like Injuns, and everything had to clear the way or get run over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1880"/>
and tromped

          <ptr target="#l11581" type="alt" xml:id="te1880"/>
to mush, and it was awful to see. Children was heeling

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1881"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l11582" type="alt" xml:id="te1881"/>
ahead of the mob, screaming and trying to get out of the way; and every window along the road was full of women’s heads, and there was nigger boys in every tree, and bucks and wenches looking over every fence; and as soon as the mob would get nearly to them they would break and skaddle back out of reach.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1882"/>
Lots

          <ptr target="#l11583" type="alt" xml:id="te1882"/>
of the women and girls was crying and taking on, scared most to death.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47029">
They swarmed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1883"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l11584" type="alt" xml:id="te1883"/>
in front of Sherburn’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1884"/>
palings

          <ptr target="#l11585" type="alt" xml:id="te1884"/>
as thick as they could

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1885"/>
jam together

          <ptr target="#l11586" type="alt" xml:id="te1885"/>
, and you couldn’t hear yourself think for the noise. It was a little twenty-foot yard. Some sung

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0163"/>
out,

          <app from="ra0163" n="189.23 (161.12)" type="hc" xml:id="da0163">
            <lem wit="MS2">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
“Tear down the fence! tear down the fence!” Then there was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0164"/>
racket

          <app from="ra0164" n="189.24 (161.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0164">
            <lem wit="A">racket</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sound</rdg>
          </app>
of ripping and tearing and smashing, and down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0165"/>
she goes

          <app from="ra0165" n="189.25 (161.16)" type="e" xml:id="da0165">
            <lem wit="A">she goes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">went the fence</rdg>
          </app>
, and the front wall of the crowd

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0166"/>
begins

          <app from="ra0166" n="189.26 (162.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0166">
            <lem wit="A">begins</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">begun</rdg>
          </app>
to roll in like a wave.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47077">
Just then Sherburn

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1886"/>
steps

          <ptr target="#l11587" type="alt" xml:id="te1886"/>
out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0167"/>
onto

          <app from="ra0167" n="189.27 (162.5)" type="hc" xml:id="da0167">
            <lem wit="MS2">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">on to</rdg>
          </app>
the roof

          <ptr target="#as0200" type="an" xml:id="vs0036"/>
of his little front porch, with a double-barrel gun in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1887"/>
his hand

          <ptr target="#l11588" type="alt" xml:id="te1887"/>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0168"/>
takes

          <app from="ra0168" n="189.28 (162.8)" type="e" xml:id="da0168">
            <lem wit="A">takes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">took</rdg>
          </app>
his stand, perfectly ca’m and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1888"/>
deliberate,

          <ptr target="#l11589" type="alt" xml:id="te1888"/>
not saying a word. The

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1889"/>
racket

          <ptr target="#l11590" type="alt" xml:id="te1889"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0169"/>
stopped, and the wave sucked back.

          <app from="ra0169" n="189.29–30 (162.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="da0169">
            <lem wit="A">stopped, and . . . back.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">stopped. The crowd fell back.</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47121">
Sherburn never said a word—just stood there, looking down.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0170"/>
The

          <app from="ra0170" n="189.31 (162.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0170">
            <lem wit="A">The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">It seemed to me that the</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="190" xml:id="pb0190"/>
stillness was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0171"/>
awful

          <app from="ra0171" n="190.1 (162.16–163.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0171">
            <lem wit="A">awful</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">as awful, now, as the racket was before; and some-how it was more</rdg>
          </app>
creepy and uncomfortable. Sherburn run his eye slow along the crowd; and wherever

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0172"/>
it

          <app from="ra0172" n="190.2 (163.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0172">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">his eye</rdg>
          </app>
struck, the people tried a little to outgaze him,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0173"/>
but they

          <app from="ra0173" n="190.3 (163.7)" type="e" xml:id="da0173">
            <lem wit="A">but they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">but</rdg>
          </app>
couldn’t; they dropped their eyes and looked

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1890"/>
sneaky

          <ptr target="#l11591" type="alt" xml:id="te1890"/>
. Then pretty soon Sherburn sort of laughed; not the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0174"/>
pleasant kind

          <app from="ra0174" n="190.5 (163.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="da0174">
            <lem wit="A">pleasant kind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kind of laugh you hear at the circus</rdg>
          </app>
, but the kind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0175"/>
that makes you feel like when you are eating bread that’s got sand in it

          <app from="ra0175" n="190.5–6 (163.12–14)" type="e" xml:id="da0175">
            <lem wit="A">that makes . . . it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that’s fitten for a funeral—the kind that makes you feel crawly</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47178">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0176"/>
Then

          <app from="ra0176" n="190.7 (163.15)" type="e" xml:id="da0176">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] Then</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de1020">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Then

            </rdg>
          </app>
he says, slow and scornful:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47191">
“The idea of

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
lynching anybody!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0177"/>
It’s

          <app from="ra0177" n="190.8 (163.17)" type="e" xml:id="da0177">
            <lem wit="A">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">It is</rdg>
          </app>
amusing. The idea of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0178"/>
you thinking

          <app from="ra0178" n="190.8–9 (164.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0178">
            <lem wit="A">you thinking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your thinking</rdg>
          </app>
you had pluck enough to lynch a

          <hi rend="italic">man!</hi>
Because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0179"/>
you’re

          <app from="ra0179" n="190.9 (164.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0179">
            <lem wit="C">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
you are (

              <ref corresp="bib20892" type="dbquery">MS2</ref>
); you re

            </rdg>
          </app>
brave enough to tar and feather poor friendless cast-out women that come along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0180"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1891"/>
here

          <ptr target="#l11592" type="alt" xml:id="te1891"/>
, did that make you think you had grit

          <app from="ra0180" n="190.11 (164.6–10)" type="e" xml:id="da0180">
            <lem wit="A">here, did . . . grit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">here lowering themselves to your level to earn a bite of bitter bread to eat, did it fool you into thinking you had courage</rdg>
          </app>
enough to lay your hands on a

          <hi rend="italic">man?</hi>
Why, a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0181"/>
          <hi rend="italic">man’s</hi>
          <app from="ra0181" n="190.12 (164.12)" type="e" xml:id="da0181">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">man’s</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">man</hi>
is

            </rdg>
          </app>
safe in the hands of ten thousand of your kind—as long as it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0182"/>
daytime

          <app from="ra0182" n="190.13 (164.14)" type="hc" xml:id="da0182">
            <lem wit="MS2">daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-time</rdg>
          </app>
and you’re not behind him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47262">
“Do I know you? I know you clear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0183"/>
through

          <app from="ra0183" n="190.15 (164.17–165.1)" type="e" xml:id="da0183">
            <lem wit="A">through</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">through to your chicken hearts</rdg>
          </app>
. I was born and raised in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0184"/>
south

          <app from="ra0184" n="190.16 (165.2)" type="hc" xml:id="da0184">
            <lem wit="MS2">south</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">South</rdg>
          </app>
, and I’ve lived in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0185"/>
north

          <app from="ra0185" n="190.16 (165.3)" type="hc" xml:id="da0185">
            <lem wit="MS2">north</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">North</rdg>
          </app>
; so I know the average

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0186"/>
all around

          <app from="ra0186" n="190.16–17 (165.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="da0186">
            <lem wit="A">all around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">man of the country, and the average man of the world</rdg>
          </app>
. The average

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0187"/>
man’s

          <app from="ra0187" n="190.17 (165.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="da0187">
            <lem wit="A">man’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">man of the world is</rdg>
          </app>
a coward. In the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0188"/>
north

          <app from="ra0188" n="190.17 (165.8)" type="hc" xml:id="da0188">
            <lem wit="MS2">north</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">North</rdg>
          </app>
he lets

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1892"/>
anybody

          <ptr target="#l11593" type="alt" xml:id="te1892"/>
walk over him that wants to, and goes home and prays for a humble spirit to bear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0189"/>
it

          <app from="ra0189" n="190.19 (165.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="da0189">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the insult</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0037"/>
In the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0190"/>
south

          <app from="ra0190" n="190.19 (165.12)" type="hc" xml:id="da0190">
            <lem wit="MS2">south</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">South</rdg>
          </app>
one man, all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0191"/>
by himself

          <app from="ra0191" n="190.19 (165.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0191">
            <lem wit="A">by himself</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">alone</rdg>
          </app>
, has stopped a stage full of men, in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0192"/>
the daytime

          <app from="ra0192" n="190.20 (165.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0192">
            <lem wit="C">the daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">broad daylight</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">the day-time</rdg>
          </app>
, and robbed the lot.

          <ptr target="#as0201" type="an" xml:id="vs0037"/>
Your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0193"/>
newspapers

          <app from="ra0193" n="190.20–21 (165.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="da0193">
            <lem wit="A">newspapers</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
news-

              <lb/>
papers

            </rdg>
          </app>
call you a brave people so much that you think you

          <hi rend="italic">are</hi>
braver than any other people—whereas you’re just

          <hi rend="italic">as</hi>
brave, and no braver. Why don’t your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0194"/>
juries

          <app from="ra0194" n="190.23 (166.5)" type="e" xml:id="da0194">
            <lem wit="A">juries</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">courts</rdg>
          </app>
hang murderers? Because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0195"/>
they’re afraid the man’s friends

          <app from="ra0195" n="190.23–24 (166.7–9)" type="e" xml:id="da0195">
            <lem wit="A">they’re . . . friends</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your juries have n’t got pluck enough to bring them in guilty—afraid the witnesses</rdg>
          </app>
will shoot them in the back, in the dark—and it’s just what they

          <hi rend="italic">would</hi>
do.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47394">
“So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0196"/>
they

          <app from="ra0196" n="190.26 (166.13)" type="e" xml:id="da0196">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you</rdg>
          </app>
always acquit; and then a

          <hi rend="italic">man</hi>
goes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0197"/>
in the

          <app from="ra0197" n="190.26 (166.14)" type="e" xml:id="da0197">
            <lem wit="A">in the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">at</rdg>
          </app>
night, with a hundred masked cowards at his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1893"/>
back, and

          <ptr target="#l11594" type="alt" xml:id="te1893"/>
lynches

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1894"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l11595" type="alt" xml:id="te1894"/>
rascal. Your mistake is, that you didn’t bring a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0198"/>
man

          <app from="ra0198" n="190.28 (167.2)" type="e" xml:id="da0198">
            <lem wit="A">man</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">man</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with you; that’s one mistake, and the other is that you didn’t come in the dark, and fetch your masks. You brought

          <hi rend="italic">part</hi>
of a man—Buck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0199"/>
Harkness, there

          <app from="ra0199" n="190.30 (167.7)" type="e" xml:id="da0199">
            <lem wit="A">Harkness, there</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Harkness</rdg>
          </app>
—and if you hadn’t had him to start you, you’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0200"/>
a taken

          <app from="ra0200" n="190.31 (167.9)" type="e" xml:id="da0200">
            <lem wit="A">a taken</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">have taken</rdg>
          </app>
it out in blowing.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47454">
“You didn’t want to come. The average man don’t like trouble and danger.

          <hi rend="italic">You</hi>
don’t like trouble and danger. But if only

          <hi rend="italic">half</hi>
a man—like Buck Harkness, there—shouts ‘Lynch him, lynch him!’ you’re afraid to back down—afraid you’ll be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0201"/>
found out

          <app from="ra0201" n="190.35 (168.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0201">
            <lem wit="A">found out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">discovered</rdg>
          </app>
to be what you are—

          <hi rend="italic">cowards</hi>
—and so you raise a yell, and hang yourselves onto that half-a-man’s coat tail, and come raging up here, swearing what big things you’re going to do. The pitifulest thing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ra0202"/>
out

          <app from="ra0202" n="190.38 (168.10)" type="e" xml:id="da0202">
            <lem wit="A">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in this world</rdg>
          </app>
is a mob;

          <pb n="191" xml:id="pb0191"/>
that’s what an army is—a mob; they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1895"/>
don’t

          <ptr target="#l11596" type="alt" xml:id="te1895"/>
fight with courage that’s born in them, but with courage

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0001"/>
that’s

          <app from="kg0001" n="191.2 (168.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0001">
            <lem wit="A">that’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma001">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
borrowed from their mass, and from their officers. But a mob without any

          <hi rend="italic">man</hi>
at the head of it, is

          <hi rend="italic">beneath</hi>
pitifulness. Now the thing for

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
to do, is to droop your tails and go home and crawl in a hole. If any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0002"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1896"/>
real

          <ptr target="#l11597" type="alt" xml:id="te1896"/>
          <app from="kg0002" n="191.5 (169.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0002">
            <lem wit="A">real</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">real</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
lynching’s going to be done, it will be done in the dark,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0003"/>
southern

          <app from="kg0003" n="191.6 (169.6)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0003">
            <lem wit="MS2">southern</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Southern</rdg>
          </app>
fashion; and when they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0004"/>
come,

          <app from="kg0004" n="191.7 (169.7)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0004">
            <lem wit="MS2">come,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
come

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1897"/>
they’ll

          <ptr target="#l11598" type="alt" xml:id="te1897"/>
bring their masks, and fetch a

          <hi rend="italic">man</hi>
along. Now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0005"/>
          <hi rend="italic">leave</hi>
          <app from="kg0005" n="191.8 (169.9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0005">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">leave</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">leave!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—and take your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0006"/>
half-a-man

          <app from="kg0006" n="191.8 (169.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="kf0006">
            <lem wit="A">half-a-man</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
half-a

              <lb/>
man

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma002">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with you”—tossing his gun up across his left arm and cocking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0007"/>
it, when he says this

          <app from="kg0007" n="191.9 (169.12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0007">
            <lem wit="A">it . . . this</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47574">
The crowd washed back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0008"/>
sudden

          <app from="kg0008" n="191.10 (169.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0008">
            <lem wit="A">sudden</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sudden, in a body</rdg>
          </app>
, and then broke all apart and went tearing off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0009"/>
every which way

          <app from="kg0009" n="191.11 (169.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0009">
            <lem wit="A">every which way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in every direction</rdg>
          </app>
, and Buck Harkness he heeled it after them, looking tolerable cheap. I could a staid, if I’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0010"/>
a wanted

          <app from="kg0010" n="191.12 (170.3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0010">
            <lem wit="A">a wanted</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wanted</rdg>
          </app>
to, but I didn’t want

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0011"/>
to.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y19101">
          <graphic url="y19101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">a dead head</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47608">
I

          <app from="kg0011" n="191.13–14 (170.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="kf0011">
            <lem wit="A">to. [¶] I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
to.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma003">extra line space</note>
[¶] I

            </rdg>
          </app>
went to the circus, and loafed around the back side till the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0012"/>
watchman

          <app from="kg0012" n="191.15 (170.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="kf0012">
            <lem wit="A">watchman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
watch-

              <lb/>
man

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1898"/>
went

          <ptr target="#l11599" type="alt" xml:id="te1898"/>
by, and then dived in under the tent. I had my twenty-dollar gold piece and some other money, but I reckoned I better save it, because there ain’t no telling how soon you are going to need it, away from home and amongst strangers, that way. You can’t be too careful. I ain’t opposed to spending money on circuses, when there ain’t no other way, but there ain’t no use in

          <hi rend="italic">wasting</hi>
it on them.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47635">
It was a real bully circus. It was the splendidest sight that ever was, when they all come riding in, two and two, a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0013"/>
gentleman

          <app from="kg0013" n="191.23 (171.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0013">
            <lem wit="A">gentleman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
gentle-

              <lb/>
man

            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <pb n="192" xml:id="pb0192"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0014"/>
lady

          <app from="kg0014" n="192.1 (171.9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0014">
            <lem wit="A">lady</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a lady</rdg>
          </app>
, side by side, the men just in their drawers

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1899"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0015"/>
undershirts

          <app from="kg0015" n="192.1 (171.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0015">
            <lem wit="MS2">undershirts</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">under-shirts</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l11600" type="alt" xml:id="te1899"/>
and no shoes nor stirrups, and resting their hands on their thighs, easy and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0016"/>
comfortable,

          <app from="kg0016" n="192.3 (171.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0016">
            <lem wit="MS2">comfortable,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
comfortable

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—there must

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0017"/>
a

          <app from="kg0017" n="192.3 (171.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0017">
            <lem wit="C">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">a ’</rdg>
          </app>
been twenty of them—and every lady with a lovely complexion, and perfectly beautiful, and looking just like a gang of real sure-enough queens, and dressed in clothes that cost millions of dollars, and just littered with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0018"/>
dimonds

          <app from="kg0018" n="192.6 (172.5)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0018">
            <lem wit="MS2">dimonds</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">diamonds</rdg>
          </app>
. It was a powerful fine sight; I never see anything so lovely. And then one by one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0019"/>
they

          <app from="kg0019" n="192.8 (172.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0019">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they they</rdg>
          </app>
got up and stood, and went a-weaving around the ring so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0020"/>
gentle,

          <app from="kg0020" n="192.9 (172.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0020">
            <lem wit="MS2">gentle,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
gentle

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and wavy and graceful, the men looking ever so tall and airy and straight,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1900"/>
with

          <ptr target="#l11601" type="alt" xml:id="te1900"/>
their heads bobbing and skimming along, away up there under the tent-roof, and every lady’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0021"/>
rose-leafy

          <app from="kg0021" n="192.11 (172.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0021">
            <lem wit="A">rose-leafy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
rose-

              <lb/>
leafy

            </rdg>
          </app>
dress flapping soft and silky around her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1901"/>
hips, and

          <ptr target="#l11602" type="alt" xml:id="te1901"/>
she looking like the most loveliest parasol.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47732">
And then faster and faster they went, all of them dancing, first one foot

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1902"/>
stuck out

          <ptr target="#l11603" type="alt" xml:id="te1902"/>
in the air and then the other, the horses leaning more and more, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0022"/>
ring-master

          <app from="kg0022" n="192.16 (173.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0022">
            <lem wit="A">ring-master</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
ring-

              <lb/>
master

            </rdg>
          </app>
going round and round the centre-pole, cracking his whip and shouting “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0023"/>
Hi!

          <app from="kg0023" n="192.17 (173.11)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0023">
            <lem wit="MS2">Hi!</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hi!</rdg>
          </app>
—hi!” and the clown cracking jokes behind him; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0024"/>
by and by,

          <app from="kg0024" n="192.18 (173.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0024">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
all hands dropped the reins, and every lady put her knuckles

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1903"/>
on her

          <ptr target="#l11604" type="alt" xml:id="te1903"/>
hips and every gentleman folded his arms, and then how the horses did lean over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1904"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l11605" type="alt" xml:id="te1904"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0025"/>
hump themselves

          <app from="kg0025" n="192.21 (174.3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0025">
            <lem wit="A">hump themselves</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">fly</rdg>
          </app>
! And so, one after the other they all skipped off into the ring, and made the sweetest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0026"/>
bow I ever see

          <app from="kg0026" n="192.22 (174.6)" type="e" xml:id="kf0026">
            <lem wit="A">bow I ever see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">bow</rdg>
          </app>
, and then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1905"/>
scampered

          <ptr target="#l11606" type="alt" xml:id="te1905"/>
out, and everybody clapped their hands and went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0027"/>
just about

          <app from="kg0027" n="192.23–24 (174.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0027">
            <lem wit="A">just about</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma004">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
wild.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e47803">
Well,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0038"/>
all through the circus they done the most astonishing things

          <ptr target="#as0202" type="an" xml:id="vs0038"/>
; and all the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0028"/>
time,

          <app from="kg0028" n="192.26 (174.11)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0028">
            <lem wit="MS2">time,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
time

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that clown carried on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0029"/>
so it

          <app from="kg0029" n="192.26 (174.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="kf0029">
            <lem wit="A">so it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in a way that</rdg>
          </app>
most killed the people. The ring-master couldn’t ever say a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1906"/>
word

          <ptr target="#l11607" type="alt" xml:id="te1906"/>
to him but he was back at him quick as a wink with the funniest things a body ever said; and how he ever

          <hi rend="italic">could</hi>
think of so many of them, and so sudden and so pat, was what I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0030"/>
no way

          <app from="kg0030" n="192.30 (175.5)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0030">
            <lem wit="MS2">no way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">noway</rdg>
          </app>
understand. Why, I couldn’t a thought of them in a year. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0031"/>
by and by

          <app from="kg0031" n="192.31 (175.8)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0031">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
a drunk man tried to get into the ring—said he wanted to ride; said he could ride as well as anybody that ever was. They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0032"/>
argued

          <app from="kg0032" n="192.33 (175.13)" type="e" xml:id="kf0032">
            <lem wit="A">argued</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">argued with him,</rdg>
          </app>
and tried to keep him out, but he wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0033"/>
listen

          <app from="kg0033" n="192.34 (175.15)" type="e" xml:id="kf0033">
            <lem wit="A">listen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">listen to them</rdg>
          </app>
, and the whole show come to a standstill. Then the people begun to holler at him and make fun of him, and that made him mad, and he begun to rip and tear;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1907"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l11608" type="alt" xml:id="te1907"/>
that stirred up the people, and a lot of men begun to pile down off of the benches and swarm towards the ring, saying, “Knock him down! throw him out!” and one or two women begun to scream. So, then, the ring-

          <pb n="193" xml:id="pb0193"/>
master he made a little speech, and said he hoped there wouldn’t be no disturbance, and if the man would promise he wouldn’t make no more

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1908"/>
trouble

          <ptr target="#l11609" type="alt" xml:id="te1908"/>
, he would let him ride, if he thought he could stay on the horse. So everybody laughed and said all right, and the man got on. The minute he was on, the horse begun to rip and tear and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0034"/>
jump,

          <app from="kg0034" n="193.6 (177.9)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0034">
            <lem wit="MS2">jump,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
jump

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and cavort around, with two

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1909"/>
circus

          <ptr target="#l11610" type="alt" xml:id="te1909"/>
men hanging

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0035"/>
onto

          <app from="kg0035" n="193.6 (177.11)" type="e" xml:id="kf0035">
            <lem wit="A">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on to</rdg>
          </app>
his bridle trying to hold him, and the drunk man hanging onto his neck, and his heels flying in the air

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0036"/>
every

          <app from="kg0036" n="193.8 (177.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0036">
            <lem wit="A">every</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">with every</rdg>
          </app>
jump, and the whole crowd of people standing up shouting and laughing till the tears rolled

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0037"/>
down

          <app from="kg0037" n="193.9 (178.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0037">
            <lem wit="A">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">down their faces</rdg>
          </app>
. And at last, sure enough, all the circus men could do, the horse broke loose, and away he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1910"/>
went

          <ptr target="#l11611" type="alt" xml:id="te1910"/>
like the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0038"/>
very nation

          <app from="kg0038" n="193.11 (178.9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0038">
            <lem wit="A">very nation</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wind</rdg>
          </app>
, round and round the ring, with that sot laying down on him and hanging to his neck, with first one leg hanging most to the ground

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1911"/>
on

          <ptr target="#l11612" type="alt" xml:id="te1911"/>
one side, and then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0039"/>
t’other one

          <app from="kg0039" n="193.14 (178.15)" type="e" xml:id="kf0039">
            <lem wit="A">t’other one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’tother one</rdg>
          </app>
on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0040"/>
t’other side

          <app from="kg0040" n="193.14 (178.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0040">
            <lem wit="A">t’other side</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’tother side</rdg>
          </app>
, and the people just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0041"/>
crazy

          <app from="kg0041" n="193.14 (179.1)" type="e" xml:id="kf0041">
            <lem wit="A">crazy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">crazy for delight</rdg>
          </app>
. It warn’t funny to me, though; I was all of a tremble to see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0042"/>
his

          <app from="kg0042" n="193.15 (179.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0042">
            <lem wit="A">his</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that man’s</rdg>
          </app>
danger. But pretty soon he struggled

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1912"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l11613" type="alt" xml:id="te1912"/>
astraddle and grabbed the bridle, a-reeling this way and that; and the next minute he sprung up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1913"/>
and dropped the

          <pb n="194" xml:id="pb0194"/>
bridle

          <ptr target="#l11614" type="alt" xml:id="te1913"/>
and stood! and the horse agoing like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0043"/>
a house afire,

          <app from="kg0043" n="194.1 (179.10)" type="e" xml:id="kf0043">
            <lem wit="C">a house afire,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sin,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">a house afire</rdg>
          </app>
too. He just

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1914"/>
stood up

          <ptr target="#l11615" type="alt" xml:id="te1914"/>
there, a-sailing around as easy and comfortable as if he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3833"/>
warn’t ever

          <app from="pr3833" n="194.3 (179.13)" type="e" xml:id="la5695">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">never was</rdg>
          </app>
drunk in his life—and then he begun to pull

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3834"/>
off his

          <app from="pr3834" n="194.3 (179.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5696">
            <lem wit="A">off his</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
clothes and

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0063"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3835"/>
fling

          <app from="pr3835" n="✱194.4 (179.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5697">
            <lem wit="MS2">fling</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sling</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0063" type="te" xml:id="tv0063"/>
them.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1915"/>
He

          <ptr target="#l11616" type="alt" xml:id="te1915"/>
shed them so thick they kind of clogged up the air, and altogether he shed seventeen suits. And then, there he was, slim and handsome, and dressed the gaudiest and prettiest you ever saw, and he lit into that horse with his whip and made him fairly hum—and finally skipped off, and made his bow and danced off to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3836"/>
dressing room

          <app from="pr3836" n="194.9 (180.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5698">
            <lem wit="MS2">dressing room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dressing-room</rdg>
          </app>
, and everybody just a-howling

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1916"/>
with

          <ptr target="#l11617" type="alt" xml:id="te1916"/>
pleasure and astonishment.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y19301">
          <graphic url="y19301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">he shed seventeen suits</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48040">
Then the ring-master

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3837"/>
he see

          <app from="pr3837" n="194.11 (180.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5699">
            <lem wit="A">he see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">see</rdg>
          </app>
how he had been fooled, and he

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1917"/>
sickest

          <ptr target="#l11618" type="alt" xml:id="te1917"/>
ring-master

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3838"/>
you ever see

          <app from="pr3838" n="194.12 (181.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5700">
            <lem wit="A">you ever see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that ever was</rdg>
          </app>
, I reckon. Why, it was one of his own men! He had got up that joke all out of his own head, and never let on to nobody. Well, I felt sheepish enough, to be took in so, but I wouldn’t a been in that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3839"/>
ring-master’s

          <app from="pr3839" n="194.15 (181.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la5701">
            <lem wit="A">ring-master’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
ring-

              <lb/>
master’s

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3840"/>
place

          <app from="pr3840" n="194.15 (181.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la5702">
            <lem wit="MS2">place</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">place,</rdg>
          </app>
not

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1918"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l11619" type="alt" xml:id="te1918"/>
a thousand dollars.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1919"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l11620" type="alt" xml:id="te1919"/>
don’t know; there may be bullier circuses than what that one was, but I never struck them yet. Anyways it was plenty good enough for

          <hi rend="italic">me;</hi>
and wherever I run across

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr3841"/>
it, it

          <app from="pr3841" n="194.18 (182.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5703">
            <lem wit="A">it, it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
it

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1920"/>
can

          <ptr target="#l11621" type="alt" xml:id="te1920"/>
have all of

          <hi rend="italic">my</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0054"/>
custom, every time.

          <app from="ra0059" n="184.4–194.19 (641.12–182.3)" type="e" xml:id="da0059">
            <lem wit="C">By and by . . . time.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS1b/MS2">By and by . . . custom.</rdg>
