      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0367">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXIII.</head>
        <pb n="196" xml:id="pb0196"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48490">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y19601">
            <graphic url="y19601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0084"/>
Chapter XXIII.

              <app from="kg0084" n="196 title (185.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0083">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XXIII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma015">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">Well,</ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf1961">
            <graphic url="hf1961.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">tragedy</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e48508">
all day him and the king was hard at it, rigging up a stage, and a curtain, and a row of candles for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="gk0084"/>
footlights

          <app from="gk0084" n="196.4 (185.8)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0084">
            <lem wit="MS2">footlights</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
foot-

              <lb/>
lights

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">foot-lights</rdg>
          </app>
; and that night the house was jam full of men in no time. When the place couldn’t hold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0085"/>
no

          <app from="kg0085" n="196.7 (185.11)" type="e" xml:id="kf0085">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">any</rdg>
          </app>
more, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0086"/>
duke he

          <app from="kg0086" n="196.8 (185.12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0086">
            <lem wit="A Cent">duke he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">duke</rdg>
          </app>
quit tending

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0087"/>
door

          <app from="kg0087" n="196.8 (185.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0087">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">door</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">door,</rdg>
          </app>
and went around the back way and come onto the stage and stood

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0088"/>
up

          <app from="kg0088" n="196.11 (185.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0088">
            <lem wit="A Cent">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma016">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before the curtain, and made a little speech, and praised up this tragedy, and said it was the most thrillingest one that ever was; and so he went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0089"/>
on,

          <app from="kg0089" n="196.16 (186.3)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0089">
            <lem wit="MS2">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0090"/>
a-bragging

          <app from="kg0090" n="196.16 (186.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0090">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a-bragging</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <lb/>
bragging

            </rdg>
          </app>
about the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0091"/>
tragedy,

          <app from="kg0091" n="196.17 (186.4)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0091">
            <lem wit="MS2">tragedy,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
tragedy

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and about Edmund Kean the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1925"/>
Elder

          <ptr target="#l11626" type="alt" xml:id="te1925"/>
, which was to play the main

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0092"/>
principal

          <app from="kg0092" n="196.18 (186.7)" type="e" xml:id="kf0092">
            <lem wit="A Cent">principal</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma017">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
part in it; and at last when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0093"/>
he’d

          <app from="kg0093" n="196.19 (186.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0093">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he had</rdg>
          </app>
got everybody’s expectations up high enough, he rolled up the curtain, and the next minute the king come a-prancing out on all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0094"/>
fours, naked

          <app from="kg0094" n="196.21 (186.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0094">
            <lem wit="A">fours, naked</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">fours and stark naked</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">fours</rdg>
          </app>
; and he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0095"/>
painted,

          <app from="kg0095" n="196.21 (186.15)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0095">
            <lem wit="MS2">painted,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
painted

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1926"/>
all over

          <ptr target="#l11627" type="alt" xml:id="te1926"/>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0096"/>
ring-streaked-and-striped

          <app from="kg0096" n="196.21–22 (186.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0096">
            <lem wit="C">ring-streaked-and-striped</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
ring-

              <lb/>
streaked-and-striped

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ring-streaked and striped</rdg>
          </app>
, all sorts of colors, as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1927"/>
splendid

          <ptr target="#l11628" type="alt" xml:id="te1927"/>
as a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0097"/>
rain-bow

          <app from="kg0097" n="196.22 (187.2)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0097">
            <lem wit="MS2">rain-bow</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">rainbow</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0098"/>
And—but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0099"/>
never mind

          <app from="kg0099" n="196.23 (187.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0099">
            <lem wit="A">never mind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I won’t describe</rdg>
          </app>
the rest of his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0100"/>
outfit,

          <app from="kg0100" n="196.23 (187.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0100">
            <lem wit="A">outfit,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">outfit, because</rdg>
          </app>
it was just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0101"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0034"/>
wild

          <ptr target="#mt0034" type="alt" xml:id="wn0034"/>
, but

          <app from="kg0101" n="196.23 (187.5)" type="e" xml:id="kf0101">
            <lem wit="A">wild, but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">outrageous, although</rdg>
          </app>
it was awful funny.

          <app from="kg0098" n="196.22–24 (187.2–6)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0098">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">And . . . funny.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma018">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
The people

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0102"/>
most

          <app from="kg0102" n="196.24 (187.7)" type="e" xml:id="kf0102">
            <lem wit="A Cent">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nearly</rdg>
          </app>
killed themselves laughing; and when the king got done capering, and capered off behind the scenes, they roared and clapped and stormed and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0103"/>
haw-hawed

          <app from="kg0103" n="196.26 (187.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0103">
            <lem wit="MS2">haw-hawed</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
haw-

              <lb/>
hawed

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hawhawed</rdg>
          </app>
till he come back and done it over again; and after that, they made him do it another time. Well, it would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0104"/>
a made

          <app from="kg0104" n="196.28 (187.16)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0104">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a made</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ made</rdg>
          </app>
a cow

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0105"/>
laugh,

          <app from="kg0105" n="196.28 (187.16)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0105">
            <lem wit="MS2">laugh,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
laugh

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to see the shines

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0106"/>
that

          <app from="kg0106" n="196.28 (188.1)" type="e" xml:id="kf0106">
            <lem wit="A Cent">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that that</rdg>
          </app>
old idiot cut.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48735">
Then the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0107"/>
duke he

          <app from="kg0107" n="196.30 (188.3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0107">
            <lem wit="A Cent">duke he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">duke</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1928"/>
lets

          <ptr target="#l11629" type="alt" xml:id="te1928"/>
the curtain down, and bows to the people, and says the great tragedy will be performed only two nights more, on accounts of pressing London engagements, where the seats is all

          <pb n="197" xml:id="pb0197"/>
sold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0108"/>
aready

          <app from="kg0108" n="197.1 (188.10)" type="e" xml:id="kf0108">
            <lem wit="A Cent">aready</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">already</rdg>
          </app>
for it in Drury Lane; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0109"/>
then he

          <app from="kg0109" n="197.1 (188.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0109">
            <lem wit="A Cent">then he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">then the duke</rdg>
          </app>
makes them another bow, and says if he has succeeded in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0110"/>
pleasing them

          <app from="kg0110" n="197.2 (188.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0110">
            <lem wit="A Cent">pleasing them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">pleasing</rdg>
          </app>
and instructing them, he will

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1929"/>
be

          <ptr target="#l11630" type="alt" xml:id="te1929"/>
deeply

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0111"/>
obleeged

          <app from="kg0111" n="197.3 (188.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0111">
            <lem wit="A Cent">obleeged</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gratified</rdg>
          </app>
if they will mention

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0112"/>
it

          <app from="kg0112" n="197.3 (189.1)" type="e" xml:id="kf0112">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the piece</rdg>
          </app>
to their friends and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0113"/>
get

          <app from="kg0113" n="197.4 (189.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0113">
            <lem wit="A Cent">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">use their influence to get</rdg>
          </app>
them to come and see it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48805">
Twenty people

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0114"/>
sings

          <app from="kg0114" n="197.5 (189.5)" type="e" xml:id="kf0114">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sings</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sung</rdg>
          </app>
out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48815">
“What, is it over? Is that

          <hi rend="italic">all?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48820">
The duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0115"/>
says

          <app from="kg0115" n="197.7 (189.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0115">
            <lem wit="A Cent">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
yes. Then there was a fine time. Everybody

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1930"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0116"/>
sings

          <app from="kg0116" n="197.7 (189.10)" type="e" xml:id="kf0116">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sings</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sung</rdg>
          </app>
out “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0117"/>
Sold!

          <app from="kg0117" n="197.8 (189.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0117">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Sold!</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sold,</rdg>
          </app>
” and

          <ptr target="#l11631" type="alt" xml:id="te1930"/>
rose up mad, and was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0118"/>
agoing

          <app from="kg0118" n="197.8 (189.11)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0118">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
for that stage and them tragedians. But a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0119"/>
big

          <app from="kg0119" n="197.9 (189.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0119">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">big</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">big,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0120"/>
fine looking

          <app from="kg0120" n="197.9 (189.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0120">
            <lem wit="MS2">fine looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">fine-looking</rdg>
          </app>
man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1931"/>
jumps

          <ptr target="#l11632" type="alt" xml:id="te1931"/>
up on a bench and shouts:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48878">
“Hold on! Just a word, gentlemen.” They stopped to listen. “We are sold—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0121"/>
mighty

          <app from="kg0121" n="197.12 (190.2)" type="e" xml:id="kf0121">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mighty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma019">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
badly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0122"/>
sold

          <app from="kg0122" n="197.12 (190.3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0122">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sold</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sold—I grant you that</rdg>
          </app>
. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0123"/>
we don’t

          <app from="kg0123" n="197.12 (190.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0123">
            <lem wit="A Cent">we don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">do we</rdg>
          </app>
want to be the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0124"/>
laughing-stock

          <app from="kg0124" n="197.12–13 (190.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="kf0124">
            <lem wit="A Cent">laughing-stock</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
laughing-

              <lb/>
stock

            </rdg>
          </app>
of this whole town,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0125"/>
I reckon,

          <app from="kg0125" n="197.13 (190.5)" type="e" xml:id="kf0125">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I reckon,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma020">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and never hear the last of this thing as long as we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0126"/>
live.

          <app from="kg0126" n="197.14 (190.7)" type="e" xml:id="kf0126">
            <lem wit="A Cent">live.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">live?</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">No.</hi>
What we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0127"/>
want,

          <app from="kg0127" n="197.14 (190.8)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0127">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">want,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
want

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
is to go out of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1932"/>
here

          <ptr target="#l11633" type="alt" xml:id="te1932"/>
quiet, and talk this show up, and sell the

          <hi rend="italic">rest</hi>
of the town! Then we’ll all be in the same boat. Ain’t that sensible?”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0128"/>
[“You

          <app from="kg0128" n="197.17 (190.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0128">
            <lem wit="MS2">[“You</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">“You</rdg>
          </app>
bet it is!—the jedge is right!” everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0129"/>
sings

          <app from="kg0129" n="197.19 (190.15)" type="e" xml:id="kf0129">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sings</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sung</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0130"/>
out.]

          <app from="kg0130" n="197.19 (190.15)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0130">
            <lem wit="MS2">out.]</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">out.)</rdg>
          </app>
“All right, then—not a word about any sell. Go along home, and advise everybody to come and see the tragedy.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e48976">
Next day you couldn’t hear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0131"/>
nothing

          <app from="kg0131" n="197.25 (191.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0131">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
around that town but how splendid that show was. House was jammed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0132"/>
again,

          <app from="kg0132" n="197.27 (191.7)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0132">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
again

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1933"/>
that night,

          <ptr target="#l11634" type="alt" xml:id="te1933"/>
and we sold this crowd the same way. When me and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1934"/>
the king

          <ptr target="#l11635" type="alt" xml:id="te1934"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1935"/>
the duke

          <ptr target="#l11636" type="alt" xml:id="te1935"/>
got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1936"/>
home

          <ptr target="#l11637" type="alt" xml:id="te1936"/>
to the raft, we all had a supper; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0133"/>
by and by

          <app from="kg0133" n="197.32 (191.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0133">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, about midnight, they made Jim and me back her out and float her down the middle of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0134"/>
river

          <app from="kg0134" n="197.36 (191.15)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0134">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">river,</rdg>
          </app>
and fetch her in and hide her about two mile below town.

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y19701">
          <graphic url="y19701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">their pockets bulged</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49033">
          <pb n="198" xml:id="pb0198"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0040"/>
The third night the house was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0135"/>
crammed

          <app from="kg0135" n="198.1 (192.2)" type="e" xml:id="kf0135">
            <lem wit="A Cent">crammed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">packed and crammed</rdg>
          </app>
again—and they warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0136"/>
newcomers,

          <app from="kg0136" n="198.2 (192.3)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0136">
            <lem wit="MS2">newcomers,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">new-comers,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">new-comers</rdg>
          </app>
this time, but people that was at the show the other two nights. I stood by the duke at the door, and I see that every man that went in had his pockets bulging, or something muffled up under his coat—and I see it warn’t no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0137"/>
perfumery,

          <app from="kg0137" n="198.5 (192.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0137">
            <lem wit="MS2">perfumery,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
perfumery

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
neither, not by a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0138"/>
long

          <app from="kg0138" n="198.6 (192.13)" type="e" xml:id="kf0138">
            <lem wit="A Cent">long</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blame’</rdg>
          </app>
sight. I smelt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0139"/>
sickly

          <app from="kg0139" n="198.6 (192.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0139">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sickly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rotten</rdg>
          </app>
eggs by the barrel, and rotten cabbages, and such

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0140"/>
things;

          <app from="kg0140" n="198.7 (192.16)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0140">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">things;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">things.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0141"/>
and if I know the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0142"/>
signs

          <app from="kg0142" n="198.7 (192.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0142">
            <lem wit="A">signs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">smell</rdg>
          </app>
of a dead cat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0143"/>
being around

          <app from="kg0143" n="198.7 (193.1)" type="e" xml:id="kf0143">
            <lem wit="A">being around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma022">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, and I bet I do, there was sixty-four of them went in.

          <ptr target="#as0204" type="an" xml:id="vs0040"/>
I shoved in there for a minute, but it was too

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0144"/>
various

          <app from="kg0144" n="198.9 (193.5)" type="e" xml:id="kf0144">
            <lem wit="A">various</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rancid</rdg>
          </app>
for me, I couldn’t stand it.

          <app from="kg0141" n="198.7–9 (192.16–193.6)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0141">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">and if . . . it.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma021">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Well, when the place couldn’t hold no more people, the duke he give a fellow a quarter and told him to tend door for him a minute, and then he started around for the stage door, I after him; but the minute we turned the corner and was in the dark, he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49125">“Walk fast, now, till you get away from the houses, and then shin for the raft like the dickens was after you!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49127">
I done it, and he done the same. We struck the raft at the same time, and in less than two seconds we was gliding down stream, all dark and still, and edging towards the middle

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0145"/>
of the river

          <app from="kg0145" n="198.18 (194.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0145">
            <lem wit="A Cent">of the river</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma023">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, nobody saying a word. I reckoned the poor king was in for a gaudy time of it with the audience; but nothing of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0146"/>
sort:

          <app from="kg0146" n="198.20 (194.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0146">
            <lem wit="MS2">sort:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">sort;</rdg>
          </app>
pretty soon he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0147"/>
crawls

          <app from="kg0147" n="198.20 (194.13)" type="e" xml:id="kf0147">
            <lem wit="A Cent">crawls</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">crawled</rdg>
          </app>
out from under the wigwam, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49155">
“Well, how’d

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1937"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l11638" type="alt" xml:id="te1937"/>
old thing pan out this time,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0148"/>
duke

          <app from="kg0148" n="198.22 (194.16)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0148">
            <lem wit="MS2">duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Duke</rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49169">
He

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1938"/>
hadn’t

          <ptr target="#l11639" type="alt" xml:id="te1938"/>
been up town at all.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49175">
We never showed a light till we was about ten mile below that village. Then we lit up and had a supper, and the king and the duke fairly laughed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0149"/>
their bones loose

          <app from="kg0149" n="198.26 (195.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0149">
            <lem wit="A Cent">their bones loose</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">themselves hoarse</rdg>
          </app>
over the way they’d served them people. The duke says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49185">
“Greenhorns, flatheads!

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
knew the first house would keep mum and let the rest of the town get roped in; and I knew they’d lay for us the third night, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0150"/>
consider

          <app from="kg0150" n="198.30 (196.1)" type="e" xml:id="kf0150">
            <lem wit="A Cent">consider</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">consider that now</rdg>
          </app>
it was

          <hi rend="italic">their</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0151"/>
turn now

          <app from="kg0151" n="198.30 (196.2)" type="e" xml:id="kf0151">
            <lem wit="A Cent">turn now</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">turn</rdg>
          </app>
. Well, it

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
their turn, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1939"/>
I’d give something to know

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0152"/>
how much

          <app from="kg0152" n="198.31 (196.3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0152">
            <lem wit="A Cent">how much</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">what</rdg>
          </app>
they’d take for it.

          <ptr target="#l11640" type="alt" xml:id="te1939"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0153"/>
I

          <app from="kg0153" n="198.31 (196.3)" type="e" xml:id="kf0153">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Now I</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">would</hi>
just like to know how they’re putting in their opportunity.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0154"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1940"/>
They

          <ptr target="#l11641" type="alt" xml:id="te1940"/>
can turn it into a picnic, if they want to—they brought plenty provisions.

          <app from="kg0154" n="198.33–34 (196.6–8)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0154">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">They . . . provisions.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma024">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49246">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0041"/>
Them rapscallions took in four hundred and sixty-five dollars

          <ptr target="#as0205" type="an" xml:id="vs0041"/>
in that three nights. I never see money hauled in by the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0155"/>
wagon load

          <app from="kg0155" n="198.36 (196.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0155">
            <lem wit="MS2">wagon load</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wagon-load</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
wagon-

              <lb/>
load

            </rdg>
          </app>
like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0156"/>
that,

          <app from="kg0156" n="198.37 (196.14)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0156">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0157"/>
before.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49273">
By and by

          <app from="kg0157" n="198.37–38 (196.14–197.1)" type="e" xml:id="kf0157">
            <lem wit="Cent">before. [¶] By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
before.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma025">extra line space</note>
              <milestone unit="page"/>
[¶] By and by

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">before. [¶] By-and by</rdg>
          </app>
, when they was asleep and snoring, Jim says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49287">
          <pb n="199" xml:id="pb0199"/>
“Don’t it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0158"/>
sprise

          <app from="kg0158" n="199.1 (197.3)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0158">
            <lem wit="MS2">sprise</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">’sprise</rdg>
          </app>
you, de way dem kings carries on,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0159"/>
Huck?”

          <app from="kg0159" n="199.1 (197.4)" type="e" xml:id="kf0159">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Huck?”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Huck?ʍ

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma026">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49307">“No,” I says, “it don’t.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49310">“Why don’t it, Huck?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49312">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0160"/>
it

          <app from="kg0160" n="199.4 (197.7)" type="e" xml:id="kf0160">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I</rdg>
          </app>
don’t, because it’s in the breed. I reckon they’re all alike.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49322">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0161"/>
But

          <app from="kg0161" n="199.6 (197.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0161">
            <lem wit="MS2">But</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">But,</rdg>
          </app>
Huck, dese kings o’ ourn is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0162"/>
reglar

          <app from="kg0162" n="199.6 (197.11)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0162">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">reglar</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">regular</rdg>
          </app>
rapscallions; dat’s jist what dey is;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0163"/>
dey’s

          <app from="kg0163" n="199.7 (197.12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0163">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dey’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">deys</rdg>
          </app>
reglar rapscallions.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49349">“Well, that’s what I’m a-saying; all kings is mostly rapscallions, as fur as I can make out.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49351">“Is dat so?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49353">
“You read about them once—you’ll see. Look at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1941"/>
Henry

          <ptr target="#l11642" type="alt" xml:id="te1941"/>
the Eight;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0164"/>
this’n ’s

          <app from="kg0164" n="199.12 (198.5)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0164">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">this’n ’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">this’n’s</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0165"/>
Sunday School superintendent

          <app from="kg0165" n="199.12 (198.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0165">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sunday School superintendent</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sunday-School Superintendent</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
Sunday-

              <lb/>
school superintendent

            </rdg>
          </app>
to

          <hi rend="italic">him.</hi>
And look at Charles Second,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1942"/>
and Louis Fourteen, and Louis Fifteen,

          <ptr target="#l11643" type="alt" xml:id="te1942"/>
and James Second, and Edward Second, and Richard Third, and forty more; besides all them

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0042"/>
Saxon heptarchies

          <ptr target="#as0206" type="an" xml:id="vs0042"/>
that used to rip around so in old times and raise Cain. My, you ought to seen old

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0043"/>
Henry the Eight when he was in bloom.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1943"/>
He

          <ptr target="#l11644" type="alt" xml:id="te1943"/>
          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
a blossom. He used to marry a new wife every

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0166"/>
day,

          <app from="kg0166" n="199.18 (199.1)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0166">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">day,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
day

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and chop off her head next morning. And he would do it just as indifferent as if he was ordering up eggs. ‘Fetch up Nell Gwynn,’ he says. They fetch her up. Next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0167"/>
morning,

          <app from="kg0167" n="199.22 (199.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0167">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">morning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
morning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
‘Chop off her head!’ And they chop it off. ‘Fetch up Jane Shore,’ he says; and up she comes. Next morning, ‘Chop off her head’—and they chop it off.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1944"/>
‘Ring

          <ptr target="#l11645" type="alt" xml:id="te1944"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1945"/>
up Fair

          <ptr target="#l11646" type="alt" xml:id="te1945"/>
Rosamun.’ Fair Rosamun

          <ptr target="#as0207" type="an" xml:id="vs0043"/>
answers the bell. Next morning, ‘Chop off her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0168"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1946"/>
head.’

          <ptr target="#l11647" type="alt" xml:id="te1946"/>
          <app from="kg0168" n="199.24 (199.15–17)" type="e" xml:id="kf0168">
            <lem wit="A">head.’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">head’—and next thing you see is the chief of police with it in a rag.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">head.’ ”</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0169"/>
And he made every one of them

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0044"/>
tell him a tale every night; and he kept that up till he had hogged a thousand and one tales that way, and then he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0170"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1947"/>
put

          <ptr target="#l11648" type="alt" xml:id="te1947"/>
          <app from="kg0170" n="199.26 (200.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="kf0170">
            <lem wit="A">put</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">got out a copyright, and published</rdg>
          </app>
them all in a book, and called it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0171"/>
Domesday

          <app from="kg0171" n="199.27 (200.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0171">
            <lem wit="A">Domesday</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Domes-

              <lb/>
day

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1948"/>
Book

          <ptr target="#as0208" type="an" xml:id="vs0044"/>
—which was a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0172"/>
name,

          <app from="kg0172" n="199.27 (200.8)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0172">
            <lem wit="MS2">name,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
name

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and stated the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0173"/>
case.

          <ptr target="#l11649" type="alt" xml:id="te1948"/>
          <app from="kg0173" n="199.27 (200.8–12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0173">
            <lem wit="A">case.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">case. Of course most any publisher would do that, but you wouldn’t think a king would. If you didn’t know kings.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0174"/>
You don’t know kings, Jim, but

          <app from="kg0174" n="199.28 (200.12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0174">
            <lem wit="A">You . . . Jim, but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">But</rdg>
          </app>
I know them; and this old rip of ourn is one of the cleanest I’ve struck in history. Well, Henry he takes a notion he wants to get up some trouble with this country. How does he go at it—give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0175"/>
notice?—give

          <app from="kg0175" n="199.31 (200.19–201.1)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0175">
            <lem wit="A">notice?—give</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
notice?—

              <milestone unit="page"/>
give

            </rdg>
          </app>
the country a show? No.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1949"/>
All

          <ptr target="#l11650" type="alt" xml:id="te1949"/>
of a sudden he heaves all the tea in Boston

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0176"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1950"/>
harbor

          <ptr target="#l11651" type="alt" xml:id="te1950"/>
          <app from="kg0176" n="199.32 (201.4)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0176">
            <lem wit="MS2">harbor</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Harbor</rdg>
          </app>
overboard, and whacks out a declaration of independence, and dares them to come on. That was

          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
style—he never give anybody a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1951"/>
chance.

          <ptr target="#l11652" type="alt" xml:id="te1951"/>
He had suspicions of his father, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0177"/>
duke

          <app from="kg0177" n="199.35 (201.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0177">
            <lem wit="MS2">duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Duke</rdg>
          </app>
of Wellington. Well, what did he do?—ask him to show up? No—drownded him in a butt of mamsey, like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0178"/>
cat

          <app from="kg0178" n="199.37 (201.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0178">
            <lem wit="A">cat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dog</rdg>
          </app>
. Spose people left money laying around where he was—what did he do? He collared it. Spose he contracted to do a thing; and you

          <pb n="200" xml:id="pb0200"/>
paid him, and didn’t set down there and see that he done

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1952"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l11653" type="alt" xml:id="te1952"/>
—what did he do? He always done the other thing. Spose he opened his mouth—what then?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1953"/>
If

          <ptr target="#l11654" type="alt" xml:id="te1953"/>
he didn’t shut it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0179"/>
up

          <app from="kg0179" n="200.3 (203.7)" type="e" xml:id="kf0179">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma028">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
powerful quick, he’d lose a lie, every time. That’s the kind of a bug Henry was; and if we’d a had him along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0180"/>
stead

          <app from="kg0180" n="200.5 (203.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0180">
            <lem wit="MS2">stead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’stead</rdg>
          </app>
of our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0181"/>
kings,

          <app from="kg0181" n="200.5 (203.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0181">
            <lem wit="MS2">kings,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
kings

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he’d a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0182"/>
fooled

          <app from="kg0182" n="200.5 (203.13)" type="e" xml:id="kf0182">
            <lem wit="A">fooled</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">bilked</rdg>
          </app>
that town a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1954"/>
heap

          <ptr target="#l11655" type="alt" xml:id="te1954"/>
worse than ourn done. I don’t say that ourn is lambs, because they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0183"/>
ain’t

          <app from="kg0183" n="200.7 (203.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0183">
            <lem wit="A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">aint</rdg>
          </app>
, when you come right down to the cold facts; but they ain’t nothing to

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
old ram, anyway. All I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0184"/>
say,

          <app from="kg0184" n="200.8 (204.1)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0184">
            <lem wit="MS2">say,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
say

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
is, kings is kings, and you got to make allowances. Take them all around, they’re a mighty ornery lot. It’s the way they’re raised.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y20001">
          <graphic url="y20001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">henry the eighth in boston harbor</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49615">
“But dis one do

          <hi rend="italic">smell</hi>
so like de nation, Huck.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49620">
“Well, they all do, Jim.

          <hi rend="italic">We</hi>
can’t help the way a king smells; history don’t tell no way.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49625">
“Now de duke,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1955"/>
he’s

          <ptr target="#l11656" type="alt" xml:id="te1955"/>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0185"/>
tolerble

          <app from="kg0185" n="200.14 (204.12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0185">
            <lem wit="A">tolerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tolerable</rdg>
          </app>
likely

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1956"/>
man, in some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0186"/>
ways.

          <ptr target="#l11657" type="alt" xml:id="te1956"/>
          <app from="kg0186" n="200.14 (204.12)" type="e" xml:id="kf0186">
            <lem wit="A">ways.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
ways

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49651">
“Yes, a duke’s different. But not

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1957"/>
very

          <ptr target="#l11658" type="alt" xml:id="te1957"/>
different.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1958"/>
This one’s

          <ptr target="#l11659" type="alt" xml:id="te1958"/>
a middling hard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0187"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1959"/>
lot,—

          <ptr target="#l11660" type="alt" xml:id="te1959"/>
          <app from="kg0187" n="200.16 (204.15)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0187">
            <lem wit="MS2">lot,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
lot,

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for a duke. When he’s drunk, there ain’t no near-sighted man

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1960"/>
could tell

          <ptr target="#l11661" type="alt" xml:id="te1960"/>
him from a king.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49677">
“Well, anyways, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0188"/>
doan

          <app from="kg0188" n="200.18 (205.1)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0188">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
hanker for no mo’ un um, Huck. Dese is all I kin stan’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49687">
          <pb n="201" xml:id="pb0201"/>
“It’s the way I feel, too, Jim. But we’ve got them on our hands, and we got to remember what they are, and make allowances. Sometimes I wish we could hear of a country that’s out of kings.”

          <app from="kg0169" n="199.24–201.3 (200.1–205.9)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0169">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">And he . . . kings.”</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma027">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49696">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0189"/>
What was the use to tell Jim these warn’t real kings and dukes? It wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0190"/>
a done

          <app from="kg0190" n="201.5" type="hc" xml:id="kf0190">
            <lem wit="A">a done</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ done</rdg>
          </app>
no good; and besides, it was just as I said; you couldn’t tell them from the real kind.

          <app from="kg0189" n="201.4–6 (205.10)" type="e" xml:id="kf0189">
            <lem wit="A Cent">What . . . kind.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma029">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49713">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0191"/>
I went to sleep, and Jim didn’t call me when it was my turn. He often done that. When I waked up, just at daybreak, he was setting there with his head down betwixt his knees, moaning and mourning to himself. I didn’t take notice, nor let on. I knowed what it was about. He was thinking about his wife and his children, away up yonder, and he was low and homesick; because he hadn’t ever been away from home before in his life; and I do believe he cared just as much for his people as white folks does for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0192"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1961"/>
theirn

          <app from="kg0192" n="201.14 (206.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0192">
            <lem wit="MS2">theirn</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">their’n</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11662" type="alt" xml:id="te1961"/>
. It don’t seem natural, but I reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0193"/>
it’s

          <app from="kg0193" n="201.15 (206.11)" type="e" xml:id="kf0193">
            <lem wit="A">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">its</rdg>
          </app>
so. He was often moaning and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0194"/>
mourning,

          <app from="kg0194" n="201.15 (206.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0194">
            <lem wit="MS2">mourning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
mourning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that way, nights,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1962"/>
when he judged I was asleep,

          <ptr target="#l11663" type="alt" xml:id="te1962"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0195"/>
saying

          <app from="kg0195" n="201.16 (206.13)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0195">
            <lem wit="MS2">saying</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">saying,</rdg>
          </app>
“Po’ little ’Lizabeth! po’ little Johnny!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0196"/>
it

          <app from="kg0196" n="201.17 (206.15)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0196">
            <lem wit="MS2">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">its</rdg>
          </app>
mighty hard; I spec’ I ain’t ever gwyne to see you no mo’, no mo’!” He was a mighty good nigger,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1963"/>
Jim was.

          <ptr target="#l11664" type="alt" xml:id="te1963"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49767">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1964"/>
But this time I somehow got to talking to him about his wife and young ones; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0197"/>
by and by

          <app from="kg0197" n="201.20 (207.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0197">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49778">
“What

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0198"/>
make

          <app from="kg0198" n="201.21 (207.5)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0198">
            <lem wit="MS2">make</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">makes</rdg>
          </app>
me feel so bad dis time, ’uz bekase I hear sumpn over yonder on de bank like a whack, er a slam, while ago, en it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0199"/>
mine

          <app from="kg0199" n="201.22 (207.9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0199">
            <lem wit="A">mine</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">remine</rdg>
          </app>
me er de time I treat my little ’Lizabeth so ornery. She warn’t on’y ’bout fo’ year ole, en she tuck de sk’yarlet fever, en had a powful rough spell; but she got well, en one day she was a-stannin’ aroun’, en I says to her, I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49796">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0200"/>
“ ‘Shet

          <app from="kg0200" n="201.27 (208.1)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0200">
            <lem wit="MS2">“ ‘Shet</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
“

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
Shet

            </rdg>
          </app>
de do’.’

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49805">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0201"/>
“She

          <app from="kg0201" n="201.28 (208.2)" type="e" xml:id="kf0201">
            <lem wit="A">“She</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
She

            </rdg>
          </app>
never done it;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1965"/>
jis’

          <ptr target="#l11666" type="alt" xml:id="te1965"/>
stood dah, kiner smilin’ up at me. It make me mad; en I says agin, mighty loud, I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49818">
“ ‘

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0202"/>
Doan

          <app from="kg0202" n="201.30 (208.7)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0202">
            <lem wit="MS2">Doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Doan’</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1966"/>
hear

          <ptr target="#l11667" type="alt" xml:id="te1966"/>
me?—shet de do’!’

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49832">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0203"/>
“She

          <app from="kg0203" n="201.31 (208.9)" type="e" xml:id="kf0203">
            <lem wit="A">“She</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
She

            </rdg>
          </app>
jis’ stood

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1967"/>
de

          <ptr target="#l11668" type="alt" xml:id="te1967"/>
same way, kiner smilin’ up. I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0204"/>
a-bilin’!

          <app from="kg0204" n="201.31 (208.11)" type="e" xml:id="kf0204">
            <lem wit="A">a-bilin’!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a-bilin’.</rdg>
          </app>
I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49853">
“ ‘I lay I

          <hi rend="italic">make</hi>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0205"/>
mine

          <app from="kg0205" n="201.32 (208.13)" type="e" xml:id="kf0205">
            <lem wit="A">mine</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mind</rdg>
          </app>
!’

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e49867">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0206"/>
“En

          <app from="kg0206" n="201.33 (208.14)" type="e" xml:id="kf0206">
            <lem wit="A">“En</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
En

            </rdg>
          </app>
wid dat I fetch’ her a slap side de head dat

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1968"/>
sont her

          <ptr target="#l11669" type="alt" xml:id="te1968"/>
a-sprawlin’. Den I went into de yuther room,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1969"/>
en ’uz

          <ptr target="#l11670" type="alt" xml:id="te1969"/>
gone ’bout ten minutes; en when I come back, dah was dat do’ a-stannin’ open

          <hi rend="italic">yit</hi>
, en dat chile stannin’ mos’ right in it, a-lookin’ down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0207"/>
en

          <app from="kg0207" n="201.36 (209.7)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0207">
            <lem wit="MS2">en</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and</rdg>
          </app>
mournin’, en de tears runnin’ down. My, but I

          <hi rend="italic">wuz</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0208"/>
mad.

          <app from="kg0208" n="201.37 (209.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0208">
            <lem wit="MS2">mad.</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mad,</rdg>
          </app>
I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1970"/>
agwyne

          <ptr target="#l11671" type="alt" xml:id="te1970"/>
for de chile, but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1971"/>
jis’

          <ptr target="#l11672" type="alt" xml:id="te1971"/>
den—it was a do’ dat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0209"/>
open’

          <app from="kg0209" n="201.38 (209.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0209">
            <lem wit="MS2">open’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">open</rdg>
          </app>
innerds—jis’ den, ’long come de wind en

          <pb n="202" xml:id="pb0202"/>
slam it to, behine de chile, ker-

          <hi rend="italic">blam!</hi>
—en my lan’, de chile

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1972"/>
never

          <ptr target="#l11673" type="alt" xml:id="te1972"/>
move’! My breff mos’ hop outer me; en I feel so—so—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0210"/>
doan

          <app from="kg0210" n="202.2 (210.2)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0210">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
know

          <hi rend="italic">how</hi>
I feel.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1973"/>
I crope

          <ptr target="#l11674" type="alt" xml:id="te1973"/>
out, all a-tremblin’, en crope aroun’ en open de do’ easy en slow, en poke my head in behine de chile, sof’ en still, en all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0211"/>
uv

          <app from="kg0211" n="202.5 (210.8)" type="e" xml:id="kf0211">
            <lem wit="A">uv</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0212"/>
sudden

          <app from="kg0212" n="202.5 (210.8)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0212">
            <lem wit="MS2">sudden</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sudden,</rdg>
          </app>
I says

          <hi rend="italic">pow!</hi>
jis’ as loud as I could yell.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1974"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0213"/>
          <hi rend="italic">She never budge!</hi>
          <app from="kg0213" n="202.5–6 (210.10)" type="e" xml:id="kf0213">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">She never budge!</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">She never move’!</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11675" type="alt" xml:id="te1974"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0214"/>
O

          <app from="kg0214" n="202.6 (210.10)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0214">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, Huck, I bust out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0215"/>
a-cryin’,

          <app from="kg0215" n="202.6 (210.11)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0215">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-cryin’,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a-cryin’</rdg>
          </app>
en grab her up in my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0216"/>
arms

          <app from="kg0216" n="202.6 (210.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0216">
            <lem wit="MS2">arms</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">arms,</rdg>
          </app>
en say, ‘

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0217"/>
O

          <app from="kg0217" n="202.7 (210.12)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0217">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh,</rdg>
          </app>
de po’ little thing!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0035"/>
de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1975"/>
Lord

          <ptr target="#l11676" type="alt" xml:id="te1975"/>
God Amighty

          <ptr target="#mt0035" type="alt" xml:id="wn0035"/>
fogive po’ ole Jim, kaze he never gwyne to fogive

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0218"/>
hisseff

          <app from="kg0218" n="202.8 (210.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0218">
            <lem wit="C">hisseff</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hisself</rdg>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
his-

              <lb/>
seff

            </rdg>
          </app>
as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0219"/>
long’s

          <app from="kg0219" n="202.8 (210.16)" type="e" xml:id="kf0219">
            <lem wit="A">long’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">long as</rdg>
          </app>
he live!’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0220"/>
O

          <app from="kg0220" n="202.8 (210.16)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0220">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sv0045"/>
she was plumb deef en dumb

          <ptr target="#as0209" type="an" xml:id="vs0045"/>
, Huck, plumb deef en dumb—en I’d ben

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="kg0221"/>
a treat’n

          <app from="kg0221" n="202.9–10 (210.18)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0221">
            <lem wit="MS2">a treat’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a-treat’n</rdg>
          </app>
her so!”

          <app from="kg0191" n="201.7–202.10 (205.10–210.18)" type="hc" xml:id="kf0191">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">I . . . so!”</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="uma030">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11665" type="alt" xml:id="te1964"/>
        </p>
      </div1>
