        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e50094">
day, towards night, we laid up under a little willow

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4012"/>
towhead

          <app from="pr4012" n="203.2 (211.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la5902">
            <lem wit="MS2">towhead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">tow-head</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1977"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l11678" type="alt" xml:id="te1977"/>
in the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1978"/>
middle

          <ptr target="#l11679" type="alt" xml:id="te1978"/>
, where there was a village on each side of the river, and the duke and the king begun to lay out a plan for working them towns. Jim he spoke to the duke, and said he hoped it wouldn’t take but a few hours, because it got mighty heavy and tiresome to him when he had to lay all day in the wigwam tied with the rope. You see, when we left him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4013"/>
all

          <app from="pr4013" n="203.14 (211.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5903">
            <lem wit="A Cent">all</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5904">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
alone we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4014"/>
had

          <app from="pr4014" n="203.14 (211.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5905">
            <lem wit="A Cent">had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was obliged</rdg>
          </app>
to tie him, because if anybody happened on him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1979"/>
all

          <ptr target="#l11680" type="alt" xml:id="te1979"/>
          <ptr target="#l11677" type="alt" xml:id="te1976"/>
by himself and not tied, it wouldn’t look much like he was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4015"/>
runaway

          <app from="pr4015" n="203.18 (211½.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la5906">
            <lem wit="A Cent">runaway</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
run-

              <lb/>
away

            </rdg>
          </app>
nigger, you know. So the duke

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1980"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l11681" type="alt" xml:id="te1980"/>
it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
kind of hard to have to lay roped all day, and he’d cipher out some way to get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1981"/>
around

          <ptr target="#l11682" type="alt" xml:id="te1981"/>
it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50157">
He was uncommon bright, the duke was, and he soon

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1982"/>
struck it.

          <ptr target="#l11683" type="alt" xml:id="te1982"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1984"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4016"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1983"/>
He

          <app from="pr4016" n="203.22 (212[¼][A].1)" type="e" xml:id="la5907">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5908">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
He

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">[¶] He</rdg>
          </app>
dressed Jim up in King

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4017"/>
Lear’s

          <app from="pr4017" n="203.22 (212[¼][A].1)" type="e" xml:id="la5909">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Lear’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Leer’s</rdg>
          </app>
outfit—it

          <ptr target="#l11685" type="alt" xml:id="te1984"/>
was a long curtain-calico gown, and a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1985"/>
white

          <ptr target="#l11686" type="alt" xml:id="te1985"/>
horse-hair wig and whiskers; and then he took his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4018"/>
theatre-

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1986"/>
paint

          <ptr target="#l11687" type="alt" xml:id="te1986"/>
          <app from="pr4018" n="203.24 (212[¼][A].7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5910">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">theatre-paint</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">theater-paint</rdg>
          </app>
and painted Jim’s face and hands and ears and neck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4019"/>
all over

          <app from="pr4019" n="203.25 (212[¼][A].9)" type="e" xml:id="la5911">
            <lem wit="A Cent">all over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5912">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a dead dull solid blue, like a man that’s been drownded nine days.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4020"/>
Blamed

          <app from="pr4020" n="203.26 (212[¼][A].11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la5913">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Blamed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m blamed</rdg>
          </app>
if he warn’t the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4021"/>
horriblest looking

          <app from="pr4021" n="203.26 (212[¼][A].12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5914">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">horriblest looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">horriblest-looking</rdg>
          </app>
outrage I ever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1987"/>
see. Then the duke took and wrote

          <ptr target="#l11688" type="alt" xml:id="te1987"/>
          <ptr target="#l11684" type="alt" xml:id="te1983"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1988"/>
out a sign

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1989"/>
on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4022"/>
shingle,

          <app from="pr4022" n="203.27 (212½[B].1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5915">
            <lem wit="MS2">shingle,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
shingle

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11690" type="alt" xml:id="te1989"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4023"/>
so—

          <app from="pr4023" n="203.27 (212½[B].1)" type="hc" xml:id="la5916">
            <lem wit="MS2">
so—

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5917">extra line space</note>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
so—

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5918">no extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
so:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5919">extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <p rend="center" xml:id="d1e50262">
            <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0064"/>
            <hi rend="italic">Sick</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4024"/>
            <hi rend="italic">Arab</hi>
            <app from="pr4024" n="✱203.28 (212½[B].2)" type="e" xml:id="la5920">
              <lem wit="A Cent">
                <hi rend="italic">Arab</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="italic">A-rab</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <ptr target="#tb0064" type="te" xml:id="tv0064"/>
—

            <hi rend="italic">but harmless when not out of his</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4025"/>
            <hi rend="italic">head.</hi>
            <app from="pr4025" n="203.28 (212½[B].3)" type="e" xml:id="la5921">
              <lem wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="italic">head.</hi>
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5922">extra line space</note>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2 A">
                <hi rend="italic">head.</hi>
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5923">no extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </p>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50292">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4026"/>
And

          <app from="pr4026" n="203.29 (212½[B].4)" type="e" xml:id="la5924">
            <lem wit="A Cent">[¶] And</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5925">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
—and

            </rdg>
          </app>
he nailed that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1990"/>
shingle

          <ptr target="#l11691" type="alt" xml:id="te1990"/>
to a lath, and stood

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1991"/>
the lath

          <ptr target="#l11692" type="alt" xml:id="te1991"/>
up four

          <ptr target="#l11689" type="alt" xml:id="te1988"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1992"/>
or five

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1993"/>
foot

          <ptr target="#l11694" type="alt" xml:id="te1993"/>
in front of the wigwam.

          <ptr target="#l11693" type="alt" xml:id="te1992"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1994"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ar6000"/>
Jim

          <app from="ar6000" n="203.30 (212[D].1)" type="e" xml:id="la5926">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5927">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Jim

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">[¶] Jim</rdg>
          </app>
was satisfied. He said it was a

          <pb n="204" xml:id="pb0204"/>
sight better than laying tied a couple of years

          <ptr target="#l11695" type="alt" xml:id="te1994"/>
every day and trembling all over every time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4028"/>
there was

          <app from="pr4028" n="204.2 (213.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5928">
            <lem wit="A Cent">there was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he heard</rdg>
          </app>
a sound. The duke told him to make himself

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4029"/>
free

          <app from="pr4029" n="204.3 (213.4)" type="e" xml:id="la5929">
            <lem wit="A Cent">free</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">perfectly free</rdg>
          </app>
and easy, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1995"/>
if anybody

          <ptr target="#l11707" type="alt" xml:id="te1995"/>
ever come meddling around, he must

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1996"/>
hop out of the wigwam, and

          <ptr target="#l11708" type="alt" xml:id="te1996"/>
carry on a little, and fetch a howl or two like a wild beast, and he reckoned they would light out and leave him alone.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1997"/>
Which was sound enough judgment; but you take the average man, and he wouldn’t wait for him to howl.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4030"/>
Why, he didn’t only look like he was dead, he looked considerable more than that.

          <app from="pr4030" n="204.8–9 (213verso.4–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5930">
            <lem wit="A">Why . . . considerable more than that.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Why . . . like he was mortified.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5931">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11709" type="alt" xml:id="te1997"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50377">
These rapscallions wanted to try the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4031"/>
Nonesuch

          <app from="pr4031" n="204.10 (213.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5932">
            <lem wit="A">Nonesuch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
None-

              <lb/>
such

            </rdg>
          </app>
again, because there was so much money in it, but they judged it wouldn’t be safe, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4032"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4032" n="204.12 (213.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5933">
            <lem wit="A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
mayb

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5934">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">maybe</rdg>
          </app>
the news

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4033"/>
might a

          <app from="pr4033" n="204.12 (213.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5935">
            <lem wit="A">might a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of it had</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">might ’a’</rdg>
          </app>
worked along down by this time.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1998"/>
They

          <ptr target="#l11710" type="alt" xml:id="te1998"/>
couldn’t hit

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4034"/>
no

          <app from="pr4034" n="204.13 (213.18)" type="e" xml:id="la5936">
            <lem wit="A Cent">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on any</rdg>
          </app>
project that suited, exactly; so at last the duke said he reckoned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4035"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr4035" n="204.14 (214.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5937">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he would</rdg>
          </app>
lay off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1999"/>
and work his brains

          <ptr target="#l11711" type="alt" xml:id="te1999"/>
an hour or two and see if he couldn’t put up something

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4036"/>
on

          <app from="pr4036" n="204.15 (214.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la5938">
            <lem wit="A Cent">on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for the benefit of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="svm045"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4037"/>
Arkansaw

          <app from="pr4037" n="204.15 (214.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5939">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Arkansaw</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Arkansas</rdg>
          </app>
village; and the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4038"/>
he allowed

          <app from="pr4038" n="204.16 (214.7)" type="e" xml:id="la5940">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he allowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">allowed</rdg>
          </app>
he would drop over to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4039"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr4039" n="204.16 (214.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5941">
            <lem wit="A Cent">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
village

          <ptr target="#as0210" type="an" xml:id="vsm045"/>
, without any plan, but just trust in Providence to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4040"/>
lead

          <app from="pr4040" n="204.17 (214.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5942">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">direct</rdg>
          </app>
him the profitable way—meaning the devil, I reckon. We had all bought store clothes where we stopped last; and now the king put

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2000"/>
his’n

          <ptr target="#l11712" type="alt" xml:id="te2000"/>
on, and he told me to put mine on. I done it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2001"/>
of course.

          <ptr target="#l11713" type="alt" xml:id="te2001"/>
The king’s duds was all black, and he did look real swell and starchy. I never knowed how clothes could change a body

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4041"/>
before.

          <app from="pr4041" n="204.22 (215.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5943">
            <lem wit="A Cent">before.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
before

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5944">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Why, before, he looked like the orneriest old rip that ever was; but now, when he’d take off his new white beaver and make a bow and do a smile, he looked that grand and good and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4042"/>
pious

          <app from="pr4042" n="204.25 (215.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5945">
            <lem wit="A Cent">pious</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">noble</rdg>
          </app>
that you’d say he had walked right out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4043"/>
ark

          <app from="pr4043" n="204.26 (215.17)" type="e" xml:id="la5946">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ark</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Bible</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4044"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4044" n="204.26 (215.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la5947">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
was old Leviticus himself. Jim cleaned up the canoe, and I got my paddle ready. There was a big steamboat laying at the shore away up under the point, about three mile above town—been there a couple of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2002"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4045"/>
hours—

          <app from="pr4045" n="204.29 (216.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5948">
            <lem wit="MS2">hours—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">hours,</rdg>
          </app>
taking on freight.

          <ptr target="#l11714" type="alt" xml:id="te2002"/>
Says the king:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50540">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4046"/>
Seein’

          <app from="pr4046" n="204.30 (216.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5949">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Seein’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Seeing</rdg>
          </app>
how I’m dressed, I reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4047"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4047" n="204.30 (216.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5950">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4048"/>
I better

          <app from="pr4048" n="204.30 (216.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5951">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I better</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’d better</rdg>
          </app>
arrive

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4049"/>
down

          <app from="pr4049" n="204.30 (216.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5952">
            <lem wit="A Cent">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5953">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4050"/>
St.

          <app from="pr4050" n="204.31 (216.12)" type="e" xml:id="la5954">
            <lem wit="A Cent">St.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
St

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Louis or Cincinnati, or some other big place. Go for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4051"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr4051" n="204.32 (216.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la5955">
            <lem wit="A Cent">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
, Huckleberry; we’ll come down to the village on her.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50593">
I didn’t have to be ordered twice, to go and take a steamboat ride. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2003"/>
fetched

          <ptr target="#l11715" type="alt" xml:id="te2003"/>
the shore a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4052"/>
half a mile

          <app from="pr4052" n="204.34 (217.4–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5956">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">half a mile</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">half-mile</rdg>
          </app>
above the village, and then went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4053"/>
scooting

          <app from="pr4053" n="204.35 (217.6)" type="e" xml:id="la5957">
            <lem wit="A Cent">scooting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">skimming</rdg>
          </app>
along the bluff bank in the easy water. Pretty soon we come to a nice

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4054"/>
innocent looking

          <app from="pr4054" n="204.36 (217.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la5958">
            <lem wit="MS2">innocent looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">innocent-looking</rdg>
          </app>
young country

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4055"/>
jake

          <app from="pr4055" n="204.36 (217.10)" type="e" xml:id="la5959">
            <lem wit="A Cent">jake</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">fellow</rdg>
          </app>
setting on a log swabbing the sweat off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4056"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2004"/>
of

          <ptr target="#l11716" type="alt" xml:id="te2004"/>
          <app from="pr4056" n="204.37 (217.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5960">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5961">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
his face, for it was powerful warm weather; and he had a couple of big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4057"/>
carpet bags

          <app from="pr4057" n="204.38 (217.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5962">
            <lem wit="MS2">carpet bags</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">carpet-bags</rdg>
          </app>
by him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50653">
          <pb n="205" xml:id="pb0205"/>
“Run her nose in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2005"/>
shore,”

          <ptr target="#l11717" type="alt" xml:id="te2005"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2006"/>
says the

          <ptr target="#l11718" type="alt" xml:id="te2006"/>
king. I done it. “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4058"/>
Wher’

          <app from="pr4058" n="205.1 (218.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5963">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Wher’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Where</rdg>
          </app>
you bound

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2007"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l11719" type="alt" xml:id="te2007"/>
, young man?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50675">“For the steamboat; going to Orleans.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50677">
“Git aboard,” says the king. “Hold on a minute, my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4059"/>
servant ’ll

          <app from="pr4059" n="205.4 (218.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5964">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">servant ’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">servant’ll</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4060"/>
he’p you

          <app from="pr4060" n="205.5 (218.7)" type="e" xml:id="la5965">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’p you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">help you</rdg>
          </app>
with them bags. Jump out and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4061"/>
he’p the

          <app from="pr4061" n="205.5 (218.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5966">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’p the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">help the</rdg>
          </app>
gentleman, Adolphus”—meaning me, I see.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y20501">
          <graphic url="y20501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">adolphus</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50707">
I done so, and then we all three started on again. The young chap was mighty thankful; said it was tough work toting his baggage such weather. He asked the king where he was going, and the king told him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4062"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr4062" n="205.10 (219.2)" type="e" xml:id="la5967">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he had</rdg>
          </app>
come down the river and landed at the other village this morning, and now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4063"/>
he

          <app from="pr4063" n="205.11 (219.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5968">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5969">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
was going up a few mile to see an old friend on a farm up there. The young fellow says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50726">
“When I first see you, I says to myself, ‘It’s Mr. Wilks,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2008"/>
sure

          <ptr target="#l11720" type="alt" xml:id="te2008"/>
, and he come mighty near getting here in time.’ But then I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4064"/>
says,

          <app from="pr4064" n="205.14 (219.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la5970">
            <lem wit="MS2">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
says

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
again, ‘No, I reckon it ain’t him, or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4065"/>
else

          <app from="pr4065" n="205.15 (219.14)" type="e" xml:id="la5971">
            <lem wit="A Cent">else</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de5972">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2009"/>
wouldn’t

          <ptr target="#l11721" type="alt" xml:id="te2009"/>
be paddling up the river.’ You

          <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
him, are you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50757">
“No, my name’s Blodgett—Elexander Blodgett—

          <hi rend="italic">Reverend</hi>
Elexander Blodgett, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4066"/>
spose

          <app from="pr4066" n="205.18 (220.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5973">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">spose</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">s’pose</rdg>
          </app>
I must say, as I’m one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4067"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4067" n="205.18 (220.3)" type="e" xml:id="la5974">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
the Lord’s poor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2010"/>
servants.

          <ptr target="#l11722" type="alt" xml:id="te2010"/>
But still I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4068"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2011"/>
jest

          <ptr target="#l11723" type="alt" xml:id="te2011"/>
          <app from="pr4068" n="205.19 (220.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5975">
            <lem wit="MS2">jest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">jist</rdg>
          </app>
as able to be sorry for Mr. Wilks for not arriving in time, all the same, if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2012"/>
he’s

          <ptr target="#l11724" type="alt" xml:id="te2012"/>
missed anything by it—which I hope

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2013"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l11725" type="alt" xml:id="te2013"/>
hasn’t.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50802">
          <pb n="206" xml:id="pb0206"/>
“Well, he don’t miss any property by it, because he’ll get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4069"/>
that,

          <app from="pr4069" n="206.1 (220.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5976">
            <lem wit="MS2">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all right; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4070"/>
he ’s

          <app from="pr4070" n="206.2 (220.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la5977">
            <lem wit="MS2">he ’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">he’s</rdg>
          </app>
missed seeing his brother Peter die—which he mayn’t mind, nobody

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2014"/>
can

          <ptr target="#l11726" type="alt" xml:id="te2014"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4071"/>
tell,

          <app from="pr4071" n="206.3 (220.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5978">
            <lem wit="MS2">tell,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
tell

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
as to that—but his brother

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4072"/>
would

          <app from="pr4072" n="206.3 (220.16)" type="e" xml:id="la5979">
            <lem wit="A Cent">would</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Peter would</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4073"/>
a

          <app from="pr4073" n="206.3 (220.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la5980">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’</rdg>
          </app>
give anything in this world to see

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
before he died; never talked about nothing else all these three weeks; hadn’t seen him since they was boys together—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2015"/>
and hadn’t ever seen

          <ptr target="#l11727" type="alt" xml:id="te2015"/>
his brother

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4074"/>
William,

          <app from="pr4074" n="206.6 (221.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la5981">
            <lem wit="MS2">William,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
William

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2016"/>
at all—

          <ptr target="#l11728" type="alt" xml:id="te2016"/>
that’s the deef and dumb one—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2017"/>
William ain’t

          <ptr target="#l11729" type="alt" xml:id="te2017"/>
more than thirty or thirty-five. Peter and George was the only ones that come out here; George was the married brother; him and his wife both died last year.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2018"/>
Harvey and William’s

          <ptr target="#l11730" type="alt" xml:id="te2018"/>
the only

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2019"/>
ones

          <ptr target="#l11731" type="alt" xml:id="te2019"/>
that’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4075"/>
left,

          <app from="pr4075" n="206.10 (221.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la5982">
            <lem wit="MS2">left,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
left

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now; and as I was saying,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2020"/>
they

          <ptr target="#l11732" type="alt" xml:id="te2020"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2021"/>
haven’t

          <ptr target="#l11733" type="alt" xml:id="te2021"/>
got here in time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50896">
“Did

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2022"/>
anybody

          <ptr target="#l11734" type="alt" xml:id="te2022"/>
send

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2023"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4076"/>
’em

          <app from="pr4076" n="206.12 (222.1)" type="e" xml:id="la5983">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11735" type="alt" xml:id="te2023"/>
word?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e50912">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4077"/>
O

          <app from="pr4077" n="206.13 (222.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5984">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4078"/>
yes;

          <app from="pr4078" n="206.13 (222.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la5985">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">yes;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">yes—</rdg>
          </app>
a month

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2024"/>
or two

          <ptr target="#l11736" type="alt" xml:id="te2024"/>
ago, when Peter was first took; because Peter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4079"/>
said, then,

          <app from="pr4079" n="206.14 (222.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la5986">
            <lem wit="MS2">said, then,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
said

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
then

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2025"/>
sorter

          <ptr target="#l11737" type="alt" xml:id="te2025"/>
felt like he warn’t going to get well this time. You see, he was pretty old,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2026"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l11738" type="alt" xml:id="te2026"/>
George’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4080"/>
g’yirls

          <app from="pr4080" n="206.15 (222.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5987">
            <lem wit="A Cent">g’yirls</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gals</rdg>
          </app>
was too young to be much company for him, except Mary

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4081"/>
Jane

          <app from="pr4081" n="206.16 (222.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la5988">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Jane</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Jane,</rdg>
          </app>
the red-headed one; and so he was kinder

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4082"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0065"/>
lonesome

          <app from="pr4082" n="✱206.17 (222.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la5989">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lonesome</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
lonse-

              <lb/>
some

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0065" type="te" xml:id="tv0065"/>
after George and his wife died, and didn’t seem to care much to live. He most desperately wanted to see Harvey—and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4083"/>
William too,

          <app from="pr4083" n="206.19 (222.17)" type="e" xml:id="la5990">
            <lem wit="A">William too,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
William, too

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">William, too,</rdg>
          </app>
for that matter—because he was one of them kind that can’t bear to make a will. He left a letter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4084"/>
behind,

          <app from="pr4084" n="206.21 (223.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la5991">
            <lem wit="MS2">behind,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
behind

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for Harvey, and said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4085"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr4085" n="206.21 (223.5)" type="e" xml:id="la5992">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he had</rdg>
          </app>
told in it where his money was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2027"/>
hid,

          <ptr target="#l11739" type="alt" xml:id="te2027"/>
and how

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2028"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l11740" type="alt" xml:id="te2028"/>
wanted the rest of the property divided up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4086"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2029"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l11741" type="alt" xml:id="te2029"/>
          <app from="pr4086" n="206.22 (223.8)" type="e" xml:id="la5993">
            <lem wit="A Cent">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">so that</rdg>
          </app>
George’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4087"/>
g’yirls

          <app from="pr4087" n="206.23 (223.9)" type="e" xml:id="la5994">
            <lem wit="A Cent">g’yirls</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gals</rdg>
          </app>
would be all right—for George didn’t leave

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2030"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4088"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr4088" n="206.23 (223.11)" type="e" xml:id="la5995">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l11742" type="alt" xml:id="te2030"/>
And that letter was all they could get him to put a pen to.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51047">
“Why do you reckon Harvey don’t come?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4089"/>
Wher’

          <app from="pr4089" n="206.25 (223.15)" type="e" xml:id="la5996">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Wher’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Where</rdg>
          </app>
does he live?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51058">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4090"/>
O

          <app from="pr4090" n="206.26 (223.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la5997">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, he lives in England—Sheffield—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2031"/>
preaches there—

          <ptr target="#l11743" type="alt" xml:id="te2031"/>
hasn’t ever been in this country. He hasn’t had

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2032"/>
any

          <ptr target="#l11744" type="alt" xml:id="te2032"/>
too much time—and besides he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2033"/>
mightn’t

          <ptr target="#l11745" type="alt" xml:id="te2033"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4091"/>
a got

          <app from="pr4091" n="206.28 (224.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la5998">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a got</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ got</rdg>
          </app>
the letter at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2034"/>
all,

          <ptr target="#l11746" type="alt" xml:id="te2034"/>
you know.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51093">
“Too bad, too bad he couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4092"/>
a lived

          <app from="pr4092" n="206.29 (224.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la5999">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a lived</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ lived</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4093"/>
to

          <app from="pr4093" n="206.29 (224.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6000">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">too</rdg>
          </app>
see his brothers, poor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4094"/>
soul.

          <app from="pr4094" n="206.30 (224.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6001">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">soul.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">soul!</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4095"/>
You

          <app from="pr4095" n="206.30 (224.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6002">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">did you</rdg>
          </app>
going to Orleans, you say?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51126">
“Yes, but that ain’t only a part of it.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="svm046"/>
I’m going in a ship, next Wednesday, for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4096"/>
Ryo

          <app from="pr4096" n="206.32 (224.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6003">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Ryo</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Rio</rdg>
          </app>
Janeero

          <ptr target="#as0211" type="an" xml:id="vsm046"/>
, where my uncle lives.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51140">
“It’s a pretty long journey. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4097"/>
it ’ll

          <app from="pr4097" n="206.33 (225.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6004">
            <lem wit="MS2">it ’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">it’ll</rdg>
          </app>
be lovely; I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2035"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4098"/>
wisht

          <app from="pr4098" n="206.33 (225.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6005">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wisht</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wish</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11747" type="alt" xml:id="te2035"/>
I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2036"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4099"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr4099" n="206.33 (225.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6006">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l11748" type="alt" xml:id="te2036"/>
Is Mary Jane the oldest? How old is the others?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51172">
“Mary Jane’s nineteen, Susan’s fifteen, and Joanna’s about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2037"/>
fourteen

          <ptr target="#l11749" type="alt" xml:id="te2037"/>
—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2038"/>
that’s the

          <ptr target="#l11750" type="alt" xml:id="te2038"/>
one that gives herself to good works and has a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4100"/>
harelip

          <app from="pr4100" n="206.36–37 (225.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6007">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51191">
“Poor things! to be left alone in the cold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4101"/>
world,

          <app from="pr4101" n="206.38 (225.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6008">
            <lem wit="MS2">world,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
world

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
so.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51201">
          <pb n="207" xml:id="pb0207"/>
“Well, they could be worse off. Old Peter had friends, and they ain’t going to let them come to no harm. There’s Hobson, the Babtis’ preacher; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2039"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4102"/>
deacon

          <app from="pr4102" n="207.3 (226.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6009">
            <lem wit="MS2">deacon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Deacon</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11751" type="alt" xml:id="te2039"/>
Lot Hovey, and Ben Rucker, and Abner

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4103"/>
Shackleford;

          <app from="pr4103" n="207.4 (226.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6010">
            <lem wit="MS2">Shackleford;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Shackleford,</rdg>
          </app>
and Levi Bell, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4104"/>
lawyer;

          <app from="pr4104" n="207.4 (226.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6011">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">lawyer;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">lawyer,</rdg>
          </app>
and Dr.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4105"/>
Robinson;

          <app from="pr4105" n="207.4 (226.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6012">
            <lem wit="MS2">Robinson;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Robinson,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2040"/>
and their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4106"/>
wives;

          <app from="pr4106" n="207.5 (226.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6013">
            <lem wit="MS2">wives;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">wives,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11752" type="alt" xml:id="te2040"/>
and the widow Bartley, and—well, there’s a lot of them;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2041"/>
but

          <ptr target="#l11753" type="alt" xml:id="te2041"/>
these are the ones that Peter

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2042"/>
was thickest with,

          <ptr target="#l11754" type="alt" xml:id="te2042"/>
and used to write

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4107"/>
about,

          <app from="pr4107" n="207.7 (226.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6014">
            <lem wit="MS2">about,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
about

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
sometimes, when he wrote home; so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4108"/>
Harvey’ll

          <app from="pr4108" n="207.7 (226.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6015">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Harvey’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Harvey ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
know where to look for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4109"/>
friends

          <app from="pr4109" n="207.8 (226.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6016">
            <lem wit="A Cent">friends</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">friends, too,</rdg>
          </app>
when he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4110"/>
gets

          <app from="pr4110" n="207.8 (226.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6017">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">gets</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">get’s</rdg>
          </app>
here.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51291">
Well, the old man he went on asking questions till he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0036"/>
just fairly emptied that young fellow. Blamed if he didn’t inquire about everybody and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4111"/>
every thing

          <app from="pr4111" n="207.11 (227.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6018">
            <lem wit="MS2">every thing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">everything</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2043"/>
in that blessed

          <ptr target="#l11755" type="alt" xml:id="te2043"/>
town, and all about all the Wilkses; and about Peter’s business—which was a tanner; and about George’s—which was a carpenter; and about Harvey’s—which was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2044"/>
dissentering

          <ptr target="#l11756" type="alt" xml:id="te2044"/>
minister;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4112"/>
and so on,

          <app from="pr4112" n="207.14 (227.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6019">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">and so on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6020">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and so on. Then he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51320">
“What did you want to walk all the way up to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4113"/>
steamboat,

          <app from="pr4113" n="207.16 (227.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6021">
            <lem wit="MS2">steamboat,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
steamboat

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for?”

          <ptr target="#mt0036" type="alt" xml:id="wn0036"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51331">
“Because she’s a big Orleans boat, and I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2045"/>
afeard

          <ptr target="#l11757" type="alt" xml:id="te2045"/>
she mightn’t stop there. When they’re deep they won’t stop for a hail. A Cincinnati boat will, but this is a St. Louis one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51337">“Was Peter Wilks well off?”</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y20701">
          <graphic url="y20701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">he fairly emptied that young fellow</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51345">
          <pb n="208" xml:id="pb0208"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4114"/>
O

          <app from="pr4114" n="208.1 (228.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6022">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes, pretty well off. He had houses and land, and it’s reckoned he left

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2046"/>
three

          <ptr target="#l11758" type="alt" xml:id="te2046"/>
or four thousand in cash hid up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4115"/>
som’ers.

          <app from="pr4115" n="208.2 (228.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la6023">
            <lem wit="A Cent">som’ers.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">som’ers. They say he said he had.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51368">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2047"/>
“When did you say he died?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51371">
“I didn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4116"/>
say;

          <app from="pr4116" n="208.4 (228verso.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6024">
            <lem wit="MS2">say;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">say,</rdg>
          </app>
but it was last night.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51381">“Funeral to-morrow, likely?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51383">
“Yes,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2048"/>
’bout

          <ptr target="#l11760" type="alt" xml:id="te2048"/>
the middle of the day.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51389">
“Well, it’s all terrible sad; but we’ve all got to go, one time or another. So what we want to do is to be prepared; then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4117"/>
we’re

          <app from="pr4117" n="208.8 (228verso.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6025">
            <lem wit="A Cent">we’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we are</rdg>
          </app>
all right.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51399">
“Yes, sir,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4118"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr4118" n="208.10 (228verso.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6026">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">its</rdg>
          </app>
the best way.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2049"/>
Ma used to always say that.”

          <ptr target="#l11761" type="alt" xml:id="te2049"/>
          <ptr target="#l11759" type="alt" xml:id="te2047"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51413">
When we struck the boat, she was about done loading, and pretty soon she got off. The king never said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4119"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr4119" n="208.12 (229.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la6027">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
about going aboard, so I lost my ride, after all. When the boat was gone, the king made me paddle up another

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4120"/>
mile,

          <app from="pr4120" n="208.14 (229.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6028">
            <lem wit="MS2">mile,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
mile

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to a lonesome place, and then he got ashore and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2050"/>
says

          <ptr target="#l11762" type="alt" xml:id="te2050"/>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51436">
“Now hustle back, right off, and fetch the duke up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2051"/>
here, and the new carpet-bags.

          <ptr target="#l11763" type="alt" xml:id="te2051"/>
And if he’s gone over to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4121"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2052"/>
t’other

          <ptr target="#l11764" type="alt" xml:id="te2052"/>
          <app from="pr4121" n="208.17 (229.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6029">
            <lem wit="A Cent">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
side, go over there

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2053"/>
and git

          <ptr target="#l11765" type="alt" xml:id="te2053"/>
him. And tell him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2054"/>
to git

          <ptr target="#l11766" type="alt" xml:id="te2054"/>
himself up regardless. Shove along, now.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51461">
I see what

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
was up to; but I never said

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2055"/>
nothing,

          <ptr target="#l11767" type="alt" xml:id="te2055"/>
of course. When I got back with the duke,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2056"/>
we hid the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4122"/>
canoe,

          <app from="pr4122" n="208.21 (230.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6030">
            <lem wit="MS2">canoe,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
canoe

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and then

          <ptr target="#l11768" type="alt" xml:id="te2056"/>
they set down on a log, and the king told him everything, just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4123"/>
like

          <app from="pr4123" n="208.22 (230.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6031">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">as</rdg>
          </app>
the young fellow had said it—every last word of it. And all the time he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4124"/>
a doing

          <app from="pr4124" n="208.23 (230.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6032">
            <lem wit="A">a doing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">doing</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-doing</rdg>
          </app>
it, he tried to talk like an Englishman; and he done it pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4125"/>
well,

          <app from="pr4125" n="208.24 (230.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6033">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">well,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
well

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2057"/>
too, for a slouch.

          <ptr target="#l11769" type="alt" xml:id="te2057"/>
I can’t imitate

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2058"/>
him,

          <ptr target="#l11770" type="alt" xml:id="te2058"/>
and so I ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4126"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr4126" n="208.25 (230.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6034">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2059"/>
try to

          <ptr target="#l11771" type="alt" xml:id="te2059"/>
; but he really done it pretty

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2060"/>
good. Then

          <ptr target="#l11772" type="alt" xml:id="te2060"/>
he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51535">
“How are you on the deef and dumb,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2061"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4127"/>
Bilgewater

          <app from="pr4127" n="208.27 (231.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6035">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Bilgewater</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Bilgegwater</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11773" type="alt" xml:id="te2061"/>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51547">
The duke said, leave him alone for that; said he had played a deef and dumb person on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4128"/>
histrionic

          <app from="pr4128" n="208.29 (231.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6036">
            <lem wit="A Cent">histrionic</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">histeronic</rdg>
          </app>
boards.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2062"/>
So then they waited for a steamboat.

          <ptr target="#l11774" type="alt" xml:id="te2062"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51560">
About the middle of the afternoon a couple of little boats come along, but they didn’t come from high enough up the river; but at last there was a big

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2063"/>
one, and they

          <ptr target="#l11775" type="alt" xml:id="te2063"/>
hailed her. She sent out her yawl, and we went aboard, and she was from Cincinnati; and when they found we only wanted to go four or five mile, they was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2064"/>
booming

          <ptr target="#l11776" type="alt" xml:id="te2064"/>
mad, and give us a cussing, and said they wouldn’t land us. But the king was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4129"/>
ca’m

          <app from="pr4129" n="208.37 (232.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6037">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ca’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">c’am</rdg>
          </app>
. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51579">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="an0050"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4130"/>
If

          <app from="pr4130" n="208.38 (232.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6038">
            <lem wit="A Cent">If</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Ef</rdg>
          </app>
gentlemen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4131"/>
kin

          <app from="pr4131" n="208.38 (232.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6039">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">can</rdg>
          </app>
afford to pay a dollar a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4132"/>
mile,

          <app from="pr4132" n="208.38 (232.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6040">
            <lem wit="MS2">mile,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
mile

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
apiece, to be took

          <pb n="209" xml:id="pb0209"/>
on and put off in a yawl, a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4133"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr4133" n="209.1 (232.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6041">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4134"/>
kin

          <app from="pr4134" n="209.1 (232.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6042">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">can</rdg>
          </app>
afford to carry ’em

          <ptr target="#as0212" type="an" xml:id="pt0001"/>
, can’t it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51626">
So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4135"/>
they

          <app from="pr4135" n="209.3 (232.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6043">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">then they</rdg>
          </app>
softened down and said it was all right; and when we got to the village, they yawled us ashore. About two dozen men flocked down, when they see the yawl

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4136"/>
a coming

          <app from="pr4136" n="209.5 (232.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6044">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-coming</rdg>
          </app>
; and when the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4137"/>
says—

          <app from="pr4137" n="209.5 (233.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6045">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">says—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51652">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4138"/>
“Kin

          <app from="pr4138" n="209.6 (233.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6046">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] “Kin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">[¶] “Can</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6047">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
“Kin

            </rdg>
          </app>
any of you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4139"/>
gentlemen

          <app from="pr4139" n="209.6 (233.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la6048">
            <lem wit="A Cent">gentlemen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
gentle-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
tell me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4140"/>
wher’

          <app from="pr4140" n="209.6 (233.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6049">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wher’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">where</rdg>
          </app>
Mr. Peter Wilks lives?” they give a glance at one another, and nodded their heads, as much as to say, “What

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2065"/>
d’

          <ptr target="#l11777" type="alt" xml:id="te2065"/>
I tell you?” Then one of them says, kind of soft and gentle:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51690">
“I’m sorry, sir, but the best we can do is to tell you where he

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4141"/>
live,

          <app from="pr4141" n="209.11 (233.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6050">
            <lem wit="MS2">live,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
live

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yesterday evening.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51702">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2066"/>
Sudden as winking, the

          <ptr target="#l11778" type="alt" xml:id="te2066"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4142"/>
ornery

          <app from="pr4142" n="209.12 (233.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6051">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ornery</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">derned</rdg>
          </app>
old

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2067"/>
cretur went all to smash, and

          <ptr target="#l11779" type="alt" xml:id="te2067"/>
fell up against

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2068"/>
the man,

          <ptr target="#l11780" type="alt" xml:id="te2068"/>
and put his chin on his shoulder, and cried down his back, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51723">
“Alas, alas, our poor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2069"/>
brother—gone, and we never got to see him; oh,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4143"/>
it’s too,

          <app from="pr4143" n="209.16 (234.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6052">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
it’s too,

              <hi rend="italic">too</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
it is

              <hi rend="italic">too</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">too</hi>
hard!”

          <ptr target="#l11781" type="alt" xml:id="te2069"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51742">
Then he turns around, blubbering, and makes a lot of idiotic signs to the duke on his hands, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4144"/>
blamed

          <app from="pr4144" n="209.18 (234.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6053">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blamed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m blamed</rdg>
          </app>
if

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
didn’t drop a carpet-bag

          <pb n="210" xml:id="pb0210"/>
and bust out a-crying. If they warn’t the beatenest lot, them two frauds, that ever I struck.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y20901">
          <graphic url="y20901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4145"/>
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">alas, our poor brother.</hi>
”

            <app from="pr4145" n="209 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la6054">
              <lem wit="A">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">alas, our poor brother</hi>
.”

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6055">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">alas, our poor brother</hi>
!

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51777">
Well, the men gethered around, and sympathized with them, and said all sorts of kind things to them, and carried their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4146"/>
carpet bags

          <app from="pr4146" n="210.4 (234.17–235.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6056">
            <lem wit="MS2">carpet bags</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">carpet-bags</rdg>
          </app>
up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2070"/>
the hill

          <ptr target="#l11782" type="alt" xml:id="te2070"/>
for them, and let them lean on them and cry, and told the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2071"/>
king all

          <ptr target="#l11783" type="alt" xml:id="te2071"/>
about his brother’s last moments, and the king he told it all over again on his hands to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4147"/>
duke, and both of them took on about that dead tanner like they’d lost the twelve disciples. Well, if ever I struck anything like it, I’m a nigger

          <app from="pr4147" n="210.7–9 (235.7–12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6057">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">duke, and . . . nigger</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">duke</rdg>
          </app>
. It was enough to make a body ashamed of the human race.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0376">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXV.</head>
        <pb n="211" xml:id="pb0211"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y21101">
          <graphic url="y21101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4148"/>
Chapter XXV.

            <app from="pr4148" n="211 title (235.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6058">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXV.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6059">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">The</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2111">
          <graphic url="hf2111.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">you bet it is.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e51825">
news was all over town in two minutes, and you could see the people tearing down on the run,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4149"/>
from

          <app from="pr4149" n="211.4 (236.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6060">
            <lem wit="A Cent">from</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in</rdg>
          </app>
every

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4150"/>
which way

          <app from="pr4150" n="211.4 (236.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6061">
            <lem wit="A Cent">which way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">direction</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0002"/>
some of them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4151"/>
putting on their coats

          <app from="pr4151" n="211.5 (236.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la6062">
            <lem wit="A Cent">putting on their coats</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">putting their coats on</rdg>
          </app>
as they come

          <ptr target="#as0213" type="an" xml:id="an0002"/>
. Pretty soon we was in the middle of a crowd, and the noise of the tramping was like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4152"/>
soldier-march

          <app from="pr4152" n="211.9 (236.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6063">
            <lem wit="A">soldier-march</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
soldier-

              <lb/>
march

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">soldier march</rdg>
          </app>
. The windows and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4153"/>
door-yards

          <app from="pr4153" n="211.10 (236.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6064">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">door-yards</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
door-

              <lb/>
yards

            </rdg>
          </app>
was full; and every minute somebody would say, over a fence:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51879">
“Is it

          <hi rend="italic">them?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51884">
And somebody trotting along with the gang would answer back and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4154"/>
say:

          <app from="pr4154" n="211.16 (236.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6065">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">say:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">say,</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51893">“You bet it is.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51895">
When we got to the house, the street in front of it was packed, and the three girls was standing in the door. Mary Jane

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4155"/>
red-headed

          <app from="pr4155" n="211.19–20 (237.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6066">
            <lem wit="A">red-headed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">read-headed;</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
red-

              <lb/>
headed

            </rdg>
          </app>
, but that don’t make no difference, she was most awful beautiful, and her face and her eyes was all lit up like glory, she was so glad her uncles was come. The king he spread his arms, and Mary Jane she jumped for them,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2072"/>
and the

          <ptr target="#l11784" type="alt" xml:id="te2072"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4156"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4156" n="211.23 (237.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6067">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
          </app>
jumped for the duke, and there they

          <hi rend="italic">had</hi>
it!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4157"/>
Everybody,

          <app from="pr4157" n="211.24 (237.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6068">
            <lem wit="MS2">Everybody,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
Everybody

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
most, leastways women, cried for joy to see them

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0066"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4158"/>
meet

          <app from="pr4158" n="✱211.25 (238.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6069">
            <lem wit="C">meet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A Cent">meet again</rdg>
          </app>
at last

          <ptr target="#tb0066" type="te" xml:id="tv0066"/>
and have such good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4159"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2073"/>
times.

          <ptr target="#l11785" type="alt" xml:id="te2073"/>
          <app from="pr4159" n="211.25 (238.3–11)" type="e" xml:id="la6070">
            <lem wit="A Cent">times.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">times. Soon as he could, the duke shook the hair-lip, and sampled Susan, which was better looking. After the king had kissed Mary Jane fourteen or fifteen times, he give the duke a show, and tapered off on the others.</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e51955">
Then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4160"/>
the king

          <app from="pr4160" n="211.26 (238.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6071">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the king</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6072">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he hunched the duke, private—I see him do it—and then he looked around and see the coffin, over in the corner on two chairs; so then, him and the duke, with a hand across each other’s shoulder, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4161"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr4161" n="211.29 (239.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6073">
            <lem wit="A Cent">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
hand to their eyes, walked slow and solemn over there, everybody dropping back to give them room, and all the talk and noise stopping, people saying

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2074"/>
“Sh!” and

          <ptr target="#l11786" type="alt" xml:id="te2074"/>
all the men taking their hats off and drooping their heads, so you could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4162"/>
a heard

          <app from="pr4162" n="211.32 (239.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6074">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a heard</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ heard</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="212" xml:id="pb0212"/>
a pin fall. And when they got there, they bent over and looked in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2075"/>
the coffin,

          <ptr target="#l11787" type="alt" xml:id="te2075"/>
and took one sight, and then they bust out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4163"/>
a crying

          <app from="pr4163" n="212.2 (239.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6075">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a crying</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-crying</rdg>
          </app>
so you could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4164"/>
a heard

          <app from="pr4164" n="212.3 (239.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6076">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a heard</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ heard</rdg>
          </app>
them to Orleans, most; and then they put their arms around each other’s necks, and hung their chins over each other’s shoulders; and then for three minutes, or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4165"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4165" n="212.5 (240.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6077">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
four, I never see two men leak the way they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4166"/>
done

          <app from="pr4166" n="212.6 (240.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6078">
            <lem wit="A Cent">done</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">did</rdg>
          </app>
. And mind you, everybody was doing the same; and the place was that damp I never see anything like it. Then one of them got on one side of the coffin, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4167"/>
t’other on t’other

          <app from="pr4167" n="212.8–9 (240.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6079">
            <lem wit="A Cent">t’other on t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’tother on ’tother</rdg>
          </app>
side, and they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4168"/>
kneeled

          <app from="pr4168" n="212.9 (240.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6080">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kneeled</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">knelt</rdg>
          </app>
down and rested their foreheads on the coffin, and let on to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4169"/>
pray,

          <app from="pr4169" n="212.10 (240.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6081">
            <lem wit="MS2">pray,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
pray

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4170"/>
their selves

          <app from="pr4170" n="212.10 (240.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6082">
            <lem wit="MS2">their selves</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">theirselves</rdg>
          </app>
. Well, when it come to that, it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4171"/>
worked the crowd like you never see anything like it, and so

          <app from="pr4171" n="212.11–12 (240.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6083">
            <lem wit="A Cent">worked . . . and so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was so moving that</rdg>
          </app>
everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4172"/>
broke down and

          <app from="pr4172" n="212.12 (240.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6084">
            <lem wit="A Cent">broke down and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6085">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
went to sobbing right out loud—the poor girls, too; and every woman, nearly, went up to the girls, without saying a word, and kissed them, solemn, on the forehead, and then put their hand on their head, and looked up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4173"/>
towards

          <app from="pr4173" n="212.16 (241.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6086">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">towards</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">toward</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4174"/>
sky

          <app from="pr4174" n="212.16 (241.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6087">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sky</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Throne</rdg>
          </app>
, with the tears running down, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2076"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l11788" type="alt" xml:id="te2076"/>
busted out and went off sobbing and swabbing, and give the next

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2077"/>
woman

          <ptr target="#l11789" type="alt" xml:id="te2077"/>
a show.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4175"/>
I never see anything so disgusting.

          <app from="pr4175" n="212.18 (241.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6088">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">I . . . disgusting.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6089">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y21201">
          <graphic url="y21201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">leaking</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52114">
Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4176"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr4176" n="212.19 (241.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6090">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
the king he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4177"/>
gets

          <app from="pr4177" n="212.19 (241.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6091">
            <lem wit="A Cent">gets</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">got</rdg>
          </app>
up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4178"/>
comes

          <app from="pr4178" n="212.19 (241.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6092">
            <lem wit="A Cent">comes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">come</rdg>
          </app>
forward a little,

          <pb n="213" xml:id="pb0213"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4179"/>
works himself up and slobbers out a speech, all full of tears and flapdoodle about its being a sore trial for him and his poor brother to lose the diseased, and to miss seeing diseased

          <app from="pr4179" n="213.1–3 (241.14–242.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6093">
            <lem wit="A Cent">works . . . seeing diseased</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says: [¶] “Friends—good friends of the diseased, and ourn to, I trust—it’s indeed a sore trial to lose him, and a sore trial to miss seeing of him</rdg>
          </app>
alive, after the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4180"/>
long

          <app from="pr4180" n="213.3 (242.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la6094">
            <lem wit="A Cent">long</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wearisome long</rdg>
          </app>
journey of four thousand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4181"/>
mile,

          <app from="pr4181" n="213.4 (242.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6095">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mile,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mile;</rdg>
          </app>
but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4182"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr4182" n="213.4 (242.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6096">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">its</rdg>
          </app>
a trial that’s sweetened and sanctified to us by this dear sympathy and these holy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4183"/>
tears,

          <app from="pr4183" n="213.5 (242.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6097">
            <lem wit="A">tears,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">tears;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4184"/>
and so he thanks them out of his heart and out of his brother’s heart, because out of their mouths they can’t, words being too weak and cold,

          <app from="pr4184" n="213.5–8 (242.6–9)" type="e" xml:id="la6098">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and so . . . weak and cold,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and so, out of our hearts we thank you, for out of our mouths we cannot, words being too weak and cold.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4185"/>
and all that kind of rot and slush, till it was just sickening; and then he blubbers out a pious goody-goody Amen, and turns himself loose and goes to crying fit to bust.

          <app from="pr4185" n="213.8–10 (242.10–17)" type="e" xml:id="la6099">
            <lem wit="A">and all that kind of rot and slush . . . bust.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">May you find sech friends and sech sympathy yourselves, when your own time of trial comes, and may the affliction be softened to you as ourn is to-day, by the soothing ba’m of earthly love and the healing of heavenly grace. Amen.”</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">and all that kind of slush . . . bust.</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52199">
And the minute the words was out of his mouth somebody

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2078"/>
over

          <ptr target="#l11790" type="alt" xml:id="te2078"/>
in the crowd struck up the doxolojer, and everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4186"/>
joined

          <app from="pr4186" n="213.12 (243.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6100">
            <lem wit="A Cent">joined</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jined</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4187"/>
in with all their might

