            <rdg wit="Cent">soul-butter</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0214" type="an" xml:id="an0003"/>
, I never see it freshen up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4189"/>
things

          <app from="pr4189" n="213.15 (243.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6103">
            <lem wit="A Cent">things</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the air</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4190"/>
so,

          <app from="pr4190" n="213.15 (243.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6104">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and sound so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4191"/>
honest and

          <app from="pr4191" n="213.16 (243.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6105">
            <lem wit="A Cent">honest and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6106">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2079"/>
bully.

          <ptr target="#l11791" type="alt" xml:id="te2079"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52266">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2080"/>
Then the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4192"/>
begins to work his jaw again, and says how him and his nieces

          <ptr target="#l11792" type="alt" xml:id="te2080"/>
          <app from="pr4192" n="213.17–18 (243.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la6107">
            <lem wit="A Cent">begins . . . his nieces</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says: [¶] “My brother and me, and our nieces,</rdg>
          </app>
would be glad if a few of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4193"/>
main principal

          <app from="pr4193" n="213.18 (243.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6108">
            <lem wit="A Cent">main principal</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nearest</rdg>
          </app>
friends of the family would take supper

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4194"/>
here

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2081"/>
with

          <ptr target="#l11793" type="alt" xml:id="te2081"/>
them

          <app from="pr4194" n="213.19 (243.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la6109">
            <lem wit="A Cent">here with them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">with us, here,</rdg>
          </app>
this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4195"/>
evening,

          <app from="pr4195" n="213.19 (243.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la6110">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">evening,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
evening

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4196"/>
help

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="an0004"/>
set

          <app from="pr4196" n="213.19–20 (243.18–19)" type="e" xml:id="la6111">
            <lem wit="A Cent">help set</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">assist in setting</rdg>
          </app>
up with the ashes of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4197"/>
diseased

          <ptr target="#as0215" type="an" xml:id="pt0004"/>
; and says if

          <app from="pr4197" n="213.20 (244.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6112">
            <lem wit="A Cent">diseased; and says if</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">diseased. If</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4198"/>
his

          <app from="pr4198" n="213.20 (244.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6113">
            <lem wit="A Cent">his</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">my</rdg>
          </app>
poor brother laying yonder could speak,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4199"/>
he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2082"/>
knows

          <ptr target="#l11794" type="alt" xml:id="te2082"/>
          <app from="pr4199" n="213.21 (244.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la6114">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he knows</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I know</rdg>
          </app>
who he would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4200"/>
name,

          <app from="pr4200" n="213.21 (244.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6115">
            <lem wit="A Cent">name,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">name;</rdg>
          </app>
for they was names that was very dear to him, and mentioned often in his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4201"/>
letters; and so

          <app from="pr4201" n="213.23 (244.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6116">
            <lem wit="A Cent">letters; and so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">letters. So</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4202"/>
he

          <app from="pr4202" n="213.23 (244.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6117">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I</rdg>
          </app>
will name the same,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4203"/>
to-wit

          <app from="pr4203" n="213.23 (244.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6118">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">to-wit</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">to wit</rdg>
          </app>
, as follows,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4204"/>
vizz:

          <app from="pr4204" n="213.23 (244.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6119">
            <lem wit="C">vizz:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">vizz:</hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">vizz:—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">vizz.:</rdg>
          </app>
Rev. Mr. Hobson, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4205"/>
deacon

          <app from="pr4205" n="213.24 (244.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6120">
            <lem wit="MS2">deacon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Deacon</rdg>
          </app>
Lot Hovey,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2083"/>
and Mr.

          <ptr target="#l11795" type="alt" xml:id="te2083"/>
Ben Rucker, and Abner Shackleford, and Levi Bell, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4206"/>
Dr.

          <app from="pr4206" n="213.25 (244.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6121">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Dr.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Dr

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Robinson, and their wives, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4207"/>
widow Bartley.

          <app from="pr4207" n="213.26 (244.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6122">
            <lem wit="A Cent">widow Bartley.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
wid’r Bartley.’

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6123">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52423">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2084"/>
Rev.

          <ptr target="#l11796" type="alt" xml:id="te2084"/>
Hobson and Dr. Robinson was down to the end of the town,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4208"/>
a-hunting

          <app from="pr4208" n="213.28 (244.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6124">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a-hunting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hunting</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2085"/>
together;

          <ptr target="#l11797" type="alt" xml:id="te2085"/>
that is, I mean the doctor was shipping a sick man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4209"/>
to t’other

          <app from="pr4209" n="213.29 (244.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6125">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">out of the</rdg>
          </app>
world, and the preacher was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4210"/>
pinting

          <app from="pr4210" n="213.29 (244.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la6126">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">pinting</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">p’inting</rdg>
          </app>
him right. Lawyer Bell was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2086"/>
away

          <ptr target="#l11798" type="alt" xml:id="te2086"/>
up to Louisville on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4211"/>
some

          <app from="pr4211" n="213.30 (245.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6127">
            <lem wit="A Cent">some</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6128">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
business. But the rest was on hand, and so they all come and shook hands with the king and thanked him and talked to him; and then they shook hands with the duke, and didn’t say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4212"/>
nothing,

          <app from="pr4212" n="213.33 (245.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6129">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">nothing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
nothing

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
but just kept a-smiling and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4213"/>
bobbing

          <app from="pr4213" n="213.34 (245.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6130">
            <lem wit="A Cent">bobbing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nodding</rdg>
          </app>
their heads like a passel of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2087"/>
sapheads

          <ptr target="#l11799" type="alt" xml:id="te2087"/>
whilst he made all sorts of signs with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4214"/>
hands

          <app from="pr4214" n="213.35 (245.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6131">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">hands</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hands,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4215"/>
said

          <app from="pr4215" n="213.35 (245.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6132">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">said,</rdg>
          </app>
“Goo-goo—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2088"/>
goo-goo-goo

          <ptr target="#l11800" type="alt" xml:id="te2088"/>
,” all the time, like a baby that can’t talk.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52512">
So the king he blatted along, and managed to inquire about pretty much everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4216"/>
and dog

          <app from="pr4216" n="213.38 (245.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6133">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and dog</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6134">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4217"/>
town,

          <app from="pr4217" n="213.38 (245.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6135">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">town,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
town

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
by

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4218"/>
his

          <app from="pr4218" n="213.38 (245.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6136">
            <lem wit="A Cent">his</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6137">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
name, and mentioned all

          <pb n="214" xml:id="pb0214"/>
sorts of little things that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4219"/>
happened

          <app from="pr4219" n="214.1 (246.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6138">
            <lem wit="A Cent">happened</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">had happened</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4220"/>
one time or another

          <app from="pr4220" n="214.1 (246.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6139">
            <lem wit="A Cent">one time or another</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6140">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the town, or to George’s family, or

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2089"/>
to Peter

          <ptr target="#l11801" type="alt" xml:id="te2089"/>
; and he always let on that Peter wrote him the things, but that was a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4221"/>
lie, he

          <app from="pr4221" n="214.3 (246.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6141">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">lie, he</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">lie. He</rdg>
          </app>
got every blessed one of them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4222"/>
out of

          <app from="pr4222" n="214.4 (246.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6142">
            <lem wit="A Cent">out of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">from</rdg>
          </app>
that young flathead that we canoed up to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4223"/>
steamboat

          <app from="pr4223" n="214.4 (246.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la6143">
            <lem wit="A Cent">steamboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
steam-

              <lb/>
boat

            </rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52589">
Then Mary Jane she fetched the letter her

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0067"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4224"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr4224" n="✱214.5 (246.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6144">
            <lem wit="C">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A Cent">father</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0067" type="te" xml:id="tv0067"/>
left behind, and the king he read it out loud and cried over it. It give the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4225"/>
dwelling

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2090"/>
house

          <app from="pr4225" n="214.6–7 (246.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6145">
            <lem wit="MS2">dwelling house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">dwelling-house</rdg>
          </app>
and three thousand dollars, gold, to the girls; and it give the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4226"/>
tanyard

          <ptr target="#l11802" type="alt" xml:id="te2090"/>
,

          <app from="pr4226" n="214.8 (246.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6146">
            <lem wit="MS2">tanyard,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tanyard</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">tan-yard</rdg>
          </app>
(which was doing a good

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2091"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4227"/>
business,)

          <app from="pr4227" n="214.8 (246.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6147">
            <lem wit="MS2">business,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">business),</rdg>
          </app>
along with some other

          <ptr target="#l11803" type="alt" xml:id="te2091"/>
houses and land (worth

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2092"/>
about seven

          <ptr target="#l11804" type="alt" xml:id="te2092"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4228"/>
thousand,)

          <app from="pr4228" n="214.9 (246.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la6148">
            <lem wit="MS2">thousand,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">thousand),</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
thousand

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
)

            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2093"/>
three thousand

          <ptr target="#l11805" type="alt" xml:id="te2093"/>
dollars in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4229"/>
gold,

          <app from="pr4229" n="214.10 (247.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6149">
            <lem wit="MS2">gold,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
gold

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to Harvey and William, and told where the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2094"/>
six thousand cash

          <ptr target="#l11806" type="alt" xml:id="te2094"/>
was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4230"/>
hid,

          <app from="pr4230" n="214.11 (247.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6150">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">hid,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
hid

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
down cellar. So these two frauds said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4231"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr4231" n="214.11 (247.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6151">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they would</rdg>
          </app>
go and fetch it up, and have everything square and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4232"/>
aboveboard;

          <app from="pr4232" n="214.12 (247.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6152">
            <lem wit="MS2">aboveboard;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">above-board</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
above-

              <lb/>
board,

            </rdg>
          </app>
and told me to come with a candle. We shut the cellar door

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4233"/>
behind

          <app from="pr4233" n="214.13 (247.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6153">
            <lem wit="A Cent">behind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">after</rdg>
          </app>
us, and when they found the bag they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4234"/>
spilt

          <app from="pr4234" n="214.14 (247.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6154">
            <lem wit="A Cent">spilt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">emptied</rdg>
          </app>
it out on the floor, and it was a lovely sight, all them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4235"/>
yaller-boys

          <app from="pr4235" n="214.15 (247.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6155">
            <lem wit="Cent">yaller-boys</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yellow-boys</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
yaller-

              <lb/>
boys

            </rdg>
          </app>
. My, the way the king’s eyes did shine! He slaps the duke on the shoulder, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52724">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4236"/>
“O

          <app from="pr4236" n="214.17 (247.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6156">
            <lem wit="MS2">“O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">“Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4237"/>
bully

          <app from="pr4237" n="214.17 (247.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6157">
            <lem wit="MS2">bully</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">bully,</rdg>
          </app>
nor noth’n!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4238"/>
O,

          <app from="pr4238" n="214.17 (247.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6158">
            <lem wit="MS2">O,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh,</rdg>
          </app>
no, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4239"/>
reckon

          <app from="pr4239" n="214.17 (247.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6159">
            <lem wit="A Cent">reckon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckin</rdg>
          </app>
not! Why, Biljy, it beats the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4240"/>
Nonesuch—

          <app from="pr4240" n="214.18 (247.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6160">
            <lem wit="C">Nonesuch—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burnin’ Shame—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Nonesuch,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
None-

              <lb/>
such,

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
it!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52777">
The duke allowed it did. They pawed the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4241"/>
yaller-boys

          <app from="pr4241" n="214.19 (248.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6161">
            <lem wit="A Cent">yaller-boys</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yellow-boys</rdg>
          </app>
, and sifted them through their fingers and let them jingle

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4242"/>
down

          <app from="pr4242" n="214.20 (248.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6162">
            <lem wit="A Cent">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6163">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
on the floor; and the king says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52796">
“It ain’t no use

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4243"/>
talkin’:

          <app from="pr4243" n="214.22 (248.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6164">
            <lem wit="MS2">talkin’:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">talkin’;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2095"/>
bein’

          <ptr target="#l11807" type="alt" xml:id="te2095"/>
brothers to a rich dead man, and representatives of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4244"/>
furrin

          <app from="pr4244" n="214.23 (248.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6165">
            <lem wit="A Cent">furrin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">foreign</rdg>
          </app>
heirs that’s got left, is the line for you and me, Bilge.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4245"/>
Thish-yer comes of trust’n to Providence. It’s the best way, in the long run. I’ve tried ’em all, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4246"/>
ther’

          <app from="pr4246" n="214.25 (248.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6168">
            <lem wit="A">ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">there</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no better way.

          <app from="pr4245" n="214.24–25 (248.11–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6166">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Thish-yer . . . way.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6167">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52835">
Most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4247"/>
everybody

          <app from="pr4247" n="214.26 (248.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6169">
            <lem wit="A Cent">everybody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4248"/>
a been

          <app from="pr4248" n="214.26 (248.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6170">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a been</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ been</rdg>
          </app>
satisfied with the pile, and took it on trust; but no, they must count it. So they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4249"/>
counts

          <app from="pr4249" n="214.27 (248.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6171">
            <lem wit="A Cent">counts</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">counted</rdg>
          </app>
it, and it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4250"/>
comes

          <app from="pr4250" n="214.27 (248.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6172">
            <lem wit="A Cent">comes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">come</rdg>
          </app>
out four hundred and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2096"/>
fifteen

          <ptr target="#l11808" type="alt" xml:id="te2096"/>
dollars short. Says the king:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52874">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4251"/>
Dern him,

          <app from="pr4251" n="214.29 (249.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6173">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Dern him,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Dern him!</rdg>
          </app>
I wonder what he done with that four

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4252"/>
hunderd

          <app from="pr4252" n="214.29 (249.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6174">
            <lem wit="A">hunderd</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">hundred</rdg>
          </app>
and fifteen dollars?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52892">
They worried over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4253"/>
that,

          <app from="pr4253" n="214.31 (249.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6175">
            <lem wit="MS2">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4254"/>
a while

          <app from="pr4254" n="214.31 (249.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6176">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
, and ransacked all around for it. Then the duke says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52910">“Well, he was a pretty sick man, and likely he made a mistake—I reckon that’s the way of it. The best way’s to let it go, and keep still about it. We can spare it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52912">
“Oh, shucks, yes, we can

          <hi rend="italic">spare</hi>
it. I don’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4255"/>
k’yer noth’n ’bout

          <app from="pr4255" n="214.36 (249.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6177">
            <lem wit="A Cent">k’yer noth’n ’bout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">care nothing about</rdg>
          </app>
that—it’s the

          <hi rend="italic">count</hi>
I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4256"/>
thinkin’

          <app from="pr4256" n="214.37 (249.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6178">
            <lem wit="A">thinkin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a thinking</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">thinking</rdg>
          </app>
about. We want to be awful square and open and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4257"/>
aboveboard

          <app from="pr4257" n="214.38 (250.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6179">
            <lem wit="MS2">aboveboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
above-

              <lb/>
board

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">above-board</rdg>
          </app>
, here, you know. We want to lug

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4258"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0068"/>
thish-yer

          <ptr target="#tb0068" type="te" xml:id="tv0068"/>
          <app from="pr4258" n="✱214.38 (250.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6180">
            <lem wit="C">thish-yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">this</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">this h-yer</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="215" xml:id="pb0215"/>
money up stairs and count it before everybody—then

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4259"/>
ther’

          <app from="pr4259" n="215.1 (250.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6181">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">there</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4260"/>
noth’n

          <app from="pr4260" n="215.2 (250.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6182">
            <lem wit="A Cent">noth’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nothing</rdg>
          </app>
suspicious. But when the dead man says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4261"/>
ther’s six thous’n

          <app from="pr4261" n="215.2 (250.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6183">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ther’s six thous’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">there’s four thousand and thirty</rdg>
          </app>
dollars, you know, we don’t want

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4262"/>
to—

          <app from="pr4262" n="215.3 (250.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6184">
            <lem wit="MS2">to—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">to——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e52997">
“Hold on,” says the duke. “Less make up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4263"/>
deffisit

          <app from="pr4263" n="215.4 (250.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6185">
            <lem wit="A Cent">deffisit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">deffersit</rdg>
          </app>
”—and he begun to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2097"/>
haul

          <ptr target="#l11809" type="alt" xml:id="te2097"/>
out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4264"/>
yaller-boys

          <app from="pr4264" n="215.5 (250.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la6186">
            <lem wit="Cent">yaller-boys</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
yellow-

              <lb/>
boys

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
yaller-

              <lb/>
boys

            </rdg>
          </app>
out of his pocket.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y21501">
          <graphic url="y21501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">making up the “deffisit.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53031">
“It’s a most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4265"/>
amaz’n’

          <app from="pr4265" n="215.6 (250.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6187">
            <lem wit="A Cent">amaz’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">amazin</rdg>
          </app>
good idea, duke—you

          <hi rend="italic">have</hi>
got a rattlin’ clever head on you,” says the king. “Blest if the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4266"/>
Nonesuch

          <app from="pr4266" n="215.7 (251.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6188">
            <lem wit="C">Nonesuch—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Nonesuch,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burnin’ Shame—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
None-

              <lb/>
such,

            </rdg>
          </app>
ain’t a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4267"/>
heppin’

          <app from="pr4267" n="215.8 (251.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6189">
            <lem wit="A">heppin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">helpin’</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">heppen’</rdg>
          </app>
us out agin”—and

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
begun to haul out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4268"/>
yaller-jackets

          <app from="pr4268" n="215.8 (251.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6190">
            <lem wit="Cent">yaller-jackets</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yellow-jackets</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
yaller-

              <lb/>
jackets

            </rdg>
          </app>
and stack them up.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53084">
It most busted them, but they made up the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2098"/>
six

          <ptr target="#l11810" type="alt" xml:id="te2098"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2099"/>
thousand

          <ptr target="#l11811" type="alt" xml:id="te2099"/>
clean and clear.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53093">
“Say,” says the duke, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4269"/>
I

          <app from="pr4269" n="215.12 (251.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6191">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’ve</rdg>
          </app>
got another idea.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4270"/>
Le’s

          <app from="pr4270" n="215.12 (251.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6192">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">“Less</rdg>
          </app>
go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4271"/>
up stairs

          <app from="pr4271" n="215.12 (251.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6193">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">up stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">upstairs</rdg>
          </app>
and count this money, and then take and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2100"/>
          <hi rend="italic">give it to the girls</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11812" type="alt" xml:id="te2100"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53126">
“Good land, duke, lemme hug you! It’s the most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4272"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2101"/>
dazzling

          <ptr target="#l11813" type="alt" xml:id="te2101"/>
          <app from="pr4272" n="215.14 (251.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6194">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dazzling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gorjis</rdg>
          </app>
idea ’at ever a man struck. You have cert’nly got the most astonishin’ head I ever see.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4273"/>
O

          <app from="pr4273" n="215.16 (251.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6195">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, this is the boss

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4274"/>
dodge

          <app from="pr4274" n="215.16 (252.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6196">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dodge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">trick</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4275"/>
ther’

          <app from="pr4275" n="215.16 (252.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6197">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">there</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no mistake

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4276"/>
’bout

          <app from="pr4276" n="215.16 (252.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6198">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’bout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">about</rdg>
          </app>
it.

          <pb n="216" xml:id="pb0216"/>
Let ’em fetch along their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4277"/>
suspicions,

          <app from="pr4277" n="216.1 (252.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6199">
            <lem wit="MS2">suspicions,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
suspicions

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, if they want to—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4278"/>
this ’ll

          <app from="pr4278" n="216.1 (252.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6200">
            <lem wit="MS2">this ’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">this’ll</rdg>
          </app>
lay ’em out.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53188">
When

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2102"/>
we

          <ptr target="#l11814" type="alt" xml:id="te2102"/>
got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4279"/>
up stairs

          <app from="pr4279" n="216.3 (252.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6201">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">up stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">upstairs</rdg>
          </app>
, everybody gethered around the table, and the king he counted it and stacked it up, three hundred dollars in a pile—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2103"/>
twenty

          <ptr target="#l11815" type="alt" xml:id="te2103"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4280"/>
elegant

          <app from="pr4280" n="216.5 (252.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6202">
            <lem wit="A Cent">elegant</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">beautiful</rdg>
          </app>
little piles. Everybody looked hungry at it, and licked their chops. Then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2104"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4281"/>
they

          <app from="pr4281" n="216.6 (252.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6203">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’twas</rdg>
          </app>
raked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4282"/>
it

          <app from="pr4282" n="216.6 (252.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6204">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6205">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
into the bag again, and

          <ptr target="#l11816" type="alt" xml:id="te2104"/>
I see the king begin to swell himself up for another speech. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53235">
“Friends all, my poor brother that lays

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4283"/>
yonder,

          <app from="pr4283" n="216.8 (252.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6206">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">yonder,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
yonder

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
has done generous by them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2105"/>
that’s

          <ptr target="#l11817" type="alt" xml:id="te2105"/>
left behind in the vale of sorrers. He has

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2106"/>
done

          <ptr target="#l11818" type="alt" xml:id="te2106"/>
generous by

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4284"/>
these-yer

          <app from="pr4284" n="216.10 (253.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6207">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">these-yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">these yer</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2107"/>
poor

          <ptr target="#l11819" type="alt" xml:id="te2107"/>
little lambs that he loved and sheltered, and that’s left fatherless and motherless. Yes, and we that knowed him, knows that he would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4285"/>
a done

          <app from="pr4285" n="216.12 (253.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6208">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a done</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ done</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">more</hi>
generous by ’em

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4286"/>
if

          <app from="pr4286" n="216.12 (253.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6209">
            <lem wit="A Cent">if</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ef</rdg>
          </app>
he hadn’t ben afeard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4287"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4287" n="216.13 (253.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6210">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2108"/>
woundin’

          <ptr target="#l11820" type="alt" xml:id="te2108"/>
his dear William and me. Now,

          <hi rend="italic">wouldn’t</hi>
he?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4288"/>
Ther’

          <app from="pr4288" n="216.14 (253.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6211">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">There</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no question

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4289"/>
’bout

          <app from="pr4289" n="216.14 (253.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6212">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’bout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">about</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4290"/>
it,

          <app from="pr4290" n="216.14 (253.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6213">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in

          <hi rend="italic">my</hi>
mind. Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4291"/>
then—

          <app from="pr4291" n="216.14 (253.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6214">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">then—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">then,</rdg>
          </app>
what kind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4292"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4292" n="216.15 (253.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6215">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
brothers would it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4293"/>
be,

          <app from="pr4293" n="216.15 (253.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6216">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">be,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
be

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4294"/>
that ’d

          <app from="pr4294" n="216.15 (253.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6217">
            <lem wit="A">that ’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that would</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">that’d</rdg>
          </app>
stand in his way at sech a time? And what kind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4295"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4295" n="216.16 (253.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6218">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
uncles would it be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4296"/>
that ’d

          <app from="pr4296" n="216.16 (253.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6219">
            <lem wit="A">that ’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that would</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">that’d</rdg>
          </app>
rob—yes,

          <hi rend="italic">rob</hi>
—sech poor sweet lambs as these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4297"/>
’at

          <app from="pr4297" n="216.17 (254.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6220">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’at</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6221">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he loved so, at sech a time?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4298"/>
If

          <app from="pr4298" n="216.17 (254.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6222">
            <lem wit="A Cent">If</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Ef</rdg>
          </app>
I know William—and I

          <hi rend="italic">think</hi>
I do—he—well, I’ll jest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4299"/>
ask

          <app from="pr4299" n="216.18 (254.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6223">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ask</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">ask</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
him.” He turns around and begins to make a lot of signs to the duke with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4300"/>
hands; and

          <app from="pr4300" n="216.19–20 (254.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6224">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hands; and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hands;</rdg>
          </app>
the duke he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4301"/>
looks

          <app from="pr4301" n="216.20 (254.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6225">
            <lem wit="A Cent">looks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">looked</rdg>
          </app>
at him stupid and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4302"/>
leatherheaded

          <app from="pr4302" n="216.20 (254.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6226">
            <lem wit="MS2">leatherheaded</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">leather-headed</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4303"/>
a while

          <app from="pr4303" n="216.20 (254.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6227">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
, then all of a sudden he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4304"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2109"/>
seems

          <ptr target="#l11821" type="alt" xml:id="te2109"/>
          <app from="pr4304" n="216.21 (254.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6228">
            <lem wit="A Cent">seems</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">seem</rdg>
          </app>
to catch his meaning, and jumps for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4305"/>
king

          <app from="pr4305" n="216.22 (254.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6229">
            <lem wit="MS2">king</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">king,</rdg>
          </app>
goo-gooing with all his might for joy, and hugs

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2110"/>
him

          <ptr target="#l11822" type="alt" xml:id="te2110"/>
about fifteen times before he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4306"/>
lets

          <app from="pr4306" n="216.23 (254.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6230">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lets</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">let</rdg>
          </app>
up. Then the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4307"/>
says,

          <app from="pr4307" n="216.23 (254.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6231">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
“I knowed it; I reckon

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2111"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4308"/>
          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11823" type="alt" xml:id="te2111"/>
’ll

          <app from="pr4308" n="216.24 (254.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6232">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
’ll

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
’ll

            </rdg>
          </app>
convince anybody the way

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
feels about it. Here, Mary Jane, Susan, Joanner, take the money—take it

          <hi rend="italic">all.</hi>
It’s the gift of him that lays yonder, cold but joyful.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53507">
Mary Jane she went for him, Susan and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4309"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4309" n="216.27 (255.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6233">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
          </app>
went for the duke, and then such another hugging and kissing I never see yet. And everybody crowded

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tq2112"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4310"/>
up,

          <app from="pr4310" n="216.29 (255.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6234">
            <lem wit="MS2">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with the tears in their eyes, and

          <ptr target="#l11824" type="alt" xml:id="te2112"/>
most shook the hands off of them frauds, saying all the time:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53529">
“You

          <hi rend="italic">dear</hi>
good souls!—how

          <hi rend="italic">lovely!</hi>
—how

          <hi rend="italic">could</hi>
you!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53540">
Well, then,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2113"/>
pretty soon

          <ptr target="#l11825" type="alt" xml:id="te2113"/>
all hands got to talking about the diseased again, and how good he was, and what a loss he was, and all that; and before long a big iron-jawed man worked himself in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4311"/>
there from

          <app from="pr4311" n="216.34 (256.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6235">
            <lem wit="A Cent">there from</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">from the</rdg>
          </app>
outside, and stood

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4312"/>
a-listening

          <app from="pr4312" n="216.35 (256.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6236">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">a-listening</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a listening</rdg>
          </app>
and looking, and not saying anything; and nobody saying anything to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4313"/>
him,

          <app from="pr4313" n="216.36 (256.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6237">
            <lem wit="MS2">him,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
him

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
either, because

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2114"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l11826" type="alt" xml:id="te2114"/>
king was talking and they was all busy listening. The king was saying—in the middle of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4314"/>
something he’d started in on—

          <app from="pr4314" n="216.38 (256.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6238">
            <lem wit="A">something . . . on—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a sentence:</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">something . . . on:</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53585">
          <pb n="217" xml:id="pb0217"/>
“—they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4315"/>
bein’

          <app from="pr4315" n="217.1 (256.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6239">
            <lem wit="A Cent">bein’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">being</rdg>
          </app>
partickler friends

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4316"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4316" n="217.1 (256.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6240">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2115"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l11827" type="alt" xml:id="te2115"/>
diseased. That’s why they’re invited here this evenin’; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4317"/>
to-morrow

          <app from="pr4317" n="217.2 (256.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6241">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to-morrow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to-morrer</rdg>
          </app>
we want

          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
to come—everybody; for he respected everybody, he liked everybody, and so it’s fitten that his funeral

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4318"/>
orgies sh’d

          <app from="pr4318" n="217.4 (256.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6242">
            <lem wit="Cent">orgies sh’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">orgies should</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">orgies h’d</rdg>
          </app>
be public.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y21701">
          <graphic url="y21701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">going for him</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53633">
And

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2116"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l11828" type="alt" xml:id="te2116"/>
he went a-mooning on and on, liking to hear himself talk, and every little while he fetched in his funeral orgies again, till the duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4319"/>
he couldn’t

          <app from="pr4319" n="217.7 (257.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6243">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">couldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
stand it no more; so he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4320"/>
writes

          <app from="pr4320" n="217.7 (257.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6244">
            <lem wit="A Cent">writes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wrote</rdg>
          </app>
on a little scrap of paper, “

          <hi rend="italic">obsequies</hi>
, you old fool,” and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2117"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4321"/>
folds

          <app from="pr4321" n="217.8 (257.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6245">
            <lem wit="A Cent">folds</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">folded</rdg>
          </app>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4322"/>
up

          <app from="pr4322" n="217.8 (257.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6246">
            <lem wit="A Cent">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6247">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <ptr target="#l11829" type="alt" xml:id="te2117"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4323"/>
goes

          <app from="pr4323" n="217.8 (257.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6248">
            <lem wit="A Cent">goes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">went</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2118"/>
goo-gooing

          <ptr target="#l11830" type="alt" xml:id="te2118"/>
and reaching it over people’s heads to him. The king he reads it, and puts it in his pocket, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53691">
“Poor William,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2119"/>
afflicted as he is,

          <ptr target="#l11831" type="alt" xml:id="te2119"/>
his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2120"/>
          <hi rend="italic">heart’s</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11832" type="alt" xml:id="te2120"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4324"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2121"/>
aluz

          <ptr target="#l11833" type="alt" xml:id="te2121"/>
          <app from="pr4324" n="217.11 (257.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6249">
            <lem wit="A Cent">aluz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">always</rdg>
          </app>
right. Asks me to invite everybody to come to the funeral—wants me to make ’em all welcome. But he needn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4325"/>
a worried

          <app from="pr4325" n="217.13 (258.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6250">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a worried</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ worried</rdg>
          </app>
—it was jest what I was at.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53720">
Then he weaves

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4326"/>
along,

          <app from="pr4326" n="217.14 (258.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6251">
            <lem wit="MS2">along,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
along

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
again, perfectly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4327"/>
ca’m

          <app from="pr4327" n="217.14 (258.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6252">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ca’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">c’am</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4328"/>
goes to

          <app from="pr4328" n="217.14 (258.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6253">
            <lem wit="A Cent">goes to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6254">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
dropping in his funeral orgies again every now and then, just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4329"/>
like

          <app from="pr4329" n="217.15 (258.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6255">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">as</rdg>
          </app>
he done

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2122"/>
before.

          <ptr target="#l11834" type="alt" xml:id="te2122"/>
And when he done it the third time, he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53760">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4330"/>
say

          <app from="pr4330" n="217.17 (258.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6256">
            <lem wit="A Cent">say</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">use the word</rdg>
          </app>
orgies, not because it’s the common term, because it ain’t—

          <pb n="218" xml:id="pb0218"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2123"/>
obsequies

          <ptr target="#l11835" type="alt" xml:id="te2123"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2124"/>
bein’

          <ptr target="#l11836" type="alt" xml:id="te2124"/>
the common term—but because

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2125"/>
orgies is

          <ptr target="#l11837" type="alt" xml:id="te2125"/>
the right term. Obsequies ain’t used in England no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4331"/>
more,

          <app from="pr4331" n="218.2 (258.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6257">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">more,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
more

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now—it’s gone out. We say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4332"/>
orgies, now,

          <app from="pr4332" n="218.3 (259.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6258">
            <lem wit="MS2">orgies, now,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
orgies

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
now,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
orgies

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
now

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in England. Orgies is better, because it means the thing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4333"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr4333" n="218.4 (259.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6259">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you are</rdg>
          </app>
after, more exact. It’s

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="an0005"/>
a word that’s made up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4334"/>
out’n

          <app from="pr4334" n="218.4 (259.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6260">
            <lem wit="A Cent">out’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">out of</rdg>
          </app>
the Greek

          <hi rend="italic">orgo</hi>
, outside, open, abroad; and the Hebrew

          <hi rend="italic">jeesum</hi>
          <ptr target="#as0216" type="an" xml:id="pt0005"/>
, to plant, cover up; hence

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4335"/>
in

          <hi rend="italic">ter</hi>
          <app from="pr4335" n="218.6 (259.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6261">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
in

              <hi rend="italic">ter</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">inter</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. So,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4336"/>
you

          <app from="pr4336" n="218.6 (259.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6262">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">as you</rdg>
          </app>
see, funeral orgies is an open

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4337"/>
er

          <app from="pr4337" n="218.6 (259.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6263">
            <lem wit="A Cent">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or</rdg>
          </app>
public funeral.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53857">
He was the

          <hi rend="italic">worst</hi>
I ever struck.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4338"/>
Well,

          <app from="pr4338" n="218.8 (259.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6264">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Well,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Well, sir,</rdg>
          </app>
the iron-jawed man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4339"/>
he

          <app from="pr4339" n="218.8 (259.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6265">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6266">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
laughed right in his face. Everybody was shocked. Everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4340"/>
says

          <app from="pr4340" n="218.11 (259.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6267">
            <lem wit="A Cent">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4341"/>
Why

          <app from="pr4341" n="218.11 (259.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6268">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">doctor!</hi>
” and Abner Shackleford says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53898">
“Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4342"/>
Robinson,

          <app from="pr4342" n="218.13 (259.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6269">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Robinson,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Robinson

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
hain’t you heard the news? This is Harvey Wilks.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53908">
The king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4343"/>
he

          <app from="pr4343" n="218.16 (260.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6270">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6271">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4344"/>
smiled,

          <app from="pr4344" n="218.16 (260.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6272">
            <lem wit="MS2">smiled,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
smiled

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2126"/>
eager,

          <ptr target="#l11838" type="alt" xml:id="te2126"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2127"/>
shoved

          <ptr target="#l11839" type="alt" xml:id="te2127"/>
out his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2128"/>
flapper,

          <ptr target="#l11840" type="alt" xml:id="te2128"/>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53939">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Is</hi>
it my poor brother’s dear good friend and physician?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4345"/>
I—

          <app from="pr4345" n="218.20 (260.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6273">
            <lem wit="MS2">I—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">I——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e53952">
“Keep your hands off of me!” says the doctor. “

          <hi rend="italic">You</hi>
talk like an Englishman—

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
you? It’s the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4346"/>
worst

          <app from="pr4346" n="218.24 (260.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6274">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">worst</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">worse</rdg>
          </app>
imitation I ever heard.

          <hi rend="italic">You</hi>
Peter Wilks’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4347"/>
brother.

          <app from="pr4347" n="218.25 (260.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6275">
            <lem wit="A">brother.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">brother!</rdg>
          </app>
You’re a fraud, that’s what you are!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="left" xml:id="y21801">
          <graphic url="y21801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4348"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the doctor.</hi>
            <app from="pr4348" n="218 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la6276">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">the doctor</hi>
.

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6277">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">
                  <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
talk like an englishman

                </hi>
!”

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54000">
Well, how they all took on! They crowded around the doctor, and tried to quiet him down, and tried to explain to him, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4349"/>
tell him

          <app from="pr4349" n="218.30 (260.17–261.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6278">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">tell him</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">tell</rdg>
          </app>
how Harvey’d showed in forty ways that he

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
Harvey, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2129"/>
knowed

          <ptr target="#l11841" type="alt" xml:id="te2129"/>
everybody

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2130"/>
by

          <ptr target="#l11842" type="alt" xml:id="te2130"/>
name, and the names of the very dogs, and begged and

          <hi rend="italic">begged</hi>
him not to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2131"/>
hurt

          <ptr target="#l11843" type="alt" xml:id="te2131"/>
Harvey’s feelings and the poor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4350"/>
girls’

          <app from="pr4350" n="218.33 (261.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6279">
            <lem wit="A Cent">girls’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">girls’s</rdg>
          </app>
feelings, and all that; but it warn’t no use, he stormed right along, and said any man that pretended to be an Englishman and couldn’t imitate the lingo no better than what he did, was a fraud and a liar. The poor girls was hanging to the king and crying; and all of a sudden the doctor ups and turns on

          <hi rend="italic">them.</hi>
He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54041">
          <pb n="219" xml:id="pb0219"/>
“I was your father’s friend, and I’m your friend; and I warn you

          <hi rend="italic">as</hi>
a friend, and an honest one, that wants to protect you and keep you out of harm and trouble, to turn your backs on that scoundrel, and have nothing to do with him, the ignorant

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4351"/>
tramp

          <app from="pr4351" n="219.4 (262.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6280">
            <lem wit="A Cent">tramp</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hog</rdg>
          </app>
, with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4352"/>
idiotic

          <app from="pr4352" n="219.4 (262.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6281">
            <lem wit="A Cent">idiotic</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">putrid and idiotic</rdg>
          </app>
Greek and Hebrew as he calls it. He is the thinnest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4353"/>
kind of an imposter

          <app from="pr4353" n="219.5–6 (262.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6282">
            <lem wit="C">kind of an imposter</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of thin imposters</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">kind of an impostor</rdg>
          </app>
—has come here with a lot of empty names and facts which he has picked up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4354"/>
somewheres

          <app from="pr4354" n="219.7 (262.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6283">
            <lem wit="A Cent">somewheres</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">somewhere</rdg>
          </app>
, and you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4355"/>
take

          <app from="pr4355" n="219.7 (262.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6284">
            <lem wit="A Cent">take</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">weakly take</rdg>
          </app>
them for

          <hi rend="italic">proofs</hi>
, and are

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4356"/>
helped to fool

          <app from="pr4356" n="219.8 (262.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la6285">
            <lem wit="A Cent">helped to fool</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">assisted in deceiving</rdg>
          </app>
yourselves by these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4357"/>
foolish

          <app from="pr4357" n="219.8 (263.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6286">
            <lem wit="A Cent">foolish</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thoughtless unreasoning</rdg>
          </app>
friends here, who ought to know better. Mary Jane Wilks, you know me for your friend, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4358"/>
for

          <app from="pr4358" n="219.10 (263.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6287">
            <lem wit="A Cent">for</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6288">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4359"/>
unselfish

          <app from="pr4359" n="219.10 (263.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la6289">
            <lem wit="A Cent">unselfish</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">honest and unselfish</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4360"/>
friend, too

          <app from="pr4360" n="219.10 (263.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6290">
            <lem wit="A Cent">friend, too</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">friend</rdg>
          </app>
. Now listen to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4361"/>
me:

          <app from="pr4361" n="219.10 (263.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6291">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">me:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">me;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4362"/>
turn this pitiful rascal

          <app from="pr4362" n="219.10–11 (263.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6292">
            <lem wit="A Cent">turn this pitiful rascal</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cast this paltry villain</rdg>
          </app>
out—I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4363"/>
          <hi rend="italic">beg</hi>
          <app from="pr4363" n="219.11 (263.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6293">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">beg</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">beg</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4364"/>
you to

          <app from="pr4364" n="219.11 (263.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la6294">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you, I beseech you to</rdg>
          </app>
do it. Will you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54167">
Mary Jane straightened herself up, and my, but she was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4365"/>
handsome

          <app from="pr4365" n="219.12–13 (263.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6295">
            <lem wit="A Cent">handsome</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">beautiful</rdg>
          </app>
! She says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54177">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4366"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Here</hi>
          <app from="pr4366" n="219.14 (263.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6296">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">Here</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Here</rdg>
          </app>
is my answer.” She hove up the bag of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4367"/>
money,

          <app from="pr4367" n="219.14 (263.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6297">
            <lem wit="MS2">money,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
money

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and put it in the king’s hands, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4368"/>
says,

          <app from="pr4368" n="219.15 (263.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6298">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says:</rdg>
          </app>
“Take this

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2132"/>
six

          <ptr target="#l11844" type="alt" xml:id="te2132"/>
thousand dollars, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4369"/>
invest

          <app from="pr4369" n="219.16 (263.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6299">
            <lem wit="A Cent">invest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">invest it</rdg>
          </app>
for me and my sisters any way you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4370"/>
want to

          <app from="pr4370" n="219.16 (264.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6300">
            <lem wit="A Cent">want to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">like</rdg>
          </app>
, and don’t give us no receipt for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4371"/>
it.

          <app from="pr4371" n="219.17 (264.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6301">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54235">
Then she put her arm around the king on one side, and Susan and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4372"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4372" n="219.19 (264.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6302">
            <lem wit="Cent">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
hare-

              <lb/>
lip

            </rdg>
          </app>
done the same on the other. Everybody clapped their hands and stomped on the floor like a perfect storm, whilst the king held up his head and smiled proud. The doctor says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54249">
“All

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4373"/>
right;

          <app from="pr4373" n="219.22 (264.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6303">
            <lem wit="MS2">right;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">right,</rdg>
          </app>
I wash

          <hi rend="italic">my</hi>
hands of the matter. But I warn you all that a time’s coming when you’re going to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2133"/>
feel

          <ptr target="#l11845" type="alt" xml:id="te2133"/>
sick whenever you think of this day”—and away he went.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54266">
“All right,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4374"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2134"/>
doctor

          <ptr target="#l11846" type="alt" xml:id="te2134"/>
,”

          <app from="pr4374" n="219.25 (265.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6304">
            <lem wit="A Cent">doctor,”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
doctor

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
”

            </rdg>
          </app>
says the king, kinder mocking him, “we’ll try and

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0069"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4375"/>
git

          <app from="pr4375" n="✱***219.26 (265.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6305">
            <lem wit="MS2">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">get</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0069" type="te" xml:id="tv0069"/>
’em to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2135"/>
send

          <ptr target="#l11847" type="alt" xml:id="te2135"/>
for you”—which made them all laugh, and they said it was a prime good hit.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y21901">
          <graphic url="y21901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the bag of money</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0383">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXVI.</head>
        <pb n="220" xml:id="pb0220"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y22001">
          <graphic url="y22001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4376"/>
Chapter XXVI.

            <app from="pr4376" n="220 title (265.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6306">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXVI.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6308">not in; extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6307">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4377"/>
Well,

            <app from="pr4377" n="220.1 (265.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6309">
              <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Well,</lem>
              <rdg wit="A">
Well

                <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2201">
          <graphic url="hf2201.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the cubby</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e54328">
when they was all gone, the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4378"/>
he asks

          <app from="pr4378" n="220.2 (265.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6310">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he asks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">asked</rdg>
          </app>
Mary Jane how they was off for spare rooms, and she said

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2136"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2137"/>
she had

          <ptr target="#l11849" type="alt" xml:id="te2137"/>
one spare room, which would do for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2138"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4379"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr4379" n="220.5 (265-A.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6311">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11850" type="alt" xml:id="te2138"/>
William, and she’d give her own room to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4380"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr4380" n="220.6 (265-A.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6312">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Harvey, which was a little bigger, and she would turn into the room with her sisters and sleep on a cot; and up garret was a little cubby, with a pallet in it. The king said the cubby would do for his valley—meaning me.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54362">
So Mary Jane took us up, and she showed them their rooms, which was plain but nice. She said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4381"/>
she’d

          <app from="pr4381" n="220.17 (265-A.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6313">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">she would</rdg>
          </app>
have her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4382"/>
frocks

          <app from="pr4382" n="220.17 (265-A.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6314">
            <lem wit="A Cent">frocks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dresses</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2139"/>
and a lot of other traps

          <ptr target="#l11851" type="alt" xml:id="te2139"/>
took out of her room if they was in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4383"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr4383" n="220.18 (265-A.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6315">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Harvey’s way, but he said they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4384"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr4384" n="220.19 (265-A.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6316">
            <lem wit="A Cent">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
. The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4385"/>
frocks

          <app from="pr4385" n="220.19 (265-A.19)" type="e" xml:id="la6317">
            <lem wit="A Cent">frocks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dresses</rdg>
          </app>
was hung along the wall, and before them was a curtain

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4386"/>
made out

          <app from="pr4386" n="220.20 (265-B.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6318">
            <lem wit="A Cent">made out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6319">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of calico that hung

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4387"/>
down

          <app from="pr4387" n="220.20 (265-B.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6320">
            <lem wit="A Cent">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6321">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to the floor. There was an old hair trunk in one corner, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4388"/>
guitar box

          <app from="pr4388" n="220.21–22 (265-B.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6322">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">guitar box</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">guitar-box</rdg>
          </app>
in another, and all sorts of little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4389"/>
knick-knacks

          <app from="pr4389" n="220.22 (265-B.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6323">
            <lem wit="MS2">knick-knacks</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
knick-

              <lb/>
knacks

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">knickknacks</rdg>
          </app>
and jimcracks around,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4390"/>
like

          <app from="pr4390" n="220.23 (265-B.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6324">
            <lem wit="A Cent">like</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">such as</rdg>
          </app>
girls brisken up a room with. The king said it was all the more homely and more pleasanter for these fixings, and so don’t disturb them.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4391"/>
The duke’s room was pretty small, but plenty good enough, and so was my cubby.

          <app from="pr4391" n="220.25–26 (265-B.11–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6325">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">The duke’s . . . cubby.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6326">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11848" type="alt" xml:id="te2136"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54466">
That night they had a big supper, and all them men and women was there, and I stood behind the king and the duke’s chairs and waited on them, and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2140"/>
niggers waited on the

          <ptr target="#l11852" type="alt" xml:id="te2140"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2141"/>
rest.

          <ptr target="#l11853" type="alt" xml:id="te2141"/>
Mary Jane she set at the head of the table, with Susan

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4392"/>
alongside

          <app from="pr4392" n="220.30 (267.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6327">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">alongside</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">along side</rdg>
          </app>
of her, and said how bad the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2142"/>
biscuits was,

          <ptr target="#l11854" type="alt" xml:id="te2142"/>
and how mean the preserves was, and how ornery and tough the fried chickens

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4393"/>
was,

          <app from="pr4393" n="220.32 (267.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6328">
            <lem wit="MS2">was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4394"/>
and all that kind of

          <pb n="221" xml:id="pb0221"/>
rot

          <app from="pr4394" n="220.32–221.1 (267.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la6329">
            <lem wit="A">and all . . . rot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
and all . . . rot and hum-

              <lb/>
bug

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6330">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, the way women

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2143"/>
always

          <ptr target="#l11855" type="alt" xml:id="te2143"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4395"/>
do

          <app from="pr4395" n="221.1 (267.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6331">
            <lem wit="A Cent">do</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">done, in them days,</rdg>
          </app>
for to force out compliments; and the people all knowed everything was tip-top, and said so—said “How

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
you get biscuits to brown so nice?” and “Where, for the land’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4396"/>
sake

          <app from="pr4396" n="221.4 (267.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6332">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">sake</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sake,</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
you get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2144"/>
these

          <ptr target="#l11856" type="alt" xml:id="te2144"/>
amaz’n pickles?” and all that kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4397"/>
humbug

          <app from="pr4397" n="221.5 (267.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6333">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">humbug</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
hum-

              <lb/>
bug

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4398"/>
talky-talk

          <app from="pr4398" n="221.5 (267.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la6334">
            <lem wit="A">talky-talk</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">
talky-

              <lb/>
talk

            </rdg>
          </app>
, just the way people always does at a supper, you know.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54559">
And when it was all done, me and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4401"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4401" n="221.7 (268.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6338">
            <lem wit="A">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
hare-

              <lb/>
lip

            </rdg>
          </app>
had supper in the kitchen off of the leavings, whilst the others was helping the niggers

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2145"/>
clean

          <ptr target="#l11857" type="alt" xml:id="te2145"/>
up the things.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4400"/>
The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4399"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4399" n="221.9 (268.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6335">
            <lem wit="A">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
          </app>
she got to pumping me about England, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4402"/>
blest

          <app from="pr4402" n="221.10 (268.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6339">
            <lem wit="A">blest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m blest</rdg>
          </app>
if I didn’t think the ice was getting mighty thin, sometimes. She says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54596">
“Did you ever see the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4403"/>
king?”

          <app from="pr4403" n="221.12 (268.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6340">
            <lem wit="A">king?”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
king?

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6341">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54607">
“Who?

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0006"/>
William Fourth?

          <ptr target="#as0217" type="an" xml:id="an0006"/>
Well, I bet I have—he goes to our church.”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4404"/>
I knowed he was dead years ago, but I never let on. So when I says he goes to our church, she says:

          <app from="pr4404" n="221.14–15 (268.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6342">
            <lem wit="A">I knowed . . . says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6343">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54621">“What—regular?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54623">
“Yes—regular. His pew’s right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2146"/>
over

          <ptr target="#l11858" type="alt" xml:id="te2146"/>
opposite ourn—on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4405"/>
t’other

          <app from="pr4405" n="221.17 (269.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6344">
            <lem wit="C">t’other</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’t’other</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">’tother</rdg>
          </app>
side the pulpit.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y22101">
          <graphic url="y22101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">supper with the hare-lip</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54645">
          <pb n="222" xml:id="pb0222"/>
“I thought he lived in London?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54647">
“Well, he does. Where

          <hi rend="italic">would</hi>
he live?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54652">
“But I thought

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
lived in Sheffield?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54657">
I see I was up a stump. I had to let on to get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2147"/>
choked

          <ptr target="#l11859" type="alt" xml:id="te2147"/>
with a chicken bone,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2148"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l11860" type="alt" xml:id="te2148"/>
as to get time to think how to get down again. Then I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54667">
“I mean he goes to our church regular when he’s in Sheffield. That’s only in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4406"/>
summer time

          <app from="pr4406" n="222.7 (269.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6345">
            <lem wit="MS2">summer time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">summer-time</rdg>
          </app>
, when he comes

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2149"/>
there

          <ptr target="#l11861" type="alt" xml:id="te2149"/>
to take the sea baths.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54681">
“Why, how you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4407"/>
talk—

          <app from="pr4407" n="222.9 (270.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6346">
            <lem wit="A">talk—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">talk!—</rdg>
          </app>
Sheffield ain’t on the sea.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54691">“Well, who said it was?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54693">“Why, you did.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54695">
“I

          <hi rend="italic">didn’t</hi>
, nuther.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54700">“You did!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54703">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4408"/>
“I didn’t.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54706">
“You did.”

          <app from="pr4408" n="222.14–15 (270.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6347">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] “I didn’t.” [¶] “You did.”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6348">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54714">“I never said nothing of the kind.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54716">
“Well, what

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
you say,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4409"/>
then?”

          <app from="pr4409" n="222.17 (270.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6349">
            <lem wit="A">then?”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
then?

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6350">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54730">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4410"/>
Said

          <app from="pr4410" n="222.18 (270.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6351">
            <lem wit="A">Said</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I said</rdg>
          </app>
he come to take the sea

          <hi rend="italic">baths</hi>
—that’s what I said.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54743">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4411"/>
Well

          <app from="pr4411" n="222.19 (270.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6352">
            <lem wit="C">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4412"/>
then!—

          <app from="pr4412" n="222.19 (270.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6353">
            <lem wit="MS2">then!—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
then!

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
how’s he going to take the sea baths if it ain’t on the sea?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54763">
“Looky

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2150"/>
here,” I says; “did

          <ptr target="#l11862" type="alt" xml:id="te2150"/>
you ever see any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4413"/>
Congress-water

          <app from="pr4413" n="222.21 (271.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6354">
            <lem wit="MS2">Congress-water</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Congress water</rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54777">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54779">“Well, did you have to go to Congress to get it?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54781">“Why, no.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54783">“Well, neither does William Fourth have to go to the sea to get a sea bath.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54786">
“How

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4414"/>
does

          <app from="pr4414" n="222.27 (271.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6355">
            <lem wit="A">does</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">does</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he get it, then?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54797">“Gets it the way people down here gets Congress-water—in barrels. There in the palace at Sheffield they’ve got furnaces, and he wants his water hot. They can’t bile that amount of water away off there at the sea. They haven’t got no conveniences for it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54799">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4415"/>
O

          <app from="pr4415" n="222.32 (272.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6356">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, I see, now. You might a said that in the first

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4416"/>
place,

          <app from="pr4416" n="222.32 (272.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6357">
            <lem wit="MS2">place,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
place

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and saved time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54817">When she said that, I see I was out of the woods again, and so I was comfortable and glad. Next, she says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54819">“Do you go to church, too?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54821">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2151"/>
“Yes—regular.”

          <ptr target="#l11863" type="alt" xml:id="te2151"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54825">“Where do you set?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54827">
          <pb n="223" xml:id="pb0223"/>
“Why, in our pew.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54829">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Whose</hi>
pew?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54834">
“Why,

          <hi rend="italic">ourn</hi>
—your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4417"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr4417" n="223.3 (272.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6358">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Harvey’s.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54847">
“His’n? What does

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2152"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11864" type="alt" xml:id="te2152"/>
want with a pew?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54855">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2153"/>
“Wants it to

          <ptr target="#l11865" type="alt" xml:id="te2153"/>
set in. What did you

          <hi rend="italic">reckon</hi>
he wanted with it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54863">
“Why, I thought

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4418"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr4418" n="223.6 (273.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6359">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
’d

            </rdg>
          </app>
be in the pulpit.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54875">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4419"/>
Rot

          <app from="pr4419" n="223.7 (273.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6360">
            <lem wit="A">Rot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Dern</rdg>
          </app>
him, I forgot he was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2154"/>
a preacher

          <ptr target="#l11866" type="alt" xml:id="te2154"/>
. I see I was up a stump

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4420"/>
again;

          <app from="pr4420" n="223.7 (273.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6361">
            <lem wit="MS2">again;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">again,</rdg>
          </app>
so I played another chicken bone and got another think.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2155"/>
Then I says

          <ptr target="#l11867" type="alt" xml:id="te2155"/>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54901">
“Blame it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2156"/>
do

          <ptr target="#l11868" type="alt" xml:id="te2156"/>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4421"/>
suppose

          <app from="pr4421" n="223.9 (273.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6362">
            <lem wit="A">suppose</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">spose</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4422"/>
there ain’t but

          <app from="pr4422" n="223.9 (273.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6363">
            <lem wit="A">there ain’t but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">there’s only</rdg>
          </app>
one preacher to a church?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54922">“Why, what do they want with more?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54924">“What!—to preach before a king? I never see such a girl as you. They don’t have no less than seventeen.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54926">
“Seventeen! My land! Why, I wouldn’t set out such a string as that, not if I

          <hi rend="italic">never</hi>
got to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="ht0176"/>
glory.

          <ptr target="#te2157" type="alt" xml:id="l11869"/>
It must take ’em a week.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54935">
“Shucks, they don’t

          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
of ’em preach the same day—only

          <hi rend="italic">one</hi>
of ’em.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54943">“Well, then, what does the rest of ’em do?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54945">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2158"/>
Oh

          <ptr target="#l11870" type="alt" xml:id="te2158"/>
, nothing much. Loll around, pass the plate—and one thing or another. But mainly they don’t do nothing.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54951">
“Well, then, what are they

          <hi rend="italic">for?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54957">
“Why, they’re for

          <hi rend="italic">style.</hi>
Don’t you know nothing?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54962">
“Well, I don’t

          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
to know no such foolishness as that. How is servants treated in England? Do they treat ’em

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4423"/>
better’n

          <app from="pr4423" n="223.24 (275.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6364">
            <lem wit="MS2">better’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">better ’n</rdg>
          </app>
we treat our niggers?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54975">
“

          <hi rend="italic">No!</hi>
A servant ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4424"/>
nobody,

          <app from="pr4424" n="223.26 (275.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6365">
            <lem wit="MS2">nobody,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
nobody

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
there. They treat

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2159"/>
them

          <ptr target="#l11871" type="alt" xml:id="te2159"/>
worse than dogs.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e54992">
“Don’t they give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4425"/>
’em

          <app from="pr4425" n="223.28 (275.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6366">
            <lem wit="A">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them</rdg>
          </app>
holidays, the way we do,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4426"/>
Christmas,

          <app from="pr4426" n="223.28 (275.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6367">
            <lem wit="MS2">Christmas,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Christmas

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and New Year’s week, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4427"/>
fourth

          <app from="pr4427" n="223.29 (275.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6368">
            <lem wit="MS2">fourth</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Fourth</rdg>
          </app>
of July?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55019">
“Oh, just listen! A body could tell

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
hain’t ever been to England, by that. Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4428"/>
Hare-l

          <app from="pr4428" n="223.31 (275.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6369">
            <lem wit="A">Hare-l</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Hair-l</rdg>
          </app>
—why,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2160"/>
Joanna

          <ptr target="#l11872" type="alt" xml:id="te2160"/>
, they never see a holiday from year’s end to year’s end; never go to the circus, nor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4429"/>
theatre

          <app from="pr4429" n="223.32 (276.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6370">
            <lem wit="A">theatre</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the theatre</rdg>
          </app>
, nor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2161"/>
nigger

          <ptr target="#l11873" type="alt" xml:id="te2161"/>
shows, nor nowheres.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55049">
“Nor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2162"/>
church

          <ptr target="#l11874" type="alt" xml:id="te2162"/>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55055">
“Nor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2163"/>
church

          <ptr target="#l11875" type="alt" xml:id="te2163"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55061">
“But

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
always went to church.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55066">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4430"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2164"/>
Well

          <ptr target="#l11876" type="alt" xml:id="te2164"/>
          <app from="pr4430" n="223.37 (276.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6371">
            <lem wit="A">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Well, sir</rdg>
          </app>
, I was gone up again. I forgot I was the old man’s servant. But next minute I whirled in on a kind of an explanation how a

          <pb n="224" xml:id="pb0224"/>
valley was different from a common servant, and

          <hi rend="italic">had</hi>
to go to church whether he wanted to or not, and set with the family, on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4431"/>
account

          <app from="pr4431" n="224.2 (277.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la6372">
            <lem wit="A">account</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">accounts</rdg>
          </app>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4432"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr4432" n="224.3 (277.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6373">
            <lem wit="A">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">its</rdg>
          </app>
being the law. But I didn’t do it pretty good, and when I got done I see she warn’t satisfied. She says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55097">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0007"/>
Honest injun

          <ptr target="#as0218" type="an" xml:id="an0007"/>
, now, hain’t you been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4433"/>
telling

          <app from="pr4433" n="224.5 (277.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6374">
            <lem wit="A">telling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tellin’</rdg>
          </app>
me a lot of lies?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55111">“Honest injun,” says I.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55114">“None of it at all?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55116">“None of it at all. Not a lie in it,” says I.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55118">“Lay your hand on this book and say it.”</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y22401">
          <graphic url="y22401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">honest injun.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55126">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0008"/>
I see it warn’t nothing but a dictionary

          <ptr target="#as0219" type="an" xml:id="an0008"/>
, so I laid my hand on it and said it. So then she looked a little better satisfied, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55131">
“Well, then, I’ll believe some of it; but I hope to gracious if I’ll believe the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2165"/>
rest.”

          <ptr target="#l11877" type="alt" xml:id="te2165"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55136">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2166"/>
“What is it you won’t believe,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2167"/>
Joe?

          <ptr target="#l11879" type="alt" xml:id="te2167"/>
” says Mary Jane, stepping

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4434"/>
in,

          <app from="pr4434" n="224.14 (279.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6375">
            <lem wit="MS2">in,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
in

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with Susan behind her. “It ain’t right nor kind for you to talk so to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2168"/>
him,

          <ptr target="#l11880" type="alt" xml:id="te2168"/>
and him a stranger and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4435"/>
so far

          <app from="pr4435" n="224.16 (279.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6376">
            <lem wit="A">so far</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
from his people. How would you like to be treated so?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55164">
          <pb n="225" xml:id="pb0225"/>
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2169"/>
That’s

          <ptr target="#l11881" type="alt" xml:id="te2169"/>
always your way, Maim—always

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2170"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4436"/>
sailing

          <app from="pr4436" n="225.1 (279.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6377">
            <lem wit="A">sailing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a-sailin’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11882" type="alt" xml:id="te2170"/>
in to help somebody before they’re hurt.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4437"/>
I

          <app from="pr4437" n="225.2 (279.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6378">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
hain’t done nothing to him. He’s told some stretchers, I reckon; and I said I wouldn’t swallow it all; and that’s every bit and grain

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2171"/>
I

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11883" type="alt" xml:id="te2171"/>
say. I reckon he can stand a little thing like that, can’t he?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55196">
“I don’t care whether ’twas little or whether ’twas big, he’s here in our house and a stranger, and it wasn’t good of you to say it. If you was in his place, it would make you feel ashamed; and so you oughtn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2172"/>
to say

          <ptr target="#l11884" type="alt" xml:id="te2172"/>
a thing to another person that will make

          <hi rend="italic">them</hi>
feel ashamed.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55205">
“Why, Maim, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4438"/>
said—

          <app from="pr4438" n="225.11 (280.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6379">
            <lem wit="MS2">said—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">said——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55215">
“It don’t make no difference what he

          <hi rend="italic">said</hi>
—that ain’t the thing. The thing is for you to treat him

          <hi rend="italic">kind</hi>
, and not be saying things to make him remember he ain’t in his own country and amongst his own folks.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55224">
I says to myself,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4439"/>
          <hi rend="italic">This</hi>
          <app from="pr4439" n="225.16 (281.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6380">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">This</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
is a girl that I’m letting that old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4440"/>
reptle

          <app from="pr4440" n="225.16 (281.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6381">
            <lem wit="A">reptle</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reptyle</rdg>
          </app>
rob her of her money!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55245">
Then Susan

          <hi rend="italic">she</hi>
waltzed in; and if you’ll believe me, she did give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4441"/>
Hare-Lip

          <app from="pr4441" n="225.19 (281.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6382">
            <lem wit="C">Hare-Lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Hair-Lip</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Hare-lip</rdg>
          </app>
hark from the tomb!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55260">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2173"/>
Says I

          <ptr target="#l11885" type="alt" xml:id="te2173"/>
to myself, And this is

          <hi rend="italic">another</hi>
one that I’m letting him rob

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4442"/>
her of her money

          <app from="pr4442" n="225.21 (281.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6383">
            <lem wit="A">her of her money</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6384">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55277">
Then Mary Jane she took another inning, and went in sweet and lovely

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2174"/>
again

          <ptr target="#l11886" type="alt" xml:id="te2174"/>
—which was her way—but when she got done there warn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2175"/>
hardly

          <ptr target="#l11887" type="alt" xml:id="te2175"/>
anything left

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4443"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4443" n="225.24 (281.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6385">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
poor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4444"/>
Hare-Lip

          <app from="pr4444" n="225.24 (282.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6386">
            <lem wit="C">Hare-Lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Hare-lip</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">Hair-Lip</rdg>
          </app>
. So she hollered.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55306">
“All right, then,” says the other girls, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4445"/>
you

          <app from="pr4445" n="225.25 (282.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6387">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">You</rdg>
          </app>
just ask his pardon.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55316">She done it, too. And she done it beautiful. She done it so beautiful it was good to hear; and I wished I could tell her a thousand lies, so she could do it again.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55318">
I says to myself,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4446"/>
This

          <app from="pr4446" n="225.29 (282.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6388">
            <lem wit="MS2">This</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">this</rdg>
          </app>
is

          <hi rend="italic">another</hi>
one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4447"/>
that I’m letting him rob her of her money

          <app from="pr4447" n="225.29–30 (282.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6389">
            <lem wit="A">that . . . money</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6390">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. And when she got through,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4448"/>
they

          <app from="pr4448" n="225.30 (282.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6391">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and they</rdg>
          </app>
all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4449"/>
just

          <app from="pr4449" n="225.30 (282.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6392">
            <lem wit="MS2">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jest</rdg>
          </app>
laid theirselves out to make me feel at home and know I was amongst

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4450"/>
friends.

          <app from="pr4450" n="225.31 (283.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6393">
            <lem wit="A">friends.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">friends,</rdg>
          </app>
I felt so ornery and low down and mean, that I says to myself, My mind’s made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4451"/>
up:

          <app from="pr4451" n="225.33 (283.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6394">
            <lem wit="MS2">up:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">up;</rdg>
          </app>
I’ll hive that money for them or bust.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55374">
So then I lit out—for bed, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4452"/>
said, meaning some time or another

          <app from="pr4400" n="221.9–225.34 (268.7–283.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6336">
            <lem wit="A">The . . . another.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">The . . . another stretcher.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6337">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <app from="pr4452" n="225.34 (283.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6395">
            <lem wit="A">said, meaning . . . another</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said—which was another stretcher</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4453"/>
When

          <app from="pr4453" n="225.35 (283.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6396">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6397">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
When

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">[¶] When</rdg>
          </app>
I got by myself, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4454"/>
went to thinking the thing over

          <app from="pr4454" n="225.35 (283.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6398">
            <lem wit="A Cent">went . . . over</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">took a think</rdg>
          </app>
. I says to myself,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4455"/>
Shall

          <app from="pr4455" n="225.36 (283.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6399">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Shall</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shall</rdg>
          </app>
I go to that doctor, private, and blow on these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4456"/>
frauds

          <app from="pr4456" n="225.36 (283.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6400">
            <lem wit="A Cent">frauds</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rips</rdg>
          </app>
? No—that won’t do. He might tell who told him; then the king and the duke would make it warm for me. Shall I go, private, and tell Mary Jane? No—I dasn’t do it.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2176"/>
Her

          <ptr target="#l11888" type="alt" xml:id="te2176"/>
face would give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4457"/>
them

          <app from="pr4457" n="225.39 (284.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6401">
            <lem wit="A Cent">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them rips</rdg>
          </app>
a hint,

          <pb n="226" xml:id="pb0226"/>
sure;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2177"/>
they’ve

          <ptr target="#l11889" type="alt" xml:id="te2177"/>
got the money, and they’d slide

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4458"/>
right

          <app from="pr4458" n="226.1 (284.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6402">
            <lem wit="A Cent">right</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6403">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
out and get away with it. If she was to fetch in help, I’d get mixed up in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4459"/>
business,

          <app from="pr4459" n="226.2 (284.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6404">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">business,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
business

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before it was done with, I judge. No, there ain’t no good way but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4460"/>
one.

          <app from="pr4460" n="226.4 (284.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6405">
            <lem wit="A Cent">one.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">one:</rdg>
          </app>
I got to steal that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4461"/>
money,

          <app from="pr4461" n="226.4 (284.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6406">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">money,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
money

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
some how; and I got to steal it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4462"/>
some

          <app from="pr4462" n="226.4 (284.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6407">
            <lem wit="A Cent">some</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in some</rdg>
          </app>
way that they won’t suspicion that I done it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4463"/>
They’ve got a good thing, here; and they ain’t agoing to leave till they’ve played this family and this town for all they’re worth, so I’ll find a chance time enough.

          <app from="pr4463" n="226.5–8 (284.13–285.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6408">
            <lem wit="A">They’ve . . . time enough.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">They’ve . . . sooner or later.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6409">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2178"/>
I’ll

          <ptr target="#l11890" type="alt" xml:id="te2178"/>
steal it, and hide it; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4464"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr4464" n="226.8 (285.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6410">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, when I’m away down the river, I’ll write a letter and tell Mary Jane where it’s hid. But

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2179"/>
I better

          <ptr target="#l11891" type="alt" xml:id="te2179"/>
hive it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4465"/>
tonight

          <app from="pr4465" n="226.10 (285.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6411">
            <lem wit="MS2">tonight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">to-night</rdg>
          </app>
, if I can, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4466"/>
the

          <app from="pr4466" n="226.10 (285.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6412">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that</rdg>
          </app>
doctor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4467"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4467" n="226.10 (285.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6413">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
hasn’t let up as much as he lets on he has; he might scare them out of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4468"/>
here,

          <app from="pr4468" n="226.11 (285.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6414">
            <lem wit="A">here,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">this,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">here</rdg>
          </app>
yet.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55557">
So, thinks I, I’ll go and search them rooms.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4469"/>
Up stairs

          <app from="pr4469" n="226.13 (285.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6415">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Up stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Upstairs</rdg>
          </app>
the hall was dark, but I found the duke’s room, and started to paw around it with my hands; but I recollected it wouldn’t be much like the king to let anybody else take care of that money but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4470"/>
his own self

          <app from="pr4470" n="226.16 (286.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6416">
            <lem wit="A Cent">his own self</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">himself</rdg>
          </app>
; so then I went to his room and begun to paw around there. But I see I couldn’t do nothing without a candle, and I dasn’t light one, of course.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2180"/>
So I judged I’d got to do the other thing—lay for them, and eavesdrop. About that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4471"/>
time,

          <app from="pr4471" n="226.20 (286verso.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6417">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">time,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
time

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I

          <ptr target="#l11892" type="alt" xml:id="te2180"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4472"/>
hears

          <app from="pr4472" n="226.20 (286.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6418">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">heard</rdg>
          </app>
their

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2181"/>
footsteps

          <ptr target="#l11893" type="alt" xml:id="te2181"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4473"/>
coming

          <app from="pr4473" n="226.20 (286.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6419">
            <lem wit="A Cent">coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a-coming</rdg>
          </app>
, and was going to skip under the bed;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2182"/>
I reached

          <ptr target="#l11894" type="alt" xml:id="te2182"/>
for it, but it wasn’t where I thought it would be; but I touched the curtain that hid Mary Jane’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4474"/>
frocks

          <app from="pr4474" n="226.22 (286.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6420">
            <lem wit="A Cent">frocks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dresses</rdg>
          </app>
, so I jumped in behind that and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4475"/>
snuggled

          <app from="pr4475" n="226.23 (286.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la6421">
            <lem wit="A Cent">snuggled</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">snuggled myself</rdg>
          </app>
in amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4476"/>
gowns, and stood there perfectly

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2183"/>
still.

          <ptr target="#l11895" type="alt" xml:id="te2183"/>
          <app from="pr4476" n="226.23–24 (286.16–17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6422">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">gowns, and . . . still</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gowns</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55639">
They come in and shut the door; and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4477"/>
first

          <app from="pr4477" n="226.25 (287.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6423">
            <lem wit="A Cent">first</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">very first</rdg>
          </app>
thing the duke done was to get down and look under the bed.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4478"/>
Then I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4479"/>
glad

          <app from="pr4479" n="226.26 (287.8)" type="e" xml:id="lap426">
            <lem wit="A">glad</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kinder glad</rdg>
          </app>
I hadn’t found

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4480"/>
the

          <app from="pr4480" n="226.27 (287.9)" type="e" xml:id="laq427">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that</rdg>
          </app>
bed when I wanted it. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4481"/>
yet you know

          <app from="pr4481" n="226.27 (287.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6428">
            <lem wit="MS2">yet you know</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">yet, you know,</rdg>
          </app>
it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4482"/>
kind of

          <app from="pr4482" n="226.27 (287.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la6429">
            <lem wit="A">kind of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">perfectly</rdg>
          </app>
natural to hide under

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4483"/>
the

          <app from="pr4483" n="226.28 (287.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6430">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a</rdg>
          </app>
bed when you are up to anything private.

          <app from="pr4478" n="226.26–28 (287.7–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6424">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Then . . . private.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6425">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
They sets

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4484"/>
down,

          <app from="pr4484" n="226.29 (287.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6431">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">down,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
down

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then, and the king says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55709">
“Well, what is it?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4485"/>
And

          <app from="pr4485" n="226.30 (287.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6432">
            <lem wit="MS2">And</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">and</rdg>
          </app>
cut it middlin’ short,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4486"/>
because

          <app from="pr4486" n="226.30 (287.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6433">
            <lem wit="A Cent">because</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">becuz</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2184"/>
it’s better

          <ptr target="#l11896" type="alt" xml:id="te2184"/>
for us to be down there a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4487"/>
whoopin’-up

          <app from="pr4487" n="226.31 (287.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6434">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">whoopin’-up</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">whoopin’ up</rdg>
          </app>
the mournin’, than up here givin’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4488"/>
’em

          <app from="pr4488" n="226.32 (287.19)" type="e" xml:id="la6435">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">em</rdg>
          </app>
a chance to talk us over.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55747">
“Well, this is it, Capet. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4489"/>
ain’t easy

          <app from="pr4489" n="226.33 (288.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6436">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ain’t easy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">aint easy</rdg>
          </app>
; I ain’t comfortable. That

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4490"/>
doctor

          <app from="pr4490" n="226.34 (288.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6437">
            <lem wit="A Cent">doctor</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cussed doctor</rdg>
          </app>
lays on my mind. I wanted to know

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4491"/>
your plans

          <app from="pr4491" n="226.34 (288.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la6438">
            <lem wit="A Cent">your plans</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">what your plans is</rdg>
          </app>
. I’ve got a notion, and I think it’s a sound one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55774">“What is it, duke?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55776">
“That we better glide out of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4492"/>
this,

          <app from="pr4492" n="226.37 (288.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6439">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">this,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
this

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before three in the morning, and clip it down the river with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2185"/>
what

          <ptr target="#l11897" type="alt" xml:id="te2185"/>
we’ve

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2186"/>
got. Specially, seeing we

          <pb n="227" xml:id="pb0227"/>
got it so easy—

          <hi rend="italic">given</hi>
back to us, flung at our heads, as you may say, when of course we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4493"/>
allowed

          <app from="pr4493" n="227.2 (288verso.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6440">
            <lem wit="A Cent">allowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was expecting</rdg>
          </app>
to have to steal it back. I’m for knocking off and lighting out.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y22701">
          <graphic url="y22701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the duke looks under the bed</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55804">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4494"/>
That

          <ptr target="#l11898" type="alt" xml:id="te2186"/>
made me feel pretty bad.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4495"/>
About an

          <app from="pr4495" n="227.4 (288.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6443">
            <lem wit="A">About an</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">An</rdg>
          </app>
hour or two ago, it would a been a little different, but now it made me feel

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2187"/>
bad and

          <ptr target="#l11899" type="alt" xml:id="te2187"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4496"/>
disappointed.

          <app from="pr4496" n="227.5–6 (288.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6444">
            <lem wit="A">disappointed.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
disappointed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6445">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4497"/>
king

          <app from="pr4497" n="227.6 (288.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6446">
            <lem wit="A">king</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">king he</rdg>
          </app>
rips

          <ptr target="#l11878" type="alt" xml:id="te2166"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2188"/>
out and says:

          <app from="pr4494" n="227.4–6 (288.12–289.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6441">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">That . . . says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6442">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55849">
“What! And not sell out the rest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4498"/>
o’

          <app from="pr4498" n="227.7 (289.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6447">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
the property? March off like a passel

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4499"/>
o’ fools

          <app from="pr4499" n="227.8 (289.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6448">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’ fools</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of fools</rdg>
          </app>
and leave

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2189"/>
eight or nine

          <ptr target="#l11901" type="alt" xml:id="te2189"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4500"/>
thous’n’

          <app from="pr4500" n="227.8 (289.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6449">
            <lem wit="A Cent">thous’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thousand</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4501"/>
dollars’

          <app from="pr4501" n="227.8 (289.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6450">
            <lem wit="A Cent">dollars’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dollars</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2190"/>
worth

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4502"/>
o’ property

          <app from="pr4502" n="227.8–9 (289.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6451">
            <lem wit="A Cent">o’ property</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of property</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11902" type="alt" xml:id="te2190"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4503"/>
layin’

          <app from="pr4503" n="227.9 (289.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6452">
            <lem wit="A Cent">layin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">laying</rdg>
          </app>
around jest sufferin’ to be scooped in?—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2191"/>
and all good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4504"/>
saleable

          <app from="pr4504" n="227.10 (289.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6453">
            <lem wit="MS2">saleable</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">salable</rdg>
          </app>
stuff, too.”

          <ptr target="#l11903" type="alt" xml:id="te2191"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55916">
The duke he grumbled; said the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2192"/>
bag of gold

          <ptr target="#l11904" type="alt" xml:id="te2192"/>
was enough, and he didn’t want to go no deeper—didn’t want to rob a lot of orphans of

          <hi rend="italic">everything</hi>
they had.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e55925">
“Why, how you talk!” says the king. “We

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4505"/>
shan’t

          <app from="pr4505" n="227.14 (290.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6454">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">shan’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sha’n’t</rdg>
          </app>
rob ’em of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4506"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr4506" n="227.15 (290.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6455">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
at all but jest

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4507"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2193"/>
this

          <ptr target="#l11905" type="alt" xml:id="te2193"/>
          <app from="pr4507" n="227.15 (290.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6456">
            <lem wit="A Cent">this</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">their</rdg>
          </app>
money. The people that

          <hi rend="italic">buys</hi>
the property is the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4508"/>
suff’rers

          <app from="pr4508" n="227.16 (290.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6457">
            <lem wit="A Cent">suff’rers</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sufferers</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4509"/>
because

          <app from="pr4509" n="227.16 (290.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6458">
            <lem wit="A Cent">because</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">becuz</rdg>
          </app>
as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4510"/>
soon’s

          <app from="pr4510" n="227.16 (290.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la6459">
            <lem wit="A Cent">soon’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">soon as</rdg>
          </app>
it’s found out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4511"/>
’at

          <app from="pr4511" n="227.16 (290.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6460">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’at</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that</rdg>
          </app>
we didn’t own it—which won’t be long after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4512"/>
we’ve slid

          <app from="pr4512" n="227.17 (290.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6461">
            <lem wit="A Cent">we’ve slid</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we disappear</rdg>
          </app>
—the sale won’t be valid, and it’ll

          <ptr target="#l11900" type="alt" xml:id="te2188"/>
all go back to the estate.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4513"/>
These-yer

          <app from="pr4513" n="227.18 (291.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la6462">
            <lem wit="A">These-yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
These-

              <lb/>
yer

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">These yer</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4514"/>
orphans ’ll

          <app from="pr4514" n="227.18 (291.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6463">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">orphans ’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">orphans’ll</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4515"/>
git

          <app from="pr4515" n="227.18 (291.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6464">
            <lem wit="A Cent">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">get</rdg>
          </app>
their house back

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2194"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4516"/>
agin

          <app from="pr4516" n="227.19 (291.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6465">
            <lem wit="A Cent">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">again</rdg>
          </app>
, and that’s enough for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4517"/>
          <hi rend="italic">them:</hi>
          <app from="pr4517" n="227.19 (291.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6466">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">them:</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">them;</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
they’re

          <ptr target="#l11906" type="alt" xml:id="te2194"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4518"/>
young,

          <app from="pr4518" n="227.19 (291.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6467">
            <lem wit="MS2">young,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
young

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and spry, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4519"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr4519" n="227.20 (291.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6468">
            <lem wit="A Cent">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">can</rdg>
          </app>
easy earn a livin’.

          <hi rend="italic">They</hi>
ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4520"/>
agoing

          <app from="pr4520" n="227.20 (291.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6469">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">agoing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-going</rdg>
          </app>
to suffer. Why, jest

          <pb n="228" xml:id="pb0228"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2195"/>
think

          <ptr target="#l11907" type="alt" xml:id="te2195"/>
—there’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4521"/>
thous’n’s and thous’n’s

          <app from="pr4521" n="228.1 (291.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6470">
            <lem wit="A Cent">thous’n’s and thous’n’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thousands and thousands</rdg>
          </app>
that ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2196"/>
nigh

          <ptr target="#l11908" type="alt" xml:id="te2196"/>
so well off. Bless you,

          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
ain’t got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2197"/>
noth’n

          <ptr target="#l11909" type="alt" xml:id="te2197"/>
to complain of.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56102">
Well, the king he talked him blind; so at last he give in, and said all right, but said he believed it was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4522"/>
blame’

          <app from="pr4522" n="228.4 (291.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6471">
            <lem wit="MS2">blame’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">blame</rdg>
          </app>
foolishness to stay, and that doctor hanging over them. But the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4523"/>
says

          <app from="pr4523" n="228.5 (291.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6472">
            <lem wit="A Cent">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56120">
“Cuss the doctor! What do we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4524"/>
k’yer

          <app from="pr4524" n="228.6 (291.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6473">
            <lem wit="A Cent">k’yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">care</rdg>
          </app>
for

          <hi rend="italic">him?</hi>
Hain’t we got all the fools in town on our side? and ain’t that a big enough majority in any town?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56133">
So they got ready to go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4525"/>
down stairs

          <app from="pr4525" n="228.9 (292.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6474">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">down stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">down-stairs</rdg>
          </app>
again. The duke says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56144">“I don’t think we put that money in a good place.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56146">
That cheered me up.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4526"/>
I’d begun

          <app from="pr4526" n="228.11 (292.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6475">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d begun</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I was beginning</rdg>
          </app>
to think I warn’t going to get a hint of no kind to help me. The king says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56156">“Why?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56158">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2198"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4527"/>
Because

          <app from="pr4527" n="228.14 (292.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6476">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Because</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Becuz</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11910" type="alt" xml:id="te2198"/>
Mary

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4528"/>
Jane’ll

          <app from="pr4528" n="228.14 (292.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6477">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Jane’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jane ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
be in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4529"/>
mourning

          <app from="pr4529" n="228.14 (292.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6478">
            <lem wit="A Cent">mourning</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mournin’</rdg>
          </app>
from this out; and first you know the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2199"/>
nigger

          <ptr target="#l11911" type="alt" xml:id="te2199"/>
that does up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4530"/>
rooms will

          <app from="pr4530" n="228.15 (292.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6479">
            <lem wit="A Cent">rooms will</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rooms ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
get an order to box these

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2200"/>
duds

          <ptr target="#l11912" type="alt" xml:id="te2200"/>
up and put ’em away; and do you reckon a nigger can run across money and not borrow some of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4531"/>
it?

          <app from="pr4531" n="228.17 (293.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6480">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56212">
“Your head’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4532"/>
level,

          <app from="pr4532" n="228.18 (293.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6481">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">level,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
level

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4533"/>
agin

          <app from="pr4533" n="228.18 (293.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6482">
            <lem wit="A Cent">agin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">again</rdg>
          </app>
, duke,” says the king; and he come a fumbling under the curtain

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2201"/>
two or three foot from

          <ptr target="#l11913" type="alt" xml:id="te2201"/>
where I was. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2202"/>
stuck

          <ptr target="#l11914" type="alt" xml:id="te2202"/>
tight to the wall, and kept mighty

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2203"/>
still, though quivery;

          <ptr target="#l11915" type="alt" xml:id="te2203"/>
and I wondered what them fellows would say to me if they catched me; and I tried to think what

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4534"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr4534" n="228.22 (293.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6483">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I had</rdg>
          </app>
better do if they did catch me. But the king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4535"/>
he

          <app from="pr4535" n="228.23 (293.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6484">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6485">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
got the bag before I could think more than about a half a thought, and he never

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4536"/>
suspicioned

          <app from="pr4536" n="228.24 (293.16–17)" type="e" xml:id="la6486">
            <lem wit="A Cent">suspicioned</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">suspicioned that</rdg>
          </app>
I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2204"/>
around.

          <ptr target="#l11916" type="alt" xml:id="te2204"/>
They took and shoved the bag through a rip in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2205"/>
the straw

          <ptr target="#l11917" type="alt" xml:id="te2205"/>
tick that was under the feather bed, and crammed it in a foot or two amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4537"/>
straw,

          <app from="pr4537" n="228.26 (294.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6487">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">straw,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
straw

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and said it was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4538"/>
right,

          <app from="pr4538" n="228.27 (294.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6488">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, because a nigger only makes up the feather bed, and don’t turn over the straw tick only about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2206"/>
twice

          <ptr target="#l11918" type="alt" xml:id="te2206"/>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4539"/>
year, and so it warn’t in no danger of getting stole, now

          <app from="pr4539" n="228.28–29 (294.8–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6489">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">year, and . . . now</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">year</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56306">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4540"/>
But I knowed better. I

          <app from="pr4540" n="228.30 (294.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6490">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] But I knowed better. I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">[¶] Which was a mistake. I</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6491">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
I

            </rdg>
          </app>
had it out of there before they was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4541"/>
half way

          <app from="pr4541" n="228.30 (294.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6492">
            <lem wit="MS2">half way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">half-way</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4542"/>
down stairs

          <app from="pr4542" n="228.31 (294.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6493">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">down stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">down-stairs</rdg>
          </app>
. I groped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4543"/>
along

          <app from="pr4543" n="228.31 (294.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6494">
            <lem wit="A Cent">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6495">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
up to my cubby, and hid it there till I could get a chance to do better. I judged I better hide it outside

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4544"/>
of

          <app from="pr4544" n="228.32 (294.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6496">
            <lem wit="A Cent">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6497">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the house somewheres, because if they missed it they would give the house a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4545"/>
ransacking.

          <app from="pr4545" n="228.34 (295.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6498">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ransacking.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ransacking,</rdg>
          </app>
I knowed that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4546"/>
very

          <app from="pr4546" n="228.34 (295.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6499">
            <lem wit="A Cent">very</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">pretty</rdg>
          </app>
well. Then I turned in, with my clothes all on; but I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4547"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2207"/>
a gone

          <ptr target="#l11919" type="alt" xml:id="te2207"/>
          <app from="pr4547" n="228.35 (295.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6500">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a gone</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ gone</rdg>
          </app>
to sleep, if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4548"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr4548" n="228.35 (295.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6501">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I had</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4549"/>
a wanted

          <app from="pr4549" n="228.35 (295.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6502">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a wanted</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ wanted</rdg>
          </app>
to, I was in such a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4550"/>
sweat

          <app from="pr4550" n="228.36 (295.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6503">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">sweat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hurry</rdg>
          </app>
to get through with the business.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4551"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr4551" n="228.36 (295.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6504">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I heard the king and the duke come up; so I rolled off of my pallet

          <pb n="229" xml:id="pb0229"/>
and laid with my chin at the top of my ladder and waited to see if anything was going to happen. But nothing did.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56415">
So I held on till all the late sounds had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4552"/>
quit

          <app from="pr4552" n="229.3 (295.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6505">
            <lem wit="A Cent">quit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">died out</rdg>
          </app>
and the early ones

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2208"/>
hadn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4553"/>
begun,

          <app from="pr4553" n="229.4 (295.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6506">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">begun,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
begun

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11920" type="alt" xml:id="te2208"/>
yet; and then I slipped down the ladder.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y22901">
          <graphic url="y22901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">huck takes the money</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0389">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXVII.</head>
        <pb n="230" xml:id="pb0230"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y23001">
          <graphic url="y23001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4554"/>
Chapter XXVII.

            <app from="pr4554" n="230 title–1 (295.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6507">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXVII. [¶] I</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6508">
no

                  <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
                </note>
I

              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">[¶] I</rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">I</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2301">
          <graphic url="hf2301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">
a crack in the

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="prg600"/>
dining room

            </hi>
            <app from="prg600" n="230 caption" type="e" xml:id="laf563">
              <lem wit="C">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">dining room</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="deg513">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">dining-room</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">door</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e56480">
crept to their doors and listened; they was snoring, so I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4555"/>
tip-toed

          <app from="pr4555" n="230.2 (296.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6509">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">tip-toed</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">tiptoed</rdg>
          </app>
along, and got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4556"/>
down stairs

          <app from="pr4556" n="230.3 (296.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6510">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">down stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">down-stairs</rdg>
          </app>
all right. There warn’t a sound

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2209"/>
anywheres

          <ptr target="#l11921" type="alt" xml:id="te2209"/>
. I peeped through a crack of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4557"/>
dining room

          <app from="pr4557" n="230.6 (296.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6511">
            <lem wit="MS2">dining room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">dining-room</rdg>
          </app>
door, and see the men that was watching the corpse all sound asleep on their chairs. The door was open into the parlor, where the corpse was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4558"/>
laying

          <app from="pr4558" n="230.11 (296.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6512">
            <lem wit="A Cent">laying</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6513">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, and there was a candle in both rooms. I passed along, and the parlor door was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4559"/>
open;

          <app from="pr4559" n="230.13 (296.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6514">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">open;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">open,</rdg>
          </app>
but I see there warn’t nobody in there but the remainders of Peter; so I shoved on by; but the front door was locked, and the key

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4560"/>
wasn’t

          <app from="pr4560" n="230.17 (296.18)" type="e" xml:id="la6515">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wasn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">not</rdg>
          </app>
there. Just then I heard somebody coming down the stairs, back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4562"/>
behind me

          <app from="pr4562" n="230.19 (297.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6518">
            <lem wit="A Cent">behind me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yonder</rdg>
          </app>
. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4563"/>
run in

          <app from="pr4563" n="230.19 (297.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la6519">
            <lem wit="A Cent">run in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">skipped into</rdg>
          </app>
the parlor, and took a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4564"/>
swift

          <app from="pr4564" n="230.19 (297.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la6520">
            <lem wit="A Cent">swift</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mighty swift</rdg>
          </app>
look around, and the only place I see to hide the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4565"/>
bag,

          <app from="pr4565" n="230.20 (297.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6521">
            <lem wit="MS2">bag,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
bag

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
was in the coffin.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4566"/>
The lid was shoved

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4567"/>
along

          <app from="pr4567" n="230.21 (297.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6524">
            <lem wit="A">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">back</rdg>
          </app>
about a foot, showing the dead man’s face down in there, with a wet cloth over it, and his shroud on.

          <app from="pr4566" n="230.20–22 (297.6–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6522">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">The . . . on.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6523">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I tucked the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4568"/>
money bag

          <app from="pr4568" n="230.22 (297.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6525">
            <lem wit="MS2">money bag</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">money-bag</rdg>
          </app>
in under the lid,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2210"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4569"/>
just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4570"/>
down

          <app from="pr4570" n="230.23 (297.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6528">
            <lem wit="A">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6529">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
beyond

          <ptr target="#l11922" type="alt" xml:id="te2210"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4571"/>
where

          <app from="pr4571" n="230.23 (297.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6530">
            <lem wit="A">where</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6531">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4572"/>
hands was crossed

          <app from="pr4572" n="230.23 (297.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6532">
            <lem wit="A">hands was crossed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">crossed hands</rdg>
          </app>
, which made me creep, they was so cold,

          <app from="pr4569" n="230.23–24 (297.12–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6526">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">just . . . cold,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6527">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and then I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4573"/>
run back

          <app from="pr4573" n="230.24 (297.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6533">
            <lem wit="A Cent">run back</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">skipped</rdg>
          </app>
across the room and in behind the door.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56643">
The person coming was Mary Jane. She went to the coffin, very soft, and kneeled down and looked in; then she put up her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4574"/>
handkerchief

          <app from="pr4574" n="230.27–28 (298.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6534">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">handkerchief</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">handkerchief,</rdg>
          </app>
and I see she begun to cry, though I couldn’t hear her, and her back was to me. I slid out, and as I passed the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4575"/>
dining room

          <app from="pr4575" n="230.29 (298.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6535">
            <lem wit="MS2">dining room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">dining-room</rdg>
          </app>
I thought

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4576"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr4576" n="230.30 (298.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la6536">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I would</rdg>
          </app>
make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4577"/>
sure

          <app from="pr4577" n="230.30 (298.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6537">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sure</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sure that</rdg>
          </app>
them watchers hadn’t seen me; so I looked through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4578"/>
crack

          <app from="pr4578" n="230.31 (298.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6538">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">crack</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">crack,</rdg>
          </app>
and everything was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4579"/>
right. They

          <app from="pr4579" n="230.31 (298.10–11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6539">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">right. They</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">right; they</rdg>
          </app>
hadn’t stirred.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56695">
          <pb n="231" xml:id="pb0231"/>
I slipped up to bed, feeling

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4580"/>
ruther

          <app from="pr4580" n="231.1 (298.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6540">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ruther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">pretty</rdg>
          </app>
blue, on accounts of the thing playing out that way after I had took so much trouble and run so much

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4581"/>
resk

          <app from="pr4581" n="231.3 (298.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6541">
            <lem wit="A Cent">resk</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">risk</rdg>
          </app>
about it. Says I,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2211"/>
if it

          <ptr target="#l11923" type="alt" xml:id="te2211"/>
could stay where it is, all right; because when we get down the river

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4582"/>
a

          <app from="pr4582" n="231.4 (299.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6542">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">several</rdg>
          </app>
hundred mile

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4583"/>
or two,

          <app from="pr4583" n="231.4 (299.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6543">
            <lem wit="A">or two,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6544">not in</note>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
or two

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I could write back to Mary Jane, and she could dig him up again and get it; but that ain’t the thing that’s going to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4584"/>
happen; the

          <app from="pr4584" n="231.6 (299.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6545">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">happen; the</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">happen. The</rdg>
          </app>
thing that’s going to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4585"/>
happen,

          <app from="pr4585" n="231.7 (299.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6546">
            <lem wit="MS2">happen,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
happen

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
is, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4586"/>
money’ll

          <app from="pr4586" n="231.7 (299.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6547">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">money’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">money ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
be found when they come to screw on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4587"/>
lid

          <app from="pr4587" n="231.8 (299.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6548">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lid</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">coffin lid</rdg>
          </app>
. Then the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4588"/>
king ’ll

          <app from="pr4588" n="231.8 (299.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6549">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">king ’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">king’ll</rdg>
          </app>
get it again, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4589"/>
it’ll

          <app from="pr4589" n="231.8 (299.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6550">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">it’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it ’ll</rdg>
          </app>
be a long day before he gives anybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4590"/>
another

          <app from="pr4590" n="231.9 (299.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6551">
            <lem wit="A Cent">another</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">another</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
chance to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2212"/>
smouch

          <ptr target="#l11924" type="alt" xml:id="te2212"/>
it from him. Of course I

          <hi rend="italic">wanted</hi>
to slide down and get it out of there, but I dasn’t try it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4591"/>
Every minute it was getting earlier, now, and pretty soon

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2213"/>
some

          <ptr target="#l11925" type="alt" xml:id="te2213"/>
of them watchers would begin to stir, and I might get catched—catched with six thousand dollars in my hands that nobody hadn’t hired me to take care of.

          <app from="pr4591" n="231.10–14 (300.1–8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6552">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Every . . . of.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6553">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4592"/>
I don’t wish to be mixed up in no such business as that, I says to myself.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56819">
When

          <app from="pr4592" n="231.14–15 (300.8–10)" type="e" xml:id="la6554">
            <lem wit="A">I don’t . . . myself. [¶] When</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Not any of the pie for me, says I.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6555">extra line space</note>
[¶] When

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">[¶] When</rdg>
          </app>
I got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4593"/>
down stairs

          <app from="pr4593" n="231.16 (300.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6556">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">down stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">down-stairs</rdg>
          </app>
in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4594"/>
morning,

          <app from="pr4594" n="231.16 (300.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6557">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">morning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
morning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the parlor was shut

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2214"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4595"/>
up,

          <app from="pr4595" n="231.16 (300.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6558">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11926" type="alt" xml:id="te2214"/>
and the watchers was gone. There warn’t nobody around but the family and the widow Bartley and our tribe. I watched their faces to see if anything had been happening, but I couldn’t tell.

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y23101">
          <graphic url="y23101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the undertaker</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56864">
Towards the middle of the day the undertaker

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4596"/>
come

          <app from="pr4596" n="231.22 (301.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6559">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">come</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">came</rdg>
          </app>
, with his man, and they set the coffin in the middle of the room on a couple of chairs, and then set all our chairs in rows, and borrowed more from the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4597"/>
neighbors

          <app from="pr4597" n="231.26 (301.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6560">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">neighbors</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">neighbors,</rdg>
          </app>
till the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4598"/>
hall

          <app from="pr4598" n="231.26 (301.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6561">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">hall</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">hall,</rdg>
          </app>
and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4599"/>
parlor

          <app from="pr4599" n="231.27 (301.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6562">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">parlor</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">parlor,</rdg>
          </app>
and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4600"/>
dining room

          <app from="pr4600" n="231.27 (301.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6563">
            <lem wit="MS2">dining room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">dining-room</rdg>
          </app>
was full. I see the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4601"/>
coffin lid

          <app from="pr4601" n="231.28 (301.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6564">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">coffin lid</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">coffin-lid</rdg>
          </app>
was the way it was before, but I dasn’t go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4602"/>
to

          <app from="pr4602" n="231.29 (301.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6565">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and</rdg>
          </app>
look in under

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4603"/>
it,

          <app from="pr4603" n="231.30 (301.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6566">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with folks around.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e56932">
Then the people begun to flock in, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4604"/>
beats

          <app from="pr4604" n="231.32 (302.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6567">
            <lem wit="A Cent">beats</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">frauds</rdg>
          </app>
and the girls took seats in the front row

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2215"/>
at

          <ptr target="#l11927" type="alt" xml:id="te2215"/>
the head of the coffin, and for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4605"/>
a half

          <app from="pr4605" n="231.34 (302.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6568">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a half</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">half</rdg>
          </app>
an hour the people filed around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4606"/>
slow,

          <app from="pr4606" n="231.35 (302.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6569">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">slow,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
slow

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in single

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4607"/>
rank,

          <app from="pr4607" n="231.35 (302.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6570">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">rank,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">rank;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4608"/>
and looked down at the dead man’s face a minute, and some dropped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4609"/>
in

          <app from="pr4609" n="231.37 (302.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6573">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6574">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a tear,

          <app from="pr4608" n="231.35–37 (302.6–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6571">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">and looked . . . tear,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6572">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and it was all very still and solemn, only the girls

          <pb n="232" xml:id="pb0232"/>
and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="prf611"/>
beats

          <app from="prf611" n="232.1 (302.11)" type="e" xml:id="laa561">
            <lem wit="A Cent">beats</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">frauds</rdg>
          </app>
holding handkerchiefs to their eyes and keeping their heads

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4611"/>
bent,

          <app from="pr4611" n="232.2 (302.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6576">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">bent,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
bent

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and sobbing a little.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4612"/>
There warn’t no other sound but the scraping of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4613"/>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2216"/>
feet

          <app from="pr4613" n="232.3 (302.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6579">
            <lem wit="A">the feet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">feet</rdg>
          </app>
on the floor, and blowing noses—because people always blows them more at a funeral than they do at other places except church.

          <ptr target="#l11928" type="alt" xml:id="te2216"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57019">
When the place was packed full, the undertaker he slid around in his black gloves

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4614"/>
with

          <app from="pr4614" n="232.7 (303.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6580">
            <lem wit="A">with</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and</rdg>
          </app>
his softy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4615"/>
soothering

          <app from="pr4615" n="232.7 (303.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6581">
            <lem wit="A">soothering</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">soothing</rdg>
          </app>
ways, putting on the last touches, and getting people and things all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4616"/>
ship-shape

          <app from="pr4616" n="232.8 (303.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6582">
            <lem wit="MS2">ship-shape</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
ship-

              <lb/>
shape

            </rdg>
          </app>
and comfortable, and making no more sound than a cat. He never spoke; he moved people around,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4617"/>
he squeezed

          <app from="pr4617" n="232.10 (303.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6583">
            <lem wit="A">he squeezed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">squeezed</rdg>
          </app>
in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4618"/>
late ones

          <app from="pr4618" n="232.10 (303.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6584">
            <lem wit="A">late ones</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">late-comers</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4619"/>
he opened

          <app from="pr4619" n="232.10 (303.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6585">
            <lem wit="A">he opened</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">opened</rdg>
          </app>
up passage-ways, and done it all with nods, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4620"/>
signs

          <app from="pr4620" n="232.11 (303.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la6586">
            <lem wit="A">signs</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">by signs</rdg>
          </app>
with his hands. Then he took his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4621"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2217"/>
place

          <ptr target="#l11929" type="alt" xml:id="te2217"/>
          <app from="pr4621" n="232.12 (303.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6587">
            <lem wit="A">place</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">station</rdg>
          </app>
over against the wall.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0009"/>
He was the softest, glidingest, stealthiest man

          <ptr target="#as0220" type="an" xml:id="tp0009"/>
I ever see; and there warn’t no more smile to him than there is to a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2218"/>
ham.

          <ptr target="#l11930" type="alt" xml:id="te2218"/>
          <app from="pr4612" n="232.2–14 (302.14–304.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6577">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">There . . . ham.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6578">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57106">
They had borrowed a melodeum

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2219"/>
—a sick one

          <ptr target="#l11931" type="alt" xml:id="te2219"/>
; and when everything was ready, a young woman set down and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4622"/>
worked it, and it was pretty skreeky and colicky

          <app from="pr4622" n="232.16–17 (304.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la6588">
            <lem wit="A">worked it, . . . colicky</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">pumped up its sufferings</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">worked it; . . . colicky</rdg>
          </app>
, and everybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4623"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2220"/>
joined

          <ptr target="#l11932" type="alt" xml:id="te2220"/>
          <app from="pr4623" n="232.17 (304.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6589">
            <lem wit="A Cent">joined</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jined</rdg>
          </app>
in and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4624"/>
sung, and Peter was the only one that had a good thing, according to my notion

          <app from="pr4624" n="232.17–18 (304.8–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6590">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">sung, and . . . notion</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sung</rdg>
          </app>
. Then the Reverend Hobson opened up, slow and solemn, and begun to talk; and straight off the most outrageous row busted out in the cellar

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4625"/>
a body

          <app from="pr4625" n="232.21 (304.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6591">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a body</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that was</rdg>
          </app>
ever heard; it was only one dog, but he made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4626"/>
a most powerful racket,

          <app from="pr4626" n="232.21–22 (304.17–305.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6592">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a most powerful racket,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">racket for a million;</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2221"/>
he kept

          <ptr target="#l11933" type="alt" xml:id="te2221"/>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4627"/>
up,

          <app from="pr4627" n="232.22 (305.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6593">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4628"/>
along; the

          <app from="pr4628" n="232.22 (305.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6594">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">along; the</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">along. The</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4629"/>
parson he

          <app from="pr4629" n="232.22 (305.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6595">
            <lem wit="A Cent">parson he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">parson</rdg>
          </app>
had to stand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4630"/>
there,

          <app from="pr4630" n="232.23 (305.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6596">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">there,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
there

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4631"/>
over the coffin,

          <app from="pr4631" n="232.23 (305.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6597">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">over the coffin,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6598">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4632"/>
wait—

          <app from="pr4632" n="232.23 (305.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6599">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">wait—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">wait;</rdg>
          </app>
you couldn’t hear yourself think. It was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4633"/>
right down

          <app from="pr4633" n="232.24 (305.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6600">
            <lem wit="A Cent">right down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dreadful</rdg>
          </app>
awkward, and nobody didn’t seem to know what to do. But pretty soon they see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4634"/>
that

          <app from="pr4634" n="232.25 (305.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6601">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">the</rdg>
          </app>
long-legged undertaker make a sign to the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2222"/>
preacher

          <ptr target="#l11934" type="alt" xml:id="te2222"/>
as much as to say, “Don’t you worry—just depend on me.” Then he stooped down and begun to glide along the wall, just his shoulders showing over the people’s heads. So he glided

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4635"/>
along, and

          <app from="pr4635" n="232.29 (306.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6602">
            <lem wit="A Cent">along, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">along,</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4636"/>
pow-wow

          <app from="pr4636" n="232.29 (306.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6603">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">pow-wow</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">powwow</rdg>
          </app>
and racket getting more and more outrageous all the time; and at last, when he had gone around two sides of the room, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4637"/>
disappears

          <app from="pr4637" n="232.31 (306.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6604">
            <lem wit="A Cent">disappears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">disappeared</rdg>
          </app>
down cellar. Then, in about two seconds we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4638"/>
heard

          <app from="pr4638" n="232.32 (306.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6605">
            <lem wit="A Cent">heard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hear</rdg>
          </app>
a whack, and the dog

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4639"/>
he

          <app from="pr4639" n="232.32 (306.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6606">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6607">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
finished up with a most amazing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4640"/>
howl

          <app from="pr4640" n="232.33 (306.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6608">
            <lem wit="A Cent">howl</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yelp</rdg>
          </app>
or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4641"/>
two

          <app from="pr4641" n="232.33 (306.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6609">
            <lem wit="MS2">two</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">two,</rdg>
          </app>
and then everything was dead

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4642"/>
still

          <app from="pr4642" n="232.33 (306.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6610">
            <lem wit="A Cent">still</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">still again</rdg>
          </app>
, and the parson begun his solemn talk where he left off. In a minute

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4643"/>
or two

          <app from="pr4643" n="232.34 (306.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6611">
            <lem wit="A Cent">or two</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6612">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
here comes this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4644"/>
undertaker’s

          <app from="pr4644" n="232.35 (306.16–307.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6613">
            <lem wit="Cent">undertaker’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
un-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
taker’s

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
under-

              <lb/>
taker’s

            </rdg>
          </app>
back and shoulders gliding along

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2223"/>
the wall

          <ptr target="#l11935" type="alt" xml:id="te2223"/>
again; and so he glided, and glided, around three sides of the room, and then rose up, and

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0070"/>
shaded his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2224"/>
mouth

          <ptr target="#l11936" type="alt" xml:id="te2224"/>
with his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4645"/>
hands

          <app from="pr4645" n="232.37 (307.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6614">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hands</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hand</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0070" type="te" xml:id="tv0070"/>
, and stretched his neck out towards the preacher, over the people’s heads,

          <pb n="233" xml:id="pb0233"/>
and says, in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4646"/>
kind of a

          <app from="pr4646" n="233.1 (307.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6615">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kind of a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6616">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
coarse whisper,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0010"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4647"/>
          <hi rend="italic">He had a rat!</hi>
          <app from="pr4647" n="233.1 (307.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la6617">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">He had a rat</hi>
!

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">He had a rat!</rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#as0221" type="an" xml:id="an0010"/>
Then he drooped down and glided along the wall

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4648"/>
again,

          <app from="pr4648" n="233.2 (307.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6618">
            <lem wit="MS2">again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
again

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to his place.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2225"/>
You

          <ptr target="#l11937" type="alt" xml:id="te2225"/>
could see it was a great satisfaction to the people, because naturally they wanted to know. A little thing like that don’t cost nothing, and it’s just the little things that makes a man to be looked up to and liked. There warn’t no more popular man in town than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4649"/>
what

          <app from="pr4649" n="233.6 (308.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6619">
            <lem wit="A Cent">what</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6620">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that undertaker

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4650"/>
was

          <app from="pr4650" n="233.7 (308.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6621">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6622">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y23301">
          <graphic url="y23301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4651"/>
            <hi rend="italic">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">he had a rat!</hi>
”

            </hi>
            <app from="pr4651" n="233 caption" type="e" xml:id="la6623">
              <lem wit="C">
“

                <hi rend="italic">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">he had a rat</hi>
!

                </hi>
”

              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6624">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A Cent">
“

                <hi rend="smallcaps">he had a rat</hi>
!”

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57424">
Well, the funeral sermon was very good, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4652"/>
pison-long

          <app from="pr4652" n="233.8 (308.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la6625">
            <lem wit="C">pison-long</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
pison-

              <lb/>
long

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">pison long</rdg>
          </app>
and tiresome; and then the king he shoved in and got off some of his usual

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4653"/>
rubbage,

          <app from="pr4653" n="233.10 (308.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6626">
            <lem wit="A">rubbage,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rot,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">rubbage;</rdg>
          </app>
and at last the job was through, and the undertaker begun to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2226"/>
sneak up on

          <ptr target="#l11938" type="alt" xml:id="te2226"/>
the coffin with his screw-driver. I was in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4654"/>
sweat,

          <app from="pr4654" n="233.12 (309.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6627">
            <lem wit="MS2">sweat,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
sweat

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4655"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2227"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l11939" type="alt" xml:id="te2227"/>
          <app from="pr4655" n="233.12 (309.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6628">
            <lem wit="A Cent">then</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">now</rdg>
          </app>
, and watched him pretty keen. But he never meddled at all; just slid the lid along,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4656"/>
as soft as mush,

          <app from="pr4656" n="233.13 (309.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6629">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">as soft as mush,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6630">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and screwed it down tight and fast. So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4657"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2228"/>
there

          <ptr target="#l11940" type="alt" xml:id="te2228"/>
          <app from="pr4657" n="233.15 (309.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6631">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">there</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">there,</rdg>
          </app>
I was! I didn’t know whether the money was in there or not. So, says I,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4658"/>
spose

          <app from="pr4658" n="233.15 (309.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6632">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">spose</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">s’pose</rdg>
          </app>
somebody has hogged that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4659"/>
bag,

          <app from="pr4659" n="233.15 (309.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6633">
            <lem wit="MS2">bag,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
bag

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
on the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2229"/>
sly?

          <ptr target="#l11941" type="alt" xml:id="te2229"/>
—now how do

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know whether to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4660"/>
write to

          <app from="pr4660" n="233.16 (309.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6634">
            <lem wit="A Cent">write to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">write</rdg>
          </app>
Mary Jane or not?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4661"/>
Spose

          <app from="pr4661" n="233.17 (309.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6635">
            <lem wit="MS2">Spose</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’Spose</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">S’pose</rdg>
          </app>
she dug him up and didn’t find nothing—what would she think of me? Blame it, I says, I might get hunted up and jailed;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4662"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr4662" n="233.18 (310.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6636">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I</rdg>
          </app>
better lay low and keep dark, and not write at all; the thing’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2230"/>
awful

          <ptr target="#l11942" type="alt" xml:id="te2230"/>
mixed, now; trying to better it, I’ve worsened it a hundred

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4663"/>
times, and I wish to goodness I’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4664"/>
just

          <app from="pr4664" n="233.21 (310.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6638">
            <lem wit="A">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a just</rdg>
          </app>
let it alone, dad fetch the whole business!

          <app from="pr4663" n="233.20–22 (310.6–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6637">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">times, and . . . business!</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">times.</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57561">
They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4665"/>
buried

          <app from="pr4665" n="233.23 (310.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6639">
            <lem wit="A Cent">buried</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">planted</rdg>
          </app>
him, and we come back home, and I went to

          <pb n="234" xml:id="pb0234"/>
watching faces again—I couldn’t help it, and I couldn’t rest easy. But nothing come of it; the faces didn’t tell me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4666"/>
nothing.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57573">
The

          <app from="pr4666" n="234.2–3 (310.16–311.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6640">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing. [¶] The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
nothing.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6641">extra line space</note>
[¶] The

            </rdg>
          </app>
king he visited

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4667"/>
around,

          <app from="pr4667" n="234.3 (311.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6642">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
around

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the evening, and sweetened

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4668"/>
everybody

          <app from="pr4668" n="234.3–4 (311.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6643">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">everybody</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">every body</rdg>
          </app>
up, and made himself ever so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4669"/>
friendly

          <app from="pr4669" n="234.4 (311.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6644">
            <lem wit="A Cent">friendly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">popular</rdg>
          </app>
; and he give out the idea that his congregation over in England would be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4670"/>
in a sweat

          <app from="pr4670" n="234.5 (311.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6645">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">in a sweat</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">worrying</rdg>
          </app>
about him, so he must hurry and settle up the estate right away, and leave for home. He was very sorry he was so pushed, and so was everybody; they wished he could stay longer, but they said they could see it couldn’t be done. And he said of course him and William would take the girls home with them; and that pleased

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4671"/>
everybody

          <app from="pr4671" n="234.10 (312.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6646">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">everybody</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">everybody,</rdg>
          </app>
too, because then the girls would be well fixed, and amongst their own relations; and it pleased the girls, too—tickled them so they clean forgot they ever had a trouble in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4672"/>
world,

          <app from="pr4672" n="234.13 (312.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6647">
            <lem wit="Cent">world,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">world;</rdg>
          </app>
and told him to sell out as quick as he wanted to, they would be ready.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2231"/>
Them poor

          <ptr target="#l11943" type="alt" xml:id="te2231"/>
things was that glad and happy it made my heart ache to see them getting fooled and lied

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4673"/>
to,

          <app from="pr4673" n="234.16 (312.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6648">
            <lem wit="MS2">to,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
to

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
so, but I didn’t see no safe way for me to chip

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2232"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l11944" type="alt" xml:id="te2232"/>
and change the general tune.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57652">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4674"/>
Well,

          <app from="pr4674" n="234.18 (313.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6649">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Well,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Well, sir, I’m</rdg>
          </app>
blamed if the king didn’t bill the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2233"/>
house and the niggers and

          <ptr target="#l11945" type="alt" xml:id="te2233"/>
all the property for auction straight off—sale two days after the funeral; but anybody could buy private beforehand if they wanted to.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57665">
So the next day after the funeral, along about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4675"/>
noontime

          <app from="pr4675" n="234.22 (313.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la6650">
            <lem wit="A">noontime</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
noon-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">noon-time</rdg>
          </app>
, the girls’ joy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4676"/>
got the

          <app from="pr4676" n="234.23 (313.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6651">
            <lem wit="A Cent">got the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">got its</rdg>
          </app>
first

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4677"/>
jolt:

          <app from="pr4677" n="234.23 (313.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6652">
            <lem wit="MS2">jolt:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">jolt;</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2234"/>
couple of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4678"/>
nigger traders

          <app from="pr4678" n="234.23 (313.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6653">
            <lem wit="A">nigger traders</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">traders</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">nigger-traders</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11946" type="alt" xml:id="te2234"/>
come along, and the king sold

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2235"/>
them the

          <ptr target="#l11947" type="alt" xml:id="te2235"/>
niggers

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2236"/>
reasonable, for three-day drafts

          <ptr target="#l11948" type="alt" xml:id="te2236"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4679"/>
as they called it

          <app from="pr4679" n="234.24–25 (313.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6654">
            <lem wit="A Cent">as they called it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6655">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, and away they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4680"/>
went—

          <app from="pr4680" n="234.25 (313.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6656">
            <lem wit="MS2">went—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">went,</rdg>
          </app>
the two sons up the river to Memphis, and their mother down the river to Orleans. I thought them poor girls and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2237"/>
them

          <ptr target="#l11949" type="alt" xml:id="te2237"/>
niggers would break their hearts for grief; they cried around each other, and took

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2238"/>
on so it

          <ptr target="#l11950" type="alt" xml:id="te2238"/>
most made me down sick to see it. The girls said they hadn’t ever dreamed of seeing the family separated or sold away from the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4681"/>
town

          <app from="pr4681" n="234.30 (314.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6657">
            <lem wit="A Cent">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">village</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="ptt012"/>
I can’t ever get it out of my memory

          <ptr target="#as0222" type="an" xml:id="an0011"/>
, the sight of them poor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4682"/>
miserable

          <app from="pr4682" n="234.31 (314.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6658">
            <lem wit="A Cent">miserable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6659">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
girls and niggers hanging around each other’s necks and crying; and I reckon

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2239"/>
I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4683"/>
a stood

          <app from="pr4683" n="234.32 (315.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6660">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a stood</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ stood</rdg>
          </app>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4684"/>
all

          <app from="pr4684" n="234.33 (315.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6661">
            <lem wit="A">all</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">at all</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">all,</rdg>
          </app>
but would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4685"/>
a had

          <app from="pr4685" n="234.33 (315.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6662">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a had</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ had</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11951" type="alt" xml:id="te2239"/>
to bust out and tell on our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4686"/>
gang

          <app from="pr4686" n="234.33 (315.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6663">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">gang</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">gang,</rdg>
          </app>
if I hadn’t knowed the sale warn’t no account and the niggers would be back home in a week or two.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57804">
The thing made a big stir in the town, too, and a good many come out

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2240"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4687"/>
flatfooted

          <app from="pr4687" n="234.37 (315.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6664">
            <lem wit="MS2">flatfooted</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
flat-

              <lb/>
footed

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">flat-footed</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11952" type="alt" xml:id="te2240"/>
and said it was scandalous to separate the mother and the children that way. It injured the frauds

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4688"/>
some,

          <app from="pr4688" n="234.38 (315.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6665">
            <lem wit="MS2">some,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">some;</rdg>
          </app>
but the old fool he

          <pb n="235" xml:id="pb0235"/>
bulled right along, spite of all the duke could say or do, and I tell you the duke was powerful uneasy.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57828">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2241"/>
Next day

          <ptr target="#l11953" type="alt" xml:id="te2241"/>
was auction day. About

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4689"/>
broad-day

          <app from="pr4689" n="235.3 (316.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6666">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">broad-day</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">broad day</rdg>
          </app>
in the morning, the king and the duke come up in the garret and woke me up, and I see by their look that there was trouble. The

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2242"/>
king

          <ptr target="#l11954" type="alt" xml:id="te2242"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57845">“Was you in my room night before last?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57847">
“No,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4690"/>
your majesty

          <app from="pr4690" n="235.7 (317.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6667">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">your majesty</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Your Majesty</rdg>
          </app>
”—which was the way I always

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4691"/>
called

          <app from="pr4691" n="235.7 (317.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6668">
            <lem wit="A Cent">called</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">had to call</rdg>
          </app>
him when nobody but our gang warn’t around.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y23501">
          <graphic url="y23501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">was you in my room?</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57872">
“Was you in there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="rp4693"/>
yisterday

          <app from="rp4693" n="235.9 (317.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="al6701">
            <lem wit="A Cent">yisterday</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yesterday</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4693"/>
er

          <app from="pr4693" n="235.9 (317.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6670">
            <lem wit="A Cent">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or</rdg>
          </app>
last night?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57889">
“No,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4694"/>
your majesty

          <app from="pr4694" n="235.10 (317.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6671">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">your majesty</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Your Majesty</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57899">“Honor bright, now—no lies.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57901">
“Honor bright,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4695"/>
your majesty,

          <app from="pr4695" n="235.12 (317.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6672">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">your majesty,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Your Majesty;</rdg>
          </app>
I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4696"/>
telling

          <app from="pr4696" n="235.12 (317.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6673">
            <lem wit="A Cent">telling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a telling</rdg>
          </app>
you the truth. I hain’t been anear your room since Miss Mary Jane took you and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2243"/>
the duke

          <ptr target="#l11955" type="alt" xml:id="te2243"/>
and showed it to you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57924">The duke says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57926">“Have you seen anybody else go in there?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57928">
          <pb n="236" xml:id="pb0236"/>
“No, your grace, not as I remember, I believe.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57930">“Stop and think.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57932">
I studied

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4697"/>
a while

          <app from="pr4697" n="236.3 (318.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6674">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2244"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4698"/>
see

          <app from="pr4698" n="236.3 (318.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6675">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I see</rdg>
          </app>
my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4699"/>
chance;

          <app from="pr4699" n="236.3 (318.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6676">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">chance;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">chance,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11956" type="alt" xml:id="te2244"/>
then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2245"/>
I says

          <ptr target="#l11957" type="alt" xml:id="te2245"/>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57966">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4700"/>
I see

          <app from="pr4700" n="236.4 (318.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6677">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’ve seen</rdg>
          </app>
the niggers go in there several

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4701"/>
times.

          <app from="pr4701" n="236.4 (318.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6678">
            <lem wit="A Cent">times.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">times?</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e57985">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2246"/>
Both of them give a little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4702"/>
jump;

          <app from="pr4702" n="236.5 (318verso.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6679">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">jump;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">jump,</rdg>
          </app>
and looked like they hadn’t ever expected it, and then like they

          <hi rend="italic">had.</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2247"/>
Then

          <ptr target="#l11959" type="alt" xml:id="te2247"/>
the duke says:

          <ptr target="#l11958" type="alt" xml:id="te2246"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58004">
“What,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2248"/>
          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11960" type="alt" xml:id="te2248"/>
of them?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58011">
“No—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4703"/>
leastways

          <app from="pr4703" n="236.8 (318.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6680">
            <lem wit="A Cent">leastways</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">at least</rdg>
          </app>
not all at once. That is, I don’t think I ever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2249"/>
see

          <ptr target="#l11961" type="alt" xml:id="te2249"/>
them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4704"/>
all

          <app from="pr4704" n="236.9 (319.1–3)" type="e" xml:id="la6681">
            <lem wit="A Cent">all</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
all go

              <hi rend="italic">in</hi>
at once; and I believe I never see them all

            </rdg>
          </app>
come

          <hi rend="italic">out</hi>
at once but just one time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58040">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4705"/>
Hello—when

          <app from="pr4705" n="236.10 (319.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6682">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Hello—when</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">When</rdg>
          </app>
was that?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58050">“It was the day we had the funeral. In the morning. It warn’t early, because I overslept. I was just starting down the ladder, and I see them.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58052">
“Well, go on,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2250"/>
          <hi rend="italic">go</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4706"/>
on

          <ptr target="#l11962" type="alt" xml:id="te2250"/>
—what

          <app from="pr4706" n="236.14 (319.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6683">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">on—what</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">on. What</rdg>
          </app>
did they do?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4707"/>
how’d

          <app from="pr4707" n="236.14 (319.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6684">
            <lem wit="C">how’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">how did</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">How’d</rdg>
          </app>
they act?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58078">
“They didn’t do nothing. And they didn’t act anyway, much, as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4708"/>
fur

          <app from="pr4708" n="236.16 (319.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6685">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
as I see. They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4709"/>
tip-toed

          <app from="pr4709" n="236.16 (319.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6686">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">tip-toed</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">tiptoed</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2251"/>
away;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4710"/>
so,

          <app from="pr4710" n="236.16 (320.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6687">
            <lem wit="MS2">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l11963" type="alt" xml:id="te2251"/>
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2252"/>
seen,

          <ptr target="#l11964" type="alt" xml:id="te2252"/>
easy enough, that they’d shoved in there to do up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4711"/>
your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2253"/>
majesty’s

          <ptr target="#l11965" type="alt" xml:id="te2253"/>
          <app from="pr4711" n="236.17 (320.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6688">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">your majesty’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Your Majesty’s</rdg>
          </app>
room, or something,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4712"/>
sposing

          <app from="pr4712" n="236.17 (320.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6689">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">sposing</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">s’posing</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4713"/>
was up;

          <app from="pr4713" n="236.18 (320.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6690">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">was up;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">was up,</rdg>
          </app>
and found you

          <hi rend="italic">warn’t</hi>
up, and so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2254"/>
they

          <ptr target="#l11966" type="alt" xml:id="te2254"/>
was hoping to slide out of the way of trouble

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2255"/>
without

          <ptr target="#l11967" type="alt" xml:id="te2255"/>
waking you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4714"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2256"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l11968" type="alt" xml:id="te2256"/>
, if they hadn’t already waked you up

          <app from="pr4714" n="236.19–20 (320.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6691">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">up, if . . . up</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">up</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58163">
“Great

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4715"/>
guns,

          <app from="pr4715" n="236.21 (320.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6692">
            <lem wit="A Cent">guns,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">guns!</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
is a go!” says the king; and both of them looked pretty sick, and tolerable silly. They stood there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4716"/>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2257"/>
thinking

          <ptr target="#l11969" type="alt" xml:id="te2257"/>
          <app from="pr4716" n="236.22 (320.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6693">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a thinking</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-thinking</rdg>
          </app>
and scratching their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4717"/>
heads,

          <app from="pr4717" n="236.23 (320.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6694">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">heads,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
heads

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a minute, and then the duke he bust into a kind of a little raspy chuckle, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58195">
“It does beat all, how neat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4718"/>
the

          <app from="pr4718" n="236.25 (321.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6695">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them</rdg>
          </app>
niggers played their hand. They let on to be

          <hi rend="italic">sorry</hi>
they was going out of this

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2258"/>
region!

          <ptr target="#l11970" type="alt" xml:id="te2258"/>
and I believed they

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
sorry. And so did you, and so did everybody. Don’t ever tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4719"/>
          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
,

          <app from="pr4719" n="236.27 (321.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6696">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4720"/>
any more,

          <app from="pr4720" n="236.28 (321.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6697">
            <lem wit="C">any more,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">no more,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">any more</rdg>
          </app>
that a nigger

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4721"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr4721" n="236.28 (321.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6698">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hain’t</rdg>
          </app>
got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4722"/>
any histrionic

          <app from="pr4722" n="236.28 (321.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6699">
            <lem wit="A Cent">any histrionic</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">no histeronic</rdg>
          </app>
talent. Why, the way they played that thing, it would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4723"/>
fool

          <app from="pr4723" n="236.29 (321.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6700">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fool</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a fooled</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4724"/>
          <hi rend="italic">anybody</hi>
          <app from="pr4724" n="236.29 (321.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la6701">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">anybody</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
-

              <lb/>
body

            </rdg>
          </app>
. In my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4725"/>
opinion,

          <app from="pr4725" n="236.29 (321.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6702">
            <lem wit="MS2">opinion,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
opinion

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
there’s a fortune in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4726"/>
’em

          <app from="pr4726" n="236.30 (321.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6703">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them niggers</rdg>
          </app>
. If I had capital and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4727"/>
theatre

          <app from="pr4727" n="236.30 (321.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6704">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">theatre</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">theater</rdg>
          </app>
, I wouldn’t want

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4728"/>
a better

          <app from="pr4728" n="236.30–31 (321.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6705">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a better</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">no better</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4729"/>
layout

          <app from="pr4729" n="236.31 (321.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6706">
            <lem wit="MS2">layout</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lay out</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">lay-out</rdg>
          </app>
than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4730"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2259"/>
that

          <ptr target="#l11971" type="alt" xml:id="te2259"/>
—and

          <app from="pr4730" n="236.31 (321.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6707">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">that—and</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">that. And</rdg>
          </app>
here we’ve

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2260"/>
gone and

          <ptr target="#l11972" type="alt" xml:id="te2260"/>
sold ’em for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4731"/>
song. Yes

          <app from="pr4731" n="236.32 (322.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6708">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">song. Yes</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">song—yes</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2261"/>
and ain’t

          <ptr target="#l11973" type="alt" xml:id="te2261"/>
privileged to sing the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4732"/>
song,

          <app from="pr4732" n="236.32 (322.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6709">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">song,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
song

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4733"/>
yet

          <app from="pr4733" n="236.32 (322.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6710">
            <lem wit="A Cent">yet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">yet</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. Say, where

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4734"/>
song?—

          <app from="pr4734" n="236.33 (322.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6711">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">song?—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
song

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
—

            </rdg>
          </app>
that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4735"/>
draft.

          <app from="pr4735" n="236.33 (322.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6712">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">draft.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">draft?</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58385">
“In the bank for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4736"/>
to be collected

          <app from="pr4736" n="236.34 (322.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la6713">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to be collected</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">collection</rdg>
          </app>
. Where

          <hi rend="italic">would</hi>
it be?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58398">
“Well,

          <hi rend="italic">that’s</hi>
all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4737"/>
right,

          <app from="pr4737" n="236.35 (322.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6714">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then, thank goodness.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58412">
Says I, kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4738"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2262"/>
timid-like

          <ptr target="#l11974" type="alt" xml:id="te2262"/>
:

          <app from="pr4738" n="236.36 (322.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6715">
            <lem wit="A Cent">timid-like:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
timid-like

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6716">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58426">
“Is something gone

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2263"/>
wrong?

          <ptr target="#l11975" type="alt" xml:id="te2263"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58432">The king whirls on me and rips out:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58434">
          <pb n="237" xml:id="pb0237"/>
“None o’ your business! You keep your head shet, and mind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4739"/>
y’r

          <app from="pr4739" n="237.1 (323.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6717">
            <lem wit="A Cent">y’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your</rdg>
          </app>
own affairs—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4740"/>
if you

          <app from="pr4740" n="237.2 (323.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6718">
            <lem wit="A Cent">if you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ef you’ve</rdg>
          </app>
got any. Long as you’re in this town, don’t you forgit

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4741"/>
          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
,

          <app from="pr4741" n="237.3 (323.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6719">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
—

            </rdg>
          </app>
you hear?” Then he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2264"/>
says

          <ptr target="#l11976" type="alt" xml:id="te2264"/>
to the duke, “We got to jest swaller it, and say

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2265"/>
noth’n:

          <ptr target="#l11977" type="alt" xml:id="te2265"/>
mum’s the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4742"/>
word,

          <app from="pr4742" n="237.4 (323.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6720">
            <lem wit="MS2">word,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
word

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for

          <hi rend="italic">us.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58487">
As they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4743"/>
was starting

          <app from="pr4743" n="237.5 (323.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6721">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was starting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">started</rdg>
          </app>
down the ladder, the duke he chuckles again, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4744"/>
says

          <app from="pr4744" n="237.6 (323.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6722">
            <lem wit="A Cent">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rasps out</rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58505">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0012"/>
Quick sales

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4745"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2266"/>
          <hi rend="italic">and</hi>
          <ptr target="#l11978" type="alt" xml:id="te2266"/>
small

          <app from="pr4745" n="237.7 (323.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6723">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">and</hi>
small

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
and

              <hi rend="italic">small</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
profits

          <ptr target="#as0223" type="an" xml:id="an0012"/>
! It’s a good

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4746"/>
business

          <app from="pr4746" n="237.7 (323.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la6724">
            <lem wit="A Cent">business</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">business motto</rdg>
          </app>
—yes.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58536">
The king snarls around on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4747"/>
him

          <app from="pr4747" n="237.8 (323.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6725">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">him</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">him,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4748"/>
says:

          <app from="pr4748" n="237.8 (323.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6726">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">says,</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58553">
“I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4749"/>
trying

          <app from="pr4749" n="237.9 (323.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6727">
            <lem wit="A Cent">trying</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tryin’</rdg>
          </app>
to do for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4750"/>
best,

          <app from="pr4750" n="237.9 (324.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6728">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">best,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
best

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4751"/>
sellin’

          <app from="pr4751" n="237.9 (324.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6729">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sellin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">selling</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4752"/>
’m

          <app from="pr4752" n="237.9 (324.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6730">
            <lem wit="A Cent">’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’em</rdg>
          </app>
out so quick. If the profits has turned out to be none, lackin’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4753"/>
considable

          <app from="pr4753" n="237.10 (324.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6731">
            <lem wit="A Cent">considable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
, and none to carry, is it my fault any more’n it’s yourn?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58595">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4754"/>
          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
’d

          <app from="pr4754" n="237.12 (324.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6732">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">they’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
be in this house yet, and we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4755"/>
          <hi rend="italic">wouldn’t</hi>
,

          <app from="pr4755" n="237.12 (324.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6733">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">wouldn’t</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">wouldn’t</hi>
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
if I could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4756"/>
a got

          <app from="pr4756" n="237.12–13 (324.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6734">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a got</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ got</rdg>
          </app>
my advice listened to.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58633">
The king sassed back, as much as was safe for him, and then swapped around and lit into

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
again. He give me down the banks for not coming and

          <hi rend="italic">telling</hi>
him I see the niggers come out of his room acting that way—said any fool would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4757"/>
a

          <hi rend="italic">knowed</hi>
          <app from="pr4757" n="237.17 (325.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6735">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">
a

              <hi rend="italic">knowed</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
’a’

              <hi rend="italic">knowed</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
something was up. And then waltzed in and cussed

          <hi rend="italic">himself</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4758"/>
a while

          <app from="pr4758" n="237.18 (325.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6736">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
; and said it all come of him not laying late and taking his natural rest that morning, and he’d be blamed if he’d ever do it again. So they went off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4759"/>
a-jawing; and I felt dreadful glad

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4760"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr4760" n="237.21 (325.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6738">
            <lem wit="A">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I had</rdg>
          </app>
worked it all off onto the niggers and yet hadn’t done the niggers

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4761"/>
no

          <app from="pr4761" n="237.22 (325.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6739">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">any</rdg>
          </app>
harm by it

          <app from="pr4759" n="237.21–22 (325.12–16)" type="e" xml:id="la6737">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-jawing; and . . . it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a jawing; and . . . it</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-jawing</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y23701">
          <graphic url="y23701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4762"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">jawing.</hi>
            <app from="pr4762" n="237 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la6740">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">jawing.</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6741">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="Cent">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">a coolness between friends</hi>
.

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0395">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXVIII.</head>
        <pb n="238" xml:id="pb0238"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y23801">
          <graphic url="y23801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4763"/>
Chapter XXVIII.

            <app from="pr4763" n="238 title (326.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6742">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXVIII.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6743">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">By</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2381">
          <graphic url="hf2381.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">in trouble</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e58729">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4764"/>
          <sic>and by</sic>
          <app from="pr4764" n="238.1 (326.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6744">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="Aa">By and-by</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Ab Can">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
it was getting-up time; so I come down the ladder and started for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4765"/>
down stairs

          <app from="pr4765" n="238.3 (326.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6745">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">down stairs</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
down-

              <lb/>
stairs

            </rdg>
          </app>
, but as I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2267"/>
come

          <ptr target="#l11979" type="alt" xml:id="te2267"/>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2268"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4766"/>
girls’

          <ptr target="#l11980" type="alt" xml:id="te2268"/>
          <app from="pr4766" n="238.4 (326.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6746">
            <lem wit="A Cent">girls’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">girls’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4767"/>
room,

          <app from="pr4767" n="238.4 (326.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6747">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">room,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
room

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the door was open, and I see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2269"/>
Mary Jane

          <ptr target="#l11981" type="alt" xml:id="te2269"/>
setting by her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2270"/>
old hair

          <ptr target="#l11982" type="alt" xml:id="te2270"/>
trunk, which was open and she’d been packing things in it—getting ready to go to England. But she had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4768"/>
stopped,

          <app from="pr4768" n="238.10 (326.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6748">
            <lem wit="MS2">stopped,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
stopped

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, with a folded gown in her lap, and had her face in her hands, crying.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4769"/>
I felt awful bad to see it; of course anybody would.

          <app from="pr4769" n="238.13–14 (326.13–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6749">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">I . . . would.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6750">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I went in there, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58801">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2271"/>
“Miss Mary Jane, you can’t abear to see people in trouble, and

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
can’t—most always. Tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4770"/>
me

          <app from="pr4770" n="238.18 (327.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6751">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">em</rdg>
          </app>
about it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58815">
So she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4771"/>
done it

          <app from="pr4771" n="238.19 (327.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6752">
            <lem wit="A Cent">done it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">did</rdg>
          </app>
. And it was the niggers—I just expected it.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2272"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4772"/>
She said

          <app from="pr4772" n="238.19 (327.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6753">
            <lem wit="A Cent">She said</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Said</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <ptr target="#l11984" type="alt" xml:id="te2272"/>
beautiful trip to England was most about spoiled for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4773"/>
her; she didn’t know

          <hi rend="italic">how</hi>
she was ever going to be happy there, knowing the mother and the children warn’t ever going to see each other no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2273"/>
more—

          <ptr target="#l11985" type="alt" xml:id="te2273"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2274"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l11986" type="alt" xml:id="te2274"/>
busted out bitterer

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2275"/>
than

          <ptr target="#l11987" type="alt" xml:id="te2275"/>
ever, and flung up her hands and says:

          <app from="pr4773" n="238.20–24 (327.10–328.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6754">
            <lem wit="MS2">her; she . . . hands and says:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">her; she . . . hands, and says</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">her</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58862">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4774"/>
O

          <app from="pr4774" n="238.25 (328.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6755">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4775"/>
dear, dear,

          <app from="pr4775" n="238.25 (328.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6756">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">dear, dear,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">dear, dear!</rdg>
          </app>
to think they ain’t

          <hi rend="italic">ever</hi>
going to see each other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4776"/>
any more

          <app from="pr4776" n="238.25–26 (328.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6757">
            <lem wit="A Cent">any more</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">again</rdg>
          </app>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58892">
“But they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4777"/>
          <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
—

          <app from="pr4777" n="238.27 (328.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6758">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
—

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">will!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and inside of two weeks—and I

          <hi rend="italic">know</hi>
it!”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4778"/>
says I.

          <app from="pr4778" n="238.27 (328.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6759">
            <lem wit="A Cent">says I.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6760">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58918">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4779"/>
Laws,

          <app from="pr4779" n="238.28 (328.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6761">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">Laws,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Laws

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
it was out before I could

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2276"/>
think!

          <ptr target="#l11988" type="alt" xml:id="te2276"/>
—and before I could budge,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4780"/>
she throws

          <app from="pr4780" n="238.29 (328.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6762">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she throws</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">slam</hi>
comes

            </rdg>
          </app>
her arms around my neck, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4781"/>
told

          <app from="pr4781" n="238.29 (328.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la6763">
            <lem wit="A Cent">told</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">she kissed me right on the mouth, and told</rdg>
          </app>
me to say it

          <hi rend="italic">again</hi>
, say it

          <hi rend="italic">again</hi>
, say it

          <hi rend="italic">again!</hi>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e58958">
          <pb n="239" xml:id="pb0239"/>
I see I had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4782"/>
spoke

          <ptr target="#l11983" type="alt" xml:id="te2271"/>
too sudden, and said too much

          <app from="pr4782" n="239.1 (328.15–329.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6764">
            <lem wit="A Cent">spoke . . . much</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">shot my mouth off once too often</rdg>
          </app>
, and was in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4783"/>
close

          <app from="pr4783" n="239.1 (329.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6765">
            <lem wit="A Cent">close</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mighty close</rdg>
          </app>
place. I asked her to let me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4784"/>
think,

          <app from="pr4784" n="239.2 (329.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6766">
            <lem wit="MS2">think,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
think

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a minute; and she set there,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4785"/>
very

          <app from="pr4785" n="239.2 (329.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6767">
            <lem wit="A Cent">very</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mighty</rdg>
          </app>
impatient and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4786"/>
excited

          <app from="pr4786" n="239.3 (329.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6768">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">excited</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">excited,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4787"/>
handsome

          <app from="pr4787" n="239.3 (329.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6769">
            <lem wit="A Cent">handsome</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">beautiful</rdg>
          </app>
, but looking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4788"/>
kind of

          <app from="pr4788" n="239.3 (329.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6770">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kind of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kinder</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2277"/>
happy and eased-up, like a person that’s had a tooth pulled out.

          <ptr target="#l11989" type="alt" xml:id="te2277"/>
So I went to studying it out. I says to myself,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2278"/>
I reckon

          <ptr target="#l11990" type="alt" xml:id="te2278"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2279"/>
a body

          <ptr target="#l11991" type="alt" xml:id="te2279"/>
that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2280"/>
ups and

          <ptr target="#l11992" type="alt" xml:id="te2280"/>
tells the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2281"/>
truth

          <ptr target="#l11993" type="alt" xml:id="te2281"/>
when he is in a tight place, is taking considerable many

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4789"/>
resks;

          <app from="pr4789" n="239.7 (329.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6771">
            <lem wit="C">resks;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">risks;</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">resks,</rdg>
          </app>
though I ain’t had no experience, and can’t say for certain; but it looks so to me, anyway; and yet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4790"/>
here’s

          <app from="pr4790" n="239.8 (329.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6772">
            <lem wit="A Cent">here’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">here’s</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a case where I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4791"/>
blest

          <app from="pr4791" n="239.8 (329.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6773">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blamed</rdg>
          </app>
if it don’t look to me like the truth is

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2282"/>
better

          <ptr target="#l11994" type="alt" xml:id="te2282"/>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4792"/>
actuly

          <app from="pr4792" n="239.9 (330.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6774">
            <lem wit="A">actuly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">actually</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">actully</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">safer</hi>
, than a lie. I must lay it by in my mind, and think it over some time or other, it’s so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4793"/>
kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2283"/>
strange

          <ptr target="#l11995" type="alt" xml:id="te2283"/>
          <app from="pr4793" n="239.11 (330.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6775">
            <lem wit="A Cent">kind of strange</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">curious</rdg>
          </app>
and unregular. I never see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4794"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr4794" n="239.11 (330.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6776">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
like it. Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4795"/>
I says

          <app from="pr4795" n="239.12 (330.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6777">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says I</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4796"/>
myself,

          <app from="pr4796" n="239.12 (330.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6778">
            <lem wit="MS2">myself,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
myself

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at last,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4797"/>
I’m agoing to

          <app from="pr4797" n="239.12 (330.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la6779">
            <lem wit="A">I’m agoing to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dog my cats if I don’t</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">I’m a-going to</rdg>
          </app>
chance it; I’ll up and tell the truth this time,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4798"/>
though

          <app from="pr4798" n="239.13 (330.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la6780">
            <lem wit="A Cent">though</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or bust—though</rdg>
          </app>
it does seem most like setting down on a kag of powder and touching it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4799"/>
off,

          <app from="pr4799" n="239.14 (330.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6781">
            <lem wit="MS2">off,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
off

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4800"/>
just

          <app from="pr4800" n="239.14 (330.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6782">
            <lem wit="A Cent">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">just out of curiosity</rdg>
          </app>
to see where

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4801"/>
you’ll

          <app from="pr4801" n="239.14 (330.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6783">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
you

              <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
go to. Then I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59166">
“Miss Mary Jane, is there any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4802"/>
place,

          <app from="pr4802" n="239.16 (331.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6784">
            <lem wit="MS2">place,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
place

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
out of town

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2284"/>
a little ways,

          <ptr target="#l11996" type="alt" xml:id="te2284"/>
where you could go and stay three or four days?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59181">“Yes—Mr. Lothrop’s. Why?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59183">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4803"/>
Never

          <app from="pr4803" n="239.19 (331.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6785">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Never</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Never you</rdg>
          </app>
mind why, yet. If

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2285"/>
I’ll

          <ptr target="#l11997" type="alt" xml:id="te2285"/>
tell you how I know the niggers will see each other again—inside of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2286"/>
two

          <ptr target="#l11998" type="alt" xml:id="te2286"/>
weeks—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4804"/>
here,

          <app from="pr4804" n="239.20 (331.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6786">
            <lem wit="C">here,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">here</hi>
,

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">here</rdg>
          </app>
in this house—and

          <hi rend="italic">prove</hi>
how I know it—will you go to Mr. Lothrop’s and stay four days?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59217">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2287"/>
“Four days

          <ptr target="#l11999" type="alt" xml:id="te2287"/>
!”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2288"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l12000" type="alt" xml:id="te2288"/>
says; “I’ll stay a year!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59226">
“All right,” I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4805"/>
says,

          <app from="pr4805" n="239.24 (331.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6787">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">says,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says;</rdg>
          </app>
“I don’t want nothing more out of

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
than just your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4806"/>
word

          <app from="pr4806" n="239.25 (332.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6788">
            <lem wit="A Cent">word</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">word</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4807"/>
I druther

          <app from="pr4807" n="239.25 (332.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6789">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I druther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’d druther</rdg>
          </app>
have it than another man’s kiss-the-Bible.” She smiled, and reddened up very sweet, and I says, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4808"/>
if

          <app from="pr4808" n="239.26 (332.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6790">
            <lem wit="MS2">if</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">If</rdg>
          </app>
you don’t mind it, I’ll shut the door—and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2289"/>
bolt

          <ptr target="#l12001" type="alt" xml:id="te2289"/>
it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59269">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4809"/>
Then I come back and set down again, and

          <app from="pr4809" n="239.28 (332.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6791">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Then I come . . . again, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Which I done. Then I</rdg>
          </app>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59278">
“Don’t you holler. Just set still, and take it like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4810"/>
man

          <app from="pr4810" n="239.29 (332.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6792">
            <lem wit="A Cent">man</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">major</rdg>
          </app>
. I got to tell the truth, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4811"/>
you want to brace up, Miss Mary, because it

          <app from="pr4811" n="239.30–31 (332.13–15)" type="e" xml:id="la6793">
            <lem wit="A Cent">you want . . . it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it ain’t got no resemblance to pie, neither, so don’t you be disappointed</rdg>
          </app>
’s a bad kind, and going to be hard to take, but there ain’t no help for it. These uncles of yourn ain’t no uncles at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4812"/>
all—

          <app from="pr4812" n="239.32 (332.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6794">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">all—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">all;</rdg>
          </app>
they’re a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4813"/>
couple

          <app from="pr4813" n="239.32 (333.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6795">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">couple</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">couples</rdg>
          </app>
of frauds—regular dead-beats. There,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4814"/>
now,

          <app from="pr4814" n="239.33 (333.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6796">
            <lem wit="MS2">now,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
now

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
we’re over the worst of it—you can stand the rest

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2290"/>
middling

          <ptr target="#l12002" type="alt" xml:id="te2290"/>
easy.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59326">
It jolted her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4815"/>
up,

          <app from="pr4815" n="239.35 (333.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6797">
            <lem wit="MS2">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
like everything, of course; but I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2291"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l12003" type="alt" xml:id="te2291"/>
over the shoal

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4816"/>
water,

          <app from="pr4816" n="239.36 (333.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6798">
            <lem wit="MS2">water,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
water

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, so I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4817"/>
went

          <app from="pr4817" n="239.36 (333.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6799">
            <lem wit="A Cent">went</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">warbled</rdg>
          </app>
right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4818"/>
along,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2292"/>
—

          <app from="pr4818" n="239.36 (333.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6800">
            <lem wit="MS2">along,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
along,

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
her eyes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4819"/>
a-blazing

          <app from="pr4819" n="239.36 (333.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6801">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">a-blazing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a blazing</rdg>
          </app>
higher and higher all the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4820"/>
time—

          <app from="pr4820" n="239.37 (333.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6802">
            <lem wit="MS2">time—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">time,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <ptr target="#l12004" type="alt" xml:id="te2292"/>
told her every blame thing, from where we first struck that young fool going

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2293"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l12005" type="alt" xml:id="te2293"/>
to the steamboat,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4821"/>
clear

          <app from="pr4821" n="239.38 (333.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6803">
            <lem wit="A Cent">clear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">plumb</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="240" xml:id="pb0240"/>
through to where she flung herself onto the king’s breast at the front door and he kissed her sixteen or seventeen

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4822"/>
times—and

          <app from="pr4822" n="240.2 (333.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6804">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">times—and</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">times. And</rdg>
          </app>
then up she jumps, with her face afire like sunset, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59407">
“The brute! Come—don’t waste a minute—not a

          <hi rend="italic">second</hi>
—we’ll have them tarred and feathered, and flung in the river!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="left" xml:id="y24001">
          <graphic url="y24001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">indignation</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59417">Says I:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59419">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2294"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4823"/>
Cert’nly

          <app from="pr4823" n="240.7 (334.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6805">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Cert’nly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Exackly</rdg>
          </app>
. But do

          <ptr target="#l12006" type="alt" xml:id="te2294"/>
you mean,

          <hi rend="italic">before</hi>
you go to Mr. Lothrop’s,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4824"/>
or—

          <app from="pr4824" n="240.8 (334.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6806">
            <lem wit="MS2">or—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">or——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59445">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4825"/>
O,” she says, “what

          <app from="pr4825" n="240.9 (334.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6807">
            <lem wit="C">O,” she says, “what</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">O, what</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh,” she says, “what</rdg>
          </app>
am I

          <hi rend="italic">thinking</hi>
about!” she says, and set right down again. “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4826"/>
Don’t

          <app from="pr4826" n="240.11 (334.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6808">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Don’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
mind what I said—please don’t—you

          <hi rend="italic">won’t</hi>
, now,

          <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4827"/>
you?” laying

          <app from="pr4827" n="240.13 (334.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6809">
            <lem wit="MS2">you?” laying</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you?” Laying</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">you?”—laying</rdg>
          </app>
her silky hand on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4828"/>
mine

          <app from="pr4828" n="240.13 (335.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6810">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">mine</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mind</rdg>
          </app>
in that kind of a way that I said I would die first. “I never thought, I was so stirred up,” she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4829"/>
says; “now

          <app from="pr4829" n="240.16 (335.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6811">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">says; “now</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">says. “Now</rdg>
          </app>
go on, and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2295"/>
won’t

          <ptr target="#l12007" type="alt" xml:id="te2295"/>
do

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2296"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l12008" type="alt" xml:id="te2296"/>
any more. You tell me what to do, and whatever you say, I’ll do it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59510">
“Well,” I says,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2297"/>
“it’s

          <ptr target="#l12009" type="alt" xml:id="te2297"/>
a rough gang, them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2298"/>
two

          <ptr target="#l12010" type="alt" xml:id="te2298"/>
frauds, and I’m fixed so I got to travel with them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4830"/>
a while

          <app from="pr4830" n="240.22 (335.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6812">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
longer, whether I want to or not—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4831"/>
I druther

          <app from="pr4831" n="240.23 (335.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6813">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I druther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">druther</rdg>
          </app>
not tell you why—and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4832"/>
if you was to blow on them this town would get me out of their claws, and

          <app from="pr4832" n="240.24–26 (335.13–16)" type="e" xml:id="la6814">
            <lem wit="A Cent">if you . . . claws, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">although this town would get me out of their hands if you was to blow on them,</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">I’d</hi>
be all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4833"/>
right,

          <app from="pr4833" n="240.26 (335.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6815">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">right;</rdg>
          </app>
but there’d be another person that you don’t know about who’d be in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4834"/>
big

          <app from="pr4834" n="240.28 (336.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6816">
            <lem wit="A Cent">big</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">awful</rdg>
          </app>
trouble. Well, we got to save

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4835"/>
          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
          <app from="pr4835" n="240.28 (336.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6817">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
,

            </rdg>
          </app>
hain’t we? Of course.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4836"/>
Well

          <app from="pr4836" n="240.29 (336.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6818">
            <lem wit="MS2">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
then, we won’t blow on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2299"/>
them.”

          <ptr target="#l12011" type="alt" xml:id="te2299"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59588">
Saying them words put a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4837"/>
good

          <app from="pr4837" n="240.30 (336.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6819">
            <lem wit="A Cent">good</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">first-rate</rdg>
          </app>
idea

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4838"/>
in

          <app from="pr4838" n="240.30 (336.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6820">
            <lem wit="A Cent">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">into</rdg>
          </app>
my head.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2300"/>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4839"/>
see

          <app from="pr4839" n="240.30 (336.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la6821">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">see in a minute</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12012" type="alt" xml:id="te2300"/>
how

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4840"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4840" n="240.30 (336.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6822">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
I could get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4841"/>
me and Jim

          <app from="pr4841" n="240.31 (336.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6823">
            <lem wit="A Cent">me and Jim</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Jim and me</rdg>
          </app>
rid of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4842"/>
the

          <app from="pr4842" n="240.31 (336.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6824">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4843"/>
frauds:

          <app from="pr4843" n="240.31 (336.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6825">
            <lem wit="MS2">frauds:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">frauds;</rdg>
          </app>
get them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4844"/>
jailed,

          <app from="pr4844" n="240.31 (336.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6826">
            <lem wit="MS2">jailed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
jailed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
here, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tz2301"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l12013" type="alt" xml:id="te2301"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4845"/>
leave.

          <app from="pr4845" n="240.32 (336.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6827">
            <lem wit="A Cent">leave.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">give them the slip!</rdg>
          </app>
But I didn’t want to run the raft in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4846"/>
daytime

          <app from="pr4846" n="240.32 (337.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la6828">
            <lem wit="Cent">daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
day-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">day-time</rdg>
          </app>
, without anybody aboard to answer questions but me; so I didn’t want the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4847"/>
plan

          <app from="pr4847" n="240.34 (337.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6829">
            <lem wit="A Cent">plan</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">circus</rdg>
          </app>
to begin

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4848"/>
working

          <app from="pr4848" n="240.34 (337.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6830">
            <lem wit="A Cent">working</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6831">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
till pretty late to-night. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59700">
“Miss Mary Jane, I’ll tell you what we’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2302"/>
do—

          <ptr target="#l12014" type="alt" xml:id="te2302"/>
and you won’t have to stay at Mr. Lothrop’s so long,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4849"/>
nuther

          <app from="pr4849" n="240.36 (337.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6832">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nuther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">neither</rdg>
          </app>
. How

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4850"/>
fur

          <app from="pr4850" n="240.36 (337.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6833">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
is it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59723">
“A little short of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2303"/>
four

          <ptr target="#l12015" type="alt" xml:id="te2303"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2304"/>
miles—right out in the country, back here.”

          <ptr target="#l12016" type="alt" xml:id="te2304"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59731">
“Well, that’ll answer. Now you go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4851"/>
along

          <app from="pr4851" n="240.38 (337.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6834">
            <lem wit="A Cent">along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’long</rdg>
          </app>
out there, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4852"/>
lay low

          <app from="pr4852" n="240.38 (337.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la6835">
            <lem wit="A Cent">lay low</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">just lay low and keep shady</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="241" xml:id="pb0241"/>
till

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2305"/>
nine

          <ptr target="#l12017" type="alt" xml:id="te2305"/>
or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4853"/>
half-past,

          <app from="pr4853" n="241.1 (337.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6836">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">half-past,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">half-past</rdg>
          </app>
to-night, and then get them to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4854"/>
fetch

          <app from="pr4854" n="241.1 (338.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6837">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fetch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rustle</rdg>
          </app>
you home again—tell them you’ve thought of something. If you get here before eleven,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2306"/>
put a candle in this window, and if I don’t turn up,

          <ptr target="#l12018" type="alt" xml:id="te2306"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2307"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4855"/>
wait

          <app from="pr4855" n="241.3 (338.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6838">
            <lem wit="A Cent">wait</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">all right—wait</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12019" type="alt" xml:id="te2307"/>
          <hi rend="italic">till</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4856"/>
eleven,

          <app from="pr4856" n="241.4 (338.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6839">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">eleven,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">eleven;</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4857"/>
          <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
          <app from="pr4857" n="241.4 (338.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6840">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">then</rdg>
          </app>
if I don’t turn

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4858"/>
up,

          <app from="pr4858" n="241.4 (338.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6841">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4859"/>
it means

          <app from="pr4859" n="241.4 (338.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6842">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it means</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">consider that</rdg>
          </app>
I’m gone, and out of the way, and safe. Then you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4860"/>
come

          <app from="pr4860" n="241.5 (338.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6843">
            <lem wit="A Cent">come</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hop</rdg>
          </app>
out and spread the news

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4861"/>
around,

          <app from="pr4861" n="241.5 (338.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6844">
            <lem wit="A Cent">around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6845">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and get these beats jailed.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59837">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4862"/>
Good,” she says, “I’ll

          <app from="pr4862" n="241.7 (338.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6846">
            <lem wit="A">Good,” she says, “I’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Good—I’ll</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Good,” she says. “I’ll</rdg>
          </app>
do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4863"/>
it.

          <app from="pr4863" n="241.7 (338.12)" type="e" xml:id="la6847">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59857">
“And if it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2308"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l12020" type="alt" xml:id="te2308"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4864"/>
happens so

          <app from="pr4864" n="241.8 (338.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6848">
            <lem wit="A Cent">happens so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">so happens</rdg>
          </app>
that I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4865"/>
don’t

          <app from="pr4865" n="241.8 (338.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6849">
            <lem wit="A Cent">don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">miss fire, and don’t</rdg>
          </app>
get away, but get took

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4866"/>
up,

          <app from="pr4866" n="241.8 (338.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6850">
            <lem wit="MS2">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
along with them, you must up and say I told you the whole thing beforehand, and you must stand by me all you can.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59887">
“Stand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4867"/>
by

          <app from="pr4867" n="241.11 (339.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6851">
            <lem wit="A Cent">by</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">by</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4868"/>
you, indeed I will.

          <app from="pr4868" n="241.11 (339.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6852">
            <lem wit="A">you, indeed I will.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you!</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">you! indeed I will.</rdg>
          </app>
They

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4869"/>
shan’t

          <app from="pr4869" n="241.11 (339.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6853">
            <lem wit="MS2">shan’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">sha’n’t</rdg>
          </app>
touch a hair of your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4870"/>
head!” she says, and I see her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2309"/>
nostrils

          <ptr target="#l12021" type="alt" xml:id="te2309"/>
spread and her eyes snap when she said it, too

          <app from="pr4870" n="241.12–13 (339.7–10)" type="e" xml:id="la6854">
            <lem wit="A">head!” she says, and I see . . . snap when she said it, too.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">head!” [¶] Well, I always liked to see . . . snap, that way.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">head!” she says.</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e59930">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2310"/>
“If I get away, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4871"/>
shan’t

          <app from="pr4871" n="241.14 (339.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la6855">
            <lem wit="MS2">shan’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">sha’n’t</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12022" type="alt" xml:id="te2310"/>
be here,” I says, “to prove these rapscallions ain’t your uncles, and I couldn’t do

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2311"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12023" type="alt" xml:id="te2311"/>
if I

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
here. I could swear they was beats and bummers, that’s all; though that’s worth

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4872"/>
something

          <app from="pr4872" n="241.16–17 (340.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6856">
            <lem wit="A Cent">something</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">something</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
. Well, there’s others can do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4873"/>
that,

          <app from="pr4873" n="241.17 (340.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6857">
            <lem wit="MS2">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2312"/>
better

          <ptr target="#l12024" type="alt" xml:id="te2312"/>
than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4874"/>
what

          <app from="pr4874" n="241.17 (340.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6858">
            <lem wit="A Cent">what</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6859">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I can—and they’re people that ain’t going to be doubted as quick as I’d be. I’ll tell you how to find them. Gimme a pencil and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2313"/>
a piece

          <ptr target="#l12025" type="alt" xml:id="te2313"/>
of paper.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4875"/>
There

          <app from="pr4875" n="241.20 (340.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la6860">
            <lem wit="A Cent">There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">There, now</rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4876"/>
‘

          <hi rend="italic">Royal Nonesuch</hi>
          <app from="pr4876" n="241.20 (340.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6861">
            <lem wit="Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">Royal Nonesuch</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Burning Shame</hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Royal None</hi>
-

              <lb/>
              <hi rend="italic">such</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <hi rend="italic">Bricksville</hi>
.’ Put it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4877"/>
away

          <app from="pr4877" n="241.20 (340.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la6862">
            <lem wit="A Cent">away</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in your pocket</rdg>
          </app>
, and don’t lose it. When the court wants to find out

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2314"/>
something

          <ptr target="#l12026" type="alt" xml:id="te2314"/>
about these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4878"/>
two

          <app from="pr4878" n="241.21 (340.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6863">
            <lem wit="A Cent">two</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">two pills</rdg>
          </app>
, let them send up to Bricksville and say they’ve got the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4879"/>
men

          <app from="pr4879" n="241.22 (341.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6864">
            <lem wit="A Cent">men</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">boys</rdg>
          </app>
that played the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4880"/>
Royal Nonesuch,

          <app from="pr4880" n="241.23 (341.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6865">
            <lem wit="A">Royal Nonesuch,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">‘Royal Nonesuch,’</rdg>
          </app>
and ask for some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4881"/>
witnesses—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2315"/>
why

          <ptr target="#l12027" type="alt" xml:id="te2315"/>
          <app from="pr4881" n="241.23 (341.3–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6866">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">witnesses—why</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">witnesses. Why</rdg>
          </app>
, you’ll have that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4882"/>
entire

          <app from="pr4882" n="241.24 (341.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6867">
            <lem wit="A Cent">entire</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">en-tire</rdg>
          </app>
town down here before you can

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4883"/>
hardly

          <app from="pr4883" n="241.24 (341.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6868">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hardly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6869">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2316"/>
wink, Miss

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4884"/>
Mary.

          <ptr target="#l12028" type="alt" xml:id="te2316"/>
And

          <app from="pr4884" n="241.24–25 (341.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6870">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Mary. And</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Mary; and</rdg>
          </app>
they’ll come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4885"/>
a-biling

          <app from="pr4885" n="241.25 (341.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6871">
            <lem wit="A Cent">a-biling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a-bilin’</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4886"/>
too

          <app from="pr4886" n="241.25 (341.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6872">
            <lem wit="A Cent">too</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
too, you hear

              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y24101">
          <graphic url="y24101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">how to find them</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60121">
          <pb n="242" xml:id="pb0242"/>
I judged we had got everything fixed about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4887"/>
right,

          <app from="pr4887" n="242.1 (341.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6873">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4888"/>
now. So

          <app from="pr4888" n="242.1 (341.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6874">
            <lem wit="A">now. So</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">now.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">now; so</rdg>
          </app>
I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60140">
“Just let the auction go right along, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4889"/>
don’t

          <app from="pr4889" n="242.2 (341.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6875">
            <lem wit="A Cent">don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">don’t you</rdg>
          </app>
worry. Nobody don’t have to pay for the things they buy till a whole day after the auction, on accounts of the short notice, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4890"/>
they

          <app from="pr4890" n="242.4 (342.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6876">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you bet these chaps</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t going out of this till they get that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4891"/>
money—

          <app from="pr4891" n="242.5 (342.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6877">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">money—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">money;</rdg>
          </app>
and the way we’ve fixed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4892"/>
it

          <app from="pr4892" n="242.5 (342.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6878">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it,</rdg>
          </app>
the sale ain’t going to count, and they ain’t going to

          <hi rend="italic">get</hi>
no money. It’s just like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4893"/>
the way it was with

          <app from="pr4893" n="242.7 (342.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6879">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the way it was with</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6880">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the niggers—it warn’t no sale, and the niggers will be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4894"/>
back

          <app from="pr4894" n="242.8 (342.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6881">
            <lem wit="A Cent">back</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">back here</rdg>
          </app>
before long. Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4895"/>
they

          <app from="pr4895" n="242.8 (342.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6882">
            <lem wit="A Cent">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">these rascals</rdg>
          </app>
can’t collect the money for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4896"/>
          <hi rend="italic">niggers</hi>
,

          <app from="pr4896" n="242.9 (342.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6883">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">
              <hi rend="italic">niggers</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">niggers</hi>
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet—they’re in the worst kind of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4897"/>
fix, Miss Mary

          <app from="pr4897" n="242.9 (342.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6884">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fix, Miss Mary</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">fix</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60227">
“Well,” she says, “I’ll run down to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4898"/>
breakfast,

          <app from="pr4898" n="242.10 (342.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la6885">
            <lem wit="MS2">breakfast,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
breakfast

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, and then I’ll start straight for Mr. Lothrop’s.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60237">
“ ’Deed,

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
ain’t the ticket, Miss Mary Jane,” I says, “by no manner of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4899"/>
means;

          <app from="pr4899" n="242.13 (343.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la6886">
            <lem wit="A Cent">means;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">means. I want you to</rdg>
          </app>
go

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2317"/>
          <hi rend="italic">before</hi>
          <ptr target="#l12029" type="alt" xml:id="te2317"/>
breakfast.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60255">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4900"/>
“Why?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60258">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4901"/>
What

          <app from="pr4901" n="242.15 (343.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6889">
            <lem wit="A">What</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Now what</rdg>
          </app>
did you reckon I wanted you to go at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4902"/>
all,

          <app from="pr4902" n="242.15 (334.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6890">
            <lem wit="MS2">all,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
all

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4903"/>
for, Miss Mary

          <app from="pr4903" n="242.15 (343.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6891">
            <lem wit="A">for, Miss Mary</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60283">“Well, I never thought—and come to think, I don’t know. What was it?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60285">
“Why, it’s because you ain’t one of these

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4904"/>
leather-face

          <app from="pr4904" n="242.18 (343.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6892">
            <lem wit="A">leather-face</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">leather-faced</rdg>
          </app>
people. I don’t want no better book

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4905"/>
than

          <app from="pr4905" n="242.19 (343.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6893">
            <lem wit="MS2">than</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">that</rdg>
          </app>
what your face is. A body can

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4906"/>
set

          <app from="pr4906" n="242.19 (344.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la6894">
            <lem wit="A">set</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">just set</rdg>
          </app>
down and read it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4907"/>
off

          <app from="pr4907" n="242.20 (344.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6895">
            <lem wit="A">off</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">right off</rdg>
          </app>
like coarse print.

          <app from="pr4900" n="242.14–20 (343.7–344.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6887">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">“Why? . . . print.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6888">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Do you reckon you can

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4908"/>
go and

          <app from="pr4908" n="242.20 (344.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6896">
            <lem wit="A Cent">go and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6897">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
face your uncles,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4909"/>
when they come to kiss you

          <app from="pr4909" n="242.21 (344.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la6898">
            <lem wit="A Cent">when . . . kiss you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and take your regular three or four</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4910"/>
good-morning

          <app from="pr4910" n="242.21 (344.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la6899">
            <lem wit="A Cent">good-morning</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">good-morning smacks</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4911"/>
never—

          <app from="pr4911" n="242.22 (344.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6900">
            <lem wit="MS2">never—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">never——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60360">
“There, there,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4912"/>
don’t!

          <app from="pr4912" n="242.23 (344.8–10)" type="e" xml:id="la6901">
            <lem wit="A Cent">don’t!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">don’t!</hi>
I’d rather go hang myself than ever see them again.

            </rdg>
          </app>
Yes, I’ll go before breakfast—I’ll be glad to. And leave my sisters with them?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60372">
“Yes—never mind about them.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2318"/>
They’ve

          <ptr target="#l12030" type="alt" xml:id="te2318"/>
got to stand it yet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4913"/>
awhile

          <app from="pr4913" n="242.25 (344.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6902">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">awhile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a while</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4914"/>
They

          <app from="pr4914" n="242.26 (344.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6903">
            <lem wit="A Cent">They</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">These ducks</rdg>
          </app>
might suspicion something if all of you was to go. I don’t want you to see them,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4915"/>
nor your sisters, nor nobody

          <app from="pr4915" n="242.27 (345.2–4)" type="e" xml:id="la6904">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nor your . . . nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and I don’t want you to see anybody</rdg>
          </app>
in this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4916"/>
town—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2319"/>
if

          <ptr target="#l12031" type="alt" xml:id="te2319"/>
          <app from="pr4916" n="242.27 (345.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6905">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">town—if</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">town. If</rdg>
          </app>
a neighbor was to ask how is your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2320"/>
uncles

          <ptr target="#l12032" type="alt" xml:id="te2320"/>
this morning, your face would tell something.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4917"/>
No,

          <app from="pr4917" n="242.29 (345.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6906">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">No,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">No;</rdg>
          </app>
you go right along, Miss Mary Jane, and I’ll fix it with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4918"/>
all of them

          <app from="pr4918" n="242.30 (345.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la6907">
            <lem wit="A Cent">all of them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">these ducks</rdg>
          </app>
. I’ll tell Miss Susan to give your love to your uncles and say you’ve

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4919"/>
went

          <app from="pr4919" n="242.31 (345.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6908">
            <lem wit="A Cent">went</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gone</rdg>
          </app>
away for a few hours

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4920"/>
for to

          <app from="pr4920" n="242.31 (345.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6909">
            <lem wit="A Cent">for to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to</rdg>
          </app>
get a little rest and change,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2321"/>
or to see a friend,

          <ptr target="#l12033" type="alt" xml:id="te2321"/>
and you’ll be back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4921"/>
tonight

          <app from="pr4921" n="242.32 (345.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6910">
            <lem wit="MS2">tonight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">to-night</rdg>
          </app>
or early in the morning.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60465">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2322"/>
“Gone to see a friend

          <ptr target="#l12034" type="alt" xml:id="te2322"/>
is all right, but I won’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4922"/>
have

          <app from="pr4922" n="242.34 (346.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6911">
            <lem wit="A Cent">have</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">have</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
my love given to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4923"/>
them.

          <app from="pr4923" n="242.35 (346.4)" type="e" xml:id="la6912">
            <lem wit="A Cent">them.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60488">
“Well, then, it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4924"/>
shan’t

          <app from="pr4924" n="242.36 (346.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la6913">
            <lem wit="MS2">shan’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">sha’n’t</rdg>
          </app>
be.” It was well enough to tell

          <hi rend="italic">her</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4925"/>
so—

          <app from="pr4925" n="242.36 (346.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6914">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">so—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">so.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4926"/>
no harm

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4927"/>
in it

          <app from="pr4927" n="242.37 (346.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6917">
            <lem wit="A">in it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in that</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2323"/>
It was only a little thing to do, and no trouble; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2324"/>
it’s

          <ptr target="#l12036" type="alt" xml:id="te2324"/>
the little things

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2325"/>
that smoothes

          <ptr target="#l12037" type="alt" xml:id="te2325"/>
people’s roads the most, down here

          <pb n="243" xml:id="pb0243"/>
below; it would make Mary Jane comfortable,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2326"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4928"/>
it wouldn’t

          <app from="pr4928" n="243.1 (346verso.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6918">
            <lem wit="A">it wouldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wouldn’t</rdg>
          </app>
cost nothing.

          <ptr target="#l12038" type="alt" xml:id="te2326"/>
          <ptr target="#l12035" type="alt" xml:id="te2323"/>
          <app from="pr4926" n="242.36–243.2 (346.7–346verso.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6915">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">no . . . nothing.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6916">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Then I says: “There’s one more thing—that bag of money.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60548">
“Well, they’ve got that; and it makes me feel pretty silly to think

          <hi rend="italic">how</hi>
they got it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60553">
“No, you’re

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4929"/>
out,

          <app from="pr4929" n="243.5 (346.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6919">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
there. They hain’t got it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60563">
“Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4930"/>
who’s

          <app from="pr4930" n="243.6 (347.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6920">
            <lem wit="A Cent">who’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">who has</rdg>
          </app>
got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4931"/>
it?

          <app from="pr4931" n="243.6 (347.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6921">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60581">
“I wish I knowed, but I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2327"/>
don’t.

          <ptr target="#l12039" type="alt" xml:id="te2327"/>
I

          <hi rend="italic">had</hi>
it, because I stole it from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4932"/>
them;

          <app from="pr4932" n="243.8 (347.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la6922">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">them;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">them:</rdg>
          </app>
and I stole it to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4933"/>
give

          <app from="pr4933" n="243.8 (347.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6923">
            <lem wit="A Cent">give</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">give it</rdg>
          </app>
to you; and I know where I hid it, but I’m afraid it ain’t there no more. I’m awful sorry, Miss Mary Jane, I’m just as sorry as I can be; but I done the best I could; I did,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4934"/>
honest

          <app from="pr4934" n="243.10 (347.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6924">
            <lem wit="A Cent">honest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">indeed</rdg>
          </app>
. I come nigh getting caught, and I had to shove it into the first place I come to, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4935"/>
run

          <app from="pr4935" n="243.12 (347.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6925">
            <lem wit="A Cent">run</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">git</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—and it warn’t a good place.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60624">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4936"/>
O

          <app from="pr4936" n="243.13 (347.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6926">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4937"/>
stop

          <app from="pr4937" n="243.13 (347.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6927">
            <lem wit="A Cent">stop</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">come, stop</rdg>
          </app>
blaming yourself—it’s too bad to do it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2328"/>
and I won’t allow

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4938"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12040" type="alt" xml:id="te2328"/>
—

          <app from="pr4938" n="243.14 (348.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6928">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">it—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it;</rdg>
          </app>
you couldn’t help

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4939"/>
it;

          <app from="pr4939" n="243.14 (348.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6929">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">it;</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it—</rdg>
          </app>
it wasn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4940"/>
your

          <app from="pr4940" n="243.14 (348.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6930">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">your</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2329"/>
fault.

          <ptr target="#l12041" type="alt" xml:id="te2329"/>
Where did you hide it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60675">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4941"/>
I didn’t

          <app from="pr4941" n="243.16 (348.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6931">
            <lem wit="A Cent">I didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Blame it, I didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
want to set her to thinking about her troubles

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4942"/>
again

          <app from="pr4942" n="243.16 (348.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la6932">
            <lem wit="A Cent">again</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">again, and her poor old dead uncle</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4943"/>
and I couldn’t seem to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4944"/>
get

          <app from="pr4944" n="243.17 (348.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6935">
            <lem wit="A">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">frame</rdg>
          </app>
my mouth to tell her what would make her see that corpse laying in the coffin with that bag of money on his stomach.

          <app from="pr4943" n="243.16–19 (348.8–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6933">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">and I . . . stomach.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6934">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4945"/>
So,

          <app from="pr4945" n="243.19 (348.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6936">
            <lem wit="MS2">So,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">So</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">so</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2330"/>
for a

          <ptr target="#l12042" type="alt" xml:id="te2330"/>
minute I didn’t say

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2331"/>
nothing

          <ptr target="#l12043" type="alt" xml:id="te2331"/>
—then I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60727">
“I’d ruther not

          <hi rend="italic">tell</hi>
you where I put it, Miss Mary Jane, if you don’t mind letting me off; but I’ll write it for you on a piece of paper, and you can read it along the road to Mr. Lothrop’s, if you want to. Do you reckon that’ll do?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60732">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4946"/>
O

          <app from="pr4946" n="243.24 (349.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6937">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y24301">
          <graphic url="y24301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">he wrote</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60747">So I wrote: “I put it in the coffin. It was in there when you was crying there, away in the night. I was behind the door, and I was mighty sorry for you, Miss Mary Jane.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60750">
It

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4947"/>
made

          <app from="pr4947" n="243.28 (349.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6938">
            <lem wit="A Cent">made</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kinder made</rdg>
          </app>
my eyes water a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4948"/>
little,

          <app from="pr4948" n="243.28 (349.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la6939">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">little,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
little

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to remember her crying there all by herself in the night, and them devils laying there right under her own roof,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0071"/>
shaming

          <ptr target="#tb0071" type="te" xml:id="tv0071"/>
her and robbing her; and when I folded it up and

          <pb n="244" xml:id="pb0244"/>
give it to her, I see the water come into her eyes, too; and she shook me by the hand, hard, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60773">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4949"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Good</hi>
-bye—

          <app from="pr4949" n="244.3 (350.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6940">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">
              <hi rend="italic">Good</hi>
-bye—

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">Good</hi>
-by.

            </rdg>
          </app>
I’m going to do everything just as you’ve told me; and if I don’t ever see you again, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4950"/>
shan’t

          <app from="pr4950" n="244.4 (350.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6941">
            <lem wit="MS2">shan’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">sha’n’t</rdg>
          </app>
ever forget you, and I’ll think of you a many and a many a time, and I’ll

          <hi rend="italic">pray</hi>
for you,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2332"/>
too

          <ptr target="#l12044" type="alt" xml:id="te2332"/>
!”—and she was gone.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60805">
Pray

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4951"/>
for me

          <app from="pr4951" n="244.7 (351.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6942">
            <lem wit="A Cent">for me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for me—good land</rdg>
          </app>
! I reckoned if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2333"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l12045" type="alt" xml:id="te2333"/>
knowed me she’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4952"/>
take

          <app from="pr4952" n="244.7 (351.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6943">
            <lem wit="A Cent">take</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tackle</rdg>
          </app>
a job that was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2334"/>
more

          <ptr target="#l12046" type="alt" xml:id="te2334"/>
nearer her size. But I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4953"/>
bet

          <app from="pr4953" n="244.8 (351.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la6944">
            <lem wit="A Cent">bet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">bet you</rdg>
          </app>
she done it, just the same—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2335"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l12047" type="alt" xml:id="te2335"/>
was just that kind. She had the grit to pray for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4954"/>
Judus

          <app from="pr4954" n="244.9 (351.8)" type="e" xml:id="la6945">
            <lem wit="A">Judus</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Judas Iscarott</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Judas,</rdg>
          </app>
if she took the notion—there warn’t no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4955"/>
back-down

          <app from="pr4955" n="244.10 (351.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6946">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">back-down</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
back-

              <lb/>
down

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4956"/>
to her, I judge

          <app from="pr4956" n="244.10 (351.10–12)" type="e" xml:id="la6947">
            <lem wit="A Cent">to her, I judge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">to</hi>
her, if

              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know a girl by the rake of her stem; and I think I do

            </rdg>
          </app>
. You may say what you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4957"/>
want to

          <app from="pr4957" n="244.11 (351.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6948">
            <lem wit="A Cent">want to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">please</rdg>
          </app>
, but in my opinion

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4958"/>
she

          <app from="pr4958" n="244.11 (351.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6949">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that girl</rdg>
          </app>
had more sand in her than any girl I ever see; in my opinion she was just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4959"/>
full

          <app from="pr4959" n="244.12 (351.17)" type="e" xml:id="la6950">
            <lem wit="A Cent">full</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">full</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of sand.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2336"/>
It sounds like flattery, but it ain’t no flattery.

          <ptr target="#l12048" type="alt" xml:id="te2336"/>
And when it comes to beauty—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4960"/>
and

          <app from="pr4960" n="244.14 (352.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6951">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">and</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4961"/>
goodness too

          <app from="pr4961" n="244.14 (352.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6952">
            <lem wit="A">goodness too</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">goodness</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">goodness, too</rdg>
          </app>
—she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2337"/>
lays

          <ptr target="#l12049" type="alt" xml:id="te2337"/>
over them all. I hain’t ever seen her since that time that I see her go out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4962"/>
of

          <app from="pr4962" n="244.15 (352.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6953">
            <lem wit="A Cent">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">at</rdg>
          </app>
that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2338"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4963"/>
door

          <app from="pr4963" n="244.15 (352.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6954">
            <lem wit="A Cent">door</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">door, like light and comfort agoing out of a body’s life</rdg>
          </app>
; no

          <ptr target="#l12050" type="alt" xml:id="te2338"/>
, I hain’t ever seen her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4964"/>
since;

          <app from="pr4964" n="244.16 (352.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6955">
            <lem wit="MS2">since;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">since,</rdg>
          </app>
but I reckon I’ve thought of her a many and a many a million times, and of her saying she would pray for me; and if ever I’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4965"/>
a thought

          <app from="pr4965" n="244.18 (352.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la6956">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a thought</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">thought</rdg>
          </app>
it would do any good for me to pray for

          <hi rend="italic">her</hi>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4966"/>
blamed

          <app from="pr4966" n="244.18 (352.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6957">
            <lem wit="A Cent">blamed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m dum’d</rdg>
          </app>
if I wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4967"/>
a done

          <app from="pr4967" n="244.19 (352.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la6958">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a done</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ done</rdg>
          </app>
it or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4968"/>
bust.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e60990">
Well

          <app from="pr4968" n="244.19–20 (352.17–353.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6959">
            <lem wit="A Cent">bust. [¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
bust.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6960">extra line space</note>
[¶] Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, Mary Jane she lit out the back way, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4969"/>
reckon,

          <app from="pr4969" n="244.20 (353.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la6961">
            <lem wit="MS2">reckon,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">reckon;</rdg>
          </app>
because nobody see her go. When I struck Susan and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2339"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4970"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4970" n="244.21 (353.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6962">
            <lem wit="A Cent">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hair-lip</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12051" type="alt" xml:id="te2339"/>
, I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61021">
“What’s the name of them people over on t’other side of the river that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4971"/>
you-all

          <app from="pr4971" n="244.23 (353.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6963">
            <lem wit="MS2">you-all</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you. all</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">you all</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2340"/>
goes

          <ptr target="#l12052" type="alt" xml:id="te2340"/>
to see sometimes?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61036">They says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61038">
“There’s several; but it’s the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4972"/>
Proctors,

          <app from="pr4972" n="244.25 (353.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la6964">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">Proctors,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
Proctors

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
mainly.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61048">
“That’s the name,” I says; “I most forgot it. Well, Miss Mary

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2341"/>
Jane she told me to tell you she’s gone

          <ptr target="#l12053" type="alt" xml:id="te2341"/>
over there in a dreadful hurry—one of them’s sick.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61054">“Which one?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61056">
“I don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2342"/>
know;

          <ptr target="#l12054" type="alt" xml:id="te2342"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4973"/>
leastways

          <app from="pr4973" n="244.30 (354.6)" type="e" xml:id="la6965">
            <lem wit="A Cent">leastways</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">at least</rdg>
          </app>
I kinder forget; but I think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4974"/>
it’s—

          <app from="pr4974" n="244.30 (354.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6966">
            <lem wit="MS2">it’s—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">it’s——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61077">
“Sakes alive, I hope it ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4975"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Hanner?</hi>
          <app from="pr4975" n="244.31 (354.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6967">
            <lem wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">Hanner?</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Hanner!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61091">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2343"/>
“I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4976"/>
sorry

          <app from="pr4976" n="244.32 (354.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6968">
            <lem wit="A Cent">sorry</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rotten sorry</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12055" type="alt" xml:id="te2343"/>
to say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4977"/>
it,” I says, “but

          <app from="pr4977" n="244.32 (354.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6969">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it,” I says, “but</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it, but</rdg>
          </app>
Hanner’s the very one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61111">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2344"/>
My goodness

          <ptr target="#l12056" type="alt" xml:id="te2344"/>
—and she so well only last week! Is she took bad?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61117">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2345"/>
It ain’t no name for it.

          <ptr target="#l12057" type="alt" xml:id="te2345"/>
They set up with her all night, Miss Mary Jane said, and they don’t think she’ll last many hours.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61123">
“Only think of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2346"/>
that,

          <ptr target="#l12058" type="alt" xml:id="te2346"/>
now! What’s the matter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4978"/>
with

          <app from="pr4978" n="244.36 (355.7)" type="e" xml:id="la6970">
            <lem wit="A Cent">with</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4979"/>
her?

          <app from="pr4979" n="244.36 (355.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6971">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">her?</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">her!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61144">
I couldn’t think of anything reasonable, right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2347"/>
off

          <ptr target="#l12059" type="alt" xml:id="te2347"/>
that way, so I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61150">
          <pb n="245" xml:id="pb0245"/>
“Mumps.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61152">
“Mumps your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4980"/>
granny!—they

          <app from="pr4980" n="245.2 (355.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6972">
            <lem wit="MS2">granny!—they</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">granny! They</rdg>
          </app>
don’t set up with people that’s got the mumps.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61162">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2348"/>
“They don’t, don’t they? You better bet they do with

          <hi rend="italic">these</hi>
mumps. These

          <ptr target="#l12060" type="alt" xml:id="te2348"/>
mumps is different. It’s a new kind, Miss Mary Jane said.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y24501">
          <graphic url="y24501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">hanner with the mumps</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61175">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4981"/>
How’s

          <app from="pr4981" n="245.7 (356.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6973">
            <lem wit="A Cent">How’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">How is</rdg>
          </app>
it a new kind?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61185">“Because it’s mixed up with other things.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61188">“What other things?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61190">
“Well, measles, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4982"/>
whooping cough

          <app from="pr4982" n="245.10 (356.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la6974">
            <lem wit="MS2">whooping cough</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">whooping-cough</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4983"/>
erysiplas

          <app from="pr4983" n="245.10 (356.10)" type="e" xml:id="la6975">
            <lem wit="A Cent">erysiplas</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dysentery</rdg>
          </app>
, and consumption, and yaller janders, and brain fever, and I don’t know what all.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61208">
“My land! And they call it the

          <hi rend="italic">mumps?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61213">“That’s what Miss Mary Jane said.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61215">
“Well, what in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4984"/>
nation

          <app from="pr4984" n="245.15 (357.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la6976">
            <lem wit="A Cent">nation</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">very nation</rdg>
          </app>
do they call it the

          <hi rend="italic">mumps</hi>
for?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61228">
“Why, because it

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
the mumps. That’s what it starts with.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61233">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4985"/>
ther’

          <app from="pr4985" n="245.17 (357.9)" type="e" xml:id="la6977">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no sense in it. A body might stump his toe, and take pison, and fall down the well, and break his neck, and bust his brains out, and somebody come along and ask what killed him, and

          <pb n="246" xml:id="pb0246"/>
some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4986"/>
numskull

          <app from="pr4986" n="246.1 (357.15)" type="e" xml:id="la6978">
            <lem wit="A Cent">numskull</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mullet-head</rdg>
          </app>
up and say, ‘Why, he stumped his

          <hi rend="italic">toe.</hi>
’ Would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4987"/>
ther’

          <app from="pr4987" n="246.1 (358.1)" type="e" xml:id="la6979">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they</rdg>
          </app>
be any sense in that?

          <hi rend="italic">No.</hi>
And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4988"/>
ther’

          <app from="pr4988" n="246.2 (358.3)" type="e" xml:id="la6980">
            <lem wit="A Cent">ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no sense in

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
, nuther. Is it ketching?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61277">
“Is it

          <hi rend="italic">ketching?</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2349"/>
Why

          <ptr target="#l12061" type="alt" xml:id="te2349"/>
, how you talk. Is a

          <hi rend="italic">harrow</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4989"/>
catching

          <app from="pr4989" n="246.4 (358.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6981">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">catching</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">ketching</rdg>
          </app>
?—in the dark?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4990"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2350"/>
If

          <ptr target="#l12062" type="alt" xml:id="te2350"/>
you don’t hitch onto one tooth, you’re bound to on another, ain’t you? And you can’t get away with that tooth without fetching the whole harrow along, can you? Well, these kind of mumps is a kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2351"/>
a harrow, as

          <ptr target="#l12063" type="alt" xml:id="te2351"/>
you may say—and it ain’t no slouch of a harrow,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4991"/>
nuther

          <app from="pr4991" n="246.9 (359.2)" type="e" xml:id="la6984">
            <lem wit="A">nuther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">neither</rdg>
          </app>
, you come to get it hitched on good.

          <app from="pr4990" n="246.5–9 (358.7–359.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la6982">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">If . . . good.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de6983">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61321">
“Well, it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4992"/>
awful

          <app from="pr4992" n="246.10 (359.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la6985">
            <lem wit="A Cent">awful</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jest perfectly awful</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
think,” says the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4993"/>
hare-lip

          <app from="pr4993" n="246.10 (359.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la6986">
            <lem wit="A">hare-lip</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
hair-

              <lb/>
lip

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
hare-

              <lb/>
lip

            </rdg>
          </app>
. “I’ll go to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4994"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr4994" n="246.10 (359.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la6987">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Harvey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4995"/>
and—

          <app from="pr4995" n="246.11 (359.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la6988">
            <lem wit="MS2">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61365">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4996"/>
O

          <app from="pr4996" n="246.12 (359.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la6989">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes,” I says, “I

          <hi rend="italic">would.</hi>
Of

          <hi rend="italic">course</hi>
I would. I wouldn’t lose no time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61381">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4997"/>
why

          <app from="pr4997" n="246.14 (359.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6990">
            <lem wit="A Cent">why</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">why</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
wouldn’t you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61393">
“Just look at it a minute, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4998"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr4998" n="246.15 (359.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la6991">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
you can

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr4999"/>
see

          <app from="pr4999" n="246.15 (359.13)" type="e" xml:id="la6992">
            <lem wit="A Cent">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">see why</rdg>
          </app>
. Hain’t your uncles

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5000"/>
obleeged

          <app from="pr5000" n="246.16 (359.14)" type="e" xml:id="la6993">
            <lem wit="A Cent">obleeged</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">obliged</rdg>
          </app>
to get along home to England as fast as they can?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2352"/>
And do

          <ptr target="#l12064" type="alt" xml:id="te2352"/>
you reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5001"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr5001" n="246.17 (359.16–360.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la6994">
            <lem wit="MS2">they ’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">they’d</rdg>
          </app>
be mean enough to go off and leave you to go all that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5002"/>
journey

          <app from="pr5002" n="246.18 (360.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la6995">
            <lem wit="A Cent">journey</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">awful journey</rdg>
          </app>
by

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2353"/>
yourselves

          <ptr target="#l12065" type="alt" xml:id="te2353"/>
?

          <hi rend="italic">You</hi>
know they’ll wait for you. So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5003"/>
fur

          <app from="pr5003" n="246.19 (360.5)" type="e" xml:id="la6996">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
, so good. Your uncle Harvey’s a preacher, ain’t he? Very well, then; is

          <hi rend="italic">a preacher</hi>
going to deceive a steamboat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5004"/>
clerk?

          <app from="pr5004" n="246.20 (360.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la6997">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">clerk?</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">clerk—</rdg>
          </app>
is he going to deceive a

          <hi rend="italic">ship</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5005"/>
          <hi rend="italic">clerk?</hi>
          <app from="pr5005" n="246.21 (360.11)" type="e" xml:id="la6998">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">clerk?</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">clerk?</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">clerk</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—so as to get them to let Miss Mary Jane go aboard? Now

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
know he ain’t. What

          <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
he do, then? Why, he’ll say, ‘It’s a great pity, but my church

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5006"/>
matters has got to get along the best way they can

          <app from="pr5006" n="246.23–24 (360.16)" type="e" xml:id="la6999">
            <lem wit="A Cent">matters . . . can</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and my affairs must suffer</rdg>
          </app>
; for my niece has been exposed to

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0013"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2354"/>
the dreadful pluribus-unum

          <ptr target="#l12066" type="alt" xml:id="te2354"/>
mumps

          <ptr target="#as0224" type="an" xml:id="an0013"/>
, and so it’s my bounden duty to set down here and wait the three months it takes to show on her if she’s got it.’ But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5007"/>
never mind

          <app from="pr5007" n="246.27 (361.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7000">
            <lem wit="A Cent">never mind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">still</rdg>
          </app>
, if you think it’s best to tell your uncle

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5008"/>
Harvey—

          <app from="pr5008" n="246.28 (361.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7001">
            <lem wit="MS2">Harvey—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Harvey——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61522">
“Shucks, and stay

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5009"/>
fooling

          <app from="pr5009" n="246.29 (361.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7002">
            <lem wit="A Cent">fooling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a-fooling</rdg>
          </app>
around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5010"/>
here

          <app from="pr5010" n="246.29 (361.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7003">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">here</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">here,</rdg>
          </app>
when we could all be having good times in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5011"/>
England

          <app from="pr5011" n="246.30 (361.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7004">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">England</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">England,</rdg>
          </app>
whilst we was waiting to find out whether Mary Jane’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5012"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2355"/>
got

          <ptr target="#l12067" type="alt" xml:id="te2355"/>
          <app from="pr5012" n="246.31 (361.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7005">
            <lem wit="A Cent">got</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ketched</rdg>
          </app>
it or not? Why, you talk like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5013"/>
muggins

          <app from="pr5013" n="246.31 (362.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7006">
            <lem wit="A Cent">muggins</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">regular muggins</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61567">
“Well, anyway,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5014"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr5014" n="246.32 (362.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7007">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
you better tell some of the neighbors.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61577">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2356"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5015"/>
Listen at that, now. You

          <ptr target="#l12068" type="alt" xml:id="te2356"/>
          <app from="pr5015" n="246.33 (362.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7008">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Listen at that, now. You</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">My, but you</rdg>
          </app>
do beat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5016"/>
all,

          <app from="pr5016" n="246.33 (362.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7009">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">all,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
all

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2357"/>
natural

          <ptr target="#l12069" type="alt" xml:id="te2357"/>
stupidness. Can’t you

          <hi rend="italic">see</hi>
that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5017"/>
          <hi rend="italic">they’</hi>
d

          <app from="pr5017" n="246.34 (362.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7010">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">they’</hi>
d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
              <hi rend="italic">they’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
go and tell?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5018"/>
Ther’

          <app from="pr5018" n="246.34 (362.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7011">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Ther’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">They</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no way but just to not tell anybody at

          <hi rend="italic">all.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61630">
“Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5019"/>
maybe

          <app from="pr5019" n="246.36 (362.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7012">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">maybe</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">may be</rdg>
          </app>
you’re right—yes, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5020"/>
judge

          <app from="pr5020" n="246.36 (362.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7013">
            <lem wit="A Cent">judge</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">believe</rdg>
          </app>
you

          <hi rend="italic">are</hi>
right.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61651">
“But I reckon we ought to tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5021"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5021" n="246.37 (362.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7014">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Harvey she’s gone out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5022"/>
a while

          <app from="pr5022" n="246.37–38 (362.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7015">
            <lem wit="A">a while</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for a while</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">awhile</rdg>
          </app>
, anyway, so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5023"/>
he

          <app from="pr5023" n="246.38 (363.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7016">
            <lem wit="A Cent">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5024"/>
won’t

          <app from="pr5024" n="246.38 (363.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7017">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">won’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wont</rdg>
          </app>
be uneasy about her?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61687">
          <pb n="247" xml:id="pb0247"/>
“Yes, Miss Mary Jane

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5025"/>
she

          <app from="pr5025" n="247.1 (363.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7018">
            <lem wit="A Cent">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7019">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
wanted you to do that. She says, ‘Tell them to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2358"/>
give

          <ptr target="#l12070" type="alt" xml:id="te2358"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5026"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5026" n="247.2 (363.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7020">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Harvey and William my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5027"/>
love

          <app from="pr5027" n="247.2 (363.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la7021">
            <lem wit="A Cent">love</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dear dear love</rdg>
          </app>
and a kiss, and say I’ve run over the river to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2359"/>
see

          <ptr target="#l12071" type="alt" xml:id="te2359"/>
Mr.—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5028"/>
Mr.’—

          <app from="pr5028" n="247.3 (363.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7022">
            <lem wit="MS2">Mr.’—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
Mr.

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
—

            </rdg>
          </app>
what

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
the name of that rich family your uncle Peter used to think so much of?—I mean the one that—”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61734">
“Why, you must mean the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5029"/>
Apthorps

          <app from="pr5029" n="247.6 (364.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7023">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Apthorps</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Apthorps</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, ain’t it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61745">
“Of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5030"/>
course; bother

          <app from="pr5030" n="247.7 (364.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7024">
            <lem wit="A">course; bother</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">course;</hi>
blame

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">course. Bother</rdg>
          </app>
them kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5031"/>
names,

          <app from="pr5031" n="247.7 (364.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7025">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">names,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">names!</rdg>
          </app>
a body can’t ever seem to remember them, half the time, somehow. Yes, she said, say she has run over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2360"/>
for to

          <ptr target="#l12072" type="alt" xml:id="te2360"/>
ask the Apthorps to be sure and come to the auction and buy this house, because she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5032"/>
allowed

          <app from="pr5032" n="247.10 (364.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7026">
            <lem wit="A Cent">allowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thought</rdg>
          </app>
her uncle Peter would ruther they had it than anybody else; and she’s going to stick to them till they say they’ll

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5033"/>
come;

          <app from="pr5033" n="247.12 (364.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7027">
            <lem wit="MS2">come;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">come,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2361"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l12073" type="alt" xml:id="te2361"/>
then if she ain’t too tired, she’s coming home; and if she is, she’ll be home in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5034"/>
morning,

          <app from="pr5034" n="247.13 (365.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7028">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">morning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
morning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
anyway. She said, don’t say nothing about the Proctors, but only

          <pb n="248" xml:id="pb0248"/>
about the Apthorps—which’ll be perfectly true, because she

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
going there to speak about their buying the house; I know it, because she told me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5035"/>
so,

          <app from="pr5035" n="248.3 (365.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7029">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
herself.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y24701">
          <graphic url="y24701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the auction</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61816">
“All right,” they said, and cleared out to lay for their

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2362"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5036"/>
uncles

          <app from="pr5036" n="248.4 (365.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7030">
            <lem wit="A Cent">uncles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cussed uncles</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l12074" type="alt" xml:id="te2362"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2363"/>
give

          <ptr target="#l12075" type="alt" xml:id="te2363"/>
them the love and the kisses, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5037"/>
tell them

          <app from="pr5037" n="248.5 (365.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7031">
            <lem wit="A Cent">tell them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tell the old principal hog</rdg>
          </app>
the message.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61843">
Everything was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5038"/>
right,

          <app from="pr5038" n="248.6 (365.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7032">
            <lem wit="MS2">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now. The girls wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5039"/>
say nothing,

          <app from="pr5039" n="248.6 (365.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7033">
            <lem wit="C">say nothing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">squeak,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">say nothing</rdg>
          </app>
because they wanted to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5040"/>
go to

          <app from="pr5040" n="248.7 (366.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7034">
            <lem wit="A Cent">go to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">git for</rdg>
          </app>
England; and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5041"/>
king and the duke

          <app from="pr5041" n="248.7 (366.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7035">
            <lem wit="A Cent">king and the duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dead beats</rdg>
          </app>
would ruther Mary Jane was off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5042"/>
working

          <app from="pr5042" n="248.8 (366.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7036">
            <lem wit="A Cent">working</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">legging</rdg>
          </app>
for the auction

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2364"/>
than

          <ptr target="#l12076" type="alt" xml:id="te2364"/>
around in reach of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5043"/>
doctor

          <app from="pr5043" n="248.9 (366.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7037">
            <lem wit="MS2">doctor</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Doctor</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Dr.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5044"/>
Robinson

          <app from="pr5044" n="248.9 (366.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la7038">
            <lem wit="A Cent">Robinson</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Robinson’s meddlings</rdg>
          </app>
. I felt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5045"/>
very good; I

          <app from="pr5045" n="248.9 (366.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7039">
            <lem wit="A">very good; I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">good; I</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">very good. I</rdg>
          </app>
judged I had done

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5046"/>
it

          <app from="pr5046" n="248.9 (366.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7040">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that thing</rdg>
          </app>
pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5047"/>
neat—

          <app from="pr5047" n="248.10 (366.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7041">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">neat—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">neat;</rdg>
          </app>
I reckoned Tom Sawyer couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5048"/>
a done

          <app from="pr5048" n="248.10 (366.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7042">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a done</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ done</rdg>
          </app>
it no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2365"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5049"/>
neater,

          <app from="pr5049" n="248.10 (366.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7043">
            <lem wit="MS2">neater,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
neater

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
himself.

          <ptr target="#l12077" type="alt" xml:id="te2365"/>
Of course

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2366"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l12078" type="alt" xml:id="te2366"/>
would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5050"/>
a throwed

          <app from="pr5050" n="248.11 (366.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7044">
            <lem wit="A">a throwed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a slung</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">’a’ throwed</rdg>
          </app>
more style into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5051"/>
it,

          <app from="pr5051" n="248.11 (366.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7045">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">it;</rdg>
          </app>
but I can’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5052"/>
do that

          <app from="pr5052" n="248.12 (366.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7046">
            <lem wit="A Cent">do that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sling style</rdg>
          </app>
very handy, not being brung up to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5053"/>
it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e61991">
Well

          <app from="pr5053" n="248.12–13 (366.14–367.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7047">
            <lem wit="A Cent">it. [¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
it.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7048">extra line space</note>
[¶] Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, they held the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5054"/>
auction,

          <app from="pr5054" n="248.13 (367.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7049">
            <lem wit="MS2">auction,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
auction

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in the public square,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2367"/>
along towards the end of the afternoon,

          <ptr target="#l12079" type="alt" xml:id="te2367"/>
and it strung along,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5055"/>
and strung along,

          <app from="pr5055" n="248.14 (367.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7050">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">and strung along,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">and strung along;</rdg>
          </app>
and the old man he was on hand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5056"/>
and looking

          <app from="pr5056" n="248.15 (367.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7051">
            <lem wit="A Cent">and looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a looking</rdg>
          </app>
his level

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0072"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5057"/>
piousest

          <app from="pr5057" n="248.15 (367.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7052">
            <lem wit="MS2">piousest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">pisonest</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0072" type="te" xml:id="tv0072"/>
, up there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5058"/>
longside

          <app from="pr5058" n="248.16 (367.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7053">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">longside</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">alongside</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5059"/>
of

          <app from="pr5059" n="248.16 (367.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7054">
            <lem wit="A Cent">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7055">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the auctioneer, and chipping in a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2368"/>
little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5060"/>
Scripture

          <ptr target="#l12080" type="alt" xml:id="te2368"/>
,

          <app from="pr5060" n="248.16 (367.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7056">
            <lem wit="A">Scripture,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dab of Scripture,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">Scripture</rdg>
          </app>
now and then, or a little goody-goody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5061"/>
saying,

          <app from="pr5061" n="248.17 (367.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7057">
            <lem wit="A">saying,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">remark,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">saying</rdg>
          </app>
of some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5062"/>
kind,

          <app from="pr5062" n="248.17 (367.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7058">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">kind,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">kind;</rdg>
          </app>
and the duke he was around goo-gooing for sympathy all he knowed how, and just

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2369"/>
spreading

          <ptr target="#l12081" type="alt" xml:id="te2369"/>
himself

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5063"/>
generly

          <app from="pr5063" n="248.19 (368.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7059">
            <lem wit="A Cent">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">generally</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62105">
But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5064"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5064" n="248.20 (368.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7060">
            <lem wit="MS2 Cent">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2370"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l12082" type="alt" xml:id="te2370"/>
thing dragged through, and everything was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5065"/>
sold. Everything

          <app from="pr5065" n="248.21 (368.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7061">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">sold. Everything</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">sold—everything</rdg>
          </app>
but a little old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5066"/>
trifling

          <app from="pr5066" n="248.21 (368.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7062">
            <lem wit="A Cent">trifling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ten-cent</rdg>
          </app>
lot in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5067"/>
graveyard. So

          <app from="pr5067" n="248.21 (368.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7063">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">graveyard. So</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">graveyard; so</rdg>
          </app>
they’d got to work

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5068"/>
off—

          <app from="pr5068" n="248.22 (368.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7064">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">off—</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">off.</rdg>
          </app>
I never see such a girafft as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5069"/>
the

          <app from="pr5069" n="248.22 (368.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7065">
            <lem wit="A Cent">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that</rdg>
          </app>
king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5070"/>
was

          <app from="pr5070" n="248.22 (368.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7066">
            <lem wit="A Cent">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7067">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for wanting to swallow

          <hi rend="italic">everything.</hi>
Well, whilst they was at it, a steamboat landed, and in about two

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5071"/>
minutes,

          <app from="pr5071" n="248.24 (368.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7068">
            <lem wit="MS2">minutes,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A Cent">
minutes

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
up comes a crowd

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5072"/>
a whooping

          <app from="pr5072" n="248.24–25 (368.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7069">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">a whooping</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">a-whooping</rdg>
          </app>
and yelling and laughing and carrying

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5073"/>
on,

          <app from="pr5073" n="248.25 (369.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7070">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">on.</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5074"/>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2371"/>
singing

          <ptr target="#l12083" type="alt" xml:id="te2371"/>
out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62205">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Here’s</hi>
your opposition line!

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0014"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5075"/>
Here’s

          <app from="pr5075" n="248.27 (369.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7073">
            <lem wit="MS2">Here’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">here’s</rdg>
          </app>
your two sets o’ heirs

          <ptr target="#as0225" type="an" xml:id="an0014"/>
to old Peter Wilks—and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="pt0015"/>
you pays your money and you takes your choice

          <ptr target="#as0226" type="an" xml:id="an0015"/>
!”

          <app from="pr5074" n="248.25–28 (369.2–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7071">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">and singing . . . choice!”</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7072">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0402">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXIX.</head>
        <pb n="249" xml:id="pb0249"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y24901">
          <graphic url="y24901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5076"/>
Chapter XXIX.

            <app from="pr5076" n="249 title (369.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7074">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXIX.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2 Cent">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7075">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5077"/>
They

            <app from="pr5077" n="249.1 (369.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7076">
              <lem wit="A Cent">They</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">And they</rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2491">
          <graphic url="hf2491.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the true brothers</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e62258">
was fetching a very

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5078"/>
nice looking

          <app from="pr5078" n="249.1–2 (369.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7077">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">nice looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">nice-looking</rdg>
          </app>
old gentleman along, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5079"/>
nice looking

          <app from="pr5079" n="249.3 (369.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7078">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">nice looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">nice-looking</rdg>
          </app>
younger one, with his right arm in a sling. And my souls, how the people yelled, and laughed, and kept it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5080"/>
up.

          <app from="pr5080" n="249.6 (369.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7079">
            <lem wit="MS2,A">up.</lem>
            <rdg wit="Cent">up!</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="rp5081"/>
But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5082"/>
I

          <app from="pr5082" n="249.7 (370.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7082">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
didn’t see no joke about it, and I judged it would strain the duke and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2372"/>
king

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5083"/>
some,

          <app from="pr5083" n="249.9 (370.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7083">
            <lem wit="MS2">some,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
some

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to

          <ptr target="#l12084" type="alt" xml:id="te2372"/>
see any. I reckoned

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2373"/>
they’d

          <ptr target="#l12085" type="alt" xml:id="te2373"/>
turn pale. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5084"/>
no

          <app from="pr5084" n="249.11 (370.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7084">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">no, sir</rdg>
          </app>
, nary a pale did

          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5085"/>
turn

          <app from="pr5085" n="249.11 (370.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7085">
            <lem wit="A">turn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">pale</rdg>
          </app>
. The duke he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2374"/>
never

          <ptr target="#l12086" type="alt" xml:id="te2374"/>
let

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5086"/>
on he

          <app from="pr5086" n="249.12 (370.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7086">
            <lem wit="A">on he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on that he</rdg>
          </app>
suspicioned what was up, but just went a goo-gooing around, happy and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5087"/>
satisfied

          <app from="pr5087" n="249.15 (370.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7087">
            <lem wit="A">satisfied</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">content</rdg>
          </app>
, like a jug that’s googling out buttermilk; and as for the king, he just gazed and gazed down

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2375"/>
sorrowful

          <ptr target="#l12087" type="alt" xml:id="te2375"/>
on them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5088"/>
newcomers

          <app from="pr5088" n="249.18 (370.15–371.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7088">
            <lem wit="C">newcomers</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
new-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
comers

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
new-

              <lb/>
comers

            </rdg>
          </app>
like it give him the stomach-ache in his very heart to think there could be such frauds and rascals in the world.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5089"/>
O

          <app from="pr5089" n="249.20 (371.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7089">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, he done it admirable. Lots of the principal people gethered around the king, to let him see they was on his side. That old gentleman that had just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5090"/>
come,

          <app from="pr5090" n="249.22 (371.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7090">
            <lem wit="MS2">come,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
come

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
looked all puzzled to death. Pretty soon he begun to speak, and I see, straight

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5091"/>
off,

          <app from="pr5091" n="249.23 (371.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la7091">
            <lem wit="A">off,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">off, that</rdg>
          </app>
he pronounced

          <hi rend="italic">like</hi>
an

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5092"/>
Englishman;

          <app from="pr5092" n="249.24 (371.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7092">
            <lem wit="MS2">Englishman;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Englishman,</rdg>
          </app>
not the king’s way, though the king’s

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
pretty good, for an imitation. I can’t give the old gent’s words, nor I can’t imitate him; but he turned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5093"/>
around

          <app from="pr5093" n="249.26 (372.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7093">
            <lem wit="A">around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7094">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to the crowd, and says, about like this:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62420">
“This is a surprise to me which I wasn’t looking for; and I’ll acknowledge, candid and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5094"/>
frank,

          <app from="pr5094" n="249.29 (372.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7095">
            <lem wit="A">frank,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">frank, that</rdg>
          </app>
I ain’t very well fixed to meet it and answer it; for my brother and me has had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5095"/>
misfortunes:

          <app from="pr5095" n="249.30 (372.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7096">
            <lem wit="MS2">misfortunes:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">misfortunes,</rdg>
          </app>
he’s broke his arm, and our baggage got put off at a town above here, last night in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5096"/>
night,

          <app from="pr5096" n="249.32 (372.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7097">
            <lem wit="MS2">night,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
night

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
by

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5097"/>
a mistake

          <app from="pr5097" n="249.32 (372.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7098">
            <lem wit="A">a mistake</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mistake</rdg>
          </app>
. I am Peter Wilks’s brother Harvey, and this is his brother William, which can’t hear nor speak—and can’t

          <pb n="250" xml:id="pb0250"/>
even make signs to amount to much, now’t he’s only got one hand to work them with. We are who we say we are; and in a day or two, when I get the baggage, I can prove it. But,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5098"/>
up

          <app from="pr5098" n="250.3 (373.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7099">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7100">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
till then, I won’t say nothing more, but go to the hotel and wait.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62464">So him and the new dummy started off; and the king he laughs, and blethers out:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62466">
“Broke his arm—

          <hi rend="italic">very</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5099"/>
likely,

          <app from="pr5099" n="250.7 (374.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7101">
            <lem wit="MS2">likely,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
likely

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
it?—and very convenient, too, for a fraud that’s got to make signs, and hain’t learnt how. Lost their baggage! That’s

          <hi rend="italic">mighty</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2376"/>
good!—and

          <ptr target="#l12088" type="alt" xml:id="te2376"/>
mighty ingenious—under the

          <hi rend="italic">circumstances!</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62490">
So he laughed again; and so did everybody else, except three or four, or maybe half a dozen. One of these was that doctor; another one was a sharp looking

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5100"/>
gentleman,

          <app from="pr5100" n="250.13 (374.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7102">
            <lem wit="A">gentleman,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
gentleman

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5101"/>
carpet bag of the old-fashioned kind made out of carpet-stuff,

          <app from="pr5101" n="250.13–14 (375.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7103">
            <lem wit="C">carpet bag of . . . carpet-stuff,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">carpet bag</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">carpet-bag of . . . carpet-stuff,</rdg>
          </app>
that had just come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2377"/>
off of

          <ptr target="#l12089" type="alt" xml:id="te2377"/>
the steamboat and was talking to him in a low voice,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2378"/>
and glancing

          <ptr target="#l12090" type="alt" xml:id="te2378"/>
towards the king now and then and nodding their heads—it was Levi Bell, the lawyer that was gone up to Louisville; and another one was a big rough husky that come along and listened to all the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5102"/>
gentleman

          <app from="pr5102" n="250.19 (375.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7104">
            <lem wit="A">gentleman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gent</rdg>
          </app>
said, and was listening to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5103"/>
king,

          <app from="pr5103" n="250.19 (375.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7105">
            <lem wit="MS2">king,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
king

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now. And when the king got done, this husky up and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62536">
“Say,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5104"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr5104" n="250.21 (375.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7106">
            <lem wit="MS2">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
; if you are Harvey Wilks,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5105"/>
when’d

          <app from="pr5105" n="250.21 (376.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7107">
            <lem wit="A">when’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">when did</rdg>
          </app>
you come to this town?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62554">“The day before the funeral, friend,” says the king.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62556">“But what time o’ day?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62559">
“In the evenin’—’bout an hour

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5106"/>
er

          <app from="pr5106" n="250.25 (376.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7108">
            <lem wit="A">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or</rdg>
          </app>
two before sundown.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62569">
“

          <hi rend="italic">How’d</hi>
you come?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62574">
“I come down on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5107"/>
Susan

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2379"/>
Powell

          <app from="pr5107" n="250.27 (376.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7109">
            <lem wit="MS2">Susan Powell</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Susan Powell</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5108"/>
Cincinnati.

          <app from="pr5108" n="250.27 (376.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7110">
            <lem wit="A">Cincinnati.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Cincinnati

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#l12091" type="alt" xml:id="te2379"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62597">
“Well, then, how’d you come to be up at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5109"/>
Pint

          <app from="pr5109" n="250.28 (376.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7111">
            <lem wit="A">Pint</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Point</rdg>
          </app>
in the

          <hi rend="italic">mornin</hi>
’—in a canoe?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62610">
“I warn’t up at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5110"/>
Pint

          <app from="pr5110" n="250.30 (377.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7112">
            <lem wit="A">Pint</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Point</rdg>
          </app>
in the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2380"/>
mornin’

          <ptr target="#l12092" type="alt" xml:id="te2380"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62624">“It’s a lie.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62626">
Several of them jumped for him and begged him not to talk

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5111"/>
that way

          <app from="pr5111" n="250.32–33 (377.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7113">
            <lem wit="A">that way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">so</rdg>
          </app>
to an old man and a preacher.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62636">
“Preacher be hanged, he’s a fraud and a liar. He was up at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5112"/>
Pint

          <app from="pr5112" n="250.34 (377.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7114">
            <lem wit="A">Pint</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Point</rdg>
          </app>
that mornin’. I live up there, don’t I? Well, I was up there, and he was up there. I

          <hi rend="italic">see</hi>
him there. He come in a canoe, along with Tim Collins and a boy.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62649">
The doctor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2381"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l12093" type="alt" xml:id="te2381"/>
up and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62655">
          <pb n="251" xml:id="pb0251"/>
“Would you know the boy again if you was to see him, Hines?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62657">“I reckon I would, but I don’t know. Why, yonder he is, now. I know him perfectly easy.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62660">It was me he pointed at. The doctor says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62662">
“Neighbors, I don’t know whether the new couple is frauds or not; but if

          <hi rend="italic">these</hi>
two ain’t frauds,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5113"/>
I am

          <app from="pr5113" n="251.6 (378.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7115">
            <lem wit="A">I am</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m</rdg>
          </app>
an idiot, that’s all. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2382"/>
think

          <ptr target="#l12094" type="alt" xml:id="te2382"/>
it’s our duty to see that they don’t get away from here till we’ve looked into this thing. Come along, Hines; come along, the rest of you. We’ll take these fellows to the tavern and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2383"/>
affront

          <ptr target="#l12095" type="alt" xml:id="te2383"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5114"/>
them

          <app from="pr5114" n="251.9 (379.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7116">
            <lem wit="A">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’em</rdg>
          </app>
with t’other couple, and I reckon we’ll find out

          <hi rend="italic">something</hi>
before we get through.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y25101">
          <graphic url="y25101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the doctor leads huck</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62699">
It was nuts for the crowd, though maybe not for the king’s friends; so we all started.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2384"/>
It was about sundown.

          <ptr target="#l12096" type="alt" xml:id="te2384"/>
The doctor he led me along by the hand, and was plenty kind enough, but he never let

          <hi rend="italic">go</hi>
my hand.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62708">
We all got in a big room in the hotel,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2385"/>
and lit up some candles,

          <ptr target="#l12097" type="alt" xml:id="te2385"/>
and fetched in the new

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2386"/>
couple

          <ptr target="#l12098" type="alt" xml:id="te2386"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62718">
          <pb n="252" xml:id="pb0252"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5115"/>
First

          <app from="pr5115" n="252.1 (380-A-1.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7117">
            <lem wit="MS2">[¶] First</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7118">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
First

            </rdg>
          </app>
, the doctor says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62731">
“I don’t wish to be too hard on these two men, but

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
think they’re frauds, and they may have complices that we don’t know nothing about. If they have, won’t the complices get away with that bag of gold Peter Wilks left? It ain’t unlikely. If these men ain’t frauds, they won’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2387"/>
object

          <ptr target="#l12099" type="alt" xml:id="te2387"/>
to sending for that money and letting us keep it till they prove they’re all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2388"/>
right—

          <ptr target="#l12100" type="alt" xml:id="te2388"/>
ain’t that so?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62744">
Everybody agreed to that. So I judged they had our gang in a pretty tight place, right at the outstart. But the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2389"/>
king

          <ptr target="#l12101" type="alt" xml:id="te2389"/>
he only looked sorrowful, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62750">
“Gentlemen, I wish the money was there, for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2390"/>
I ain’t

          <ptr target="#l12102" type="alt" xml:id="te2390"/>
got no disposition to throw anything in the way of a fair, open, out-and-out investigation

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5116"/>
o’

          <app from="pr5116" n="252.13 (381-2.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7119">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5117"/>
misable

          <app from="pr5117" n="252.13 (381-2.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la7120">
            <lem wit="A">misable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mournful</rdg>
          </app>
business; but alas, the money ain’t there; you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5118"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr5118" n="252.14 (381-2.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7121">
            <lem wit="A">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">can</rdg>
          </app>
send and see, if you want to.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62781">“Where is it, then?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62783">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2391"/>
Well, when

          <ptr target="#l12103" type="alt" xml:id="te2391"/>
my niece give it to me to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2392"/>
keep

          <ptr target="#l12104" type="alt" xml:id="te2392"/>
for her, I took and hid it inside

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5119"/>
o’ the

          <app from="pr5119" n="252.17 (381-3.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7122">
            <lem wit="A">o’ the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of the</rdg>
          </app>
straw tick

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5120"/>
o’ my

          <app from="pr5120" n="252.17 (381-3.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7123">
            <lem wit="A">o’ my</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of my</rdg>
          </app>
bed,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2393"/>
not

          <ptr target="#l12105" type="alt" xml:id="te2393"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5121"/>
wishin’

          <app from="pr5121" n="252.17 (381-3.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7124">
            <lem wit="A">wishin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wishing</rdg>
          </app>
to bank it for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2394"/>
the few

          <ptr target="#l12106" type="alt" xml:id="te2394"/>
days we’d be here, and considerin’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2395"/>
the bed a

          <ptr target="#l12107" type="alt" xml:id="te2395"/>
safe place, we not bein’ used to niggers, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5122"/>
suppos’n’

          <app from="pr5122" n="252.19 (381-3.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7125">
            <lem wit="A">suppos’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">supposin’</rdg>
          </app>
’em

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2396"/>
honest, like servants in England.

          <ptr target="#l12108" type="alt" xml:id="te2396"/>
The niggers stole it the very next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5123"/>
mornin’,

          <app from="pr5123" n="252.20 (381-3.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la7126">
            <lem wit="C">mornin’,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">morning,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">mornin’</rdg>
          </app>
after I had went down stairs; and when I sold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5124"/>
’em

          <app from="pr5124" n="252.21 (381-3.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7127">
            <lem wit="A">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them</rdg>
          </app>
, I hadn’t missed the money

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5125"/>
yit

          <app from="pr5125" n="252.21 (381-4.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7128">
            <lem wit="A">yit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">yet</rdg>
          </app>
, so they got clean away with it. My servant here

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5126"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr5126" n="252.22 (381-4.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7129">
            <lem wit="A">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">can</rdg>
          </app>
tell you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5127"/>
’bout

          <app from="pr5127" n="252.22 (381-4.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7130">
            <lem wit="A">’bout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">about</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5128"/>
it,

          <app from="pr5128" n="252.22 (381-4.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7131">
            <lem wit="MS2">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
gentlemen.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62895">
The doctor and several said “Shucks!” and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2397"/>
I see

          <ptr target="#l12109" type="alt" xml:id="te2397"/>
nobody didn’t altogether believe him. One man asked me if I see the niggers steal it. I said no, but I see them sneaking out of the room and hustling away, and I never thought nothing, only I reckoned they was afraid they had waked up my master and was trying to get away before he made trouble with them. That was all they asked me. Then the doctor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2398"/>
whirls

          <ptr target="#l12110" type="alt" xml:id="te2398"/>
on me and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62905">
“Are

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5129"/>
English,

          <app from="pr5129" n="252.31 (381-5.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7132">
            <lem wit="MS2">English,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
English

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62917">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2399"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l12111" type="alt" xml:id="te2399"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5130"/>
says

          <app from="pr5130" n="252.32 (381-5.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7133">
            <lem wit="A">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
yes; and him and some others laughed, and said, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5131"/>
Stuff

          <app from="pr5131" n="252.32 (381-5.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7134">
            <lem wit="A">Stuff</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Bosh</rdg>
          </app>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e62937">
Well, then they sailed in on the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2400"/>
general

          <ptr target="#l12112" type="alt" xml:id="te2400"/>
investigation, and there we had it, up and down, hour in, hour out,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2401"/>
and nobody

          <ptr target="#l12113" type="alt" xml:id="te2401"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5132"/>
never

          <app from="pr5132" n="252.34 (380.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7135">
            <lem wit="A">never</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ever</rdg>
          </app>
said a word about supper, nor ever seemed to think about it—and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2402"/>
so they

          <ptr target="#l12114" type="alt" xml:id="te2402"/>
kept it up, and kept it up; and it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
the worst mixed-up thing you ever see. They made the king tell his yarn, and they made the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5133"/>
gentleman

          <app from="pr5133" n="252.38 (381.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7136">
            <lem wit="A">gentleman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gent</rdg>
          </app>
tell his’n; and anybody but a lot of prejudiced chuckleheads would a

          <hi rend="italic">seen</hi>
that the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5134"/>
gentleman

          <app from="pr5134" n="252.39 (381.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7137">
            <lem wit="A">gentleman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gent</rdg>
          </app>
was spinning truth and

          <pb n="253" xml:id="pb0253"/>
t’other one lies. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5135"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5135" n="253.1 (381.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7138">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
they had me up to tell what I knowed. The king he give me a left-handed look out of the corner of his eye, and so I knowed enough to talk on the right side.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5136"/>
I begun

          <app from="pr5136" n="253.3 (381.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7139">
            <lem wit="A">I begun</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I sailed in, and begun</rdg>
          </app>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5137"/>
tell

          <app from="pr5137" n="253.3 (381.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la7140">
            <lem wit="A">tell</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tell all</rdg>
          </app>
about Sheffield, and how we lived there, and all about the English

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2403"/>
Wilkses

          <ptr target="#l12115" type="alt" xml:id="te2403"/>
, and so on; but I didn’t get pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5138"/>
fur

          <app from="pr5138" n="253.5 (382.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7141">
            <lem wit="A">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
till

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2404"/>
the doctor begun to laugh; and

          <ptr target="#l12116" type="alt" xml:id="te2404"/>
Levi Bell, the lawyer, says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63024">
“Set down, my boy, I wouldn’t strain myself, if I was you. I reckon you ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2405"/>
used

          <ptr target="#l12117" type="alt" xml:id="te2405"/>
to lying, it don’t seem to come handy; what you want is practice. You do it pretty awkward.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63030">
I didn’t care nothing for the compliment, but I was glad to be let off,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5139"/>
any way

          <app from="pr5139" n="253.11 (382.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7142">
            <lem wit="MS2">any way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">anyway</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63040">
The doctor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5140"/>
he

          <app from="pr5140" n="253.12 (382.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7143">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7144">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
started to say something, and turns and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63051">
“If you’d been in town at first, Levi

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5141"/>
Bell—

          <app from="pr5141" n="253.13 (383.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7145">
            <lem wit="MS2">Bell—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Bell——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63061">
The king broke in and reached out his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5142"/>
hand

          <app from="pr5142" n="253.14 (383.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7146">
            <lem wit="MS2">hand</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hand,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63071">“Why, is this my poor dead brother’s old friend that he’s wrote so often about?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63073">
The lawyer and him shook hands, and the lawyer

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5143"/>
smiled,

          <app from="pr5143" n="253.17 (383.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7147">
            <lem wit="MS2">smiled,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
smiled

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and looked pleased, and they talked right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5144"/>
along,

          <app from="pr5144" n="253.18 (383.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7148">
            <lem wit="MS2">along,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
along

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a while, and then got to one side and talked low; and at last the lawyer

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5145"/>
speaks

          <app from="pr5145" n="253.19 (383.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7149">
            <lem wit="A">speaks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">spoke</rdg>
          </app>
up and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63101">
“That’ll fix it. I’ll take the order and send

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2406"/>
it,

          <ptr target="#l12118" type="alt" xml:id="te2406"/>
along with your brother’s, and then they’ll know it’s all right.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63107">
So they got some paper and a pen, and the king he set down and twisted his head to one side, and chawed his tongue, and scrawled off something; and then they give the pen to the duke—and then for the first time, the duke looked sick. But he took the pen and wrote. So then the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2407"/>
lawyer

          <ptr target="#l12119" type="alt" xml:id="te2407"/>
turns to the new old gentleman and says:

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y25301">
          <graphic url="y25301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the duke wrote</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63118">
          <pb n="254" xml:id="pb0254"/>
“You and your brother please write a line or two and sign your names.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63120">
The old gentleman wrote, but nobody couldn’t read it. The lawyer

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2408"/>
looked

          <ptr target="#l12120" type="alt" xml:id="te2408"/>
powerful astonished,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2409"/>
and says:

          <ptr target="#l12121" type="alt" xml:id="te2409"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63129">
“Well, it beats

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
”—and snaked a lot of old letters out of his pocket, and examined them, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5146"/>
then examined

          <app from="pr5146" n="254.6 (385.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7150">
            <lem wit="A">then examined</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">then</rdg>
          </app>
the old man’s writing, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5147"/>
then

          <hi rend="italic">them</hi>
          <app from="pr5147" n="254.7 (385.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7151">
            <lem wit="A">
then

              <hi rend="italic">them</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">them</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
again; and then says: “These old letters is from Harvey Wilks; and here’s

          <hi rend="italic">these</hi>
two’s handwritings, and anybody can see

          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
didn’t write them” (the king and the duke looked sold and foolish, I tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5148"/>
you, to see how the lawyer had took them in),

          <app from="pr5148" n="254.10–11 (386.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7152">
            <lem wit="A">you, to . . . in),</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you!)</rdg>
          </app>
“and here’s

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
old gentleman’s handwriting, and anybody can tell, easy enough,

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
didn’t write them—fact is, the scratches he makes ain’t properly

          <hi rend="italic">writing</hi>
, at all. Now here’s some letters

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5149"/>
from—

          <app from="pr5149" n="254.14 (386.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7153">
            <lem wit="MS2">from—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">from——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63188">The new old gentleman says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63190">
“If you please, let me explain. Nobody can read my hand but my brother there—so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2410"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5150"/>
he

          <app from="pr5150" n="254.17 (387.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7154">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he always</rdg>
          </app>
copies

          <ptr target="#l12122" type="alt" xml:id="te2410"/>
for me. It’s

          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
hand you’ve got there, not mine.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63206">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Well!</hi>
” says the lawyer, “this

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
a state of things. I’ve got some of William’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5151"/>
letters,

          <app from="pr5151" n="254.20 (387.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7155">
            <lem wit="MS2">letters,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
letters

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2411"/>
too

          <ptr target="#l12123" type="alt" xml:id="te2411"/>
; so if you’ll get him to write a line

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5152"/>
or

          <app from="pr5152" n="254.20 (387.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7156">
            <lem wit="A">or</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7157">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
so we can

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5153"/>
com—

          <app from="pr5153" n="254.21 (387.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7158">
            <lem wit="MS2">com—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">com——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63243">
“He

          <hi rend="italic">can’t</hi>
write with his left hand,” says the old gentleman. “If he could use his right hand, you would see that he wrote his own letters and mine too. Look at both, please—they’re by the same hand.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63248">The lawyer done it, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63251">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2412"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l12124" type="alt" xml:id="te2412"/>
believe it’s so—and if it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5154"/>
ain’t so

          <app from="pr5154" n="254.27 (388.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7159">
            <lem wit="MS2">ain’t so</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">ain’t so,</rdg>
          </app>
there’s a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2413"/>
heap

          <ptr target="#l12125" type="alt" xml:id="te2413"/>
stronger resemblance than I’d noticed before, anyway. Well, well, well! I thought we was right on the track of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5155"/>
slution

          <app from="pr5155" n="254.29 (389.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7160">
            <lem wit="A">slution</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">solution</rdg>
          </app>
, but it’s gone to grass, partly. But anyway,

          <hi rend="italic">one</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5156"/>
thing is

          <app from="pr5156" n="254.30 (389.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7161">
            <lem wit="A">thing is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thing’s</rdg>
          </app>
proved—

          <hi rend="italic">these</hi>
two ain’t either of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2414"/>
’em

          <ptr target="#l12126" type="alt" xml:id="te2414"/>
Wilkses”—and he wagged his head towards the king and the duke.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63296">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2415"/>
Well

          <ptr target="#l12127" type="alt" xml:id="te2415"/>
, what do you think?—that muleheaded old fool wouldn’t give in

          <hi rend="italic">then!</hi>
Indeed he wouldn’t. Said it warn’t no fair test. Said his brother William was the cussedest joker in the world, and hadn’t

          <hi rend="italic">tried</hi>
to write—

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
see William was going to play one of his jokes the minute he put the pen to paper. And so he warmed up and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5157"/>
went

          <app from="pr5157" n="254.36 (390.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7162">
            <lem wit="A">went</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">went to</rdg>
          </app>
warbling and warbling right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2416"/>
along, till he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5158"/>
actuly

          <app from="pr5158" n="254.37 (390.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7163">
            <lem wit="A">actuly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">actually</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12128" type="alt" xml:id="te2416"/>
beginning to believe what he was saying,

          <hi rend="italic">himself</hi>
—but pretty soon the new old gentleman

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2417"/>
broke

          <ptr target="#l12129" type="alt" xml:id="te2417"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5159"/>
in

          <app from="pr5159" n="254.39 (390.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7164">
            <lem wit="MS2">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">in,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63345">
          <pb n="255" xml:id="pb0255"/>
“I’ve thought of something. Is there anybody here that helped

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2418"/>
to lay out

          <ptr target="#l12130" type="alt" xml:id="te2418"/>
my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5160"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2419"/>
br—

          <ptr target="#l12131" type="alt" xml:id="te2419"/>
          <app from="pr5160" n="255.2 (390.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7165">
            <lem wit="A">br—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">b—</rdg>
          </app>
helped to lay out the late Peter Wilks for burying?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63361">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5161"/>
Yes

          <app from="pr5161" n="255.3 (391.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7166">
            <lem wit="MS2">Yes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Yes,</rdg>
          </app>
” says somebody, “me and Ab Turner done it.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2420"/>
We’re

          <ptr target="#l12132" type="alt" xml:id="te2420"/>
both here.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63375">
Then the old man turns towards the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5162"/>
king

          <app from="pr5162" n="255.5 (391.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7167">
            <lem wit="MS2">king</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">king,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63385">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2421"/>
“Peraps

          <ptr target="#l12133" type="alt" xml:id="te2421"/>
this gentleman can tell me what was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5163"/>
tattooed

          <app from="pr5163" n="255.6 (391.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7168">
            <lem wit="MS2">tattooed</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tatooed</rdg>
          </app>
on his breast?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63398">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5164"/>
Blamed

          <app from="pr5164" n="255.8 (391.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7169">
            <lem wit="A">Blamed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m blamed</rdg>
          </app>
if the king didn’t have to brace up mighty quick, or he’d a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5165"/>
squshed down like a bluff bank that the river has cut under

          <app from="pr5165" n="255.9 (391.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7170">
            <lem wit="A">squshed . . . under</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kerflummuxed</rdg>
          </app>
, it took him so sudden—and mind

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5166"/>
you

          <app from="pr5166" n="255.10 (392.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7171">
            <lem wit="MS2">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you,</rdg>
          </app>
it was a thing that was calculated to make most

          <hi rend="italic">anybody</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5167"/>
sqush,

          <app from="pr5167" n="255.11 (392.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7172">
            <lem wit="C">sqush,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kerflummux,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">sqush</rdg>
          </app>
to get fetched such a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5168"/>
solid one

          <app from="pr5168" n="255.11 (392.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7173">
            <lem wit="A">solid one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">stunner</rdg>
          </app>
as that without any notice—because how was

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
going to know what was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5169"/>
tattooed

          <app from="pr5169" n="255.13 (392.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7174">
            <lem wit="C">tattooed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">tattoed</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">tatooed</rdg>
          </app>
on the man? He whitened a little; he couldn’t help it; and it was mighty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5170"/>
still,

          <app from="pr5170" n="255.14 (392.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7175">
            <lem wit="MS2">still,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
still

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in there, and everybody bending a little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5171"/>
forwards

          <app from="pr5171" n="255.14–15 (392.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7176">
            <lem wit="A">forwards</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">forward</rdg>
          </app>
and gazing at him. Says I to myself,

          <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
he’ll throw up the sponge—there ain’t no more use. Well, did he?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5172"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2422"/>
A body can’t hardly believe it, but he didn’t.

          <ptr target="#l12134" type="alt" xml:id="te2422"/>
          <app from="pr5172" n="255.16–17 (393.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7177">
            <lem wit="A">A . . . didn’t.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I wish I’m a nigger if he did.</rdg>
          </app>
I reckon he thought he’d keep the thing up till he tired them people out, so they’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5173"/>
thin out

          <app from="pr5173" n="255.18 (393.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7178">
            <lem wit="MS2">thin out</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">thin out,</rdg>
          </app>
and him and the duke could break loose and get away. Anyway, he set there, and pretty soon he begun to smile, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63496">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2423"/>
“Mf!

          <ptr target="#l12135" type="alt" xml:id="te2423"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5174"/>
It’s

          <app from="pr5174" n="255.21 (393.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7179">
            <lem wit="A">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Its</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <hi rend="italic">very</hi>
tough question,

          <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
it!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5175"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Yes</hi>
          <app from="pr5175" n="255.21 (393.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7180">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Yes</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Yes</rdg>
          </app>
, sir, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5176"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr5176" n="255.21 (393.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7181">
            <lem wit="A">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">can</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
tell you what’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5177"/>
tattooed

          <app from="pr5177" n="255.22 (393.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7182">
            <lem wit="MS2">tattooed</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">tatooed</rdg>
          </app>
on his breast. It’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5178"/>
jest

          <app from="pr5178" n="255.22 (393.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7183">
            <lem wit="A">jest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">just</rdg>
          </app>
a small, thin, blue arrow—that’s what it is; and if you don’t look

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2424"/>
clost

          <ptr target="#l12136" type="alt" xml:id="te2424"/>
, you can’t see it.

          <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
what do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5179"/>
you say

          <app from="pr5179" n="255.24 (394.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7184">
            <lem wit="A">you say</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">say</rdg>
          </app>
—hey?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63567">
Well,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
never see anything like that old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5180"/>
blister,

          <app from="pr5180" n="255.25 (394.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7185">
            <lem wit="C">blister,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rip,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">blister</rdg>
          </app>
for clean out-and-out cheek.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63582">
The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5181"/>
new old

          <app from="pr5181" n="255.27 (394.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7186">
            <lem wit="A">new old</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">old new</rdg>
          </app>
gentleman turns brisk towards Ab Turner and his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2425"/>
pard,

          <ptr target="#l12137" type="alt" xml:id="te2425"/>
and his eye lights up like he judged he’d got the king

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
time, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63599">“There—you’ve heard what he said! Was there any such mark on Peter Wilks’s breast?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63602">Both of them spoke up and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63604">“We didn’t see no such mark.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63606">
“Good!” says the old gentleman. “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5182"/>
Now

          <app from="pr5182" n="255.34 (395.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7187">
            <lem wit="MS2">Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Now,</rdg>
          </app>
what you

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
see on his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5183"/>
breast

          <app from="pr5183" n="255.35 (395.7–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7188">
            <lem wit="A">breast</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
breast—or what you

              <hi rend="italic">could</hi>
a seen, anyway, for they’re there—

            </rdg>
          </app>
was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2426"/>
small dim

          <ptr target="#l12138" type="alt" xml:id="te2426"/>
P, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5184"/>
B,

          <app from="pr5184" n="255.35 (395.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7189">
            <lem wit="MS2">B,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
B

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2427"/>
(which is an initial he dropped when he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5185"/>
young,)

          <ptr target="#l12139" type="alt" xml:id="te2427"/>
          <app from="pr5185" n="255.36 (395.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7190">
            <lem wit="MS2">young,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">young),</rdg>
          </app>
and a W, with dashes between them, so: P—B—W”—and he marked them that way on a piece of paper. “Come—ain’t that what you saw?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63654">Both of them spoke up again, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63656">
          <pb n="pb0256" xml:id="pb0256"/>
“No, we

          <hi rend="italic">didn’t.</hi>
We never

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2428"/>
seen

          <ptr target="#l12140" type="alt" xml:id="te2428"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5186"/>
any

          <app from="pr5186" n="256.1 (396.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7191">
            <lem wit="A">any</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5187"/>
marks,

          <app from="pr5187" n="256.1 (396.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7192">
            <lem wit="MS2">marks,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
marks

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at all.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63681">
Well, everybody

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
in a state of mind,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5188"/>
now;

          <app from="pr5188" n="256.2 (396.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7193">
            <lem wit="A">now;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">now!</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5189"/>
they sings out

          <app from="pr5189" n="256.2 (396.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la7194">
            <lem wit="A">they sings out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">some shouted out and said</rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63702">
“The whole

          <hi rend="italic">bilin</hi>
’ of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5190"/>
’m

          <app from="pr5190" n="256.3 (396.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7195">
            <lem wit="A">’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’em</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5191"/>
’s

          <app from="pr5191" n="256.3 (396.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7196">
            <lem wit="A">’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">is</rdg>
          </app>
frauds!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5192"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2429"/>
Le’s

          <ptr target="#l12141" type="alt" xml:id="te2429"/>
          <app from="pr5192" n="256.3 (396.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7197">
            <lem wit="A">Le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Less</rdg>
          </app>
duck ’em!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5193"/>
le’s

          <app from="pr5193" n="256.3 (396.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7198">
            <lem wit="A">le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">less</rdg>
          </app>
drown ’em!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5194"/>
le’s

          <app from="pr5194" n="256.4 (396.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7199">
            <lem wit="A">le’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">less</rdg>
          </app>
ride ’em on a rail!” and everybody was whooping at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2430"/>
once

          <ptr target="#l12142" type="alt" xml:id="te2430"/>
, and there was a rattling pow-wow. But the lawyer he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5195"/>
jumps

          <app from="pr5195" n="256.5 (397.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7200">
            <lem wit="A">jumps</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jumps up</rdg>
          </app>
on the table and yells, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63762">
“Gentlemen—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5196"/>
gentle

          <hi rend="italic">men</hi>
          <app from="pr5196" n="256.7 (397.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7201">
            <lem wit="A">
gentle

              <hi rend="italic">men</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
gentle-

              <lb/>
              <hi rend="italic">men</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2431"/>
Hear

          <ptr target="#l12143" type="alt" xml:id="te2431"/>
me just a word—just a

          <hi rend="italic">single</hi>
word—if you

          <hi rend="smallcaps">please</hi>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5197"/>
There’s

          <app from="pr5197" n="256.8 (397.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7202">
            <lem wit="A">There’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">There</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5198"/>
one

          <app from="pr5198" n="256.8 (397.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7203">
            <lem wit="A">one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">one</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5199"/>
way,

          <app from="pr5199" n="256.8 (397.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7204">
            <lem wit="MS2">way,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
way

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2432"/>
let’s

          <ptr target="#l12144" type="alt" xml:id="te2432"/>
go and dig up the corpse and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5200"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2433"/>
look

          <ptr target="#l12145" type="alt" xml:id="te2433"/>
.

          <app from="pr5200" n="256.9 (397.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7205">
            <lem wit="A">look.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">look!</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63830">That took them.</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y25601">
          <graphic url="y25601.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">gentlemen</hi>
—

            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5201"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">gentle</hi>
            <hi rend="italic">men!</hi>
            <app from="pr5201" n="256 caption" type="e" xml:id="la7206">
              <lem wit="C">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">gentle</hi>
                <hi rend="italic">men!</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7207">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">gentlemen</hi>
!

              </rdg>
            </app>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63857">“Hooray!” they all shouted, and was starting right off; but the lawyer and the doctor sung out:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63860">
“Hold on, hold on! Collar all these four men and the boy, and fetch

          <hi rend="italic">them</hi>
along,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2434"/>
too!”

          <ptr target="#l12146" type="alt" xml:id="te2434"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63868">
“We’ll do it!” they all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5202"/>
shouted;

          <app from="pr5202" n="256.15 (398.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7208">
            <lem wit="MS2">shouted;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shouted:</rdg>
          </app>
“and if we don’t find them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5203"/>
marks,

          <app from="pr5203" n="256.15 (398.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7209">
            <lem wit="MS2">marks,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
marks

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
we’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2435"/>
lynch

          <ptr target="#l12147" type="alt" xml:id="te2435"/>
the whole gang!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63891">
I

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
scared, now, I tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5204"/>
you.

          <app from="pr5204" n="256.17 (398.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7210">
            <lem wit="A">you.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you!</rdg>
          </app>
But there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5205"/>
no

          <app from="pr5205" n="256.17 (398.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7211">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">any</rdg>
          </app>
getting away, you know. They gripped us all, and marched us right along, straight

          <pb n="257" xml:id="pb0257"/>
for the graveyard, which was a mile and a half down the river, and the whole town at our heels, for we made noise

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5206"/>
enough

          <app from="pr5206" n="257.2 (399.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7212">
            <lem wit="A">enough</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">enough, you bet</rdg>
          </app>
, and it was only

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2436"/>
nine

          <ptr target="#l12148" type="alt" xml:id="te2436"/>
in the evening.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63925">
As we went by our house I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5207"/>
wished

          <app from="pr5207" n="257.4 (399.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7213">
            <lem wit="A">wished</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">did wish</rdg>
          </app>
I hadn’t sent Mary Jane out of town; because now if I could tip her the wink, she’d light out and save me, and blow on our

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5208"/>
dead-beats.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e63937">
Well

          <app from="pr5208" n="257.6–7 (399.15–400.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7214">
            <lem wit="A">dead-beats. [¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
dead-beats.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7215">extra line space</note>
[¶] Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, we swarmed along down the river road, just carrying on like wild-cats; and to make it more scary, the sky was darking up, and the lightning beginning to wink and flitter, and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2437"/>
wind

          <ptr target="#l12149" type="alt" xml:id="te2437"/>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5209"/>
shiver

          <app from="pr5209" n="257.10 (400.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la7216">
            <lem wit="A">shiver</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">moan and shiver</rdg>
          </app>
amongst the leaves. This was the most awful trouble and most dangersome I ever was in; and I was kinder

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5210"/>
stunned,

          <app from="pr5210" n="257.11 (400.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7217">
            <lem wit="MS2">stunned,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stunned;</rdg>
          </app>
everything was going so different from what I had allowed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5211"/>
for:

          <app from="pr5211" n="257.12 (400.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7218">
            <lem wit="MS2">for:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">for;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5212"/>
’stead

          <app from="pr5212" n="257.12 (400.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7219">
            <lem wit="MS2">’stead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stead</rdg>
          </app>
of being fixed so I could take my own time, if I wanted to, and see all the fun, and have Mary Jane at my back to save me and set me free when the close-fit come, here was nothing in the world betwixt me and sudden

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5213"/>
death

          <app from="pr5213" n="257.16 (401.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7220">
            <lem wit="A">death</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">death with a halter</rdg>
          </app>
but just them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5214"/>
tattoo-marks

          <app from="pr5214" n="257.16 (401.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7221">
            <lem wit="C">tattoo-marks</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">little tattoo-marks</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">tatoo-marks</rdg>
          </app>
. If they didn’t find them—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64004">
I couldn’t bear to think about it; and yet, somehow, I couldn’t think about nothing else. It got darker and darker, and it was a beautiful time to give the crowd the slip; but that big husky had me by the wrist—Hines—and a body might as well try to give

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5215"/>
Goliar

          <app from="pr5215" n="257.21 (401.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7222">
            <lem wit="A">Goliar</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a vise</rdg>
          </app>
the slip. He dragged me right along, he was so excited; and I had to run to keep up.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64014">
When they got there they swarmed into the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5216"/>
graveyard,

          <app from="pr5216" n="257.24 (401.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7223">
            <lem wit="MS2">graveyard,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
graveyard

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5217"/>
washed

          <app from="pr5217" n="257.25 (401.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7224">
            <lem wit="A">washed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">washed out</rdg>
          </app>
over it like an overflow. And when they got to the grave, they found they had about a hundred times as many

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5218"/>
shovels

          <app from="pr5218" n="257.26 (402.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7225">
            <lem wit="A">shovels</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">spades</rdg>
          </app>
as they wanted, but nobody hadn’t thought to fetch a lantern. But they sailed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5219"/>
in to

          <app from="pr5219" n="257.28 (402.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7226">
            <lem wit="MS2">in to</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">into</rdg>
          </app>
digging, anyway, by the flicker of the lightning, and sent a man to the nearest house a half a mile off, to borrow one.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64049">
So they dug and dug, like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5220"/>
everything

          <app from="pr5220" n="257.30 (402.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7227">
            <lem wit="A">everything</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mad</rdg>
          </app>
; and it got awful dark, and the rain started, and the wind swished and swushed along, and the lightning come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5221"/>
brisker and brisker

          <app from="pr5221" n="257.32 (402.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7228">
            <lem wit="A">brisker and brisker</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">faster and sharper</rdg>
          </app>
, and the thunder boomed; but them people never took no notice of it, they was so full of this business; and one minute you could see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5222"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2438"/>
every thing

          <ptr target="#l12150" type="alt" xml:id="te2438"/>
          <app from="pr5222" n="257.34 (403.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7229">
            <lem wit="MS2">every thing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">everything</rdg>
          </app>
and every face in that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5223"/>
big

          <app from="pr5223" n="257.35 (403.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7230">
            <lem wit="A">big</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">packed</rdg>
          </app>
crowd, and the shovelfuls of dirt sailing up out of the grave, and the next second the dark

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5224"/>
wiped

          <app from="pr5224" n="257.36 (403.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7231">
            <lem wit="A">wiped</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blotted</rdg>
          </app>
it all out, and you couldn’t see nothing at all.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64094">
At last they got out the coffin, and begun to unscrew the lid, and

          <pb n="258" xml:id="pb0258"/>
then such another crowding, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5225"/>
shouldering

          <app from="pr5225" n="258.1 (403.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7232">
            <lem wit="MS2">shouldering</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shouldering,</rdg>
          </app>
and shoving as there was, to scrouge in and get a sight, you never see; and in the dark, that way, it was awful.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2439"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5226"/>
Hines he

          <app from="pr5226" n="258.3 (403.18)" type="e" xml:id="la7233">
            <lem wit="A">Hines he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Hines</rdg>
          </app>
hurt my wrist dreadful,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5227"/>
pulling

          <app from="pr5227" n="258.3 (403verso.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7234">
            <lem wit="A">pulling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a pulling</rdg>
          </app>
and tugging so, and I reckon he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5228"/>
clean

          <app from="pr5228" n="258.4 (403verso.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7235">
            <lem wit="A">clean</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">had clean</rdg>
          </app>
forgot I was in the world, he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5229"/>
so

          <app from="pr5229" n="258.5 (403verso.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7236">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that</rdg>
          </app>
excited and panting.

          <ptr target="#l12151" type="alt" xml:id="te2439"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64139">All of a sudden the lightning let go a perfect sluice of white glare, and somebody sings out:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64141">“By the living jingo, here’s the bag of gold on his breast!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64144">
Hines let out a whoop, like everybody else, and dropped my wrist and give a big surge to bust his way in and get a look, and the way I lit out and shinned for the road in the dark,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5230"/>
there ain’t nobody can tell

          <app from="pr5230" n="258.11–12 (404.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la7237">
            <lem wit="A">there . . . tell</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was as near as I can state it, undescribable</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64154">
I had the road all to myself, and I fairly flew—leastways I had it all to myself except

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2440"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5231"/>
solid

          <app from="pr5231" n="258.14 (405.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7238">
            <lem wit="A">solid</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">company of the solid</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12152" type="alt" xml:id="te2440"/>
dark, and the now-and-then glares, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5232"/>
buzzing

          <app from="pr5232" n="258.15 (405.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7239">
            <lem wit="A">buzzing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">singing</rdg>
          </app>
of the rain, and the thrashing of the wind, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5233"/>
splitting

          <app from="pr5233" n="258.16 (405.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7240">
            <lem wit="A">splitting</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">booming</rdg>
          </app>
of the thunder; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5234"/>
sure as you are born

          <app from="pr5234" n="258.16 (405.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7241">
            <lem wit="A">sure as you are born</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you bet you</rdg>
          </app>
I did clip it along!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64192">
When I struck the town, I see there warn’t nobody out in the storm, so I never hunted for no back streets, but humped it straight through the main one; and when I begun to get towards our house I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5235"/>
aimed

          <app from="pr5235" n="258.20 (405.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7242">
            <lem wit="A">aimed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">peeled</rdg>
          </app>
my eye and set it. No light there; the house all dark—which made me feel

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5236"/>
sorry

          <app from="pr5236" n="258.21 (405.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7243">
            <lem wit="A">sorry</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kinder sorry</rdg>
          </app>
and disappointed, I didn’t know why. But at last, just as I was sailing by,

          <hi rend="italic">flash</hi>
comes the light in Mary Jane’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2441"/>
window!

          <ptr target="#l12153" type="alt" xml:id="te2441"/>
and my heart swelled up sudden, like to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2442"/>
bust;

          <ptr target="#l12154" type="alt" xml:id="te2442"/>
and the same second the house and all was behind me in the dark, and wasn’t ever

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5237"/>
going

          <app from="pr5237" n="258.24 (406.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7244">
            <lem wit="A">going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7245">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to be before me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5238"/>
no more

          <app from="pr5238" n="258.25 (406.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7246">
            <lem wit="A">no more</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">again</rdg>
          </app>
in this world. She

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
the best girl

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5239"/>
I ever see,

          <app from="pr5239" n="258.25–26 (406.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7247">
            <lem wit="A">I ever see,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that ever was!</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5240"/>
had the most sand

          <app from="pr5240" n="258.26 (406.10–12)" type="e" xml:id="la7248">
            <lem wit="A">had the most sand</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you could depend on her like the everlasting sun and the stars, every time</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64260">
The minute I was far enough above the town to see I could make the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5241"/>
towhead

          <app from="pr5241" n="258.28 (406.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7249">
            <lem wit="MS2">towhead</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
tow-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
, I begun to look sharp for a boat to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2443"/>
borrow

          <ptr target="#l12155" type="alt" xml:id="te2443"/>
; and the first time the lightning showed me one that wasn’t chained, I snatched it and shoved. It was a canoe, and warn’t fastened with nothing but a rope. The

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5242"/>
towhead

          <app from="pr5242" n="258.31 (407.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7250">
            <lem wit="A">towhead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
tow-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
was a rattling big distance off, away out there in the middle of the river, but I didn’t lose no time; and when I struck the raft at last, I was so fagged I would a just laid down to blow and gasp if I could afforded it. But I didn’t. As I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5243"/>
sprung

          <app from="pr5243" n="258.34 (407.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7251">
            <lem wit="A">sprung</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hopped</rdg>
          </app>
aboard I sung out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64295">
“Out with you Jim,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2444"/>
and set

          <ptr target="#l12156" type="alt" xml:id="te2444"/>
her loose! Glory be to goodness, we’re shut of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5244"/>
them

          <app from="pr5244" n="258.37 (407.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7252">
            <lem wit="A">them</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them rapscallions</rdg>
          </app>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="noindent">
          <pb n="259" xml:id="pb0259"/>
        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y25901">
          <graphic url="y25901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">
jim

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5253"/>
lit

            </hi>
            <app from="pr5253" n="259 caption" type="e" xml:id="la7261">
              <lem wit="C">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">lit</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7262">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">let</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">out</hi>
.”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64329">
Jim lit out, and was a coming for me with both

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2445"/>
arms

          <ptr target="#l12157" type="alt" xml:id="te2445"/>
spread,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2446"/>
he was so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5245"/>
full

          <app from="pr5245" n="259.2 (408.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7253">
            <lem wit="A">full</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">brim full</rdg>
          </app>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5246"/>
joy,

          <app from="pr5246" n="259.2 (408.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7254">
            <lem wit="MS2">joy,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">joy;</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12158" type="alt" xml:id="te2446"/>
but when I glimpsed him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5247"/>
in

          <app from="pr5247" n="259.2 (408.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7255">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">under</rdg>
          </app>
the lightning,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2447"/>
my

          <ptr target="#l12159" type="alt" xml:id="te2447"/>
heart

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5248"/>
shot

          <app from="pr5248" n="259.3 (408.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7256">
            <lem wit="A">shot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">flopped</rdg>
          </app>
up in my mouth, and I went overboard backwards; for I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5249"/>
forgot

          <app from="pr5249" n="259.4 (408.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7257">
            <lem wit="A">forgot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">had forgot</rdg>
          </app>
he was old King

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5250"/>
Lear

          <app from="pr5250" n="259.4 (408.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7258">
            <lem wit="A">Lear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Leer</rdg>
          </app>
and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5251"/>
drownded

          <app from="pr5251" n="259.4 (408.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7259">
            <lem wit="A">drownded</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sick, solid-blue</rdg>
          </app>
A-rab

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5252"/>
all in one

          <app from="pr5252" n="259.4 (408.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7260">
            <lem wit="A">all in one</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">combined</rdg>
          </app>
, and it most scared the livers and lights out of me. But Jim fished me out, and was going to hug me and bless me, and so on, he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5254"/>
so glad

          <app from="pr5254" n="259.6 (408.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7263">
            <lem wit="A">so glad</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">glad</rdg>
          </app>
I was back and we was shut of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5255"/>
king and the duke

          <app from="pr5255" n="259.7 (408.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7264">
            <lem wit="A">king and the duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rapscallions</rdg>
          </app>
, but I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64426">“Not now—have it for breakfast, have it for breakfast! Cut loose and let her slide!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64428">
So, in two seconds, away we went, a sliding down the river, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2448"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12160" type="alt" xml:id="te2448"/>
          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
seem so good to be free again and all by

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5256"/>
ourselves

          <app from="pr5256" n="259.11 (409.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7265">
            <lem wit="A">ourselves</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">our two selves</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5257"/>
on the big river and nobody to bother us.

          <app from="pr5257" n="259.11–12 (409.6–8)" type="e" xml:id="la7266">
            <lem wit="A">on . . . us.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">once more, and the big friendly river stretching out so homelike before us!</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5258"/>
I had

          <app from="pr5258" n="259.12 (409.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la7267">
            <lem wit="A">I had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Well, sir, I just

              <hi rend="italic">had</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to skip around a bit, and jump up and crack my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5259"/>
heels

          <app from="pr5259" n="259.13 (409.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la7268">
            <lem wit="A">heels</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">heels together</rdg>
          </app>
a few times, I couldn’t help it; but about the third crack, I noticed a sound that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5260"/>
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2449"/>
knowed

          <ptr target="#l12161" type="alt" xml:id="te2449"/>
          <app from="pr5260" n="259.14 (409.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7269">
            <lem wit="A">I knowed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
knowed

            </rdg>
          </app>
mighty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5261"/>
well,

          <app from="pr5261" n="259.14 (409.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7270">
            <lem wit="MS2">well,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
well

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5262"/>
held my breath,

          <app from="pr5262" n="259.14–15 (409.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la7271">
            <lem wit="C">held my breath,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cocked eye and ear,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">held my breath</rdg>
          </app>
and listened and waited—and sure enough, when the

          <pb n="260" xml:id="pb0260"/>
next flash

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5263"/>
busted

          <app from="pr5263" n="260.1 (409.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7272">
            <lem wit="A">busted</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">glared</rdg>
          </app>
out over the water, here they come!—and just a laying to their oars and making their skiff hum! It was the king and the duke.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64510">
So I wilted right down onto the planks, then, and give

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2450"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l12162" type="alt" xml:id="te2450"/>
; and it was all I could do to keep from crying.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0408">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXX.</head>
        <pb n="261" xml:id="pb0261"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y26101">
          <graphic url="y26101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5264"/>
Chapter XXX. When

            <app from="pr5264" n="261 title–1 (410.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7273">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXX. [¶] When</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7274">
no

                  <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
                </note>
When

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2611">
          <graphic url="hf2611.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the king shakes huck</hi>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e64536">they got aboard, the king went for me, and shook me by the collar, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64538">“Tryin’ to give us the slip, was ye, you pup! Tired of our company—hey?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64540">I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64542">
“No, your majesty, we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5265"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr5265" n="261.8 (410.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7275">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">warnt</rdg>
          </app>
—

          <hi rend="italic">please</hi>
don’t, your majesty!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64555">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2451"/>
Quick

          <ptr target="#l12163" type="alt" xml:id="te2451"/>
, then, and tell us what

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
your idea, or I’ll shake the insides out o’ you!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64564">
“Honest, I’ll tell you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5266"/>
every thing

          <app from="pr5266" n="261.13–14 (411.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7276">
            <lem wit="MS2">every thing</lem>
            <rdg>everything</rdg>
          </app>
, just as it happened, your majesty. The man that had aholt of me was very good to me, and kept saying he had a boy about as big as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5267"/>
me,

          <app from="pr5267" n="261.18 (411.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7277">
            <lem wit="MS2">me,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that died last year, and he was sorry to see a boy in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2452"/>
such

          <ptr target="#l12164" type="alt" xml:id="te2452"/>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5268"/>
dangerous

          <app from="pr5268" n="261.19 (411.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7278">
            <lem wit="A">dangerous</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dangersome</rdg>
          </app>
fix; and when they was all took by surprise by finding the gold, and made a rush for the coffin, he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2453"/>
lets

          <ptr target="#l12165" type="alt" xml:id="te2453"/>
go of me and whispers, ‘Heel it, now, or they’ll hang ye, sure!’ and I lit out. It didn’t seem no good for

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
to stay—

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
couldn’t do nothing, and I didn’t want to be hung if I could get away. So I never stopped running till I found

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5269"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0073"/>
the canoe

          <ptr target="#tb0073" type="te" xml:id="tv0073"/>
          <app from="pr5269" n="261.24 (412.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7279">
            <lem wit="A">the canoe</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a canoe</rdg>
          </app>
; and when I got here I told Jim to hurry, or they’d catch me and hang

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5270"/>
me,

          <app from="pr5270" n="261.25 (412.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7280">
            <lem wit="MS2">me,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet, and said I was afeard you and the duke wasn’t alive, now, and I was awful sorry, and so was Jim, and was awful glad when we see you coming, you may ask Jim if I didn’t.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64624">
Jim said it was so; and the king told him to shut up, and said, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5271"/>
O

          <app from="pr5271" n="261.28 (412.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7281">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, yes, it’s

          <hi rend="italic">mighty</hi>
likely!” and shook me up again, and said he reckoned he’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5272"/>
drownd

          <app from="pr5272" n="261.30 (412.18)" type="e" xml:id="la7282">
            <lem wit="A">drownd</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">drown</rdg>
          </app>
me. But the duke says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64645">
          <pb n="262" xml:id="pb0262"/>
“Leggo

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2454"/>
the boy,

          <ptr target="#l12166" type="alt" xml:id="te2454"/>
you old idiot! Would

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
a done any different? Did you inquire

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5273"/>
around

          <app from="pr5273" n="262.2 (413.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7283">
            <lem wit="A">around</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <lb/>
round

            </rdg>
          </app>
for

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
, when you got loose?

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t remember it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64672">
So the king let go of me, and begun to cuss that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5274"/>
town,

          <app from="pr5274" n="262.4 (413.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7284">
            <lem wit="MS2">town,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
town

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and everybody in it. But the duke says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64682">
“You better a blame sight give

          <hi rend="italic">yourself</hi>
a good cussing, for you’re the one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2455"/>
that’s entitled to it

          <ptr target="#l12167" type="alt" xml:id="te2455"/>
most. You hain’t done a thing, from the start, that had any sense in it, except coming out so cool and cheeky with that imaginary blue-arrow mark. That

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
bright—it was right down bully; and it was the thing that saved us. For if it hadn’t been for that, they’d a jailed us till

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2456"/>
them

          <ptr target="#l12168" type="alt" xml:id="te2456"/>
Englishmen’s baggage

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5275"/>
come,

          <app from="pr5275" n="262.11 (414.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7285">
            <lem wit="MS2">come,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">come—</rdg>
          </app>
and then—the penitentiary, you bet! But that trick took ’em to the graveyard, and the gold done us a still bigger kindness; for if the excited fools hadn’t let go all holts and made that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2457"/>
rush

          <ptr target="#l12169" type="alt" xml:id="te2457"/>
to get a look, we’d a slept in our cravats to-night—cravats warranted to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2458"/>
          <hi rend="italic">wear</hi>
,

          <ptr target="#l12170" type="alt" xml:id="te2458"/>
too—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5276"/>
longer than

          <app from="pr5276" n="262.16 (414.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7286">
            <lem wit="A">longer than</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">longer’n</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">we’d</hi>
need ’em.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64728">
They was still a minute—thinking—then the king says, kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5277"/>
absent-minded

          <app from="pr5277" n="262.18 (415.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7287">
            <lem wit="MS2">absent-minded</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
absent-

              <lb/>
minded

            </rdg>
          </app>
like:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64740">
“Mf! And we reckoned the

          <hi rend="italic">niggers</hi>
stole it!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64745">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2459"/>
That made me squirm!

          <ptr target="#l12171" type="alt" xml:id="te2459"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64749">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5278"/>
Yes

          <app from="pr5278" n="262.21 (415.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7288">
            <lem wit="A">Yes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Yes</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
,” says the duke,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5279"/>
kinder

          <app from="pr5279" n="262.21 (415.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7289">
            <lem wit="A">kinder</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kind of</rdg>
          </app>
slow, and deliberate, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5280"/>
sarcastic.

          <app from="pr5280" n="262.21 (415.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7290">
            <lem wit="MS2">sarcastic.</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sarcastic,</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <hi rend="italic">We</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5281"/>
did.

          <app from="pr5281" n="262.22 (415.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7291">
            <lem wit="A">did.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">did!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64787">After about a half a minute, the king drawls out:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64789">
“Leastways—

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
did.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64794">The duke says, the same way:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64796">
“On the contrary—

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
did.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64801">The king kind of ruffles up, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64804">
“Looky here, Bilgewater, what’r you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2460"/>
referrin’

          <ptr target="#l12172" type="alt" xml:id="te2460"/>
to?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64810">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2461"/>
The duke

          <ptr target="#l12173" type="alt" xml:id="te2461"/>
says, pretty brisk:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64815">
“When it comes to that, maybe you’ll let me ask, what was

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
referring to?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64820">
“Shucks!” says the king, very sarcastic; “but

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t know—maybe you was asleep, and didn’t know what you was about.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64825">The duke bristles right up, now, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64827">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5282"/>
O

          <app from="pr5282" n="262.35 (416.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7292">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, let

          <hi rend="italic">up</hi>
on this cussed nonsense—do you take me for a blame’ fool? Don’t you reckon

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know who

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2462"/>
hid

          <ptr target="#l12174" type="alt" xml:id="te2462"/>
that money in that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2463"/>
coffin?”

          <ptr target="#l12175" type="alt" xml:id="te2463"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64851">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5283"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Yes</hi>
          <app from="pr5283" n="262.37 (417.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7293">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Yes</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Yes</hi>
,

            </rdg>
          </app>
sir! I know you

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
know—because you done it yourself!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64868">“It’s a lie!”—and the duke went for him. The king sings out:</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y26301">
          <graphic url="y26301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the duke went for him</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64875">
          <pb n="263" xml:id="pb0263"/>
“Take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5284"/>
y’r

          <app from="pr5284" n="263.1 (417.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7294">
            <lem wit="A">y’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your</rdg>
          </app>
hands off!—leggo my throat!—I take it all back!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64885">The duke says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64888">
“Well, you just own up,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2464"/>
first,

          <ptr target="#l12176" type="alt" xml:id="te2464"/>
that you

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
hide that money there, intending to give me the slip one of these days, and come back and dig it up, and have it all to yourself.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64897">
“Wait

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2465"/>
jest

          <ptr target="#l12177" type="alt" xml:id="te2465"/>
a minute, duke—answer me this

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2466"/>
one question,

          <ptr target="#l12178" type="alt" xml:id="te2466"/>
honest and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5285"/>
fair:

          <app from="pr5285" n="263.7 (418.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7295">
            <lem wit="MS2">fair:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fair;</rdg>
          </app>
if you didn’t put the money there, say it, and I’ll

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5286"/>
b’lieve

          <app from="pr5286" n="263.7 (418.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7296">
            <lem wit="A">b’lieve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">believe</rdg>
          </app>
you, and take back everything

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5287"/>
I

          <app from="pr5287" n="263.8 (418.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7297">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’ve</rdg>
          </app>
said.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64932">
“You old scoundrel, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2467"/>
didn’t, and

          <ptr target="#l12179" type="alt" xml:id="te2467"/>
you know I didn’t. There, now!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64938">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5288"/>
Well

          <app from="pr5288" n="263.10 (418.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7298">
            <lem wit="MS2">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
then, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5289"/>
b’lieve

          <app from="pr5289" n="263.10 (418.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7299">
            <lem wit="A">b’lieve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">believe</rdg>
          </app>
you. But answer me

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2468"/>
only jest this

          <ptr target="#l12180" type="alt" xml:id="te2468"/>
one more—now

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
git

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5290"/>
mad:

          <app from="pr5290" n="263.11 (418.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7300">
            <lem wit="MS2">mad:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mad;</rdg>
          </app>
didn’t you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2469"/>
have

          <ptr target="#l12181" type="alt" xml:id="te2469"/>
it in your

          <hi rend="italic">mind</hi>
to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2470"/>
hook the money and hide

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5291"/>
it?

          <ptr target="#l12182" type="alt" xml:id="te2470"/>
”

          <app from="pr5291" n="263.12 (418.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7301">
            <lem wit="A">it?”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
it?

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7302">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64993">The duke never said nothing for a little bit; then he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e64995">
“Well—I don’t care if I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2471"/>
          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
,

          <ptr target="#l12183" type="alt" xml:id="te2471"/>
I didn’t

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
it, anyway. But you not only had it in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5292"/>
mind

          <app from="pr5292" n="263.15 (419.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7303">
            <lem wit="A">mind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your mind</rdg>
          </app>
to do it, but you

          <hi rend="italic">done</hi>
it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65018">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5293"/>
wisht

          <app from="pr5293" n="263.16 (419.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7304">
            <lem wit="A">wisht</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wish</rdg>
          </app>
I may never die if I done it, duke, and that’s honest. I won’t say I warn’t

          <hi rend="italic">goin’</hi>
to do it,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5294"/>
because

          <app from="pr5294" n="263.17 (419.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7305">
            <lem wit="A">because</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">becuz</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <hi rend="italic">was;</hi>
but you—I mean

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2472"/>
somebody

          <ptr target="#l12184" type="alt" xml:id="te2472"/>
—got in ahead

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5295"/>
o’

          <app from="pr5295" n="263.18 (419.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7306">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
me.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65055">
“It’s a lie! You done it, and you got to

          <hi rend="italic">say</hi>
you done it,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5296"/>
or—

          <app from="pr5296" n="263.19 (419.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7307">
            <lem wit="MS2">or—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">or——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65068">
The king begun to gurgle, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2473"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l12185" type="alt" xml:id="te2473"/>
he gasps out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65074">
“ ’Nough!—

          <hi rend="italic">I own up!</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65079">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5297"/>
I was very glad to hear him say that, it made me feel much more easier than what I was feeling before.

          <app from="pr5297" n="263.22–23 (420.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7308">
            <lem wit="A">I was . . . before.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7309">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
So the duke took his hands off, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65090">
          <pb n="264" xml:id="pb0264"/>
“If you ever deny it again, I’ll drown you. It’s

          <hi rend="italic">well</hi>
for you to set there and blubber like a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2474"/>
baby

          <ptr target="#l12186" type="alt" xml:id="te2474"/>
—it’s fitten for you, after the way you’ve acted. I never see such an old

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2475"/>
ostrich

          <ptr target="#l12187" type="alt" xml:id="te2475"/>
for wanting to gobble everything—and I a trusting you all the time, like you was my own father. You ought to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2476"/>
been

          <ptr target="#l12188" type="alt" xml:id="te2476"/>
ashamed of yourself to stand by and hear it saddled onto a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5298"/>
lot

          <app from="pr5298" n="264.6 (420.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7310">
            <lem wit="A">lot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">passel</rdg>
          </app>
of poor niggers and you never say a word for ’em. It makes me feel

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5299"/>
ridiculous

          <app from="pr5299" n="264.7 (421.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7311">
            <lem wit="A">ridiculous</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">right down ridicklous</rdg>
          </app>
to think I was soft enough to

          <hi rend="italic">believe</hi>
that rubbage. Cuss you, I can see, now, why you was so anxious to make up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5300"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2477"/>
deffesit

          <ptr target="#l12189" type="alt" xml:id="te2477"/>
          <app from="pr5300" n="264.9 (421.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7312">
            <lem wit="A">deffesit</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">deffersit</rdg>
          </app>
—you wanted to get what money I’d got out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5301"/>
Nonesuch

          <app from="pr5301" n="264.10 (421.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la7313">
            <lem wit="A">Nonesuch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame</rdg>
          </app>
and one thing or another, and scoop it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5302"/>
          <hi rend="italic">all!</hi>
          <app from="pr5302" n="264.10 (421.9–11)" type="e" xml:id="la7314">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">all!</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
, you unsatisfiable, tunnel-bellied old sewer!

            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65159">The king says, timid, and still a snuffling:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65161">“Why, duke, it was you that said make up the deffersit, it warn’t me.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65163">
“Dry

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5303"/>
up!

          <app from="pr5303" n="264.14 (421.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7315">
            <lem wit="A">up!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">up,</rdg>
          </app>
I don’t want to hear no more

          <hi rend="italic">out</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5304"/>
of

          <app from="pr5304" n="264.14 (421.18)" type="e" xml:id="la7316">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">o’</rdg>
          </app>
you!” says the duke. “And

          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
you see what you

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
by it. They’ve got all their own money back, and all of

          <hi rend="italic">ourn</hi>
but a shekel or two,

          <hi rend="italic">besides.</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2478"/>
G’long

          <ptr target="#l12190" type="alt" xml:id="te2478"/>
to bed—and don’t you deffersit

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
no more deffersits,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5305"/>
long’s

          <app from="pr5305" n="264.17 (422.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7317">
            <lem wit="A">long’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">long</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
live!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65213">
So the king sneaked into the wigwam, and took to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5306"/>
his

          <app from="pr5306" n="264.18 (422.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7318">
            <lem wit="A">his</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the</rdg>
          </app>
bottle for comfort; and before long the duke tackled

          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
bottle; and so in about a half an hour they was as thick as thieves again, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5307"/>
tighter

          <app from="pr5307" n="264.20 (422.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7319">
            <lem wit="A">tighter</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">drunker</rdg>
          </app>
they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5308"/>
got the

          <app from="pr5308" n="264.21 (422.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7320">
            <lem wit="MS2">got the</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">got, the</rdg>
          </app>
lovinger they got; and went off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5309"/>
a-snoring

          <app from="pr5309" n="264.21 (422.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7321">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-snoring</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a snoring</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2479"/>
in each other’s arms. They both got powerful

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5310"/>
mellow

          <app from="pr5310" n="264.22 (423.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7322">
            <lem wit="A">mellow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">drunk</rdg>
          </app>
, but I noticed the king didn’t get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5311"/>
mellow

          <app from="pr5311" n="264.23 (423.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7323">
            <lem wit="A">mellow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">drunk</rdg>
          </app>
enough to forget to remember to not deny about hiding the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5312"/>
money-bag,

          <app from="pr5312" n="264.24 (423.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7324">
            <lem wit="MS2">money-bag,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">money-bag</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2480"/>
again.

          <ptr target="#l12192" type="alt" xml:id="te2480"/>
That made me feel easy and satisfied. Of course when they got to snoring, we had a long gabble, and I told Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5313"/>
everything.

          <app from="pr5313" n="264.26 (423.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7325">
            <lem wit="A">everything.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
everything

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12191" type="alt" xml:id="te2479"/>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0411">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXI.</head>
        <pb n="265" xml:id="pb0265"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y26501">
          <graphic url="y26501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5314"/>
Chapter XXXI.

            <app from="pr5314" n="265 title (424.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7326">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXI.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7327">not in; chapter sink</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">We</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2651">
          <graphic url="hf2651.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">spanish moss</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e65309">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0037"/>
dasn’t stop again at any town, for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2481"/>
days and

          <ptr target="#l12193" type="alt" xml:id="te2481"/>
days; kept right along down the river. We was down south in the warm weather, now, and a mighty long ways from home. We begun to come to

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="sa0003"/>
trees with Spanish moss on them, hanging down from the limbs like long gray beards. It was the first I ever see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2482"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12194" type="alt" xml:id="te2482"/>
          <ptr target="#as0227" type="an" xml:id="aa0003"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2483"/>
growing,

          <ptr target="#l12195" type="alt" xml:id="te2483"/>
and it made the woods look solemn

          <ptr target="#mt0037" type="alt" xml:id="wn0037"/>
and dismal. So now the frauds reckoned they was out of danger, and they begun to work the villages again.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65329">
First they done a lecture on temperance; but they didn’t make enough for them both to get drunk on. Then in another village they started a dancing school; but they didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2484"/>
know

          <ptr target="#l12196" type="alt" xml:id="te2484"/>
no more how to dance than a kangaroo does; so the first prance they made, the general public jumped in and pranced them out of town. Another time they tried a go at yellocution; but they didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2485"/>
yellocute

          <ptr target="#l12197" type="alt" xml:id="te2485"/>
long till the audience got up and give them a solid good cussing and made them skip out. They tackled missionarying, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5315"/>
mesmerizering

          <app from="pr5315" n="265.24 (426.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7328">
            <lem wit="A">mesmerizering</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mesmerising</rdg>
          </app>
, and doctoring, and telling fortunes, and a little of everything; but they couldn’t seem to have no luck. So at last they got just about dead broke, and laid around the raft, as she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2486"/>
floated

          <ptr target="#l12198" type="alt" xml:id="te2486"/>
along, thinking, and thinking, and never saying nothing, by the half a day at a time, and dreadful blue and desperate.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65352">
And at last they took a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5316"/>
change

          <app from="pr5316" n="265.30 (426.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7329">
            <lem wit="MS2">change</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">change,</rdg>
          </app>
and begun to lay their heads together in the wigwam and talk low and confidential two or three

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2487"/>
hours

          <ptr target="#l12199" type="alt" xml:id="te2487"/>
at a time. Jim and me got uneasy. We didn’t like the look of it.

          <pb n="266" xml:id="pb0266"/>
We judged they was studying up some kind of worse deviltry than ever. We turned it over and over, and at last we made up our minds

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5317"/>
they

          <app from="pr5317" n="266.3 (427.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7330">
            <lem wit="A">they</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that they</rdg>
          </app>
was going to break into somebody’s house or store, or was going into the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5318"/>
counterfeit money

          <app from="pr5318" n="266.4 (427.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7331">
            <lem wit="MS2">counterfeit money</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">counterfeit-money</rdg>
          </app>
business, or something. So then we was pretty scared, and made up an agreement that we wouldn’t have nothing in the world to do with such actions, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5319"/>
if

          <app from="pr5319" n="266.6 (428.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7332">
            <lem wit="A">if</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that if</rdg>
          </app>
we ever got the least show we would give them the cold shake, and clear out and leave them behind. Well, early one morning we hid the raft in a good safe place about two mile below a little bit of

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0004"/>
a shabby village,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2488"/>
named

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5320"/>
Pikesville

          <app from="pr5320" n="266.10 (428.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7333">
            <lem wit="A">Pikesville</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Pikeville</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l12200" type="alt" xml:id="te2488"/>
and the king he went ashore, and told us all to stay hid whilst he went up to town and smelt around to see if anybody had

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2489"/>
got any

          <ptr target="#l12201" type="alt" xml:id="te2489"/>
wind of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5321"/>
Royal Nonesuch

          <app from="pr5321" n="266.12 (428.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la7334">
            <lem wit="A">Royal Nonesuch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame</rdg>
          </app>
there yet.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2490"/>
(“House to rob, you

          <hi rend="italic">mean</hi>
,” says I to myself; “and when you get through robbing it you’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2491"/>
come

          <ptr target="#l12203" type="alt" xml:id="te2491"/>
back here and wonder what’s become of me and Jim and the raft—and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2492"/>
you’ll

          <ptr target="#l12204" type="alt" xml:id="te2492"/>
have to take it out in wondering.”)

          <ptr target="#l12202" type="alt" xml:id="te2490"/>
And he said if he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5322"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr5322" n="266.16 (428.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7335">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
back by midday, the duke and me would know it was all right, and we was to come along.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65443">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0038"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2493"/>
So we staid where we

          <ptr target="#l12205" type="alt" xml:id="te2493"/>
was. The duke he fretted and sweated around, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2494"/>
was in

          <ptr target="#l12206" type="alt" xml:id="te2494"/>
a mighty sour way. He scolded us for everything, and we couldn’t seem to do nothing right; he found fault with every little

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2495"/>
thing. Something was a-brewing, sure.

          <ptr target="#l12207" type="alt" xml:id="te2495"/>
I was good and glad when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5323"/>
midday

          <app from="pr5323" n="266.22 (429.17–430.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7336">
            <lem wit="A">midday</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
mid-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
day

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#mt0038" type="alt" xml:id="wn0038"/>
come and no king; we could have a change,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2496"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5324"/>
anyway

          <app from="pr5324" n="266.22 (430.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7337">
            <lem wit="A">anyway</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
any-

              <lb/>
way

            </rdg>
          </app>
—and maybe a chance for

          <hi rend="italic">the</hi>
change, on top of it.

          <ptr target="#l12208" type="alt" xml:id="te2496"/>
So

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5325"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2497"/>
me and the duke

          <ptr target="#l12209" type="alt" xml:id="te2497"/>
          <app from="pr5325" n="266.23 (430.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7338">
            <lem wit="A">me and the duke</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the duke and me</rdg>
          </app>
went up to the village, and hunted around there for the king, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5326"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5326" n="266.24–25 (430.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7339">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
we found him in the back room of a little low doggery, very tight, and a lot of loafers bullyragging him for sport, and he a cussing and threatening with all his might, and so tight he couldn’t walk, and couldn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2498"/>
do

          <ptr target="#l12210" type="alt" xml:id="te2498"/>
nothing to them. The duke

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5327"/>
he

          <app from="pr5327" n="266.28 (430.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7340">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7341">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
begun to abuse him for an old fool, and the king begun to sass back; and the minute they was fairly at it, I lit out, and shook the reefs out of my hind legs, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5328"/>
spun

          <app from="pr5328" n="266.31 (431.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7342">
            <lem wit="A">spun</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">shinned it</rdg>
          </app>
down the river road like a deer—for I see our chance; and I made

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2499"/>
up my mind

          <ptr target="#l12211" type="alt" xml:id="te2499"/>
that it would be a long day before they ever see me and Jim again. I got down there

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2500"/>
all

          <ptr target="#l12212" type="alt" xml:id="te2500"/>
out of breath but loaded

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2501"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l12213" type="alt" xml:id="te2501"/>
with joy, and sung out—

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65540">“Set her loose, Jim, we’re all right, now!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65542">
But there warn’t no answer, and nobody come out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5329"/>
wigwam

          <app from="pr5329" n="266.36 (431.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7343">
            <lem wit="A">wigwam</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
wig-

              <lb/>
wam

            </rdg>
          </app>
. Jim was gone! I set up a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5330"/>
shout,

          <app from="pr5330" n="266.37 (431.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7344">
            <lem wit="MS2">shout,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
shout

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—and then another—and then another one; and run this way and that in the woods, whooping and screeching; but it warn’t no use—old Jim was gone. Then I set down and

          <pb n="267" xml:id="pb0267"/>
cried; I couldn’t help it. But I couldn’t set still long. Pretty soon I went out on the road, trying to think what I better do, and I run across a boy walking, and asked him if he’d seen a strange nigger, dressed so and so, and he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65562">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65564">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2502"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5331"/>
Wherebouts

          <app from="pr5331" n="267.6 (432.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7345">
            <lem wit="A">Wherebouts</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Where</rdg>
          </app>
?

          <ptr target="#l12214" type="alt" xml:id="te2502"/>
” says I.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65578">
“Down

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2503"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l12215" type="alt" xml:id="te2503"/>
Silas Phelps’s place, two mile below

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2504"/>
here

          <ptr target="#as0228" type="an" xml:id="as0004"/>
.

          <ptr target="#l12216" type="alt" xml:id="te2504"/>
He’s a runaway nigger, and they’ve got him. Was you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5332"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2505"/>
looking

          <ptr target="#l12217" type="alt" xml:id="te2505"/>
          <app from="pr5332" n="267.8 (433.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7346">
            <lem wit="A">looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">lookin’</rdg>
          </app>
for him?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65601">
“You bet I ain’t! I run across him in the woods

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2506"/>
about

          <ptr target="#l12218" type="alt" xml:id="te2506"/>
an hour or two ago, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2507"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l12219" type="alt" xml:id="te2507"/>
said if I hollered he’d cut my livers out—and told me to lay down and stay where I was; and I done it. Been there ever since; afeard to come out.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65611">
“Well,” he says, “you needn’t be afeard no more, becuz they’ve got him. He run off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2508"/>
f’m

          <ptr target="#l12220" type="alt" xml:id="te2508"/>
down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5333"/>
south

          <app from="pr5333" n="267.14 (433.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7347">
            <lem wit="MS2">south</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">South</rdg>
          </app>
, som’ers.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65625">“It’s a good job they got him.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65627">
“Well, I

          <hi rend="italic">reckon!</hi>
There’s two hunderd dollars reward on him. It’s like picking up money out’n the road.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65632">
“Yes, it is—and

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2509"/>
could

          <ptr target="#l12221" type="alt" xml:id="te2509"/>
a had it if I’d been big

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5334"/>
enough:

          <app from="pr5334" n="267.18 (434.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7348">
            <lem wit="MS2">enough:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">enough;</rdg>
          </app>
I see him

          <hi rend="italic">first.</hi>
Who nailed him?”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y26701">
          <graphic url="y26701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">who nailed him?</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65657">
          <pb n="268" xml:id="pb0268"/>
“It was an old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5335"/>
fellow

          <app from="pr5335" n="268.1 (434.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7349">
            <lem wit="A">fellow</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">feller</rdg>
          </app>
—a stranger—and he sold out his chance in him for forty dollars, becuz he’s got to go up the river and can’t wait. Think o’ that, now! You bet

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5336"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’d

          <app from="pr5336" n="268.3 (434.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7350">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
wait, if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2510"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12222" type="alt" xml:id="te2510"/>
was seven year.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65685">“That’s me, every time,” says I. “But maybe his chance ain’t worth no more than that, if he’ll sell it so cheap. Maybe there’s something ain’t straight about it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65687">
“But it

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
, though—straight as a string. I see the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5337"/>
handbill

          <app from="pr5337" n="268.7 (435.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la7351">
            <lem wit="A">handbill</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
hand-

              <lb/>
bill

            </rdg>
          </app>
myself. It tells all about him, to a dot—paints him like a picture, and tells the plantation he’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5338"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0074"/>
frum

          <ptr target="#tb0074" type="te" xml:id="tv0074"/>
          <app from="pr5338" n="268.9 (435.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7352">
            <lem wit="A">frum</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">from</rdg>
          </app>
, below

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5339"/>
Newr

          <hi rend="italic">leans</hi>
          <app from="pr5339" n="268.9 (435.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la7353">
            <lem wit="A">
Newr

              <hi rend="italic">leans</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Newr-

              <lb/>
              <hi rend="italic">leans</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2511"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5340"/>
No-sir-ree-

          <hi rend="italic">bob</hi>
          <app from="pr5340" n="268.9 (435.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7354">
            <lem wit="MS2">
No-sir-ree-

              <hi rend="italic">bob</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
No-sirree-

              <hi rend="italic">bob</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l12223" type="alt" xml:id="te2511"/>
they ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2512"/>
no

          <ptr target="#l12224" type="alt" xml:id="te2512"/>
trouble ’bout

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
speculation, you bet

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2513"/>
you.

          <ptr target="#l12225" type="alt" xml:id="te2513"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2514"/>
Say, gimme

          <ptr target="#l12226" type="alt" xml:id="te2514"/>
a chaw

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2515"/>
tobacker,

          <ptr target="#l12227" type="alt" xml:id="te2515"/>
won’t ye?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65765">
I didn’t have none, so he left. I went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2516"/>
to the raft

          <ptr target="#l12228" type="alt" xml:id="te2516"/>
, and set down in the wigwam to think. But I couldn’t come to nothing. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5341"/>
thought,

          <app from="pr5341" n="268.13 (436.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7355">
            <lem wit="MS2">thought,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
thought

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2517"/>
till I wore

          <ptr target="#l12229" type="alt" xml:id="te2517"/>
my head sore, but I couldn’t see no way out of the trouble. After all this long journey, and after all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2518"/>
we’d

          <ptr target="#l12230" type="alt" xml:id="te2518"/>
done for them scoundrels, here was it all come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2519"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l12231" type="alt" xml:id="te2519"/>
nothing, everything all busted up and ruined, because they could have the heart

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2520"/>
to serve

          <ptr target="#l12232" type="alt" xml:id="te2520"/>
Jim such a trick as that, and make him a slave again all his life, and amongst strangers,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2521"/>
too,

          <ptr target="#l12233" type="alt" xml:id="te2521"/>
for forty dirty dollars.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65801">
Once I said

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2522"/>
to myself

          <ptr target="#l12234" type="alt" xml:id="te2522"/>
it would be a thousand times better for Jim to be a slave at home where his family was, as long as he’d

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to be a slave, and so I’d better write a letter to Tom Sawyer and tell him to tell Miss Watson where he was. But I soon give up that notion, for two things: she’d be mad and disgusted at his rascality and ungratefulness for leaving her, and so she’d sell him straight down the river again; and if she didn’t, everybody naturally despises an ungrateful nigger, and they’d make Jim feel it all the time, and so he’d feel ornery and disgraced. And then think of

          <hi rend="italic">me!</hi>
It would get all around, that Huck Finn

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2523"/>
helped

          <ptr target="#l12235" type="alt" xml:id="te2523"/>
a nigger

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5342"/>
to

          <app from="pr5342" n="268.29 (438.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7356">
            <lem wit="A">to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7357">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
get his freedom; and if I was to ever see anybody from that town again, I’d be ready to get down and lick his boots for shame. That’s just the way: a person does a low-down thing, and then he don’t want to take no consequences of it. Thinks as long as he can hide it, it ain’t no disgrace. That

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5343"/>
was

          <app from="pr5343" n="268.34 (438.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la7358">
            <lem wit="A">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was just</rdg>
          </app>
my fix

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5344"/>
exactly

          <app from="pr5344" n="268.34 (438.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7359">
            <lem wit="A">exactly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">exackly</rdg>
          </app>
. The more I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5345"/>
studied

          <app from="pr5345" n="268.34 (438.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7360">
            <lem wit="A">studied</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thought</rdg>
          </app>
about this, the more my conscience

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5346"/>
went

          <app from="pr5346" n="268.35 (438.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7361">
            <lem wit="A">went</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">got</rdg>
          </app>
to grinding me, and the more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5347"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2524"/>
wicked,

          <ptr target="#l12236" type="alt" xml:id="te2524"/>
          <app from="pr5347" n="268.35 (438.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7362">
            <lem wit="MS2">wicked,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
wicked

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and low-down and ornery I got to feeling. And at last, when it hit me all of a sudden that here was the plain hand of Providence slapping me in the face and letting me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5348"/>
know

          <app from="pr5348" n="268.38 (439.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7363">
            <lem wit="A">know</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">know that</rdg>
          </app>
my wickedness was being watched all

          <pb n="269" xml:id="pb0269"/>
the time from up there in heaven, whilst I was stealing a poor old woman’s nigger that hadn’t ever done me

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2525"/>
no

          <ptr target="#l12237" type="alt" xml:id="te2525"/>
harm, and now was showing

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2526"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5349"/>
me

          <app from="pr5349" n="269.3 (439.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7364">
            <lem wit="A">me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">me that</rdg>
          </app>
there’s

          <ptr target="#l12238" type="alt" xml:id="te2526"/>
One that’s always on the lookout, and ain’t agoing to allow no such miserable doings to go only

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2527"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l12239" type="alt" xml:id="te2527"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2528"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l12240" type="alt" xml:id="te2528"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5350"/>
fur

          <app from="pr5350" n="269.4 (439.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7365">
            <lem wit="A">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
and no further, I most dropped in my tracks I was so scared. Well, I tried the best I could to kinder soften it up somehow for myself, by saying I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5351"/>
brung

          <app from="pr5351" n="269.7 (440.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7366">
            <lem wit="A">brung</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">brought</rdg>
          </app>
up wicked, and so I warn’t so much to blame; but something inside of me kept saying, “There was the Sunday

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5352"/>
School

          <app from="pr5352" n="269.8 (440.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7367">
            <lem wit="MS2">School</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">school</rdg>
          </app>
, you could a gone to it; and if you’d a done it they’d a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5353"/>
learnt

          <app from="pr5353" n="269.9 (440.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7368">
            <lem wit="A">learnt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">learned</rdg>
          </app>
you,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2529"/>
there

          <ptr target="#l12241" type="alt" xml:id="te2529"/>
, that people that acts as I’d been acting about that nigger goes to everlasting fire.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65939">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2530"/>
It made me shiver. And I about made up my mind to pray; and see if I couldn’t try to quit being the kind of a boy I was, and be better. So I kneeled down. But the words wouldn’t come. Why wouldn’t they? It warn’t no use to try

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5354"/>
and

          <app from="pr5354" n="269.15 (441.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7369">
            <lem wit="A">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to</rdg>
          </app>
hide it from Him. Nor from

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
, neither. I knowed very well why they wouldn’t come. It was because my heart warn’t right; it was because I warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5355"/>
square; it

          <app from="pr5355" n="269.17 (441.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7370">
            <lem wit="MS2">square; it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">square; is</rdg>
          </app>
was because I was playing double. I was letting

          <hi rend="italic">on</hi>
to give up sin, but away inside of me I was holding on to the biggest one of all. I was trying to make my mouth

          <hi rend="italic">say</hi>
I would do the right thing and the clean thing, and go and write to that nigger’s owner and tell where he was; but deep down in me I knowed it was a lie—and He knowed it. You can’t pray a lie—I found that out.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65968">
So I was full of trouble, full as I could be; and didn’t know what to do. At last I had an idea; and I says, I’ll go and write the letter—and

          <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
see if I can pray. Why, it was astonishing, the way I felt as light as a feather, right straight off, and my troubles all gone. So I got a piece of paper and a pencil, all glad and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2531"/>
excited

          <ptr target="#l12243" type="alt" xml:id="te2531"/>
, and set down and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5356"/>
wrote:

          <app from="pr5356" n="269.29 (442.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7371">
            <lem wit="C">
wrote:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7372">extra line space</note>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
wrote:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7373">no extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e65989">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5357"/>
            <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0075"/>
Miss Watson

            <app from="pr5357" n="269.30 (443.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7374">
              <lem wit="A">Miss Watson</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">Miss Watson,</rdg>
            </app>
your

            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5358"/>
runaway

            <app from="pr5358" n="269.30 (443.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la7375">
              <lem wit="A">runaway</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
run-

                <lb/>
away

              </rdg>
            </app>
nigger

            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2532"/>
Jim

            <ptr target="#l12244" type="alt" xml:id="te2532"/>
is down here two mile below

            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5359"/>
Pikesville

            <app from="pr5359" n="269.31 (443.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7376">
              <lem wit="A">Pikesville</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">Pikesville,</rdg>
            </app>
and Mr. Phelps has

            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5360"/>
got him

            <app from="pr5360" n="269.31 (443.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7377">
              <lem wit="A">got him</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">got him,</rdg>
            </app>
and he will give him up for the reward if you send.

            <hi rend="smallcaps">Huck</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5361"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">Finn</hi>
.

            <ptr target="#tb0075" type="te" xml:id="tv0075"/>
            <app from="pr5361" n="269.32 (443.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7378">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">Finn</hi>
.

                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7379">extra line space</note>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">Finn</hi>
.

                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7380">no extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </p>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66051">
I felt good and all washed clean of sin for the first time I had ever felt so in my life, and I knowed I could

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5362"/>
pray,

          <app from="pr5362" n="269.34 (443.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7381">
            <lem wit="MS2">pray,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
pray

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now. But I didn’t do it straight off, but laid the paper down and set there

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5363"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2533"/>
thinking;

          <ptr target="#l12245" type="alt" xml:id="te2533"/>
thinking

          <app from="pr5363" n="269.35 (443.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7382">
            <lem wit="MS2">thinking; thinking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">thinking—thinking</rdg>
          </app>
how good it was all this happened so, and how near I come to being lost and going to hell. And went on thinking. And got to thinking

          <pb n="270" xml:id="pb0270"/>
over our trip down the river;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2534"/>
and I see

          <ptr target="#l12246" type="alt" xml:id="te2534"/>
Jim before me, all the time, in the day, and in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5364"/>
night-time

          <app from="pr5364" n="270.2 (444.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7383">
            <lem wit="MS2">night-time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
night-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
          </app>
, sometimes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5365"/>
moonlight

          <app from="pr5365" n="270.2 (444.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la7384">
            <lem wit="A">moonlight</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
moon-

              <lb/>
light

            </rdg>
          </app>
, sometimes storms, and we a floating along, talking,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2535"/>
and singing, and laughing.

          <ptr target="#l12247" type="alt" xml:id="te2535"/>
But somehow I couldn’t seem to strike no places to harden me against him, but only the other kind. I’d see him standing my watch on top of his’n, stead of calling

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5366"/>
me—

          <app from="pr5366" n="270.6 (444.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7385">
            <lem wit="MS2">me—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">me,</rdg>
          </app>
so I could go on sleeping; and see him how glad he was when I come back out of the fog; and when I come to him again in the swamp, up there where the feud was; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2536"/>
such-like

          <ptr target="#l12248" type="alt" xml:id="te2536"/>
times; and would always call me honey, and pet me, and do everything he could think of for me, and how good he always was; and at last I struck the time I saved him by telling the men we had small-pox aboard, and he was so grateful, and said I was the best friend old Jim ever had in the world, and the

          <hi rend="italic">only</hi>
one he’s got now; and then I happened to look around, and see that paper.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y27001">
          <graphic url="y27001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">thinking</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66123">
It was a close

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2537"/>
place.

          <ptr target="#l12249" type="alt" xml:id="te2537"/>
I took it up, and held it in my hand. I was a trembling, because I’d got to decide,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5367"/>
forever

          <app from="pr5367" n="270.16 (445.18)" type="e" xml:id="la7386">
            <lem wit="A">forever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">once and forever</rdg>
          </app>
, betwixt two things, and I knowed it. I studied a minute, sort of holding my breath, and then says to myself:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66137">
          <pb n="271" xml:id="pb0271"/>
“All right, then, I’ll

          <hi rend="italic">go</hi>
to hell”—and tore it up.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66142">
It was awful thoughts, and awful words, but they was said. And I let them stay said; and never thought no more about reforming. I shoved the whole thing out of my head; and said I would take up wickedness again, which was in my line, being

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5368"/>
brung

          <app from="pr5368" n="271.5 (446.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7387">
            <lem wit="A">brung</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">brought</rdg>
          </app>
up to it, and the other warn’t. And for a starter, I would go to work and steal Jim out of slavery again; and if I could think up anything worse, I would do that, too; because as long as I was in, and in for good, I might as well go the whole hog.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66152">
Then I set to thinking over how to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5369"/>
get

          <app from="pr5369" n="271.10 (447.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7388">
            <lem wit="A">get</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">go</rdg>
          </app>
at it, and turned over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2538"/>
considerable

          <ptr target="#l12250" type="alt" xml:id="te2538"/>
many ways in my mind; and at last fixed up a plan that suited me. So then

          <ptr target="#l12242" type="alt" xml:id="te2530"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0039"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2539"/>
I took the bearings of a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2540"/>
woody

          <ptr target="#l12252" type="alt" xml:id="te2540"/>
island that was down the river

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5370"/>
a piece

          <app from="pr5370" n="271.13 (448.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7389">
            <lem wit="A">a piece</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">apiece</rdg>
          </app>
, and as soon as it was fairly dark I crept out with my raft

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2542"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2541"/>
and went

          <ptr target="#l12253" type="alt" xml:id="te2541"/>
for it, and hid it there, and

          <ptr target="#l12254" type="alt" xml:id="te2542"/>
          <ptr target="#mt0039" type="alt" xml:id="wn0039"/>
then turned in. I slept the night through, and got up before it was light, and had my breakfast, and put on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0040"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2543"/>
my store

          <ptr target="#l12255" type="alt" xml:id="te2543"/>
clothes

          <ptr target="#mt0040" type="alt" xml:id="wn0040"/>
, and tied up some

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2544"/>
others and one thing or another

          <ptr target="#l12256" type="alt" xml:id="te2544"/>
in a bundle, and took the canoe and cleared for shore. I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2545"/>
landed

          <ptr target="#l12257" type="alt" xml:id="te2545"/>
below where I judged was Phelps’s place, and hid my bundle in the woods, and then filled up the canoe with water, and loaded rocks into her and sunk her where I could find her again when I wanted

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2546"/>
her,

          <ptr target="#l12258" type="alt" xml:id="te2546"/>
about a quarter of a mile below a little steam sawmill that was on the bank.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66213">
Then I struck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5371"/>
up

          <app from="pr5371" n="271.23 (448-B.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7390">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">up to</rdg>
          </app>
the road, and when I passed the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2547"/>
mill

          <ptr target="#l12259" type="alt" xml:id="te2547"/>
I see a sign on it, “Phelps’s Sawmill,” and when I come to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5372"/>
farm houses

          <app from="pr5372" n="271.24 (448-B.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7391">
            <lem wit="MS2">farm houses</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">farm-houses</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2548"/>
two

          <ptr target="#l12260" type="alt" xml:id="te2548"/>
or three hundred yards further along, I kept my eyes peeled, but didn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5373"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr5373" n="271.27 (448-B.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7392">
            <lem wit="A">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
around, though it was good daylight, now. But I didn’t mind, because I didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2549"/>
want

          <ptr target="#l12261" type="alt" xml:id="te2549"/>
to see nobody just yet—I only wanted to get the lay of the land. According to my plan, I was going to turn up there from the village, not from below. So I just took a look, and shoved along, straight for town.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5374"/>
Well

          <app from="pr5374" n="271.30 (448-C.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7393">
            <lem wit="A">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Well, sir</rdg>
          </app>
, the very first man I see, when I got there, was the duke. He was sticking up a bill for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5375"/>
Royal Nonesuch

          <app from="pr5375" n="271.32 (448-C.7–8)" type="e" xml:id="la7394">
            <lem wit="A">Royal Nonesuch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame</rdg>
          </app>
—three-night

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5376"/>
performance,

          <app from="pr5376" n="271.32 (448-C.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7395">
            <lem wit="MS2">performance,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">performance—</rdg>
          </app>
like that other time.

          <hi rend="italic">They</hi>
had the cheek, them frauds! I was right on him, before I could shirk. He

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2550"/>
looked

          <ptr target="#l12262" type="alt" xml:id="te2550"/>
astonished, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66286">
“Hel-

          <hi rend="italic">lo!</hi>
Where’d

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
come from?” Then he says, kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5377"/>
glad,

          <app from="pr5377" n="271.35 (448-C.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7396">
            <lem wit="MS2">glad,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
glad

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and eager, “Where’s the raft?—got her in a good place?”

          <ptr target="#l12251" type="alt" xml:id="te2539"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66303">I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66305">“Why, that’s just what I was agoing to ask your grace.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66307">
          <pb n="272" xml:id="pb0272"/>
Then he didn’t look so joyful—and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66309">
“What was your idea for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5378"/>
asking

          <app from="pr5378" n="272.2 (449.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7397">
            <lem wit="A">asking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">askin’</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">me?</hi>
” he says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66321">
“Well,” I says, “when I see the king in that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5379"/>
doggery,

          <app from="pr5379" n="272.3 (449.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7398">
            <lem wit="C">doggery,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gin-mill,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">doggery</rdg>
          </app>
yesterday, I says to myself, we can’t get him home for hours, till he’s soberer; so I went a loafing around town to put in the time, and wait. A man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5380"/>
up and

          <app from="pr5380" n="272.5–6 (449.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7399">
            <lem wit="A">up and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7400">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
offered me ten cents to help him pull a skiff over the river and back to fetch a sheep, and so I went along; but when we was dragging him to the boat, and the man left me aholt of the rope and went behind him to shove him along, he was too strong for me, and jerked loose and run, and we after him. We didn’t have no dog, and so we had to chase him all over the country till we tired him out. We never got him till dark, then we fetched him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2551"/>
over,

          <ptr target="#l12263" type="alt" xml:id="te2551"/>
and I started down for the raft. When I got there and see it was gone, I says to myself,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2552"/>
‘

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5381"/>
They’ve

          <app from="pr5381" n="272.14 (451.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7401">
            <lem wit="MS2">They’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">they’ve</rdg>
          </app>
got into trouble and had to leave; and they’ve took my nigger, which is the only nigger I’ve got in the world, and now I’m in a strange country, and ain’t got no property no more, nor nothing, and no way to make my living;’

          <ptr target="#l12264" type="alt" xml:id="te2552"/>
so I set down and cried.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2553"/>
I slept in the woods all night.

          <ptr target="#l12265" type="alt" xml:id="te2553"/>
But what

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
become of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5382"/>
raft,

          <app from="pr5382" n="272.18 (451.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7402">
            <lem wit="MS2">raft,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
raft

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2554"/>
then?

          <ptr target="#l12266" type="alt" xml:id="te2554"/>
—and Jim, poor

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2555"/>
Jim!”

          <ptr target="#l12267" type="alt" xml:id="te2555"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66382">
“Blamed if

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know—that is, what’s become of the raft. That old fool had made a trade and got forty dollars, and when we found him in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5383"/>
doggery,

          <app from="pr5383" n="272.22 (452.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7403">
            <lem wit="C">doggery,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gin-mill,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">doggery</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5384"/>
the loafers

          <app from="pr5384" n="272.22 (452.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7404">
            <lem wit="A">the loafers</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them loafers</rdg>
          </app>
had matched half dollars with him and got every cent but what he’d spent for whisky; and when I got him home late last night and found the raft gone, we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5385"/>
said

          <app from="pr5385" n="272.24 (452.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7405">
            <lem wit="A">said</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2556"/>
‘That

          <ptr target="#l12268" type="alt" xml:id="te2556"/>
little rascal has stole our raft and shook us, and run off down the river.’ ”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66417">
“I wouldn’t shake my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2557"/>
          <hi rend="italic">nigger</hi>
          <ptr target="#l12269" type="alt" xml:id="te2557"/>
, would I?—the only nigger I had in the world, and the only property.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66424">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2558"/>
We never

          <ptr target="#l12270" type="alt" xml:id="te2558"/>
thought of that. Fact is, I reckon we’d come to consider him

          <hi rend="italic">our</hi>
nigger; yes, we did consider him so—goodness knows we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5386"/>
had

          <app from="pr5386" n="272.30 (453.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7406">
            <lem wit="A">had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">had took</rdg>
          </app>
trouble enough for him.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5387"/>
So,

          <app from="pr5387" n="272.30 (453.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7407">
            <lem wit="MS2">So,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
So

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
when we see the raft was gone, and we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5388"/>
flat broke

          <app from="pr5388" n="272.31 (453.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7408">
            <lem wit="A">flat broke</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">busted</rdg>
          </app>
, there warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5389"/>
anything

          <app from="pr5389" n="272.31 (453.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7409">
            <lem wit="A">anything</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nothing</rdg>
          </app>
for it but to try the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5390"/>
Royal Nonesuch

          <app from="pr5390" n="272.31–32 (453.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7410">
            <lem wit="A">Royal Nonesuch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame</rdg>
          </app>
another shake. And I’ve pegged along ever since,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2559"/>
dry

          <ptr target="#l12271" type="alt" xml:id="te2559"/>
as a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5391"/>
powder horn

          <app from="pr5391" n="272.33 (453.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7411">
            <lem wit="MS2">powder horn</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
powder-

              <lb/>
horn

            </rdg>
          </app>
. Where’s that ten

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5392"/>
cents?

          <app from="pr5392" n="272.33 (453.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7412">
            <lem wit="A">cents?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cents.</rdg>
          </app>
Give it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5393"/>
here

          <app from="pr5393" n="272.33 (453.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7413">
            <lem wit="A">here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to me</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66506">
I had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5394"/>
considerable

          <app from="pr5394" n="272.34 (453.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7414">
            <lem wit="A">considerable</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7415">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
money, so I give him ten cents, but begged him to spend it for something to eat, and give me some,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5395"/>
because

          <app from="pr5395" n="272.35 (454.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7416">
            <lem wit="A">because</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">because I said</rdg>
          </app>
it was all the money I had, and I hadn’t had nothing to eat since yesterday. He never said nothing.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5396"/>
The

          <app from="pr5396" n="272.37 (454.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7417">
            <lem wit="A">The</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Then</rdg>
          </app>
next minute he whirls on me and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66534">
          <pb n="273" xml:id="pb0273"/>
“Do you reckon that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5397"/>
nigger would

          <app from="pr5397" n="273.1 (454.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7418">
            <lem wit="A">nigger would</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nigger’ll</rdg>
          </app>
blow on us?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2560"/>
We’d

          <ptr target="#l12272" type="alt" xml:id="te2560"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5398"/>
skin

          <app from="pr5398" n="273.1 (454.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7419">
            <lem wit="A">skin</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kill</rdg>
          </app>
him if he done that!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66556">
“How can he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2561"/>
blow?

          <ptr target="#l12273" type="alt" xml:id="te2561"/>
Hain’t he run off?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66562">“No! That old fool sold him, and never divided with me, and the money’s gone.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66564">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Sold</hi>
him?” I says, and begun to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5399"/>
cry:

          <app from="pr5399" n="273.6 (455.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7420">
            <lem wit="MS2">cry:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cry;</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5400"/>
Why

          <app from="pr5400" n="273.6 (455.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7421">
            <lem wit="MS2">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">why</rdg>
          </app>
, he was

          <hi rend="italic">my</hi>
nigger, and that was my money. Where is he?—I want my nigger.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y27301">
          <graphic url="y27301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">he gave him ten cents</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66594">
“Well, you can’t

          <hi rend="italic">get</hi>
your nigger, that’s all—so dry up your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2562"/>
blubbering.

          <ptr target="#l12274" type="alt" xml:id="te2562"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5401"/>
Looky-here

          <app from="pr5401" n="273.9 (455.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7422">
            <lem wit="MS2">Looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Looky here</rdg>
          </app>
—do you think

          <hi rend="italic">you’d</hi>
venture to blow on us? Blamed if I think I’d trust you.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2563"/>
Why,

          <ptr target="#l12275" type="alt" xml:id="te2563"/>
if you

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
to blow on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5402"/>
us—

          <app from="pr5402" n="273.10 (455.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7423">
            <lem wit="MS2">us—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">us——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66629">
He stopped, but I never see the duke look so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2564"/>
ugly

          <ptr target="#l12276" type="alt" xml:id="te2564"/>
out of his eyes before. I went on a-whimpering, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66635">
“I don’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5403"/>
want

          <app from="pr5403" n="273.13 (456.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7424">
            <lem wit="A">want</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wish</rdg>
          </app>
to blow on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2565"/>
nobody;

          <ptr target="#l12277" type="alt" xml:id="te2565"/>
and I ain’t got no time to blow, nohow. I got to turn out and find my nigger.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66649">
          <pb n="274" xml:id="pb0274"/>
He looked kinder bothered, and stood there with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2566"/>
his bills

          <ptr target="#l12278" type="alt" xml:id="te2566"/>
fluttering on his arm, thinking, and wrinkling

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5404"/>
up

          <app from="pr5404" n="274.2 (456.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7425">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7426">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
his forehead. At last he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66664">“I’ll tell you something. We got to be here three days. If you’ll promise you won’t blow, and won’t let the nigger blow, I’ll tell you where to find him.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66666">
So I promised,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2567"/>
and he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66670">
“A farmer by the name of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2568"/>
Silas

          <ptr target="#l12280" type="alt" xml:id="te2568"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5405"/>
Ph—

          <app from="pr5405" n="274.8 (457verso.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7427">
            <lem wit="MS2">Ph—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Ph——</rdg>
          </app>
” and then he stopped. You

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5406"/>
see,

          <app from="pr5406" n="274.9 (457verso.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7428">
            <lem wit="MS2">see,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
see

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he started to tell me the truth; but when he stopped, that way, and begun to study and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5407"/>
think,

          <app from="pr5407" n="274.10 (457verso.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7429">
            <lem wit="MS2">think,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
think

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
again, I reckoned he was changing his mind. And so he was. He wouldn’t trust me; he wanted to make sure of having me out of the way the whole three days. So pretty soon he says:

          <ptr target="#l12279" type="alt" xml:id="te2567"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66702">
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0076"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5408"/>
“The

          <app from="pr5408" n="274.14 (457.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7430">
            <lem wit="MS2">[¶] “The</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7431">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
“The

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0076" type="te" xml:id="tv0076"/>
man that bought him is named Abram Foster—Abram G. Foster—and he lives

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0005"/>
forty mile back here in the country, on the road to Lafayette

          <ptr target="#as0229" type="an" xml:id="as0005"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66721">
“All right,” I says, “I can walk it in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2569"/>
three

          <ptr target="#l12281" type="alt" xml:id="te2569"/>
days. And I’ll start this very afternoon.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66727">
          <pb n="73" xml:id="pb0073"/>
“No you won’t, you’ll start

          <hi rend="italic">now;</hi>
and don’t you lose

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5409"/>
any

          <app from="pr5409" n="274.19 (457.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7432">
            <lem wit="A">any</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">no</rdg>
          </app>
time about it, neither, nor do any gabbling by the way. Just keep a tight tongue in your head and move right along, and then you won’t get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5410"/>
into

          <app from="pr5410" n="274.22 (458.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7433">
            <lem wit="A">into</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">into no</rdg>
          </app>
trouble with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2570"/>
          <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
,

          <ptr target="#l12282" type="alt" xml:id="te2570"/>
d’ye hear?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66756">That was the order I wanted, and that was the one I played for. I wanted to be left free to work my plans.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66758">
“So clear out,” he says; “and you can tell Mr.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2571"/>
Foster

          <ptr target="#l12283" type="alt" xml:id="te2571"/>
whatever you want to. Maybe you can get him to believe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5411"/>
that

          <app from="pr5411" n="274.26 (458.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7434">
            <lem wit="A">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7435">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Jim

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
your nigger—some idiots don’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5412"/>
require

          <app from="pr5412" n="274.27 (458.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7436">
            <lem wit="A">require</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">require no</rdg>
          </app>
documents—leastways I’ve heard there’s such down South here. And when

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2572"/>
you

          <ptr target="#l12284" type="alt" xml:id="te2572"/>
tell him the handbill and the reward’s bogus, maybe he’ll believe you when you explain to him what the idea was for getting

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2573"/>
’em

          <ptr target="#l12285" type="alt" xml:id="te2573"/>
out. Go ’long, now, and tell him anything you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2574"/>
want

          <ptr target="#l12286" type="alt" xml:id="te2574"/>
to; but mind you don’t work your jaw any

          <hi rend="italic">between</hi>
here and there.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66801">
So I left, and struck for the back country. I didn’t look around, but I kinder felt like he was watching me. But I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2575"/>
knowed

          <ptr target="#l12287" type="alt" xml:id="te2575"/>
I could tire him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2576"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l12288" type="alt" xml:id="te2576"/>
at that. I went straight out in the country as much as a mile, before I stopped; then I doubled back through the woods towards Phelps’s. I reckoned I better start in on my plan straight off, without

          <pb n="275" xml:id="pb0275"/>
fooling around, because I wanted to stop Jim’s mouth till these fellows could get away. I didn’t want no trouble with their kind. I’d seen all I wanted to of them, and wanted to get entirely shut of them.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y27501">
          <graphic url="y27501.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">striking for the back country</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0417">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXII.</head>
        <pb n="276" xml:id="pb0276"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y27601">
          <graphic url="y27601.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5413"/>
Chapter XXXII.

            <app from="pr5413" n="276 title (461.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7437">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXII.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7438">not in; extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">When</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2761">
          <graphic url="hf2761.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">still and sunday-like</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e66836">
I got there it was all still and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5414"/>
Sunday-like

          <app from="pr5414" n="276.2 (461.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7439">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sunday-like</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Sunday-

              <lb/>
like

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and hot and sunshiny

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2577"/>
—the hands was gone to the fields

          <ptr target="#l12289" type="alt" xml:id="te2577"/>
; and there was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2578"/>
them

          <ptr target="#l12290" type="alt" xml:id="te2578"/>
kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2579"/>
faint

          <ptr target="#l12291" type="alt" xml:id="te2579"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5415"/>
dronings of bugs and flies

          <app from="pr5415" n="276.5–6 (461.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7440">
            <lem wit="A">dronings of bugs and flies</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">insect-dronings</rdg>
          </app>
in the air that makes it seem so lonesome and like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5416"/>
everybody’s

          <app from="pr5416" n="276.8 (461.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7441">
            <lem wit="A">everybody’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">everybody</rdg>
          </app>
dead and gone; and if a breeze fans along and quivers the leaves, it makes

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2580"/>
you

          <ptr target="#l12292" type="alt" xml:id="te2580"/>
feel mournful, because you feel like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5417"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr5417" n="276.12 (461.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7442">
            <lem wit="A">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it is</rdg>
          </app>
spirits whispering—spirits that’s been

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2581"/>
dead

          <ptr target="#l12293" type="alt" xml:id="te2581"/>
ever so many years—and you always think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5418"/>
they’re

          <app from="pr5418" n="276.15 (461.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7443">
            <lem wit="A">they’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they are</rdg>
          </app>
talking about

          <hi rend="italic">you.</hi>
As a general

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5419"/>
thing,

          <app from="pr5419" n="276.17 (461.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7444">
            <lem wit="MS2">thing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
thing

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
it makes a body wish

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
was dead, too, and done with it all.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e66917">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0006"/>
Phelps’s was one of these little one-horse cotton plantations

          <ptr target="#as0230" type="an" xml:id="as0006"/>
; and they all look alike. A rail fence

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5420"/>
round

          <app from="pr5420" n="276.19 (462.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7445">
            <lem wit="A">round</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">around</rdg>
          </app>
a two-acre yard; a stile, made

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5421"/>
out

          <app from="pr5421" n="276.20 (462.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7446">
            <lem wit="A">out</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7447">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
of logs sawed off and up-ended, in steps, like barrels of a different length, to climb over the fence with, and for the women to stand on when they are going to jump onto a horse; some sickly grass-patches in the big yard, but mostly it was bare and smooth, like an old hat with the nap rubbed off; big double log house for the white

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5422"/>
folks,

          <app from="pr5422" n="276.24 (462.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7448">
            <lem wit="MS2">folks,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
folks

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
—hewed logs, with the chinks stopped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5423"/>
up

          <app from="pr5423" n="276.25 (463.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7449">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7450">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with mud or mortar, and these

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2582"/>
mud-stripes

          <ptr target="#l12294" type="alt" xml:id="te2582"/>
been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5424"/>
whitewashed

          <app from="pr5424" n="276.26 (463.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7451">
            <lem wit="A">whitewashed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
white-

              <lb/>
washed

            </rdg>
          </app>
some time or

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5425"/>
another

          <app from="pr5425" n="276.26 (463.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7452">
            <lem wit="A">another</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">other</rdg>
          </app>
; round-log kitchen, with a big broad,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5426"/>
open,

          <app from="pr5426" n="276.27 (463.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7453">
            <lem wit="MS2">open,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
open

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
but roofed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5427"/>
passage,

          <app from="pr5427" n="276.27 (463.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7454">
            <lem wit="MS2">passage,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
passage

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
joining it to the house;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2583"/>
log

          <ptr target="#l12295" type="alt" xml:id="te2583"/>
smoke-house back of the kitchen; three little log nigger-cabins in a row

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5428"/>
t’other side

          <app from="pr5428" n="276.29 (463.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7455">
            <lem wit="A">t’other side</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">beyond</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5429"/>
smoke-house

          <app from="pr5429" n="276.29 (463.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7456">
            <lem wit="MS2">smoke-house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
smoke-

              <lb/>
house

            </rdg>
          </app>
; one little hut

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2584"/>
all

          <ptr target="#l12296" type="alt" xml:id="te2584"/>
by

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5430"/>
itself,

          <app from="pr5430" n="276.30 (463.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7457">
            <lem wit="MS2">itself,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
itself

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2585"/>
away

          <ptr target="#l12297" type="alt" xml:id="te2585"/>
down against the back fence, and some

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5431"/>
out-buildings

          <app from="pr5431" n="276.30–31 (463.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la7458">
            <lem wit="C">out-buildings</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
out-

              <lb/>
buildings

            </rdg>
          </app>
down a piece the other side; ash-hopper, and big kettle to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5432"/>
bile

          <app from="pr5432" n="276.32 (463.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7459">
            <lem wit="A">bile</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">boil</rdg>
          </app>
soap in, by the little hut; bench by the kitchen door, with bucket

          <pb n="277" xml:id="pb0277"/>
of water and a gourd; hound asleep there, in the sun; more hounds asleep,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5433"/>
round

          <app from="pr5433" n="277.2 (464.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7460">
            <lem wit="A">round</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">around</rdg>
          </app>
about;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2586"/>
about three

          <ptr target="#l12298" type="alt" xml:id="te2586"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5434"/>
shade

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2587"/>
trees,

          <app from="pr5434" n="277.2 (464.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7461">
            <lem wit="MS2">shade trees,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
shade-

              <lb/>
trees

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5435"/>
away

          <app from="pr5435" n="277.2 (464.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7462">
            <lem wit="A">away</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">way</rdg>
          </app>
off in a corner

          <ptr target="#l12299" type="alt" xml:id="te2587"/>
; some currant bushes and gooseberry bushes in one place by the fence; outside

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5436"/>
of

          <app from="pr5436" n="277.4 (464.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7463">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7464">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5437"/>
fence,

          <app from="pr5437" n="277.4 (464.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7465">
            <lem wit="MS2">fence,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
fence

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a garden

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5438"/>
and a

          <app from="pr5438" n="277.4 (464.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7466">
            <lem wit="A">and a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5439"/>
watermelon

          <app from="pr5439" n="277.4 (464.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7467">
            <lem wit="MS2">watermelon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">water-melon</rdg>
          </app>
patch;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5440"/>
then

          <app from="pr5440" n="277.4 (464.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7468">
            <lem wit="A">then</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the other side of that,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2588"/>
the cotton

          <ptr target="#l12300" type="alt" xml:id="te2588"/>
fields

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2589"/>
begins

          <ptr target="#l12301" type="alt" xml:id="te2589"/>
; and after the fields, the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5441"/>
woods.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67140">
I

          <app from="pr5441" n="277.5–6 (464.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7469">
            <lem wit="A">woods. [¶] I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
woods.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7470">extra line space</note>
[¶] I

            </rdg>
          </app>
went around and clumb over the back stile by the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5442"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2590"/>
ash-hopper

          <ptr target="#l12302" type="alt" xml:id="te2590"/>
          <app from="pr5442" n="277.6 (464.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la7471">
            <lem wit="A">ash-hopper</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
ash-

              <lb/>
hopper

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and started for the kitchen. When I got a little

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2591"/>
ways

          <ptr target="#l12303" type="alt" xml:id="te2591"/>
, I heard the dim

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0007"/>
hum of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5443"/>
spinning wheel

          <app from="pr5443" n="277.8 (464.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7472">
            <lem wit="MS2">spinning wheel</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">spinning-wheel</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5444"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2592"/>
wailing along up

          <ptr target="#l12304" type="alt" xml:id="te2592"/>
          <app from="pr5444" n="277.8 (464.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7473">
            <lem wit="A">wailing along up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">raising up its wail</rdg>
          </app>
and sinking along down

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5445"/>
again:

          <app from="pr5445" n="277.9 (464.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7474">
            <lem wit="MS2">again:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">again;</rdg>
          </app>
and then I knowed for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5446"/>
certain

          <app from="pr5446" n="277.9 (464.17–18)" type="e" xml:id="la7475">
            <lem wit="A">certain</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">certain that</rdg>
          </app>
I wished I was dead—for that

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2593"/>
lonesomest

          <ptr target="#l12305" type="alt" xml:id="te2593"/>
sound in the whole world

          <ptr target="#as0231" type="an" xml:id="as0007"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67214">
I went right along, not fixing up any particular plan, but just trusting

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2594"/>
to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5447"/>
Providence

          <app from="pr5447" n="277.12 (465.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7476">
            <lem wit="A">Providence</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">luck</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12306" type="alt" xml:id="te2594"/>
to put the right words in my mouth when the time come; for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5448"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr5448" n="277.13 (465.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7477">
            <lem wit="A">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I had</rdg>
          </app>
noticed that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5449"/>
Providence

          <app from="pr5449" n="277.13 (465.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7478">
            <lem wit="A">Providence</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">luck</rdg>
          </app>
always did put the right words in my mouth, if I left it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2595"/>
alone.

          <ptr target="#l12307" type="alt" xml:id="te2595"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67247">
When I got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5450"/>
half way

          <app from="pr5450" n="277.15 (465.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7479">
            <lem wit="MS2">half way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half-way</rdg>
          </app>
, first one hound and then another got up and went for me, and of course I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5451"/>
stopped,

          <app from="pr5451" n="277.16 (465.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7480">
            <lem wit="MS2">stopped,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
stopped

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and faced them, and kept still. And such another pow-wow

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2596"/>
as they made!

          <ptr target="#l12308" type="alt" xml:id="te2596"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5452"/>
in

          <app from="pr5452" n="277.17 (466.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7481">
            <lem wit="MS2">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">In</rdg>
          </app>
a quarter of a minute I was a kind of a hub of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2597"/>
a wheel

          <ptr target="#l12309" type="alt" xml:id="te2597"/>
, as you may say—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2598"/>
spokes

          <ptr target="#l12310" type="alt" xml:id="te2598"/>
made out of dogs—circle of fifteen of them packed together around me, with their necks and noses stretched up towards me,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2599"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5453"/>
a-barking

          <app from="pr5453" n="277.20 (466.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7482">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-barking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a barking</rdg>
          </app>
and howling;

          <ptr target="#l12311" type="alt" xml:id="te2599"/>
and more

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5454"/>
a-coming

          <app from="pr5454" n="277.21 (466.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7483">
            <lem wit="C">a-coming</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <lb/>
coming

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">a coming</rdg>
          </app>
; you could see them sailing over fences and around

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5455"/>
corners,

          <app from="pr5455" n="277.22 (466.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7484">
            <lem wit="MS2">corners,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
corners

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
from everywheres.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67318">
A nigger woman come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2600"/>
tearing

          <ptr target="#l12312" type="alt" xml:id="te2600"/>
out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5456"/>
kitchen,

          <app from="pr5456" n="277.23 (466.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7485">
            <lem wit="MS2">kitchen,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
kitchen

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
with a rolling-pin in her hand,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2601"/>
singing

          <ptr target="#l12313" type="alt" xml:id="te2601"/>
out, “Begone!

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
Tige! you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2602"/>
Spot

          <ptr target="#l12314" type="alt" xml:id="te2602"/>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5457"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0077"/>
bedone

          <ptr target="#tb0077" type="te" xml:id="tv0077"/>
          <app from="pr5457" n="277.24 (466.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7486">
            <lem wit="MS2">bedone</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">begone</rdg>
          </app>
, sah!” and she fetched first one and then another of them a clip and sent him howling, and then the rest followed; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2603"/>
the next

          <ptr target="#l12315" type="alt" xml:id="te2603"/>
second, half of them come back, wagging their tails around me and making friends with me. There ain’t no harm in a hound, nohow.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67359">
And behind the woman comes a little nigger girl and two little nigger boys, without anything on but tow-linen shirts, and they hung onto their mother’s gown, and peeped out from behind her at me, bashful, the way they always do. And here comes the white

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0041"/>
woman

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2604"/>
running

          <ptr target="#l12316" type="alt" xml:id="te2604"/>
from the house, about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2605"/>
forty-five or fifty

          <ptr target="#l12317" type="alt" xml:id="te2605"/>
year old,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5458"/>
bareheaded

          <app from="pr5458" n="277.34 (468.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7487">
            <lem wit="A">bareheaded</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
bare-

              <lb/>
headed

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5459"/>
spinning-stick

          <app from="pr5459" n="277.34 (468.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7488">
            <lem wit="A">spinning-stick</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
spinning-

              <lb/>
stick

            </rdg>
          </app>
in her hand; and behind her comes her little white children, acting the same way the little niggers was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2606"/>
doing.

          <ptr target="#l12318" type="alt" xml:id="te2606"/>
She was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2607"/>
smiling

          <ptr target="#l12319" type="alt" xml:id="te2607"/>
all over so she could hardly stand—and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67401">
“It’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5460"/>
          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
, at last

          <app from="pr5460" n="277.38 (468.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7489">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
, at last

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Tom</rdg>
          </app>
!—

          <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67419">
          <pb n="278" xml:id="pb0278"/>
I out with a “Yes’m,” before I thought.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67421">
She grabbed me

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2608"/>
and hugged me tight; and then gripped me

          <ptr target="#l12320" type="alt" xml:id="te2608"/>
by both

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5461"/>
hands,

          <app from="pr5461" n="278.3 (468.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7490">
            <lem wit="MS2">hands,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
hands

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2609"/>
shook and shook;

          <ptr target="#l12321" type="alt" xml:id="te2609"/>
and the tears come in her eyes, and run down over; and she couldn’t

          <ptr target="#mt0041" type="alt" xml:id="wn0041"/>
seem to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2610"/>
hug and

          <ptr target="#l12322" type="alt" xml:id="te2610"/>
shake enough, and kept saying, “You don’t look as much like your mother as I reckoned you would, but law sakes, I don’t care for that, I’m

          <hi rend="italic">so</hi>
glad to see you! Dear, dear, it does seem like I could eat you up!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5462"/>
Childern

          <app from="pr5462" n="278.7 (469.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7491">
            <lem wit="A">Childern</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Children</rdg>
          </app>
, it’s your cousin Tom!—tell him howdy.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y27801">
          <graphic url="y27801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">she hugged him tight</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67463">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2611"/>
But

          <ptr target="#l12323" type="alt" xml:id="te2611"/>
they ducked their heads, and put their fingers in their mouths, and hid behind her. So she run on:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67468">
“Lize, hurry up and get him a hot breakfast, right away—or did you get your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0042"/>
breakfast on the boat?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67472">
I said I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5463"/>
had

          <app from="pr5463" n="278.13 (470.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7492">
            <lem wit="A">had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7493">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
got it on the boat. So then she started for the house, leading me by the hand, and the children tagging after. When we got there, she set me down in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5464"/>
split-bottomed

          <app from="pr5464" n="278.15 (470.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7494">
            <lem wit="A">split-bottomed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">split-bottom</rdg>
          </app>
chair, and set herself down on a little low stool in front of me,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2612"/>
holding

          <ptr target="#l12324" type="alt" xml:id="te2612"/>
both of my hands, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67496">
“Now I can have a

          <hi rend="italic">good</hi>
look at you; and laws-a-me,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2613"/>
I’ve

          <ptr target="#l12325" type="alt" xml:id="te2613"/>
been

          <pb n="279" xml:id="pb0279"/>
hungry for it a many and a many a time,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2614"/>
all these long years,

          <ptr target="#l12326" type="alt" xml:id="te2614"/>
and it’s come at last! We been

          <ptr target="#mt0042" type="alt" xml:id="wn0042"/>
expecting you a couple of days

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2615"/>
and more

          <ptr target="#l12327" type="alt" xml:id="te2615"/>
. What’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5465"/>
kep’

          <app from="pr5465" n="279.3 (471.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7495">
            <lem wit="A">kep’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kept</rdg>
          </app>
you?—boat get aground?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67524">
“Yes’m—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5466"/>
she—

          <app from="pr5466" n="279.4 (471.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7496">
            <lem wit="MS2">she—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">she——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67534">
“Don’t say yes’m—say

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5467"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5467" n="279.5 (471.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7497">
            <lem wit="C">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
Aunt

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7498">
see textual note to

                <ref corresp="#tb0022" type="noteref">47.18</ref>
              </note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Sally. Where’d she get aground?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67548">
I didn’t rightly know what to say, because I didn’t know whether the boat would be coming up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2616"/>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5468"/>
river,

          <app from="pr5468" n="279.7 (471.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7499">
            <lem wit="MS2">river,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
river

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12328" type="alt" xml:id="te2616"/>
or

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2617"/>
down.

          <ptr target="#l12329" type="alt" xml:id="te2617"/>
But I go a good deal on instinct; and my instinct

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2618"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l12330" type="alt" xml:id="te2618"/>
she would be coming up—from

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2619"/>
down towards

          <ptr target="#l12331" type="alt" xml:id="te2619"/>
Orleans. That didn’t help me much, though; for I didn’t know the names of bars down that way. I see I’d got to invent a bar, or forget the name of the one we got aground on—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5469"/>
or—

          <app from="pr5469" n="279.11 (472.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7500">
            <lem wit="A">or—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or—.</rdg>
          </app>
Now I struck an idea, and fetched it out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67582">“It warn’t the grounding—that didn’t keep us back but a little. We blowed out a cylinder-head.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67585">“Good gracious! anybody hurt?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67587">“No’m. Killed a nigger.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67589">
“Well, it’s lucky; because sometimes people do get hurt. Two years ago last Christmas, your uncle Silas was coming up from Newrleans on the old

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0008"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5470"/>
Lally Rook

          <app from="pr5470" n="279.19 (473.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7501">
            <lem wit="MS2">Lally Rook</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Lally Rook</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0232" type="an" xml:id="uu0008"/>
, and she blowed out a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5471"/>
cylinder-head

          <app from="pr5471" n="279.19–20 (473.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7502">
            <lem wit="A">cylinder-head</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
cylinder-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
and crippled a man. And I think he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5472"/>
died,

          <app from="pr5472" n="279.20 (473.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7503">
            <lem wit="MS2">died,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
died

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
afterwards. He was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2620"/>
Babtist

          <ptr target="#l12332" type="alt" xml:id="te2620"/>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2621"/>
Your uncle Silas knowed a family in Baton Rouge that knowed his people very well. Yes, I remember,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5473"/>
now,

          <app from="pr5473" n="279.22 (473.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7504">
            <lem wit="MS2">now,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
now

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
he

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
die. Mortification set in, and they had to amputate him. But it didn’t save him. Yes, it was mortification—that was it. He turned blue all over, and died in the hope of a glorious resurrection. They say he was a sight to look at. Your uncle’s been up to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5474"/>
town

          <app from="pr5474" n="279.26 (474verso.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7505">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">village</rdg>
          </app>
every day to fetch you. And he’s gone again, not more’n an hour ago; he’ll be back any minute, now. You must a met him on the road, didn’t you?—oldish man, with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5475"/>
a—

          <app from="pr5475" n="279.29 (474verso.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7506">
            <lem wit="MS2">a—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a——</rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#l12333" type="alt" xml:id="te2621"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67657">
“No, I didn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5476"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr5476" n="279.30 (474.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7507">
            <lem wit="A">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5477"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5477" n="279.30 (474.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7508">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally. The boat landed just at daylight, and I left my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2622"/>
baggage

          <ptr target="#l12334" type="alt" xml:id="te2622"/>
on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5478"/>
wharfboat

          <app from="pr5478" n="279.31 (474.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7509">
            <lem wit="MS2">wharfboat</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wharf-boat</rdg>
          </app>
and went looking around the town and out a piece in the country, to put in the time and not get here too soon; and so I come down the back way.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67688">
“Who’d you give the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2623"/>
baggage

          <ptr target="#l12335" type="alt" xml:id="te2623"/>
to?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67694">“Nobody.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67696">“Why, child, it’ll be stole!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67698">
“Not where

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
hid it I reckon it won’t,”

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5479"/>
I says

          <app from="pr5479" n="279.37 (475.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7510">
            <lem wit="A">I says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says I</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67711">“How’d you get your breakfast so early on the boat?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67713">
          <pb n="280" xml:id="pb0280"/>
It was kinder thin ice, but I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67715">
“The captain see me standing around,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2624"/>
and told

          <ptr target="#l12336" type="alt" xml:id="te2624"/>
me I better have something to eat before I went ashore; so he took me in the texas to the officers’ lunch, and give me all I wanted.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67722">
I was getting so uneasy I couldn’t listen good. I had my mind on the children all the time; I wanted to get them out to one side, and pump them a little, and find out who I was. But I couldn’t get no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2625"/>
show,

          <ptr target="#l12337" type="alt" xml:id="te2625"/>
Mrs. Phelps kept it up and run on so. Pretty soon she made the cold chills streak all down my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5480"/>
back;

          <app from="pr5480" n="280.9 (477.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7511">
            <lem wit="MS2">back;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">back,</rdg>
          </app>
because she says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67736">
“But here we’re a running

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5481"/>
on,

          <app from="pr5481" n="280.10 (477.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7512">
            <lem wit="MS2">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
this way, and you hain’t told me a word about Sis, nor any of them. Now I’ll rest my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2626"/>
works

          <ptr target="#l12338" type="alt" xml:id="te2626"/>
a little, and you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2627"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5482"/>
start-up

          <app from="pr5482" n="280.12 (477.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7513">
            <lem wit="MS2">start-up</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">start up</rdg>
          </app>
yourn;

          <ptr target="#l12339" type="alt" xml:id="te2627"/>
just tell me

          <hi rend="italic">everything</hi>
—tell me all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5483"/>
about ’m

          <app from="pr5483" n="280.12 (477.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7514">
            <lem wit="A">about ’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">about them</rdg>
          </app>
all—every one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5484"/>
of ’m

          <app from="pr5484" n="280.13 (477.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7515">
            <lem wit="A">of ’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of them</rdg>
          </app>
; and how they are, and what they’re doing, and what they told you to tell me; and every last thing you can think of.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67782">
Well, I see I was up a stump—and up it good.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5485"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2628"/>
Providence

          <ptr target="#l12340" type="alt" xml:id="te2628"/>
          <app from="pr5485" n="280.16 (478.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7516">
            <lem wit="A">Providence</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Luck</rdg>
          </app>
had stood by me this

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5486"/>
fur

          <app from="pr5486" n="280.17 (478.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7517">
            <lem wit="A">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
, all right, but I was hard and tight aground, now. I see it warn’t a bit of use to try to go ahead—I’d

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to throw up my hand. So I says to myself, here’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5487"/>
another

          <app from="pr5487" n="280.19 (478.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7518">
            <lem wit="A">another</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">another</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
place where I got to resk the truth. I opened my mouth to begin; but she grabbed me and hustled me in behind the bed, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67815">
“Here

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2629"/>
he comes

          <ptr target="#l12341" type="alt" xml:id="te2629"/>
!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5488"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2630"/>
Stick

          <ptr target="#l12342" type="alt" xml:id="te2630"/>
          <app from="pr5488" n="280.22 (478.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7519">
            <lem wit="MS2">Stick</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stick</rdg>
          </app>
your head down lower—there, that’ll do; you can’t be seen, now. Don’t you let on you’re

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5489"/>
here.

          <app from="pr5489" n="280.23 (479.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7520">
            <lem wit="A">here.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">here:</rdg>
          </app>
I’ll play a joke on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2631"/>
him.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5490"/>
Childern

          <app from="pr5490" n="280.24 (479.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7521">
            <lem wit="A">Childern</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Children</rdg>
          </app>
, don’t you say a word.”

          <ptr target="#l12343" type="alt" xml:id="te2631"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67851">I see I was in a fix, now. But it warn’t no use to worry; there warn’t nothing to do but just hold still, and try and be ready to stand from under when the lightning struck.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67853">
I had just one little glimpse of the old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5491"/>
gentleman

          <app from="pr5491" n="280.28 (480.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7522">
            <lem wit="A">gentleman</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
gentle-

              <lb/>
man

            </rdg>
          </app>
when he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2632"/>
come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5492"/>
in,

          <ptr target="#l12344" type="alt" xml:id="te2632"/>
—

          <app from="pr5492" n="280.29 (480.3–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7523">
            <lem wit="MS2">in,—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
in,

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then the bed hid

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2633"/>
him.

          <ptr target="#l12345" type="alt" xml:id="te2633"/>
Mrs. Phelps she jumps

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2634"/>
for him

          <ptr target="#l12346" type="alt" xml:id="te2634"/>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67886">“Has he come?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67888">“No,” says her husband.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67890">
“Good-

          <hi rend="italic">ness</hi>
gracious!” she says, “what in the world

          <hi rend="italic">can</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5493"/>
have

          <app from="pr5493" n="280.32 (480.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7524">
            <lem wit="A">have</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
become

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2635"/>
of

          <ptr target="#l12347" type="alt" xml:id="te2635"/>
him?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67909">“I can’t imagine,” says the old gentleman; “and I must say, it makes me dreadful uneasy.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67911">
“Uneasy!” she says, “I’m ready to go distracted! He

          <hi rend="italic">must</hi>
a come; and you’ve missed him along the road. I

          <hi rend="italic">know</hi>
it’s so—something

          <hi rend="italic">tells</hi>
me so.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67923">
          <pb n="281" xml:id="pb0281"/>
“Why

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2636"/>
Sally,

          <ptr target="#l12348" type="alt" xml:id="te2636"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5494"/>
I

          <app from="pr5494" n="281.1 (481.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7525">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
miss him along the road—

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
know that.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67941">
“But oh, dear, dear, what

          <hi rend="italic">will</hi>
Sis say!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2637"/>
He must

          <ptr target="#l12349" type="alt" xml:id="te2637"/>
a come!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5495"/>
You must

          <app from="pr5495" n="281.2 (481.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la7526">
            <lem wit="A">You must</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
You

              <hi rend="italic">must</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a missed him.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5496"/>
He—

          <app from="pr5496" n="281.3 (481.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7527">
            <lem wit="MS2">He—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">He——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e67969">
“Oh, don’t distress me any more’n I’m already distressed. I don’t know what in the world to make of it. I’m at my wit’s end, and I don’t mind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2638"/>
acknowledging’t

          <ptr target="#l12350" type="alt" xml:id="te2638"/>
I’m right down scared. But there’s no hope that he’s come; for he

          <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
come and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2639"/>
me

          <ptr target="#l12351" type="alt" xml:id="te2639"/>
miss

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2640"/>
him.

          <ptr target="#l12352" type="alt" xml:id="te2640"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5497"/>
Sally

          <app from="pr5497" n="281.7 (482.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7528">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sally</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sally,</rdg>
          </app>
it’s terrible—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5498"/>
just

          <app from="pr5498" n="281.8 (482.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7529">
            <lem wit="A">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it’s just</rdg>
          </app>
terrible—something’s happened to the boat,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2641"/>
sure

          <ptr target="#l12353" type="alt" xml:id="te2641"/>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68007">
“Why,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2642"/>
Silas

          <ptr target="#l12354" type="alt" xml:id="te2642"/>
! Look yonder!—up the road!—ain’t that somebody coming?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68013">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2643"/>
He sprung

          <ptr target="#l12355" type="alt" xml:id="te2643"/>
to the window at the head of the bed, and that give Mrs. Phelps the chance she wanted. She stooped down quick, at the foot of the bed, and give me a pull, and out I come; and when

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2644"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l12356" type="alt" xml:id="te2644"/>
turned back from the window, there she stood, a-beaming and a-smiling like a house afire, and I standing pretty meek and sweaty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5499"/>
alongside

          <app from="pr5499" n="281.17 (483.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la7530">
            <lem wit="A">alongside</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
along-

              <lb/>
side

            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2645"/>
The old gentleman stared, and says:

          <ptr target="#l12357" type="alt" xml:id="te2645"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68036">“Why, who’s that?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68038">
“Who do you reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5500"/>
’t

          <app from="pr5500" n="281.19 (483.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7531">
            <lem wit="A">’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
is?”

        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e68048">
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="us0008"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y28101">
            <graphic url="y28101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">
who do you reckon

                <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5501"/>
’t

              </hi>
              <app from="pr5501" n="281 caption" type="e" xml:id="la7532">
                <lem wit="C">
’

                  <hi rend="smallcaps">t</hi>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7533">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">it</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">is</hi>
?”

            </ab>
          </figure>
          <ptr target="#as0233" type="an" xml:id="um0008"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68072">
          <pb n="282" xml:id="pb0282"/>
“I hain’t no idea. Who

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68077">
“It’s

          <hi rend="italic">Tom Sawyer!</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68082">
By jings, I most slumped

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5502"/>
through

          <app from="pr5502" n="282.3 (484.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7534">
            <lem wit="MS2">through</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">though</rdg>
          </app>
the floor. But there warn’t no time to swap

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5503"/>
knives:

          <app from="pr5503" n="282.4 (484.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7535">
            <lem wit="MS2">knives:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">knives;</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2646"/>
the old man grabbed me by the hand and shook, and kept on shaking; and

          <ptr target="#l12358" type="alt" xml:id="te2646"/>
all the time, how the woman did dance around and laugh and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2650"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2647"/>
cry;

          <ptr target="#l12359" type="alt" xml:id="te2647"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2648"/>
and then how they both did

          <ptr target="#l12360" type="alt" xml:id="te2648"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2649"/>
fire off questions about Sid, and Mary, and the rest of the tribe.

          <ptr target="#l12361" type="alt" xml:id="te2649"/>
          <ptr target="#l12362" type="alt" xml:id="te2650"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68116">
But if they was joyful, it warn’t nothing to what I was; for it was like being born again, I was so glad to find out who I was. Well, they froze to me for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2651"/>
two

          <ptr target="#l12363" type="alt" xml:id="te2651"/>
hours; and at last when my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2652"/>
chin

          <ptr target="#l12364" type="alt" xml:id="te2652"/>
was so tired it couldn’t hardly

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2653"/>
go,

          <ptr target="#l12365" type="alt" xml:id="te2653"/>
any more, I had told them more about my family—I mean the Sawyer family—than ever happened to any six Sawyer families. And I explained all about how we blowed out a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5504"/>
cylinder head

          <app from="pr5504" n="282.14 (485.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7536">
            <lem wit="MS2">cylinder head</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cylinder-head</rdg>
          </app>
at

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0010"/>
the mouth of White

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5505"/>
river

          <app from="pr5505" n="282.14 (485.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7537">
            <lem wit="MS2">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">River</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0234" type="an" xml:id="uu0010"/>
and it took us three days to fix it. Which was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2654"/>
all right

          <ptr target="#l12366" type="alt" xml:id="te2654"/>
, and worked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5506"/>
first-rate

          <app from="pr5506" n="282.15 (485.17–486.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7538">
            <lem wit="C">first-rate</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
first-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
rate

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">first rate</rdg>
          </app>
; because

          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
didn’t know but what it would take three days to fix it. If I’d a called it a bolt-head it would a done just as well.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68170">
Now I was feeling

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2655"/>
pretty

          <ptr target="#l12367" type="alt" xml:id="te2655"/>
comfortable all down one side, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2656"/>
pretty

          <ptr target="#l12368" type="alt" xml:id="te2656"/>
uncomfortable all up the other. Being Tom Sawyer was easy and comfortable; and it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5507"/>
staid

          <app from="pr5507" n="282.20 (486.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7539">
            <lem wit="MS2">staid</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">stayed</rdg>
          </app>
easy and comfortable till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5508"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5508" n="282.20 (486.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7540">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
I hear a steamboat coughing along down the river—then I says to myself,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5509"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2657"/>
spose Tom

          <ptr target="#l12369" type="alt" xml:id="te2657"/>
          <app from="pr5509" n="282.22 (486.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7541">
            <lem wit="A">spose Tom</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
suppose/

              <add>spose</add>
Tom

            </rdg>
          </app>
Sawyer come down on that boat?—and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5510"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2658"/>
spose he

          <ptr target="#l12370" type="alt" xml:id="te2658"/>
          <app from="pr5510" n="282.22 (487.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la7542">
            <lem wit="A">spose he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
suppose/

              <add>spose</add>
he

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2659"/>
steps

          <ptr target="#l12371" type="alt" xml:id="te2659"/>
in here, any minute, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2660"/>
sings

          <ptr target="#l12372" type="alt" xml:id="te2660"/>
out my name before I can

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2661"/>
throw

          <ptr target="#l12373" type="alt" xml:id="te2661"/>
him a wink to keep

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2662"/>
quiet?

          <ptr target="#l12374" type="alt" xml:id="te2662"/>
Well, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2663"/>
couldn’t

          <ptr target="#l12375" type="alt" xml:id="te2663"/>
          <hi rend="italic">have</hi>
it that way—it wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5511"/>
do,

          <app from="pr5511" n="282.25 (487.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7543">
            <lem wit="MS2">do,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
do

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at all. I must go up the road and waylay him. So I told the folks I reckoned I would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2664"/>
go

          <ptr target="#l12376" type="alt" xml:id="te2664"/>
up to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5512"/>
town

          <app from="pr5512" n="282.26 (487.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la7544">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">village</rdg>
          </app>
and fetch down my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2665"/>
baggage. The old gentleman

          <ptr target="#l12377" type="alt" xml:id="te2665"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2666"/>
was for going along with me, but I said no, I could drive the horse myself, and I druther he wouldn’t take no trouble about me.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0421">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXIII.</head>
        <pb n="283" xml:id="pb0283"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y28301">
          <graphic url="y28301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5513"/>
Chapter XXXIII. So

            <app from="pr5513" n="283 title–1 (488.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7545">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXIII. [¶] So</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7546">
no

                  <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
                </note>
So

              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2831">
          <graphic url="hf2831.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">it was tom sawyer.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e68295">
I started for town, in the wagon, and when I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5514"/>
half way

          <app from="pr5514" n="283.2 (488.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7547">
            <lem wit="MS2">half way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half-way</rdg>
          </app>
I see a wagon coming, and sure enough it was Tom Sawyer, and I stopped and waited till he come along.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2667"/>
I says

          <ptr target="#l12379" type="alt" xml:id="te2667"/>
“Hold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5515"/>
on!

          <app from="pr5515" n="283.6 (488.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7548">
            <lem wit="A">on!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on!;</rdg>
          </app>
” and it stopped alongside, and his mouth

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5516"/>
opened up

          <app from="pr5516" n="283.8 (488.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la7549">
            <lem wit="A">opened up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">fell open</rdg>
          </app>
like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5517"/>
trunk

          <app from="pr5517" n="283.8 (488.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7550">
            <lem wit="A">trunk</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">portmonny</rdg>
          </app>
, and staid so; and he swallowed two or three

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5518"/>
times,

          <app from="pr5518" n="283.10 (488.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7551">
            <lem wit="MS2">times,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
times

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
like a person that’s got a dry throat, and then says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68343">
“I hain’t ever done you no harm. You know that. So then, what you want to come back and ha’nt

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
, for?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68348">I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68350">
“I hain’t come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2668"/>
back

          <ptr target="#l12380" type="alt" xml:id="te2668"/>
—I hain’t been

          <hi rend="italic">gone.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68359">
When he heard my voice, it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2669"/>
righted

          <ptr target="#l12381" type="alt" xml:id="te2669"/>
him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5519"/>
up,

          <app from="pr5519" n="283.19 (489.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7552">
            <lem wit="MS2">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
some, but he warn’t quite

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5520"/>
satisfied,

          <app from="pr5520" n="283.20 (489.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7553">
            <lem wit="MS2">satisfied,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
satisfied

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68382">“Don’t you play nothing on me, because I wouldn’t on you. Honest injun, now, you ain’t a ghost?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68384">
“Honest

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2670"/>
injun, I ain’t,” I says.

          <ptr target="#l12382" type="alt" xml:id="te2670"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68389">
“Well—I—I—well, that ought to settle it, of course; but I can’t somehow seem to understand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5521"/>
it,

          <app from="pr5521" n="283.25 (490.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7554">
            <lem wit="MS2">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
no way.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5522"/>
Lookyhere

          <app from="pr5522" n="283.25 (490.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7555">
            <lem wit="MS2">Lookyhere</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Looky here</rdg>
          </app>
, warn’t you ever murdered

          <hi rend="italic">at all?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68411">“No. I warn’t ever murdered at all—I played it on them. You come in here and feel of me if you don’t believe me.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68413">
So he done it; and it satisfied him; and he was that glad to see me again, he didn’t know what to do. And he wanted to know all about it, right off; because it was a grand adventure, and mysterious, and so it hit him where he lived. But I said, leave it alone till

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5523"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5523" n="283.32 (491.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7556">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <pb n="284" xml:id="pb0284"/>
and told his driver to wait, and we drove off a little piece, and I told him the kind of a fix I was in, and what did he reckon we better do? He said, let him alone a minute, and don’t disturb him. So he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2671"/>
thought and

          <ptr target="#l12383" type="alt" xml:id="te2671"/>
thought, and pretty soon he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68427">
“It’s all right, I’ve got it. Take my trunk in your wagon, and let on it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5524"/>
your’n

          <app from="pr5524" n="284.6 (491.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7557">
            <lem wit="A">your’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your own</rdg>
          </app>
; and you turn back and fool along slow, so as to get to the house about the time you ought to; and I’ll go towards town a piece, and take a fresh start, and get there a quarter or a half an hour after you; and you needn’t let on to know me, at first.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68437">
I says:

          <ptr target="#l12378" type="alt" xml:id="te2666"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68440">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2672"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2673"/>
“All right; but wait a minute. There’s

          <ptr target="#l12385" type="alt" xml:id="te2673"/>
one more thing—a thing that

          <hi rend="italic">nobody</hi>
don’t know but me. And that is, there’s a nigger here that I’m a trying to steal out of slavery—and his name

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2674"/>
is

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5525"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
          <app from="pr5525" n="284.13 (493.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7558">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
—

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
.—

            </rdg>
          </app>
—old Miss Watson’s Jim.

          <ptr target="#l12386" type="alt" xml:id="te2674"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68467">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2675"/>
He says:

          <ptr target="#l12387" type="alt" xml:id="te2675"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68471">
“What! Why Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5526"/>
is—

          <app from="pr5526" n="284.16 (493.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7559">
            <lem wit="MS2">is—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">is——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68481">
He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5527"/>
stopped,

          <app from="pr5527" n="284.17 (493.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7560">
            <lem wit="MS2">stopped,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
stopped

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and went to studying. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68491">
“

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know what you’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2676"/>
say. You’ll

          <ptr target="#l12388" type="alt" xml:id="te2676"/>
say it’s dirty low-down business; but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2677"/>
what if it is?—

          <ptr target="#l12389" type="alt" xml:id="te2677"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5528"/>
low-down

          <app from="pr5528" n="284.19 (494.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7561">
            <lem wit="MS2">low-down</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">low down</rdg>
          </app>
; and I’m agoing to steal him, and I want you to keep mum and not let on. Will you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68515">His eye lit up, and he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68517">
“I’ll

          <hi rend="italic">help</hi>
you steal him!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68523">
Well, I let go all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5529"/>
holts,

          <app from="pr5529" n="284.23 (494.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7562">
            <lem wit="MS2">holts,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
holts

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then, like I was shot. It was the most astonishing speech I ever

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5530"/>
heard

          <app from="pr5530" n="284.24 (494.14–15)" type="e" xml:id="la7563">
            <lem wit="A">heard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">heard in my life</rdg>
          </app>
—and I’m bound to say Tom Sawyer fell, considerable, in my estimation. Only I couldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5531"/>
believe

          <app from="pr5531" n="284.25 (495.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7564">
            <lem wit="A">believe</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">quite believe</rdg>
          </app>
it. Tom Sawyer a

          <hi rend="italic">nigger stealer!</hi>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68552">
“Oh, shucks,” I says,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5532"/>
“you’re

          <app from="pr5532" n="284.27 (495.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7565">
            <lem wit="A">“you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you’re</rdg>
          </app>
joking.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68562">“I ain’t joking, either.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68564">
“Well, then,” I says, “joking or no joking, if you hear anything said about a runaway nigger, don’t forget to remember that

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
don’t know nothing about him, and

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t know nothing about him.

          <ptr target="#l12384" type="alt" xml:id="te2672"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68574">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2678"/>
Then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2679"/>
we

          <ptr target="#l12391" type="alt" xml:id="te2679"/>
took the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2680"/>
trunk

          <ptr target="#l12392" type="alt" xml:id="te2680"/>
and put it in my wagon, and he drove off his way, and I drove mine. But of course I forgot all about driving slow, on accounts of being glad and full of thinking; so I got home

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2681"/>
a heap

          <ptr target="#l12393" type="alt" xml:id="te2681"/>
too

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2682"/>
quick

          <ptr target="#l12394" type="alt" xml:id="te2682"/>
for that length of a trip. The old gentleman was at the door, and he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68594">
“Why, this is wonderful. Who ever would a thought it was in that

          <pb n="285" xml:id="pb0285"/>
mare to do it. I wish we’d a timed her. And she hain’t sweated a hair—not a hair. It’s wonderful. Why, I wouldn’t take a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5533"/>
hunderd

          <app from="pr5533" n="285.2 (496.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7566">
            <lem wit="A">hunderd</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hundred</rdg>
          </app>
dollars for that horse now; I wouldn’t, honest; and yet I’d a sold her for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5534"/>
fifteen,

          <app from="pr5534" n="285.4 (496.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la7567">
            <lem wit="MS2">fifteen,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
fifteen

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
before, and thought ’twas all she was worth.”

          <ptr target="#l12390" type="alt" xml:id="te2678"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68613">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2683"/>
That’s all he said. He was the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5535"/>
innocentest

          <app from="pr5535" n="285.5 (497.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7568">
            <lem wit="MS2">innocentest</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">innocentest,</rdg>
          </app>
best old soul I ever see. But it warn’t surprising; because he warn’t only just a farmer, he was a preacher, too, and had a little one-horse log church down back of the plantation, which he built it himself at his own expense, for a church and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5536"/>
school house

          <app from="pr5536" n="285.9 (498.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7569">
            <lem wit="MS2">school house</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">school-house</rdg>
          </app>
, and never charged nothing for his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2684"/>
preaching, and it was worth it, too.

          <ptr target="#l12396" type="alt" xml:id="te2684"/>
There was plenty other farmer-preachers like that, and done the same way, down South.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68637">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2685"/>
In about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5537"/>
half

          <app from="pr5537" n="285.12 (499.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7570">
            <lem wit="A">half</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a half</rdg>
          </app>
an hour Tom’s wagon drove

          <ptr target="#l12397" type="alt" xml:id="te2685"/>
up to the front stile,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2686"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l12398" type="alt" xml:id="te2686"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5538"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5538" n="285.13 (499.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7571">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally she see it through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5539"/>
window—

          <app from="pr5539" n="285.13 (499.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7572">
            <lem wit="MS2">window—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
window

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
because it was only about fifty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5540"/>
yards—

          <app from="pr5540" n="285.14 (499.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7573">
            <lem wit="MS2">yards—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">yards,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68678">
“Why, there’s somebody come! I wonder who ’tis? Why, I do believe it’s a stranger.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5541"/>
Jimmy,

          <app from="pr5541" n="285.16 (499.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7574">
            <lem wit="MS2">Jimmy,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Jimmy

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
” (that’s one of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5542"/>
children,)

          <app from="pr5542" n="285.16 (499.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7575">
            <lem wit="MS2">children,)</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">children),</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2687"/>
run

          <ptr target="#l12399" type="alt" xml:id="te2687"/>
and tell Lize to put on another plate for dinner.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68701">
Everybody made a rush for the front

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5543"/>
door—

          <app from="pr5543" n="285.18 (499.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7576">
            <lem wit="MS2">door—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">door,</rdg>
          </app>
because, of course, a stranger don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2688"/>
come

          <ptr target="#l12400" type="alt" xml:id="te2688"/>
          <hi rend="italic">every</hi>
year, and so he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2689"/>
lays

          <ptr target="#l12401" type="alt" xml:id="te2689"/>
over the yaller fever, for interest, when he does come. Tom was over the stile and starting for the house; the wagon was spinning up the road for the village, and we was all bunched in the front door. Tom had his store clothes on, and an audience—and that was always nuts for Tom Sawyer. In them circumstances

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2690"/>
it warn’t no trouble to him to throw

          <ptr target="#l12402" type="alt" xml:id="te2690"/>
in an amount of style that was suitable. He warn’t a boy to meeky along up that yard like a sheep; no, he come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5544"/>
ca’m

          <app from="pr5544" n="285.26 (500.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7577">
            <lem wit="A">ca’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">c’am</rdg>
          </app>
and important, like the ram. When he got afront of us, he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5545"/>
lifts

          <app from="pr5545" n="285.27 (501.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7578">
            <lem wit="A">lifts</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">lifted up</rdg>
          </app>
his hat ever so gracious and dainty, like it was the lid of a box that had butterflies asleep in it and he didn’t want to disturb them, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68743">“Mr. Archibald Nichols, I presume?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68746">
“No, my

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2691"/>
boy,” says the old gentleman, “I’m

          <ptr target="#l12403" type="alt" xml:id="te2691"/>
sorry to say ’t your driver has deceived you; Nichols’s place is down a matter of three mile more. Come in, come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2692"/>
in.

          <ptr target="#l12404" type="alt" xml:id="te2692"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68756">
Tom he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2693"/>
took a look back over his shoulder, and

          <ptr target="#l12405" type="alt" xml:id="te2693"/>
says, “Too late—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5546"/>
he

          <app from="pr5546" n="285.34 (501.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7579">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7580">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
’s out of sight.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68771">
“Yes, he’s gone, my son, and you must come in and eat your dinner with us; and then we’ll hitch up and take you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2694"/>
down to Nichols’s.”

          <ptr target="#l12406" type="alt" xml:id="te2694"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e68776">
          <pb n="286" xml:id="pb0286"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y28601">
            <graphic url="y28601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">mr. archibald nichols, i presume?</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68783">
“Oh, I

          <hi rend="italic">can’t</hi>
make you so much

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5547"/>
trouble,

          <app from="pr5547" n="286.1 (502.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7581">
            <lem wit="MS2">trouble,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">trouble;</rdg>
          </app>
I couldn’t think of it. I’ll walk—I don’t mind the distance.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68796">
“But we won’t

          <hi rend="italic">let</hi>
you walk—it wouldn’t be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5548"/>
southern

          <app from="pr5548" n="286.3 (502.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7582">
            <lem wit="MS2">southern</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Southern</rdg>
          </app>
hospitality to do it. Come right in.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68809">
“Oh,

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
,” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5549"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5549" n="286.5 (502.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7583">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally; “it ain’t a bit of trouble to us, not a bit in the world. You

          <hi rend="italic">must</hi>
stay. It’s a long, dusty three mile, and we

          <hi rend="italic">can’t</hi>
let you walk. And besides, I’ve

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2695"/>
already

          <ptr target="#l12407" type="alt" xml:id="te2695"/>
told ’em to put on another plate, when I see you coming; so you mustn’t disappoint us. Come right in, and make yourself at home.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68833">
So Tom he thanked them very hearty and handsome, and let himself be persuaded, and come in; and when he was in, he said he was a stranger from

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0011"/>
Hicksville, Ohio

          <ptr target="#as0235" type="an" xml:id="uu0011"/>
, and his name was William Thompson—and he made another bow.

          <ptr target="#l12395" type="alt" xml:id="te2683"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68840">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5550"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2696"/>
Well

          <app from="pr5550" n="286.14 (504.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7584">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7585">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, he run on, and on, and on, making up stuff about Hicksville and everybody in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5551"/>
it

          <app from="pr5551" n="286.15 (504.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7586">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it that</rdg>
          </app>
he could invent, and I getting a little

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5552"/>
nervious

          <app from="pr5552" n="286.15 (504.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7587">
            <lem wit="A">nervious</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">nervous</rdg>
          </app>
, and wondering how this was going to help me out of my scrape; and at last, still talking along, he reached over and kissed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5553"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5553" n="286.17 (504.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7588">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally

          <pb n="287" xml:id="pb0287"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2697"/>
right

          <ptr target="#l12409" type="alt" xml:id="te2697"/>
on the mouth, and then settled back

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5554"/>
again,

          <app from="pr5554" n="287.1 (504.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7589">
            <lem wit="MS2">again,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
again

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
in his chair, comfortable, and was going on talking; but she jumped up and wiped it off with the back of her hand, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68892">“You owdacious puppy!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68894">
He looked

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2698"/>
kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5555"/>
hurt

          <app from="pr5555" n="287.5 (504.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7590">
            <lem wit="A">hurt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">injured</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <ptr target="#l12410" type="alt" xml:id="te2698"/>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68909">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2699"/>
I’m

          <ptr target="#l12411" type="alt" xml:id="te2699"/>
surprised at you, m’am.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68915">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5556"/>
You’re

          <app from="pr5556" n="287.7 (504.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7591">
            <lem wit="A">You’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">You’re</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5557"/>
s’rp—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2700"/>
Why

          <ptr target="#l12412" type="alt" xml:id="te2700"/>
          <app from="pr5557" n="287.7 (504.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7592">
            <lem wit="A">s’rp—Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sur—why</rdg>
          </app>
, what do you reckon

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
am? I’ve a good notion to take and—say, what do you mean by kissing me?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68940">He looked kind of humble, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68942">“I didn’t mean nothing, m’am. I didn’t mean no harm. I—I—thought you’d like it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68944">“Why, you born fool!” She took up the spinning-stick, and it looked like it was all she could do to keep from giving him a crack with it. “What made you think I’d like it?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68946">“Well, I don’t know. Only, they—they—told me you would.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68948">
“

          <hi rend="italic">They</hi>
told you I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5558"/>
would.

          <app from="pr5558" n="287.16 (505.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7593">
            <lem wit="A">would.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">would!</rdg>
          </app>
Whoever told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5559"/>
you,

          <app from="pr5559" n="287.16 (506.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7594">
            <lem wit="MS2">you,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
you

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
’s

          <hi rend="italic">another</hi>
lunatic. I never heard the beat of it. Who’s

          <hi rend="italic">they?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68976">“Why—everybody. They all said so, m’am.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68978">It was all she could do to hold in; and her eyes snapped, and her fingers worked like she wanted to scratch him; and she says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68980">“Who’s ‘everybody?’ Out with their names—or ther’ll be an idiot short.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68982">He got up and looked distressed, and fumbled his hat, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68985">
“I’m sorry, and I warn’t expecting it. They told me to. They all told me to. They all said kiss her;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5560"/>
and said,

          <app from="pr5560" n="287.25 (506.17–507.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7595">
            <lem wit="MS2">and said,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
and said

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
she’ll like it. They all said

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2701"/>
it—every one of them.

          <ptr target="#l12413" type="alt" xml:id="te2701"/>
But I’m sorry, m’am, and I won’t do it no more—I won’t, honest.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e68999">
“You won’t, won’t you? Well, I sh’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5561"/>
          <hi rend="italic">reckon</hi>
          <app from="pr5561" n="287.28 (507.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7596">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">reckon</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
jest

              <hi rend="italic">reckon</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
you won’t!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69013">“No’m, I’m honest about it; I won’t ever do it again. Till you ask me.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69015">
“Till I

          <hi rend="italic">ask</hi>
you! Well, I never see the beat of it in my born days! I lay you’ll be the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5562"/>
Methusalem-numskull

          <app from="pr5562" n="287.32 (507.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la7597">
            <lem wit="A">Methusalem-numskull</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
Methusalem-num-

              <lb/>
skull

            </rdg>
          </app>
of creation before ever

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
ask you—or the likes of you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69033">
“Well,” he says, “it does surprise me so. I can’t make it out, somehow. They said you would, and I thought you would. But—” He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5563"/>
stopped,

          <app from="pr5563" n="287.36 (507.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7598">
            <lem wit="MS2">stopped,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
stopped

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and looked around slow, like he wished he could run across a friendly eye,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5564"/>
somewheres

          <app from="pr5564" n="287.37 (508.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7599">
            <lem wit="MS2">somewheres</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">somewhere’s</rdg>
          </app>
; and fetched up on the old gentleman’s, and says, “Didn’t

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
think she’d like me to kiss her, sir?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69054">
          <pb n="288" xml:id="pb0288"/>
“Why, no, I—I—well, no, I b’lieve I didn’t.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69056">Then he looks on around, the same way, to me—and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69058">
“Tom, didn’t

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5565"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5565" n="288.3 (508.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7600">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5566"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2702"/>
Sally’d

          <ptr target="#l12414" type="alt" xml:id="te2702"/>
          <app from="pr5566" n="288.3 (508.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7601">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sally’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sally ’d</rdg>
          </app>
open out her arms and say, ‘Sid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5567"/>
Sawyer’—

          <app from="pr5567" n="288.4 (508.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7602">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sawyer’—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sawyer——’</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69089">“My land!” she says, breaking in and jumping for him, “you impudent young rascal, to fool a body so—” and was going to hug him, but he fended her off, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69091">“No, not till you’ve asked me, first.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69093">
So she didn’t lose no time, but asked him; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2703"/>
hugged him

          <ptr target="#l12415" type="alt" xml:id="te2703"/>
and kissed him, over and over again, and then turned him over to the old man, and he took what was left. And after they got a little quiet again, she says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69100">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5568"/>
Why

          <app from="pr5568" n="288.13 (509.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7603">
            <lem wit="MS2">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
dear me, I never see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5569"/>
such

          <app from="pr5569" n="288.13 (509.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7604">
            <lem wit="A">such</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sech</rdg>
          </app>
a surprise. We warn’t looking for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5570"/>
          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
          <app from="pr5570" n="288.14 (509.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7605">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you</rdg>
          </app>
, at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2704"/>
all,

          <ptr target="#l12416" type="alt" xml:id="te2704"/>
but only

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2705"/>
Tom.

          <ptr target="#l12417" type="alt" xml:id="te2705"/>
Sis never wrote to me about anybody coming but him.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69137">
“It’s because it warn’t

          <hi rend="italic">intended</hi>
for any of us to come but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2706"/>
Tom,

          <ptr target="#l12418" type="alt" xml:id="te2706"/>
” he says; “but I begged and begged, and at the last minute she let me come, too; so, coming down the river, me and Tom thought it would be a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5571"/>
first rate

          <app from="pr5571" n="288.19 (510.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7606">
            <lem wit="MS2">first rate</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">first-rate</rdg>
          </app>
surprise for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2707"/>
him

          <ptr target="#l12419" type="alt" xml:id="te2707"/>
to come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2708"/>
here to the house

          <ptr target="#l12420" type="alt" xml:id="te2708"/>
first, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2709"/>
for me to

          <ptr target="#l12421" type="alt" xml:id="te2709"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5572"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5572" n="288.20 (510.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7607">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2710"/>
tag along and

          <ptr target="#l12422" type="alt" xml:id="te2710"/>
drop in and let on to be a stranger. But it was a mistake,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5573"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5573" n="288.21 (510.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7608">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally. This

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2711"/>
ain’t

          <ptr target="#l12423" type="alt" xml:id="te2711"/>
no healthy place for a stranger to come.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69191">
“No—not impudent whelps, Sid. You ought to had your jaws boxed; I hain’t been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5574"/>
so put out since

          <app from="pr5574" n="288.24 (510.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7609">
            <lem wit="A">so put out since</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">put out so,</rdg>
          </app>
I don’t know

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2712"/>
when.

          <ptr target="#l12424" type="alt" xml:id="te2712"/>
But I don’t care, I don’t mind the terms—I’d be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5575"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2713"/>
willing

          <ptr target="#l12425" type="alt" xml:id="te2713"/>
          <app from="pr5575" n="288.25 (510.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7610">
            <lem wit="A">willing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">willin’</rdg>
          </app>
to stand a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5576"/>
thousand

          <app from="pr5576" n="288.25 (510.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7611">
            <lem wit="A">thousand</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thousan’</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5577"/>
such

          <app from="pr5577" n="288.26 (510.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7612">
            <lem wit="A">such</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sech</rdg>
          </app>
jokes to have you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2714"/>
here.

          <ptr target="#l12426" type="alt" xml:id="te2714"/>
Well, to think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5578"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2715"/>
of

          <ptr target="#l12427" type="alt" xml:id="te2715"/>
          <app from="pr5578" n="288.26 (510.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7613">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">o’</rdg>
          </app>
that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5579"/>
performance

          <app from="pr5579" n="288.26 (510.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7614">
            <lem wit="A">performance</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">p’formance</rdg>
          </app>
! I don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2716"/>
deny

          <ptr target="#l12428" type="alt" xml:id="te2716"/>
it, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5580"/>
was

          <app from="pr5580" n="288.27 (510.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7615">
            <lem wit="A">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5581"/>
most

          <app from="pr5581" n="288.27 (510.17)" type="e" xml:id="la7616">
            <lem wit="A">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">plumb</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5582"/>
putrefied

          <app from="pr5582" n="288.27 (510.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7617">
            <lem wit="MS2">putrefied</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">putrified</rdg>
          </app>
with astonishment when you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5583"/>
give me

          <app from="pr5583" n="288.28 (510.18)" type="e" xml:id="la7618">
            <lem wit="A">give me</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gimme</rdg>
          </app>
that smack.”

          <ptr target="#l12408" type="alt" xml:id="te2696"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69292">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2717"/>
We had

          <ptr target="#l12429" type="alt" xml:id="te2717"/>
dinner out in that broad open passage

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5584"/>
betwixt

          <app from="pr5584" n="288.29 (517.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7619">
            <lem wit="A">betwixt</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">between</rdg>
          </app>
the house and the kitchen; and there was things enough on that table for seven families—and all hot, too; none of your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5585"/>
flabby tough

          <app from="pr5585" n="288.31 (517.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7620">
            <lem wit="A">flabby tough</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blamed</rdg>
          </app>
meat that’s laid in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5586"/>
cupboard

          <app from="pr5586" n="288.32 (517.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7621">
            <lem wit="A">cupboard</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cubboard</rdg>
          </app>
in a damp cellar all night and tastes like a hunk of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5587"/>
old

          <app from="pr5587" n="288.33 (517.17–518.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7622">
            <lem wit="A">old</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">your old</rdg>
          </app>
cold

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5588"/>
cannibal

          <app from="pr5588" n="288.33 (518.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7623">
            <lem wit="A">cannibal</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">grandfather</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2718"/>
in the morning

          <ptr target="#l12430" type="alt" xml:id="te2718"/>
. Uncle Silas he asked a pretty long blessing over it, but it was worth it; and it didn’t cool it a bit,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2719"/>
neither, the way I’ve seen them kind of interruptions do, lots of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5589"/>
times.

          <ptr target="#l12431" type="alt" xml:id="te2719"/>
        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y28901">
          <graphic url="y28901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">a pretty long blessing</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69352">
There

          <app from="pr5589" n="288.36–37 (518.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la7624">
            <lem wit="A">times. [¶] There</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
times.

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7625">extra line space</note>
[¶] There

            </rdg>
          </app>
was a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2720"/>
considerable

          <ptr target="#l12432" type="alt" xml:id="te2720"/>
good deal of talk, all the afternoon, and me and Tom was on the lookout all the time, but it warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5590"/>
no

          <app from="pr5590" n="288.38 (518.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7626">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">any</rdg>
          </app>
use,

          <pb n="289" xml:id="pb0289"/>
they didn’t happen to say nothing about any runaway nigger, and we was afraid to try to work up to it. But at supper, at night,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2721"/>
one of the little boys

          <ptr target="#l12433" type="alt" xml:id="te2721"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69380">“Pa, mayn’t Tom and Sid and me go to the show?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69382">
“No,” says the old man, “I reckon there ain’t going to be any; and you couldn’t go if there was; because the runaway nigger told Burton and me all about that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2722"/>
scandalous

          <ptr target="#l12434" type="alt" xml:id="te2722"/>
show, and Burton said he would tell the people; so I reckon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5591"/>
they’ve

          <app from="pr5591" n="289.8 (519.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7627">
            <lem wit="A">they’ve</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them loafers has been</rdg>
          </app>
drove

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5592"/>
the owdacious loafers

          <app from="pr5592" n="289.8 (519.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7628">
            <lem wit="A">the owdacious loafers</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7629">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
out of town before this time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69406">
So there it was!—but

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
couldn’t help it. Tom and me was to sleep in the same room and bed; so, being tired, we bid

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5593"/>
good night

          <app from="pr5593" n="289.11 (519.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7630">
            <lem wit="MS2">good night</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">good-night</rdg>
          </app>
and went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2723"/>
up

          <ptr target="#l12435" type="alt" xml:id="te2723"/>
to bed, right after supper, and clumb out of the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2724"/>
window

          <ptr target="#l12436" type="alt" xml:id="te2724"/>
and down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5594"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr5594" n="289.13 (520.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7631">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
, and shoved for the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2725"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5595"/>
town

          <app from="pr5595" n="289.13 (520.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7632">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">village</rdg>
          </app>
; for I didn’t believe anybody was going to give the king and the duke a hint, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5596"/>
so

          <app from="pr5596" n="289.14 (520verso.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7633">
            <lem wit="MS2">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">so,</rdg>
          </app>
if I didn’t hurry up and give them one they’d get into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5597"/>
trouble,

          <app from="pr5597" n="289.15 (520verso.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7634">
            <lem wit="MS2">trouble,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
trouble

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
sure.

          <ptr target="#l12437" type="alt" xml:id="te2725"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69463">
On the road Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5598"/>
he

          <app from="pr5598" n="289.16 (520.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7635">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7636">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
told me all about how it was reckoned I was murdered, and how pap disappeared, pretty soon, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5599"/>
didn’t

          <app from="pr5599" n="289.17 (520.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7637">
            <lem wit="MS2">didn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">didn t</rdg>
          </app>
come back no more, and what a stir there was when Jim run away; and I told Tom all about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2726"/>
our

          <ptr target="#l12438" type="alt" xml:id="te2726"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5600"/>
Royal Nonesuch

          <app from="pr5600" n="289.19 (520.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7638">
            <lem wit="C">Royal Nonesuch</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Burning Shame</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
Royal None-

              <lb/>
such

            </rdg>
          </app>
rapscallions, and as much of the raft-voyage as I had time to; and as we struck into the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5601"/>
town

          <app from="pr5601" n="289.20 (521.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7639">
            <lem wit="A">town</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">village</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2727"/>
and up through the middle of it

          <ptr target="#l12439" type="alt" xml:id="te2727"/>
—it was as much as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5602"/>
half after

          <app from="pr5602" n="289.21 (521.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7640">
            <lem wit="MS2">half after</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half-after</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2728"/>
eight,

          <ptr target="#l12440" type="alt" xml:id="te2728"/>
          <pb n="290" xml:id="pb0290"/>
then—here comes a raging rush of people, with torches, and an awful whooping and yelling, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5603"/>
banging

          <app from="pr5603" n="290.2 (521.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7641">
            <lem wit="A">banging</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">banging of</rdg>
          </app>
tin pans and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5604"/>
blowing

          <app from="pr5604" n="290.2 (521.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la7642">
            <lem wit="A">blowing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blowing of</rdg>
          </app>
horns; and we jumped to one side to let them go by; and as they went by, I see they had the king and the duke astraddle of a rail—that is, I knowed it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
the king and the duke, though they was all over tar and feathers, and didn’t look like nothing in the world that was human—just looked like a couple of monstrous

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5605"/>
big

          <app from="pr5605" n="290.7 (522.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7643">
            <lem wit="A">big</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7644">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
soldier-plumes. Well, it made me sick to see it; and I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5606"/>
sorry

          <app from="pr5606" n="290.8 (522.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7645">
            <lem wit="A">sorry</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">so sorry</rdg>
          </app>
for them poor pitiful rascals,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5607"/>
it

          <app from="pr5607" n="290.9 (522.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7646">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that it</rdg>
          </app>
seemed like I couldn’t ever feel any hardness against them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2729"/>
any more

          <ptr target="#l12441" type="alt" xml:id="te2729"/>
in the world. It was a dreadful thing to see. Human beings

          <hi rend="italic">can</hi>
be awful cruel to one another.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69574">
We see we was too late—couldn’t do no good. We asked some stragglers about it, and they said everybody went to the show

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2730"/>
looking

          <ptr target="#l12442" type="alt" xml:id="te2730"/>
very innocent; and laid low and kept dark till the poor old king was in the middle of his cavortings on the stage; then somebody give a signal, and the house rose up and went for them.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69581">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2731"/>
So we

          <ptr target="#l12443" type="alt" xml:id="te2731"/>
poked along back home, and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5608"/>
warn’t

          <app from="pr5608" n="290.17 (523.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7647">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
feeling so brash as I was before, but kind of ornery, and humble, and to blame, somehow—though

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
hadn’t done nothing. But that’s always the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5609"/>
way:

          <app from="pr5609" n="290.19 (523.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7648">
            <lem wit="MS2">way:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">way;</rdg>
          </app>
it don’t make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5610"/>
no

          <app from="pr5610" n="290.20 (523.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7649">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a blame bit of</rdg>
          </app>
difference whether you do right or wrong, a person’s conscience ain’t got no sense, and just goes for him

          <hi rend="italic">anyway.</hi>
If I had a yaller dog that didn’t know no more than a person’s conscience

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5611"/>
does

          <app from="pr5611" n="290.23 (524.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7650">
            <lem wit="A">does</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7651">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
, I would pison him. It takes up more room than

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5612"/>
all the rest of

          <app from="pr5612" n="290.23 (524.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7652">
            <lem wit="A">all the rest of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7653">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a person’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5613"/>
insides

          <app from="pr5613" n="290.24 (524.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7654">
            <lem wit="A">insides</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">bowels</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5614"/>
yet

          <app from="pr5614" n="290.24 (524.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7655">
            <lem wit="A">yet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7656">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no good, nohow. Tom Sawyer he says the same.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69653">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y29001">
            <graphic url="y29001.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5615"/>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">traveling</hi>
              <app from="pr5615" n="290 caption" type="e" xml:id="la7657">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">traveling</hi>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7658">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">travelling</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">by rail</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0426">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXIV.</head>
        <pb n="291" xml:id="pb0291"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y29101">
          <graphic url="y29101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5616"/>
Chapter XXXIV.

            <app from="pr5616" n="291 title (524.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7659">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXIV.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7660">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">We</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2911">
          <graphic url="hf2911.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">vittles</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e69693">
stopped talking, and got to thinking.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5617"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr5617" n="291.2 (524.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7661">
            <lem wit="MS2">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
, Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69703">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5618"/>
Looky-here

          <app from="pr5618" n="291.3 (524.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7662">
            <lem wit="MS2">Looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Looky here</rdg>
          </app>
, Huck, what fools we are, to not think of it before!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5619"/>
I bet

          <app from="pr5619" n="291.5 (524.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7663">
            <lem wit="A">I bet</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’ll bet</rdg>
          </app>
I know where Jim is.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69721">“No! Where?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69723">
“In that hut

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5620"/>
down

          <app from="pr5620" n="291.8 (525.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7664">
            <lem wit="A">down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7665">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
by the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5621"/>
ash-hopper

          <app from="pr5621" n="291.9 (525.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la7666">
            <lem wit="C">ash-hopper</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
ash-

              <lb/>
hopper

            </rdg>
          </app>
. Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5622"/>
looky-here

          <app from="pr5622" n="291.9 (525.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7667">
            <lem wit="MS2">looky-here</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
. When we was at dinner, didn’t you see a nigger man go in there with some vittles?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69753">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69755">“What did you think the vittles was for?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69757">“For a dog.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69759">
“So’d I. Well, it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5623"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2732"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l12444" type="alt" xml:id="te2732"/>
          <app from="pr5623" n="291.17 (525.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7668">
            <lem wit="MS2">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
for a dog.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69772">“Why?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69774">“Because part of it was watermelon.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69776">
“So it was—I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2733"/>
noticed it.

          <ptr target="#l12445" type="alt" xml:id="te2733"/>
Well, it does beat all, that I never thought about a dog not eating

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2734"/>
watermelon.

          <ptr target="#l12446" type="alt" xml:id="te2734"/>
It shows how a body can see and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5624"/>
don’t

          <app from="pr5624" n="291.22 (526.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7669">
            <lem wit="A">don’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">not</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5625"/>
see,

          <app from="pr5625" n="291.22 (526.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7670">
            <lem wit="MS2">see,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
see

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at the same time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69802">
“Well, the nigger unlocked the padlock when he went in,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5626"/>
and he

          <app from="pr5626" n="291.23 (526.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7671">
            <lem wit="A">and he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and</rdg>
          </app>
locked it again when he

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5627"/>
come

          <app from="pr5627" n="291.24 (526.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7672">
            <lem wit="A">come</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">went</rdg>
          </app>
out.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2735"/>
He fetched uncle a key, about the time we got up from table—same key,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2736"/>
I bet.

          <ptr target="#l12448" type="alt" xml:id="te2736"/>
          <ptr target="#l12447" type="alt" xml:id="te2735"/>
Watermelon shows man, lock shows prisoner; and it ain’t likely there’s two prisoners on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2737"/>
such

          <ptr target="#l12449" type="alt" xml:id="te2737"/>
a little plantation, and where the people’s all so kind and good. Jim’s the prisoner. All right—I’m glad we found it out detective fashion; I wouldn’t give shucks for any other way. Now you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5628"/>
work your mind

          <app from="pr5628" n="291.30 (527.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7673">
            <lem wit="A">work your mind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sail in</rdg>
          </app>
and study out a plan to steal Jim, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5629"/>
I will

          <app from="pr5629" n="291.30 (527.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7674">
            <lem wit="A">I will</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’ll</rdg>
          </app>
study out one,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2738"/>
too;

          <ptr target="#l12450" type="alt" xml:id="te2738"/>
and we’ll take the one we like the best.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69853">
What a head for just a boy to have! If I had Tom Sawyer’s head, I wouldn’t trade it off to be a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2739"/>
duke, nor

          <ptr target="#l12451" type="alt" xml:id="te2739"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2740"/>
mate

          <ptr target="#l12452" type="alt" xml:id="te2740"/>
of a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2741"/>
steamboat, nor

          <pb n="292" xml:id="pb0292"/>
clown in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5630"/>
circus

          <app from="pr5630" n="292.1 (527.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7675">
            <lem wit="A">circus</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cicus</rdg>
          </app>
, nor nothing I can think of.

          <ptr target="#l12453" type="alt" xml:id="te2741"/>
I went to thinking out a plan, but only just to be doing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5631"/>
something:

          <app from="pr5631" n="292.2 (527.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7676">
            <lem wit="MS2">something:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">something;</rdg>
          </app>
I knowed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2742"/>
very

          <ptr target="#l12454" type="alt" xml:id="te2742"/>
well where the right plan

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5632"/>
was going to

          <app from="pr5632" n="292.3 (528.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7677">
            <lem wit="A">was going to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">would</rdg>
          </app>
come from. Pretty soon, Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69896">“Ready?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69898">“Yes,” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69900">
“All

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5633"/>
right,

          <app from="pr5633" n="292.7 (528.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7678">
            <lem wit="MS2">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2743"/>
—bring it out.”

          <ptr target="#l12455" type="alt" xml:id="te2743"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69912">
“My plan is this,” I says. “We can easy find out if it’s Jim in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2744"/>
there.

          <ptr target="#l12456" type="alt" xml:id="te2744"/>
Then get up my canoe

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5634"/>
tomorrow

          <app from="pr5634" n="292.9 (528.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7679">
            <lem wit="MS2">tomorrow</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">to-morrow</rdg>
          </app>
night, and fetch my raft over from the island. Then the first dark night that comes, steal the key out of the old man’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2745"/>
britches

          <ptr target="#l12457" type="alt" xml:id="te2745"/>
, after he goes to bed, and shove off down the river on the raft, with Jim, hiding

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5635"/>
daytimes

          <app from="pr5635" n="292.12 (529.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7680">
            <lem wit="MS2">daytimes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
day-

              <lb/>
times

            </rdg>
          </app>
and running nights,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5636"/>
the way

          <app from="pr5636" n="292.12–13 (529.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7681">
            <lem wit="A">the way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">just as</rdg>
          </app>
me and Jim used to do before. Wouldn’t that plan work?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69949">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Work?</hi>
Why cert’nly, it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2746"/>
would

          <ptr target="#l12458" type="alt" xml:id="te2746"/>
work,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2747"/>
like

          <ptr target="#l12459" type="alt" xml:id="te2747"/>
rats

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5637"/>
a-fighting

          <app from="pr5637" n="292.14 (529.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7682">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-fighting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a fighting</rdg>
          </app>
. But it’s too blame’ simple; there ain’t nothing

          <hi rend="italic">to</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2748"/>
it.

          <ptr target="#l12460" type="alt" xml:id="te2748"/>
What’s the good of a plan that ain’t no more trouble than that? It’s as mild as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5638"/>
goose-milk

          <app from="pr5638" n="292.16 (530.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7683">
            <lem wit="A">goose-milk</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Sunday school</rdg>
          </app>
. Why, Huck, it wouldn’t make no more talk than breaking into a soap factory.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69986">
I never said nothing, because I warn’t expecting nothing different; but I knowed mighty well that whenever he got

          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
plan ready it wouldn’t have none of them objections to it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e69992">
And it didn’t. He told me what it was, and I see in a minute it was worth fifteen of mine, for style, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2749"/>
would

          <ptr target="#l12461" type="alt" xml:id="te2749"/>
make Jim just as free a man as mine would, and maybe get us all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5639"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2750"/>
killed,

          <ptr target="#l12462" type="alt" xml:id="te2750"/>
          <app from="pr5639" n="292.24 (531.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7684">
            <lem wit="MS2">killed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
killed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
besides. So I was satisfied, and said we would waltz in on it. I needn’t tell what it was, here, because I knowed it wouldn’t stay the way it was. I knowed he would be changing it around, every which

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5640"/>
way

          <app from="pr5640" n="292.27 (531.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7685">
            <lem wit="A">way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">way, and picturesquing it up</rdg>
          </app>
, as we went along, and heaving in new bullinesses wherever he got a chance. And that is what he done.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70017">
Well, one thing was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5641"/>
dead

          <app from="pr5641" n="292.30 (531.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7686">
            <lem wit="A">dead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">perfectly dead</rdg>
          </app>
sure; and that was, that Tom Sawyer was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2751"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l12463" type="alt" xml:id="te2751"/>
earnest, and was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5642"/>
actuly

          <app from="pr5642" n="292.31 (532.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7687">
            <lem wit="A">actuly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">actually</rdg>
          </app>
going to help steal that nigger out of slavery.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2752"/>
That was

          <ptr target="#l12464" type="alt" xml:id="te2752"/>
the thing that was too many for me. Here was a boy that was respectable, and well

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2753"/>
brung

          <ptr target="#l12465" type="alt" xml:id="te2753"/>
up; and had a character to lose; and folks at home that had characters; and he was bright and not

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5643"/>
leatherheaded

          <app from="pr5643" n="292.35 (532.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7688">
            <lem wit="MS2">leatherheaded</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">leather-headed</rdg>
          </app>
; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5644"/>
knowing,

          <app from="pr5644" n="292.35 (532.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7689">
            <lem wit="MS2">knowing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
knowing

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and not ignorant;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2754"/>
and not mean, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5645"/>
kind

          <app from="pr5645" n="292.36 (532.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7690">
            <lem wit="A">kind</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kind hearted</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <ptr target="#l12466" type="alt" xml:id="te2754"/>
and yet here he was, without any more pride, or rightness, or feeling, than to stoop to this

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2755"/>
business

          <ptr target="#l12467" type="alt" xml:id="te2755"/>
, and make himself a shame, and his family a shame, before everybody. I

          <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
understand it,

          <pb n="293" xml:id="pb0293"/>
no way at all. It was outrageous, and I knowed I ought to just up and tell him so; and so be his true friend, and let him quit the thing right where he was, and save himself. And I

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
start to tell him; but he shut

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2756"/>
me up,

          <ptr target="#l12468" type="alt" xml:id="te2756"/>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70093">
“Don’t you reckon I know what I’m about? Don’t I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5646"/>
generly

          <app from="pr5646" n="293.5 (533.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7691">
            <lem wit="A">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">generally</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
know what I’m about?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70104">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2757"/>
“Yes.”

          <ptr target="#l12469" type="alt" xml:id="te2757"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70108">
“Didn’t I

          <hi rend="italic">say</hi>
I was going to help steal the nigger?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70113">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70115">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5647"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Well,</hi>
          <app from="pr5647" n="293.10 (534.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7692">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Well

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70128">
That’s all he said, and that’s all I said. It warn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2758"/>
no

          <ptr target="#l12470" type="alt" xml:id="te2758"/>
use to say any more; because when he said he’d do a thing, he always done it. But

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
couldn’t make out how he was willing to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2759"/>
go into this thing;

          <ptr target="#l12471" type="alt" xml:id="te2759"/>
so I just let it go, and never bothered no more about it. If he was bound to have it so,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
couldn’t help

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5648"/>
it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70147">
When

          <app from="pr5648" n="293.15–16 (534.18–535.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7693">
            <lem wit="A">it. [¶] When</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
it.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7694">chapter sink</note>
[¶] When

            </rdg>
          </app>
we got home, the house was all dark and still; so we went on down to the hut by the ash-hopper, for to examine it. We went through the yard, so as to see what the hounds would do. They knowed us, and didn’t make no more noise than

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2760"/>
country dogs is

          <ptr target="#l12472" type="alt" xml:id="te2760"/>
always doing when anything comes by in the night. When we got to the cabin, we took a look at the front and the two sides; and on the side I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2761"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l12473" type="alt" xml:id="te2761"/>
acquainted with—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5649"/>
which was

          <app from="pr5649" n="293.22 (536.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7695">
            <lem wit="A">which was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7696">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the north side—we found a square window-hole, up tolerable high, with just one stout board nailed across it. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70177">“Here’s the ticket. This hole’s big enough for Jim to get through, if we wrench off the board.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70179">Tom says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70182">
“It’s as simple as tit-tat-toe, three-in-a-row, and as easy as playing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5650"/>
hookey

          <app from="pr5650" n="293.29 (536.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7697">
            <lem wit="MS2">hookey</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hooky</rdg>
          </app>
. I should

          <hi rend="italic">hope</hi>
we can find a way that’s a little more complicated

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2762"/>
than

          <ptr target="#l12474" type="alt" xml:id="te2762"/>
          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
, Huck Finn.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70201">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5651"/>
Well,

          <app from="pr5651" n="293.31 (537.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7698">
            <lem wit="MS2">Well,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Well

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
then,” I says, “how’ll it do to saw him out, the way I done before I was murdered, that time?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70211">
“That’s more

          <hi rend="italic">like,</hi>
” he says. “It’s real mysterious, and troublesome, and good,” he says; “but I bet we can find a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2763"/>
way

          <ptr target="#l12475" type="alt" xml:id="te2763"/>
that’s twice as long. There ain’t no hurry; le’s keep on looking around.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70225">
Betwixt the hut and the fence, on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5652"/>
backside

          <app from="pr5652" n="293.36 (537.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7699">
            <lem wit="MS2">backside</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">back side</rdg>
          </app>
, was a lean-to, that joined the hut at the eaves, and was made out of plank. It was as long as the hut, but narrow—only about six foot wide. The door

          <pb n="294" xml:id="pb0294"/>
to it was at the south end, and was padlocked. Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5653"/>
he

          <app from="pr5653" n="294.1 (538.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7700">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7701">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
went to the soap kettle, and searched around and fetched back the iron thing they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5654"/>
lift

          <app from="pr5654" n="294.3 (538.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7702">
            <lem wit="A">lift</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">lift off</rdg>
          </app>
the lid with;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2764"/>
so he took it

          <ptr target="#l12476" type="alt" xml:id="te2764"/>
and prized out one of the staples.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2765"/>
The chain

          <ptr target="#l12477" type="alt" xml:id="te2765"/>
fell down, and we opened the door and went in, and shut

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2766"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5655"/>
it

          <app from="pr5655" n="294.5 (538.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7703">
            <lem wit="MS2">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it,</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12478" type="alt" xml:id="te2766"/>
and struck a match, and see the shed was only built against the cabin and hadn’t no connection with it; and there warn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2767"/>
no floor

          <ptr target="#l12479" type="alt" xml:id="te2767"/>
to the shed, nor nothing in it but some old rusty played-out hoes, and spades, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5656"/>
picks

          <app from="pr5656" n="294.8 (539.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7704">
            <lem wit="MS2">picks</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">picks,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2768"/>
a crippled

          <ptr target="#l12480" type="alt" xml:id="te2768"/>
plow. The match went out, and so did we, and shoved in the staple again, and the door was locked as good as ever. Tom was joyful. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70289">
“Now we’re all right.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2769"/>
We’ll

          <ptr target="#l12481" type="alt" xml:id="te2769"/>
          <hi rend="italic">dig</hi>
him out. It’ll take about a week!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y29401">
          <graphic url="y29401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">a simple job</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70297">
Then we started for the house, and I went in the back door—you only

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2770"/>
have

          <ptr target="#l12482" type="alt" xml:id="te2770"/>
to pull a buckskin latch-string, they don’t fasten the doors—but that warn’t romantical enough for Tom Sawyer: no way

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2771"/>
would

          <ptr target="#l12483" type="alt" xml:id="te2771"/>
do him but he must climb

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5657"/>
up

          <app from="pr5657" n="294.15 (540.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7705">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7706">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5658"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr5658" n="294.15 (540.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7707">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
. But after he got up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5659"/>
half way

          <app from="pr5659" n="294.16 (540.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7708">
            <lem wit="MS2">half way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half-way</rdg>
          </app>
about three times, and missed fire and fell every

          <pb n="295" xml:id="pb0295"/>
time, and the last time most busted his brains out, he thought he’d got to give it up; but after he was rested, he allowed he would give her one more turn for luck, and this time he made

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2772"/>
the trip.

          <ptr target="#l12484" type="alt" xml:id="te2772"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70337">
In the morning we was up at break of day, and down to the nigger cabins to pet the dogs and make friends with the nigger that fed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2773"/>
Jim—if it

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
Jim that was being fed.

          <ptr target="#l12485" type="alt" xml:id="te2773"/>
The niggers was just getting through breakfast and starting for the fields; and Jim’s nigger was piling up a tin pan with bread and meat and things; and whilst the others was leaving, the key come from the house.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70346">
This nigger had a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5660"/>
good-natured

          <app from="pr5660" n="295.10 (541.17–542.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7709">
            <lem wit="C">good-natured</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
good-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
natured

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">good-natured,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5661"/>
chuckleheaded

          <app from="pr5661" n="295.10 (542.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7710">
            <lem wit="MS2">chuckleheaded</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">chuckle-headed</rdg>
          </app>
face, and his wool was all tied up in little bunches with thread. That was to keep witches off. He said the witches was pestering him awful, these nights, and making him see all kinds of strange things, and hear all kinds of strange words and noises, and he didn’t believe he was ever witched so long, before, in his life. He got so worked up, and got to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5662"/>
running

          <app from="pr5662" n="295.16 (542.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7711">
            <lem wit="MS2">running</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">runinng</rdg>
          </app>
on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5663"/>
so,

          <app from="pr5663" n="295.16 (542.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7712">
            <lem wit="MS2">so,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
so

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
about his troubles,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5664"/>
he

          <app from="pr5664" n="295.16 (542.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7713">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that he</rdg>
          </app>
forgot all about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2774"/>
what he’d been agoing to do.

          <ptr target="#l12486" type="alt" xml:id="te2774"/>
So Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70396">“What’s the vittles for? Going to feed the dogs?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70398">
The nigger

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5665"/>
kind of

          <app from="pr5665" n="295.19 (543.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7714">
            <lem wit="A">kind of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kinder</rdg>
          </app>
smiled around graduly over his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5666"/>
face

          <app from="pr5666" n="295.19 (543.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7715">
            <lem wit="MS2">face</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">face,</rdg>
          </app>
like when you heave a brickbat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5667"/>
in

          <app from="pr5667" n="295.20 (543.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7716">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">into</rdg>
          </app>
a mud puddle, and he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70426">
“Yes,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5668"/>
mars

          <app from="pr5668" n="295.21 (543.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7717">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Sid,

          <hi rend="italic">a</hi>
dog. Cur’us dog, too. Does you want to go en look at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5669"/>
’im

          <app from="pr5669" n="295.22 (543.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7718">
            <lem wit="A">’im</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">him</rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70447">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70449">
I hunched Tom,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2775"/>
and whispers:

          <ptr target="#l12487" type="alt" xml:id="te2775"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70454">
“You going,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2776"/>
right

          <ptr target="#l12488" type="alt" xml:id="te2776"/>
here in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5670"/>
daybreak

          <app from="pr5670" n="295.25 (544.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7719">
            <lem wit="MS2">daybreak</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-break</rdg>
          </app>
?

          <hi rend="italic">That</hi>
warn’t the plan.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70471">
“No, it warn’t—but it’s the plan

          <hi rend="italic">now.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70476">
So, drat him, we went along, but I didn’t like it much. When we got in, we couldn’t hardly see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2777"/>
anything,

          <ptr target="#l12489" type="alt" xml:id="te2777"/>
it was so dark; but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2778"/>
Jim was there, sure enough, and

          <ptr target="#l12490" type="alt" xml:id="te2778"/>
could see us; and he sings

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2779"/>
out:

          <ptr target="#l12491" type="alt" xml:id="te2779"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70490">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5671"/>
Why

          <app from="pr5671" n="295.30 (544.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7720">
            <lem wit="MS2">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">Huck!</hi>
En good

          <hi rend="italic">lan’!</hi>
ain’ dat Misto Tom?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70505">
I just knowed how it would be; I just expected it.

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
didn’t know nothing to do; and if I had, I couldn’t a done it; because that nigger busted in and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70510">
“Why, de gracious sakes!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2780"/>
do

          <ptr target="#l12492" type="alt" xml:id="te2780"/>
he know you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5672"/>
genlmen

          <app from="pr5672" n="295.34 (545.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7721">
            <lem wit="A">genlmen</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
genl-

              <lb/>
men

            </rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70526">
We could see pretty well, now. Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5673"/>
he

          <app from="pr5673" n="295.35 (545.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7722">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7723">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
looked at the nigger, steady and kind of wondering, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70537">
“Does

          <hi rend="italic">who</hi>
know us?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70543">“Why, dish-yer runaway nigger.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70545">
          <pb n="296" xml:id="pb0296"/>
“I don’t reckon he does; but what put that into your head?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70547">
“What

          <hi rend="italic">put</hi>
it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5674"/>
dar

          <app from="pr5674" n="296.2 (546.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7724">
            <lem wit="A">dar</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dah</rdg>
          </app>
? Didn’ he jis’ dis minute sing out like he knowed you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70560">
Tom

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2781"/>
says, in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5675"/>
puzzled-up

          <app from="pr5675" n="296.4 (546.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7725">
            <lem wit="A">puzzled-up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">puzzled</rdg>
          </app>
kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5676"/>
way

          <app from="pr5676" n="296.4 (546.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7726">
            <lem wit="A">way</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a way</rdg>
          </app>
:

          <ptr target="#l12493" type="alt" xml:id="te2781"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70582">
“Well, that’s mighty curious.

          <hi rend="italic">Who</hi>
sung out?

          <hi rend="italic">When</hi>
did he sing out?

          <hi rend="italic">What</hi>
did he sing out?” And turns to me, perfectly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5677"/>
ca’m

          <app from="pr5677" n="296.6 (546.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7727">
            <lem wit="C">ca’m</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">c’am</rdg>
          </app>
, and says, “Did

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
hear anybody sing out?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70605">Of course there warn’t nothing to be said but the one thing; so I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70607">
“No;

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
ain’t heard nobody say nothing.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70612">Then he turns to Jim, and looks him over like he never see him before; and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70614">“Did you sing out?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70616">
“No, sah,” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5678"/>
Jim,

          <app from="pr5678" n="296.14 (547.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7728">
            <lem wit="MS2">Jim,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jim;</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
hain’t said nothing, sah.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70629">“Not a word?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70632">
“No,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2782"/>
sah

          <ptr target="#l12494" type="alt" xml:id="te2782"/>
, I hain’t said a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5679"/>
word

          <app from="pr5679" n="296.16 (547.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7729">
            <lem wit="A">word</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">single word</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70646">“Did you ever see us before?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70648">
“No, sah; not as

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
knows on.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70653">
So Tom turns to the nigger, which was looking wild and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5680"/>
distressed

          <app from="pr5680" n="296.19–20 (548.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7730">
            <lem wit="A">distressed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">distressed, now</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2783"/>
says, kind

          <ptr target="#l12495" type="alt" xml:id="te2783"/>
of severe:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70667">
“What do you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5681"/>
reckon’s

          <app from="pr5681" n="296.22 (548.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7731">
            <lem wit="A">reckon’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon is</rdg>
          </app>
the matter with you, anyway? What made you think somebody sung out?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70677">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5682"/>
O

          <app from="pr5682" n="296.26 (548.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7732">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, it’s de dad-blame’ witches, sah,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2784"/>
en

          <ptr target="#l12496" type="alt" xml:id="te2784"/>
I wisht I was dead, I do. Dey’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2785"/>
awluz

          <ptr target="#l12497" type="alt" xml:id="te2785"/>
at it, sah, en dey do mos’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2786"/>
kill

          <ptr target="#l12498" type="alt" xml:id="te2786"/>
me, dey sk’yers me so. Please to don’t tell nobody ’bout

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5683"/>
it,

          <app from="pr5683" n="296.31 (548.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7733">
            <lem wit="MS2">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2787"/>
sah

          <ptr target="#l12499" type="alt" xml:id="te2787"/>
, er ole

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5684"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2788"/>
mars

          <ptr target="#l12500" type="alt" xml:id="te2788"/>
          <app from="pr5684" n="296.32 (548.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7734">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Silas he’ll scole me; ’kase he say dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5685"/>
          <hi rend="italic">ain’</hi>
          <app from="pr5685" n="296.33 (548.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7735">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">ain</hi>
’

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
no witches. I jis’ wish to goodness he was heah now—

          <hi rend="italic">den</hi>
what would he say! I jis’ bet he couldn’ fine no way to git aroun’ it

          <hi rend="italic">dis</hi>
time. But it’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2789"/>
awluz

          <ptr target="#l12501" type="alt" xml:id="te2789"/>
jis’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5686"/>
so:

          <app from="pr5686" n="296.37 (549.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7736">
            <lem wit="MS2">so:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">so;</rdg>
          </app>
people dat’s

          <hi rend="italic">sot</hi>
, stays sot; dey won’t look into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5687"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2790"/>
noth’n

          <ptr target="#l12502" type="alt" xml:id="te2790"/>
          <app from="pr5687" n="296.38 (549.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7737">
            <lem wit="MS2">noth’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">nothn’</rdg>
          </app>
en fine it out

          <pb n="297" xml:id="pb0297"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5688"/>
f’r

          <app from="pr5688" n="297.1 (549.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7738">
            <lem wit="A">f’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
deyselves, en when

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
fine it out en tell um ’bout it, dey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5689"/>
doan

          <app from="pr5689" n="297.1 (549.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7739">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2791"/>
b’lieve

          <ptr target="#l12503" type="alt" xml:id="te2791"/>
you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70790">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y29601">
            <graphic url="y29601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">witches</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70796">
Tom give him a dime, and said we wouldn’t tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5690"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr5690" n="297.3 (549.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la7740">
            <lem wit="C">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
any-

              <lb/>
body

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
no-

              <lb/>
body

            </rdg>
          </app>
; and told him to buy some more thread to tie up his wool with; and then looks at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5691"/>
Jim

          <app from="pr5691" n="297.5 (549.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7741">
            <lem wit="MS2">Jim</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Jim,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70820">
“I wonder if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5692"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5692" n="297.6 (549.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la7742">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas is going to hang this nigger. If I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2792"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l12504" type="alt" xml:id="te2792"/>
to catch a nigger that was ungrateful enough to run away,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
wouldn’t give him up, I’d hang him.”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2793"/>
And

          <ptr target="#l12505" type="alt" xml:id="te2793"/>
whilst the nigger stepped to the door to look at the dime and bite it to see if it was good, he whispers to Jim, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70842">
“Don’t ever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2794"/>
let on

          <ptr target="#l12506" type="alt" xml:id="te2794"/>
to know us. And if you hear any digging going

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5693"/>
on,

          <app from="pr5693" n="297.12 (550.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7743">
            <lem wit="MS2">on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
on

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2795"/>
nights

          <ptr target="#l12507" type="alt" xml:id="te2795"/>
, it’s us: we’re going to set you free.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70859">
Jim only had time to grab us by the hand and squeeze it, then the nigger come back, and we said we’d come again some time if the nigger wanted us to; and he said he would,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5694"/>
more particular

          <app from="pr5694" n="297.15 (551.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7744">
            <lem wit="A">more particular</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">speshally</rdg>
          </app>
if it was dark, because the witches went for him mostly in the dark, and it was good to have folks

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5695"/>
around,

          <app from="pr5695" n="297.17 (551.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7745">
            <lem wit="MS2">around,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
around

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2796"/>
then.

          <ptr target="#l12508" type="alt" xml:id="te2796"/>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0430">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXV.</head>
        <pb n="298" xml:id="pb0298"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y29801">
          <graphic url="y29801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5696"/>
Chapter XXXV.

            <app from="pr5696" n="298 title (551.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7746">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXV.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7747">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">It</ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf2981">
          <graphic url="hf2981.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">getting wood</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e70900">
would be

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2797"/>
most an

          <ptr target="#l12509" type="alt" xml:id="te2797"/>
hour, yet, till breakfast, so we left, and struck down into the woods; because Tom said we got to have

          <hi rend="italic">some</hi>
light to see how to dig by, and a lantern

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5697"/>
makes

          <app from="pr5697" n="298.6 (551.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7748">
            <lem wit="A">makes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">would make</rdg>
          </app>
too much, and might get us into trouble; what we must have was a lot of them rotten chunks

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5698"/>
that’s

          <app from="pr5698" n="298.9 (552.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7749">
            <lem wit="A">that’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that is</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2798"/>
called

          <ptr target="#l12510" type="alt" xml:id="te2798"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5699"/>
fox-fire,

          <app from="pr5699" n="298.9–10 (552.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7750">
            <lem wit="MS2">fox-fire,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">fox-fire</rdg>
          </app>
and just makes a soft kind of a glow when you lay them in a dark place. We fetched an armful and hid it in the weeds,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2799"/>
and set down to rest, and Tom says

          <ptr target="#l12511" type="alt" xml:id="te2799"/>
, kind of dissatisfied:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e70941">
“Blame it, this whole

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2800"/>
thing

          <ptr target="#l12512" type="alt" xml:id="te2800"/>
is

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2801"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l12513" type="alt" xml:id="te2801"/>
as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2802"/>
easy and awkard as

          <ptr target="#l12514" type="alt" xml:id="te2802"/>
it can be.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2803"/>
And so it

          <ptr target="#l12515" type="alt" xml:id="te2803"/>
makes it so

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2804"/>
rotten

          <ptr target="#l12516" type="alt" xml:id="te2804"/>
difficult to get up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2805"/>
a difficult

          <ptr target="#l12517" type="alt" xml:id="te2805"/>
plan. There ain’t no watchman to be drugged—now there

          <hi rend="italic">ought</hi>
to be a watchman. There ain’t even a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5700"/>
dog,

          <app from="pr5700" n="298.21 (552.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7751">
            <lem wit="MS2">dog,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
dog

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to give a sleeping-mixture to. And there’s Jim chained by one leg, with a ten-foot chain, to the leg of his bed: why, all you got to do is to lift up the bedstead and slip off the chain. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5701"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5701" n="298.23 (553.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7752">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5702"/>
he

          <app from="pr5702" n="298.23 (553.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7753">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7754">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
trusts everybody; sends the key

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5703"/>
to the

          <app from="pr5703" n="298.24 (553.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7755">
            <lem wit="A">to the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to that</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5704"/>
punkinheaded

          <app from="pr5704" n="298.24 (553.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7756">
            <lem wit="MS2">punkinheaded</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
punkin-

              <lb/>
headed

            </rdg>
          </app>
nigger, and don’t send

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5705"/>
nobody

          <app from="pr5705" n="298.25 (553.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7757">
            <lem wit="A">nobody</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anybody</rdg>
          </app>
to watch

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2806"/>
the nigger.

          <ptr target="#l12518" type="alt" xml:id="te2806"/>
Jim could a got out of that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5706"/>
window-hole,

          <app from="pr5706" n="298.26 (553.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7758">
            <lem wit="MS2">window-hole,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">window hole</rdg>
          </app>
before this, only there wouldn’t be no use

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5707"/>
trying

          <app from="pr5707" n="298.26 (553.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7759">
            <lem wit="A">trying</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in trying</rdg>
          </app>
to travel with a ten-foot chain on his leg. Why, drat it, Huck,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5708"/>
it’s

          <app from="pr5708" n="298.27 (554.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7760">
            <lem wit="A">it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">its</rdg>
          </app>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2807"/>
stupidest arrangement

          <ptr target="#l12519" type="alt" xml:id="te2807"/>
I ever

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5709"/>
see.

          <app from="pr5709" n="298.28 (554.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7761">
            <lem wit="A">see.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">see:</rdg>
          </app>
You got to invent

          <hi rend="italic">all</hi>
the difficulties. Well, we can’t help it, we got to do the best we can with the materials we’ve got. Anyhow, there’s one thing—there’s more honor in getting him out through a lot of difficulties and dangers, where there warn’t one of them furnished to you by the people who

          <pb n="299" xml:id="pb0299"/>
it was their duty to furnish them, and you had to contrive them all out of your own head. Now look at just that one thing of the lantern. When you come

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2808"/>
down

          <ptr target="#l12520" type="alt" xml:id="te2808"/>
to the cold facts, we simply got to

          <hi rend="italic">let on</hi>
that a lantern’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5710"/>
resky

          <app from="pr5710" n="299.4 (555.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7762">
            <lem wit="A">resky</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">risky</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2809"/>
Why,

          <ptr target="#l12521" type="alt" xml:id="te2809"/>
we could work with a torchlight procession if we wanted

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2810"/>
to,

          <ptr target="#l12522" type="alt" xml:id="te2810"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
believe.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5711"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2811"/>
Now

          <ptr target="#l12523" type="alt" xml:id="te2811"/>
          <app from="pr5711" n="299.5 (555.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7763">
            <lem wit="MS2">Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Now,</rdg>
          </app>
whilst I think of it, we got to hunt up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2812"/>
something to make a saw out of, the first

          <ptr target="#l12524" type="alt" xml:id="te2812"/>
chance we get.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71113">“What do we want of a saw?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71115">
“What do we

          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
of it? Hain’t we got to saw the leg of Jim’s bed off, so as to get the chain loose?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71120">
“Why, you just said a body could lift up the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5712"/>
bedstead

          <app from="pr5712" n="299.10 (556.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7764">
            <lem wit="A">bedstead</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
bed-

              <lb/>
stead

            </rdg>
          </app>
and slip the chain off.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71132">
“Well, if that ain’t just

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2813"/>
like

          <ptr target="#l12525" type="alt" xml:id="te2813"/>
you, Huck

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2814"/>
Finn.

          <ptr target="#l12526" type="alt" xml:id="te2814"/>
You

          <hi rend="italic">can</hi>
get up the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2815"/>
infant-schooliest

          <ptr target="#l12527" type="alt" xml:id="te2815"/>
ways of going at a thing. Why, hain’t you ever read any books at all?—

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0012"/>
Baron Trenck, nor Casanova, nor Benvenuto Chelleeny,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2816"/>
nor Henri

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5713"/>
IV

          <app from="pr5713" n="299.15 (556.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7765">
            <lem wit="MS2">IV</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">IV.</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0236" type="an" xml:id="uu0012"/>
,

          <ptr target="#l12528" type="alt" xml:id="te2816"/>
nor none of them heroes? Whoever heard of getting a prisoner loose in such an old-maidy way as that? No; the way all the best authorities does, is to saw the bed-leg in two, and leave it just so, and swallow the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5714"/>
sawdust

          <app from="pr5714" n="299.18 (557.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7766">
            <lem wit="A">sawdust</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
saw-

              <lb/>
dust

            </rdg>
          </app>
, so it can’t be found, and put some dirt and grease around the sawed place so the very keenest seneskal can’t see no sign of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5715"/>
its

          <app from="pr5715" n="299.20 (557.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7767">
            <lem wit="C">its</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">it’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2817"/>
being

          <ptr target="#l12529" type="alt" xml:id="te2817"/>
sawed, and thinks

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5716"/>
the

          <app from="pr5716" n="299.20 (557.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7768">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that that</rdg>
          </app>
bed-leg is perfectly sound. Then, the night you’re ready, fetch the leg a kick,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2818"/>
down

          <ptr target="#l12530" type="alt" xml:id="te2818"/>
she goes; slip off your chain, and there you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5717"/>
are. Nothing

          <app from="pr5717" n="299.22–23 (557.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7769">
            <lem wit="A">are. Nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">are: nothing</rdg>
          </app>
to do but hitch your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5718"/>
rope-ladder

          <app from="pr5718" n="299.24 (558.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la7770">
            <lem wit="A">rope-ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
rope-

              <lb/>
ladder

            </rdg>
          </app>
to the battlements, shin down it,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0013"/>
break your leg in the moat—because a rope-ladder is nineteen foot too short

          <ptr target="#as0237" type="an" xml:id="uu0013"/>
, you know—and there’s your horses and your trusty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5719"/>
vassles

          <app from="pr5719" n="299.26 (558.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7771">
            <lem wit="A">vassles</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">friends</rdg>
          </app>
, and they scoop you up and fling you across a saddle and away you go, to your native

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0014"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5720"/>
Langudoc

          <app from="pr5720" n="299.27 (558.10)" type="e" xml:id="la7772">
            <lem wit="A">Langudoc</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Languedoc</rdg>
          </app>
, or Navarre

          <ptr target="#as0238" type="an" xml:id="uu0014"/>
, or wherever it is. It’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5721"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2819"/>
gaudy

          <ptr target="#l12531" type="alt" xml:id="te2819"/>
          <app from="pr5721" n="299.28 (558.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7773">
            <lem wit="A">gaudy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gorgeous</rdg>
          </app>
, Huck. I wish there was a moat to this cabin. If we get time, the night of the escape, we’ll dig one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71254">I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71257">“What do we want of a moat, when we’re going to snake him out from under the cabin?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71259">
But he never heard me. He had forgot me and everything else. He had his chin in his hand, thinking. Pretty soon, he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2820"/>
sighs,

          <ptr target="#l12532" type="alt" xml:id="te2820"/>
and shakes his head; then sighs again, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71265">“No, it wouldn’t do—there ain’t necessity enough for it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71267">“For what?” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71269">“Why, to saw Jim’s leg off,” he says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71271">
          <pb n="300" xml:id="pb0300"/>
“Good land!” I says, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5722"/>
Why,

          <app from="pr5722" n="300.1 (560.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7774">
            <lem wit="MS2">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">why</rdg>
          </app>
there ain’t

          <hi rend="italic">no</hi>
necessity for it. And what would you want to saw his leg

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5723"/>
off,

          <app from="pr5723" n="300.2 (560.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7775">
            <lem wit="MS2">off,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
off

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for, anyway?”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y30001">
          <graphic url="y30001.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">one of the best authorities</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71298">
“Well, some of the best authorities has done it. They couldn’t get the chain off, so they just cut their hand off, and shoved.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2821"/>
And a leg would be better still.

          <ptr target="#l12533" type="alt" xml:id="te2821"/>
But we got to let that go. There ain’t necessity enough in this case; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2822"/>
besides,

          <ptr target="#l12534" type="alt" xml:id="te2822"/>
Jim’s a nigger and wouldn’t understand the reasons for it, and how it’s the custom in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2823"/>
Europe;

          <ptr target="#l12535" type="alt" xml:id="te2823"/>
so we’ll let it go. But there’s one thing—he can have a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5724"/>
rope ladder

          <app from="pr5724" n="300.8 (561.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7776">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rope-ladder</rdg>
          </app>
;

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0015"/>
we can tear up our sheets and make him a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5725"/>
rope ladder

          <app from="pr5725" n="300.9 (561.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7777">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rope-

              <lb/>
ladder

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0239" type="an" xml:id="uu0015"/>
easy

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2824"/>
enough.

          <ptr target="#l12536" type="alt" xml:id="te2824"/>
And we can send it to him in a pie; it’s mostly done that way. And I’ve et worse pies.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71339">
“Why, Tom Sawyer, how you talk,” I says; “Jim ain’t got no use for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5726"/>
rope ladder

          <app from="pr5726" n="300.13 (561.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7778">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rope-

              <lb/>
ladder

            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71351">
“He

          <hi rend="italic">has</hi>
got use for it. How

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
talk, you better

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5727"/>
say:

          <app from="pr5727" n="300.14 (562.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7779">
            <lem wit="MS2">say:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">say;</rdg>
          </app>
you don’t know nothing about it. He’s

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to have a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5728"/>
rope ladder:

          <app from="pr5728" n="300.15 (562.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7780">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rope ladder;</rdg>
          </app>
they all do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71379">
“What in the nation can he

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
with it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71385">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Do</hi>
with it? He can hide it in his bed, can’t he? That’s what they all do; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5729"/>
he’s

          <app from="pr5729" n="300.18 (562.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7781">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">he’s</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">he ’s</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2825"/>
got to, too

          <ptr target="#l12537" type="alt" xml:id="te2825"/>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2826"/>
Huck, you

          <ptr target="#l12538" type="alt" xml:id="te2826"/>
don’t ever seem to want to do

          <pb n="301" xml:id="pb0301"/>
anything that’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5730"/>
regular:

          <app from="pr5730" n="301.1 (562.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7782">
            <lem wit="MS2">regular:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">regular;</rdg>
          </app>
you want to be starting something fresh all the time. Spose he

          <hi rend="italic">don’t</hi>
do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5731"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr5731" n="301.2 (562.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7783">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
with it? ain’t it there in his bed, for a clew, after he’s gone? and don’t you reckon

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2827"/>
they’ll

          <ptr target="#l12539" type="alt" xml:id="te2827"/>
want clews? Of course they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2828"/>
will

          <ptr target="#l12540" type="alt" xml:id="te2828"/>
. And you wouldn’t leave them any? That would be a

          <hi rend="italic">pretty</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2829"/>
howdy-do

          <ptr target="#l12541" type="alt" xml:id="te2829"/>
,

          <hi rend="italic">wouldn’t</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2830"/>
it!

          <ptr target="#l12542" type="alt" xml:id="te2830"/>
I never heard of such a thing.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71451">
“Well,” I says, “if it’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2831"/>
in the

          <ptr target="#l12543" type="alt" xml:id="te2831"/>
regulations, and he’s got to have it, all right, let him have it; because I don’t wish to go back on no regulations; but there’s one thing, Tom Sawyer—if we go to tearing up our sheets to make Jim a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5732"/>
rope ladder

          <app from="pr5732" n="301.9 (563.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7784">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rope-

              <lb/>
ladder

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5733"/>
we’re

          <app from="pr5733" n="301.9 (563.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7785">
            <lem wit="A">we’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we are</rdg>
          </app>
going to get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2832"/>
into trouble with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5734"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5734" n="301.10 (564.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7786">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally,

          <ptr target="#l12544" type="alt" xml:id="te2832"/>
just as sure as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5735"/>
you’re

          <app from="pr5735" n="301.10 (564.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7787">
            <lem wit="A">you’re</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you are</rdg>
          </app>
born.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5736"/>
Now

          <app from="pr5736" n="301.10 (564.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7788">
            <lem wit="MS2">Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Now,</rdg>
          </app>
the way I look at it, a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5737"/>
hickry bark

          <app from="pr5737" n="301.11 (564.4–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7789">
            <lem wit="MS2">hickry bark</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hickry-bark</rdg>
          </app>
ladder don’t cost nothing, and don’t waste nothing, and is just as good to load up a pie with, and hide in a straw tick, as any

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5738"/>
rag-ladder

          <app from="pr5738" n="301.13 (564.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7790">
            <lem wit="C">rag-ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
rag-

              <lb/>
ladder

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">rag ladder</rdg>
          </app>
you can

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2833"/>
start;

          <ptr target="#l12545" type="alt" xml:id="te2833"/>
and as for Jim,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2834"/>
he ain’t had no experience, and so

          <ptr target="#l12546" type="alt" xml:id="te2834"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
don’t care what kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5739"/>
a—

          <app from="pr5739" n="301.14 (564.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7791">
            <lem wit="MS2">a—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71545">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5740"/>
O

          <app from="pr5740" n="301.15 (564.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7792">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh,</rdg>
          </app>
shucks, Huck Finn, if I was as ignorant as you, I’d keep still—that’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2835"/>
what

          <ptr target="#l12547" type="alt" xml:id="te2835"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I’d</hi>
do. Who ever heard of a state prisoner escaping by a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5741"/>
hickry bark

          <app from="pr5741" n="301.17 (565.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7793">
            <lem wit="MS2">hickry bark</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">hickry-bark</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2836"/>
ladder?

          <ptr target="#l12548" type="alt" xml:id="te2836"/>
Why, it’s perfectly

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5742"/>
ridiculous

          <app from="pr5742" n="301.17 (565.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7794">
            <lem wit="A">ridiculous</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ridiclous</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71581">
“Well, all right, Tom, fix it your own way; but if you’ll take my advice, you’ll let me borrow a sheet off of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5743"/>
clothes line

          <app from="pr5743" n="301.19 (565.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7795">
            <lem wit="MS2">clothes line</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">clothes-line</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71591">He said that would do. And that give him another idea, and he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71593">“Borrow a shirt, too.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71595">
“What do we want of

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0016"/>
a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2837"/>
shirt, Tom?”

          <ptr target="#l12549" type="alt" xml:id="te2837"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71602">
“Want it for Jim to keep a journal on

          <ptr target="#as0240" type="an" xml:id="uu0016"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71606">
“Journal your granny—

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0017"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
can’t write

          <ptr target="#as0241" type="an" xml:id="uu0017"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71614">
“Spose he

          <hi rend="italic">can’t</hi>
write—he can make marks on the shirt, can’t he, if we make him a pen out of an old pewter spoon or a piece of an old iron barrel-hoop?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71619">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2838"/>
“Why, Tom, we

          <ptr target="#l12550" type="alt" xml:id="te2838"/>
can pull a feather out of a goose and make him a better one; and quicker, too.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71625">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Prisoners</hi>
don’t have geese running around the donjon-keep to pull pens out of, you muggins. They

          <hi rend="italic">always</hi>
make their pens out of the hardest, toughest, troublesomest piece of old brass candlestick or something like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5744"/>
that

          <app from="pr5744" n="301.34 (567.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7796">
            <lem wit="A">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that that</rdg>
          </app>
they can get their hands on; and it takes them weeks and weeks, and months and months to file it out,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2839"/>
too,

          <ptr target="#l12551" type="alt" xml:id="te2839"/>
because they’ve got to do it by rubbing it on the wall.

          <hi rend="italic">They</hi>
wouldn’t use a goose-quill if they had it. It ain’t regular.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71649">
“Well, then,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5745"/>
what’ll

          <app from="pr5745" n="301.38 (568.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7797">
            <lem wit="A">what’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">what will</rdg>
          </app>
we make him the ink out of?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71659">
          <pb n="302" xml:id="pb0302"/>
“Many makes it out of iron-rust and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5746"/>
tears

          <app from="pr5746" n="302.1 (568.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7798">
            <lem wit="A">tears</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">spit</rdg>
          </app>
; but that’s the common sort

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5747"/>
and women

          <app from="pr5747" n="302.2 (568.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7799">
            <lem wit="A">and women</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7800">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
;

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0018"/>
the best authorities

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2840"/>
uses

          <ptr target="#l12552" type="alt" xml:id="te2840"/>
their own blood

          <ptr target="#as0242" type="an" xml:id="uu0018"/>
. Jim can do that; and when he wants to send any little common ordinary mysterious message to let the world know where he’s captivated, he can

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0019"/>
write it on the bottom of a tin plate with a fork and throw it out of the window. The Iron Mask

          <ptr target="#as0243" type="an" xml:id="uu0019"/>
always done

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2841"/>
that,

          <ptr target="#l12553" type="alt" xml:id="te2841"/>
and it’s a blame’ good way, too.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71697">
“Jim ain’t got no tin

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2842"/>
plates. They

          <ptr target="#l12554" type="alt" xml:id="te2842"/>
feed him in a pan.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71703">“That ain’t anything; we can get him some.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71705">
“Can’t nobody

          <hi rend="italic">read</hi>
his plates.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71710">
“That ain’t got nothing to

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
with it, Huck Finn. All

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2843"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5748"/>
          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
’s

          <app from="pr5748" n="302.11 (569.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7801">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">he’</hi>
s

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">he’s</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12555" type="alt" xml:id="te2843"/>
got to do is to write on the plate and throw it out. You don’t

          <hi rend="italic">have</hi>
to be able to read it. Why, half the time you can’t read anything a prisoner writes on a tin plate, or anywhere else.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71733">“Well, then, what’s the sense in wasting the plates?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71735">
“Why, blame it all, it ain’t the

          <hi rend="italic">prisoner’s</hi>
plates.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71740">
“But it’s

          <hi rend="italic">somebody’s</hi>
plates, ain’t it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71745">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y30201">
            <graphic url="y30201.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">
the

                <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5749"/>
breakfast horn

              </hi>
              <app from="pr5749" n="302 caption" type="e" xml:id="la7802">
                <lem wit="C">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">breakfast horn</hi>
                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7803">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">breakfast-horn</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71764">
          <pb n="303" xml:id="pb0303"/>
“Well, spos’n it is? What does the

          <hi rend="italic">prisoner</hi>
care

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5750"/>
whose—

          <app from="pr5750" n="303.1 (570.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7804">
            <lem wit="MS2">whose—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">whose——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71778">
He broke off there, because we heard the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5751"/>
breakfast horn

          <app from="pr5751" n="303.2 (570.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7805">
            <lem wit="MS2">breakfast horn</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">breakfast-horn</rdg>
          </app>
blowing. So we cleared out for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5752"/>
house.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71790">
Along

          <app from="pr5752" n="303.3–4 (570.15–571.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7806">
            <lem wit="A">house. [¶] Along</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
house.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7807">chapter sink</note>
[¶] Along

            </rdg>
          </app>
during that morning I borrowed a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2844"/>
sheet

          <ptr target="#l12556" type="alt" xml:id="te2844"/>
and a white shirt off of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5753"/>
clothes line

          <app from="pr5753" n="303.5 (571.3–4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7808">
            <lem wit="MS2">clothes line</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">clothes-line</rdg>
          </app>
; and I found an old sack and put them in it, and we went down and got the fox-fire, and put that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5754"/>
in,

          <app from="pr5754" n="303.6 (571.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7809">
            <lem wit="MS2">in,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
in

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too. I called it borrowing, because that was what pap always called it; but Tom said it warn’t borrowing, it was stealing. He said we was representing prisoners; and prisoners don’t care how they get a thing so they get it, and nobody don’t blame them for it, either. It ain’t no crime in a prisoner to steal the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5755"/>
thing

          <app from="pr5755" n="303.11 (572.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7810">
            <lem wit="A">thing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">things</rdg>
          </app>
he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2845"/>
needs

          <ptr target="#l12557" type="alt" xml:id="te2845"/>
to get away with, Tom said; it’s his right; and so, as long as we was representing a prisoner, we had a perfect right to steal anything on this place we had the least use for, to get ourselves out of prison with. He said if we warn’t prisoners it would be a very different thing, and nobody but a mean ornery person would steal when he warn’t a prisoner. So we allowed we would steal everything there was that come handy. And yet he made a mighty fuss, one day, after that, when I stole a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5756"/>
watermelon

          <app from="pr5756" n="303.18 (573.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7811">
            <lem wit="MS2">watermelon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
water-

              <lb/>
melon

            </rdg>
          </app>
out of the nigger patch and eat it; and he made me go and give the niggers a dime, without telling them what it was for. Tom

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2846"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l12558" type="alt" xml:id="te2846"/>
that what he meant was, we could steal anything we

          <hi rend="italic">needed.</hi>
Well, I says, I needed the watermelon. But he said I didn’t need it to get out of prison with,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5757"/>
there’s

          <app from="pr5757" n="303.23 (574.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7812">
            <lem wit="A">there’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and there’s</rdg>
          </app>
where the difference was. He said if

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5758"/>
I’d

          <app from="pr5758" n="303.23 (574.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7813">
            <lem wit="A">I’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I had</rdg>
          </app>
a wanted it to hide a knife in, and smuggle it to Jim to kill the seneskal with, it would a been all right. So I let it go at that, though I couldn’t see no advantage in my representing a prisoner, if I got to set down and chaw over a lot of gold-leaf distinctions like that, every time I see a chance to hog a watermelon.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71870">
Well, as I was saying, we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5759"/>
waited,

          <app from="pr5759" n="303.29 (575.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7814">
            <lem wit="MS2">waited,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
waited

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5760"/>
morning,

          <app from="pr5760" n="303.29 (575.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7815">
            <lem wit="MS2">morning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
morning

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2847"/>
till

          <ptr target="#l12560" type="alt" xml:id="te2847"/>
everybody was settled down to business, and nobody in sight around the yard; then Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5761"/>
he

          <app from="pr5761" n="303.31 (575.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7816">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7817">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
carried the sack into the lean-to whilst I stood off a piece to keep watch.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5762"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr5762" n="303.32 (575.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7818">
            <lem wit="MS2">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he come out, and we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2848"/>
went

          <ptr target="#l12562" type="alt" xml:id="te2848"/>
and set down on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5763"/>
woodpile

          <app from="pr5763" n="303.33 (575.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7819">
            <lem wit="MS2">woodpile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wood-pile</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2849"/>
to talk

          <ptr target="#l12564" type="alt" xml:id="te2849"/>
. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71926">“Everything’s all right, now, except tools; and that’s easy fixed.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71928">“Tools?” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71930">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71932">“Tools for what?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71934">
“Why, to dig with. We ain’t agoing to

          <hi rend="italic">gnaw</hi>
him out, are we?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71939">
          <pb n="304" xml:id="pb0304"/>
“Ain’t them old

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2850"/>
crippled

          <ptr target="#l12566" type="alt" xml:id="te2850"/>
picks and things in there good enough to dig a nigger out with?” I says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71946">
He turns on me looking pitying enough to make a body

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5764"/>
cry;

          <app from="pr5764" n="304.3 (577.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7820">
            <lem wit="MS2">cry;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">cry,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71957">
“Huck Finn, did you

          <hi rend="italic">ever</hi>
hear of a prisoner having picks and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5765"/>
shovels

          <app from="pr5765" n="304.6 (577.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7821">
            <lem wit="MS2">shovels</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shovels,</rdg>
          </app>
and all the modern conveniences in his wardrobe to dig himself out with? Now I want to ask you—if you got any reasonableness in you at all—what kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2851"/>
a show

          <ptr target="#l12568" type="alt" xml:id="te2851"/>
would

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
give him to be a hero?

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5766"/>
Why

          <app from="pr5766" n="304.9 (577.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7822">
            <lem wit="MS2">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
they might as well lend him the key, and done with it. Picks and shovels—why they wouldn’t furnish ’em to a king.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71986">“Well, then,” I says, “if we don’t want the picks and shovels, what do we want?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71988">
“A couple of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5767"/>
caseknives

          <app from="pr5767" n="304.13 (578.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7823">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknives</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knives</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e71998">“To dig the foundations out from under that cabin with?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72000">“Yes.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72002">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5768"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0078"/>
Confound

          <ptr target="#tb0078" type="te" xml:id="tv0078"/>
          <app from="pr5768" n="304.16 (578.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7824">
            <lem wit="A">Confound</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Consound</rdg>
          </app>
it, it’s foolish, Tom.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72014">
“It don’t make no difference how foolish it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2852"/>
is,

          <ptr target="#l12570" type="alt" xml:id="te2852"/>
it’s the

          <hi rend="italic">right</hi>
way—and it’s the regular way. And there ain’t no

          <hi rend="italic">other</hi>
way, that ever

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
heard

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5769"/>
of;

          <app from="pr5769" n="304.19 (578.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7825">
            <lem wit="MS2">of;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">of,</rdg>
          </app>
and I’ve read all the books that gives

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0043"/>
any information about these things. They always

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0020"/>
dig out with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5770"/>
caseknife

          <app from="pr5770" n="304.20 (579.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7826">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknife</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knife</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0244" type="an" xml:id="uu0020"/>
—and not through dirt, mind you;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5771"/>
generly

          <app from="pr5771" n="304.21 (579.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7827">
            <lem wit="A">generly</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">generally</rdg>
          </app>
it’s through solid rock. And it takes them weeks and weeks and weeks, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5772"/>
forever

          <app from="pr5772" n="304.22 (579.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7828">
            <lem wit="MS2">forever</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">for ever</rdg>
          </app>
and ever. Why, look at one of them prisoners in the bottom dungeon of the

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0021"/>
Castle Deef

          <ptr target="#as0245" type="an" xml:id="uu0021"/>
, in the harbor of Marseilles, that dug himself out that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5773"/>
way:

          <app from="pr5773" n="304.24 (579.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7829">
            <lem wit="MS2">way:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">way;</rdg>
          </app>
how long was

          <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
at it,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5774"/>
you

          <app from="pr5774" n="304.25 (579.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7830">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">do you</rdg>
          </app>
reckon?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72092">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5775"/>
I

          <app from="pr5775" n="304.28 (580.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7831">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
don’t know.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72103">
“Well, guess.”

          <ptr target="#mt0043" type="alt" xml:id="wn0043"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72106">“I don’t know. A month and a half?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72108">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="su0022"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Thirty-seven year</hi>
          <ptr target="#as0246" type="an" xml:id="uu0022"/>
—and he come out in China.

          <hi rend="italic">That’s</hi>
the kind. I wish the bottom of

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
fortress was solid rock.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72122">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
don’t know nobody in China.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72127">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2853"/>
“What’s

          <ptr target="#l12572" type="alt" xml:id="te2853"/>
          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
got to do with it? Neither did that other fellow. But you’re always a-wandering off on a side issue. Why can’t you stick to the main point?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72134">
“All right—

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t care where he comes out, so he

          <hi rend="italic">comes</hi>
out; and Jim don’t, either, I reckon. But there’s one thing, anyway—Jim’s too old to be dug out with a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5776"/>
caseknife

          <app from="pr5776" n="304.37 (581.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7832">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknife</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knife</rdg>
          </app>
. He won’t last.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72150">
“Yes he will

          <hi rend="italic">last</hi>
, too. You don’t reckon it’s going to take thirty-seven

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2854"/>
years

          <ptr target="#l12574" type="alt" xml:id="te2854"/>
to dig out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5777"/>
through

          <app from="pr5777" n="304.39 (581.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7833">
            <lem wit="A">through</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7834">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a

          <hi rend="italic">dirt</hi>
foundation, do you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72172">
          <pb n="305" xml:id="pb0305"/>
“How long will it take, Tom?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72175">
“Well, we can’t resk being as long as we ought to, because

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2855"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12576" type="alt" xml:id="te2855"/>
mayn’t take very long for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5778"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5778" n="305.3 (582.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7835">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2856"/>
hear

          <ptr target="#l12578" type="alt" xml:id="te2856"/>
from down there by New Orleans. He’ll

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5779"/>
hear

          <app from="pr5779" n="305.4 (582.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7836">
            <lem wit="A">hear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">hear that</rdg>
          </app>
Jim ain’t from there. Then his next move will be to advertise Jim, or something like that. So we can’t resk being as long digging him out as we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2857"/>
ought to.

          <ptr target="#l12580" type="alt" xml:id="te2857"/>
By rights I reckon we ought to be a couple of years; but we can’t. Things being so uncertain, what I recommend is this: that we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2858"/>
really

          <ptr target="#l12582" type="alt" xml:id="te2858"/>
dig right in, as quick as we can; and after that, we can

          <hi rend="italic">let on</hi>
, to ourselves, that we was at it thirty-seven years. Then we can snatch him out and rush him away the first time there’s an alarm. Yes, I reckon that’ll be the best

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5780"/>
way.

          <app from="pr5780" n="305.14 (583.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7837">
            <lem wit="MS2">way.</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
way

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72222">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5781"/>
Now

          <app from="pr5781" n="305.15 (583.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7838">
            <lem wit="MS2">Now</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Now,</rdg>
          </app>
there’s

          <hi rend="italic">sense</hi>
in that,” I says. “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5782"/>
Letting-on

          <app from="pr5782" n="305.16 (583.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7839">
            <lem wit="MS2">Letting-on</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Letting on</rdg>
          </app>
don’t cost nothing;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5783"/>
letting-on

          <app from="pr5783" n="305.17 (583.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7840">
            <lem wit="C">letting-on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
letting-

              <lb/>
on

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">letting on</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t no trouble; and if it’s any object, I don’t mind letting on we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2859"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l12584" type="alt" xml:id="te2859"/>
at it a hundred and fifty year. It wouldn’t strain me none, after I got my hand in. So I’ll mosey

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5784"/>
along,

          <app from="pr5784" n="305.23 (583.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7841">
            <lem wit="MS2">along,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
along

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, and smouch a couple of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5785"/>
caseknives

          <app from="pr5785" n="305.24–25 (584.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7842">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknives</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knives</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72277">“Smouch three,” he says; “we want one to make a saw out of.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72279">
“Tom, if it ain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2860"/>
unregular

          <ptr target="#l12586" type="alt" xml:id="te2860"/>
and irreligious to sejest it,” I says, “there’s an old rusty saw-blade around yonder sticking under the weatherboarding behind the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5786"/>
smokehouse

          <app from="pr5786" n="305.33 (584.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7843">
            <lem wit="MS2">smokehouse</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">smoke-house</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72293">He looked kind of weary and discouraged-like, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72295">
“It ain’t no use to try to learn you nothing, Huck. Run along and smouch the knives—three of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5787"/>
them.” So

          <app from="pr5787" n="305.36 (585.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7844">
            <lem wit="A">
them.”

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7845">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
So

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">them.” [¶] So</rdg>
          </app>
I done

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5788"/>
it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72313">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y30501">
            <graphic url="y30501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">smouching the knives</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0435">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXVI.</head>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72322">
          <pb n="306" xml:id="pb0306"/>
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y30601">
            <graphic url="y30601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">Chapter XXXVI.</ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
As

              <app from="pr5788" n="305.36–306.1 (585.3)" type="e" xml:id="laq345">
                <lem wit="A">
it.

                  <milestone unit="page"/>
Chapter XXXVI.[¶] As

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
it.

                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de2346">
no

                    <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
                  </note>
As

                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3061">
            <graphic url="hf3061.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">
going down the

                <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5798"/>
lightning rod

              </hi>
              <app from="pr5798" n="306 caption" type="e" xml:id="la7858">
                <lem wit="C">lightning rod</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="mtp" type="ed" xml:id="de7859">not in</note>
                </rdg>
                <rdg wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">lightning-rod</hi>
                </rdg>
              </app>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e72357">
soon as we reckoned everybody was asleep, that night, we went down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5789"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr5789" n="306.3 (585.6–7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7848">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
, and shut ourselves up in the lean-to, and got out our pile of fox-fire, and went to work. We cleared everything out of the way, about four or five

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5790"/>
foot

          <app from="pr5790" n="306.8 (585.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7849">
            <lem wit="A">foot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">feet</rdg>
          </app>
along the middle of the bottom log. Tom said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5791"/>
we

          <app from="pr5791" n="306.9 (585.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7850">
            <lem wit="MS2">we</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">he</rdg>
          </app>
was right behind Jim’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5792"/>
bed,

          <app from="pr5792" n="306.10 (585.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7851">
            <lem wit="MS2">bed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
bed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5793"/>
we’d

          <app from="pr5793" n="306.11 (585.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7852">
            <lem wit="A">we’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we would</rdg>
          </app>
dig in under it, and when we got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5794"/>
through,

          <app from="pr5794" n="306.12 (585.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7853">
            <lem wit="MS2">through,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
through

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5795"/>
there couldn’t

          <app from="pr5795" n="306.12 (586.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7854">
            <lem wit="A">there couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7855">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
nobody in the cabin

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5796"/>
ever

          <app from="pr5796" n="306.13 (586.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7856">
            <lem wit="A">ever</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">would</rdg>
          </app>
know there was any hole there, because Jim’s counterpin hung down most to the ground, and you’d have to raise it up and look

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5797"/>
under,

          <app from="pr5797" n="306.17 (586.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7857">
            <lem wit="MS2">under,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
under

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to see the hole. So we dug and dug, with the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5799"/>
caseknives

          <app from="pr5799" n="306.19 (586.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7860">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknives</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knives</rdg>
          </app>
, till most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5800"/>
midnight

          <app from="pr5800" n="306.19 (586.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7861">
            <lem wit="MS2">midnight</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
mid-

              <lb/>
night

            </rdg>
          </app>
; and then we was dog-tired, and our hands was blistered, and yet you couldn’t see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5801"/>
we’d

          <app from="pr5801" n="306.20 (586.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la7862">
            <lem wit="A">we’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we had</rdg>
          </app>
done anything, hardly. At last I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72461">“This ain’t no thirty-seven year job, this is a thirty-eight year job, Tom Sawyer.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72463">He never said nothing. But he sighed, and pretty soon he stopped digging, and then for a good little while I knowed he was thinking. Then he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72465">
“It ain’t no use, Huck, it ain’t agoing to work. If we was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5802"/>
prisoners,

          <app from="pr5802" n="306.27 (587.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7863">
            <lem wit="MS2">prisoners,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
prisoners

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
it would, because then we’d have as many years as we wanted, and no hurry; and we wouldn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2861"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l12588" type="alt" xml:id="te2861"/>
but a few minutes to dig, every day, while they was changing watches, and so our hands wouldn’t get blistered, and we could keep it up right along, year in and year out, and do it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5803"/>
right

          <app from="pr5803" n="306.32 (588.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7864">
            <lem wit="MS2">right</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">right,</rdg>
          </app>
and the way it ought to be done. But

          <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
can’t fool

          <pb n="307" xml:id="pb0307"/>
along, we got to rush; we ain’t got no time to spare. If we was to put in another night this way, we’d have to knock off for a week to let our hands get well—couldn’t touch a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5804"/>
caseknife

          <app from="pr5804" n="307.3 (588.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7865">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknife</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knife</rdg>
          </app>
with them sooner.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72501">
“Well, then, what we going to do,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5805"/>
Tom?

          <app from="pr5805" n="307.4 (588.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7866">
            <lem wit="A">Tom?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Tom.</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72511">
“I’ll tell you. It ain’t right,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2862"/>
and it

          <ptr target="#l12590" type="alt" xml:id="te2862"/>
ain’t moral, and I wouldn’t like it to get out—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2863"/>
but

          <ptr target="#l12592" type="alt" xml:id="te2863"/>
there ain’t only just the one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5806"/>
way:

          <app from="pr5806" n="307.6 (589.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7867">
            <lem wit="MS2">way:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">way;</rdg>
          </app>
we got to dig him out with the picks, and

          <hi rend="italic">let on</hi>
it’s case-knives.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72533">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2864"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5807"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
you’re

          <app from="pr5807" n="307.8 (589.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7868">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
you’re

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Now your’e</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">talking!</hi>
” I says;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5808"/>
“Your

          <app from="pr5808" n="307.8 (589.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7869">
            <lem wit="C">“Your</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Your</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">“your</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12594" type="alt" xml:id="te2864"/>
head gets leveler and leveler all the time, Tom Sawyer,” I says. “Picks is the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5809"/>
thing

          <app from="pr5809" n="307.9 (589.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7870">
            <lem wit="A">thing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ticket</rdg>
          </app>
, moral or no moral; and as for me, I don’t care shucks for the morality of it, nohow. When I start in to steal a nigger, or a watermelon, or a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5810"/>
Sunday school

          <app from="pr5810" n="307.11–12 (589.13–14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7871">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sunday school</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sunday-school</rdg>
          </app>
book, I ain’t no ways particular how it’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5811"/>
done,

          <app from="pr5811" n="307.12 (589.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la7872">
            <lem wit="MS2">done,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
done

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2865"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l12596" type="alt" xml:id="te2865"/>
it’s done. What I want is my nigger; or what I want is my watermelon; or what I want is my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5812"/>
Sunday school book:

          <app from="pr5812" n="307.14 (590.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7873">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sunday school book:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sunday-school book;</rdg>
          </app>
and if a pick’s the handiest thing, that’s the thing I’m agoing to dig that nigger or that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5813"/>
watermelon

          <app from="pr5813" n="307.15 (590.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7874">
            <lem wit="A">watermelon</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
water-

              <lb/>
melon

            </rdg>
          </app>
or that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5814"/>
Sunday school

          <app from="pr5814" n="307.16 (590.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7875">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sunday school</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sunday-school</rdg>
          </app>
book out with; and I don’t give a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5815"/>
dead rat

          <app from="pr5815" n="307.16 (590.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7876">
            <lem wit="A">dead rat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">cuss</rdg>
          </app>
what the authorities thinks

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2866"/>
about

          <ptr target="#l12598" type="alt" xml:id="te2866"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2867"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5816"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12600" type="alt" xml:id="te2867"/>
,

          <app from="pr5816" n="307.17 (590.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7877">
            <lem wit="MS2">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5817"/>
nuther

          <app from="pr5817" n="307.17 (590.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7878">
            <lem wit="A">nuther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">neither</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72647">
“Well,” he says, “there’s excuse for picks and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5818"/>
letting-on,

          <app from="pr5818" n="307.18 (590.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7879">
            <lem wit="MS2">letting-on,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">letting-on</rdg>
          </app>
in a case like this; if it warn’t so, I wouldn’t approve of it, nor I wouldn’t stand by and see the rules broke—because right is right, and wrong is wrong, and a body ain’t got no business doing

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2868"/>
wrong when

          <ptr target="#l12602" type="alt" xml:id="te2868"/>
he ain’t ignorant and knows better. It might answer for

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
to dig Jim out with a pick,

          <hi rend="italic">without</hi>
any letting-on, because you don’t know no better; but it wouldn’t for me, because I do know better. Gimme a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5819"/>
caseknife

          <app from="pr5819" n="307.25 (591.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7880">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknife</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
case-

              <lb/>
knife

            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72678">
He had his own by him, but I handed him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2869"/>
mine.

          <ptr target="#l12604" type="alt" xml:id="te2869"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2870"/>
He flung it down, and says:

          <ptr target="#l12606" type="alt" xml:id="te2870"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72687">
“Gimme a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pry820"/>
          <hi rend="italic">caseknife</hi>
          <app from="pry820" n="307.28 (591.13)" type="hc" xml:id="lan881">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">caseknife</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">case-knife</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72700">
I didn’t know just what to do—but then I thought. I scratched around amongst the old tools,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0044"/>
and got a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2871"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5821"/>
pick-axe

          <app from="pr5821" n="307.30 (592.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7882">
            <lem wit="MS2">pick-axe</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pick-ax</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12608" type="alt" xml:id="te2871"/>
and give it to him, and he took it and went to work, and never said a word.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72714">He was always just that particular. Full of principle.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72716">
So then I got a shovel, and then we picked and shoveled, turn about, and made the fur fly. We stuck to it about a half an hour, which was as long as we could stand up; but we had a good deal of a hole to show for it. When I got up stairs, I looked out at the window and see Tom doing his level best with the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5822"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr5822" n="307.37 (592.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7883">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
, but he couldn’t come it, his hands was so sore. At last he says:

          <ptr target="#mt0044" type="alt" xml:id="wn0044"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72727">
          <pb n="308" xml:id="pb0308"/>
“It ain’t no use, it can’t be done. What you reckon I better do? Can’t you think

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5823"/>
up

          <app from="pr5823" n="308.2 (593.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7884">
            <lem wit="A">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
no way?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72738">
“Yes,” I says, “but I reckon it ain’t regular. Come up the stairs, and let on it’s a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5824"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr5824" n="308.4 (593.7–8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7885">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72748">So he done it.</p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y30801">
          <graphic url="y30801.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">stealing spoons</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72755">
Next day Tom stole a pewter spoon and a brass candlestick in the house,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5825"/>
for to

          <app from="pr5825" n="308.7 (593.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7886">
            <lem wit="A">for to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2872"/>
make

          <ptr target="#l12610" type="alt" xml:id="te2872"/>
some pens for Jim out of, and six tallow candles; and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5826"/>
hung

          <app from="pr5826" n="308.8 (593.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7887">
            <lem wit="A">hung</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">used</rdg>
          </app>
around the nigger cabins, and laid for a chance, and stole three tin plates. Tom said it wasn’t enough; but I said nobody wouldn’t ever see the plates that Jim throwed out, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5827"/>
they’d

          <app from="pr5827" n="308.10 (594.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7888">
            <lem wit="A">they’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">they would</rdg>
          </app>
fall in the dog-fennel and jimpson weeds under the window-hole—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2873"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l12612" type="alt" xml:id="te2873"/>
we could tote them back and he could use them over again. So Tom was satisfied. Then he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72789">
“Now, the thing to study

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5828"/>
out,

          <app from="pr5828" n="308.14 (594.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7889">
            <lem wit="MS2">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
is, how to get the things to Jim.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72799">“Take them in through the hole,” I says, “when we get it done.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72802">
He only just looked scornful, and said something about nobody ever heard of such an idiotic idea, and then he went to studying.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5829"/>
By

          <pb n="309" xml:id="pb0309"/>
and by

          <app from="pr5829" n="308.17–309.1 (595.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7890">
            <lem wit="MS2">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2874"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l12614" type="alt" xml:id="te2874"/>
he had ciphered out two or three ways, but there warn’t no need to decide on any of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5830"/>
them,

          <app from="pr5830" n="309.2 (595.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7891">
            <lem wit="MS2">them,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
them

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
yet. Said we’d got to post

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5831"/>
Jim,

          <app from="pr5831" n="309.3 (595.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7892">
            <lem wit="MS2">Jim,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
Jim

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
first.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72835">
That night we went down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5832"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr5832" n="309.4 (595.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7893">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
a little after ten, and took one of the candles along, and listened under the window-hole, and heard Jim snoring; so we pitched it in, and it didn’t wake him. Then we whirled in with the pick and shovel, and in about two hours and a half the job was done. We crept in under Jim’s bed and into the cabin, and pawed around and found the candle and lit it, and stood over Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5833"/>
awhile

          <app from="pr5833" n="309.10 (596.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7894">
            <lem wit="MS2">awhile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a while</rdg>
          </app>
, and found him looking hearty and healthy, and then we woke him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5834"/>
up,

          <app from="pr5834" n="309.11 (596.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7895">
            <lem wit="MS2">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
gentle and gradual. He was so glad to see us he most cried; and called us honey, and all the pet names he could think of; and was for having us hunt up a cold chisel to cut the chain off of his leg with, right away, and clearing out without losing any time. But Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5835"/>
he

          <app from="pr5835" n="309.15 (596.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7896">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7897">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
showed him how unregular it would be, and set down and told him all about our plans, and how we could alter them in a minute any time there was an alarm; and not to be the least afraid, because we would

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5836"/>
see

          <app from="pr5836" n="309.18 (597.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7898">
            <lem wit="A">see</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">see that</rdg>
          </app>
he got away,

          <hi rend="italic">sure.</hi>
So Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5837"/>
he

          <app from="pr5837" n="309.19 (597.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7899">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7900">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
said it was all right, and we set there and talked over old times a while, and then Tom asked a lot of questions, and when Jim told him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5838"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5838" n="309.21 (597.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7901">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas come in every day or two to pray with him, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5839"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5839" n="309.22 (597.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7902">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2875"/>
come

          <ptr target="#l12616" type="alt" xml:id="te2875"/>
in to see if he was comfortable and had plenty to eat, and both of them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5840"/>
was

          <app from="pr5840" n="309.23 (597.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7903">
            <lem wit="A">was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was as</rdg>
          </app>
kind as they could be, Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72921">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
I know how to fix it. We’ll send you some things by

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2876"/>
them.”

          <ptr target="#l12618" type="alt" xml:id="te2876"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72929">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5841"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0001"/>
I said, “Don’t do nothing of the kind; it’s one of the most jackass ideas I ever struck;” but he never paid no attention to me; went right on. It was his way when he’d got his plans set.

          <ptr target="#as0247" type="an" xml:id="tr0001"/>
          <app from="pr5841" n="309.25–27 (598.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7904">
            <lem wit="A">I said . . . set.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7905">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e72940">
So he told Jim how

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5842"/>
we’d

          <app from="pr5842" n="309.28 (598.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la7906">
            <lem wit="A">we’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we would</rdg>
          </app>
have to smuggle in the rope-ladder pie, and other large things, by Nat, the nigger that fed him, and he must be on the lookout, and not be surprised, and not let Nat see him open them; and we would put small things in uncle’s coat pockets and he must steal them out; and we would tie things to aunt’s apron strings

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2877"/>
or put them in her apron pocket,

          <ptr target="#l12620" type="alt" xml:id="te2877"/>
if we got a chance; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5843"/>
told

          <app from="pr5843" n="309.33 (599.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7907">
            <lem wit="A">told</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we told</rdg>
          </app>
him what they would be and what they was for. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5844"/>
told

          <app from="pr5844" n="309.34 (599.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7908">
            <lem wit="A">told</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we told</rdg>
          </app>
him how to keep a journal on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2878"/>
the shirt

          <ptr target="#l12622" type="alt" xml:id="te2878"/>
with his blood, and all that.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5845"/>
He

          <app from="pr5845" n="309.35 (599.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7909">
            <lem wit="A">He</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">We</rdg>
          </app>
told him everything. Jim he couldn’t see no sense in the most of it, but he allowed we was white folks and knowed better than him; so he was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5846"/>
satisfied

          <app from="pr5846" n="309.38 (599.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7910">
            <lem wit="MS2">satisfied</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">satisfied,</rdg>
          </app>
and said he would do it all just as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5847"/>
Tom

          <app from="pr5847" n="309.38 (599.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7911">
            <lem wit="A">Tom</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we</rdg>
          </app>
said.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73000">
          <pb n="310" xml:id="pb0310"/>
Jim had

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5848"/>
plenty

          <app from="pr5848" n="310.1 (599.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7912">
            <lem wit="A">plenty</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">plenty of</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2879"/>
corn-cob

          <ptr target="#l12624" type="alt" xml:id="te2879"/>
pipes and tobacco; so we had a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2880"/>
right down

          <ptr target="#l12626" type="alt" xml:id="te2880"/>
good sociable time; then we crawled out through the hole, and so home to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2881"/>
bed,

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0079"/>
with hands that looked like they’d been chawed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5849"/>
by a dog

          <app from="pr5849" n="310.4 (600.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7913">
            <lem wit="MS2">by a dog</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7914">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0079" type="te" xml:id="tv0079"/>
.

          <ptr target="#l12628" type="alt" xml:id="te2881"/>
Tom was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2882"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l12630" type="alt" xml:id="te2882"/>
high spirits. He said it was the best fun he ever had in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2883"/>
his

          <ptr target="#l12632" type="alt" xml:id="te2883"/>
life, and the most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5850"/>
intellectural

          <app from="pr5850" n="310.5 (600.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7915">
            <lem wit="A">intellectural</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">intellectual</rdg>
          </app>
; and said if he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2884"/>
only

          <ptr target="#l12634" type="alt" xml:id="te2884"/>
could see his way to it we would keep it up all the rest of our lives and leave Jim to our children to get out; for he believed Jim would come to like it better and better the more he got used to it. He said that in that way it could be strung out to as much as eighty year, and would be the best time on record. And he said it would make us all celebrated that had a hand in it.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73057">
In the morning we went out to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5851"/>
woodpile

          <app from="pr5851" n="310.12 (601.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7916">
            <lem wit="MS2">woodpile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">wood-pile</rdg>
          </app>
and chopped up the brass

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5852"/>
candlestick

          <app from="pr5852" n="310.13 (601.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7917">
            <lem wit="MS2">candlestick</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
candle-

              <lb/>
stick

            </rdg>
          </app>
into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5853"/>
handy sizes

          <app from="pr5853" n="310.13 (601.4)" type="e" xml:id="la7918">
            <lem wit="A">handy</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">convenient</rdg>
          </app>
, and Tom put them and the pewter spoon in his pocket. Then we went to the nigger cabins, and while I got Nat’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5854"/>
notice

          <app from="pr5854" n="310.15 (601.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7919">
            <lem wit="A">notice</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">attention</rdg>
          </app>
off, Tom shoved a piece of candlestick into the middle of a corn-pone that was in Jim’s pan, and we went along with Nat to see how it would work, and it just worked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5855"/>
noble:

          <app from="pr5855" n="310.17 (601.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7920">
            <lem wit="C">noble:</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">first-rate:</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">noble;</rdg>
          </app>
when Jim bit into it it most mashed all his teeth out; and there warn’t ever anything could a worked better. Tom said so himself. Jim he never let on but what it was only just a piece of rock or something like that that’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2885"/>
always getting

          <ptr target="#l12636" type="alt" xml:id="te2885"/>
into bread, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5856"/>
know,

          <app from="pr5856" n="310.21 (602.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7921">
            <lem wit="MS2">know,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">know;</rdg>
          </app>
but after that he never bit into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5857"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr5857" n="310.22 (602.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7922">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
but what he jabbed his fork into it in three or four places, first.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73125">
And whilst we was a standing there in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5858"/>
dimmish

          <app from="pr5858" n="310.24 (602.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7923">
            <lem wit="A">dimmish</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dim</rdg>
          </app>
light, here comes a couple of the hounds bulging in, from under Jim’s bed; and they kept on piling in till there was eleven of them, and there warn’t hardly room

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2886"/>
in there

          <ptr target="#l12638" type="alt" xml:id="te2886"/>
to get your breath. By

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5859"/>
jings

          <app from="pr5859" n="310.27 (603.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7924">
            <lem wit="MS2">jings</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jings,</rdg>
          </app>
we

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5860"/>
forgot

          <app from="pr5860" n="310.27 (603.3)" type="e" xml:id="la7925">
            <lem wit="A">forgot</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">had forgot</rdg>
          </app>
to fasten that lean-to door. The nigger Nat

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5861"/>
he only

          <app from="pr5861" n="310.28 (603.5)" type="e" xml:id="la7926">
            <lem wit="A">he only</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7927">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
just hollered “witches!” once, and keeled over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5862"/>
onto

          <app from="pr5862" n="310.29 (603.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7928">
            <lem wit="A">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on</rdg>
          </app>
the floor amongst the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5863"/>
dogs

          <app from="pr5863" n="310.29 (603.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7929">
            <lem wit="MS2">dogs</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">dogs,</rdg>
          </app>
and begun to groan like he was dying. Tom jerked the door open and flung out a slab of Jim’s meat, and the dogs went for

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5864"/>
it;

          <app from="pr5864" n="310.31 (603.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7930">
            <lem wit="MS2">it;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it,</rdg>
          </app>
and in two seconds he was out himself and back again and shut the door, and I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2887"/>
knowed

          <ptr target="#l12640" type="alt" xml:id="te2887"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5865"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr5865" n="310.33 (603.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7931">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he had</rdg>
          </app>
fixed the other

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5866"/>
door,

          <app from="pr5866" n="310.33 (603.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7932">
            <lem wit="MS2">door,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
door

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too. Then he went to work on the nigger, coaxing him and petting him, and asking him if he’d been imagining he saw something again. He raised up, and blinked his eyes around, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73210">
“Mars Sid, you’ll say I’s a fool, but if I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5867"/>
didn’

          <app from="pr5867" n="310.37 (604.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7933">
            <lem wit="MS2">didn’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">didn’t</rdg>
          </app>
b’lieve I see most a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2888"/>
million

          <ptr target="#l12642" type="alt" xml:id="te2888"/>
dogs,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5868"/>
er devils, er

          <app from="pr5868" n="310.38 (604.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7934">
            <lem wit="A">er devils, er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or devils, or</rdg>
          </app>
some’n, I wisht I may die right heah in

          <pb n="311" xml:id="pb0311"/>
dese tracks. I did, mos’ sholy. Mars

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2889"/>
Sid, I

          <hi rend="italic">felt</hi>
          <ptr target="#l12644" type="alt" xml:id="te2889"/>
um—I

          <hi rend="italic">felt</hi>
um, sah; dey was all over me.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2890"/>
Dad

          <ptr target="#l12646" type="alt" xml:id="te2890"/>
fetch it, I jis’ wisht I could git my han’s on one er dem witches jis’ wunst—on’y jis’ wunst—it’s all

          <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
d ast. But mos’ly I wisht dey’d lemme ’lone, I does.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73252">Tom says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73254">
“Well, I tell you what

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
think. What makes them come here just at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2891"/>
this

          <ptr target="#l12648" type="alt" xml:id="te2891"/>
runaway nigger’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5869"/>
breakfast time

          <app from="pr5869" n="311.7 (605.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7935">
            <lem wit="MS2">breakfast time</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">breakfast-time</rdg>
          </app>
? It’s because they’re hungry; that’s the reason. You

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0002"/>
make them a witch pie

          <ptr target="#as0248" type="an" xml:id="tr0002"/>
; that’s the thing for

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
to do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73280">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y31101">
            <graphic url="y31101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">tom advises a witch pie</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73286">
“But my lan’,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5870"/>
mars

          <app from="pr5870" n="311.10 (605.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7936">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Sid, how’s

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
gwyne to make ’m a witch pie? I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5871"/>
doan

          <app from="pr5871" n="311.11 (605.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7937">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
know how to make it. I hain’t ever hearn er sich a thing

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5872"/>
b’fo’.

          <app from="pr5872" n="311.11 (606.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7938">
            <lem wit="C">b’fo’.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">befo’.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">b’fo.’</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73318">“Well, then, I’ll have to make it myself.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73320">
“Will you do it, honey?—will you? I’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2892"/>
wusshup

          <ptr target="#l12650" type="alt" xml:id="te2892"/>
de groun’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2893"/>
und’

          <ptr target="#l12652" type="alt" xml:id="te2893"/>
yo’ foot, I will!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73330">
“All right, I’ll do it, seeing it’s you, and you’ve been good to us

          <pb n="312" xml:id="pb0312"/>
and showed us the runaway nigger. But you got to be mighty careful. When we come around, you turn your back; and then whatever

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2894"/>
we’ve

          <ptr target="#l12654" type="alt" xml:id="te2894"/>
put in the pan, don’t you let

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5873"/>
on

          <app from="pr5873" n="312.3 (606.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la7939">
            <lem wit="A">on</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on that</rdg>
          </app>
you see it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2895"/>
at

          <ptr target="#l12656" type="alt" xml:id="te2895"/>
all. And don’t you look, when Jim unloads the pan—something might happen, I don’t know what. And above all, don’t you

          <hi rend="italic">handle</hi>
the witch-things.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73354">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2896"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Hannel</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5874"/>
’m,

          <ptr target="#l12658" type="alt" xml:id="te2896"/>
          <app from="pr5874" n="312.6 (607.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7940">
            <lem wit="MS2">’m,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’m</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5875"/>
mars

          <app from="pr5875" n="312.6 (607.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7941">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Sid? What

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
you a talkin’ ’bout? I wouldn’ lay de weight er my finger on um, not

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5876"/>
f’r

          <app from="pr5876" n="312.7 (607.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7942">
            <lem wit="A">f’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
ten hund’d

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5877"/>
thous’n’

          <app from="pr5877" n="312.7 (607.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7943">
            <lem wit="A">thous’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">thousan’</rdg>
          </app>
billion dollars, I wouldn’t.”

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0439">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXVII.</head>
        <pb n="313" xml:id="pb0313"/>
        <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y31301">
          <graphic url="y31301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5878"/>
Chapter XXXVII.

            <app from="pr5878" n="313 title (607.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7944">
              <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXVII.</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7945">not in</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
          <ab type="transcript">
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5879"/>
That

            <app from="pr5879" n="313.1 (607.11)" type="e" xml:id="la7946">
              <lem wit="A">That</lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="italic">That</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
          </ab>
        </figure>
        <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3131">
          <graphic url="hf3131.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">
the

              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5886"/>
rubbage pile

            </hi>
            <app from="pr5886" n="313 caption" type="hc" xml:id="la7953">
              <lem wit="C">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">rubbage pile</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7954">not in</note>
              </rdg>
              <rdg wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">rubbage-pile</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e73435">
was all fixed. So then we went

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5880"/>
away,

          <app from="pr5880" n="313.2 (607.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7947">
            <lem wit="MS2">away,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
away

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and went to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5881"/>
rubbage pile

          <app from="pr5881" n="313.2–3 (607.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la7948">
            <lem wit="MS2">rubbage pile</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rubbage-pile</rdg>
          </app>
in the back yard where they keep the old boots, and rags, and pieces of bottles, and wore-out tin

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2897"/>
things

          <ptr target="#l12660" type="alt" xml:id="te2897"/>
, and all such truck, and scratched around and found an old tin

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5882"/>
washpan

          <app from="pr5882" n="313.9 (608.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7949">
            <lem wit="MS2">washpan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
wash-

              <lb/>
pan

            </rdg>
          </app>
and stopped up the holes as well as we could, to bake the pie in, and took it down cellar and stole it full of flour, and started

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5883"/>
for

          <app from="pr5883" n="313.13 (608.6)" type="e" xml:id="la7950">
            <lem wit="A">for</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">to</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5884"/>
breakfast,

          <app from="pr5884" n="313.13 (608.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7951">
            <lem wit="MS2">breakfast,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
breakfast

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and found a couple of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5885"/>
shingle nails

          <app from="pr5885" n="313.14–15 (608.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la7952">
            <lem wit="MS2">shingle nails</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shingle-nails</rdg>
          </app>
that Tom said would be handy for a prisoner to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2898"/>
scrabble

          <ptr target="#l12662" type="alt" xml:id="te2898"/>
his name and sorrows on the dungeon walls with, and dropped one of them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2899"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l12664" type="alt" xml:id="te2899"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5887"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5887" n="313.17 (608.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la7955">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally’s apron pocket which was hanging on a chair, and t’other we stuck in the band of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5888"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5888" n="313.19 (608.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la7956">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas’s hat, which was on the bureau, because we heard the children say their pa and ma was going to the runaway nigger’s house this morning, and then went to breakfast, and Tom dropped the pewter spoon

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5889"/>
in

          <app from="pr5889" n="313.22 (609.9)" type="e" xml:id="la7957">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">into</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5890"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5890" n="313.22 (609.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7958">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas’s coat pocket, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5891"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5891" n="313.22 (609.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7959">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally wasn’t come yet, so we had to wait a little while.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73540">
And when she come she was hot, and red, and cross, and couldn’t hardly wait for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5892"/>
blessing,

          <app from="pr5892" n="313.25 (610.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7960">
            <lem wit="MS2">blessing,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">blessing;</rdg>
          </app>
and then she went to sluicing out coffee with one hand and cracking the handiest child’s head with her thimble with the other, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73550">
“I’ve hunted high, and I’ve hunted low, and it does beat all, what

          <hi rend="italic">has</hi>
become of your other shirt.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73555">
My heart fell down amongst my lungs and livers and things, and a hard piece of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2900"/>
corn-crust

          <ptr target="#l12666" type="alt" xml:id="te2900"/>
started down my throat after it and got met on the road with a cough and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2901"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l12668" type="alt" xml:id="te2901"/>
shot across the table and took

          <pb n="314" xml:id="pb0314"/>
one of the children in the eye and curled him up like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5893"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2902"/>
fishing-worm

          <ptr target="#l12670" type="alt" xml:id="te2902"/>
          <app from="pr5893" n="314.1 (611.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la7961">
            <lem wit="A">fishing-worm</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
fishing-

              <lb/>
worm

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and let a cry out of him the size of a war-whoop, and Tom he turned kinder blue around the gills, and it all amounted to a considerable state of things for about a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2903"/>
quarter of

          <ptr target="#l12672" type="alt" xml:id="te2903"/>
a minute or as much as that, and I would a sold out for half price if there was a bidder. But after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5894"/>
that,

          <app from="pr5894" n="314.6 (611.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7962">
            <lem wit="MS2">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
we was all right again—it was the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2904"/>
sudden

          <ptr target="#l12674" type="alt" xml:id="te2904"/>
surprise of it that knocked us so kind of cold. Uncle Silas

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5895"/>
he

          <app from="pr5895" n="314.7 (611.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7963">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de7964">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73606">
“It’s most uncommon curious, I can’t understand it. I know perfectly well I took it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2905"/>
          <hi rend="italic">
off

            <ptr target="#l12676" type="alt" xml:id="te2905"/>
          </hi>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5896"/>
because—

          <app from="pr5896" n="314.9 (611.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la7965">
            <lem wit="MS2">because—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">because——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73621">
“Because you hain’t got but one

          <hi rend="italic">on.</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5897"/>
Just

          <app from="pr5897" n="314.10 (612.2)" type="e" xml:id="la7966">
            <lem wit="A">Just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Jest</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">listen</hi>
at the man!

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
know you took it off, and know it by a better way than your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5898"/>
wool-gethering

          <app from="pr5898" n="314.11 (612.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la7967">
            <lem wit="A">wool-gethering</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
wool-

              <lb/>
gethering

            </rdg>
          </app>
memory, too, because it was on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5899"/>
clo’es line

          <app from="pr5899" n="314.12 (612.8)" type="e" xml:id="la7968">
            <lem wit="C">clo’es line</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">clothes line</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">clo’es-line</rdg>
          </app>
yesterday—I see it there myself. But it’s gone—that’s the long and the short of it, and you’ll just have to change to a red

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5900"/>
flann’l

          <app from="pr5900" n="314.14 (612.12)" type="e" xml:id="la7969">
            <lem wit="A">flann’l</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">flannel</rdg>
          </app>
one till I can get time to make a new one. And it’ll be

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2906"/>
the third

          <ptr target="#l12678" type="alt" xml:id="te2906"/>
I’ve made in two years; it just keeps a body on the jump to keep you in shirts; and whatever you do manage to

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
with ’m all, is more’n

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
can make out. A body’d think you

          <hi rend="italic">would</hi>
learn to take some sort of care of ’em, at your time of life.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73681">
“I know it, Sally, and I do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5901"/>
try,

          <app from="pr5901" n="314.20 (613.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7970">
            <lem wit="MS2">try,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
try

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all I can. But it oughtn’t to be altogether my fault, because you know I don’t see them

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2907"/>
nor

          <ptr target="#l12680" type="alt" xml:id="te2907"/>
have nothing to do with them except when they’re on me; and I don’t believe I’ve ever lost one of them

          <hi rend="italic">off</hi>
of me.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73699">
“Well, it ain’t

          <hi rend="italic">your</hi>
fault if you haven’t, Silas—you’d a done it if you could, I reckon. And the shirt ain’t all that’s gone, nuther. Ther’s a spoon gone; and

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
ain’t all.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2908"/>
There was ten, and now ther’s only nine.

          <ptr target="#l12682" type="alt" xml:id="te2908"/>
The calf got the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5902"/>
shirt,

          <app from="pr5902" n="314.27 (614.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7971">
            <lem wit="MS2">shirt,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
shirt

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I reckon, but the calf never took the spoon,

          <hi rend="italic">that’s</hi>
certain.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73723">“Why, what else is gone, Sally?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73725">
“Ther’s six

          <hi rend="italic">candles</hi>
gone—that’s what. The rats could a got the candles, and I reckon they did; I wonder they don’t walk off with the whole place, the way you’re always going to stop their holes and don’t do it; and if they warn’t fools they’d sleep in your hair, Silas—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5903"/>
          <hi rend="italic">you’d</hi>
          <app from="pr5903" n="314.34 (615.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7972">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">you’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
never find it out; but you can’t lay the

          <hi rend="italic">spoon</hi>
on the rats, and that I

          <hi rend="italic">know.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73748">
“Well, Sally, I’m in fault, and I acknowledge it; I’ve been remiss; but I won’t let

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2909"/>
to-morrow

          <ptr target="#l12684" type="alt" xml:id="te2909"/>
go by without stopping up them holes.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73754">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5904"/>
O

          <app from="pr5904" n="314.38 (615.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7973">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, I wouldn’t hurry, next year’ll do.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0003"/>
Matilda Angelina

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5905"/>
Araminta

          <app from="pr5905" n="314.38 (615.13)" type="e" xml:id="la7974">
            <lem wit="A">Araminta</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Araminta Annunciana</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">Phelps</hi>
!

          <ptr target="#as0249" type="an" xml:id="tr0003"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73779">
          <pb n="315" xml:id="pb0315"/>
Whack comes the thimble, and the child

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5906"/>
snatches

          <app from="pr5906" n="315.1 (615.16)" type="e" xml:id="la7975">
            <lem wit="A">snatches</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gets</rdg>
          </app>
her claws out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5907"/>
sugar bowl

          <app from="pr5907" n="315.2 (616.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7976">
            <lem wit="MS2">sugar bowl</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sugar-bowl</rdg>
          </app>
without fooling around any. Just then, the nigger woman steps onto the passage, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73798">“Missus, dey’s a sheet gone.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73800">
“A

          <hi rend="italic">sheet</hi>
gone! Well, for the land’s sake!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73805">
“I’ll stop up them holes

          <hi rend="italic">to-day,</hi>
” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5908"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5908" n="315.6 (616.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la7977">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncles</rdg>
          </app>
Silas, looking sorrowful.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73818">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5909"/>
O

          <app from="pr5909" n="315.8 (616.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7978">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
shet up!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2910"/>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5910"/>
Spose

          <app from="pr5910" n="315.8 (616.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la7979">
            <lem wit="MS2">Spose</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">spose</rdg>
          </app>
the rats took the

          <hi rend="italic">sheet?</hi>
          <ptr target="#l12686" type="alt" xml:id="te2910"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Where’s</hi>
it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2911"/>
gone, Lize?”

          <ptr target="#l12688" type="alt" xml:id="te2911"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73851">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2912"/>
Clah

          <ptr target="#l12690" type="alt" xml:id="te2912"/>
to goodness I hain’t no notion, Miss Sally. She wuz on de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5911"/>
clo’s line

          <app from="pr5911" n="315.12 (617.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la7980">
            <lem wit="MS2">clo’s line</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">clo’s-line</rdg>
          </app>
yistiddy, but she done gone; she ain’ dah no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5912"/>
mo’,

          <app from="pr5912" n="315.13 (617.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la7981">
            <lem wit="MS2">mo’,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mo,’</rdg>
          </app>
now.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73875">
“I reckon the world

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
coming to an end. I

          <hi rend="italic">never</hi>
see the beat of it, in all my born days. A shirt, and a sheet, and a spoon, and six

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5913"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2913"/>
can—

          <app from="pr5913" n="315.18 (617.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la7982">
            <lem wit="MS2">can—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">can——</rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#l12692" type="alt" xml:id="te2913"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73893">“Missus,” comes a young yaller wench, “dey’s a brass cannelstick miss’n.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73895">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2914"/>
“Cler out

          <ptr target="#l12694" type="alt" xml:id="te2914"/>
from here, you hussy,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5914"/>
er

          <app from="pr5914" n="315.23 (617.14)" type="e" xml:id="la7983">
            <lem wit="A">er</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">or</rdg>
          </app>
I’ll take a skillet to ye!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73908">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y31501">
            <graphic url="y31501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
“

              <hi rend="smallcaps">missus, dey’s a sheet gone.</hi>
”

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73915">
Well, she was just a biling. I begun to lay for a chance; I reckoned I would sneak out and go for the woods till the weather moderated. She kept

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5915"/>
a-raging

          <app from="pr5915" n="315.28 (618.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7984">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-raging</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a raging</rdg>
          </app>
right along, running her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2915"/>
insurrection

          <ptr target="#l12696" type="alt" xml:id="te2915"/>
all by herself, and everybody else mighty meek and quiet; and at last

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5916"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5916" n="315.32 (618.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la7985">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas, looking kind of foolish, fishes up that spoon out of his pocket. She stopped, with her mouth open and her hands up;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2916"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l12698" type="alt" xml:id="te2916"/>
as for me, I wished I was in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2917"/>
Jeruslem

          <ptr target="#l12700" type="alt" xml:id="te2917"/>
or somewheres. But not long; because she says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73946">
“It’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5917"/>
          <hi rend="italic">just</hi>
          <app from="pr5917" n="315.36 (619.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7986">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">just</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">jest</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
as I expected. So you had it in your pocket all the time; and like as not you’ve got the other things there, too. How’d it get there?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e73959">
“I reely don’t know, Sally,”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2918"/>
he says,

          <ptr target="#l12702" type="alt" xml:id="te2918"/>
kind of apologizing, “or you

          <pb n="316" xml:id="pb0316"/>
know I would tell. I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5918"/>
a-studying

          <app from="pr5918" n="316.1 (619.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la7987">
            <lem wit="A">a-studying</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <lb/>
studying

            </rdg>
          </app>
over my text in

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0004"/>
Acts

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5919"/>
seventeen

          <app from="pr5919" n="316.1 (619.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7988">
            <lem wit="MS2">seventeen</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Seventeen</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#as0250" type="an" xml:id="tr0004"/>
, before breakfast, and I reckon I put it in there, not noticing, meaning to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2919"/>
put my Testament

          <ptr target="#l12704" type="alt" xml:id="te2919"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2920"/>
in, and it

          <ptr target="#l12706" type="alt" xml:id="te2920"/>
must be so, because my Testament

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5920"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr5920" n="316.4 (619.15)" type="e" xml:id="la7989">
            <lem wit="A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2921"/>
in, but I’ll

          <ptr target="#l12708" type="alt" xml:id="te2921"/>
go and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2922"/>
see,

          <ptr target="#l12710" type="alt" xml:id="te2922"/>
and if the Testament

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2923"/>
is

          <ptr target="#l12712" type="alt" xml:id="te2923"/>
where I had it, I’ll know I didn’t put it in, and that will show that I laid the Testament down and took up the spoon,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5921"/>
and—

          <app from="pr5921" n="316.6 (620.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la7990">
            <lem wit="MS2">and—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">and——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74026">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5922"/>
O

          <app from="pr5922" n="316.7 (620.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7991">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, for the land’s sake! Give a body a rest! Go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5923"/>
’long,

          <app from="pr5923" n="316.7 (620.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la7992">
            <lem wit="MS2">’long,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’long</rdg>
          </app>
now, the whole kit and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5924"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2924"/>
biling

          <ptr target="#l12714" type="alt" xml:id="te2924"/>
          <app from="pr5924" n="316.8 (620.7)" type="e" xml:id="la7993">
            <lem wit="A">biling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">bilin’</rdg>
          </app>
of ye; and don’t come nigh me again till I’ve got back my peace of mind.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74055">
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5925"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2925"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
d

          <ptr target="#l12716" type="alt" xml:id="te2925"/>
          <app from="pr5925" n="316.10 (620.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la7994">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2926"/>
a heard

          <ptr target="#l12718" type="alt" xml:id="te2926"/>
her, if she’d a said it to herself, let alone speaking it out; and I’d a got up and obeyed her, if I’d a been dead. As we was passing through the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5926"/>
setting room

          <app from="pr5926" n="316.12 (620.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7995">
            <lem wit="MS2">setting room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">setting-room</rdg>
          </app>
, the old man

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5927"/>
he took

          <app from="pr5927" n="316.12 (621.1)" type="e" xml:id="la7996">
            <lem wit="A">he took</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">took</rdg>
          </app>
up his hat, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5928"/>
shingle nail

          <app from="pr5928" n="316.13 (621.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la7997">
            <lem wit="MS2">shingle nail</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shingle-nail</rdg>
          </app>
fell out on the floor, and he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2927"/>
just merely

          <ptr target="#l12720" type="alt" xml:id="te2927"/>
picked it up and laid it on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5929"/>
mantel shelf

          <app from="pr5929" n="316.14 (621.4–5)" type="hc" xml:id="la7998">
            <lem wit="MS2">mantel shelf</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mantel-shelf</rdg>
          </app>
, and never said nothing, and went out. Tom see him do it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2928"/>
and remembered about the spoon,

          <ptr target="#l12722" type="alt" xml:id="te2928"/>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74116">
“Well, it ain’t no use to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2929"/>
send things by

          <ptr target="#l12724" type="alt" xml:id="te2929"/>
          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
no more, he ain’t reliable.” Then he says: “But he done us a good turn with the spoon, anyway, without knowing it, and so we’ll go and do him one without

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
knowing it—stop up his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5930"/>
rat holes

          <app from="pr5930" n="316.20 (621.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la7999">
            <lem wit="MS2">rat holes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rat-holes</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74135">
There was a noble good lot of them, down cellar, and it took us a whole hour, but we done the job tight and good, and ship-shape. Then we heard steps on the stairs, and blowed out our light, and hid; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5931"/>
here

          <app from="pr5931" n="316.24 (622.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8000">
            <lem wit="A">here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">lo and beholes, here</rdg>
          </app>
comes the old man, with a candle in one hand and a bundle of stuff in t’other, looking as absent-minded as year before last. He went a mooning around, first to one

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5932"/>
rat hole

          <app from="pr5932" n="316.26 (622.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8001">
            <lem wit="MS2">rat hole</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rat-hole</rdg>
          </app>
and then another, till he’d been to them all. Then he stood about five minutes, picking tallow-drip off of his candle and thinking. Then he turns off slow and dreamy towards the stairs, saying:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74154">
“Well, for the life of me I can’t remember when I done it. I could show

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5933"/>
her, now,

          <app from="pr5933" n="316.31 (623.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8002">
            <lem wit="MS2">her, now,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
her

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
now

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
that I warn’t to blame on account of the rats. But never mind—let it go. I reckon it wouldn’t do no good.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74164">
And so he went on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5934"/>
a-mumbling

          <app from="pr5934" n="316.33 (623.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la8003">
            <lem wit="C">a-mumbling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <lb/>
mumbling

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">a mumbling</rdg>
          </app>
up stairs, and then we left. He was a mighty nice old man. And always is.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74178">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2930"/>
Tom

          <ptr target="#l12726" type="alt" xml:id="te2930"/>
was a good deal bothered about what to do for a spoon, but he said we’d got to have it; so he took

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2931"/>
a think

          <ptr target="#l12728" type="alt" xml:id="te2931"/>
. When he had ciphered it out, he told me how we was to do; then we went and waited around the spoon-basket till we see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5935"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5935" n="316.38 (624.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8004">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally coming, and then

          <pb n="317" xml:id="pb0317"/>
Tom went to counting the spoons and laying them out to one side, and I slid one of them up my sleeve, and Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74198">
“Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5936"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr5936" n="317.3 (624.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8005">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally, there ain’t but nine spoons,

          <hi rend="italic">yet.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74211">She says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74213">“Go ’long to your play, and don’t bother me. I know better, I counted ’m myself.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74215">
“Well, I’ve counted them twice,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5937"/>
aunty

          <app from="pr5937" n="317.7 (625.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8006">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunty</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunty</rdg>
          </app>
, and

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
can’t make but nine.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74228">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2932"/>
She

          <ptr target="#l12730" type="alt" xml:id="te2932"/>
looked out of all patience, but of course she come to count—anybody would.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74233">
“I declare to gracious ther’

          <hi rend="italic">ain’t</hi>
but nine!” she says. “Why, what in the world—plague

          <hi rend="italic">take</hi>
the things, I’ll count ’m again.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74241">So I slipped back the one I had, and when she got done counting, she says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74243">
“Hang the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2933"/>
troublesome rubbage,

          <ptr target="#l12732" type="alt" xml:id="te2933"/>
ther’s

          <hi rend="italic">ten</hi>
, now!” and she looked huffy and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5938"/>
bothered

          <app from="pr5938" n="317.16 (626.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8007">
            <lem wit="A">bothered</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">flusticated</rdg>
          </app>
both. But Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74261">
“Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5939"/>
aunty

          <app from="pr5939" n="317.17 (626.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8008">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunty</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunty</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t think there’s ten.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74274">
“You

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5940"/>
numscull

          <app from="pr5940" n="317.18 (626.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8009">
            <lem wit="MS2">numscull</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">numskull</rdg>
          </app>
, didn’t you see me

          <hi rend="italic">count</hi>
’m?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74287">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y31701">
            <graphic url="y31701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">in a tearing way</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74293">
          <pb n="318" xml:id="pb0318"/>
“I know,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5941"/>
but—

          <app from="pr5941" n="318.1 (626.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8010">
            <lem wit="MS2">but—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">but——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74304">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2934"/>
“Well, I’ll

          <ptr target="#l12734" type="alt" xml:id="te2934"/>
count ’m

          <hi rend="italic">again.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74312">
So I smouched one, and they come out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5942"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2935"/>
nine,

          <ptr target="#l12736" type="alt" xml:id="te2935"/>
          <app from="pr5942" n="318.3 (626.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8011">
            <lem wit="MS2">nine,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
nine

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
same as the other time. Well, she

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
in a tearing way—just a trembling all over, she was so mad. But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5943"/>
she counted,

          <app from="pr5943" n="318.5 (627.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8012">
            <lem wit="MS2">she counted,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
she counted

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2936"/>
and counted, till she got that addled she’d start to count-in the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2937"/>
          <hi rend="italic">basket</hi>
          <ptr target="#l12740" type="alt" xml:id="te2937"/>
for a spoon,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5944"/>
sometimes:

          <app from="pr5944" n="318.6 (627.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8013">
            <lem wit="MS2">sometimes:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sometimes;</rdg>
          </app>
and so, three times they

          <ptr target="#l12738" type="alt" xml:id="te2936"/>
come out right, and three times they come out wrong. Then she grabbed up the basket and slammed it across the house and knocked the cat galley-west; and she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2938"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l12742" type="alt" xml:id="te2938"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5945"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2939"/>
“cle’r

          <app from="pr5945" n="318.9 (627.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8014">
            <lem wit="C">“cle’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">“clear</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">cle’r</rdg>
          </app>
out and let her have some peace, and if we come bothering around her again betwixt that and dinner, she’d skin

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5946"/>
us.”

          <app from="pr5946" n="318.11 (627.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8015">
            <lem wit="MS2">us.”</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
us.

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12744" type="alt" xml:id="te2939"/>
So we had the odd spoon; and dropped it in her apron

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2940"/>
pocket whilst she was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5947"/>
a-giving

          <app from="pr5947" n="318.12 (628.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8016">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-giving</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a giving</rdg>
          </app>
us our sailing-orders, and

          <ptr target="#l12746" type="alt" xml:id="te2940"/>
Jim got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5948"/>
it,

          <app from="pr5948" n="318.13 (628.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8017">
            <lem wit="MS2">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all right, along with her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2941"/>
shingle-nail, before noon.

          <ptr target="#l12748" type="alt" xml:id="te2941"/>
We was very well satisfied with this business, and Tom allowed it was worth twice the trouble it took, because he said

          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
she couldn’t ever count them spoons twice alike again to save her life; and wouldn’t believe she’d counted them right, if she

          <hi rend="italic">did;</hi>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2942"/>
said that

          <ptr target="#l12750" type="alt" xml:id="te2942"/>
after she’d

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2943"/>
about

          <ptr target="#l12752" type="alt" xml:id="te2943"/>
counted her head off, for the next three days, he judged she’d give it up and offer to kill anybody that wanted her to ever count them any more.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74417">
So we put the sheet back on the line, that night, and stole one out of her closet; and kept on

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2944"/>
putting

          <ptr target="#l12754" type="alt" xml:id="te2944"/>
it back and stealing it again, for a couple of days, till she didn’t know how many sheets she had, any more,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2945"/>
and said

          <ptr target="#l12756" type="alt" xml:id="te2945"/>
she didn’t

          <hi rend="italic">care</hi>
, and warn’t agoing to bullyrag the rest of her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2946"/>
soul

          <ptr target="#l12758" type="alt" xml:id="te2946"/>
out about it, and wouldn’t count them again not to save her life,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2947"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l12760" type="alt" xml:id="te2947"/>
druther die first.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74439">
So we was all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5949"/>
right,

          <app from="pr5949" n="318.27 (630.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8018">
            <lem wit="MS2">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, as to the shirt and the sheet and the spoon and the candles, by the help of the calf and the rats and the mixed-up counting; and as to the candlestick, it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2948"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l12762" type="alt" xml:id="te2948"/>
no consequence, it would blow over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5950"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr5950" n="318.30 (630.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8019">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74462">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2949"/>
But

          <ptr target="#l12764" type="alt" xml:id="te2949"/>
that pie was a job; we had no end of trouble with that pie.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2950"/>
We fixed

          <ptr target="#l12766" type="alt" xml:id="te2950"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2951"/>
it up

          <ptr target="#l12768" type="alt" xml:id="te2951"/>
away down in the woods, and cooked it there; and we got it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5951"/>
done,

          <app from="pr5951" n="318.33 (630.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8020">
            <lem wit="MS2">done,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
done

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
at last, and very satisfactory, too; but not all in one day; and we had to use up three

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5952"/>
washpans

          <app from="pr5952" n="318.34 (630.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8021">
            <lem wit="MS2">washpans</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
wash-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
pans

            </rdg>
          </app>
full of flour, before we got through, and we got burnt pretty much all over, in places, and eyes put out with the smoke; because, you see, we didn’t want nothing but a crust, and we couldn’t prop it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5953"/>
up,

          <app from="pr5953" n="318.37 (631.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8022">
            <lem wit="MS2">up,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
up

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
right, and she would always cave in. But of course we thought of the right way at last; which

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5954"/>
was,

          <app from="pr5954" n="318.38 (631.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8023">
            <lem wit="MS2">was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to

          <pb n="319" xml:id="pb0319"/>
cook the ladder, too, in the pie. So then we laid in with Jim, the second night, and tore up the sheet all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5955"/>
in

          <app from="pr5955" n="319.2 (631.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8024">
            <lem wit="A">in</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">into</rdg>
          </app>
little strings, and twisted them together, and long before daylight we had a lovely rope, that you could a hung a person with.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2952"/>
We let on it took nine months to make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5956"/>
it

          <app from="pr5956" n="319.5 (632.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8025">
            <lem wit="A">it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">the ladder</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l12770" type="alt" xml:id="te2952"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74532">
And in the forenoon we took it down to the woods, but it wouldn’t go in the pie. Being made of a whole sheet, that way, there was rope enough for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2953"/>
forty

          <ptr target="#l12772" type="alt" xml:id="te2953"/>
pies,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2954"/>
if we’d a wanted

          <ptr target="#l12774" type="alt" xml:id="te2954"/>
them, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2955"/>
plenty

          <ptr target="#l12776" type="alt" xml:id="te2955"/>
left over for soup, or sausage, or anything you choose. We could a had a whole dinner.

        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y31901">
          <graphic url="y31901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">one of his ancesters</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74553">
But we didn’t need it. All we needed was just enough for the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2956"/>
pie,

          <ptr target="#l12778" type="alt" xml:id="te2956"/>
and so we throwed the rest away.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2957"/>
We didn’t

          <ptr target="#l12780" type="alt" xml:id="te2957"/>
cook none of the pies in the washpan, afraid the solder would melt; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5957"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr5957" n="319.13 (632.19)" type="hc" xml:id="la8026">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5958"/>
he

          <app from="pr5958" n="319.13 (633.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8027">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8028">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
had a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2958"/>
noble

          <ptr target="#l12782" type="alt" xml:id="te2958"/>
brass

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5959"/>
warming pan

          <app from="pr5959" n="319.14 (633.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8029">
            <lem wit="MS2">warming pan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">warming-pan</rdg>
          </app>
which he thought considerable of, because it belonged to one of his

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0080"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5960"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2959"/>
ancesters

          <ptr target="#l12784" type="alt" xml:id="te2959"/>
          <app from="pr5960" n="319.15 (633.4)" type="e" xml:id="tv1080">
            <lem wit="A">ancesters</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anzesters</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0080" type="te" xml:id="tv0080"/>
with a long wooden handle that come over from England with William the Conqueror in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5961"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2960"/>
Mayflower

          <app from="pr5961" n="319.18 (633.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8031">
            <lem wit="MS2">Mayflower</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Mayflower</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
or one of them early ships and

          <ptr target="#l12786" type="alt" xml:id="te2960"/>
was hid away up garret with a lot of other old pots and things that was valuable, not on account of being

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5962"/>
any account,

          <app from="pr5962" n="319.22 (633.12–13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8032">
            <lem wit="MS2">any account,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
any account

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
because they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2961"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l12788" type="alt" xml:id="te2961"/>
, but on account of them being relicts, you know, and we snaked

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2962"/>
her

          <ptr target="#l12790" type="alt" xml:id="te2962"/>
out, private, and took

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2963"/>
her

          <ptr target="#l12792" type="alt" xml:id="te2963"/>
down there, but she failed on the first pies, because we didn’t know how, but she come up smiling on the last

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2964"/>
one.

          <ptr target="#l12794" type="alt" xml:id="te2964"/>
We took and lined her with dough,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2965"/>
and set her in the coals,

          <ptr target="#l12796" type="alt" xml:id="te2965"/>
and loaded her up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2966"/>
with

          <ptr target="#l12798" type="alt" xml:id="te2966"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5963"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2967"/>
rag-rope

          <ptr target="#l12800" type="alt" xml:id="te2967"/>
          <app from="pr5963" n="319.33 (634.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8033">
            <lem wit="MS2">rag-rope</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rag-

              <lb/>
rope

            </rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2968"/>
and put on a dough roof, and shut down the lid, and put hot embers on top,

          <ptr target="#l12802" type="alt" xml:id="te2968"/>
and stood off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2969"/>
five

          <ptr target="#l12804" type="alt" xml:id="te2969"/>
foot, with the long handle, cool and comfortable, and in fifteen minutes

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2970"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l12806" type="alt" xml:id="te2970"/>
turned out a pie that was a satisfaction to look at. But the person that et it would want to fetch a couple of kags of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2971"/>
toothpicks

          <ptr target="#l12808" type="alt" xml:id="te2971"/>
along, for if that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5964"/>
rope

          <pb n="320" xml:id="pb0320"/>
ladder

          <app from="pr5964" n="319.38–320.1 (634.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8034">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">rope-ladder</rdg>
          </app>
wouldn’t cramp him down to business, I don’t know

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0045"/>
nothing what I’m talking about, and lay him in enough stomach-ache to last him till next time, too.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74695">
Nat didn’t look, when we put the witch-pie in Jim’s pan; and we put the three tin plates in the bottom of the pan under the vittles; and so Jim got everything all right, and as soon as he was by himself he busted into the pie and hid the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5965"/>
rope ladder

          <app from="pr5965" n="320.7 (635.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8035">
            <lem wit="MS2">rope ladder</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
rope-

              <lb/>
ladder

            </rdg>
          </app>
inside of his straw tick, and scratched some marks on a tin plate and throwed it out of the window-hole.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0444">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXVIII.</head>
        <pb n="321" xml:id="pb0321"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74711">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y32101">
            <graphic url="y32101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5966"/>
Chapter XXXVIII.

              <app from="pr5966" n="321 title (635.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8036">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXVIII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8037">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2972"/>
Making

              <ptr target="#l12810" type="alt" xml:id="te2972"/>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3211">
            <graphic url="hf3211.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">jim’s coat of arms</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e74731">
them pens was a

          <ptr target="#mt0045" type="alt" xml:id="wn0045"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5967"/>
distressid tough

          <app from="pr5967" n="321.1–2 (636.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8038">
            <lem wit="MS2">distressid tough</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
distressid-

              <lb/>
tough

            </rdg>
          </app>
job, and so was the saw; and Jim allowed the inscription was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2973"/>
going to be

          <ptr target="#l12812" type="alt" xml:id="te2973"/>
the toughest of all.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5968"/>
That’s

          <app from="pr5968" n="321.5 (636.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8039">
            <lem wit="A">That’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">That is</rdg>
          </app>
the one which the prisoner has to scrabble on the wall. But we had to have it; Tom said we’d

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5969"/>
to:

          <app from="pr5969" n="321.9 (636.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8040">
            <lem wit="MS2">to:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">to;</rdg>
          </app>
there warn’t no case of a state prisoner not

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2974"/>
scrabbling

          <ptr target="#l12814" type="alt" xml:id="te2974"/>
his inscription to leave behind, and his coat of arms.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74771">
“Look at

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0005"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5970"/>
lady

          <app from="pr5970" n="321.13 (636.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8041">
            <lem wit="MS2">lady</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Lady</rdg>
          </app>
Jane Grey,” he says; “look at Gilford Dudley; look at old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5971"/>
Northumberland

          <ptr target="#as0251" type="an" xml:id="tr0005"/>
!

          <app from="pr5971" n="321.15 (636.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la8042">
            <lem wit="A">Northumberland!</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Northumberland.</rdg>
          </app>
Why, Huck, spose it

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5972"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr5972" n="321.16–17 (637.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8043">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
trouble?—what you going to do?—how you going to get around it? Jim’s

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to do his inscription and coat of arms. They all do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74806">Jim says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74808">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5973"/>
Why

          <app from="pr5973" n="321.22 (637.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8044">
            <lem wit="A">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">W’y</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5974"/>
mars

          <app from="pr5974" n="321.22 (637.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8045">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5975"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2975"/>
hain’t got no

          <ptr target="#l12816" type="alt" xml:id="te2975"/>
          <app from="pr5975" n="321.22 (637.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la8046">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t got no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’ got no</rdg>
          </app>
coat

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2976"/>
o’ arms

          <ptr target="#l12818" type="alt" xml:id="te2976"/>
; I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5976"/>
hain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2977"/>
got

          <ptr target="#l12820" type="alt" xml:id="te2977"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2978"/>
nuffn

          <ptr target="#l12822" type="alt" xml:id="te2978"/>
          <app from="pr5976" n="321.22 (637.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la8047">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t got nuffn</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’ got nuffn</rdg>
          </app>
but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5977"/>
dish-yer

          <app from="pr5977" n="321.23 (637.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8048">
            <lem wit="MS2">dish-yer</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
dish-

              <lb/>
yer

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2979"/>
ole

          <ptr target="#l12824" type="alt" xml:id="te2979"/>
shirt, en you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2980"/>
knows

          <ptr target="#l12826" type="alt" xml:id="te2980"/>
I got to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2981"/>
keep

          <ptr target="#l12828" type="alt" xml:id="te2981"/>
de journal on dat.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74878">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5978"/>
O

          <app from="pr5978" n="321.24 (637.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8049">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, you don’t understand, Jim; a coat of arms is very different.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74888">
“Well,” I says, “Jim’s right, anyway, when he says he hain’t got no coat of arms, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5979"/>
he

          <app from="pr5979" n="321.26 (638.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8050">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">haint</rdg>
          </app>
hain’t.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74898">
“I reckon

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
knowed that,” Tom says, “but you bet he’ll have one before he goes out of this—because he’s going out

          <hi rend="italic">right</hi>
, and there ain’t going to be no flaws in his record.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74906">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2982"/>
So

          <ptr target="#l12830" type="alt" xml:id="te2982"/>
whilst

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2983"/>
me and Jim

          <ptr target="#l12832" type="alt" xml:id="te2983"/>
filed away at the pens on a brickbat apiece, Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5980"/>
a making

          <app from="pr5980" n="321.31 (638.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8051">
            <lem wit="A">a making</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">making</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2984"/>
his’n

          <ptr target="#l12834" type="alt" xml:id="te2984"/>
out of the brass and I making mine out of the

          <pb n="322" xml:id="pb0322"/>
spoon, Tom set to work to think out the

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0006"/>
coat of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2985"/>
arms

          <ptr target="#as0252" type="an" xml:id="tr0006"/>
.

          <ptr target="#l12836" type="alt" xml:id="te2985"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5981"/>
By and by

          <app from="pr5981" n="322.1 (638.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8052">
            <lem wit="MS2">By and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">By-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5982"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr5982" n="322.2 (638.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8053">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he had</rdg>
          </app>
struck so many good ones he didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2986"/>
hardly

          <ptr target="#l12838" type="alt" xml:id="te2986"/>
know which to take, but there was one which he reckoned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5983"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr5983" n="322.3 (639.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8054">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he would</rdg>
          </app>
decide on. He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e74967">
“On the scutcheon we’ll have a bend

          <hi rend="italic">or</hi>
in the dexter base, a saltire

          <hi rend="italic">murrey</hi>
in the fess, with a dog,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2987"/>
couchant

          <ptr target="#l12840" type="alt" xml:id="te2987"/>
, for common charge, and under his foot a chain embattled, for slavery, with a chevron

          <hi rend="italic">vert</hi>
in a chief engrailed, and three invected lines on a field

          <hi rend="italic">azure</hi>
, with the nombril points rampant on a dancette indented; crest, a runaway nigger,

          <hi rend="italic">sable</hi>
, with his bundle over his shoulder on a bar

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5984"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2988"/>
sinister;

          <app from="pr5984" n="322.10 (640.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8055">
            <lem wit="MS2">sinister;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sinister:</rdg>
          </app>
and a

          <ptr target="#l12842" type="alt" xml:id="te2988"/>
couple of gules for supporters, which is you and me; motto,

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0007"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Maggiore fretta, minore atto</hi>
          <ptr target="#as0253" type="an" xml:id="tr0007"/>
. Got it out of a book—means, the more haste, the less speed.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75007">“Geewhillikins,” I says, “but what does the rest of it mean?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75009">“We ain’t got no time to bother over that,” he says, “we got to dig in like all git-out.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75011">
“Well, anyway,” I says, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5985"/>
what’s

          <app from="pr5985" n="322.16 (640.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8056">
            <lem wit="A">what’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">What’s</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">some</hi>
of it? What’s a fess?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75023">
“A fess

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2989"/>
—a fess

          <ptr target="#l12844" type="alt" xml:id="te2989"/>
is—

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
don’t need to know what a fess

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5986"/>
is.

          <app from="pr5986" n="322.17 (640.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8057">
            <lem wit="A">is.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">is:</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2990"/>
I’ll

          <ptr target="#l12846" type="alt" xml:id="te2990"/>
show him how to make it when he gets to it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75044">
“Shucks,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5987"/>
Tom,” I says, “I

          <app from="pr5987" n="322.19 (641.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8058">
            <lem wit="A">Tom,” I says, “I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Tom, I</rdg>
          </app>
think you might tell a person. What’s a bar sinister?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75054">
“Oh,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
don’t know. But he’s got to have it. All the nobility does.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75059">That was just his way. If it didn’t suit him to explain a thing to you, he wouldn’t do it. You might pump at him a week it wouldn’t make no difference.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75061">
He’d got all that coat of arms business fixed, so now he started in to finish up the rest

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2991"/>
of that

          <ptr target="#l12848" type="alt" xml:id="te2991"/>
part of the work, which was to plan out a mournful inscription—said Jim got to have one, like they all done. He made up a lot, and wrote them out on a paper, and read them off,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5988"/>
so:

          <app from="pr5988" n="322.29 (643.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8059">
            <lem wit="C">
so:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8060">extra line space</note>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
so:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8061">no extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75079">
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2992"/>
1.

            <hi rend="italic">Here</hi>
            <ptr target="#l12850" type="alt" xml:id="te2992"/>
            <hi rend="italic">a captive heart busted.</hi>
          </p>
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75086">
2.

            <hi rend="italic">Here a poor prisoner, forsook by the world and friends, fretted out his sorrowful life.</hi>
          </p>
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75090">
3.

            <hi rend="italic">Here a lonely heart broke, and a worn spirit went to its rest, after</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5989"/>
            <hi rend="italic">thirty seven</hi>
            <app from="pr5989" n="322.34 (643.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8062">
              <lem wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="italic">thirty seven</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">
thirty-

                  <lb/>
seven

                </hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="italic">years of</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5990"/>
            <hi rend="italic">solitary</hi>
            <app from="pr5990" n="322.34 (643.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8063">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">solitary</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="italic">solitry</hi>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="italic">captivity.</hi>
          </p>
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75118">
4.

            <hi rend="italic">Here, homeless and friendless, after thirty-seven years of bitter captivity, perished a noble stranger, natural son of</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5991"/>
            <hi rend="italic">Louis XIV</hi>
            <app from="pr5991" n="322.36 (644.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8064">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">Louis XIV.</hi>
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8065">extra line space</note>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="italic">Louis XIV.</hi>
                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8066">no extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
.

          </p>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75136">
Tom’s voice trembled,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2993"/>
whilst

          <ptr target="#l12852" type="alt" xml:id="te2993"/>
he was reading them, and he most

          <pb n="323" xml:id="pb0323"/>
broke down. When he got done, he couldn’t no way make up his mind which one

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2994"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l12854" type="alt" xml:id="te2994"/>
Jim to scrabble

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5992"/>
onto

          <app from="pr5992" n="323.2 (644.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8067">
            <lem wit="A">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on</rdg>
          </app>
the wall, they was all so good; but at last he allowed he would let him scrabble them all on. Jim said it would take him a year to scrabble such a lot of truck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5993"/>
onto

          <app from="pr5993" n="323.4 (644.15)" type="e" xml:id="la8068">
            <lem wit="A">onto</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">on</rdg>
          </app>
the logs with a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2995"/>
nail,

          <ptr target="#l12856" type="alt" xml:id="te2995"/>
and he didn’t know how to make letters, besides; but Tom said he would block them out for him, and then he wouldn’t have nothing to do but just follow the lines. Then pretty soon he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75170">
“Come to think, the logs ain’t agoing to do; they don’t have log walls in a dungeon: we got to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2996"/>
dig

          <ptr target="#l12858" type="alt" xml:id="te2996"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2997"/>
the inscriptions

          <ptr target="#l12860" type="alt" xml:id="te2997"/>
into a rock. We’ll fetch a rock.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75179">
Jim said the rock was worse than the logs; he said it would take him such a pison long time to dig them into a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5994"/>
rock,

          <app from="pr5994" n="323.13 (645.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la8069">
            <lem wit="A">rock,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rock, that</rdg>
          </app>
he wouldn’t ever get out. But Tom said he would let me help him do it. Then he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2998"/>
took a look

          <ptr target="#l12862" type="alt" xml:id="te2998"/>
to see how me and Jim was getting along with the pens. It was most pesky tedious hard work and slow, and didn’t give my hands no show to get well of the sores, and we didn’t seem to make no headway, hardly. So Tom says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75193">
“I know how to fix it. We got to have a rock for the coat of arms and mournful inscriptions, and we can kill two birds with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg2999"/>
that

          <ptr target="#l12864" type="alt" xml:id="te2999"/>
same rock. There’s a gaudy big grindstone down at the mill, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3000"/>
we’ll smouch it, and

          <ptr target="#l12866" type="alt" xml:id="te3000"/>
carve the things on it, and file out the pens and the saw on it, too.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75203">
It warn’t no slouch of an idea;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3001"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l12868" type="alt" xml:id="te3001"/>
it warn’t no slouch of a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5995"/>
grindstone,

          <app from="pr5995" n="323.25 (647.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8070">
            <lem wit="MS2">grindstone,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
grindstone

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5996"/>
nuther

          <app from="pr5996" n="323.25 (647.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8071">
            <lem wit="A">nuther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">neither</rdg>
          </app>
; but we allowed we’d tackle it. It warn’t quite midnight, yet, so we cleared out for the mill, leaving Jim at work. We smouched the grindstone, and set out to roll

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5997"/>
her

          <app from="pr5997" n="323.27 (647.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8072">
            <lem wit="A">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
homè, but it was a most nation tough job. Sometimes, do what we could, we couldn’t keep

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5998"/>
her

          <app from="pr5998" n="323.29 (647.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8073">
            <lem wit="A">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
from falling over, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr5999"/>
she

          <app from="pr5999" n="323.29 (647.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8074">
            <lem wit="A">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
come mighty near mashing us, every time. Tom said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="nr6000"/>
she

          <app from="nr6000" n="323.30 (648.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8075">
            <lem wit="A">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
was going to get one of us, sure, before we got through. We got her half way; and then we was plumb played out, and most

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3002"/>
drownded

          <ptr target="#l12870" type="alt" xml:id="te3002"/>
with sweat. We see it warn’t no use, we got to go and fetch Jim.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6001"/>
So he

          <app from="pr6001" n="323.33 (648.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8076">
            <lem wit="A">So he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">He</rdg>
          </app>
raised up his bed and slid the chain off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3003"/>
of

          <ptr target="#l12872" type="alt" xml:id="te3003"/>
the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3004"/>
bed-leg

          <ptr target="#l12874" type="alt" xml:id="te3004"/>
, and wrapt it round and round his neck, and we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3005"/>
crawled out through our hole and

          <ptr target="#l12876" type="alt" xml:id="te3005"/>
down there, and Jim and me laid into that grindstone and walked

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6002"/>
her

          <app from="pr6002" n="323.36 (648.15)" type="e" xml:id="la8077">
            <lem wit="A">her</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
along like nothing; and Tom

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3006"/>
superintended.

          <ptr target="#l12878" type="alt" xml:id="te3006"/>
He could out-superintend any boy I ever see. He knowed how to do everything.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75296">
          <pb n="324" xml:id="pb0324"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y32401">
            <graphic url="y32401.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">a tough job</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75303">
Our hole was pretty big, but it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3007"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l12880" type="alt" xml:id="te3007"/>
big enough to get the grindstone through; but Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6003"/>
he

          <app from="pr6003" n="324.2 (649.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8078">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8079">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
took the pick and soon made it big enough. Then Tom marked out them things on it with the nail, and set

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3008"/>
Jim

          <ptr target="#l12882" type="alt" xml:id="te3008"/>
to work on them, with the nail for a chisel and an iron bolt from the rubbage in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6004"/>
lean-to

          <app from="pr6004" n="324.5 (649.12–13)" type="e" xml:id="la8080">
            <lem wit="A">lean-to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
lean-

              <lb/>
to

            </rdg>
          </app>
for a hammer, and told him to work till the rest of his candle quit on him, and then he could go to bed, and hide the grindstone

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3009"/>
under

          <ptr target="#l12884" type="alt" xml:id="te3009"/>
his straw tick and sleep on it. Then we helped him fix his chain

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6005"/>
back,

          <app from="pr6005" n="324.8 (650.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8081">
            <lem wit="MS2">back,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
back

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
on the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6006"/>
bedleg

          <app from="pr6006" n="324.8 (650.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8082">
            <lem wit="MS2">bedleg</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">bed-leg</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3010"/>
and was

          <ptr target="#l12886" type="alt" xml:id="te3010"/>
ready for bed ourselves. But Tom thought of something, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75358">“You got any spiders in here, Jim?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75360">
“No, sah, thanks to goodness I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6007"/>
hain’t

          <app from="pr6007" n="324.11 (650.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8083">
            <lem wit="A">hain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">haint</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6008"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6008" n="324.11 (650.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8084">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75378">“All right, we’ll get you some.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75380">
“But bless you, honey, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6009"/>
doan

          <app from="pr6009" n="324.13 (650.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8085">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
none. I’s afeard un um. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6010"/>
jis’ ’s

          <app from="pr6010" n="324.13 (651.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8086">
            <lem wit="A">jis’ ’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jis’ as</rdg>
          </app>
soon have

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6011"/>
rattlesnakes

          <app from="pr6011" n="324.14 (651.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8087">
            <lem wit="A">rattlesnakes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a rattlesnake</rdg>
          </app>
aroun’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75409">Tom thought a minute or two, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75412">
“It’s a good idea. And I reckon it’s been done. It

          <hi rend="italic">must</hi>
a been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6012"/>
done:

          <app from="pr6012" n="324.16 (651.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8088">
            <lem wit="MS2">done:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">done;</rdg>
          </app>
it stands to reason. Yes, it’s a prime good idea. Where could you keep it?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75425">
“Keep what,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6013"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6013" n="324.19 (651.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8089">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75435">
          <pb n="325" xml:id="pb0325"/>
“Why, a rattlesnake.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75438">
“De goodness gracious alive,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6014"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6014" n="325.2 (651.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8090">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3011"/>
Tom

          <ptr target="#l12888" type="alt" xml:id="te3011"/>
! Why, if dey was a rattlesnake to come in heah, I’d take en bust right out thoo dat log wall, I would, wid my head.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75451">“Why, Jim, you wouldn’t be afraid of it, after a little. You could tame it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75453">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Tame</hi>
it!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75458">
“Yes—easy enough. Every animal is grateful for kindness and petting, and they wouldn’t

          <hi rend="italic">think</hi>
of hurting a person that pets them. Any book will tell you that. You try—that’s all I ask; just try for two or three days. Why, you can get him so, in a little while, that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6015"/>
he’ll

          <app from="pr6015" n="325.11 (652.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8091">
            <lem wit="A">he’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he will</rdg>
          </app>
love you;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3012"/>
and sleep with you; and won’t stay away from you a minute;

          <ptr target="#l12890" type="alt" xml:id="te3012"/>
and will let you wrap him round your neck and put his head in your mouth.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75475">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Please</hi>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6016"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6016" n="325.15 (653.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8092">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom—

          <hi rend="italic">doan</hi>
’ talk so! I can’t

          <hi rend="italic">stan</hi>
’ it! He’d

          <hi rend="italic">let</hi>
me shove his head in my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6017"/>
mouf

          <app from="pr6017" n="325.16 (653.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8093">
            <lem wit="A">mouf</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">mouth</rdg>
          </app>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6018"/>
fer

          <app from="pr6018" n="325.16 (653.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8094">
            <lem wit="A">fer</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
a favor, hain’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3013"/>
it?

          <ptr target="#l12892" type="alt" xml:id="te3013"/>
I lay he’d wait a pow’ful long time ’fo’ I

          <hi rend="italic">ast</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3014"/>
him. En mo’ en dat, I doan’

          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
him to sleep wid me.”

          <ptr target="#l12894" type="alt" xml:id="te3014"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75527">
“Jim, don’t act so foolish. A prisoner’s

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to have some kind of a dumb pet, and if a rattlesnake hain’t ever been tried,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6019"/>
why

          <app from="pr6019" n="325.20 (653.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8095">
            <lem wit="MS2">why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">why,</rdg>
          </app>
there’s more glory to be gained in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6020"/>
your

          <app from="pr6020" n="325.21 (653.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8096">
            <lem wit="A">your</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you</rdg>
          </app>
being the first to ever try it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6021"/>
than

          <app from="pr6021" n="325.21 (654.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la8097">
            <lem wit="A">than</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">than in</rdg>
          </app>
any other way you could ever think of to save your life.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75557">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3015"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6022"/>
Why

          <app from="pr6022" n="325.23 (654.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8098">
            <lem wit="A">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">W’y</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l12896" type="alt" xml:id="te3015"/>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6023"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6023" n="325.23 (654.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8099">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, I doan’

          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
no sich glory. Snake take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6024"/>
’n

          <app from="pr6024" n="325.23 (654.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8100">
            <lem wit="A">’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">en</rdg>
          </app>
bite Jim’s chin off, den

          <hi rend="italic">whah</hi>
is de glory?

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3016"/>
No

          <ptr target="#l12898" type="alt" xml:id="te3016"/>
, sah,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3017"/>
I doan’

          <ptr target="#l12900" type="alt" xml:id="te3017"/>
want no sich

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6025"/>
doin’s

          <app from="pr6025" n="325.25 (654.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8101">
            <lem wit="A">doin’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">doins</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75609">
“Blame it, can’t you

          <hi rend="italic">try?</hi>
I only

          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
you to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6026"/>
try

          <app from="pr6026" n="325.26 (654.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8102">
            <lem wit="A">try</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">try it</rdg>
          </app>
—you needn’t keep it up if it don’t work.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75626">
“But de trouble all

          <hi rend="italic">done</hi>
, ef de snake bite me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6027"/>
while

          <app from="pr6027" n="325.28 (654.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8103">
            <lem wit="A">while</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">whiles</rdg>
          </app>
I’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6028"/>
a-tryin’

          <app from="pr6028" n="325.28 (654.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8104">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-tryin’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a tryin’</rdg>
          </app>
him. Mars Tom, I’s willin’ to tackle

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3018"/>
mos’

          <ptr target="#l12902" type="alt" xml:id="te3018"/>
anything

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3019"/>
’at

          <ptr target="#l12904" type="alt" xml:id="te3019"/>
ain’t onreasonable, but ef you en Huck fetches a rattlesnake in heah

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3020"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l12906" type="alt" xml:id="te3020"/>
me to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0046"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3021"/>
tame

          <ptr target="#mt0046" type="alt" xml:id="wn0046"/>
, I’s

          <ptr target="#l12908" type="alt" xml:id="te3021"/>
gwyne to

          <hi rend="italic">leave</hi>
, dat’s

          <hi rend="italic">shore.</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75674">
“Well, then, let it go, let it go, if you’re so bullheaded about it. We can

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3022"/>
get you

          <ptr target="#l12910" type="alt" xml:id="te3022"/>
some garter-snakes and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3023"/>
you can

          <ptr target="#l12912" type="alt" xml:id="te3023"/>
tie some buttons on their tails, and let on they’re rattlesnakes, and I reckon that’ll have to do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75684">
“I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6029"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr6029" n="325.36 (655.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8105">
            <lem wit="A">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kin</rdg>
          </app>
stan’

          <hi rend="italic">dem</hi>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6030"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6030" n="325.36 (655.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8106">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3024"/>
Tom

          <ptr target="#l12914" type="alt" xml:id="te3024"/>
, but blame’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6031"/>
’f

          <app from="pr6031" n="325.36 (655.15)" type="e" xml:id="la8107">
            <lem wit="A">’f</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">if</rdg>
          </app>
I couldn’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6032"/>
git

          <app from="pr6032" n="325.36 (655.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8108">
            <lem wit="MS2">git</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">get</rdg>
          </app>
along widout um, I tell you dat. I never

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6033"/>
knowed,

          <app from="pr6033" n="325.37 (655.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8109">
            <lem wit="MS2">knowed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
knowed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6034"/>
b’fo’

          <app from="pr6034" n="325.37 (655.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8110">
            <lem wit="A">b’fo’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">befo’</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6035"/>
’t

          <app from="pr6035" n="325.37 (656.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8111">
            <lem wit="A">’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it</rdg>
          </app>
was so much bother and trouble to be a prisoner.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75749">
          <pb n="326" xml:id="pb0326"/>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y32601">
            <graphic url="y32601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">buttons on their tails</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75756">
“Well, it

          <hi rend="italic">always</hi>
is, when it’s done right. You got any rats around here?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75761">“No, sah, I hain’t seed none.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75763">“Well, we’ll get you some rats.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75765">
“Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6036"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6036" n="326.5 (656.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8112">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6037"/>
doan

          <app from="pr6037" n="326.5 (656.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8113">
            <lem wit="MS2">doan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">doan’</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
no rats. Dey’s de

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6038"/>
dad-blamedest

          <app from="pr6038" n="326.5 (656.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la8114">
            <lem wit="A">dad-blamedest</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
dad-

              <lb/>
blamedest

            </rdg>
          </app>
creturs to ’sturb a body,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6039"/>
en rustle

          <app from="pr6039" n="326.6 (656.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8115">
            <lem wit="A">en rustle</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and rustle</rdg>
          </app>
roun’ over

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6040"/>
’im

          <app from="pr6040" n="326.6 (656.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8116">
            <lem wit="A">’im</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">him</rdg>
          </app>
, en bite his feet, when he’s tryin’ to sleep, I ever see. No,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3025"/>
sah

          <ptr target="#l12916" type="alt" xml:id="te3025"/>
, gimme

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6041"/>
g’yarter snakes

          <app from="pr6041" n="326.7 (656.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8117">
            <lem wit="MS2">g’yarter snakes</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">g’yarter-snakes</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6042"/>
’f

          <app from="pr6042" n="326.8 (656.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8118">
            <lem wit="A">’f</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">if</rdg>
          </app>
I’s got to have ’m, but doan’ gimme no rats, I ain’ got no use

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6043"/>
f’r

          <app from="pr6043" n="326.8 (657.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8119">
            <lem wit="A">f’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
um, skasely.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75842">
“But Jim, you

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to have

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6044"/>
’em,

          <app from="pr6044" n="326.10 (657.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8120">
            <lem wit="MS2">’em,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’em</rdg>
          </app>
—they all do. So don’t make no more fuss about it.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0008"/>
Prisoners ain’t ever without rats

          <ptr target="#as0254" type="an" xml:id="tr0008"/>
. There ain’t no instance of it. And they train them, and pet them, and learn them tricks, and they get to be as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0047"/>
sociable as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3026"/>
flies.

          <ptr target="#l12918" type="alt" xml:id="te3026"/>
          <ptr target="#mt0047" type="alt" xml:id="wn0047"/>
But you got to play music to them. You got anything to play music on?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75867">
“I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3027"/>
ain’

          <ptr target="#l12920" type="alt" xml:id="te3027"/>
got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3028"/>
nuffn

          <ptr target="#l12922" type="alt" xml:id="te3028"/>
but a coase comb en a piece o’ paper, en a juice-harp; but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6045"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr6045" n="326.16 (658.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8121">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
dey wouldn’ take no stock in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6046"/>
juice-harp

          <app from="pr6046" n="326.16 (658.5–6)" type="e" xml:id="la8122">
            <lem wit="A">juice-harp</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
juice-

              <lb/>
harp

            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e75896">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3029"/>
Yes

          <ptr target="#l12924" type="alt" xml:id="te3029"/>
they would.

          <hi rend="italic">They</hi>
don’t care what kind of music ’tis. A

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6047"/>
jewsharp’s

          <app from="pr6047" n="326.18 (658.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8123">
            <lem wit="MS2">jewsharp’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jew-sharp’s</rdg>
          </app>
plenty good enough for a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3030"/>
rat.

          <ptr target="#l12926" type="alt" xml:id="te3030"/>
All animals likes music—in a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6048"/>
prison;

          <app from="pr6048" n="326.19 (658.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8124">
            <lem wit="MS2">prison;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
prison

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
they dote on it.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6049"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3031"/>
Specially

          <ptr target="#l12928" type="alt" xml:id="te3031"/>
          <app from="pr6049" n="326.19 (658.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8125">
            <lem wit="A">Specially</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Speshaly</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3032"/>
painful

          <ptr target="#l12930" type="alt" xml:id="te3032"/>
music; and you can’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3033"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l12932" type="alt" xml:id="te3033"/>
no other kind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3034"/>
out of

          <ptr target="#l12934" type="alt" xml:id="te3034"/>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6050"/>
jewsharp

          <app from="pr6050" n="326.20 (658.16–659.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8126">
            <lem wit="C">jewsharp</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
jews-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
harp

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
jews-

              <lb/>
harp

            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3035"/>
It

          <ptr target="#l12936" type="alt" xml:id="te3035"/>
always interests them; they come out to see

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3036"/>
what’s the matter with you.

          <ptr target="#l12938" type="alt" xml:id="te3036"/>
Yes, you’re all right; you’re

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3037"/>
fixed

          <ptr target="#l12940" type="alt" xml:id="te3037"/>
very well. You want to set on your bed, nights, before you go to sleep, and early in the mornings, and play your

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6051"/>
jewsharp

          <app from="pr6051" n="326.23 (659.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8127">
            <lem wit="MS2">jewsharp</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
jews-

              <lb/>
harp

            </rdg>
          </app>
; play The Last Link is Broken—that’s the thing that’ll

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3038"/>
scoop

          <ptr target="#l12942" type="alt" xml:id="te3038"/>
a rat,

          <pb n="327" xml:id="pb0327"/>
quicker’n anything else: and when you’ve played about two minutes, you’ll see all the rats, and the snakes, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3039"/>
spiders

          <ptr target="#l12944" type="alt" xml:id="te3039"/>
, and things begin to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3040"/>
feel worried about you,

          <ptr target="#l12946" type="alt" xml:id="te3040"/>
and come. And they’ll just fairly swarm over you,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3041"/>
and have

          <ptr target="#l12948" type="alt" xml:id="te3041"/>
a noble good time.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76008">
“Yes,

          <hi rend="italic">dey</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3042"/>
will, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6052"/>
reck’n,

          <ptr target="#l12950" type="alt" xml:id="te3042"/>
          <app from="pr6052" n="327.5 (660.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8128">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6053"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6053" n="327.5 (660.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8129">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, but what kine er time is

          <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3043"/>
havin’?

          <ptr target="#l12952" type="alt" xml:id="te3043"/>
Blest if I kin see de pint. But I’ll do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6054"/>
it,

          <app from="pr6054" n="327.6 (660.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8130">
            <lem wit="MS2">it,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
it

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
ef I got to. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6055"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr6055" n="327.6 (660.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8131">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
I better keep de

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3044"/>
animals

          <ptr target="#l12954" type="alt" xml:id="te3044"/>
satisfied, en not have no trouble in de house.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76058">
Tom waited to think over, and see if there

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3045"/>
wasn’t

          <ptr target="#l12956" type="alt" xml:id="te3045"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6056"/>
nothing

          <app from="pr6056" n="327.8 (660.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8132">
            <lem wit="A">nothing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">anything</rdg>
          </app>
else; and pretty soon he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76071">“Oh—there’s one thing I forgot. Could you raise a flower here, do you reckon?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76073">
“I doan’ know but maybe I could,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6057"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6057" n="327.12 (661.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8133">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom; but it’s tolable dark in heah,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3046"/>
en I

          <ptr target="#l12958" type="alt" xml:id="te3046"/>
ain’ got no use

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6058"/>
f’r

          <app from="pr6058" n="327.13 (661.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8134">
            <lem wit="A">f’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
no flower,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3047"/>
nohow,

          <ptr target="#l12960" type="alt" xml:id="te3047"/>
en she’d be a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6059"/>
powful

          <app from="pr6059" n="327.13 (661.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8135">
            <lem wit="MS2">powful</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pow’ful</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3048"/>
sight o’

          <ptr target="#l12962" type="alt" xml:id="te3048"/>
trouble.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76112">
“Well, you try it, anyway. Some

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3049"/>
other

          <ptr target="#l12964" type="alt" xml:id="te3049"/>
prisoners has done it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76118">
“One er dem big cat-tail-lookin’ mullen-stalks would grow in heah,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6060"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6060" n="327.17 (661.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8136">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6061"/>
reck’n

          <app from="pr6061" n="327.17 (661.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8137">
            <lem wit="A">reck’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reckon</rdg>
          </app>
, but she wouldn’ be wuth half de trouble she’d coss.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76136">
“Don’t you believe it. We’ll fetch you a little one, and you plant it in the corner,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3050"/>
over

          <ptr target="#l12966" type="alt" xml:id="te3050"/>
there, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3051"/>
raise it.

          <ptr target="#l12968" type="alt" xml:id="te3051"/>
And don’t call it mullen, call it

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0009"/>
Pitchiola

          <ptr target="#as0255" type="an" xml:id="tr0009"/>
—that’s its right name, when it’s in a prison. And you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3052"/>
want

          <ptr target="#l12970" type="alt" xml:id="te3052"/>
to water it with your tears.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76155">
“Why, I got plenty spring water,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6062"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6062" n="327.23 (662.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8138">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76165">
“You don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3053"/>
          <hi rend="italic">want</hi>
          <ptr target="#l12972" type="alt" xml:id="te3053"/>
spring water; you want to water it with your tears. It’s the way they always do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76172">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y32701">
            <graphic url="y32701.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">irrigation</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76178">
          <pb n="328" xml:id="pb0328"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6063"/>
Why

          <app from="pr6063" n="328.1 (663.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8139">
            <lem wit="MS2">Why</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Why,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6064"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6064" n="328.1 (663.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8140">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, I lay I kin raise one er dem mullen-stalks twyste wid spring water whiles another man’s a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pry065"/>
          <hi rend="italic">start</hi>
’n

          <app from="pry065" n="328.2 (663.5)" type="hc" xml:id="lay141">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">start</hi>
’n

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">start</hi>
’n

            </rdg>
          </app>
one wid tears.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76212">
“That ain’t the idea. You

          <hi rend="italic">got</hi>
to do it with tears.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76217">
“She’ll die on my han’s,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6066"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6066" n="328.4 (663.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8142">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom, she sholy will;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6067"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3054"/>
kase

          <ptr target="#l12974" type="alt" xml:id="te3054"/>
          <app from="pr6067" n="328.4 (663.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8143">
            <lem wit="A">kase</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kaze</rdg>
          </app>
I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6068"/>
doan’

          <app from="pr6068" n="328.4 (663.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8144">
            <lem wit="A">doan’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">don’t</rdg>
          </app>
skasely ever cry.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76246">
So Tom was stumped. But he studied

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3055"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l12976" type="alt" xml:id="te3055"/>
over, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3056"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l12978" type="alt" xml:id="te3056"/>
said Jim would have to worry along the best he could with an onion. He promised he would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3057"/>
go to the nigger cabins and

          <ptr target="#l12980" type="alt" xml:id="te3057"/>
drop one, private, in Jim’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6069"/>
coffee pot

          <app from="pr6069" n="328.9 (664.1–2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8145">
            <lem wit="MS2">coffee pot</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">coffee-pot</rdg>
          </app>
, in the morning. Jim said he would

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3058"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6070"/>
jis’ ’s

          <app from="pr6070" n="328.9 (664.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8146">
            <lem wit="A">jis’ ’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jis’ as</rdg>
          </app>
soon have tobacker in his coffee;”

          <ptr target="#l12982" type="alt" xml:id="te3058"/>
and found so much fault with it, and with the work and bother of raising the mullen, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6071"/>
jewsharping

          <app from="pr6071" n="328.11 (664.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8147">
            <lem wit="MS2">jewsharping</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">jews-harping</rdg>
          </app>
the rats, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3059"/>
petting

          <ptr target="#l12984" type="alt" xml:id="te3059"/>
and flattering up the snakes and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3060"/>
spiders

          <ptr target="#l12986" type="alt" xml:id="te3060"/>
and things, on top of all the other work

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3061"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l12988" type="alt" xml:id="te3061"/>
had to do on pens, and inscriptions, and journals, and things, which made it more trouble and worry and responsibility to be a prisoner than anything he ever undertook, that Tom most lost all patience with him; and said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6072"/>
he was

          <app from="pr6072" n="328.16 (665.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8148">
            <lem wit="A">he was</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">here he was,</rdg>
          </app>
just

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6073"/>
loadened

          <app from="pr6073" n="328.17 (665.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8149">
            <lem wit="A">loadened</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">loaded</rdg>
          </app>
down with more gaudier chances than a prisoner ever had in the world to make a name for himself, and yet he didn’t know enough to appreciate them, and they was just about wasted on him. So Jim he was sorry, and said he wouldn’t behave so no more, and then me and Tom shoved for bed.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0449">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XXXIX.</head>
        <pb n="329" xml:id="pb0329"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76324">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y32901">
            <graphic url="y32901.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6074"/>
Chapter XXXIX.

              <app from="pr6074" n="329 title (666.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8150">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XXXIX</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8151">not in; extra line space</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">In</ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3291">
            <graphic url="hf3291.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">keeping off dull times</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e76342">
the morning we went up to the village and bought a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3062"/>
wire

          <ptr target="#l12990" type="alt" xml:id="te3062"/>
rat trap and fetched it down, and unstopped the best rat hole, and in about an hour we had fifteen of the bulliest kind of ones; and then we took it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3063"/>
and put

          <ptr target="#l12992" type="alt" xml:id="te3063"/>
it in a safe place under

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6075"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6075" n="329.7 (666.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8152">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally’s bed. But while we was gone for spiders, little

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0010"/>
Thomas Franklin Benjamin Jefferson Elexander Phelps

          <ptr target="#as0256" type="an" xml:id="tr0010"/>
found it there, and opened the door of it to see if the rats would come out, and they did; and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6076"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6076" n="329.13 (666.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8153">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally she come in, and when we got back she was a standing on top of the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3064"/>
bed

          <ptr target="#l12994" type="alt" xml:id="te3064"/>
raising Cain, and the rats was doing what they could to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6077"/>
keep off the dull times for

          <app from="pr6077" n="329.17–18 (667.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8154">
            <lem wit="A">keep . . . for</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">amuse</rdg>
          </app>
her. So she took and dusted us both with the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3065"/>
hickry

          <ptr target="#l12996" type="alt" xml:id="te3065"/>
, and we was as much as two hours catching another fifteen or sixteen, drat that meddlesome

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3066"/>
cub,

          <ptr target="#l12998" type="alt" xml:id="te3066"/>
and they warn’t the likeliest,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6078"/>
nuther

          <app from="pr6078" n="329.21 (667.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8155">
            <lem wit="A">nuther</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">neither</rdg>
          </app>
, because the first haul was the pick of the flock. I never see a likelier lot of rats than what that first haul was.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76403">
We got a splendid stock of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6079"/>
sorted

          <app from="pr6079" n="329.24 (668.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8156">
            <lem wit="A">sorted</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8157">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3067"/>
spiders

          <ptr target="#l13000" type="alt" xml:id="te3067"/>
, and bugs, and frogs, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6080"/>
caterpillars

          <app from="pr6080" n="329.25 (668.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8158">
            <lem wit="MS2">caterpillars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
cater-

              <lb/>
pillars

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and one thing or another; and we like-to got a hornet’s nest, but we didn’t. The family was at home. We didn’t give it right up, but staid with them as long as we could; because we allowed we’d tire them out or they’d got to tire us out, and they done it. Then we got allycumpain and rubbed on the places, and was pretty near all

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6081"/>
right,

          <app from="pr6081" n="329.30 (668.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8159">
            <lem wit="MS2">right,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
right

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
again, but couldn’t set down convenient. And so we went for the snakes, and grabbed a couple of dozen garters and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6082"/>
house-snakes

          <app from="pr6082" n="329.31–32 (668.17–669.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8160">
            <lem wit="C">house-snakes</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
house-

              <milestone unit="page"/>
snakes

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
house-

              <lb/>
snakes

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and put them in a bag, and put it in our room, and by that time it was supper time, and a rattling good honest day’s work; and

          <pb n="330" xml:id="pb0330"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3068"/>
hungry?

          <ptr target="#l13002" type="alt" xml:id="te3068"/>
—oh, no, I reckon not! And there warn’t a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6083"/>
blessed

          <app from="pr6083" n="330.1 (669.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8161">
            <lem wit="A">blessed</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">blamed</rdg>
          </app>
snake up there, when we went back—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3069"/>
we didn’t

          <ptr target="#l13004" type="alt" xml:id="te3069"/>
half tie the sack, and they worked out, somehow, and left. But it didn’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3070"/>
matter

          <ptr target="#l13006" type="alt" xml:id="te3070"/>
much, because they was still on the premises

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3071"/>
somewheres

          <ptr target="#l13008" type="alt" xml:id="te3071"/>
. So we judged we could get some of them again. No, there warn’t no real scarcity of snakes about the house for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6084"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr6084" n="330.6 (670.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la8162">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
spell.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6085"/>
You’d

          <app from="pr6085" n="330.6 (670.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8163">
            <lem wit="A">You’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">You would</rdg>
          </app>
see them dripping from the rafters and places, every now and then; and they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3072"/>
generly

          <ptr target="#l13010" type="alt" xml:id="te3072"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3073"/>
landed

          <ptr target="#l13012" type="alt" xml:id="te3073"/>
in your plate, or down the back of your neck,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3074"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l13014" type="alt" xml:id="te3074"/>
most of the time where you didn’t want them. Well, they was handsome, and striped, and there warn’t no harm in a million of them; but that never made no difference to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6086"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6086" n="330.11 (670.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8164">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally, she despised snakes, be the breed what they might, and she couldn’t stand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6087"/>
them,

          <app from="pr6087" n="330.12 (671.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8165">
            <lem wit="MS2">them,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
them

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
no way you could fix it; and every time one of them flopped down on her, it didn’t make no difference what she was doing, she would just lay

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6088"/>
that work down

          <app from="pr6088" n="330.15 (671.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8166">
            <lem wit="A">that work down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">down that work</rdg>
          </app>
and light out. I never see such a woman. And you could hear her whoop to Jericho. You couldn’t get her to take

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3075"/>
aholt

          <ptr target="#l13016" type="alt" xml:id="te3075"/>
of one of them with the tongs. And if she turned over and found one in bed, she would scramble out

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3076"/>
and lift

          <ptr target="#l13018" type="alt" xml:id="te3076"/>
a howl that you would think the house was afire. She disturbed the old man so, that he said he could most wish there hadn’t ever been no snakes created. Why, after every last snake had been gone clear

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3077"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l13020" type="alt" xml:id="te3077"/>
of the house for as much as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3078"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l13022" type="alt" xml:id="te3078"/>
week,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6089"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6089" n="330.22 (672.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8167">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally warn’t over

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3079"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l13024" type="alt" xml:id="te3079"/>
yet; she warn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6090"/>
near

          <app from="pr6090" n="330.22 (672.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8168">
            <lem wit="A">near</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">near</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
over it; when she was setting thinking about something, you could touch her on the back of her neck with a feather and she would jump

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3080"/>
right

          <ptr target="#l13026" type="alt" xml:id="te3080"/>
out of her stockings. It was very curious. But Tom said all women was just so. He said they was made that way; for some reason or other.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76574">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3081"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6091"/>
We

          <app from="pr6091" n="330.28 (673.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8169">
            <lem wit="A">[¶] We</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8170">
no

                <hi rend="normal">¶</hi>
              </note>
We

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13028" type="alt" xml:id="te3081"/>
got a licking every time one of our snakes come in her way; and she allowed these lickings warn’t nothing to what she would do if we ever loaded up the place again with them. I didn’t mind the lickings, because they didn’t amount to nothing; but I minded the trouble we had, to lay in another lot. But we got them laid

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3082"/>
in,

          <ptr target="#l13031" type="alt" xml:id="te3082"/>
and all the other things; and you never see a cabin as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6092"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3083"/>
blithesome

          <ptr target="#l13033" type="alt" xml:id="te3083"/>
          <app from="pr6092" n="330.33 (674.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8171">
            <lem wit="A">blithesome</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">gay</rdg>
          </app>
as Jim’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3084"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l13035" type="alt" xml:id="te3084"/>
when they’d all swarm out for music and go for him. Jim didn’t like the spiders, and the spiders didn’t like Jim; and so they’d lay for him and make it mighty warm for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3085"/>
him.

          <ptr target="#l13037" type="alt" xml:id="te3085"/>
And he said that between the rats, and the snakes, and the grindstone, there warn’t no room in bed for him, skasely; and when there was, a body couldn’t sleep,

          <pb n="331" xml:id="pb0331"/>
it was so lively, and it was always lively, he said,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3086"/>
because

          <ptr target="#l13039" type="alt" xml:id="te3086"/>
          <hi rend="italic">they</hi>
never all slept at

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3087"/>
one time,

          <ptr target="#l13041" type="alt" xml:id="te3087"/>
but took turn about, so when the snakes was asleep the rats was on deck, and when the rats turned in the snakes come on watch, so he always had one gang under him, in his way, and t’other gang having a circus over him, and if he got up to hunt a new place, the spiders would take a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6093"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3088"/>
chance

          <ptr target="#l13043" type="alt" xml:id="te3088"/>
          <app from="pr6093" n="331.6 (675.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8172">
            <lem wit="A">chance</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">shy</rdg>
          </app>
at him as he crossed over. He said if he ever got out, this time, he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3089"/>
wouldn’t ever

          <ptr target="#l13045" type="alt" xml:id="te3089"/>
be a prisoner again, not for a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6094"/>
salary.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y33101">
          <graphic url="y33101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">sawdust diet</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76648">
Well

          <app from="pr6094" n="331.8–9 (675.16–676.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8173">
            <lem wit="A">salary. [¶] Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
salary.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8174">extra line space; possibly chapter sink</note>
[¶] Well

            </rdg>
          </app>
, by the end of three weeks, everything was in pretty good shape. The shirt was sent in early, in a pie, and every time a rat bit Jim he would get up and write a little in his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6095"/>
journal,

          <app from="pr6095" n="331.11 (676.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8175">
            <lem wit="MS2">journal,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
journal

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
whilst the ink was fresh; the pens was made, the inscriptions and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6096"/>
so-on

          <app from="pr6096" n="331.12 (676.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8176">
            <lem wit="MS2">so-on</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">so on</rdg>
          </app>
was all carved on the grindstone;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3090"/>
the bed-leg was sawed in two, and we had et up the sawdust, and it give us a most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6097"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3091"/>
amazing

          <ptr target="#l13049" type="alt" xml:id="te3091"/>
          <app from="pr6097" n="331.14 (676verso.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8177">
            <lem wit="A">amazing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">surprising</rdg>
          </app>
stomach-ache. We reckoned we was all going to die, but didn’t. It was the most undigestible sawdust I ever see; and Tom said the same. But as I was saying,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6098"/>
we’d

          <app from="pr6098" n="331.17 (676verso.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8178">
            <lem wit="A">we’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we had</rdg>
          </app>
got all the work done, now, at last; and we was all pretty much fagged out, too, but mainly Jim. The old

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3092"/>
man

          <ptr target="#l13051" type="alt" xml:id="te3092"/>
had wrote

          <pb n="332" xml:id="pb0332"/>
a couple of times to the plantation below Orleans to come and get their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6099"/>
runaway

          <app from="pr6099" n="332.2 (676verso.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la8179">
            <lem wit="A">runaway</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
run-

              <lb/>
away

            </rdg>
          </app>
nigger, but hadn’t got no answer, because there warn’t no such plantation; so he allowed he would advertise Jim in the St. Louis and New Orleans papers; and when he mentioned the St. Louis ones, it give me the cold shivers, and I see we hadn’t no time to lose. So Tom said, now for the nonnamous letters.

          <ptr target="#l13047" type="alt" xml:id="te3090"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76715">“What’s them?” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76717">
“Warnings to the people that something is

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3093"/>
up.

          <ptr target="#l13053" type="alt" xml:id="te3093"/>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0011"/>
Sometimes it’s done one way, sometimes another

          <ptr target="#as0257" type="an" xml:id="tr0011"/>
. But there’s always somebody spying around, that gives notice to the governor of the castle. When Louis

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6100"/>
XVI

          <app from="pr6100" n="332.11 (677.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8180">
            <lem wit="MS2">XVI</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">XVI.</rdg>
          </app>
was going to light out of the Tooleries, a servant girl done it. It’s a very good way, and so is the nonnamous letters. We’ll use them both. And

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0012"/>
it’s usual for the prisoner’s mother to change clothes with him

          <ptr target="#as0258" type="an" xml:id="tr0012"/>
, and she stays in, and he slides out in her clothes. We’ll do

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6101"/>
that,

          <app from="pr6101" n="332.15 (678.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8181">
            <lem wit="MS2">that,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
that

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
too.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76747">
“But

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6102"/>
lookyhere

          <app from="pr6102" n="332.16 (678.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8182">
            <lem wit="MS2">lookyhere</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">looky here</rdg>
          </app>
, Tom, what do we want to

          <hi rend="italic">warn</hi>
anybody for, that something’s up? Let them find it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3094"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l13055" type="alt" xml:id="te3094"/>
for themselves—it’s their

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6103"/>
lookout

          <app from="pr6103" n="332.18 (678.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la8183">
            <lem wit="A">lookout</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
look-

              <lb/>
out

            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76776">
“Yes, I know; but you can’t depend on them. It’s the way they’ve acted from the very start—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3095"/>
left us to do

          <hi rend="italic">
everything.

            <ptr target="#l13057" type="alt" xml:id="te3095"/>
          </hi>
They’re so confiding and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6104"/>
mullet-headed

          <app from="pr6104" n="332.21 (678.15–679.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8184">
            <lem wit="MS2">mullet-headed</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
mullet-

              <lb/>
headed

            </rdg>
          </app>
they don’t take notice of nothing at all. So if we don’t

          <hi rend="italic">give</hi>
them notice, there won’t be nobody nor nothing to interfere with us, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3096"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l13059" type="alt" xml:id="te3096"/>
after all our

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3097"/>
hard work and

          <ptr target="#l13061" type="alt" xml:id="te3097"/>
trouble this escape ’ll go off perfectly flat: won’t amount to nothing—won’t be nothing

          <hi rend="italic">to</hi>
it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76809">
“Well, as for me, Tom, that’s the way

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3098"/>
I’d

          <ptr target="#l13063" type="alt" xml:id="te3098"/>
like.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76815">“Shucks,” he says, and looked disgusted. So I says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76817">
“But I ain’t going to make no complaint.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6105"/>
Any way

          <app from="pr6105" n="332.28 (679.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8185">
            <lem wit="MS2">Any way</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Anyway</rdg>
          </app>
that suits you suits me. What you going to do about the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6106"/>
servant girl

          <app from="pr6106" n="332.29 (680.2–3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8186">
            <lem wit="MS2">servant girl</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">servant-girl</rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76835">
“You’ll be her. You slide in, in the middle of the night, and hook that yaller girl’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6107"/>
frock

          <app from="pr6107" n="332.31 (680.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8187">
            <lem wit="A">frock</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">dress</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76845">
“Why, Tom, that’ll make

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6108"/>
trouble,

          <app from="pr6108" n="332.32 (680.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8188">
            <lem wit="MS2">trouble,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
trouble

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6109"/>
morning,

          <app from="pr6109" n="332.32 (680.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8189">
            <lem wit="MS2">morning,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">morning;</rdg>
          </app>
because of course she

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6110"/>
prob’ly

          <app from="pr6110" n="332.33 (680.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8190">
            <lem wit="MS2">prob’ly</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
prob’-

              <lb/>
bly

            </rdg>
          </app>
hain’t got any but that one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76874">“I know; but you don’t want it but fifteen minutes, to carry the nonnamous letter and shove it under the front door.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76876">“All right, then, I’ll do it; but I could carry it just as handy in my own togs.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76878">
“You wouldn’t look like a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6111"/>
servant girl

          <app from="pr6111" n="332.38 (681.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8191">
            <lem wit="MS2">servant girl</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">servant-girl</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">then</hi>
, would you?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76890">
“No, but there won’t be nobody to see what I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3099"/>
look like,

          <ptr target="#l13065" type="alt" xml:id="te3099"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3100"/>
          <hi rend="italic">anyway</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13067" type="alt" xml:id="te3100"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76901">
          <pb n="333" xml:id="pb0333"/>
“That ain’t got nothing to do with it. The thing for us to do, is just to do our

          <hi rend="italic">duty</hi>
, and not worry about whether anybody

          <hi rend="italic">sees</hi>
us do it or not. Hain’t you got no principle at all?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76911">
“All right, I ain’t saying

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6112"/>
nothing:

          <app from="pr6112" n="333.4 (681.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8192">
            <lem wit="MS2">nothing:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">nothing;</rdg>
          </app>
I’m the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6113"/>
servant girl

          <app from="pr6113" n="333.4 (681.14–15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8193">
            <lem wit="MS2">servant girl</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">servant-girl</rdg>
          </app>
. Who’s Jim’s mother?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76929">
“I’m his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3101"/>
mother.

          <ptr target="#l13069" type="alt" xml:id="te3101"/>
I’ll hook

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3102"/>
a gown from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6114"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6114" n="333.6 (682.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8194">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally.”

          <ptr target="#l13071" type="alt" xml:id="te3102"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76947">“Well, then, you’ll have to stay in the cabin when me and Jim leaves.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76949">
“Not much. I’ll stuff Jim’s clothes full of straw and lay it on his bed to represent his mother in disguise, and Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6115"/>
’ll

          <app from="pr6115" n="333.10 (682.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8195">
            <lem wit="A">’ll</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">will</rdg>
          </app>
take

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6116"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0081"/>
aunt Sally’s

          <app from="pr6116" n="333.10 (682.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la8196">
            <lem wit="C">aunt Sally’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">the nigger woman’s</rdg>
          </app>
gown

          <ptr target="#tb0081" type="te" xml:id="tv0081"/>
off of me and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3103"/>
wear it

          <ptr target="#l13073" type="alt" xml:id="te3103"/>
, and we’ll all evade together. When a prisoner of style escapes, it’s called an evasion. It’s always called so when a king escapes,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6117"/>
frinstance

          <app from="pr6117" n="333.13 (683.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8197">
            <lem wit="MS2">frinstance</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">f’rinstance</rdg>
          </app>
. And the same with a king’s son; it don’t make no difference whether he’s a natural one or an unnatural one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e76983">
So Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6118"/>
he

          <app from="pr6118" n="333.16 (683.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8198">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8199">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
wrote the nonnamous letter, and I smouched the yaller

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6119"/>
wench’s frock

          <app from="pr6119" n="333.17 (683.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8200">
            <lem wit="A">wench’s frock</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">girl’s gown</rdg>
          </app>
, that night, and put it on, and shoved it under the front door, the way Tom told me to. It

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6120"/>
said:

          <app from="pr6120" n="333.18 (683.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8201">
            <lem wit="A">
said:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8202">extra line space</note>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
said:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8203">no extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e77014">
          <pb n="334" xml:id="pb0334"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77016">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y33301">
            <graphic url="y33301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">trouble is brewing</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77023">
            <hi rend="italic">
              <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0082"/>
Beware. Trouble is brewing. Keep a sharp lookout.

            </hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3104"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">Unknown</hi>
            <ptr target="#l13075" type="alt" xml:id="te3104"/>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6121"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">Friend</hi>
.

            <app from="pr6121" n="334.1 (683.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8204">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">Friend</hi>
.

                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8205">extra line space</note>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">Friend</hi>
.

                <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8206">no extra line space</note>
              </rdg>
            </app>
            <ptr target="#tb0082" type="te" xml:id="tv0082"/>
          </p>
        </quote>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77049">
Next

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6122"/>
night,

          <app from="pr6122" n="334.2 (684.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8207">
            <lem wit="MS2">night,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
night

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
we stuck a picture which Tom drawed in blood, of a skull and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6123"/>
crossbones

          <app from="pr6123" n="334.3 (684.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la8208">
            <lem wit="A">crossbones</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
cross-

              <lb/>
bones

            </rdg>
          </app>
, on the front door; and next night another one of a coffin, on the back door. I never see a family in such a sweat. They couldn’t a been worse scared if

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3105"/>
the place had

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3106"/>
a

          <ptr target="#l13079" type="alt" xml:id="te3106"/>
been full of ghosts laying for them behind everything and under the beds and shivering through the air.

          <ptr target="#l13077" type="alt" xml:id="te3105"/>
If a door banged,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6124"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6124" n="334.7 (684.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8209">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6125"/>
she

          <app from="pr6125" n="334.7 (684.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8210">
            <lem wit="A">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8211">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
jumped, and said “ouch!” if anything fell, she jumped and said “ouch!” if you happened to touch her,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3107"/>
when

          <ptr target="#l13081" type="alt" xml:id="te3107"/>
she warn’t noticing, she done the same; she couldn’t face noway and be satisfied, because she allowed there was something behind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3108"/>
her every time—

          <ptr target="#l13083" type="alt" xml:id="te3108"/>
so she was always a whirling around, sudden, and saying “ouch,” and before she’d get two-thirds around, she’d whirl back again, and say it again; and she was afraid to go to bed, but she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3109"/>
dasn’t

          <ptr target="#l13085" type="alt" xml:id="te3109"/>
set up. So the thing was working very well, Tom said; he said he never see a thing work more satisfactory. He said it showed it was done right.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77109">
So

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3110"/>
he said, now

          <ptr target="#l13087" type="alt" xml:id="te3110"/>
for the grand bulge! So the very next morning at the streak of dawn we got another letter

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3111"/>
ready

          <ptr target="#l13089" type="alt" xml:id="te3111"/>
, and was wondering

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3112"/>
what

          <ptr target="#l13091" type="alt" xml:id="te3112"/>
we better do with it, because

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3113"/>
we heard

          <ptr target="#l13093" type="alt" xml:id="te3113"/>
them say at supper they was going to have a nigger on watch at both doors all night. Tom

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3114"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l13095" type="alt" xml:id="te3114"/>
went down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6126"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr6126" n="334.21 (686.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8212">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
to spy around; and the nigger at the back door was asleep, and he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3115"/>
stuck it in the back of his neck

          <ptr target="#l13097" type="alt" xml:id="te3115"/>
and come back. This letter

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6127"/>
said:

          <app from="pr6127" n="334.23 (686.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8213">
            <lem wit="A">
said:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8214">extra line space</note>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
said:

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8215">no extra line space</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <quote rend="blockquote">
          <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77157">
            <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0083"/>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6128"/>
            <hi rend="italic">Don’t betray me, I wish to be your friend. There is a</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3116"/>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6129"/>
            <hi rend="italic">desprate</hi>
            <app from="pr6129" n="334.24 (687.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8217">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">desprate</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">desperate</rdg>
            </app>
            <ptr target="#l13099" type="alt" xml:id="te3116"/>
            <hi rend="italic">gang of cutthroats from over in the</hi>
            <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0013"/>
            <hi rend="italic">Ingean Territory</hi>
            <ptr target="#as0259" type="an" xml:id="tr0013"/>
            <hi rend="italic">going to steal your runaway nigger</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3117"/>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6130"/>
            <hi rend="italic">to-night</hi>
            <app from="pr6130" n="334.26 (687.6–7)" type="e" xml:id="la8218">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">to-night</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">
to-

                <lb/>
night

              </rdg>
            </app>
,

            <ptr target="#l13101" type="alt" xml:id="te3117"/>
            <hi rend="italic">and they have been trying to scare you so as you will stay in the house and not bother them. I am one of the gang,</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3118"/>
            <hi rend="italic">but</hi>
            <ptr target="#l13103" type="alt" xml:id="te3118"/>
            <hi rend="italic">have got</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6131"/>
            <hi rend="italic">religgion</hi>
            <app from="pr6131" n="334.27–28 (687.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8219">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">religgion</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">religion</rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="italic">and wish to quit it and lead a honest life again, and will betray the helish design. They will sneak down from</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3119"/>
            <hi rend="italic">northards</hi>
            <ptr target="#l13105" type="alt" xml:id="te3119"/>
,

            <hi rend="italic">along the fence, at midnight exact, with a false key, and go in the nigger’s cabin to get him. I am to be off a piece and blow a tin horn if I see any danger; but stead of that, I will</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6132"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">ba</hi>
            <app from="pr6132" n="334.32 (688.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8220">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="smallcaps">ba</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">ba</rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="italic">
like a sheep soon as they get in

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3120"/>
and not blow at all

            </hi>
            <ptr target="#l13107" type="alt" xml:id="te3120"/>
;

            <hi rend="italic">then whilst they are getting his chains loose, you slip there and lock them</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3121"/>
            <hi rend="italic">in,</hi>
            <ptr target="#l13109" type="alt" xml:id="te3121"/>
            <hi rend="italic">and can kill them at</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6133"/>
            <hi rend="italic">your</hi>
            <app from="pr6133" n="334.34 (688.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8221">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">your</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">you</rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="italic">leasure. Don’t do</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3122"/>
            <hi rend="italic">anything</hi>
            <ptr target="#l13111" type="alt" xml:id="te3122"/>
            <hi rend="italic">but just the way I am telling you, if you do they will suspicion something and raise</hi>
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3123"/>
            <hi rend="italic">whoopjamboreehoo</hi>
            <ptr target="#l13113" type="alt" xml:id="te3123"/>
.

            <hi rend="italic">I do not wish any reward but to know I have done the right thing.</hi>
            <app from="pr6128" n="334.24–37 (687.1–689.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8216">
              <lem wit="A">
                <hi rend="italic">Don’t . . . thing.</hi>
              </lem>
              <rdg wit="MS2">Don’t . . . thing.</rdg>
            </app>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">Unknown</hi>
            <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6134"/>
            <hi rend="smallcaps">Friend</hi>
.

            <ptr target="#tb0083" type="te" xml:id="tv0083"/>
          </p>
        </quote>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0453">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XL.</head>
        <pb n="335" xml:id="pb0335"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77278">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y33501">
            <graphic url="y33501.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
Chapter XL.

              <app from="pr6134" n="334.37–335 title (689.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8222">
                <lem wit="A">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">Friend</hi>
.

                  <milestone unit="page"/>
Chapter XL.

                </lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <hi rend="smallcaps">Friend</hi>
.

                  <lb/>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8223">centered rule</note>
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8224">extra line space</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">We</ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3351">
            <graphic url="hf3351.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">fishing</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e77305">
was feeling pretty good, after breakfast, and took my canoe and went over the river

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6135"/>
a-fishing

          <app from="pr6135" n="335.3–4 (689.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8225">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-fishing</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a fishing</rdg>
          </app>
, with a lunch, and had a good time, and took a look at the raft and found her all right, and got home late to supper, and found them in such a sweat and worry they didn’t know which end they was standing on, and made us go right off to bed the minute we was done supper, and wouldn’t tell us what the trouble was, and never let on a word about the new letter, but didn’t need to, because we knowed as much about it as anybody did, and as soon as we was half up stairs and her back was turned, we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3124"/>
slid

          <ptr target="#l13115" type="alt" xml:id="te3124"/>
for the cellar cubboard and loaded up a good lunch and took

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3125"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l13117" type="alt" xml:id="te3125"/>
up to our room and went to bed, and got up about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3126"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6136"/>
half past

          <app from="pr6136" n="335.20 (690.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8226">
            <lem wit="MS2">half past</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">half-past</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13119" type="alt" xml:id="te3126"/>
eleven, and Tom put on

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6137"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6137" n="335.20 (690.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8227">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally’s dress

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3127"/>
that he stole

          <ptr target="#l13121" type="alt" xml:id="te3127"/>
and was going to start with the lunch, but says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77347">“Where’s the butter?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77349">“I laid out a hunk of it,” I says, “on a piece of a corn-pone.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77351">
“Well, you

          <hi rend="italic">left</hi>
it laid out, then—it ain’t here.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77356">“We can get along without it,” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77358">
“We can get along

          <hi rend="italic">with</hi>
it, too,” he says; “just you slide down cellar and fetch it. And

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3128"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l13123" type="alt" xml:id="te3128"/>
mosey right down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6138"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr6138" n="335.27 (691.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8228">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
and come along. I’ll go and stuff the straw into Jim’s clothes to represent his mother in disguise, and be ready to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6139"/>
          <hi rend="italic">ba</hi>
          <app from="pr6139" n="335.29 (692.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8229">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">ba</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ba</rdg>
          </app>
like a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3129"/>
sheep

          <ptr target="#l13125" type="alt" xml:id="te3129"/>
and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6140"/>
shove,

          <app from="pr6140" n="335.30 (692.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8230">
            <lem wit="MS2">shove,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
shove

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
soon as you get there.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77398">
So out he went, and down cellar went I. The hunk of butter, big

          <pb n="336" xml:id="pb0336"/>
as a person’s fist, was where I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6141"/>
had

          <app from="pr6141" n="336.1 (692.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8231">
            <lem wit="A">had</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8232">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
left it, so I took up the slab of corn-pone with it on, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3130"/>
blowed

          <ptr target="#l13127" type="alt" xml:id="te3130"/>
out my light, and started up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3131"/>
stairs

          <ptr target="#l13129" type="alt" xml:id="te3131"/>
, very stealthy, and got up to the main floor all right, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6142"/>
here

          <app from="pr6142" n="336.3 (692.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8233">
            <lem wit="A">here</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">then here</rdg>
          </app>
comes

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6143"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6143" n="336.3 (693.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8234">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally with a candle, and I clapped the truck in my hat, and clapped my hat on my head, and the next second she see me; and she says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77436">“You been down cellar?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77439">“Yes’m.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77441">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3132"/>
What you

          <ptr target="#l13131" type="alt" xml:id="te3132"/>
been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6144"/>
doing

          <app from="pr6144" n="336.8 (693.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8235">
            <lem wit="A">doing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">doin’</rdg>
          </app>
down there?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77455">“Noth’n.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77457">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Noth’n!</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77462">“No’m.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77464">
“Well, then, what possessed you to go down there, this time

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6145"/>
of

          <app from="pr6145" n="336.12 (694.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8236">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">o’</rdg>
          </app>
night?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77474">
“I don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3133"/>
know’m

          <ptr target="#l13133" type="alt" xml:id="te3133"/>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77480">
“You don’t

          <hi rend="italic">know?</hi>
Don’t answer me that way, Tom, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3134"/>
want

          <ptr target="#l13135" type="alt" xml:id="te3134"/>
to know what you been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6146"/>
          <hi rend="italic">doing</hi>
          <app from="pr6146" n="336.16 (694.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8237">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">doing</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">doin’</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
down there?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77500">
“I hain’t been

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6147"/>
doing

          <app from="pr6147" n="336.17 (694.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8238">
            <lem wit="A">doing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">doin’</rdg>
          </app>
a single thing,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6148"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6148" n="336.17 (694.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8239">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally, I hope to gracious if I have.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77518">
I reckoned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6149"/>
she’d

          <app from="pr6149" n="336.19 (694.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8240">
            <lem wit="A">she’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">she would</rdg>
          </app>
let me go, now, and as a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3135"/>
generl

          <ptr target="#l13137" type="alt" xml:id="te3135"/>
thing she would; but I spose there was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3136"/>
so

          <ptr target="#l13139" type="alt" xml:id="te3136"/>
many

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3137"/>
strange

          <ptr target="#l13141" type="alt" xml:id="te3137"/>
things going on she was just in a sweat about every little thing that warn’t yard-stick straight; so she says, very decided:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77541">
“You

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6150"/>
just

          <app from="pr6150" n="336.23 (695.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8241">
            <lem wit="A">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jest</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3138"/>
march

          <ptr target="#l13143" type="alt" xml:id="te3138"/>
into that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3139"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6151"/>
setting-room

          <app from="pr6151" n="336.23 (695.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8242">
            <lem wit="A">setting-room</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sett’n-room</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13145" type="alt" xml:id="te3139"/>
and stay there till I come. You been up to something you no business to, and I lay I’ll find out what it is before

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6152"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
m

          <app from="pr6152" n="336.25 (695.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8243">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
m

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’m</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
done with you.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77579">
So she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3140"/>
went away

          <ptr target="#l13147" type="alt" xml:id="te3140"/>
as I opened the door and walked into the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6153"/>
setting room

          <app from="pr6153" n="336.26–27 (695.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8244">
            <lem wit="MS2">setting room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">setting-room</rdg>
          </app>
. My, but there was a crowd there! Fifteen farmers, and every one of them had a gun. I was most powerful sick, and slunk to a chair and set down. They was setting around, some of them talking a little, in a low voice, and all of them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6154"/>
fidgety

          <app from="pr6154" n="336.30 (696.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8245">
            <lem wit="A">fidgety</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">fidgetty</rdg>
          </app>
and uneasy, but trying to look like they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6155"/>
warn’t;

          <app from="pr6155" n="336.31 (696.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8246">
            <lem wit="A">warn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wasn’t</rdg>
          </app>
but I knowed they was, because they was always taking off their hats, and putting them on, and scratching their heads, and changing their seats, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3141"/>
fumbling

          <ptr target="#l13149" type="alt" xml:id="te3141"/>
with their

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3142"/>
buttons.

          <ptr target="#l13151" type="alt" xml:id="te3142"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3143"/>
I warn’t

          <ptr target="#l13153" type="alt" xml:id="te3143"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6156"/>
easy,

          <app from="pr6156" n="336.34 (696.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8247">
            <lem wit="MS2">easy,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
easy

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
myself, but I didn’t take my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6157"/>
hat

          <app from="pr6157" n="336.34 (696.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8248">
            <lem wit="A">hat</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">hat</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
off, all the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3144"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6158"/>
same

          <app from="pr6158" n="336.35 (697.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8249">
            <lem wit="A">same</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">same, you can depend on it</rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#l13155" type="alt" xml:id="te3144"/>
        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y33701">
          <graphic url="y33701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">every one had a gun</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77654">
I did wish

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6159"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6159" n="336.36 (697.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8250">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally would come, and get done with me, and lick me, if she wanted to, and let me get away and tell Tom

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3145"/>
how

          <ptr target="#l13157" type="alt" xml:id="te3145"/>
we’d overdone this thing, and what a thundering hornet’s nest we’d

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3146"/>
got

          <ptr target="#l13159" type="alt" xml:id="te3146"/>
          <pb n="337" xml:id="pb0337"/>
ourselves into, so we could stop fooling around,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3147"/>
straight off

          <ptr target="#l13161" type="alt" xml:id="te3147"/>
, and clear out with Jim before these rips got out of patience and come for us.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77678">
At last she come, and begun to ask me questions, but I

          <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
answer them straight, I didn’t know which end

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3148"/>
of me

          <ptr target="#l13163" type="alt" xml:id="te3148"/>
was up; because these men was in such a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6160"/>
fidget,

          <app from="pr6160" n="337.6 (698.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8251">
            <lem wit="MS2">fidget,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
fidget

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, that some was wanting to start right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3149"/>
          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13165" type="alt" xml:id="te3149"/>
and lay for them desperadoes, and saying it warn’t but a few minutes to midnight; and others was trying to get them to hold on and wait for the sheep-signal; and here was aunty pegging away at the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3150"/>
questions,

          <ptr target="#l13167" type="alt" xml:id="te3150"/>
and me a shaking all over and ready to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3151"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6161"/>
sink down

          <app from="pr6161" n="337.10–11 (699.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8252">
            <lem wit="A">sink down</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">drop</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13169" type="alt" xml:id="te3151"/>
in my tracks I was that scared; and the place getting hotter and hotter, and the butter beginning to melt and run down my neck and behind my ears; and pretty soon, when one of them says, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6162"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
m

          <app from="pr6162" n="337.13 (699.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8253">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
m

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’m</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
for going and getting in the cabin

          <hi rend="italic">first</hi>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3152"/>
and right

          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
,

          <ptr target="#l13171" type="alt" xml:id="te3152"/>
and catching them when they come,” I most

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6163"/>
dropped

          <app from="pr6163" n="337.15 (699.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8254">
            <lem wit="A">dropped</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">died</rdg>
          </app>
; and a streak of butter come a trickling down my forehead, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6164"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6164" n="337.16 (699.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8255">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6165"/>
she

          <app from="pr6165" n="337.16 (699.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8256">
            <lem wit="A">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8257">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
see it,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3153"/>
and turns

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6166"/>
white

          <app from="pr6166" n="337.17 (699.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8258">
            <lem wit="A">white</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">as white</rdg>
          </app>
as a sheet,

          <ptr target="#l13173" type="alt" xml:id="te3153"/>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77778">
“For the land’s sake what

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
the matter with the child!—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3154"/>
he’s got the

          <ptr target="#l13175" type="alt" xml:id="te3154"/>
brain fever as shore as you’re born, and they’re oozing out!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77787">
And everybody runs to see, and she snatches off my hat, and out comes the bread, and what was left of the butter, and she grabbed me, and hugged me, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3155"/>
says

          <ptr target="#l13177" type="alt" xml:id="te3155"/>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77793">
“Oh, what a turn you did give me! and how glad and grateful I am

          <pb n="338" xml:id="pb0338"/>
it ain’t no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6167"/>
worse;

          <app from="pr6167" n="338.1 (701.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8259">
            <lem wit="A">worse;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">worse!</rdg>
          </app>
for luck’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6168"/>
against

          <app from="pr6168" n="338.1 (701.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8260">
            <lem wit="A">against</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">agin</rdg>
          </app>
us, and it never rains but it pours, and when I see that truck I thought we’d lost you, for I knowed by the color and all, it was just like your brains would be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6169"/>
if—Dear

          <app from="pr6169" n="338.3 (701.8–9)" type="e" xml:id="la8261">
            <lem wit="A">if—Dear</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">if they was to come out. Dear</rdg>
          </app>
, dear,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3156"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6170"/>
whydn’t

          <app from="pr6170" n="338.4 (701.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8262">
            <lem wit="MS2">whydn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">whyd’nt</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13179" type="alt" xml:id="te3156"/>
you

          <hi rend="italic">tell</hi>
me that was what you’d been down there for,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
wouldn’t a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3157"/>
cared

          <ptr target="#l13181" type="alt" xml:id="te3157"/>
. Now

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6171"/>
cler

          <app from="pr6171" n="338.5 (701.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8263">
            <lem wit="A">cler</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">clear</rdg>
          </app>
out to bed, and don’t lemme see no more of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6172"/>
you

          <app from="pr6172" n="338.6 (701.15)" type="e" xml:id="la8264">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ye</rdg>
          </app>
till morning!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77860">
I was up stairs in a second, and down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6173"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr6173" n="338.7 (702.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8265">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
in another one, and shinning through the dark for the lean-to. I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6174"/>
couldn’t

          <app from="pr6174" n="338.8 (702.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8266">
            <lem wit="A">couldn’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">could</rdg>
          </app>
hardly get my words out, I was so anxious; but I told Tom as quick as I could,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6175"/>
we

          <app from="pr6175" n="338.10 (702.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8267">
            <lem wit="A">we</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that we</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3158"/>
must

          <ptr target="#l13183" type="alt" xml:id="te3158"/>
jump for it, now, and not a minute to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3159"/>
lose

          <ptr target="#l13185" type="alt" xml:id="te3159"/>
—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6176"/>
the

          <app from="pr6176" n="338.10 (702.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8268">
            <lem wit="A">the</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8269">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
house full of men, yonder, with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3160"/>
guns!

          <ptr target="#l13187" type="alt" xml:id="te3160"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77907">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3161"/>
His eyes just blazed; and he says:

          <ptr target="#l13189" type="alt" xml:id="te3161"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77911">
“No!—is that so?

          <hi rend="italic">Ain’t</hi>
it bully! Why,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3162"/>
Huck,

          <ptr target="#l13191" type="alt" xml:id="te3162"/>
if it was to do over again, I bet I could fetch two

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3163"/>
hundred! If we could put it off

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6177"/>
till—

          <app from="pr6177" n="338.14 (703.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8270">
            <lem wit="MS2">till—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">till——</rdg>
          </app>
”

          <ptr target="#l13193" type="alt" xml:id="te3163"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77932">
“Hurry!

          <hi rend="italic">hurry!</hi>
” I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6178"/>
says. “Where’s

          <app from="pr6178" n="338.15 (703.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8271">
            <lem wit="A">says. “Where’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">says; “where’s</rdg>
          </app>
Jim?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77946">
“Right at your elbow; if you reach out your arm you can touch him. He’s dressed, and everything’s ready. Now we’ll slide out and give the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6179"/>
sheep-signal

          <app from="pr6179" n="338.18 (703.11–12)" type="e" xml:id="la8272">
            <lem wit="C">sheep-signal</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2 A">
sheep-

              <lb/>
signal

            </rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77958">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3164"/>
But then

          <ptr target="#l13195" type="alt" xml:id="te3164"/>
we heard the tramp of men, coming to the door,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3165"/>
and heard them begin to fumble with the padlock; and heard a man say:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e77965">
“I

          <hi rend="italic">told</hi>
you we’d be too soon; they haven’t come—the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6180"/>
door is

          <app from="pr6180" n="338.21 (704.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8273">
            <lem wit="A">door is</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">door’s</rdg>
          </app>
locked.

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6181"/>
Here—

          <app from="pr6181" n="338.22 (704.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8274">
            <lem wit="MS2">Here—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Here,</rdg>
          </app>
I’ll lock some of you into the cabin and you lay for ’em in the dark

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3166"/>
and kill ’em when they come

          <ptr target="#l13201" type="alt" xml:id="te3166"/>
; and the rest scatter around a piece, and listen if you can hear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6182"/>
’em

          <app from="pr6182" n="338.24 (704.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8275">
            <lem wit="A">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’m</rdg>
          </app>
coming.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y33901">
          <graphic url="y33901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">tom caught on a splinter</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78004">
So in they come, but couldn’t see us in the dark, and most trod on us whilst we was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3167"/>
hustling to get

          <ptr target="#l13203" type="alt" xml:id="te3167"/>
under the bed. But we got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6183"/>
under,

          <app from="pr6183" n="338.26 (704.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8276">
            <lem wit="MS2">under,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
under

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3168"/>
right, and out through the hole, swift but soft—Jim

          <ptr target="#l13205" type="alt" xml:id="te3168"/>
first, me next, and Tom last, which was according to Tom’s orders. Now we was in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6184"/>
lean-to

          <app from="pr6184" n="338.29 (704.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la8277">
            <lem wit="A">lean-to</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
lean-

              <lb/>
to

            </rdg>
          </app>
, and heard trampings close

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6185"/>
by,

          <app from="pr6185" n="338.29 (704.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8278">
            <lem wit="MS2">by,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
by

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
outside. So we crept to the door, and Tom stopped us there and put his eye to the crack, but couldn’t make out nothing, it was so dark; and whispered and said he would listen for the steps to get further, and when he nudged us Jim must glide out first, and him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3169"/>
last. So he set his ear to the crack and listened

          <ptr target="#l13207" type="alt" xml:id="te3169"/>
, and listened, and listened, and the steps a scraping around, out there,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3170"/>
all the time; and

          <ptr target="#l13209" type="alt" xml:id="te3170"/>
at last he nudged us, and we slid out, and stooped down,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3171"/>
not breathing,

          <ptr target="#l13211" type="alt" xml:id="te3171"/>
and not making the least noise, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3172"/>
slipped

          <ptr target="#l13213" type="alt" xml:id="te3172"/>
stealthy

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3173"/>
towards

          <ptr target="#l13215" type="alt" xml:id="te3173"/>
the fence, in Injun file, and got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3174"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l13217" type="alt" xml:id="te3174"/>
it, all right, and me and Jim over it; but Tom’s britches

          <pb n="339" xml:id="pb0339"/>
catched fast on a splinter on the top rail, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3175"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l13219" type="alt" xml:id="te3175"/>
he hear the steps coming, so he had to pull loose,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3176"/>
which

          <ptr target="#l13221" type="alt" xml:id="te3176"/>
snapped the splinter and made a noise; and as he dropped in our tracks and started, somebody sings out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78078">“Who’s that? Answer, or I’ll shoot!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78080">
But we didn’t answer; we just unfurled our heels

          <ptr target="#l13197" type="alt" xml:id="te3165"/>
and shoved. Then there was a rush, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6186"/>
          <hi rend="italic">bang, bang,</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3177"/>
          <hi rend="italic">bang!</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13223" type="alt" xml:id="te3177"/>
          <app from="pr6186" n="339.7 (705.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la8279">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">bang, bang, bang!</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">bang, bang, bang!</rdg>
          </app>
and the bullets fairly whizzed around us! We heard them sing out:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78097">
“

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3178"/>
Here they are!

          <ptr target="#l13225" type="alt" xml:id="te3178"/>
They’ve broke for the river! after ’em,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3179"/>
boys! And turn loose the dogs!”

          <ptr target="#l13227" type="alt" xml:id="te3179"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78106">
So

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3180"/>
here

          <ptr target="#l13229" type="alt" xml:id="te3180"/>
they come, full tilt. We could hear them, because they wore boots, and yelled, but we didn’t wear no boots, and didn’t yell. We was in the path to the mill; and when they got pretty close onto us, we dodged into the bush and let them go by, and then dropped in behind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3181"/>
them.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3182"/>
They’d had

          <ptr target="#l13233" type="alt" xml:id="te3182"/>
all the dogs shut up, so they wouldn’t scare off the robbers; but by this time somebody had let them loose, and here they come, making pow-wow enough for a million; but

          <pb n="340" xml:id="pb0340"/>
they was our dogs; so we stopped in our tracks till they catched up; and when they see it warn’t nobody but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3183"/>
us,

          <ptr target="#l13235" type="alt" xml:id="te3183"/>
and no excitement to offer them, they only just said howdy,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3184"/>
and tore

          <ptr target="#l13237" type="alt" xml:id="te3184"/>
right ahead towards the shouting and clattering; and then

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3185"/>
we

          <ptr target="#l13239" type="alt" xml:id="te3185"/>
up steam again and whizzed along after them till we

          <ptr target="#l13231" type="alt" xml:id="te3181"/>
was nearly to the mill,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3186"/>
and then

          <ptr target="#l13241" type="alt" xml:id="te3186"/>
struck up through the bush to where my canoe was tied, and hopped in and pulled for dear life

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3187"/>
towards

          <ptr target="#l13243" type="alt" xml:id="te3187"/>
the middle of the river, but didn’t make no more noise than we was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6187"/>
obleeged

          <app from="pr6187" n="340.8 (706.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8280">
            <lem wit="A">obleeged</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">obliged</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3188"/>
to.

          <ptr target="#l13245" type="alt" xml:id="te3188"/>
Then we struck out, easy and comfortable, for the island where my raft was; and we could hear them yelling

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3189"/>
and barking

          <ptr target="#l13247" type="alt" xml:id="te3189"/>
at each other all up and down the bank, till we was so far away the sounds got dim and died out. And when we stepped onto the raft, I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78160">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
, old Jim,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6188"/>
you

          <app from="pr6188" n="340.13 (707.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8281">
            <lem wit="A">you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you you</rdg>
          </app>
’re a free man

          <hi rend="italic">again</hi>
, and I bet you won’t ever be a slave

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3190"/>
no

          <ptr target="#l13249" type="alt" xml:id="te3190"/>
more.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78181">
“En a mighty good job

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3191"/>
it wuz,

          <ptr target="#l13251" type="alt" xml:id="te3191"/>
too, Huck.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3192"/>
It ’uz

          <ptr target="#l13253" type="alt" xml:id="te3192"/>
planned beautiful,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3193"/>
en

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3194"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l13255" type="alt" xml:id="te3193"/>
’uz

          <ptr target="#l13257" type="alt" xml:id="te3194"/>
          <hi rend="italic">done</hi>
beautiful; en

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3195"/>
dey

          <ptr target="#l13259" type="alt" xml:id="te3195"/>
ain’t

          <hi rend="italic">nobody</hi>
kin git up a plan dat’s mo’ mixed-up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3196"/>
en splendid

          <ptr target="#l13261" type="alt" xml:id="te3196"/>
den what dat one wuz.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78215">
We was all as glad as we could be, but Tom was the gladdest of all, because he had a bullet

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3197"/>
in the

          <ptr target="#l13263" type="alt" xml:id="te3197"/>
calf of his leg.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78221">
When me and Jim heard that, we

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3198"/>
didn’t

          <ptr target="#l13265" type="alt" xml:id="te3198"/>
feel so brash as what we did before. It was hurting him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6189"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr6189" n="340.21 (708.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8282">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3199"/>
and bleeding;

          <ptr target="#l13267" type="alt" xml:id="te3199"/>
so we laid him in the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3200"/>
wigwam

          <ptr target="#l13269" type="alt" xml:id="te3200"/>
and tore up one of the duke’s shirts

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3201"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l13271" type="alt" xml:id="te3201"/>
to bandage

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6190"/>
him;

          <app from="pr6190" n="340.23 (708.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8283">
            <lem wit="MS2">him;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">him,</rdg>
          </app>
but he says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78257">
“Gimme the rags, I can do it myself. Don’t

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3202"/>
stop,

          <ptr target="#l13273" type="alt" xml:id="te3202"/>
now; don’t fool around here, and the evasion booming along so

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6191"/>
handsome:

          <app from="pr6191" n="340.25 (708.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8284">
            <lem wit="MS2">handsome:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">handsome;</rdg>
          </app>
man the sweeps, and set her

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3203"/>
loose!

          <ptr target="#l13275" type="alt" xml:id="te3203"/>
Boys, we done it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3204"/>
elegant!

          <ptr target="#l13277" type="alt" xml:id="te3204"/>
—’deed we did.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0014"/>
I wish

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6192"/>
          <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
’d

          <app from="pr6192" n="340.27 (709.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8285">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">we’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a had the handling of Louis

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6193"/>
XVI

          <app from="pr6193" n="340.27 (709.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8286">
            <lem wit="MS2">XVI</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">XVI.</rdg>
          </app>
, there wouldn’t a been no ‘Son of Saint Louis, ascend to heaven!’

          <ptr target="#as0260" type="an" xml:id="tr0014"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3205"/>
wrote

          <ptr target="#l13279" type="alt" xml:id="te3205"/>
down in

          <hi rend="italic">his</hi>
biography: no, sir, we’d a whooped him over the

          <hi rend="italic">border</hi>
—that’s what we’d a done with

          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
—and done it just as slick as nothing at all,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3206"/>
too.

          <ptr target="#l13281" type="alt" xml:id="te3206"/>
Man the sweeps—man the sweeps!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78323">
But me and Jim was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3207"/>
consulting—

          <ptr target="#l13283" type="alt" xml:id="te3207"/>
and thinking. And after we’d thought a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3208"/>
minute,

          <ptr target="#l13285" type="alt" xml:id="te3208"/>
I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78333">“Say it, Jim.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78335">So he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78337">
“Well, den, dis is de way it look to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3209"/>
me,

          <ptr target="#l13287" type="alt" xml:id="te3209"/>
Huck.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3210"/>
Ef

          <ptr target="#l13289" type="alt" xml:id="te3210"/>
it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3211"/>
wuz

          <ptr target="#l13291" type="alt" xml:id="te3211"/>
          <hi rend="italic">him</hi>
dat

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3212"/>
’uz

          <ptr target="#l13293" type="alt" xml:id="te3212"/>
bein’ sot free, en one er de boys wuz to git shot, would he say, ‘Go on en save me, nemmine ’bout a doctor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6194"/>
f’r

          <app from="pr6194" n="340.38 (710.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8287">
            <lem wit="A">f’r</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">for</rdg>
          </app>
to save dis

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6195"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3213"/>
one?’

          <ptr target="#l13295" type="alt" xml:id="te3213"/>
          <app from="pr6195" n="340.38 (710.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8288">
            <lem wit="MS2">one?’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
one?

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3214"/>
Is

          <ptr target="#l13297" type="alt" xml:id="te3214"/>
          <pb n="341" xml:id="pb0341"/>
dat like

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6196"/>
mars

          <app from="pr6196" n="341.1 (710.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8289">
            <lem wit="MS2">mars</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Mars</rdg>
          </app>
Tom Sawyer? Would he say dat? You

          <hi rend="italic">bet</hi>
he wouldn’t!

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6197"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Well den—</hi>
          <app from="pr6197" n="341.2 (710.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8290">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
den—

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
, den,

            </rdg>
          </app>
is

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3215"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Jim</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13299" type="alt" xml:id="te3215"/>
gwyne to say it? No, sah—I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3216"/>
doan’

          <ptr target="#l13301" type="alt" xml:id="te3216"/>
budge a step out’n dis place, ’dout a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3217"/>
          <hi rend="italic">doctor;</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13303" type="alt" xml:id="te3217"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3218"/>
not

          <ptr target="#l13305" type="alt" xml:id="te3218"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6198"/>
ef

          <app from="pr6198" n="341.3 (710.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8291">
            <lem wit="MS2">ef</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">if</rdg>
          </app>
it’s forty year!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y34101">
          <graphic url="y34101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">jim advises a doctor</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78437">
I knowed he was white inside, and I reckoned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6199"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr6199" n="341.4 (711.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8292">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he would</rdg>
          </app>
say what he did say—so it was all right, now, and I told Tom I was agoing for a doctor. He raised

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6200"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr6200" n="341.6 (711.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8293">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
row about it, but me and Jim stuck to it and wouldn’t budge; so he was for crawling out and setting the raft loose himself; but we wouldn’t let him. Then he give us a piece of his mind—but it didn’t do no good.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78455">So when he see me getting the canoe ready, he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78457">
“Well, then, if you’re bound to go, I’ll tell you the way to do, when you get to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6201"/>
village.

          <app from="pr6201" n="341.12 (712.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8294">
            <lem wit="A">village.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
village

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8295">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Shut the door, and blindfold the doctor tight and fast, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0015"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3219"/>
make him swear

          <ptr target="#l13307" type="alt" xml:id="te3219"/>
to be silent as the grave, and put a purse

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3220"/>
full

          <ptr target="#l13309" type="alt" xml:id="te3220"/>
of gold in his hand

          <ptr target="#as0261" type="an" xml:id="tr0015"/>
, and then take and lead him all around the back alleys and everywheres, in the dark, and then fetch him here in the canoe,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3221"/>
in a roundabout way amongst the islands,

          <ptr target="#l13311" type="alt" xml:id="te3221"/>
and

          <pb n="342" xml:id="pb0342"/>
search him and take his chalk away from him, and don’t give it back to him till you get him back to the village, or else he will chalk this raft so he can find it again. It’s the way they all do.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78488">So I said I would, and left, and Jim was to hide in the woods when he see the doctor coming, till he was gone again.</p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0458">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XLI.</head>
        <pb n="343" xml:id="pb0343"/>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78494">
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y34301">
            <graphic url="y34301.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6202"/>
Chapter XLI.

              <app from="pr6202" n="343 title (713.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8296">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XLI.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8297">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">The</ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3431">
            <graphic url="hf3431.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">the doctor</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e78512">
doctor was an old

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6203"/>
man;

          <app from="pr6203" n="343.1 (713.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8298">
            <lem wit="A">man;</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
man

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8299">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
a very nice,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6204"/>
kind looking

          <app from="pr6204" n="343.2 (713.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8300">
            <lem wit="MS2">kind looking</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">kind-looking</rdg>
          </app>
old man, when I got him up. I told him me and my brother was over on Spanish

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6205"/>
island

          <app from="pr6205" n="343.4 (713.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8301">
            <lem wit="MS2">island</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Island</rdg>
          </app>
hunting, yesterday

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6206"/>
after noon

          <app from="pr6206" n="343.5 (713.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8302">
            <lem wit="MS2">after noon</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">afternoon</rdg>
          </app>
, and camped on a piece of a raft we found, and about midnight he must a kicked his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3222"/>
gun

          <ptr target="#l13313" type="alt" xml:id="te3222"/>
in his dreams, for it went off and shot him in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6207"/>
leg;

          <app from="pr6207" n="343.9 (713.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la8303">
            <lem wit="MS2">leg;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">leg,</rdg>
          </app>
and we wanted him to go over there and fix it and not say nothing about it, nor let anybody know, because we wanted to come home this evening, and surprise the folks.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78562">“Who is your folks?” he says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78564">“The Phelpses, down yonder.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78566">“Oh,” he says. And after a minute, he says: “How’d you say he got shot?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78568">“He had a dream,” I says, “and it shot him.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78570">“Singular dream,” he says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78572">
So he lit up his lantern, and got his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6208"/>
saddlebags

          <app from="pr6208" n="343.21 (714.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8304">
            <lem wit="MS2">saddlebags</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">saddle-bags</rdg>
          </app>
, and we started. But when he see the canoe, he didn’t like the look of her—said she was big enough for one, but didn’t look pretty safe for two. I says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78582">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6209"/>
O

          <app from="pr6209" n="343.24 (715.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8305">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, you needn’t be

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3223"/>
afeard,

          <ptr target="#l13315" type="alt" xml:id="te3223"/>
sir, she carried the three of us, easy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6210"/>
enough.

          <app from="pr6210" n="343.25 (715.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8306">
            <lem wit="A">enough.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">enough?</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78606">“What three?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78608">
“Why, me and Sid, and—and—and

          <hi rend="italic">the guns;</hi>
that’s what I mean.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78613">“Oh,” he says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78615">
But he put his foot on the gunnel, and rocked her; and shook his head, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3224"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l13317" type="alt" xml:id="te3224"/>
he reckoned

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6211"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr6211" n="343.30 (715.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8307">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he would</rdg>
          </app>
look around for a bigger one. But they was all locked and chained; so he took my canoe, and said for

          <pb n="344" xml:id="pb0344"/>
me to wait till he come back, or I could hunt around further, or maybe I better go down home and get them ready for the surprise, if I wanted to. But I said I didn’t;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6212"/>
so

          <app from="pr6212" n="344.3 (716.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8308">
            <lem wit="A">so</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and so</rdg>
          </app>
I told him just how to find the raft, and then he started.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78640">
I struck an idea, pretty soon. I says to myself,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3225"/>
spos’n

          <ptr target="#l13319" type="alt" xml:id="te3225"/>
he can’t fix that leg just in three shakes of a sheep’s tail, as the saying is? spos’n it takes him three or four days? What are

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6213"/>
we

          <app from="pr6213" n="344.7 (717.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8309">
            <lem wit="A">we</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">we</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
going to do?—lay around there till he lets the cat out of the bag? No, sir, I know what

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6214"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I’ll</hi>
          <app from="pr6214" n="344.9 (717.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8310">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’ll

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’ll</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6215"/>
do.

          <app from="pr6215" n="344.9 (717.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8311">
            <lem wit="A">do.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">do:</rdg>
          </app>
I’ll wait, and when he comes back, if he says he’s got to go any more, I’ll get down there, too, if I swim; and we’ll

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6216"/>
take and

          <app from="pr6216" n="344.10 (717.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8312">
            <lem wit="A">take and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8313">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
tie him, and keep him, and shove out down the river; and when Tom’s done with him,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6217"/>
we

          <app from="pr6217" n="344.12 (717.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8314">
            <lem wit="A">we</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">we’ve</rdg>
          </app>
’ll give him what it’s worth, or all we got, and then let him get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6218"/>
ashore

          <app from="pr6218" n="344.13 (717.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8315">
            <lem wit="MS2">ashore</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">shore</rdg>
          </app>
.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y34401">
          <graphic url="y34401.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">uncle silas in danger</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78706">
So then I crept into a lumber pile to get some sleep; and next time I waked up the sun was away up

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6219"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tb0084"/>
over my head

          <ptr target="#tn0084" type="te" xml:id="tv0084"/>
          <app from="pr6219" n="344.15 (718.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la8316">
            <lem wit="A">over my head</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
over-

              <lb/>
head

            </rdg>
          </app>
! I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6220"/>
shot out,

          <app from="pr6220" n="344.15 (718.2–3)" type="e" xml:id="la8317">
            <lem wit="C">shot out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">shinned out of that,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">shot out</rdg>
          </app>
and went for the doctor’s house, but they told me he’d gone away in the night, some time or other, and warn’t back yet. Well, thinks I, that looks

          <pb n="345" xml:id="pb0345"/>
powerful bad for Tom, and I’ll dig out for the island, right off. So away I shoved, and turned the corner, and nearly

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3226"/>
rammed my head

          <ptr target="#l13321" type="alt" xml:id="te3226"/>
into

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6221"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6221" n="345.3 (718.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8318">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas’s stomach! He says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78745">
“Why,

          <hi rend="italic">
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3227"/>
Tom!

            <ptr target="#l13323" type="alt" xml:id="te3227"/>
          </hi>
Where you been, all this time, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6222"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3228"/>
rascal

          <ptr target="#l13325" type="alt" xml:id="te3228"/>
?

          <app from="pr6222" n="345.4 (719.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8319">
            <lem wit="A">rascal?</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rascal!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78763">
“

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
hain’t been nowheres,” I says, “only just hunting for the runaway nigger—me and Sid.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78768">“Why, where ever did you go?” he says. “Your aunt’s been mighty uneasy.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78770">
“She needn’t,” I says, “because we was all right. We followed the men and the dogs, but they

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6223"/>
outrun

          <app from="pr6223" n="345.10 (719.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8320">
            <lem wit="MS2">outrun</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">out-run</rdg>
          </app>
us, and we lost them; but we thought we heard them on the water, so we got a canoe and took out after them, and crossed

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6224"/>
over,

          <app from="pr6224" n="345.12 (719.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8321">
            <lem wit="MS2">over,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
over

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
but couldn’t find nothing of them; so we cruised along

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6225"/>
up shore

          <app from="pr6225" n="345.13 (720.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8322">
            <lem wit="MS2">up shore</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">up-shore</rdg>
          </app>
till we got kind of tired and beat out; and tied up the canoe and went to sleep, and never waked up till about an hour ago, then we paddled over here to hear the news, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3229"/>
Sid’s

          <ptr target="#l13327" type="alt" xml:id="te3229"/>
at the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6226"/>
postoffice

          <app from="pr6226" n="345.16 (720.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8323">
            <lem wit="MS2">postoffice</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">post-office</rdg>
          </app>
to see what he can hear, and I’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6227"/>
a-branching

          <app from="pr6227" n="345.16 (720.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8324">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-branching</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a branching</rdg>
          </app>
out to get something to eat for us, and then we’re going home.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78819">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3230"/>
So

          <ptr target="#l13329" type="alt" xml:id="te3230"/>
then we went to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6228"/>
postoffice

          <app from="pr6228" n="345.18 (720.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8325">
            <lem wit="MS2">postoffice</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">post-office</rdg>
          </app>
to get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3231"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6229"/>
‘Sid’

          <app from="pr6229" n="345.18 (720.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8326">
            <lem wit="MS2">‘Sid’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“Sid”</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13331" type="alt" xml:id="te3231"/>
;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6230"/>
but,

          <app from="pr6230" n="345.18 (720.15)" type="e" xml:id="la8327">
            <lem wit="C">but,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">but</rdg>
          </app>
just as I suspicioned, he warn’t there; so the old man he got a letter out of the office, and we waited a while

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6231"/>
longer,

          <app from="pr6231" n="345.20 (721.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8328">
            <lem wit="MS2">longer,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
longer

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
but

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3232"/>
Sid

          <ptr target="#l13333" type="alt" xml:id="te3232"/>
didn’t come; so the old man said come along,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3233"/>
let

          <ptr target="#l13335" type="alt" xml:id="te3233"/>
Sid

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3234"/>
foot it

          <ptr target="#l13337" type="alt" xml:id="te3234"/>
home, or canoe-it, when he got done fooling around—but we would ride. I couldn’t get him to let me stay and wait for Sid;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6232"/>
and he

          <app from="pr6232" n="345.23 (721.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8329">
            <lem wit="A">and he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he</rdg>
          </app>
said there warn’t no use in it, and I must come along, and let

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6233"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6233" n="345.24 (721.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8330">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally see we was all right.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78891">
When we got home,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6234"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6234" n="345.25 (721.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8331">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally was that glad to see me she laughed and cried both, and hugged me, and give me one of them lickings of hern that don’t amount to shucks, and said she’d serve Sid the same when he come.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78901">And the place was plumb full of farmers and farmers’ wives, to dinner; and such another clack a body never heard. Old Mrs. Hotchkiss was the worst; her tongue was agoing all the time. She says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e78903">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0016"/>
Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6235"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6235" n="345.32 (722.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8332">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Phelps

          <ptr target="#as0262" type="an" xml:id="tr0016"/>
, I’ve ransacked that-air cabin

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6236"/>
over,

          <app from="pr6236" n="345.32 (722.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8333">
            <lem wit="MS2">over,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
over

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
an’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="prg236"/>
I

          <app from="prg236" n="345.32 (722.15)" type="e" xml:id="lag333">
            <lem wit="A">I</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
b’lieve the nigger was crazy. I says so to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6238"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6238" n="345.33 (722.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8335">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Damrell—didn’t I,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6239"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6239" n="345.34 (722.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8336">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Damrell?—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6240"/>
s’I,

          <app from="pr6240" n="345.34 (723.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8337">
            <lem wit="A">s’I,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">S’I,</rdg>
          </app>
he’s crazy, s’I—them’s the very words I said. You all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3235"/>
hearn

          <ptr target="#l13339" type="alt" xml:id="te3235"/>
me: he’s crazy, s’I; everything shows it, s’I. Look at that-air grindstone,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6241"/>
s’I:

          <app from="pr6241" n="345.36 (723.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8338">
            <lem wit="MS2">s’I:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">s’I;</rdg>
          </app>
want to tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6242"/>
          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
’t

          <app from="pr6242" n="345.36 (723.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8339">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
’t

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">me ’t</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
’t

            </rdg>
          </app>
any cretur ’ts in his right mind ’s agoin’ to scrabble all them crazy things onto a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6243"/>
grindstone

          <app from="pr6243" n="345.37 (723.9–10)" type="e" xml:id="la8340">
            <lem wit="A">grindstone</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
grind-

              <lb/>
stone

            </rdg>
          </app>
, s’I? Here sich

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3236"/>
’n’ sich

          <ptr target="#l13341" type="alt" xml:id="te3236"/>
a person busted his heart; ’n’ here so ’n’ so

          <pb n="346" xml:id="pb0346"/>
pegged along for thirty-seven year,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6244"/>
’n’

          <app from="pr6244" n="346.1 (723.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8341">
            <lem wit="A">’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and</rdg>
          </app>
all that—natcherl son

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3237"/>
o’

          <ptr target="#l13343" type="alt" xml:id="te3237"/>
Louis somebody, ’n’ sich

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6245"/>
everlast’n

          <app from="pr6245" n="346.2 (723.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la8342">
            <lem wit="A">everlast’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
ever-

              <lb/>
last’n

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6246"/>
rubbage

          <app from="pr6246" n="346.2 (723.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8343">
            <lem wit="A">rubbage</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">rot</rdg>
          </app>
. He’s plumb crazy, s’I; it’s what I says in the fust place, it’s what I says in the middle,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6247"/>
’n’ it’s

          <app from="pr6247" n="346.3 (724.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8344">
            <lem wit="A">’n’ it’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’n’ its</rdg>
          </app>
what I says last

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6248"/>
’n’

          <app from="pr6248" n="346.4 (724.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8345">
            <lem wit="A">’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">and</rdg>
          </app>
all the time—the nigger’s crazy—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6249"/>
crazy’s

          <app from="pr6249" n="346.4 (724.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8346">
            <lem wit="A">crazy’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">crazy as</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0017"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3238"/>
Nebokoodneezer

          <ptr target="#l13345" type="alt" xml:id="te3238"/>
          <ptr target="#as0263" type="an" xml:id="tr0017"/>
, s’I.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79067">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6250"/>
An’

          <app from="pr6250" n="346.6 (724.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8347">
            <lem wit="A">An’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">And</rdg>
          </app>
look at that-air ladder made out’n rags,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6251"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6251" n="346.6 (724.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8348">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Hotchkiss,” says old Mrs. Damrell, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6252"/>
what

          <app from="pr6252" n="346.7 (724.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8349">
            <lem wit="A">what</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">What</rdg>
          </app>
in the name

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6253"/>
o’

          <app from="pr6253" n="346.7 (724.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8350">
            <lem wit="A">o’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
goodness

          <hi rend="italic">could</hi>
he ever want

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6254"/>
of—

          <app from="pr6254" n="346.8 (724.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8351">
            <lem wit="MS2">of—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">of——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79113">
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y34601">
            <graphic url="y34601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">old mrs. hotchkiss</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79119">
“The very words I was a-sayin’ no longer ago

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3239"/>
th’n

          <ptr target="#l13347" type="alt" xml:id="te3239"/>
this minute to

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0018"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6255"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6255" n="346.10 (724.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8352">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Utterback

          <ptr target="#as0264" type="an" xml:id="tr0018"/>
, ’n’ she’ll tell you so herself. Sh-she, look at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6256"/>
that-air

          <app from="pr6256" n="346.10–11 (725.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la8353">
            <lem wit="A">that-air</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
that-

              <lb/>
air

            </rdg>
          </app>
rag ladder, sh-she; ’n’ s’I, yes,

          <hi rend="italic">look</hi>
at it, s’I—what

          <hi rend="italic">could</hi>
he a wanted of it, s’I.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3240"/>
Sh-she

          <ptr target="#l13349" type="alt" xml:id="te3240"/>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6257"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6257" n="346.12 (725.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8354">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Hotchkiss,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6258"/>
sh-she—

          <app from="pr6258" n="346.12 (725.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8355">
            <lem wit="MS2">sh-she—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sh-she——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79174">
“But how in the nation’d they ever

          <hi rend="italic">git</hi>
that grindstone

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6259"/>
          <hi rend="italic">in</hi>
          <app from="pr6259" n="346.13 (725.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8356">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">in</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">in</rdg>
          </app>
there,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6260"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3241"/>
          <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
way

          <app from="pr6260" n="346.14 (725.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8357">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
way

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
-

              <lb/>
way

            </rdg>
          </app>
? ’n’

          <ptr target="#l13351" type="alt" xml:id="te3241"/>
who dug that-air

          <hi rend="italic">hole?</hi>
’n’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6261"/>
who—”

          <app from="pr6261" n="346.14 (725.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8358">
            <lem wit="C">who—”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
who—’

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8359">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">who——”</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79223">
“My very

          <hi rend="italic">words</hi>
, Brer Penrod! I was a-sayin’—pass that-air sasser o’ m’lasses, won’t ye?—I was a-sayin’ to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6262"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6262" n="346.16 (725.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8360">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Dunlap, jist this minute, how

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
they git that grindstone in there, s’I. Without

          <hi rend="italic">help</hi>
, mind you—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3242"/>
’thout

          <ptr target="#l13353" type="alt" xml:id="te3242"/>
          <hi rend="italic">help! Thar’s</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3243"/>
wher’

          <ptr target="#l13355" type="alt" xml:id="te3243"/>
’tis. Don’t tell

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
, s’I; there

          <hi rend="italic">wuz</hi>
help, s’I; ’n’ ther’

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6263"/>
wuz

          <app from="pr6263" n="346.19 (726.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8361">
            <lem wit="A">wuz</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">was</rdg>
          </app>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6264"/>
          <hi rend="italic">plenty</hi>
          <app from="pr6264" n="346.19 (726.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8362">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">plenty</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">plenty o’</rdg>
          </app>
help, too, s’I;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3244"/>
ther’s

          <ptr target="#l13357" type="alt" xml:id="te3244"/>
ben a

          <hi rend="italic">dozen</hi>
a-helpin’ that nigger,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6265"/>
’n’

          <app from="pr6265" n="346.20 (726.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8363">
            <lem wit="A">’n’</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">an’</rdg>
          </app>
I lay I’d skin every last nigger on this place, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6266"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I’</hi>
d

          <app from="pr6266" n="346.21 (726.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8364">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’d

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">I’d</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
find out who done it, s’I; ’n’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3245"/>
moreover,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6267"/>
s’I—

          <app from="pr6267" n="346.21 (726.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8365">
            <lem wit="MS2">s’I—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">s’I——</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13359" type="alt" xml:id="te3245"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79318">
“A

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6268"/>
          <hi rend="italic">dozen</hi>
,

          <app from="pr6268" n="346.22 (726.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8366">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">dozen</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">dozen</hi>
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
says you!—

          <hi rend="italic">forty</hi>
couldn’t a done everything that’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6269"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3246"/>
been

          <ptr target="#l13361" type="alt" xml:id="te3246"/>
          <app from="pr6269" n="346.22 (726.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8367">
            <lem wit="A">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ben</rdg>
          </app>
done. Look at them

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6270"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3247"/>
caseknife

          <ptr target="#l13363" type="alt" xml:id="te3247"/>
          <app from="pr6270" n="346.23 (727.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8368">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknife</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knife</rdg>
          </app>
saws and things, how tedious they’ve

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3248"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6271"/>
been

          <app from="pr6271" n="346.24 (727.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8369">
            <lem wit="A">been</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ben</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13365" type="alt" xml:id="te3248"/>
made; look at that bed-leg sawed off with ’m, a week’s work

          <pb n="347" xml:id="pb0347"/>
for six men;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3249"/>
look at that nigger made out’n straw on the bed;

          <ptr target="#l13367" type="alt" xml:id="te3249"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6272"/>
and

          <app from="pr6272" n="347.1 (727.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8370">
            <lem wit="A">and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’n’</rdg>
          </app>
look

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6273"/>
at—

          <app from="pr6273" n="347.2 (727.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8371">
            <lem wit="MS2">at—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">at——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79391">
“You may

          <hi rend="italic">well</hi>
say it, Brer Hightower! It’s jist as I was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3250"/>
a-sayin’

          <ptr target="#l13369" type="alt" xml:id="te3250"/>
to Brer Phelps, his own self.

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tb0085"/>
S’e, what do

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
think of it,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6274"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6274" n="347.4 (727.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8372">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3251"/>
Hotchkiss

          <ptr target="#l13371" type="alt" xml:id="te3251"/>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="ta0085"/>
s’e; think

          <app from="ta0085" n="347.5 (727.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8373">
            <lem wit="MS2">s’e; think</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">s’e? think</rdg>
          </app>
o’ what, Brer Phelps,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6276"/>
s’I;

          <app from="pr6276" n="347.5 (727.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8374">
            <lem wit="MS2">s’I;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">s’I?</rdg>
          </app>
think o’ that bed-leg sawed off that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6277"/>
a

          <app from="pr6277" n="347.6 (727.17)" type="e" xml:id="la8375">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8376">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
way,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6278"/>
s’e;

          <ptr target="#tn0085" type="te" xml:id="tv0085"/>
          <app from="pr6278" n="347.6 (727.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la8377">
            <lem wit="MS2">s’e;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">s’e?</rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">think</hi>
of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6279"/>
it? s’I;

          <app from="pr6279" n="347.6 (727.18)" type="hc" xml:id="la8378">
            <lem wit="MS2">it? s’I;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">it, s’I?</rdg>
          </app>
I lay it never sawed

          <hi rend="italic">itself</hi>
off, s’I—somebody

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3252"/>
          <hi rend="italic">sawed</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13373" type="alt" xml:id="te3252"/>
it, s’I; that’s my opinion, take it or leave it, it mayn’t be no

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3253"/>
’count

          <ptr target="#l13375" type="alt" xml:id="te3253"/>
, s’I, but sich

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6280"/>
as ’t

          <app from="pr6280" n="347.8 (728.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8379">
            <lem wit="A">as ’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">as it</rdg>
          </app>
is, it’s my opinion, s’I, ’n’ if anybody

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6281"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr6281" n="347.9 (728.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8380">
            <lem wit="A">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kin</rdg>
          </app>
start a better one, s’I, let him

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
it, s’I, that’s all. I says to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6282"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6282" n="347.10 (728.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8381">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Dunlap,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6283"/>
s’I—

          <app from="pr6283" n="347.10 (728.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8382">
            <lem wit="MS2">s’I—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">s’I——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79513">
“Why, dog my cats, they must a ben a house-full o’ niggers in there every night for four weeks, to a done all that work,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6284"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6284" n="347.12 (728.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8383">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Phelps. Look at that shirt—every last inch of it kivered

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3254"/>
over

          <ptr target="#l13377" type="alt" xml:id="te3254"/>
with secret African

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6285"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3255"/>
writ’n,

          <ptr target="#l13379" type="alt" xml:id="te3255"/>
          <app from="pr6285" n="347.14 (729.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8384">
            <lem wit="MS2">writ’n,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">writ’n</rdg>
          </app>
done with blood! Must a ben a raft uv ’m at it right along, all the time, amost. Why, I’d give two dollars to have it read to me; ’n’ as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3256"/>
for

          <ptr target="#l13381" type="alt" xml:id="te3256"/>
the niggers that wrote it, I ’low I’d take ’n’ lash ’m

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6286"/>
t’ll—

          <app from="pr6286" n="347.17 (729.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8385">
            <lem wit="C">t’ll—</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">till—</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">t’ll——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79552">
“People to

          <hi rend="italic">help</hi>
him, Brother Marples! Well, I reckon you’d

          <hi rend="italic">think</hi>
so, if you’d a been in this house for a while back. Why, they’ve stole everything they could lay their hands on—and we a watching, all the time, mind you. They stole that shirt right off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3257"/>
o’

          <ptr target="#l13383" type="alt" xml:id="te3257"/>
the line! and as for that sheet they made the rag ladder out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6287"/>
of,

          <app from="pr6287" n="347.22 (730.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8386">
            <lem wit="MS2">of,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
of

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3258"/>
ther’

          <ptr target="#l13385" type="alt" xml:id="te3258"/>
ain’t no telling how many times they

          <hi rend="italic">didn’t</hi>
steal that; and flour, and candles, and candlesticks, and spoons, and the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3259"/>
old

          <ptr target="#l13387" type="alt" xml:id="te3259"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6288"/>
warming pan

          <app from="pr6288" n="347.24 (730.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8387">
            <lem wit="C">warming pan</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">warmin’ pan</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">warming-pan</rdg>
          </app>
, and most a thousand things that I disremember, now, and my new calico dress; and me, and Silas, and my Sid and Tom on the constant watch day

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3260"/>
          <hi rend="italic">and</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13389" type="alt" xml:id="te3260"/>
night, as I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6289"/>
a-telling

          <app from="pr6289" n="347.27 (730.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8388">
            <lem wit="MS2">a-telling</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a telling</rdg>
          </app>
you, and not

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3261"/>
a one

          <ptr target="#l13391" type="alt" xml:id="te3261"/>
of us could catch hide nor hair, nor sight nor sound of them; and here at the last minute, lo and behold you, they slides right in

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3262"/>
under

          <ptr target="#l13393" type="alt" xml:id="te3262"/>
our noses, and fools us, and not only fools

          <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
but the Injun Territory robbers too, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3263"/>
actuly

          <ptr target="#l13395" type="alt" xml:id="te3263"/>
gets

          <hi rend="italic">away</hi>
with that nigger, safe and sound, and that with sixteen men and twenty-two dogs right on their very heels at that very time! I tell you, it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6290"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3264"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l13397" type="alt" xml:id="te3264"/>
          <app from="pr6290" n="347.33 (731.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8389">
            <lem wit="A">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jest</rdg>
          </app>
bangs anything I ever

          <hi rend="italic">heard</hi>
of. Why,

          <hi rend="italic">sperits</hi>
couldn’t a done better, and been no smarter. And

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0019"/>
I reckon they must a

          <hi rend="italic">been</hi>
sperits

          <ptr target="#as0265" type="an" xml:id="tr0019"/>
—because,

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
know our dogs, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3265"/>
ther’

          <ptr target="#l13399" type="alt" xml:id="te3265"/>
ain’t no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6291"/>
better:

          <app from="pr6291" n="347.35 (732.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8390">
            <lem wit="MS2">better:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">better;</rdg>
          </app>
well, them dogs never even got on the

          <hi rend="italic">track</hi>
of ’m, once! You explain

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
to me, if you can!—

          <hi rend="italic">any</hi>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6292"/>
of you

          <app from="pr6292" n="347.37 (732.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8391">
            <lem wit="A">of you</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of ye</rdg>
          </app>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79683">
“Well, it does

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6293"/>
beat—

          <app from="pr6293" n="347.38 (732.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8392">
            <lem wit="MS2">beat—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">beat——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79693">
          <pb n="348" xml:id="pb0348"/>
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6294"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tb0086"/>
Laws

          <app from="pr6294" n="348.1 (732.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8393">
            <lem wit="A">Laws</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Land</rdg>
          </app>
alive

          <ptr target="#tn0086" type="te" xml:id="tv0086"/>
, I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6295"/>
never—

          <app from="pr6295" n="348.1 (732.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8394">
            <lem wit="MS2">never—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">never——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79716">
“So help me, I wouldn’t a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6296"/>
be—

          <app from="pr6296" n="348.2 (732.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8395">
            <lem wit="MS2">be—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">be——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79726">
“

          <hi rend="italic">House</hi>
-thieves as well

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6297"/>
as—

          <app from="pr6297" n="348.3 (732.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8396">
            <lem wit="MS2">as—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">as——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79739">
“Goodnessgracioussakes, I’d a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3266"/>
ben

          <ptr target="#l13401" type="alt" xml:id="te3266"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3267"/>
afeard

          <ptr target="#l13403" type="alt" xml:id="te3267"/>
to

          <hi rend="italic">live</hi>
in sich

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6298"/>
a—

          <app from="pr6298" n="348.4 (732.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8397">
            <lem wit="MS2">a—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">a——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79760">
“ ’Fraid to

          <hi rend="italic">live!</hi>
—why, I was that scared I dasn’t hardly go to bed, or get up, or lay down, or

          <hi rend="italic">set</hi>
down,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6299"/>
sister

          <app from="pr6299" n="348.6 (733.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8398">
            <lem wit="MS2">sister</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sister</rdg>
          </app>
Ridgeway. Why,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3268"/>
they’d

          <ptr target="#l13405" type="alt" xml:id="te3268"/>
steal the very—why, goodness sakes, you can guess what kind of a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3269"/>
fluster

          <ptr target="#l13407" type="alt" xml:id="te3269"/>
          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
was in by the time midnight come, last

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3270"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6300"/>
night.

          <app from="pr6300" n="348.8 (733.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8399">
            <lem wit="A">night.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">night:</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13409" type="alt" xml:id="te3270"/>
I hope to gracious if I warn’t afraid they’d steal some

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3271"/>
o’

          <ptr target="#l13411" type="alt" xml:id="te3271"/>
the family! I was just to that pass, I didn’t have no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6301"/>
reasoning

          <app from="pr6301" n="348.10 (733.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8400">
            <lem wit="A">reasoning</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">reasonin’</rdg>
          </app>
faculties no more. It looks foolish enough,

          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
, in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6302"/>
daytime

          <app from="pr6302" n="348.11 (733.15–16)" type="e" xml:id="la8401">
            <lem wit="C">daytime</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
day-

              <lb/>
time

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">day-time</rdg>
          </app>
; but I says to myself, there’s

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3272"/>
my

          <ptr target="#l13413" type="alt" xml:id="te3272"/>
two

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3273"/>
poor

          <ptr target="#l13415" type="alt" xml:id="te3273"/>
boys

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6303"/>
asleep

          <app from="pr6303" n="348.12 (734.1–2)" type="e" xml:id="la8402">
            <lem wit="A">asleep</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
a-

              <lb/>
sleep

            </rdg>
          </app>
, ’way up stairs in that lonesome room, and I declare to goodness I was that uneasy

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6304"/>
’t

          <app from="pr6304" n="348.13 (734.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8403">
            <lem wit="A">’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">that</rdg>
          </app>
I crep’ up there and locked ’em in! I

          <hi rend="italic">did.</hi>
And anybody would. Because, you know, when you get scared, that way, and it keeps running on, and getting worse and worse, all the time, and your wits gets to addling, and you get to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6305"/>
doing

          <app from="pr6305" n="348.17 (734.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8404">
            <lem wit="A">doing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">doin’</rdg>
          </app>
all sorts

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3274"/>
o’

          <ptr target="#l13417" type="alt" xml:id="te3274"/>
wild things, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6306"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr6306" n="348.17 (734.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8405">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
you think to yourself, spos’n

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
was a boy, and was away up there, and the door ain’t locked, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6307"/>
you—

          <app from="pr6307" n="348.19 (735.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8406">
            <lem wit="MS2">you—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you——</rdg>
          </app>
” She stopped, looking kind of wondering, and then she turned her head around slow, and when her eye lit on me—I got up and took a walk.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79889">
Says I to myself, I can explain better how we come to not be in that room this morning, if I go out to one side and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3275"/>
study

          <ptr target="#l13419" type="alt" xml:id="te3275"/>
over it a little. So I done it. But I dasn’t go

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6308"/>
fur

          <app from="pr6308" n="348.24 (735.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8407">
            <lem wit="A">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
, or she’d a sent for me. And when it was late in the day, the people all went, and then I come in and told her the noise and shooting waked up

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3276"/>
me and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6309"/>
‘Sid,’

          <ptr target="#l13421" type="alt" xml:id="te3276"/>
          <app from="pr6309" n="348.26 (736.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8408">
            <lem wit="MS2">‘Sid,’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">“Sid,”</rdg>
          </app>
and the door was locked, and we wanted to see the fun, so we went down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6310"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr6310" n="348.28 (736.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8409">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
, and both of us got hurt a little, and we didn’t never want to try

          <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
no more. And then I went on and told her all what I told

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6311"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6311" n="348.30 (736.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8410">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas before; and then she said she’d forgive us, and maybe it was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6312"/>
all

          <app from="pr6312" n="348.31 (736.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8411">
            <lem wit="A">all</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8412">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
right

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6313"/>
enough,

          <app from="pr6313" n="348.31 (736.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8413">
            <lem wit="MS2">enough,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
enough

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
anyway, and about what a body might expect of boys, for all boys was a pretty harum-scarum lot, as

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6314"/>
fur

          <app from="pr6314" n="348.32 (737.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8414">
            <lem wit="A">fur</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">far</rdg>
          </app>
as she could see; and so, as long as no harm hadn’t come of it, she judged she better put in her time being grateful we was alive and well and she had us still, stead of fretting over what was past and done. So then she kissed me, and patted me on the head, and dropped into a kind of a brown study; and pretty soon jumps

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6315"/>
up

          <app from="pr6315" n="348.37 (737.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8415">
            <lem wit="MS2">up</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">up,</rdg>
          </app>
and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79969">
“Why, lawsamercy, it’s most night, and Sid not come yet! What

          <hi rend="italic">has</hi>
become of that boy?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79974">
          <pb n="349" xml:id="pb0349"/>
I see my chance; so I skips up and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79978">“I’ll run right up to town and get him,” I says.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79980">
“No you won’t,” she says. “You’ll stay right

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3277"/>
wher’

          <ptr target="#l13423" type="alt" xml:id="te3277"/>
you are;

          <hi rend="italic">
            <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3278"/>
one’s

            <ptr target="#l13425" type="alt" xml:id="te3278"/>
          </hi>
enough to be lost at a time. If he ain’t here to supper, your uncle ’ll go.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e79991">
Well, he warn’t there to supper; so right after

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6316"/>
supper,

          <app from="pr6316" n="349.6 (738.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8416">
            <lem wit="MS2">supper,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
supper

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
uncle went.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80001">
He come back about ten, a little bit uneasy; hadn’t run across

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3279"/>
Tom’s

          <ptr target="#l13427" type="alt" xml:id="te3279"/>
track. Aunt Sally was a good

          <hi rend="italic">deal</hi>
uneasy; but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6317"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6317" n="349.8 (739.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8417">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3280"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l13429" type="alt" xml:id="te3280"/>
said there warn’t no occasion to be—boys will be boys,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3281"/>
he said

          <ptr target="#l13431" type="alt" xml:id="te3281"/>
, and you’ll see this one turn up in the morning, all sound and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3282"/>
right.

          <ptr target="#l13433" type="alt" xml:id="te3282"/>
So she had to be satisfied. But she said she’d set up for him a while, anyway, and keep a light burning, so he could see it.

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y34901">
          <graphic url="y34901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">aunt sally talks to huck</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80036">
And then when I went up to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6318"/>
bed,

          <app from="pr6318" n="349.13 (739.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8418">
            <lem wit="MS2">bed,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
bed

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
she come up with

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6319"/>
me,

          <app from="pr6319" n="349.13 (739.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8419">
            <lem wit="MS2">me,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
me

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and fetched her candle, and tucked me in, and mothered me so good I felt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6320"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3283"/>
mean

          <ptr target="#l13435" type="alt" xml:id="te3283"/>
          <app from="pr6320" n="349.15 (740.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8420">
            <lem wit="MS2">mean</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mean,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3284"/>
and like I couldn’t look her in the face

          <ptr target="#l13437" type="alt" xml:id="te3284"/>
; and she set down on the bed and talked with me a long time, and said what a splendid boy Sid was, and didn’t seem to want to ever stop talking about him; and kept asking me every now and then, if I reckoned he could a got lost, or hurt, or maybe drownded, and might be laying at this minute, somewheres, suffering or dead, and she not by him to help

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6321"/>
him;

          <app from="pr6321" n="349.20 (740.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8421">
            <lem wit="MS2">him;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">him,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <pb n="350" xml:id="pb0350"/>
so the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3285"/>
tears

          <ptr target="#l13439" type="alt" xml:id="te3285"/>
would drip down, silent, and I would tell her

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6322"/>
that

          <app from="pr6322" n="350.1 (741.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8422">
            <lem wit="A">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8423">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Sid was all right, and would be home in the morning, sure; and she would squeeze my hand, or maybe kiss me, and tell me to say it again, and keep on saying it, because it done her good, and she was in so much trouble. And when she was going away, she looked down in my eyes, so steady and gentle, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80092">
“The door ain’t going to be locked, Tom; and there’s the window and the rod; but you’ll be good,

          <hi rend="italic">won’t</hi>
you? And you won’t go? For

          <hi rend="italic">my</hi>
sake.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80100">
Laws knows I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6323"/>
          <hi rend="italic">wanted</hi>
          <app from="pr6323" n="350.10 (742.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8424">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">wanted</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">wanted</rdg>
          </app>
to go, bad enough, to see about Tom, and was all intending to go; but after

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3286"/>
that

          <ptr target="#l13441" type="alt" xml:id="te3286"/>
, I wouldn’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6324"/>
a

          <app from="pr6324" n="350.11 (742.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8425">
            <lem wit="A">a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
went, not for kingdoms.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80124">
But she was on my mind, and Tom was on my mind; so I slept very restless. And twice I went down the rod, away in the night, and slipped around

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3287"/>
front,

          <ptr target="#l13443" type="alt" xml:id="te3287"/>
and see her setting there by her candle in the window with her eyes towards the road and the tears in them; and I wished I could do something for her, but I couldn’t, only to swear

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6325"/>
that

          <app from="pr6325" n="350.18 (743.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8426">
            <lem wit="A">that</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8427">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I wouldn’t never do nothing to grieve her any more. And the third time, I waked up at dawn, and slid down, and she was there yet, and her candle was most out, and her old gray head was resting on her hand, and she was asleep.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0463">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XLII.</head>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80142">
          <pb n="351" xml:id="pb0351"/>
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y35101">
            <graphic url="y35101.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6326"/>
Chapter XLII.

              <app from="pr6326" n="351 title (743.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8428">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter XLII.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8429">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6327"/>
The

              <app from="pr6327" n="351.1 (743.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8430">
                <lem wit="A">The</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">And the</rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3511">
            <graphic url="hf3511.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">tom sawyer wounded</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e80167">
old man was up town again, before breakfast, but couldn’t get no track of Tom; and both of them set at the table, thinking, and not saying nothing, and looking mournful, and their

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3288"/>
coffee

          <ptr target="#l13445" type="alt" xml:id="te3288"/>
getting cold, and not eating anything. And

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6328"/>
by and by

          <app from="pr6328" n="351.8 (744.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8431">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
the old man says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80181">“Did I give you the letter?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80183">“What letter?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80185">
“The one I got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6329"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3289"/>
yesterday,

          <ptr target="#l13447" type="alt" xml:id="te3289"/>
          <app from="pr6329" n="351.12 (744.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8432">
            <lem wit="MS2">yesterday,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
yesterday

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
out of the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6330"/>
postoffice

          <app from="pr6330" n="351.13 (744.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8433">
            <lem wit="MS2">postoffice</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">post-office</rdg>
          </app>
.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80205">“No, you didn’t give me no letter.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80207">“Well, I must a forgot it.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80209">
So he rummaged his pockets, and then went off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="mw0048"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3290"/>
somewheres where

          <ptr target="#l13449" type="alt" xml:id="te3290"/>
he had

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3291"/>
laid

          <ptr target="#l13451" type="alt" xml:id="te3291"/>
it down, and fetched it, and give it to her. She says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80220">
“Why, it’s from

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6331"/>
St.

          <app from="pr6331" n="351.19 (745.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la8434">
            <lem wit="A">St.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
St

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
Petersburg—it’s from

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3292"/>
Sis.”

          <ptr target="#l13453" type="alt" xml:id="te3292"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80233">
I allowed another walk would do me good; but I couldn’t stir. But before she could break it open, she dropped it and run—for she see something. And so did I. It was Tom Sawyer on a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6332"/>
mattrass

          <app from="pr6332" n="351.22 (745.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8435">
            <lem wit="MS2">mattrass</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mattress</rdg>
          </app>
; and that old doctor; and Jim, in

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6333"/>
          <hi rend="italic">her</hi>
          <app from="pr6333" n="351.23 (745.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8436">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">her</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">her</rdg>
          </app>
calico dress, with his hands tied behind

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3293"/>
him;

          <ptr target="#l13455" type="alt" xml:id="te3293"/>
and a lot of people. I hid the letter

          <ptr target="#mt0048" type="alt" xml:id="wn0048"/>
behind the first thing that come handy, and rushed. She flung herself

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3294"/>
at

          <ptr target="#l13457" type="alt" xml:id="te3294"/>
Tom,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3295"/>
crying

          <ptr target="#l13459" type="alt" xml:id="te3295"/>
, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80269">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6334"/>
O

          <app from="pr6334" n="351.26 (746.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8437">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, he’s dead, he’s dead,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3296"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l13461" type="alt" xml:id="te3296"/>
know he’s dead!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80283">And Tom he turned his head a little, and muttered something or other, which showed he warn’t in his right mind; then she flung up her hands, and says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80285">
“He’s alive, thank God! And that’s enough!” and she snatched a

          <pb n="352" xml:id="pb0352"/>
kiss of him, and flew for the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6335"/>
house,

          <app from="pr6335" n="352.1 (746.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8438">
            <lem wit="MS2">house,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
house

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to get the bed ready,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3297"/>
and scattering

          <ptr target="#l13463" type="alt" xml:id="te3297"/>
orders

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3298"/>
right and left

          <ptr target="#l13465" type="alt" xml:id="te3298"/>
at the niggers and everybody else, as fast as her tongue could go, every jump of the way.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80306">
I followed the men to see what they was going to do with Jim; and the old doctor and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6336"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6336" n="352.5 (747.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8439">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas followed after Tom into the house. The men was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3299"/>
very

          <ptr target="#l13467" type="alt" xml:id="te3299"/>
huffy, and some of them wanted to hang Jim, for an

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3300"/>
example

          <ptr target="#l13469" type="alt" xml:id="te3300"/>
to all the other niggers around there, so they wouldn’t be trying to run away, like Jim done, and making such a raft of trouble, and keeping a whole family scared most to death for days and nights. But the others said, don’t do it, it wouldn’t answer at all, he ain’t our nigger, and his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3301"/>
owner

          <ptr target="#l13471" type="alt" xml:id="te3301"/>
would turn up and make us pay for him, sure. So that

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3302"/>
cooled

          <ptr target="#l13473" type="alt" xml:id="te3302"/>
them down a little, because the people that’s always the most anxious for to hang a nigger that hain’t done just right, is always the very ones that ain’t the most anxious to pay for him when they’ve got their satisfaction out of him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80333">
They cussed Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6337"/>
considerble

          <app from="pr6337" n="352.16 (749.3–4)" type="e" xml:id="la8440">
            <lem wit="A">considerble</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">considerable</rdg>
          </app>
, though, and give him a cuff or two, side the head, once in a while, but Jim never said nothing, and he never let on to know me, and they took him to the same cabin, and put his own clothes on him, and chained him again, and not to no bed-leg, this time, but to a big staple drove into the bottom log, and chained his hands, too, and both legs, and said he warn’t to have nothing but bread and water to eat, after this, till his owner come or

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3303"/>
he was

          <ptr target="#l13475" type="alt" xml:id="te3303"/>
sold at

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6338"/>
auction

          <app from="pr6338" n="352.23 (750.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8441">
            <lem wit="MS2">auction</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">auction,</rdg>
          </app>
because he didn’t come in a certain length of time, and filled up our hole, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3304"/>
said

          <ptr target="#l13477" type="alt" xml:id="te3304"/>
a couple of farmers with guns

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3305"/>
must

          <ptr target="#l13479" type="alt" xml:id="te3305"/>
stand watch around about

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3306"/>
the cabin

          <ptr target="#l13481" type="alt" xml:id="te3306"/>
every night, and a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6339"/>
bulldog

          <app from="pr6339" n="352.26 (750.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8442">
            <lem wit="MS2">bulldog</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">bull-dog</rdg>
          </app>
tied to the door in the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6340"/>
daytime,

          <app from="pr6340" n="352.26 (750.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8443">
            <lem wit="MS2">daytime,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">day-time;</rdg>
          </app>
and about this time they was through with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3307"/>
the job

          <ptr target="#l13483" type="alt" xml:id="te3307"/>
and was tapering off

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3308"/>
with a

          <ptr target="#l13485" type="alt" xml:id="te3308"/>
kind of

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6341"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3309"/>
generl

          <ptr target="#l13487" type="alt" xml:id="te3309"/>
          <app from="pr6341" n="352.27 (750.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8444">
            <lem wit="A">generl</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">a general</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6342"/>
goodbye

          <app from="pr6342" n="352.28 (750.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8445">
            <lem wit="MS2">goodbye</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">good-bye</rdg>
          </app>
cussing, and then the old doctor

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6343"/>
comes,

          <app from="pr6343" n="352.28 (750.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8446">
            <lem wit="MS2">comes,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
comes

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and takes a look, and says:

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y35301">
          <graphic url="y35301.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">the doctor speaks for jim</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80425">
“Don’t be no rougher on him than you’re obleeged to, because

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0020"/>
he ain’t a bad nigger

          <ptr target="#as0266" type="an" xml:id="tr0020"/>
. When I got to where I found the boy, I see I couldn’t cut the bullet out without some help, and he warn’t in no condition

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3310"/>
for me

          <ptr target="#l13489" type="alt" xml:id="te3310"/>
to leave, to go and get

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3311"/>
help; and

          <ptr target="#l13491" type="alt" xml:id="te3311"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3312"/>
he got a little worse and a little worse, and after a long time he went out of his

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3313"/>
head, and wouldn’t let me come anigh him,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3314"/>
any more,

          <ptr target="#l13497" type="alt" xml:id="te3314"/>
and said if I chalked his raft he’d kill me, and no end of wild foolishness like that, and I see I couldn’t do anything at all with him; so I

          <ptr target="#l13495" type="alt" xml:id="te3313"/>
says, I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3315"/>
got

          <ptr target="#l13499" type="alt" xml:id="te3315"/>
to have

          <hi rend="italic">help</hi>
, somehow; and the minute I says it, out crawls this nigger from

          <pb n="353" xml:id="pb0353"/>
somewheres, and says he’ll

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6344"/>
help;

          <app from="pr6344" n="353.1 (752.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8447">
            <lem wit="MS2">help;</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">help,</rdg>
          </app>
and he done it, too, and done it very well.

          <ptr target="#l13493" type="alt" xml:id="te3312"/>
Of course I judged he must be a runaway nigger, and there I

          <hi rend="italic">was!</hi>
and there I had to stick, right straight

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6345"/>
along,

          <app from="pr6345" n="353.3 (753.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8448">
            <lem wit="MS2">along,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
along

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3316"/>
all the rest of the day, and all night.

          <ptr target="#l13501" type="alt" xml:id="te3316"/>
It was a fix, I tell you! I had a couple of patients with the chills, and of course I’d of liked to run up to town and see them, but I dasn’t, because the nigger might get away, and then I’d be to blame;

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3317"/>
and yet never a skiff come close enough for me to hail.

          <ptr target="#l13503" type="alt" xml:id="te3317"/>
So there I had to stick, plumb till daylight this morning; and I never see a nigger that was a better nuss

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3318"/>
or faithfuller,

          <ptr target="#l13505" type="alt" xml:id="te3318"/>
and yet he was resking his freedom to do it, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3319"/>
was

          <ptr target="#l13507" type="alt" xml:id="te3319"/>
all tired out, too, and I see plain enough

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6346"/>
he’d

          <app from="pr6346" n="353.11 (754.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8449">
            <lem wit="A">he’d</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">he had</rdg>
          </app>
been worked main hard, lately. I liked the nigger for that; I tell you, gentlemen, a nigger like that is worth a thousand dollars—and kind treatment, too. I had everything I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3320"/>
needed,

          <ptr target="#l13509" type="alt" xml:id="te3320"/>
and the boy was doing as well there as he would a done at home—better, maybe, because it was so quiet; but there I

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
, with both of ’m on my hands; and there I had to stick, till about dawn this morning; then some men in a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3321"/>
skiff come

          <ptr target="#l13511" type="alt" xml:id="te3321"/>
by, and as

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3322"/>
good

          <ptr target="#l13513" type="alt" xml:id="te3322"/>
luck would have it, the nigger was setting

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3323"/>
by the

          <ptr target="#l13515" type="alt" xml:id="te3323"/>
pallet with his head

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3324"/>
propped

          <ptr target="#l13517" type="alt" xml:id="te3324"/>
on his

          <pb n="354" xml:id="pb0354"/>
knees, sound asleep; so I motioned them in, quiet, and they slipped up on him and grabbed him and tied him before he knowed what he was about, and we never had no trouble. And the boy being in a kind of a flighty sleep, too, we muffled the oars and hitched the raft on, and towed her over very nice and quiet, and the nigger never made the least row nor said a word, from the start. He ain’t no bad nigger, gentlemen; that’s what I think about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6347"/>
him.”

          <app from="pr6347" n="354.7 (756.8)" type="e" xml:id="la8450">
            <lem wit="A">him.”</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
him.’

              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8451">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80542">Somebody says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80544">“Well, it sounds very good, doctor, I’m obleeged to say.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80546">
Then the others softened up a little, too, and I was mighty thankful to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3325"/>
that old

          <ptr target="#l13519" type="alt" xml:id="te3325"/>
doctor for doing Jim that good turn; and I was glad it was according to my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6348"/>
judgement

          <app from="pr6348" n="354.12 (757.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8452">
            <lem wit="MS2">judgement</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">judgment</rdg>
          </app>
of him, too; because I thought he had a good heart

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3326"/>
in

          <ptr target="#l13521" type="alt" xml:id="te3326"/>
him and was a good man, the first time I see him.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3327"/>
Then

          <ptr target="#l13523" type="alt" xml:id="te3327"/>
they all agreed that Jim had acted very well, and was deserving to have some notice

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3328"/>
took

          <ptr target="#l13525" type="alt" xml:id="te3328"/>
of it, and reward. So every one of them promised, right out and hearty, that they wouldn’t cuss him no more.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80573">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3329"/>
Then

          <ptr target="#l13527" type="alt" xml:id="te3329"/>
they come out and locked him up. I hoped they was going to say he could have one or two of the chains took off, because they was rotten heavy, or could have meat and greens with his bread and water, but they didn’t think of it, and I reckoned it warn’t best for me to mix in, but I judged I’d get the doctor’s yarn to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6349"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6349" n="354.22 (758.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8453">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally, somehow or other, as soon as I’d got through the breakers that was laying just ahead of me. Explanations,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3330"/>
I mean,

          <ptr target="#l13529" type="alt" xml:id="te3330"/>
of how I forgot to mention about

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6350"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3331"/>
‘Sid’

          <app from="pr6350" n="354.25 (758.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8454">
            <lem wit="MS2">‘Sid’</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
Sid

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13531" type="alt" xml:id="te3331"/>
being shot, when I was telling how him and me put in that dratted night paddling around hunting the runaway

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6351"/>
nigger.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80604">
But

          <app from="pr6351" n="354.27–28 (758.17–759.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8455">
            <lem wit="A">nigger. [¶] But</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
nigger.

              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8456">extra line space</note>
[¶] But

            </rdg>
          </app>
I had plenty time. Aunt Sally she stuck to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6352"/>
sick room

          <app from="pr6352" n="354.28 (759.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8457">
            <lem wit="MS2">sick room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sick-room</rdg>
          </app>
all day and all night; and every time I see

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6353"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6353" n="354.29 (759.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8458">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas mooning around, I dodged him.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80632">
Next morning I heard Tom was a good deal better, and they said

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6354"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6354" n="354.32 (759.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8459">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally was gone to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3332"/>
get

          <ptr target="#l13533" type="alt" xml:id="te3332"/>
a nap. So I slips to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6355"/>
sick room

          <app from="pr6355" n="354.32 (759.11)" type="hc" xml:id="la8460">
            <lem wit="MS2">sick room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sick-room,</rdg>
          </app>
and if I found him awake I reckoned we could put up a yarn for the family that would wash. But he was sleeping, and sleeping very peaceful, too; and pale, not fire-faced the way he was when he come. So I set down and laid for him to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6356"/>
wake.

          <app from="pr6356" n="354.36 (760.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8461">
            <lem wit="A">wake.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
wake

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8462">page trimmed</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
In about a half an hour,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6357"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6357" n="354.36 (760.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8463">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally comes gliding in, and there I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3333"/>
was, up

          <ptr target="#l13535" type="alt" xml:id="te3333"/>
a stump again! She motioned me to be still, and set down by me, and begun to whisper, and said

          <pb n="355" xml:id="pb0355"/>
we could all be

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6358"/>
joyful,

          <app from="pr6358" n="355.1 (760.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8464">
            <lem wit="MS2">joyful,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
joyful

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
now, because all the symptoms was first rate, and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3334"/>
he’d

          <ptr target="#l13537" type="alt" xml:id="te3334"/>
been sleeping like that for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3335"/>
ever

          <ptr target="#l13539" type="alt" xml:id="te3335"/>
so long, and looking better and peacefuller all the time, and ten to one he’d wake up in his right mind.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80697">
So we set there watching, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6359"/>
by and by,

          <app from="pr6359" n="355.5 (761.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8465">
            <lem wit="MS2">by and by,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">by-and-by</rdg>
          </app>
he stirs a bit, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6360"/>
opens

          <app from="pr6360" n="355.5 (761.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8466">
            <lem wit="MS2">opens</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">opened</rdg>
          </app>
his eyes very natural, and takes a look, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80715">
“Hello, why I’m at

          <hi rend="italic">home!</hi>
How’s that? Where’s the raft?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80720">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6361"/>
It’s

          <app from="pr6361" n="355.8 (761.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8467">
            <lem wit="A">It’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">It’s</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all right,” I says.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80731">
“And

          <hi rend="italic">Jim?</hi>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80736">
“The same,” I says, but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6362"/>
couldn’t say it

          <app from="pr6362" n="355.10 (761.13)" type="e" xml:id="la8468">
            <lem wit="A">couldn’t say it</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">not</rdg>
          </app>
pretty brash. But he never noticed, but says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80746">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6363"/>
Good

          <app from="pr6363" n="355.12 (761.15)" type="e" xml:id="la8469">
            <lem wit="A">Good</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Good</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
! Splendid!

          <hi rend="italic">Now</hi>
we’re all right and safe! Did you tell

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6364"/>
aunty

          <app from="pr6364" n="355.13 (762.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8470">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunty</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunty</rdg>
          </app>
?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80768">
I was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6365"/>
going

          <app from="pr6365" n="355.14 (762.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8471">
            <lem wit="A">going</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">agoing</rdg>
          </app>
to say yes; but she chipped in and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80778">“About what, Sid?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80780">“Why, about the way the whole thing was done.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80783">“What whole thing?”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80785">
“Why,

          <hi rend="italic">the</hi>
whole

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6366"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3336"/>
thing—there

          <app from="pr6366" n="355.18 (762.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8472">
            <lem wit="MS2">thing—there</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">thing. There</rdg>
          </app>
ain’t but

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6367"/>
one:

          <ptr target="#l13541" type="alt" xml:id="te3336"/>
          <app from="pr6367" n="355.18 (762.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8473">
            <lem wit="MS2">one:</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">one;</rdg>
          </app>
how we set the runaway nigger

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3337"/>
free—

          <ptr target="#l13543" type="alt" xml:id="te3337"/>
me and Tom.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80813">
“Good land!

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3338"/>
Set the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6368"/>
run—

          <ptr target="#l13545" type="alt" xml:id="te3338"/>
What

          <app from="pr6368" n="355.20 (762.13–14)" type="e" xml:id="la8474">
            <lem wit="A">run—What</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
run—

              <lb/>
what

            </rdg>
          </app>
          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
the child

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6369"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3339"/>
talking

          <ptr target="#l13547" type="alt" xml:id="te3339"/>
          <app from="pr6369" n="355.20 (762.14)" type="e" xml:id="la8475">
            <lem wit="A">talking</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">talkin’</rdg>
          </app>
about! Dear, dear, out of his head again!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80842">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6370"/>
          <hi rend="italic">No</hi>
          <app from="pr6370" n="355.22 (763.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8476">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">No</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">No,</rdg>
          </app>
I ain’t out

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6371"/>
of

          <app from="pr6371" n="355.22 (763.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8477">
            <lem wit="A">of</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">o’</rdg>
          </app>
my

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6372"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">head</hi>
,

          <app from="pr6372" n="355.22 (763.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8478">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">head</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">head,</rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">head;</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
I know all what I’m talking about. We

          <hi rend="italic">did</hi>
set him free—me and Tom. We laid out to

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6373"/>
do it

          <app from="pr6373" n="355.23 (763.7–8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8479">
            <lem wit="MS2">do it</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">do it,</rdg>
          </app>
and we

          <hi rend="italic">done</hi>
it. And we done it elegant, too.”

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3340"/>
He’d

          <ptr target="#l13549" type="alt" xml:id="te3340"/>
got a start, and she never checked him up, just set and stared

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3341"/>
and stared,

          <ptr target="#l13551" type="alt" xml:id="te3341"/>
and let him clip along, and I see it warn’t no use for

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
to put in. “Why,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6374"/>
aunty

          <app from="pr6374" n="355.26 (763.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8480">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunty</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunty</rdg>
          </app>
, it cost us a power of work—weeks of it—hours and hours, every night, whilst you was all asleep. And we had to steal candles,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3342"/>
and the

          <ptr target="#l13553" type="alt" xml:id="te3342"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6375"/>
sheet

          <app from="pr6375" n="355.28 (764.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8481">
            <lem wit="MS2">sheet</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sheet,</rdg>
          </app>
and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3343"/>
the

          <ptr target="#l13555" type="alt" xml:id="te3343"/>
shirt, and your dress,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3344"/>
and spoons,

          <ptr target="#l13557" type="alt" xml:id="te3344"/>
and tin plates, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6376"/>
caseknives

          <app from="pr6376" n="355.29–30 (764.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8482">
            <lem wit="MS2">caseknives</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">case-knives</rdg>
          </app>
, and the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6377"/>
warming pan

          <app from="pr6377" n="355.30 (764.8–9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8483">
            <lem wit="MS2">warming pan</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">warming-pan</rdg>
          </app>
, and the grindstone,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3345"/>
and flour,

          <ptr target="#l13559" type="alt" xml:id="te3345"/>
and just no end of things, and you can’t think what work it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6378"/>
was,

          <app from="pr6378" n="355.31 (764.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8484">
            <lem wit="MS2">was,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
was

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
to make the saws, and pens, and inscriptions, and one thing or another, and you can’t think

          <hi rend="italic">half</hi>
the fun it was. And we had to make up the pictures of coffins and things, and nonnamous letters from the robbers, and get up and down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6379"/>
lightning rod

          <app from="pr6379" n="355.35 (765.5–6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8485">
            <lem wit="MS2">lightning rod</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">lightning-rod</rdg>
          </app>
, and dig the hole into the cabin, and make the rope-ladder and send it

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6380"/>
in,

          <app from="pr6380" n="355.36 (765.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8486">
            <lem wit="MS2">in,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
in

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
cooked up in a pie, and send in spoons and things to work with, in your

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3346"/>
apron

          <ptr target="#l13561" type="alt" xml:id="te3346"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6381"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3347"/>
pocket”—

          <ptr target="#l13563" type="alt" xml:id="te3347"/>
          <app from="pr6381" n="355.37 (765.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8487">
            <lem wit="MS2">pocket”—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">pocket”——</rdg>
          </app>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e80995">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3348"/>
“Mercy

          <ptr target="#l13565" type="alt" xml:id="te3348"/>
sakes!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81000">
          <pb n="356" xml:id="pb0356"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6382"/>
—“and

          <app from="pr6382" n="356.1 (765.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8488">
            <lem wit="MS2">—“and</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">——“and</rdg>
          </app>
load up the cabin with rats and snakes and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6383"/>
so-on

          <app from="pr6383" n="356.1 (765.15)" type="hc" xml:id="la8489">
            <lem wit="MS2">so-on</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">so on</rdg>
          </app>
, for company for Jim; and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3349"/>
then

          <ptr target="#l13567" type="alt" xml:id="te3349"/>
you kept Tom here so long with the butter in his hat that you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3350"/>
come

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6384"/>
near

          <ptr target="#l13569" type="alt" xml:id="te3350"/>
          <app from="pr6384" n="356.3 (766.4–5)" type="e" xml:id="la8490">
            <lem wit="A">near</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">very near</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3351"/>
spiling

          <ptr target="#l13571" type="alt" xml:id="te3351"/>
the whole business, because the men come before we was out of the cabin, and we had to rush, and they heard us and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3352"/>
let

          <ptr target="#l13573" type="alt" xml:id="te3352"/>
drive at us, and I got my share, and we dodged out of the path and let them go by, and when the dogs come they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3353"/>
warn’t

          <ptr target="#l13575" type="alt" xml:id="te3353"/>
interested in us, but went for the most noise, and we got our canoe, and made for the raft, and was all safe, and Jim was a free man, and we done it all by ourselves, and

          <hi rend="italic">wasn’t</hi>
it bully,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6385"/>
aunty

          <app from="pr6385" n="356.10 (767.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8491">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunty</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunty</rdg>
          </app>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81058">
“Well, I never heard the likes of it in all my born days! So it was

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
, you little rapscallions, that’s been making all this trouble, and turned everybody’s wits

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3354"/>
clean

          <ptr target="#l13577" type="alt" xml:id="te3354"/>
inside out and scared us all most to death. I’ve as good a notion

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3355"/>
as ever

          <ptr target="#l13579" type="alt" xml:id="te3355"/>
I had in my life, to take

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3356"/>
it

          <ptr target="#l13581" type="alt" xml:id="te3356"/>
out o’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3357"/>
you

          <ptr target="#l13583" type="alt" xml:id="te3357"/>
this very minute. To

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3358"/>
think,

          <ptr target="#l13585" type="alt" xml:id="te3358"/>
here I’ve been, night after night, a—

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6386"/>
          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
          <app from="pr6386" n="356.16 (768.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8492">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">you</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6387"/>
just

          <app from="pr6387" n="356.16 (768.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8493">
            <lem wit="A">just</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">jest</rdg>
          </app>
get

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6388"/>
well,

          <app from="pr6388" n="356.16 (768.3)" type="hc" xml:id="la8494">
            <lem wit="MS2">well,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
well

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
once, you young scamp,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3359"/>
and

          <ptr target="#l13587" type="alt" xml:id="te3359"/>
I lay I’ll tan the Old Harry out o’

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3360"/>
both

          <ptr target="#l13589" type="alt" xml:id="te3360"/>
o’ ye!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81119">
But Tom, he

          <hi rend="italic">was</hi>
so proud and joyful, he just

          <hi rend="italic">couldn’t</hi>
hold in, and his tongue just

          <hi rend="italic">went</hi>
it—she a-chipping in, and spitting fire all along, and both of them going it at once, like a cat-convention; and she

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3361"/>
says:

          <ptr target="#l13591" type="alt" xml:id="te3361"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81133">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6389"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
          <app from="pr6389" n="356.22 (769.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8495">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Well</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Well</rdg>
          </app>
, you get all the enjoyment you can out of it

          <hi rend="italic">now</hi>
, for mind I tell you if I catch you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6390"/>
meddling

          <app from="pr6390" n="356.23 (769.4)" type="e" xml:id="la8496">
            <lem wit="A">meddling</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">meddlin’</rdg>
          </app>
with him

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6391"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3362"/>
again

          <ptr target="#l13593" type="alt" xml:id="te3362"/>
—

          <app from="pr6391" n="356.23 (769.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8497">
            <lem wit="MS2">again—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">again——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81168">
“Meddling with

          <hi rend="italic">who?</hi>
” Tom says, dropping his smile and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3363"/>
looking

          <ptr target="#l13595" type="alt" xml:id="te3363"/>
surprised.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81177">
“With

          <hi rend="italic">who?</hi>
Why, the runaway nigger, of course. Who’d you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3364"/>
reckon?”

          <ptr target="#l13597" type="alt" xml:id="te3364"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81186">
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3365"/>
Tom

          <ptr target="#l13599" type="alt" xml:id="te3365"/>
looks at me very grave, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81191">
“Tom, didn’t you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3366"/>
just

          <ptr target="#l13601" type="alt" xml:id="te3366"/>
tell me

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3367"/>
he was

          <ptr target="#l13603" type="alt" xml:id="te3367"/>
all

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3368"/>
right?

          <ptr target="#l13605" type="alt" xml:id="te3368"/>
Hasn’t he got away?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81206">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Him?</hi>
” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6392"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6392" n="356.31 (770.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8498">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally; “the runaway nigger? ’Deed he hasn’t. They’ve got him back, safe and sound, and he’s in that cabin again, on bread and water, and loaded down with chains, till he’s claimed or sold!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81219">
Tom rose square up in bed, with his eye hot, and his nostrils opening and shutting like gills, and sings

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3369"/>
out

          <ptr target="#l13607" type="alt" xml:id="te3369"/>
to me:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81225">
“They hain’t no

          <hi rend="italic">right</hi>
to shut him up!

          <hi rend="italic">Shove!</hi>
—and don’t you lose a minute. Turn him loose! he ain’t no

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6393"/>
slave,

          <app from="pr6393" n="356.38 (771.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8499">
            <lem wit="MS2">slave,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">slave;</rdg>
          </app>
he’s as free as any cretur that walks this earth!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81241">
          <pb n="357" xml:id="pb0357"/>
“What

          <hi rend="italic">does</hi>
the child

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6394"/>
mean!

          <app from="pr6394" n="357.1 (771.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8500">
            <lem wit="MS2">mean!</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">mean?</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81255">
“I mean every word I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6395"/>
          <hi rend="italic">say</hi>
          <app from="pr6395" n="357.2 (771.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8501">
            <lem wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">say</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">say</rdg>
          </app>
,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6396"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6396" n="357.2 (771.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8502">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally, and if somebody don’t go,

          <hi rend="italic">I</hi>
’ll go.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3370"/>
I’ve knowed him

          <ptr target="#l13609" type="alt" xml:id="te3370"/>
all his life, and so has Tom, there. Old Miss Watson died two months ago, and she was

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3371"/>
ashamed

          <ptr target="#l13611" type="alt" xml:id="te3371"/>
she ever was going to sell him down the river, and

          <hi rend="italic">said</hi>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3372"/>
so;

          <ptr target="#l13613" type="alt" xml:id="te3372"/>
and she set him free in her will.”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y35701">
          <graphic url="y35701.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">tom rose square up in bed</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81298">
“

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0021"/>
Then what on earth did

          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
want to set him free for,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6397"/>
seeing

          <app from="pr6397" n="357.7 (772.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8503">
            <lem wit="A">seeing</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">seein’</rdg>
          </app>
he was already free?

          <ptr target="#as0267" type="an" xml:id="tr0021"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81315">
“

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6398"/>
Well

          <app from="pr6398" n="357.9 (772.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8504">
            <lem wit="MS2">Well</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Well,</rdg>
          </app>
that

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6399"/>
question,

          <app from="pr6399" n="357.9 (772.7)" type="e" xml:id="la8505">
            <lem wit="A">question,</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
question

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3373"/>
I must say

          <ptr target="#l13615" type="alt" xml:id="te3373"/>
; and

          <hi rend="italic">just</hi>
like women! Why, I wanted the

          <hi rend="italic">adventure</hi>
of it; and I’d a waded

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6400"/>
neck-deep

          <app from="pr6400" n="357.10 (772.10–11)" type="e" xml:id="la8506">
            <lem wit="A">neck-deep</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
neck-

              <lb/>
deep

            </rdg>
          </app>
in blood to—goodness alive,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6401"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">aunt Polly</hi>
          <app from="pr6401" n="357.11 (772.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8507">
            <lem wit="C">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">aunt Polly</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">aunt Polly</hi>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">Aunt Polly</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
!”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81371">
If she warn’t standing right there, just inside the door, looking as sweet and

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3374"/>
contented

          <ptr target="#l13617" type="alt" xml:id="te3374"/>
as an angel

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6402"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3375"/>
half-full

          <ptr target="#l13619" type="alt" xml:id="te3375"/>
          <app from="pr6402" n="357.13 (773.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8508">
            <lem wit="A">half-full</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">full</rdg>
          </app>
of pie, I wish I may never!

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81388">
Aunt Sally jumped for her, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6403"/>
most

          <app from="pr6403" n="357.14 (773.5)" type="e" xml:id="la8509">
            <lem wit="A">most</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8510">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
hugged the head off of her, and cried over her, and I found a good enough place for me under the bed, for it was getting pretty

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6404"/>
sultry

          <app from="pr6404" n="357.16 (773.9)" type="e" xml:id="la8511">
            <lem wit="A">sultry</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">sultry weather</rdg>
          </app>
for

          <hi rend="italic">us</hi>
,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3376"/>
seemed to me.

          <ptr target="#l13621" type="alt" xml:id="te3376"/>
And I peeped out, and in a little while Tom’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6405"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6405" n="357.17 (773.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8512">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Polly shook

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3377"/>
herself

          <ptr target="#l13623" type="alt" xml:id="te3377"/>
loose and stood there looking across at Tom over her spectacles—kind of grinding him into the earth, you know. And then she says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81427">
“Yes, you

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3378"/>
          <hi rend="italic">better</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13625" type="alt" xml:id="te3378"/>
turn

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3379"/>
y’r

          <ptr target="#l13627" type="alt" xml:id="te3379"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6406"/>
head

          <app from="pr6406" n="357.20 (774.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8513">
            <lem wit="A">head</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8514">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
away—I would if I was you, Tom.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81446">
“Oh, deary me!” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6407"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6407" n="357.21 (774.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8515">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6408"/>
Sally,

          <app from="pr6408" n="357.21 (774.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8516">
            <lem wit="MS2">Sally,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Sally;</rdg>
          </app>
“

          <hi rend="italic">is</hi>
he changed so? Why, that

          <pb n="358" xml:id="pb0358"/>
ain’t

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6409"/>
          <hi rend="italic">Tom,</hi>
          <app from="pr6409" n="358.1 (774.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8517">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">Tom</hi>
,

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <hi rend="italic">Tom</hi>
              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
it’s Sid; Tom’s—Tom’s—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3380"/>
why,

          <ptr target="#l13629" type="alt" xml:id="te3380"/>
where

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3381"/>
is

          <ptr target="#l13631" type="alt" xml:id="te3381"/>
Tom? He was here a minute ago.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81490">
“You mean where’s Huck

          <hi rend="italic">Finn</hi>
—that’s what you mean! I reckon I hain’t raised such a scamp as my Tom all these years, not to know him when I

          <hi rend="italic">see</hi>
him. That

          <hi rend="italic">would</hi>
be a

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3382"/>
pretty

          <ptr target="#l13633" type="alt" xml:id="te3382"/>
howdy-do. Come out from under that bed, Huck

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6410"/>
Finn.

          <app from="pr6410" n="358.6 (775.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8518">
            <lem wit="A">Finn.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">Finn!</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81514">So I done it. But not feeling brash.</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81516">
Aunt Sally she was one of the mixed-upest looking persons I ever see; except one, and that was

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6411"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6411" n="358.9 (775.9)" type="hc" xml:id="la8519">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas, when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6412"/>
he

          <app from="pr6412" n="358.9 (775.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8520">
            <lem wit="A">he</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">he</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
come in, and they

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3383"/>
told

          <ptr target="#l13635" type="alt" xml:id="te3383"/>
it all to him. It kind of made him drunk, as you may say, and he didn’t know nothing at all the rest of the day, and preached a

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6413"/>
prayer meeting

          <app from="pr6413" n="358.11–12 (775.15–16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8521">
            <lem wit="MS2">prayer meeting</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">prayer-meeting</rdg>
          </app>
sermon that night that give him a rattling ruputation, because the oldest man in the world couldn’t a understood it. So

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3384"/>
Tom’s

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6414"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6414" n="358.14 (776.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8522">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6415"/>
Polly

          <app from="pr6415" n="358.14 (776.5)" type="hc" xml:id="la8523">
            <lem wit="MS2">Polly</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Polly,</rdg>
          </app>
she told all about who I was, and what; and

          <ptr target="#l13637" type="alt" xml:id="te3384"/>
I had to up and tell how I was in such a tight place that when Mrs. Phelps took me for Tom Sawyer—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3385"/>
she

          <ptr target="#l13639" type="alt" xml:id="te3385"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3386"/>
chipped

          <ptr target="#l13641" type="alt" xml:id="te3386"/>
in and says, “

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6416"/>
O

          <app from="pr6416" n="358.16 (776.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8524">
            <lem wit="MS2">O</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Oh</rdg>
          </app>
, go on and call me

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6417"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6417" n="358.17 (776.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8525">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally, I’m used to it, now, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6418"/>
’t ain’t

          <app from="pr6418" n="358.17 (776.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8526">
            <lem wit="MS2">’t ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">’tain’t</rdg>
          </app>
no need to change”—that when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6419"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6419" n="358.18 (776.13)" type="hc" xml:id="la8527">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally took me for Tom Sawyer, I had to stand it—there warn’t no other way, and I knowed

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3387"/>
he

          <ptr target="#l13643" type="alt" xml:id="te3387"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3388"/>
wouldn’t

          <ptr target="#l13645" type="alt" xml:id="te3388"/>
mind, because it

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3389"/>
would

          <ptr target="#l13647" type="alt" xml:id="te3389"/>
be nuts for him, being a mystery, and he’d make an adventure out of it and be perfectly satisfied. And so it turned out,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3390"/>
and he

          <ptr target="#l13649" type="alt" xml:id="te3390"/>
let on to be Sid, and made things

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3391"/>
as soft

          <ptr target="#l13651" type="alt" xml:id="te3391"/>
as he could for me.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81630">
And his

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6420"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6420" n="358.24 (777.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8528">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Polly she said Tom was right about old Miss Watson setting Jim free in her will; and so, sure enough, Tom

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3392"/>
Sawyer

          <ptr target="#l13653" type="alt" xml:id="te3392"/>
had gone and took all that trouble and bother to set a free nigger

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3393"/>
free!

          <ptr target="#l13655" type="alt" xml:id="te3393"/>
and I couldn’t ever understand, before,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3394"/>
until that minute and that talk, how

          <ptr target="#l13657" type="alt" xml:id="te3394"/>
he

          <hi rend="italic">could</hi>
help

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3395"/>
a body

          <ptr target="#l13659" type="alt" xml:id="te3395"/>
set a nigger free, with

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3396"/>
his

          <ptr target="#l13661" type="alt" xml:id="te3396"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3397"/>
bringing-up

          <ptr target="#l13663" type="alt" xml:id="te3397"/>
.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81668">
Well,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6421"/>
aunt Polly

          <app from="pr6421" n="358.30 (778.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8529">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt Polly</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt Polly</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6422"/>
she

          <app from="pr6422" n="358.30 (778.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8530">
            <lem wit="A">she</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8531">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
said that when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6423"/>
aunt Sally

          <app from="pr6423" n="358.30 (778.8)" type="hc" xml:id="la8532">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt Sally</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt Sally</rdg>
          </app>
wrote to her that Tom and

          <hi rend="italic">Sid</hi>
had come, all right and safe, she says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6424"/>
to herself

          <app from="pr6424" n="358.31 (778.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8533">
            <lem wit="A">to herself</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8534">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81707">
“Look at that, now! I might

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6425"/>
have

          <app from="pr6425" n="358.32 (778.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8535">
            <lem wit="A">have</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">of</rdg>
          </app>
expected it, letting him go off that way without anybody to watch him.

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0022"/>
So now I got to go and trapse all the way down the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6426"/>
river

          <app from="pr6426" n="358.34 (778.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8536">
            <lem wit="MS2">river</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">river,</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3398"/>
eleven hundred mile

          <ptr target="#as0268" type="an" xml:id="tr0022"/>
,

          <ptr target="#l13665" type="alt" xml:id="te3398"/>
and find out what that

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6427"/>
cretur’s

          <app from="pr6427" n="358.35 (778.17)" type="hc" xml:id="la8537">
            <lem wit="MS2">cretur’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">creetur’s</rdg>
          </app>
up to,

          <hi rend="italic">this</hi>
time;

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6428"/>
as long as

          <app from="pr6428" n="358.35 (778.18)" type="e" xml:id="la8538">
            <lem wit="A">as long as</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">long’s</rdg>
          </app>
I couldn’t seem to get any answer

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3399"/>
out of

          <ptr target="#l13667" type="alt" xml:id="te3399"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3400"/>
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0087"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6429"/>
          <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
          <app from="pr6429" n="358.36 (779.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8539">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="italic">you</hi>
            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">you</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#tb0087" type="te" xml:id="tv0087"/>
          <ptr target="#l13669" type="alt" xml:id="te3400"/>
about it.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81771">
“Why, I never heard nothing from you,” says

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6430"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6430" n="358.37 (779.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8540">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81781">“Well, I wonder! Why, I wrote to you twice, to ask you what you could mean by Sid being here.”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81784">
          <pb n="359" xml:id="pb0359"/>
“Well,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3401"/>
I

          <ptr target="#l13671" type="alt" xml:id="te3401"/>
never got

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6431"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3402"/>
’em,

          <ptr target="#l13673" type="alt" xml:id="te3402"/>
          <app from="pr6431" n="359.1 (779.10)" type="e" xml:id="la8541">
            <lem wit="A">’em</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">’m</rdg>
          </app>
Sis.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81801">
Aunt

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6432"/>
Polly

          <app from="pr6432" n="359.2 (779.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8542">
            <lem wit="MS2">Polly</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Polly,</rdg>
          </app>
she turns around slow and severe, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81811">“You, Tom!”</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81813">
“Well—

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3403"/>
          <hi rend="italic">what?</hi>
          <ptr target="#l13675" type="alt" xml:id="te3403"/>
” he says, kind of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3404"/>
pettish.

          <ptr target="#l13677" type="alt" xml:id="te3404"/>
        </p>
        <figure rend="right" xml:id="y35901">
          <graphic url="y35901.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
“

            <hi rend="smallcaps">hand out them letters.</hi>
”

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81829">
“Don’t you what

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
, you impudent thing—hand out them letters.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81834">
“What

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3405"/>
letters?

          <ptr target="#l13679" type="alt" xml:id="te3405"/>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81840">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Them</hi>
letters. I be bound, if I have to take aholt of you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6433"/>
I’ll—

          <app from="pr6433" n="359.10 (780.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8543">
            <lem wit="MS2">I’ll—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">I’ll——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81853">
“They’re in the trunk. There, now. And they’re just the same as they was when I got them out of the office. I hain’t looked into them, I hain’t touched them. But I knowed they’d make trouble, and I thought if you warn’t in no hurry,

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6434"/>
I’d—

          <app from="pr6434" n="359.17 (780.16)" type="hc" xml:id="la8544">
            <lem wit="MS2">I’d—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">I’d——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81863">
“Well, you

          <hi rend="italic">do</hi>
need skinning, there ain’t no mistake about it. And I wrote another one to tell you I was coming; and I spose

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6435"/>
he—

          <app from="pr6435" n="359.21 (781.6)" type="hc" xml:id="la8545">
            <lem wit="MS2">he—</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">he——</rdg>
          </app>
”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81876">
“No, it come yesterday; I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3406"/>
hain’t

          <ptr target="#l13681" type="alt" xml:id="te3406"/>
read it yet, but

          <hi rend="italic">it’s</hi>
all right, I’ve got

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3407"/>
that

          <ptr target="#l13683" type="alt" xml:id="te3407"/>
one.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81890">
I wanted to offer to

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3408"/>
bet

          <ptr target="#l13685" type="alt" xml:id="te3408"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3409"/>
two dollars

          <ptr target="#l13687" type="alt" xml:id="te3409"/>
she hadn’t, but I reckoned maybe it was just as safe to not to. So I never said nothing.

        </p>
      </div1>
      <div1 type="chapter" xml:id="la0468">
        <head rend="toc">Chapter XLIII.</head>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81902">
          <pb n="360" xml:id="pb0360"/>
          <figure rend="ch-init" xml:id="y36001">
            <graphic url="y36001.jpg"/>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6436"/>
Chapter the last.

              <app from="pr6436" n="360 title (781½.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8546">
                <lem wit="A">Chapter the last.</lem>
                <rdg wit="MS2">
                  <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8547">not in</note>
                </rdg>
              </app>
            </ab>
            <ab type="transcript">
              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3410"/>
The

            </ab>
          </figure>
          <figure rend="ch-left" xml:id="hf3601">
            <graphic url="hf3601.jpg"/>
            <ab type="caption">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">out of bondage</hi>
.

            </ab>
          </figure>
        </p>
        <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e81922">
first time I catched Tom, private, I asked

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3411"/>
him

          <ptr target="#l13691" type="alt" xml:id="te3411"/>
what

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3412"/>
was his idea,

          <ptr target="#l13693" type="alt" xml:id="te3412"/>
time of the

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3413"/>
evasion

          <ptr target="#l13695" type="alt" xml:id="te3413"/>
?—what it was he’d planned to do

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3414"/>
if

          <ptr target="#l13697" type="alt" xml:id="te3414"/>
the evasion worked all right and he managed to set a nigger free that was already free before? And he said, what he had planned in his head, from the start, if we got Jim

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6437"/>
out,

          <app from="pr6437" n="360.10 (781½.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8548">
            <lem wit="MS2">out,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
out

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
all safe, was for us to run him down the river, on the

          <ptr target="#l13689" type="alt" xml:id="te3410"/>
raft, and have adventures plumb to the mouth of the river, and then tell him about his being free, and take him back up home on a steamboat, in style, and pay him for his lost time,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3415"/>
and write word

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6438"/>
ahead,

          <ptr target="#l13699" type="alt" xml:id="te3415"/>
          <app from="pr6438" n="360.18 (782.7)" type="hc" xml:id="la8549">
            <lem wit="MS2">ahead,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
ahead

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
and get out all the niggers around, and have them waltz him into town with a torchlight

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6439"/>
procession,

          <app from="pr6439" n="360.20 (782.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8550">
            <lem wit="MS2">procession,</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
procession

              <hi rend="subscript">⁁</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3416"/>
and a brass band, and

          <ptr target="#l13701" type="alt" xml:id="te3416"/>
then he would be a hero, and so would we. But I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6440"/>
reckoned

          <app from="pr6440" n="360.21 (782.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8551">
            <lem wit="MS2">reckoned</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">reckened</rdg>
          </app>
it was about as well the way it was.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e81983">
We had Jim out of the chains in no time, and when

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6441"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6441" n="360.22 (783.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8552">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Polly and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6442"/>
uncle

          <app from="pr6442" n="360.23 (783.1)" type="hc" xml:id="la8553">
            <lem wit="MS2">uncle</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Uncle</rdg>
          </app>
Silas and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6443"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6443" n="360.23 (783.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8554">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally found out how good he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3417"/>
helped

          <ptr target="#l13703" type="alt" xml:id="te3417"/>
the doctor nurse Tom, they made a heap of

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3418"/>
fuss over

          <ptr target="#l13705" type="alt" xml:id="te3418"/>
him, and fixed him up prime, and give him all he wanted to eat, and a good

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3419"/>
time, and nothing to do.

          <ptr target="#l13707" type="alt" xml:id="te3419"/>
And we had him up to the

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6444"/>
sick room

          <app from="pr6444" n="360.26 (783.9–10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8555">
            <lem wit="MS2">sick room</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">sick-room</rdg>
          </app>
; and had a high

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3420"/>
talk

          <ptr target="#l13709" type="alt" xml:id="te3420"/>
; and Tom

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6445"/>
give Jim forty dollars for being prisoner for us so patient, and doing it up so good, and Jim was pleased most to death, and busted out, and says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82037">
“

          <hi rend="italic">Dah</hi>
, now, Huck, what I tell you?—what I tell you up dah on Jackson islan’? I

          <hi rend="italic">tole</hi>
you I got a hairy breas’, en what’s de sign un it;

          <pb n="361" xml:id="pb0361"/>
en I

          <hi rend="italic">tole</hi>
you I ben rich wunst, en

          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tb0088"/>
gwineter

          <ptr target="#tn0088" type="te" xml:id="tv0088"/>
be rich

          <hi rend="italic">agin;</hi>
en it’s come true; en heah she

          <hi rend="italic">is! Dah</hi>
, now! doan’ talk to

          <hi rend="italic">me</hi>
—signs is

          <hi rend="italic">signs</hi>
, mine I tell you; en I knowed jis’ ’s well ’at I ’uz gwineter be rich agin as I’s a stannin’ heah dis minute!”

        </p>
        <figure rend="block" xml:id="y36101">
          <graphic url="y36101.jpg"/>
          <ab type="caption">
            <hi rend="smallcaps">tom’s liberality</hi>
.

          </ab>
        </figure>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82072">
And then Tom he talked along, and

          <app from="pr6445" n="360.27–361.5 (783.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8556">
            <lem wit="C">give Jim . . . en gwineter . . . and talked along, and</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8557">not in</note>
            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="A">give Jim . . . en gwineter to . . . and talked along, and</rdg>
          </app>
talked along, and says, le’s all three slide out of here, one of these nights, and get an outfit, and

          <anchor type="an" xml:id="th0023"/>
go for

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3421"/>
howling

          <ptr target="#l13711" type="alt" xml:id="te3421"/>
adventures amongst the Injuns

          <ptr target="#as0269" type="an" xml:id="tr0023"/>
, over in the Territory, for a couple of weeks or two; and I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6446"/>
says

          <app from="pr6446" n="361.8 (784.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8558">
            <lem wit="A">says</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">said</rdg>
          </app>
, all right, that suits me, but I

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6447"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr6447" n="361.9 (784.2)" type="hc" xml:id="la8559">
            <lem wit="MS2">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">aint</rdg>
          </app>
got no money for to buy the outfit, and I reckon I couldn’t get none from home, because it’s likely pap’s been back before now, and got it all away from Judge Thatcher and drunk it up.

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82108">
“No he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3422"/>
hain’t,” Tom says; “it’s

          <ptr target="#l13713" type="alt" xml:id="te3422"/>
all there, yet—six thousand

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3423"/>
dollars

          <ptr target="#l13715" type="alt" xml:id="te3423"/>
and more; and your pap hain’t ever been back since.

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3424"/>
Hadn’t when I come away, anyhow.”

          <ptr target="#l13717" type="alt" xml:id="te3424"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82122">
Jim

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3425"/>
says, kind of solemn:

          <ptr target="#l13719" type="alt" xml:id="te3425"/>
        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82127">
“He

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6448"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3426"/>
ain’t

          <ptr target="#l13721" type="alt" xml:id="te3426"/>
a

          <app from="pr6448" n="361.16 (784.16)" type="e" xml:id="la8560">
            <lem wit="A">ain’t a</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’</rdg>
          </app>
comin’ back no mo’, Huck.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82140">
I

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3427"/>
says:

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82145">
“Why

          <ptr target="#l13723" type="alt" xml:id="te3427"/>
, Jim?”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82149">
“Nemmine why, Huck—but he

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3428"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6449"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr6449" n="361.19 (785.3)" type="e" xml:id="la8561">
            <lem wit="A">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">ain’</rdg>
          </app>
          <ptr target="#l13725" type="alt" xml:id="te3428"/>
comin’ back no mo’.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82161">But I kept at him; so at last he says:</p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82163">
“Doan’ you ’member de house dat was float’n down de river, en dey

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3429"/>
wuz

          <ptr target="#l13727" type="alt" xml:id="te3429"/>
a man in dah,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3430"/>
kivered

          <ptr target="#l13729" type="alt" xml:id="te3430"/>
up, en I went

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3431"/>
in en

          <ptr target="#l13731" type="alt" xml:id="te3431"/>
unkivered

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6450"/>
him

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3432"/>
en

          <app from="pr6450" n="361.22 (785.12)" type="hc" xml:id="la8562">
            <lem wit="MS2">him en</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">him and</rdg>
          </app>
          <pb n="362" xml:id="pb0362"/>
didn’ let you come in

          <ptr target="#l13733" type="alt" xml:id="te3432"/>
? Well, den, you

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6451"/>
k’n

          <app from="pr6451" n="362.1 (785.12)" type="e" xml:id="la8563">
            <lem wit="A">k’n</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">kin</rdg>
          </app>
git yo’ money when you wants it; kase dat

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3433"/>
wuz

          <ptr target="#l13735" type="alt" xml:id="te3433"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6452"/>
him.”

        </p>
        <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e82205">
Tom’s

          <app from="pr6452" n="362.2–3 (785.14–786.1)" type="e" xml:id="la8564">
            <lem wit="A">him.” [¶] Tom’s</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">
him.”

              <lb/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8565">centered rule</note>
              <milestone unit="page"/>
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8566">extra line space</note>
[¶] Tom’s

            </rdg>
          </app>
most well, now, and got his bullet around his neck on a watch-guard for a watch,

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3434"/>
and is always seeing what time it is, and so

          <ptr target="#l13737" type="alt" xml:id="te3434"/>
there ain’t nothing more to write about, and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6453"/>
I am

          <app from="pr6453" n="362.5 (786.6)" type="e" xml:id="la8567">
            <lem wit="A">I am</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">I’m</rdg>
          </app>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3435"/>
rotten

          <ptr target="#l13739" type="alt" xml:id="te3435"/>
glad of it, because if I’d a knowed what a trouble it was to make a book I wouldn’t a tackled it and

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6454"/>
ain’t

          <app from="pr6454" n="362.7 (786.10)" type="hc" xml:id="la8568">
            <lem wit="MS2">ain’t</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">aint’t</rdg>
          </app>
agoing

          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3436"/>
to

          <ptr target="#l13741" type="alt" xml:id="te3436"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6455"/>
no

          <app from="pr6455" n="362.7 (786.11)" type="e" xml:id="la8569">
            <lem wit="A">no</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">any</rdg>
          </app>
more. But I reckon I got to light out for the Territory ahead of the rest, because

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6456"/>
          <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg3437"/>
aunt

          <app from="pr6456" n="362.8 (786.14)" type="hc" xml:id="la8570">
            <lem wit="MS2">aunt</lem>
            <rdg wit="A">Aunt</rdg>
          </app>
Sally she’s

          <ptr target="#l13743" type="alt" xml:id="te3437"/>
going to adopt me and sivilize me and I can’t stand

          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6457"/>
it.

          <app from="pr6457" n="362.9 (787.2)" type="e" xml:id="la8571">
            <lem wit="A">it.</lem>
            <rdg wit="MS2">it,</rdg>
          </app>
I been there before.

        </p>
        <lb/>
        <p rend="center" xml:id="d1e82277">
          <anchor type="te" xml:id="tn0089"/>
          <anchor type="app" xml:id="pr6458"/>
          <hi rend="smallcaps">The end, yours truly Huck Finn</hi>
          <app from="pr6458" n="362.11 (787.4)" type="hc" xml:id="la8572">
            <lem wit="MS2">
              <hi rend="smallcaps">The end, yours truly Huck Finn</hi>
.

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de8573">caption</note>
              <hi rend="smallcaps">the end. yours truly, huck finn.</hi>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <app from="rp5081" n="249.6–362.11 (370.1–787.4)" type="hc" xml:id="al7079">
            <lem wit="MS2">
But . . .

              <hi rend="smallcaps">Finn</hi>
.

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">But . . . before.</rdg>
            <rdg wit="Cent">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de9065">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
.

          <ptr target="#tb0089" type="te" xml:id="tv0089"/>
          <app from="rp2153" n="123.22–362.11 (363.5–787.4)" type="hc" xml:id="al3872">
            <lem wit="MS">
There . . .

              <hi rend="smallcaps">Finn</hi>
.

            </lem>
            <rdg wit="A">
There . . .

              <hi rend="smallcaps">finn</hi>
.

            </rdg>
            <rdg wit="LoM">
              <note place="inline" resp="MTP" type="ed" xml:id="de0956">not in</note>
            </rdg>
          </app>
          <figure rend="block" xml:id="y36201">
            <graphic url="y36201.jpg"/>
          </figure>
          <anchor xml:id="da9872"/>
        </p>
      </div1>
