a night we would see a steamboat slipping along

              <anchor type="alt" xml:id="tg1644"/>
in the dark,

              <ptr target="#l11288" type="alt" xml:id="te1644"/>
              <del>away over on t’other side, like a long string of glow-worms,</del>
and now and then she would belch a whole world of sparks up out of her

              <del>chimneys,</del>
              <add rend="shaded">chimbleys,</add>
and they would

              <del>trail off and</del>
rain down in the river and look awful pretty; then

              <del>the boat</del>
              <add rend="shaded">she</add>
would turn a corner and her light

              <add type="print">s</add>
would wink out and her pow-wow

              <del>die down</del>
              <add rend="shaded">shut off</add>
and leave the

              <del>big</del>
river

              <del>all to us</del>
              <add rend="shaded">still</add>
again; and by and by

              <del>the wash of</del>
her waves would

              <del>travel</del>
              <add rend="shaded">get</add>
to us,

              <add rend="shaded">a</add>
long

              <add type="print">time</add>
after she was gone, and joggle

              <del>our</del>
              <add rend="shaded">the</add>
