            <lb/>
            <p rend="noindent" xml:id="d1e94407">
rock; we’ll

              <del>fetch</del>
              <add>go & get</add>
a rock.

            </p>
            <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e94414">
Jim said it would take him such a pison long time to dig them into a

              <hi rend="italic">rock</hi>
, he wouldn’t

              <hi rend="italic">ever</hi>
get out.

            </p>
            <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e94422">
But it had to be done. Tom says:

              <del>We got to have</del>
“There’s a gaudy big grindstone down at the mill; well smouch

              <hi rend="italic">that</hi>
& carve the things on it.

            </p>
            <p rend="text-indent:2" xml:id="d1e94430">
It warn’t no slouch of an idea; & it warn’t no slouch of a

              <hi rend="italic">grinds</hi>
tone,

              <hi rend="italic">nuther.</hi>
We smouched it, & set out to roll her home that hot summer night, & it was a most nation tough job. Sometimes, do what we could, we couldn’t keep her from falling over; & she come mighty

            </p>
